 비결정성 시스템의 평가에 적합합니다","es":"La evaluación de sistemas de agentes requiere enfoques diferentes a los de software tradicional","fr":"L''évaluation des systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentensystemen erfordert andere Ansätze als die traditionelle Software","pt":"O skill de avaliação permite desenvolver estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes, considerando suas características dinâmicas e não determinísticas.","ru":"Навык оценки позволяет разработать структуры оценки для систем агентов, учитывая их динамические и неопределенные характеристики.","ar":"مهارة التقييم تمكن من بناء هياكل تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء، مع الأخذ في الاعتبار سماتها الديناميكية وغير المحددة.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["构建评估框架","动态决策支持","非确定性系统评估","多样化评估方法","适用于agent系统"],"ja":["評価フレームワークの構築","動的意思決定のサポート","非決定性システムの評価","多様な評価方法","エージェントシステム向け"],"ko":["평가 프레임워크 구축","동적 의사 결정 지원","비결정성 시스템 평가","다양한 평가 방법","에이전트 시스템을 위한"],"es":["Marco de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Métodos de evaluación para sistemas dinámicos","Análisis de rendimiento de agentes","Optimización de aplicaciones"],"fr":["Cadre d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Méthodes d''évaluation pour les systèmes dynamiques","Analyse des performances des agents","Optimisation des applications"],"de":["Bewertungsrahmen für Agentensysteme","Bewertungsmethoden für dynamische Systeme","Leistungsanalyse von Agenten","Optimierung von Anwendungen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","Métodos de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Consideração de características dinâmicas e não determinísticas","Avaliação de desempenho de sistemas de agentes","Integração com sistemas de tomada de decisões"],"ru":["Разработка структур оценки","Методы оценки для систем агентов","Учет динамических и неопределенных характеристик","Оценка производительности систем агентов","Интеграция с системами принятия решений"],"ar":["بناء هياكل تقييم","أساليب تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","الاعتبار لسمات ديناميكية وغير محددة","تقييم أداء أنظمة الوكلاء","التكامل مع أنظمة اتخاذ القرارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["agent系统评估","评估技能","动态决策","非确定性系统","评估框架","agent系统开发"],"ja":["エージェントシステム評価","評価スキル","動的意思決定","非決定性システム","評価フレームワーク","エージェントシステム開発"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템 평가","평가 스킬","동적 의사 결정","비결정성 시스템","평가 프레임워크","에이전트 시스템 개발"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","marcos de evaluación","métodos de evaluación","análisis de rendimiento","optimización de aplicaciones","sistemas dinámicos"],"fr":["évaluation des systèmes d''agents","cadres d''évaluation","méthodes d''évaluation","analyse des performances","optimisation des applications","systèmes dynamiques"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentensystemen","Bewertungsrahmen","Bewertungsmethoden","Leistungsanalyse","Optimierung von Anwendungen","dynamische Systeme"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","métodos de avaliação","sistemas de agentes","tomada de decisões","inteligência artificial","aprendizado de máquina"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","разработка структур оценки","методы оценки","системы агентов","принятие решений","искусственный интеллект","обучение машин"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","بناء هياكل تقييم","أساليب تقييم","أنظمة الوكلاء","اتخاذ القرارات","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التعلم الآلي"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:08:15.676Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous Agents requiring dynamic decision-making assessment and non-deterministic outcome evaluation.","zh":"非常适合需要动态决策评估和非确定性结果评估的自主代理。","ja":"動的意思決定評価と非決定性結果評価を必要とする自律エージェントに最適です。","ko":"동적 의사결정 평가 및 비결정적 결과 평가가 필요한 자율 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Autónomos que requieren evaluación de toma de decisiones dinámicas y evaluación de resultados no deterministas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents Autonomes nécessitant une évaluation de prise de décision dynamique et une évaluation de résultats non déterministes.","de":"Perfekt für autonome Agenten, die eine dynamische Entscheidungsfindungsbewertung und eine Bewertung nicht-deterministischer Ergebnisse erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Autônomos que exigem avaliação de tomada de decisão dinâmica e avaliação de resultados não determinísticos.","ru":"Идеально для автономных агентов, требующих динамической оценки принятия решений и оценки неопределенных результатов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأوتوماتيكيين الذين يحتاجون إلى تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي وتقييم النتائج غير المحددة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build comprehensive evaluation frameworks, leveraging approaches tailored for agent systems, including dynamic decision-making and non-deterministic assessments, to ensure effective evaluation and validation of their performance.","zh":"赋予代理构建全面评估框架的能力，利用针对代理系统量身定制的方法，包括动态决策和非确定性评估，以确保有效评估和验证其性能。","ja":"エージェントは、動的意思決定と非決定性評価を含むエージェントシステムに特化したアプローチを利用して、包括的な評価フレームワークを構築することができ、効果的な評価と検証を実現します。","ko":"에이전트는 동적 의사결정 및 비결정적 평가를 포함하여 에이전트 시스템에 특화된 접근 방식을 사용하여 포괄적인 평가 프레임워크를 구축할 수 있으며, 효과적인 평가 및 검증을 달성할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear marcos de evaluación comprehensivos, aprovechando enfoques adaptados a los sistemas de agentes, incluyendo la toma de decisiones dinámicas y evaluaciones no deterministas, para garantizar una evaluación y validación efectivas de su rendimiento.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des cadres d''évaluation complets, en exploitant des approches adaptées aux systèmes d''agents, y compris la prise de décision dynamique et les évaluations non déterministes, pour assurer une évaluation et une validation efficaces de leur performance.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, umfassende Bewertungsrahmen zu erstellen, indem sie Ansätze nutzen, die auf Agentsysteme zugeschnitten sind, einschließlich dynamischer Entscheidungsfindung und nicht-deterministischer Bewertungen, um eine effektive Bewertung und Validierung ihrer Leistung sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir estruturas de avaliação abrangentes, utilizando abordagens personalizadas para sistemas de agentes, incluindo tomada de decisão dinâmica e avaliações não determinísticas, para garantir avaliação e validação eficazes do seu desempenho.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать комплексные рамки оценки, используя подходы, адаптированные для систем агентов, включая динамическую оценку принятия решений и неопределенные оценки, для обеспечения эффективной оценки и проверки их производительности.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من بناء إطارات تقييم شاملة، باستخدام طرق مخصصة لأنظمة الوكلاء، بما في ذلك اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي وتقييمات غير محددة، لضمان تقييم وتصديق فعالين لأدائهم."},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing dynamic decision-making in non-deterministic environments","Validating agent performance in multi-run scenarios"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估非确定性环境中的动态决策","验证多次运行场景中的代理性能"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの評価フレームワークを構築する","非決定性環境における動的意思決定を評価する","マルチランシナリオでのエージェントのパフォーマンスを検証する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템의 평가 프레임워크 구축","비결정적 환경에서 동적 의사결정 평가","다중 실행 시나리오에서 에이전트 성능 검증"],"es":["Creación de marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluación de la toma de decisiones dinámicas en entornos no deterministas","Validación del rendimiento de los agentes en escenarios de ejecución múltiple"],"fr":["Création de cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluation de la prise de décision dynamique dans des environnements non déterministes","Validation de la performance des agents dans des scénarios de exécution multiple"],"de":["Erstellung von Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme","Bewertung der dynamischen Entscheidungsfindung in nicht-deterministischen Umgebungen","Validierung der Leistung von Agenten in Multi-Lauf-Szenarien"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliar a tomada de decisão dinâmica em ambientes não determinísticos","Validar o desempenho do agente em cenários de várias execuções"],"ru":["Создание рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка динамического принятия решений в неопределенных средах","Проверка производительности агента в сценариях множественных запусков"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي في بيئات غير محددة","تصديق أداء الوكيل في سيناريوهات التشغيل المتعدد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent systems and their unique evaluation challenges","May need customization for specific agent system architectures"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统及其独特的评估挑战","可能需要针对特定代理系统架构的自定义"],"ja":["エージェントシステムとその独自の評価課題を理解する必要がある","特定のエージェントシステムアーキテクチャのためにカスタマイズが必要となる可能性がある"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템 및 그 고유의 평가 과제에 대한 이해가 필요함","특정 에이전트 시스템 아키텍처를 위한 사용자 지정이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los sistemas de agentes y sus desafíos de evaluación únicos","Puede necesitar personalización para arquitecturas de sistemas de agentes específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des systèmes d''agents et de leurs défis d''évaluation uniques","Peut nécessiter une personnalisation pour les architectures de systèmes d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis von Agentsystemen und ihren einzigartigen Bewertungsherausforderungen","Kann eine Anpassung für bestimmte Agentsystemarchitekturen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos sistemas de agentes e seus desafios de avaliação únicos","Pode precisar de personalização para arquiteturas de sistemas de agentes específicas"],"ru":["Требует понимания систем агентов и их уникальных проблем оценки","Может потребовать настройки для конкретных архитектур систем агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لأنظمة الوكلاء وتحديات التقييم الفريدة لها","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى تخصيص لعمارة أنظمة الوكلاء المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
