eidungsfindung","Optimierung der Systemleistung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","Métodos de avaliação eficazes","Consideração da natureza dinâmica dos sistemas","Abordagens não tradicionais de avaliação","Avaliação de sistemas com decisões não determinísticas"],"ru":["Разработка структур оценки","Эффективные методы оценки","Учет динамической природы систем","Нетрадиционные подходы к оценке","Оценка систем с неоднозначными решениями"],"ar":["تطوير هياكل تقييم","طرق تقييم فعالة","مراعاة الطبيعة الديناميكية لأنظمة الوكلاء","نهج غير تقليدي لتقييم","تقييم أنظمة مع قرارات غير حتمية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["评估技能","智能代理系统","评估框架","动态决策","非确定性行为","多种评估方法","代理系统评估"],"ja":["評価スキル","エージェントシステム","評価フレームワーク","動的決定","非決定性挙動","多様な評価方法","エージェントシステム評価"],"ko":["평가 스킬","에이전트 시스템","평가 프레임워크","동적 결정","비결정성 행동","다양한 평가 방법","에이전트 시스템 평가"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","desarrollo de agentes","sistemas de agentes","evaluación de software","tomar decisiones","sistemas no deterministas","evaluación de rendimiento","optimización del sistema"],"fr":["évaluation des systèmes d''agents","développement d''agents","systèmes d''agents","évaluation de logiciels","prise de décision","systèmes non déterministes","évaluation des performances","optimisation du système"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","Entwicklung von Agents","Agentsysteme","Bewertung von Software","Entscheidungsfindung","nicht deterministische Systeme","Bewertung der Leistung","Optimierung des Systems"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","métodos de avaliação eficazes","sistemas dinâmicos","decisões não determinísticas","agentes inteligentes"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","разработка структур оценки","эффективные методы оценки","динамические системы","неоднозначные решения","интеллектуальные агенты"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","تطوير هياكل تقييم","طرق تقييم فعالة","أنظمة ديناميكية","قرارات غير حتمية","وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي"]}},"owner":"mshraditya","repo":"SkillsForAgentRegistry","repoPath":"mshraditya/SkillsForAgentRegistry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:08:33.966Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适合于像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要动态评估框架来评估代理系统","ja":"AutoGPTやLangChainのような高度なAIエージェントに適しており、エージェントシステムのための動的評価フレームワークを必要とする","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 에이전트 시스템을 위한 동적 평가 프레임워크가 필요함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agents wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die dynamische Bewertungsrahmen für Agentensysteme erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como AutoGPT e LangChain que requerem estruturas de avaliação dinâmicas para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих динамических рамок оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمين مثل AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى إطارات تقييم ديناميكية لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build evaluation frameworks that account for dynamic decisions and non-deterministic outcomes, utilizing methods that accommodate the lack of single correct answers in agent systems, and integrating with protocols for effective assessment","zh":"能够使代理能够建立评估框架，以适应动态决策和非确定性结果，利用能够容纳代理系统中没有单一正确答案的方法，并集成有效评估的协议","ja":"エージェントが、動的な決定や非決定的な結果を考慮した評価フレームワークを構築できるようにし、エージェントシステムで単一の正解がないことを考慮した方法を利用し、有効な評価のためのプロトコルと統合する","ko":"에이전트가 동적 결정과 비결정적 결과를 고려한 평가 프레임워크를 구축할 수 있도록 하며 에이전트 시스템에서 하나의 올바른 답이 없는 경우를 고려한 방법을 사용하고 효과적인 평가를 위한 프로토콜과 통합함","es":"Permite a los agentes crear marcos de evaluación que tengan en cuenta decisiones dinámicas y resultados no deterministas, utilizando métodos que acomoden la falta de respuestas correctas únicas en los sistemas de agentes, e integrándose con protocolos para una evaluación efectiva","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des cadres d''évaluation qui tiennent compte des décisions dynamiques et des résultats non déterministes, en utilisant des méthodes qui prennent en compte l''absence de réponses correctes uniques dans les systèmes d''agents, et en s''intégrant avec des protocoles pour une évaluation efficace","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Bewertungsrahmen zu erstellen, die dynamische Entscheidungen und nichtdeterministische Ergebnisse berücksichtigen, indem Methoden verwendet werden, die den Mangel an einzelnen korrekten Antworten in Agentensystemen ausgleichen, und sich in Protokolle für eine wirksame Bewertung integrieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir estruturas de avaliação que levam em conta decisões dinâmicas e resultados não determinísticos, utilizando métodos que acomodam a falta de respostas corretas únicas em sistemas de agentes, e integrando com protocolos para avaliação eficaz","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать рамки оценки, которые учитывают динамические решения и неопределенные результаты, используя методы, которые учитывают отсутствие единственно правильных ответов в системах агентов, и интегрируются с протоколами для эффективной оценки","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من بناء إطارات تقييم تأخذ في الاعتبار القرارات الديناميكية والنتائج غير الحتمية، باستخدام أساليب تتيح عدم وجود إجابات صحيحة فريدة في أنظمة الوكلاء، وتدمج مع بروتوكولات للتقويم الفعال"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for multi-agent systems","Assessing dynamic decision-making in agent-based models","Developing non-deterministic testing protocols for AI agents"],"zh":["为多代理系统构建评估框架","评估基于代理的模型中的动态决策","为AI代理开发非确定性测试协议"],"ja":["マルチエージェントシステムのための評価フレームワークを構築する","エージェントベースモデルの動的な意思決定を評価する","AIエージェントのための非決定性テストプロトコルを開発する"],"ko":["다중 에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","에이전트 기반 모델의 동적 결정 평가","AI 에이전트를 위한 비결정적 테스트 프로토콜 개발"],"es":["Creación de marcos de evaluación para sistemas de multiagentes","Evaluación de la toma de decisiones dinámicas en modelos basados en agentes","Desarrollo de protocolos de prueba no deterministas para agentes de IA"],"fr":["Création de cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes multi-agents","Évaluation de la prise de décision dynamique dans les modèles basés sur les agents","Développement de protocoles de test non déterministes pour les agents IA"],"de":["Erstellung von Bewertungsrahmen für Multiagentensysteme","Bewertung der dynamischen Entscheidungsfindung in agentenbasierten Modellen","Entwicklung nichtdeterministischer Testprotokolle für KI-Agents"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de multiagentes","Avaliar a tomada de decisão dinâmica em modelos baseados em agentes","Desenvolver protocolos de teste não determinísticos para agentes de IA"],"ru":["Построение рамок оценки для систем многоагентных","Оценка динамического принятия решений в моделях на основе агентов","Разработка неопределенных протоколов тестирования для агентов ИИ"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة متعددة الوكلاء","تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي في نماذج قائمة على الوكلاء","تطوير بروتوكولات اختبار غير حتمية للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent system characteristics","May need customization for specific agent architectures"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统的特征","可能需要为特定的代理架构进行自定义"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの特性を理解する必要がある","特定のエージェントアーキテクチャのためにカスタマイズが必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템의 특성을 이해해야 함","특정 에이전트 아키텍처를 위해 사용자 지정이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las características de los sistemas de agentes","Puede necesitar personalización para arquitecturas de agentes específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des caractéristiques des systèmes d''agents","Peut nécessiter une personnalisation pour les architectures d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis für die Eigenschaften von Agentensystemen","Kann Anpassung für spezifische Agentenarchitekturen benötigen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das características do sistema de agentes","Pode precisar de personalização para arquiteturas de agentes específicas"],"ru":["Требует понимания характеристик системы агентов","Может потребовать настройки для конкретных архитектур агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لخصائص نظام الوكلاء","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى تخصيص للعمارة الفريدة للوكلاء"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ngxtm/devkit/evaluation', 'community', 'ngxtm', 'devkit', 'ngxtm/devkit', 'evaluation', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z', '2026-02-18T02:08:36.030Z', NULL, '{"id":"ngxtm/devkit/evaluation","name":"evaluation","description":{"zh":"评估技能是AI代码助手的统一多代理系统，用于构建评估框架。该技能支持智能技术检测和自动同步","ja":"評価スキルは、AIコーディングアシスタントの統一マルチエージェントシステムであり、評価フレームワークを構築するために使用されます","ko":"평가 스킬은 AI 코드 어시스턴트의 통일 다중 에이전트 시스템으로, 평가 프레임워크를 구축하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"La evaluación de sistemas de agentes requiere enfoques diferentes a los de software tradicional. Nuestro sistema de habilidades unificado ayuda a construir marcos de evaluación","fr":"L''évaluation de systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel. Notre système de compétences unifié aide à construire des cadres d''évaluation","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentsystemen erfordert andere Ansätze als die traditionelle Software. Unser einheitliches Skill-System hilft beim Erstellen von Bewertungsrahmen","pt":"A habilidade de avaliação é uma ferramenta fundamental para desenvolvedores de sistemas de agentes, permitindo a construção de frameworks de avaliação personalizados","ru":"Навык оценки является фундаментальным инструментом для разработчиков систем агентов, позволяющим создавать индивидуальные фреймворки оценки","ar":"مهارة التقييم هي أداة أساسية لمطوري أنظمة الوكلاء، مما يسمح ببناء إطارات تقييم مخصصة","en":"Unified multi-agent skill system for AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini) with 414+ skills, 38 agents, and 57 commands. Features smart tech   detection, per-project installation, and auto-sync from upstream sources."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"评估技能：AI 代码助手的统一多代理系统","ja":"評価スキル：AI コーディングアシスタントの統一マルチエージェントシステム","ko":"평가 스킬: AI 코드 어시스턴트의 통일 다중 에이전트 시스템","es":"Evaluación de sistemas de agentes","fr":"Évaluation de systèmes d''agents","de":"Bewertung von Agentsystemen","pt":"Avaliação de Sistemas de Agentes: Técnicas e Ferramentas","ru":"Оценка систем агентов: методы и инструменты","ar":"تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء: تقنيات وأدوات","en":"evaluation"},"description":{"zh":"评估技能是AI代码助手的统一多代理系统，用于构建评估框架。该技能支持智能技术检测和自动同步","ja":"評価スキルは、AIコーディングアシスタントの統一マルチエージェントシステムであり、評価フレームワークを構築するために使用されます","ko":"평가 스킬은 AI 코드 어시스턴트의 통일 다중 에이전트 시스템으로, 평가 프레임워크를 구축하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"La evaluación de sistemas de agentes requiere enfoques diferentes a los de software tradicional. Nuestro sistema de habilidades unificado ayuda a construir m...","fr":"L''évaluation de systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel. Notre système de compétences unifié aide à construi...","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentsystemen erfordert andere Ansätze als die traditionelle Software. Unser einheitliches Skill-System hilft beim Erstellen von Bewertungs...","pt":"A habilidade de avaliação é uma ferramenta fundamental para desenvolvedores de sistemas de agentes, permitindo a construção de frameworks de avaliação person...","ru":"Навык оценки является фундаментальным инструментом для разработчиков систем агентов, позволяющим создавать индивидуальные фреймворки оценки","ar":"مهارة التقييم هي أداة أساسية لمطوري أنظمة الوكلاء، مما يسمح ببناء إطارات تقييم مخصصة","en":"Unified multi-agent skill system for AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini) with 414+ skills, 38 agents, and 57 commands. Features smart..."},"definition":{"en":"Unified multi-agent skill system for AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini) with 414+ skills, 38 agents, and 57 commands. Features smart tech   detection, per-project installation, and auto-sync from upstream sources."},"features":{"zh":["智能技术检测","自动同步","评估框架构建","多代理系统","统一接口"],"ja":["スマートテクノロジー検出","自動同期","評価フレームワーク構築","マルチエージェントシステム","統一インターフェース"],"ko":["智能 기술 감지","자동 동기화","평가 프레임워크 구축","다중 에이전트 시스템","통일 인터페이스"],"es":["Detección de tecnología inteligente","Instalación por proyecto","Sincronización automática desde fuentes de upstream","Marco de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Soporte para múltiples agentes","Unificado con 414+ habilidades"],"fr":["Détection de technologie intelligente","Installation par projet","Synchronisation automatique depuis les sources de upstream","Cadre d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Prise en charge de plusieurs agents","Unifié avec 414+ compétences"],"de":["Intelligente Technologie-Erkennung","Projektinstallation","Automatische Synchronisation von Upstream-Quellen","Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme","Unterstützung für mehrere Agenten","Einheitlich mit 414+ Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Detecção de tecnologia inteligente","Instalação por projeto","Sincronização automática de fontes de upstream","Avaliação de frameworks de agentes","Suporte a múltiplos agentes","Integração com Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot e Gemini"],"ru":["Обнаружение умной технологии","Установка по проекту","Автоматическая синхронизация источников upstream","Оценка фреймворков агентов","Поддержка нескольких агентов","Интеграция с Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot и Gemini"],"ar":["اكتشاف التكنولوجيا الذكية","التثبيت حسب المشروع","التزامن التلقائي لمصادر Upstream","تقييم إطارات الوكلاء","دعم متعددة الوكلاء","التكامل مع Claude Code و Cursor و Copilot و Gemini"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI代码助手","评估技能","统一多代理系统","智能技术检测","自动同步","评估框架"],"ja":["AIコーディングアシスタント","評価スキル","統一マルチエージェントシステム","スマートテクノロジー検出","自動同期","評価フレームワーク"],"ko":["AI 코드 어시스턴트","평가 스킬","통일 다중 에이전트 시스템","智能 기술 감지","자동 동기화","평가 프레임워크"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","marco de evaluación","sistemas de agentes","detección de tecnología inteligente","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","evaluación de software","sistemas de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["évaluation de systèmes d''agents","cadre d''évaluation","systèmes d''agents","détection de technologie intelligente","développement de logiciel","ingénierie de logiciel","évaluation de logiciel","systèmes d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","Bewertungsrahmen","Agentsysteme","intelligente Technologie-Erkennung","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen","Software-Bewertung","Künstliche Intelligenz-Systeme"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","desenvolvimento de agentes","sistemas de agentes","ferramentas de avaliação","frameworks de avaliação","tecnologia de agentes","inteligência artificial","aprendizado de máquina"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","разработка агентов","системы агентов","инструменты оценки","фреймворки оценки","технология агентов","искусственный интеллект","машинное обучение"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","تطوير الوكلاء","أنظمة الوكلاء","أدوات التقييم","إطارات التقييم","تكنولوجيا الوكلاء","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التعلم الالي"]}},"owner":"ngxtm","repo":"devkit","repoPath":"ngxtm/devkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:08:36.030Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Coding Assistants like Claude Code, Cursor, and Copilot needing advanced evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适合于 Claude Code、Cursor 和 Copilot 等需要高级评估框架的 AI 编码助手","ja":"Claude Code、Cursor、Copilot などの高度な評価フレームワークを必要とする AI コーディング アシスタントに適しています","ko":"클로드 코드, 커서, 코파일럿 등 고급 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 AI 코딩 보조기에게 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para asistentes de codificación de IA como Claude Code, Cursor y Copilot que necesitan marcos de evaluación avanzados para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les assistants de codage IA comme Claude Code, Cursor et Copilot nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation avancés pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für AI-Coding-Assistenten wie Claude Code, Cursor und Copilot, die erweiterte Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Assistente de Codificação de IA, como Claude Code, Cursor e Copilot, que precisam de quadros de avaliação avançados para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для помощников кодирования ИИ, таких как Claude Code, Cursor и Copilot, которым необходимы продвинутые рамки оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي لمساعدات الترميز الإصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Cursor و Copilot التي تحتاج إلى إطارات تقييم متقدمة لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build dynamic evaluation frameworks using smart tech detection, per-project installation, and auto-sync from upstream sources, enabling effective assessment of non-deterministic agent systems with multiple correct answers","zh":"使代理能够使用智能技术检测、每个项目的安装和上游源的自动同步来构建动态评估框架，从而能够有效地评估具有多个正确答案的非确定性代理系统","ja":"エージェントがスマートテクノロジー検出、プロジェクトごとのインストール、および上流ソースからの自動同期を使用して動的評価フレームワークを構築できるようにし、非決定性エージェントシステムの有効な評価を可能にします","ko":"스마트 기술 감지, 프로젝트별 설치 및 업스트림 소스의 자동 동기화를 사용하여 동적 평가 프레임워크를 구축할 수 있으므로 다중 정답을 갖는 비결정적 에이전트 시스템의 효과적인 평가가 가능합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear marcos de evaluación dinámicos utilizando la detección de tecnología inteligente, la instalación por proyecto y la auto-sincronización desde fuentes de nivel superior, lo que permite una evaluación efectiva de los sistemas de agentes no deterministas con varias respuestas correctas","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques en utilisant la détection de technologie intelligente, l''installation par projet et la synchronisation automatique à partir de sources en amont, permettant ainsi une évaluation efficace des systèmes d''agents non déterministes avec plusieurs réponses correctes","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, dynamische Bewertungsframeworks mit Hilfe von Smart-Tech-Erkennung, pro-Projekt-Installation und Auto-Synchronisation aus Quellen höherer Ebene zu erstellen, wodurch eine effektive Bewertung nicht-deterministischer Agentsysteme mit mehreren richtigen Antworten ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir quadros de avaliação dinâmicos usando detecção de tecnologia inteligente, instalação por projeto e sincronização automática de fontes de upstream, permitindo uma avaliação eficaz de sistemas de agentes não determinísticos com várias respostas corretas","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать динамические рамки оценки, используя умную технологию обнаружения, установку по проекту и автоматическую синхронизацию из источников upstream, что позволяет эффективно оценивать неопределенные системы агентов с несколькими правильными ответами","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء إطارات تقييم ديناميكية باستخدام كشف التكنولوجيا الذكية والتركيب لكل مشروع والتنسيق التلقائي من المصادر الرئيسية، مما يتيح التقييم الفعال لأنظمة الوكلاء الغير محددة مع إجابات متعددة صحيحة"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing dynamic decision-making in agents","Comparing performance of different agent architectures"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估代理的动态决策","比较不同代理体系结构的性能"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの評価フレームワークを構築する","エージェントの動的意思決定を評価する","異なるエージェントアーキテクチャの性能を比較する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","에이전트의 동적 의사 결정 평가","다양한 에이전트 아키텍처의 성능 비교"],"es":["Creación de marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluación de la toma de decisiones dinámica en los agentes","Comparación del rendimiento de diferentes arquitecturas de agentes"],"fr":["Création de cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluation de la prise de décision dynamique dans les agents","Comparaison des performances de différentes architectures d''agents"],"de":["Erstellung von Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme","Bewertung der dynamischen Entscheidungsfindung in Agents","Vergleich der Leistung unterschiedlicher Agentenarchitekturen"],"pt":["Construir quadros de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliar a tomada de decisões dinâmica em agentes","Comparar o desempenho de diferentes arquiteturas de agentes"],"ru":["Создание рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка динамического принятия решений в агентах","Сравнение производительности различных архитектур агентов"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي في الوكلاء","مقارنة أداء هياكل الوكلاء المختلفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent systems and evaluation methodologies","May need additional configuration for specific agent types"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统和评估方法论","可能需要为特定代理类型进行额外配置"],"ja":["エージェントシステムと評価方法論の理解が必要","特定のエージェントタイプの場合、追加の構成が必要になる場合があります"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템 및 평가 방법론에 대한 이해가 필요함","특정 에이전트 유형의 경우 추가 구성이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los sistemas de agentes y metodologías de evaluación","Puede necesitar configuración adicional para tipos de agentes específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des systèmes d''agents et des méthodologies d''évaluation","Peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour des types d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für Agentsysteme und Bewertungsmethoden","Kann für bestimmte Agententypen zusätzliche Konfiguration erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de sistemas de agentes e metodologias de avaliação","Pode precisar de configuração adicional para tipos específicos de agentes"],"ru":["Требует понимания систем агентов и методологий оценки","Может потребовать дополнительной настройки для определенных типов агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لأنظمة الوكلاء ومنهجيات التقييم","قد تحتاج إلى تكوين إضافي لنوع معين من الوكلاء"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
