ierung von Bewertungsframeworks","Analyse von Ergebnissen und Leistung","Integration mit Entwicklungsumgebungen"],"pt":["Construção de estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Abordagens de avaliação para sistemas dinâmicos e não determinísticos","Consideração de características únicas de sistemas de agentes","Desenvolvimento de métodos de avaliação eficazes","Análise de desempenho de sistemas de agentes"],"ru":["Создание оценочных рамок для систем агентов","Подходы к оценке для динамических и недетерминированных систем","Учет уникальных характеристик систем агентов","Разработка эффективных методов оценки","Анализ производительности систем агентов"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","مناهج تقييم لأنظمة ديناميكية وغير قابلة للتحدید","الأخذ في الاعتبار لسمات أنظمة الوكلاء الفريدة","تطوير أساليب تقييم فعالة","تحليل أداء أنظمة الوكلاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["评估技能","智能代理系统","评估框架","评估方法","传统评估方法","效率和准确性","构建评估框架"],"ja":["評価スキル","エージェントシステム","評価フレームワーク","評価方法","従来の評価方法","効率と精度","評価フレームワークの構築"],"ko":["평가 스킬","에이전트 시스템","평가 프레임워크","평가 방법","전통적인 평가 방법","효율과 정확도","평가 프레임워크 구축"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","marco de evaluación","decisiones dinámicas","no determinísticas","frameworks de evaluación","análisis de resultados"],"fr":["évaluation des systèmes d''agents","cadre d''évaluation","décisions dynamiques","non déterministes","cadres d''évaluation","analyse de résultats"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","Bewertungsrahmen","dynamische Entscheidungen","nicht deterministische","Bewertungsframeworks","Analyse von Ergebnissen"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","desenvolvimento de agentes","sistemas dinâmicos","métodos de avaliação","análise de desempenho","construção de estruturas de avaliação"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","разработка агентов","динамические системы","методы оценки","анализ производительности","создание оценочных рамок"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","تطوير الوكلاء","أنظمة ديناميكية","أساليب تقييم","تحليل أداء","بناء إطارات تقييم"]}},"owner":"YPYT1","repo":"All-skills","repoPath":"YPYT1/All-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:08:42.323Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要动态评估框架的代理系统","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、エージェント システムのための動的評価フレームワークを必要とする","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 에이전트 시스템을 위한 동적 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 경우에 사용","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avanzados como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de l''IA avancés comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die dynamische Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados, como Claude Code e AutoGPT, que requerem estruturas de avaliação dinâmicas para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих динамических рамок оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون أطر تقييم ديناميكية لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build evaluation frameworks using OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode, and other platforms, incorporating non-deterministic decision-making and dynamic agent behaviors, and leveraging evaluation methods tailored for agent systems","zh":"赋予代理构建使用 OpenCLAW、ClaudeCode 和其他平台的评估框架的能力，融入非确定性决策和动态代理行为，并利用为代理系统量身定制的评估方法","ja":"OpenCLAW、ClaudeCode、その他のプラットフォームを使用して評価フレームワークを構築するエージェントの能力を付与し、非決定性の意思決定と動的なエージェントの動作を組み込み、エージェント システムのためにカスタマイズされた評価方法を利用する","ko":"OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode 및 기타 플랫폼을 사용하여 평가 프레임워크를 구축하고 비결정적 의사 결정을 포함하고 동적 에이전트 동작을 포함하며 에이전트 시스템을 위한 맞춤형 평가 방법을 활용할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir marcos de evaluación utilizando OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode y otras plataformas, incorporando toma de decisiones no determinista y comportamientos dinámicos de los agentes, y aprovechando métodos de evaluación adaptados para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des cadres d''évaluation en utilisant OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode et d''autres plateformes, en intégrant la prise de décision non déterministe et les comportements dynamiques des agents, et en exploitant les méthodes d''évaluation adaptées aux systèmes d''agents","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Bewertungsrahmen mit OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode und anderen Plattformen zu erstellen, indem nicht-deterministische Entscheidungsfindung und dynamisches Agentenverhalten integriert und Bewertungsmethoden genutzt werden, die auf Agentsysteme zugeschnitten sind","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir estruturas de avaliação utilizando OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode e outras plataformas, incorporando processos de tomada de decisão não determinísticos e comportamentos de agentes dinâmicos, e utilizando métodos de avaliação personalizados para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать рамки оценки с использованием OpenCLAW, ClaudeCode и других платформ, включая неравномерное принятие решений и динамическое поведение агентов, а также используя методы оценки, адаптированные для систем агентов","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء أطر تقييم باستخدام OpenCLAW و ClaudeCode ومنصات أخرى، متضمنةً عمليات اتخاذ قرارات غير محددة وتصرفات وكلائية ديناميكية، واستخدام أساليب تقييم مخصصة لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing non-deterministic agent behaviors","Developing dynamic decision-making models"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估非确定性代理行为","开发动态决策模型"],"ja":["エージェント システムのための評価フレームワークを構築する","非決定性のエージェントの動作を評価する","動的な意思決定モデルを開発する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","비결정적 에이전트 동작 평가","동적 의사 결정 모델 개발"],"es":["Construir marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluar comportamientos de agentes no deterministas","Desarrollar modelos de toma de decisiones dinámicos"],"fr":["Construire des cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluer les comportements d''agents non déterministes","Développer des modèles de prise de décision dynamiques"],"de":["Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme erstellen","Nicht-deterministisches Agentenverhalten bewerten","Dynamische Entscheidungsmodelle entwickeln"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliar comportamentos de agentes não determinísticos","Desenvolver modelos de tomada de decisão dinâmicos"],"ru":["Построение рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка неравномерного поведения агентов","Разработка динамических моделей принятия решений"],"ar":["بناء أطر تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم سلوكيات الوكلاء غير المحددة","تطوير نماذج اتخاذ قرارات ديناميكية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent systems and evaluation methods","May need adaptation for specific agent architectures like LangChain or Windsurf"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统和评估方法","可能需要为特定的代理体系结构（如 LangChain 或 Windsurf）进行适配"],"ja":["エージェント システムと評価方法の理解が必要","LangChain または Windsurf などの特定のエージェント アーキテクチャのために適応が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템 및 평가 방법에 대한 이해가 필요","LangChain 또는 Windsurf와 같은 특정 에이전트 아키텍처에 대한 적응이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los sistemas de agentes y métodos de evaluación","Puede necesitar adaptación para arquitecturas de agentes específicas como LangChain o Windsurf"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des systèmes d''agents et des méthodes d''évaluation","Peut nécessiter une adaptation pour des architectures d''agents spécifiques comme LangChain ou Windsurf"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis von Agentsystemen und Bewertungsmethoden","Kann Anpassung für bestimmte Agentenarchitekturen wie LangChain oder Windsurf erfordern"],"pt":["Requer entendimento de sistemas de agentes e métodos de avaliação","Pode precisar de adaptação para arquiteturas de agentes específicas, como LangChain ou Windsurf"],"ru":["Требует понимания систем агентов и методов оценки","Может потребовать адаптации для конкретных архитектур агентов, таких как LangChain или Windsurf"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لأنظمة الوكلاء وأساليب التقييم","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى التكيف مع هياكل وكلاء محددة، مثل LangChain أو Windsurf"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Kikobeats/dotfiles/schema-markup', 'community', 'Kikobeats', 'dotfiles', 'Kikobeats/dotfiles', 'schema-markup', 0, 0, 85, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z', '2026-02-18T02:08:58.608Z', NULL, '{"id":"Kikobeats/dotfiles/schema-markup","name":"schema-markup","description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据，帮助搜索引擎了解您的内容，实现丰富的搜索结果。通过 Schema 标记，开发者可以提高网站的可见性和点击率","ja":"スキーマ マークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を実現するのに役立つ構造化データです。スキーマ マークアップを使用すると、開発者は Web サイトの可視性とクリック率を向上させることができます","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를实现하는 데 도움이 되는 구조화된 데이터입니다. 스키마 마크업을 사용하면 개발자는 웹 사이트의 가시성과 클릭률을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El marcado de esquema es fundamental para que los motores de búsqueda entiendan el contenido y muestren resultados enriquecidos. Aprende a implementarlo","fr":"Les balises de schéma sont essentielles pour que les moteurs de recherche comprennent le contenu et affichent des résultats enrichis. Découvrez comment les mettre en œuvre","de":"Schema-Markup ist entscheidend für die Verständnis der Suchmaschinen und die Anzeige von erweiterten Ergebnissen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es implementieren","pt":"O esquema de markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os mecanismos de busca entendam melhor o conteúdo e forneçam resultados ricos","ru":"Схема маркировки — это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы лучше понимали контент и предоставляли богатые результаты","ar":"مخطط التنسيق هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات بحيث تفهم محركات البحث المحتوى بشكل أفضل وتقدم نتائج غنية","en":".files, including ~/.osx — sensible hacker defaults for OS X "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Schema 标记 - 结构化数据和搜索引擎优化","ja":"スキーマ マークアップ - 構造化データと検索エンジン最適化","ko":"스키마 마크업 - 구조화된 데이터와 검색 엔진 최적화","es":"Marcado de esquema para desarrolladores","fr":"Balises de schéma pour les développeurs","de":"Schema-Markup für Entwickler","pt":"Esquema de Markup: Otimização de Resultados de Busca","ru":"Схема Маркировки: Улучшение Результатов Поиска","ar":"تنسيق مخطط: تحسين نتائج البحث","en":"schema-markup"},"description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据，帮助搜索引擎了解您的内容，实现丰富的搜索结果。通过 Schema 标记，开发者可以提高网站的可见性和点击率","ja":"スキーマ マークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を実現するのに役立つ構造化データです。スキーマ マークアップを使用すると、開発者は Web サイトの可視性とクリック率を向上させることができます","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를实现하는 데 도움이 되는 구조화된 데이터입니다. 스키마 마크업을 사용하면 개발자는 웹 사이트의 가시성과 클릭률을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El marcado de esquema es fundamental para que los motores de búsqueda entiendan el contenido y muestren resultados enriquecidos. Aprende a implementarlo","fr":"Les balises de schéma sont essentielles pour que les moteurs de recherche comprennent le contenu et affichent des résultats enrichis. Découvrez comment les m...","de":"Schema-Markup ist entscheidend für die Verständnis der Suchmaschinen und die Anzeige von erweiterten Ergebnissen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es implementieren","pt":"O esquema de markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os mecanismos de busca entendam melhor o conteúdo e forneçam resultados ricos","ru":"Схема маркировки — это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы лучше понимали контент и предоставляли богатые результаты","ar":"مخطط التنسيق هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات بحيث تفهم محركات البحث المحتوى بشكل أفضل وتقدم نتائج غنية","en":".files, including ~/.osx — sensible hacker defaults for OS X "},"definition":{"en":".files, including ~/.osx — sensible hacker defaults for OS X "},"features":{"zh":["结构化数据","搜索引擎优化","丰富的搜索结果","提高可见性","提高点击率","支持多种数据类型"],"ja":["構造化データ","検索エンジン最適化","豊富な検索結果","可視性の向上","クリック率の向上","複数のデータタイプのサポート"],"ko":["구조화된 데이터","검색 엔진 최적화","풍부한 검색 결과","가시성 향상","클릭률 향상","다양한 데이터 유형 지원"],"es":["Mejora la comprensión de los motores de búsqueda","Habilita resultados enriquecidos en la búsqueda","Incrementa la visibilidad del contenido","Ayuda a los usuarios a encontrar el contenido relevante","Es compatible con la mayoría de los motores de búsqueda"],"fr":["Améliore la compréhension des moteurs de recherche","Active les résultats enrichis dans la recherche","Augmente la visibilité du contenu","Aide les utilisateurs à trouver le contenu pertinent","Est compatible avec la plupart des moteurs de recherche"],"de":["Verbessert die Verständnis der Suchmaschinen","Aktiviert erweiterte Ergebnisse in der Suche","Erhöht die Sichtbarkeit des Inhalts","Hilft den Benutzern, relevante Inhalte zu finden","Ist mit den meisten Suchmaschinen kompatibel"],"pt":["Melhoria da visibilidade em resultados de busca","Habilitação de recursos ricos em resultados de busca","Estruturação de dados para mecanismos de busca","Compatibilidade com várias plataformas de busca","Facilitação da indexação de conteúdo"],"ru":["Улучшение видимости в результатах поиска","Включение богатых результатов в результатах поиска","Структуризация данных для поисковых систем","Совместимость с несколькими поисковыми платформами","Облегчение индексации контента"],"ar":["تحسين ظهور نتائج البحث","تفعيل النتائج الغنية في نتائج البحث","تنظيم البيانات لمحركات البحث","التوافق مع منصات بحث متعددة","تسهيل فهرسة المحتوى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Schema 标记","结构化数据","搜索引擎优化","微数据","丰富的搜索结果","可见性","点击率","开发者工具","Web 开发"],"ja":["スキーマ マークアップ","構造化データ","検索エンジン最適化","マイクロデータ","豊富な検索結果","可視性","クリック率","開発者ツール","Web 開発"],"ko":["스키마 마크업","구조화된 데이터","검색 엔진 최적화","마이크로데이터","풍부한 검색 결과","가시성","클릭률","개발자 툴","웹 개발"],"es":["marcado de esquema","schema.org","etiquetas de esquema","resultados enriquecidos","optimización de motores de búsqueda","desarrollo web","SEO"],"fr":["balises de schéma","schema.org","étiquettes de schéma","résultats enrichis","optimisation des moteurs de recherche","développement web","SEO"],"de":["Schema-Markup","schema.org","Schema-Tags","erweiterte Ergebnisse","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung","Web-Entwicklung","SEO"],"pt":["esquema de markup","otimização de resultados de busca","recursos ricos","dados estruturados","mecanismos de busca","visibilidade em busca"],"ru":["схема маркировки","улучшение результатов поиска","богатые результаты","структурированные данные","поисковые системы","видимость в поиске"],"ar":["مخطط التنسيق","تحسين نتائج البحث","نتائج غنية","بيانات مهيكلة","محركات البحث","ظهور في البحث"]}},"owner":"Kikobeats","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"Kikobeats/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.394Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"schema-markup","description":"When the user wants to add, fix, or optimize schema markup and structured data on their site. Also use when the user mentions schema markup, structured data, JSON-LD, rich snippets, schema.org, FAQ schema, product schema, review schema, or breadcrumb schema. For broader SEO issues, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type","body":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type** - What kind of page? What''s the primary content? What rich results are possible?\n\n2. **Current State** - Any existing schema? Errors in implementation? Which rich results already appearing?\n\n3. **Goals** - Which rich results are you targeting? What''s the business value?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Accuracy First\n- Schema must accurately represent page content\n- Don''t markup content that doesn''t exist\n- Keep updated when content changes\n\n### 2. Use JSON-LD\n- Google recommends JSON-LD format\n- Easier to implement and maintain\n- Place in `<head>` or end of `<body>`\n\n### 3. Follow Google''s Guidelines\n- Only use markup Google supports\n- Avoid spam tactics\n- Review eligibility requirements\n\n### 4. Validate Everything\n- Test before deploying\n- Monitor Search Console\n- Fix errors promptly\n\n---\n\n## Common Schema Types\n\n| Type | Use For | Required Properties |\n|------|---------|-------------------|\n| Organization | Company homepage/about | name, url |\n| WebSite | Homepage (search box) | name, url |\n| Article | Blog posts, news | headline, image, datePublished, author |\n| Product | Product pages | name, image, offers |\n| SoftwareApplication | SaaS/app pages | name, offers |\n| FAQPage | FAQ content | mainEntity (Q&A array) |\n| HowTo | Tutorials | name, step |\n| BreadcrumbList | Any page with breadcrumbs | itemListElement |\n| LocalBusiness | Local business pages | name, address |\n| Event | Events, webinars | name, startDate, location |\n\n**For complete JSON-LD examples**: See [references/schema-examples.md](references/schema-examples.md)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Organization (Company Page)\nRequired: name, url\nRecommended: logo, sameAs (social profiles), contactPoint\n\n### Article/BlogPosting\nRequired: headline, image, datePublished, author\nRecommended: dateModified, publisher, description\n\n### Product\nRequired: name, image, offers (price + availability)\nRecommended: sku, brand, aggregateRating, review\n\n### FAQPage\nRequired: mainEntity (array of Question/Answer pairs)\n\n### BreadcrumbList\nRequired: itemListElement (array with position, name, item)\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Schema Types\n\nYou can combine multiple schema types on one page using `@graph`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    { \"@type\": \"Organization\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"WebSite\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", ... }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation and Testing\n\n### Tools\n- **Google Rich Results Test**: https://search.google.com/test/rich-results\n- **Schema.org Validator**: https://validator.schema.org/\n- **Search Console**: Enhancements reports\n\n### Common Errors\n\n**Missing required properties** - Check Google''s documentation for required fields\n\n**Invalid values** - Dates must be ISO 8601, URLs fully qualified, enumerations exact\n\n**Mismatch with page content** - Schema doesn''t match visible content\n\n---\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Static Sites\n- Add JSON-LD directly in HTML template\n- Use includes/partials for reusable schema\n\n### Dynamic Sites (React, Next.js)\n- Component that renders schema\n- Server-side rendered for SEO\n- Serialize data to JSON-LD\n\n### CMS / WordPress\n- Plugins (Yoast, Rank Math, Schema Pro)\n- Theme modifications\n- Custom fields to structured data\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Schema Implementation\n```json\n// Full JSON-LD code block\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"...\",\n  // Complete markup\n}\n```\n\n### Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Validates in Rich Results Test\n- [ ] No errors or warnings\n- [ ] Matches page content\n- [ ] All required properties included\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What type of page is this?\n2. What rich results are you hoping to achieve?\n3. What data is available to populate the schema?\n4. Is there existing schema on the page?\n5. What''s your tech stack?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **seo-audit**: For overall SEO including schema review\n- **programmatic-seo**: For templated schema at scale\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:08:58.608Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SEO Optimization Agents needing advanced schema markup implementation for rich search results.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 schema 标记实现以获得丰富搜索结果的 SEO 优化代理","ja":"SEO 最適化エージェントがリッチ検索結果を得るための高度なスキーマ・マークアップの実装に最適","ko":"豊富한 검색 결과를 얻으려는 SEO 최적화 에이전트에게 적합한 고급 스키마 마크업 구현","es":"Perfecto para agentes de optimización de SEO que necesitan una implementación avanzada de marcado de esquema para resultados de búsqueda enriquecidos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''optimisation de SEO ayant besoin d''une mise en œuvre avancée de balisage de schéma pour des résultats de recherche enrichis.","de":"Perfekt für SEO-Optimierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Schema-Markup-Implementierung für umfangreiche Suchergebnisse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de Otimização de SEO que precisam de implementação avançada de marcação de esquema para resultados de pesquisa ricos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов оптимизации SEO, которым требуется продвинутая реализация схемы разметки для богатых результатов поиска.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحسين محركات البحث التي تحتاج إلى تنفيذ متقدم لترميز مخطط لنتائج البحث الغنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement schema.org markup, enabling search engines to understand content and display rich results in search, utilizing protocols like JSON-LD and microdata.","zh":"赋予代理实现 schema.org 标记的能力，使搜索引擎能够理解内容并在搜索中显示丰富的结果，使用 JSON-LD 和微数据等协议","ja":"エージェントが schema.org マークアップを実装できるようにし、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、検索でリッチな結果を表示できるようにする。JSON-LD やマイクロデータなどのプロトコルを使用","ko":"에이전트가 schema.org 마크업을 구현할 수 있도록 하여 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 검색에서 풍부한 결과를 표시할 수 있도록 함. JSON-LD 및 마이크로 데이터와 같은 프로토콜을 사용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar el marcado de schema.org, lo que permite a los motores de búsqueda comprender el contenido y mostrar resultados enriquecidos en la búsqueda, utilizando protocolos como JSON-LD y microdatos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre le balisage de schema.org, ce qui permet aux moteurs de recherche de comprendre le contenu et d''afficher des résultats enrichis dans la recherche, en utilisant des protocoles tels que JSON-LD et microdata.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, das schema.org-Markup zu implementieren, sodass Suchmaschinen den Inhalt verstehen und umfangreiche Ergebnisse in der Suche anzeigen können, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie JSON-LD und Microdata.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar a marcação schema.org, permitindo que os mecanismos de busca entendam o conteúdo e exibam resultados ricos na pesquisa, utilizando protocolos como JSON-LD e microdata.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать разметку schema.org, что позволяет поисковым системам понимать контент и отображать богатые результаты в поиске, используя протоколы seperti JSON-LD и микроданные.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تنفيذ ترميز مخطط. org، ما يسمح لمحركات البحث بفهم المحتوى وعرض نتائج غنية في البحث، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل JSON-LD وميكرو بيانات."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing product schema for e-commerce websites","Generating schema markup for article and blog posts","Optimizing local business listings with schema.org"],"zh":["为电子商务网站实施产品 schema","为文章和博客帖子生成 schema 标记","使用 schema.org 优化本地商业列表"],"ja":["電子商取引サイトの製品スキーマを実装する","記事やブログ投稿のスキーマ・マークアップを生成する","schema.org を使用してローカルビジネスリストを最適化する"],"ko":["전자상거래 웹사이트의 제품 스키마 구현","기사 및 블로그 게시물의 스키마 마크업 생성","schema.org를 사용하여 지역 비즈니스 목록 최적화"],"es":["Implementar el esquema de producto para sitios web de comercio electrónico","Generar marcado de esquema para artículos y publicaciones de blog","Optimizar listados de negocios locales con schema.org"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre le schéma de produit pour les sites web de commerce électronique","Générer le balisage de schéma pour les articles et les publications de blog","Optimiser les listes d''entreprises locales avec schema.org"],"de":["Implementierung des Produktschemas für E-Commerce-Websites","Generierung von Schema-Markup für Artikel und Blog-Beiträge","Optimierung von lokalen Geschäftsverzeichnissen mit schema.org"],"pt":["Implementar esquema de produto para sites de comércio eletrônico","Gerar marcação de esquema para artigos e posts de blog","Otimizar listagens de empresas locais com schema.org"],"ru":["Реализовать схему продукта для электронных коммерческих сайтов","Генерировать разметку схемы для статей и постов в блоге","Оптимизировать местные списки бизнеса с помощью schema.org"],"ar":["تنفيذ مخطط المنتج لمواقع التجارة الإلكترونية","генерировать ترميز مخطط للمقالات ومنشورات المدونة","تحسين قوائم الأعمال المحلية بمخطط. org"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of schema.org vocabulary","Limited to supporting search engines that recognize schema.org markup"],"zh":["需要了解 schema.org 词汇","仅限于支持 schema.org 标记的搜索引擎"],"ja":["schema.org の語彙を理解する必要がある","schema.org マークアップを認識する検索エンジンのみをサポート"],"ko":["schema.org 어휘를 이해해야 함","schema.org 마크업을 인식하는 검색 엔진만 지원"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del vocabulario de schema.org","Limitado a la compatibilidad con motores de búsqueda que reconocen el marcado de schema.org"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du vocabulaire de schema.org","Limité à la prise en charge des moteurs de recherche qui reconnaissent le balisage de schema.org"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Vokabular von schema.org","Begrenzt auf die Unterstützung von Suchmaschinen, die das schema.org-Markup erkennen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do vocabulário schema.org","Limitado a mecanismos de busca que reconhecem a marcação schema.org"],"ru":["Требует понимания словаря schema.org","Ограничен поддержкой поисковых систем, которые распознают разметку schema.org"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مصطلحات مخطط. org","محدود بالدعم لمحركات البحث التي تعترف بترميز مخطط. org"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":85}');
