сти","Интеграция с git diff","Оценка качества и безопасности"],"ar":["تحليل رمز عميق","تحديد التغييرات في الرمز","ملاحظات مفصلة وتصنيف شدة","التكامل مع git diff","تقييم الجودة والأمان"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","代码安全性","代码可维护性","代码评估","Git diff"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","コードセキュリティ","コードメンテナンス性","コード評価","Git diff"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","코드 보안","코드 유지 보수성","코드 평가","Git diff"],"es":["revisión de código","análisis de código","calidad del código","seguridad del código","automatización de pruebas","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["révision de code","analyse de code","qualité du code","sécurité du code","automatisation des tests","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung","Code-Analyse","Code-Qualität","Code-Sicherheit","Automatisierung von Tests","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["revisão de código","análise de código","qualidade de código","segurança de código","manutenibilidade de código","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["обзор кода","анализ кода","качество кода","безопасность кода","поддерживаемость кода","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مراجعة الرمز","تحليل الرمز","جودة الرمز","أمان الرمز","ضبط الرمز","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"Yeachan-Heo","repo":"oh-my-claudecode","repoPath":"Yeachan-Heo/oh-my-claudecode","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.395Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Run a comprehensive code review","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Skill\n\nConduct a thorough code review for quality, security, and maintainability with severity-rated feedback.\n\n## When to Use\n\nThis skill activates when:\n- User requests \"review this code\", \"code review\"\n- Before merging a pull request\n- After implementing a major feature\n- User wants quality assessment\n\n## What It Does\n\nDelegates to the `code-reviewer` agent (Opus model) for deep analysis:\n\n1. **Identify Changes**\n   - Run `git diff` to find changed files\n   - Determine scope of","body":"# Code Review Skill\n\nConduct a thorough code review for quality, security, and maintainability with severity-rated feedback.\n\n## When to Use\n\nThis skill activates when:\n- User requests \"review this code\", \"code review\"\n- Before merging a pull request\n- After implementing a major feature\n- User wants quality assessment\n\n## What It Does\n\nDelegates to the `code-reviewer` agent (Opus model) for deep analysis:\n\n1. **Identify Changes**\n   - Run `git diff` to find changed files\n   - Determine scope of review (specific files or entire PR)\n\n2. **Review Categories**\n   - **Security** - Hardcoded secrets, injection risks, XSS, CSRF\n   - **Code Quality** - Function size, complexity, nesting depth\n   - **Performance** - Algorithm efficiency, N+1 queries, caching\n   - **Best Practices** - Naming, documentation, error handling\n   - **Maintainability** - Duplication, coupling, testability\n\n3. **Severity Rating**\n   - **CRITICAL** - Security vulnerability (must fix before merge)\n   - **HIGH** - Bug or major code smell (should fix before merge)\n   - **MEDIUM** - Minor issue (fix when possible)\n   - **LOW** - Style/suggestion (consider fixing)\n\n4. **Specific Recommendations**\n   - File:line locations for each issue\n   - Concrete fix suggestions\n   - Code examples where applicable\n\n## Agent Delegation\n\n```\nTask(\n  subagent_type=\"oh-my-claudecode:code-reviewer\",\n  model=\"opus\",\n  prompt=\"CODE REVIEW TASK\n\nReview code changes for quality, security, and maintainability.\n\nScope: [git diff or specific files]\n\nReview Checklist:\n- Security vulnerabilities (OWASP Top 10)\n- Code quality (complexity, duplication)\n- Performance issues (N+1, inefficient algorithms)\n- Best practices (naming, documentation, error handling)\n- Maintainability (coupling, testability)\n\nOutput: Code review report with:\n- Files reviewed count\n- Issues by severity (CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW)\n- Specific file:line locations\n- Fix recommendations\n- Approval recommendation (APPROVE / REQUEST CHANGES / COMMENT)\"\n)\n```\n\n## External Model Consultation (Preferred)\n\nThe code-reviewer agent SHOULD consult Codex for cross-validation.\n\n### Protocol\n1. **Form your OWN review FIRST** - Complete the review independently\n2. **Consult for validation** - Cross-check findings with Codex\n3. **Critically evaluate** - Never blindly adopt external findings\n4. **Graceful fallback** - Never block if tools unavailable\n\n### When to Consult\n- Security-sensitive code changes\n- Complex architectural patterns\n- Unfamiliar codebases or languages\n- High-stakes production code\n\n### When to Skip\n- Simple refactoring\n- Well-understood patterns\n- Time-critical reviews\n- Small, isolated changes\n\n### Tool Usage\nBefore first MCP tool use, call `ToolSearch(\"mcp\")` to discover deferred MCP tools.\nUse `mcp__x__ask_codex` with `agent_role: \"code-reviewer\"`.\nIf ToolSearch finds no MCP tools, fall back to the `code-reviewer` Claude agent.\n\n**Note:** Codex calls can take up to 1 hour. Consider the review timeline before consulting.\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\nCODE REVIEW REPORT\n==================\n\nFiles Reviewed: 8\nTotal Issues: 15\n\nCRITICAL (0)\n-----------\n(none)\n\nHIGH (3)\n--------\n1. src/api/auth.ts:42\n   Issue: User input not sanitized before SQL query\n   Risk: SQL injection vulnerability\n   Fix: Use parameterized queries or ORM\n\n2. src/components/UserProfile.tsx:89\n   Issue: Password displayed in plain text in logs\n   Risk: Credential exposure\n   Fix: Remove password from log statements\n\n3. src/utils/validation.ts:15\n   Issue: Email regex allows invalid formats\n   Risk: Accepts malformed emails\n   Fix: Use proven email validation library\n\nMEDIUM (7)\n----------\n...\n\nLOW (5)\n-------\n...\n\nRECOMMENDATION: REQUEST CHANGES\n\nCritical security issues must be addressed before merge.\n```\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nThe code-reviewer agent checks:\n\n### Security\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens)\n- [ ] All user inputs sanitized\n- [ ] SQL/NoSQL injection prevention\n- [ ] XSS prevention (escaped outputs)\n- [ ] CSRF protection on state-changing operations\n- [ ] Authentication/authorization properly enforced\n\n### Code Quality\n- [ ] Functions < 50 lines (guideline)\n- [ ] Cyclomatic complexity < 10\n- [ ] No deeply nested code (> 4 levels)\n- [ ] No duplicate logic (DRY principle)\n- [ ] Clear, descriptive naming\n\n### Performance\n- [ ] No N+1 query patterns\n- [ ] Appropriate caching where applicable\n- [ ] Efficient algorithms (avoid O(n²) when O(n) possible)\n- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders (React/Vue)\n\n### Best Practices\n- [ ] Error handling present and appropriate\n- [ ] Logging at appropriate levels\n- [ ] Documentation for public APIs\n- [ ] Tests for critical paths\n- [ ] No commented-out code\n\n## Approval Criteria\n\n**APPROVE** - No CRITICAL or HIGH issues, minor improvements only\n**REQUEST CHANGES** - CRITICAL or HIGH issues present\n**COMMENT** - Only LOW/MEDIUM issues, no blocking concerns\n\n## Use with Other Skills\n\n**With Pipeline:**\n```\n/pipeline review \"implement user authentication\"\n```\nIncludes code review as part of implementation workflow.\n\n**With Ralph:**\n```\n/ralph code-review then fix all issues\n```\nReview code, get feedback, fix until approved.\n\n**With Ultrawork:**\n```\n/ultrawork review all files in src/\n```\nParallel code review across multiple files.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Review early** - Catch issues before they compound\n- **Review often** - Small, frequent reviews better than huge ones\n- **Address CRITICAL/HIGH first** - Fix security and bugs immediately\n- **Consider context** - Some \"issues\" may be intentional trade-offs\n- **Learn from reviews** - Use feedback to improve coding practices\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:18:51.545Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Multi-agent Orchestration Agents like Claude Code needing thorough code analysis and review for quality, security, and maintainability.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude Code 这样的多代理编排代理，需要对代码进行彻底的分析和审查，以确保质量、安全性和可维护性。","ja":"Claude Code のようなマルチエージェントオーケストレーションエージェントに最適です。これらのエージェントは、コードの品質、セキュリティ、およびメンテナンス性を確保するために、徹底的なコード分析およびレビューを必要とします。","ko":"Claude Code 같은 멀티 에이전트 오케스트레이션 에이전트에 적합합니다. 이러한 에이전트는 코드의 품질, 보안 및 유지 보수성을 보장하기 위해 철저한 코드 분석 및 리뷰를 필요로 합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Orquestación Multiagente como Claude Code que necesitan un análisis y revisión de código exhaustivos para la calidad, la seguridad y la mantenibilidad.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Orchestration Multi-agent comme Claude Code nécessitant une analyse et une revue de code approfondies pour la qualité, la sécurité et la maintenabilité.","de":"Perfekt für Multiagenten-Orchestrierungsagenten wie Claude Code, die eine gründliche Codeanalyse und -prüfung für Qualität, Sicherheit und Wartbarkeit benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Orquestração de Múltiplos Agentes, como Claude Code, que necessitam de uma análise e revisão de código aprofundadas para garantir a qualidade, segurança e manutenção.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Многоагентной Оркестрации Агентов, таких как Claude Code, требующих тщательного анализа и обзора кода для качества, безопасности и поддерживаемости.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التوجيه المتعدد مثل Claude Code الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل ومراجعة شاملة للكود لضمان الجودة والأمان والصيانة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct deep code analysis using the Opus model, providing severity-rated feedback on git diff changes for improved code quality and security, leveraging protocols like git and utilizing libraries for thorough assessment.","zh":"赋予代理进行深入的代码分析的能力，使用 Opus 模型，对 git diff 更改提供严重性评级的反馈，以提高代码质量和安全性，利用 git 等协议，并使用库进行彻底的评估。","ja":"Opus モデルを使用して、エージェントが深いコード分析を実行できるようにし、git diff の変更について重大性評価付きのフィードバックを提供して、コード品質とセキュリティを向上させることができます。git などのプロトコルを利用し、ライブラリを使用して徹底的な評価を実行します。","ko":"에이전트가 Opus 모델을 사용하여 깊은 코드 분석을 수행할 수 있도록 하여 git diff 변경에 대한 심각도 평가 피드백을 제공하고 코드 품질 및 보안을 개선합니다. git과 같은 프로토콜을 활용하고 라이브러리를 사용하여 철저한 평가를 수행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar un análisis de código profundo utilizando el modelo Opus, proporcionando retroalimentación con calificación de gravedad sobre los cambios de git diff para mejorar la calidad y la seguridad del código, aprovechando protocolos como git y utilizando bibliotecas para una evaluación exhaustiva.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser une analyse de code approfondie en utilisant le modèle Opus, fournissant une rétroaction notée sur les modifications de git diff pour améliorer la qualité et la sécurité du code, en exploitant des protocoles comme git et en utilisant des bibliothèques pour une évaluation exhaustive.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, eine tiefe Codeanalyse mit dem Opus-Modell durchzuführen und Feedback mit Schweregradbewertung zu git-Diff-Änderungen bereitzustellen, um die Codequalität und -sicherheit zu verbessern, indem Protokolle wie git genutzt und Bibliotheken für eine gründliche Bewertung verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar uma análise de código profunda usando o modelo Opus, fornecendo feedback com classificação de gravidade sobre as alterações do git diff para melhorar a qualidade e segurança do código, aproveitando protocolos como o git e utilizando bibliotecas para uma avaliação abrangente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить глубокий анализ кода с помощью модели Opus, обеспечивая обратную связь с рейтингом тяжести по изменениям git diff для улучшения качества и безопасности кода, используя протоколы, такие как git, и использует библиотеки для всесторонней оценки.","ar":"يمكن للعميل من تنفيذ تحليل متعمق للكود باستخدام نموذج Opus، وتقديم ملاحظات مصنفة حسب الحدّة حول التغييرات في git diff لتحسين جودة وأمان الكود، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل git، واستخدام المكتبات لتقييم شامل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for pull requests","Generating quality assessment reports after major feature implementations","Debugging security vulnerabilities in code changes"],"zh":["自动化代码审查以响应拉取请求","在主要功能实现后生成质量评估报告","调试代码更改中的安全漏洞"],"ja":["プルリクエストに応じてコードレビューを自動化する","主な機能実装後の品質評価レポートの生成","コード変更の中のセキュリティ脆弱性のデバッグ"],"ko":["풀 요청에 대한 코드 리뷰 자동화","주요 기능 구현 후 품질 평가 보고서 생성","코드 변경의 보안 취약성 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para solicitudes de extracción","Generación de informes de evaluación de calidad después de implementaciones de funciones principales","Depuración de vulnerabilidades de seguridad en cambios de código"],"fr":["Automation des examens de code pour les demandes d''extraction","Génération de rapports d''évaluation de la qualité après les implémentations de fonctionnalités majeures","Débogage des vulnérabilités de sécurité dans les modifications de code"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für Pull-Requests","Erstellung von Qualitätsbewertungsberichten nach der Implementierung von Hauptfunktionen","Fehlerbehebung von Sicherheitslücken in Code-Änderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para solicitações de pull","Gerar relatórios de avaliação de qualidade após implementações de recursos importantes","Depurar vulnerabilidades de segurança em alterações de código"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обзор кода для запросов на слияние","Генерировать отчеты об оценке качества после реализации основных функций","Отладить уязвимости безопасности в изменениях кода"],"ar":["تأتمتة استعراض الكود لطلبات السحب","توليد تقارير تقييم الجودة بعد تنفيذ ميزات رئيسية","تصحيح أخطاء أمنية في تغييرات الكود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to git repository","Dependent on Opus model for code analysis","Specific to code review use cases"],"zh":["需要访问 git 仓库","依赖 Opus 模型进行代码分析","特定于代码审查用例"],"ja":["git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","コード分析に Opus モデルに依存する","コードレビュー用途に特化している"],"ko":["git 리포지토리에 대한 액세스가 필요함","코드 분석에 Opus 모델에 의존함","코드 리뷰 사용 사례에 특정됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio git","Dependiente del modelo Opus para el análisis de código","Específico para casos de uso de revisión de código"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel git","Dépendant du modèle Opus pour l''analyse de code","Spécifique aux cas d''utilisation de revue de code"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Git-Repository","Abhängig vom Opus-Modell für die Codeanalyse","Spezifisch für Code-Review-Anwendungsfälle"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório git","Dependente do modelo Opus para análise de código","Específico para casos de uso de revisão de código"],"ru":["Требует доступа к репозиторию git","Зависит от модели Opus для анализа кода","Конкретно для случаев использования обзора кода"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع git","يعتمد على نموذج Opus لتحليل الكود","محدد لاستخدامات مراجعة الكود"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('htmlstreamofficial/preline/preline-theme-generator', 'community', 'htmlstreamofficial', 'preline', 'htmlstreamofficial/preline', 'preline-theme-generator', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.395Z', '2026-02-18T02:19:10.984Z', NULL, '{"id":"htmlstreamofficial/preline/preline-theme-generator","name":"preline-theme-generator","description":{"zh":"Preline 主题生成器用于创建美观、统一的 UI。它提供了一套预建的 UI 组件，基于实用性优先的 Tailwind CSS 框架。","ja":"Preline テーマジェネレーターは美しい、統一された UI を作成するために使用されます。実用性優先の Tailwind CSS フレームワークに基づく事前構築済みの UI コンポーネントのセットを提供します。","ko":"Preline 테마 생성기는 아름답고 일관된 UI를 생성하는 데 사용됩니다. 사용하기 쉬운 Tailwind CSS 프레임워크를 기반으로 한 사전 구축 UI 구성 요소 세트를 제공합니다.","pt":"O gerador de tema Preline é uma ferramenta que ajuda a criar interfaces UI consistentes com o framework Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Генератор темы Preline - это инструмент, помогающий создать единый UI с помощью фреймворка Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مُولِّد موضوع بريلين هو أداة تساعد في إنشاء واجهات مستخدم موحدة باستخدام إطار عمل Tailwind CSS.","en":"Preline UI is an open-source set of prebuilt UI components based on the utility-first Tailwind CSS framework."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Preline 主题生成器 - 自定义 UI 组件","ja":"Preline テーマジェネレーター - カスタム UI コンポーネント","ko":"Preline 테마 생성기 - 사용자 지정 UI 구성 요소","pt":"Gerador de Tema Preline - Crie Interfaces UI Consistentes","ru":"Генератор темы Preline - Создайте единый UI","ar":"مُولِّد موضوع بريلين - قم بإنشاء واجهات مستخدم موحدة","en":"preline-theme-generator"},"description":{"zh":"Preline 主题生成器用于创建美观、统一的 UI。它提供了一套预建的 UI 组件，基于实用性优先的 Tailwind CSS 框架。","ja":"Preline テーマジェネレーターは美しい、統一された UI を作成するために使用されます。実用性優先の Tailwind CSS フレームワークに基づく事前構築済みの UI コンポーネントのセットを提供します。","ko":"Preline 테마 생성기는 아름답고 일관된 UI를 생성하는 데 사용됩니다. 사용하기 쉬운 Tailwind CSS 프레임워크를 기반으로 한 사전 구축 UI 구성 요소 세트를 제공합니다.","pt":"O gerador de tema Preline é uma ferramenta que ajuda a criar interfaces UI consistentes com o framework Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Генератор темы Preline - это инструмент, помогающий создать единый UI с помощью фреймворка Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مُولِّد موضوع بريلين هو أداة تساعد في إنشاء واجهات مستخدم موحدة باستخدام إطار عمل Tailwind CSS.","en":"Preline UI is an open-source set of prebuilt UI components based on the utility-first Tailwind CSS framework."},"definition":{"en":"Preline UI is an open-source set of prebuilt UI components based on the utility-first Tailwind CSS framework."},"features":{"zh":["基于 Tailwind CSS 框架","预建 UI 组件","自定义主题生成","统一的 UI 风格","易于使用"],"ja":["Tailwind CSS フレームワークに基づく","事前構築済みの UI コンポーネント","カスタムテーマの生成","統一された UI スタイル","使いやすい"],"ko":["Tailwind CSS 프레임워크 기반","사전 구축 UI 구성 요소","사용자 지정 테마 생성","統一された UI 스타일","사용하기 쉬운"],"pt":["Geração de arquivos CSS personalizados","Compatibilidade com o framework Tailwind CSS","Criação de interfaces UI consistentes","Otimização para dispositivos móveis","Documentação detalhada"],"ru":["Генерация пользовательских файлов CSS","Совместимость с фреймворком Tailwind CSS","Создание единого UI","Оптимизация для мобильных устройств","Подробная документация"],"ar":["توليد ملفات CSS مخصصة","التوافق مع إطار عمل Tailwind CSS","إنشاء واجهات مستخدم موحدة","التحسين للجهاز المحمول","وثائق مفصلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Preline 主题生成器","自定义 UI 组件","Tailwind CSS","统一的 UI 风格","前端开发工具","UI 设计"],"ja":["Preline テーマジェネレーター","カスタム UI コンポーネント","Tailwind CSS","統一された UI スタイル","フロントエンド開発ツール","UI デザイン"],"ko":["Preline 테마 생성기","사용자 지정 UI 구성 요소","Tailwind CSS","統一された UI 스타일","프론트엔드 개발 도구","UI 디자인"],"pt":["gerador de tema preline","tailwind css","interfaces ui","desenvolvimento web","css personalizado","otimização para dispositivos móveis"],"ru":["генератор темы preline","tailwind css","единый ui","веб-разработка","пользовательский css","оптимизация для мобильных устройств"],"ar":["مُولِّد موضوع بريلين","tailwind css","واجهات مستخدم موحدة","تطوير الويب","css مخصص","التحسين للجهاز المحمول"]}},"owner":"htmlstreamofficial","repo":"preline","repoPath":"htmlstreamofficial/preline","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.395Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"preline-theme-generator","description":"Generates beautiful, consistent Preline Theme CSS files. Agent interprets user request, runs build script, delivers complete CSS.","bodyPreview":"# Preline Theme Generator\n\n> **This file is for the AGENT (LLM) only — not end users.**\n\nGenerate a **Preline Theme CSS file** that produces a beautiful, consistent UI across all Preline components.\n\n---\n\n## Docs\n\n- `docs/step-1.md` to `docs/step-7.md` (detailed workflow guidance)\n- `docs/palette-guidance.md` (mood, hue, neutral mapping, OKLCH rules)\n- `docs/validation-checklist.md`\n- `docs/token-reference.md`\n- `docs/examples.md`\n\n---\n\n## Agent workflow (FOLLOW THIS)\n\nWhen user requests a theme","body":"# Preline Theme Generator\n\n> **This file is for the AGENT (LLM) only — not end users.**\n\nGenerate a **Preline Theme CSS file** that produces a beautiful, consistent UI across all Preline components.\n\n---\n\n## Docs\n\n- `docs/step-1.md` to `docs/step-7.md` (detailed workflow guidance)\n- `docs/palette-guidance.md` (mood, hue, neutral mapping, OKLCH rules)\n- `docs/validation-checklist.md`\n- `docs/token-reference.md`\n- `docs/examples.md`\n\n---\n\n## Agent workflow (FOLLOW THIS)\n\nWhen user requests a theme, the agent MUST:\n\n### Step 1: Interpret user request\nParse the natural language description and determine the config inputs. See `docs/step-1.md` and `docs/palette-guidance.md`.\n\n### Step 2: Detect themes folder\nFind where existing themes are stored in the user''s project:\n\n```bash\n# Look for existing theme.css to find the themes folder\nfind . -name \"theme.css\" -path \"*/themes/*\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null | head -1\n```\n\nIf no themes folder found: ask user where they want the theme file saved. See `docs/step-2.md`.\n\n### Step 3: Create temp config file (AUTO-RUN, NO PROMPT)\nWrite a JSON config. This must run silently without user approval.\n\n```bash\necho ''{\"name\":\"<theme-name>\",\"hue\":<hue>,\"style\":\"<style>\",\"useCustomDarkGray\":<true|false>,\"tailwindGray\":\"<gray>\"}'' > /tmp/preline-theme-config.json\n```\n\n### Step 4: Run the generator + cleanup (AUTO-RUN, NO PROMPT)\nRun generator and immediately delete temp file in a single command chain. This must run silently without user approval.\n\nOption A (preferred) - use npx if preline is installed:\n\n```bash\nnpx preline-theme-generator /tmp/preline-theme-config.json <themes-folder>/<theme-name>.css && rm /tmp/preline-theme-config.json\n```\n\nOption B - find and run the script directly:\n\n```bash\nnode $(find . -path \"*/preline/skills/theme-generator/scripts/generate-theme.js\" 2>/dev/null | head -1) /tmp/preline-theme-config.json <themes-folder>/<theme-name>.css && rm /tmp/preline-theme-config.json\n```\n\nOption C - if script location is known (e.g., in node_modules):\n\n```bash\nnode node_modules/preline/skills/theme-generator/scripts/generate-theme.js /tmp/preline-theme-config.json <themes-folder>/<theme-name>.css && rm /tmp/preline-theme-config.json\n```\n\n### Step 5: Confirm to user\nTell user the theme was created and show enable snippet:\n\n```css\n/* In your main CSS file */\n@import \"./themes/<theme-name>.css\";\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- On HTML element -->\n<html data-theme=\"theme-<theme-name>\">\n```\n\nSee `docs/step-5.md` and `docs/examples.md` for response examples.\n\n---\n\n## Generated themes include\n- Coherent light + dark modes\n- Safe to ship (valid CSS, correct selectors)\n- No HTML class changes required (only `data-theme` + optional `.dark`)\n- Custom color palettes in `@theme theme-<name> inline { }` block\n\n---\n\n## Example prompts\n\nSimple:\n> \"Create a sunset theme\"\n\nDescriptive:\n> \"Create a theme that feels like a cozy coffee shop — warm browns, cream backgrounds, inviting and calm\"\n\nSpecific:\n> \"Generate a cyberpunk theme with neon cyan accents on dark surfaces\"\n\nBrand-focused:\n> \"Create a theme matching this brand color #2F6BFF — professional, high-clarity SaaS feel\"\n\n---\n\n## RULES (ALL MUST BE FOLLOWED)\n\n### Rule 1 — Do not modify the shipped base theme\n- Never change `theme.css`. Always generate a separate theme file.\n\n### Rule 2 — Theme file MUST include imports in this exact order\nEvery generated theme file MUST begin with:\n\n```css\n@import \"./theme.css\";\n```\n\n### Rule 3 — Theme scoping block placement\nEvery theme file MUST include a scoping block after imports:\n\n```css\n@theme theme-<name> inline {\n  /* Theme scoping - custom palettes only */\n}\n```\n\n**What goes INSIDE this block:**\n- Custom color palettes (soft grays, brand colors) — these create Tailwind utilities\n- Example: `--color-<name>-50: oklch(98% 0.003 <hue>);` through `--color-<name>-950`\n\n**What goes OUTSIDE (in selector blocks):**\n- All semantic token overrides (`--background`, `--primary`, `--navbar-*`, etc.)\n- Tailwind core mappings are owned by the shipped base theme only\n\nSee `docs/palette-guidance.md` for palette construction details and examples.\n\n### Rule 4 — No HTML utility class edits required\n- Theme must NOT require users to change Tailwind utility classes in HTML.\n- Theme activation must work using ONLY:\n  - CSS imports\n  - `data-theme=\"theme-<name>\"`\n- Dark mode may use `.dark` if the project uses it; do not introduce new conventions.\n\n### Rule 5 — Use exact, required theme selectors\nLight mode token overrides MUST be under:\n\n```css\n:root[data-theme=\"theme-<name>\"],\n[data-theme=\"theme-<name>\"] { ... }\n```\n\nDark mode overrides MUST be theme-scoped and use:\n\n```css\n[data-theme=\"theme-<name>\"].dark { ... }\n```\n\n### Rule 6 — Full-theme mode: comprehensive token coverage is REQUIRED\nBecause this generator is full-theme mode, output MUST define a comprehensive set of token values so the theme looks complete and intentional.\n\nAt minimum, the theme MUST define:\n\n#### 6.1 Global surfaces + text\n- `--background`\n- `--background-1`\n- `--background-2`\n- `--background-plain`\n- `--foreground`\n- `--foreground-inverse`\n- `--inverse`\n\n#### 6.2 Borders (full scale)\n- `--border`\n- `--border-line-inverse`\n- `--border-line-1` through `--border-line-8` (coherent scale)\n\n#### 6.3 Primary ramp (full) + primary states\n- `--primary-50` through `--primary-950`\n- `--primary`\n- `--primary-hover`\n- `--primary-focus`\n- `--primary-active`\n- `--primary-checked`\n- `--primary-foreground` (must be readable)\n\n#### 6.4 Secondary / muted / destructive (at least)\n- `--secondary`\n- `--muted`\n- `--destructive`\n- Include related state/variant tokens if they exist in the base naming system.\n\n#### 6.5 Core component groups for a complete theme feel (prefer explicit values)\nProvide explicit values for major component groups so the theme feels cohesive:\n- `--navbar-*`\n- `--sidebar-*`\n- `--card-*`\n- `--dropdown-*`\n- `--select-*`\n- `--overlay-*`\n- `--popover-*`\n- `--tooltip-*`\n- Optionally: `--scrollbar-*`\n- Charts/maps tokens ONLY if included safely (see Rule 10)\n\n**Full-theme output MUST NOT:**\n- put token definitions inside the `@theme` block\n- invent new mappings that force HTML class edits\n\n### Rule 7 — Token naming must match Preline''s token system\n- Do not invent random token names for Preline components.\n- Only introduce new custom tokens if explicitly requested, and keep them isolated and documented in comments.\n\n### Rule 8 — Theme-scoped behavior overrides ONLY\nIf the theme changes behavior (e.g. retro-sharp radii), it MUST be scoped to the theme only.\n\n**Allowed:**\n- Override radius tokens under the theme selector\n- Add `@layer utilities` rules scoped to the theme selector\n\n**Not allowed:**\n- Global `.rounded { ... }` overrides without theme scoping\n- Any behavior overrides that affect non-theme pages\n\n### Rule 9 — Typography tokens are allowed, but font loading is separate by default\nIf fonts are requested, you MAY set:\n- `--font-sans` and/or `--font-serif` and/or `--font-mono`\n\ninside the theme selector.\n\nDo NOT add Google Fonts `@import url(...)` into the theme file unless the user explicitly requests it.\n(Font loading typically belongs in the main CSS entry file.)\n\n### Rule 10 — Charts/maps compatibility rules\nIf adjusting chart/map tokens:\n- Prefer safe formats where required by libraries.\n- Keep any `*-hex` tokens as valid hex values if the ecosystem expects hex.\n- Do not force `oklch(...)` where it may break gradients or third-party rendering.\n\n### Rule 11 — Valid CSS is mandatory\n- No missing braces\n- No invalid selectors\n- No broken comments\n- No duplicate conflicting selectors\n\n### Rule 12 — Output discipline\n- First code block must contain ONLY the generated theme CSS.\n- Optional second code block may contain ONLY the enable snippet.\n- No additional commentary unless explicitly requested.\n\n---\n\n## Required file structure (MUST follow order)\n\n1. **Imports** (`@import \"./theme.css\"`)\n2. **Theme scoping block** (`@theme theme-<name> inline { }`) — contains custom color palettes only\n3. **Light mode theme selector block** (full semantic token set using `var()` references)\n4. **Dark mode theme selector block** (override only what differs, use `var()` for consistency)\n5. **Optional theme-scoped `@layer utilities` overrides** (only if requested)\n\n---\n\n## Additional guidance\n\n- Theme construction details: `docs/step-6.md` and `docs/step-7.md`\n- Palette guidance: `docs/palette-guidance.md`\n- Validation checklist: `docs/validation-checklist.md`\n- Token reference: `docs/token-reference.md`"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:19:10.984Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI-focused Agents needing advanced CSS theme generation capabilities based on Tailwind CSS framework.","zh":"非常适合需要高级CSS主题生成能力的UI焦点代理，基于Tailwind CSS框架。","ja":"Tailwind CSSフレームワークに基づいて高度なCSSテーマ生成機能を必要とするUI中心のエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Tailwind CSS 프레임워크를 기반으로 고급 CSS 테마 생성 기능을 필요로 하는 UI 중심 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes enfocados en la interfaz de usuario que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de generación de temas CSS basados en el marco de Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur l''interface utilisateur nécessitant des capacités de génération de thèmes CSS avancées basées sur le framework Tailwind CSS.","de":"Perfekt für benutzeroberflächenorientierte Agenten, die erweiterte CSS-Theme-Generierungsfunktionen auf Basis des Tailwind-CSS-Frameworks benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em UI que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de geração de temas CSS com base no framework Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на UI, которым необходимы расширенные возможности генерации тем CSS на основе фреймворка Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لإنشاء مواضيع CSS باستخدام إطار Tailwind CSS."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate consistent UI themes across Preline components using utility-first CSS, OKLCH color rules, and mood-based palettes, producing beautiful Preline Theme CSS files.","zh":"赋予代理生成跨Preline组件的一致UI主题的能力，使用utility-first CSS、OKLCH颜色规则和基于情绪的调色板，生成漂亮的Preline主题CSS文件。","ja":"Utility-first CSS、OKLCHカラー規則、ムードベースのパレットを使用して、Prelineコンポーネント全体に一貫したUIテーマを生成するエージェントの能力を付与し、美しいPrelineテーマCSSファイルを生成します。","ko":"유틸리티 퍼스트 CSS, OKLCH 색상 규칙 및 감정 기반 팔레트를 사용하여 Preline 컴포�트 전반에 일관된 UI 테마를 생성하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하여 아름다운 Preline 테마 CSS 파일을 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar temas de interfaz de usuario coherentes en todos los componentes de Preline utilizando CSS de utilidad, reglas de color OKLCH y paletas basadas en el estado de ánimo, lo que produce hermosos archivos de tema CSS de Preline.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des thèmes d''interface utilisateur cohérents à travers les composants Preline en utilisant le CSS utility-first, les règles de couleur OKLCH et les palettes basées sur l''humeur, produisant ainsi de beaux fichiers de thème CSS Preline.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, konsistente Benutzeroberflächenthemen über alle Preline-Komponenten hinweg zu generieren, indem sie utility-first-CSS, OKLCH-Farbrechen und stimmungsorientierte Paletten verwenden, was zu schönen Preline-Theme-CSS-Dateien führt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar temas de UI consistentes em componentes Preline usando CSS de utilidade primeiro, regras de cor OKLCH e paletas baseadas em humor, produzindo arquivos CSS de tema Preline bonitos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать последовательные темы UI в компонентах Preline, используя утилитарный CSS, правила цвета OKLCH и палитры на основе настроения, производя красивые файлы CSS-темы Preline.","ar":"يمنح العميل القدرة على إنشاء مواضيع واجهة المستخدم المتسقة عبر مكونات Preline باستخدام CSS الأولي للوظيفة وقواعد الألوان OKLCH والصندوق اللوني القائم على المزاج، مما ينتج عنه ملفات CSS جميلة لموضوع Preline."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating Preline Theme CSS files for consistent UI","Creating customized UI components based on Tailwind CSS","Validating theme consistency across multiple Preline components"],"zh":["生成一致的UI的Preline主题CSS文件","基于Tailwind CSS创建自定义UI组件","验证多个Preline组件的主题一致性"],"ja":["一貫したUIを持つPrelineテーマCSSファイルを生成する","Tailwind CSSに基づいてカスタマイズされたUIコンポーネントを作成する","複数のPrelineコンポーネントのテーマの一貫性を検証する"],"ko":["일관된 UI를 가진 Preline 테마 CSS 파일을 생성한다","Tailwind CSS를 기반으로 사용자 정의 UI 컴포�트를 생성한다","여러 개의 Preline 컴포�트의 테마 일관성을 검증한다"],"es":["Generación de archivos de tema CSS de Preline para una interfaz de usuario coherente","Creación de componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizados en función de Tailwind CSS","Validación de la coherencia del tema en varios componentes de Preline"],"fr":["Génération de fichiers de thème CSS Preline pour une interface utilisateur cohérente","Création de composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisés basés sur Tailwind CSS","Validation de la cohérence du thème sur plusieurs composants Preline"],"de":["Generierung von Preline-Theme-CSS-Dateien für eine konsistente Benutzeroberfläche","Erstellung von benutzeroberflächenorientierten Komponenten auf Basis von Tailwind CSS","Überprüfung der Themenkonsistenz über mehrere Preline-Komponenten hinweg"],"pt":["Gerar arquivos CSS de tema Preline para UI consistente","Criar componentes de UI personalizados com base no Tailwind CSS","Validar a consistência do tema em vários componentes Preline"],"ru":["Генерировать файлы CSS-темы Preline для последовательного UI","Создавать настраиваемые компоненты UI на основе Tailwind CSS","Проверять последовательность темы в нескольких компонентах Preline"],"ar":["إنشاء ملفات CSS لموضوع Preline من أجل واجهة المستخدم الثابتة","إنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم المخصصة باستخدام Tailwind CSS","التحقق من استمرارية الموضوع عبر مكونات Preline المتعددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Tailwind CSS and utility-first framework","Limited to generating themes for Preline UI components","Needs documentation guidance from docs/step-1.md to docs/step-7.md for workflow"],"zh":["需要了解Tailwind CSS和utility-first框架","仅限于生成Preline UI组件的主题","需要从docs/step-1.md到docs/step-7.md的文档指导来进行工作流"],"ja":["Tailwind CSSとUtility-firstフレームワークの理解が必要","Preline UIコンポーネントのテーマの生成のみに限定","ワークフローを実行するために、docs/step-1.mdからdocs/step-7.mdまでのドキュメントのガイダンスが必要"],"ko":["Tailwind CSS 및 유틸리티 퍼스트 프레임워크에 대한 이해가 필요","Preline UI 컴포넌트의 테마 생성에만 제한","작업 흐름을 수행하기 위해 docs/step-1.md부터 docs/step-7.md까지의 문서 안내가 필요"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de Tailwind CSS y del marco de utilidad","Limitado a la generación de temas para componentes de interfaz de usuario de Preline","Necesita orientación documental de docs/step-1.md a docs/step-7.md para el flujo de trabajo"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de Tailwind CSS et du framework utility-first","Limité à la génération de thèmes pour les composants d''interface utilisateur Preline","Nécessite une orientation documentaire de docs/step-1.md à docs/step-7.md pour le workflow"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis von Tailwind CSS und dem utility-first-Framework","Begrenzt auf die Generierung von Themen für Preline-Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten","Benötigt Dokumentationsanleitung von docs/step-1.md bis docs/step-7.md für den Arbeitsablauf"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do Tailwind CSS e do framework de utilidade primeiro","Limitado à geração de temas para componentes de UI Preline","Necessita de orientação de documentação de docs/step-1.md a docs/step-7.md para o fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Требует понимания Tailwind CSS и утилитарного фреймворка","Ограничен генерацией тем для компонентов UI Preline","Требует руководства по документации из docs/step-1.md до docs/step-7.md для рабочего процесса"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لإطار Tailwind CSS وأولويات الوظيفة","محدود بإنشاء مواضيع لمكونات واجهة المستخدم في Preline","يحتاج إلى إرشادات وثائق من docs/step-1.md إلى docs/step-7.md من أجل سير العمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
