EF Core para Desenvolvedores .NET","ru":"Шаблоны EF Core для разработчиков .NET","ar":"نماذج EF Core для مطورين .NET","en":"efcore-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Entity Framework Core 模式提供了一系列的最佳实践和方法，帮助 .NET 开发者提高开发效率和性能","ja":"Entity Framework Core パターンは、.NET 開発者が開発効率とパフォーマンスを向上させるためのベストプラクティスと方法を提供する","ko":"Entity Framework Core 패턴은 .NET 개발자가 개발 효율성과 성능을 향상시키는 데 도움이 되는 모범 사례와 방법을 제공한다","es":"Entity Framework Core es un conjunto de patrones para desarrolladores .NET que buscan optimizar el rendimiento y gestionar migraciones de bases de datos de m...","fr":"Entity Framework Core est un ensemble de modèles pour les développeurs .NET qui cherchent à optimiser les performances et à gérer les migrations de bases de ...","de":"Entity Framework Core ist eine Sammlung von Mustern für .NET-Entwickler, die das Leistungsverhalten optimieren und Datenbankmigrationen effektiv verwalten mö...","pt":"EF Core é uma biblioteca de acesso a dados para .NET, e este skill fornece padrões para melhorar o desempenho e gerenciar migrações de banco de dados.","ru":"EF Core - это библиотека доступа к данным для .NET, а этот скилл предоставляет шаблоны для улучшения производительности и управления миграциями базы данных.","ar":"EF Core هي مكتبة الوصول إلى البيانات ل .NET، وهذا المهارة يوفر أنماطا لتحسين الأداء وإدارة هجرات قاعدة البيانات.","en":"Claude Code skills and sub-agents for .NET Developers"},"definition":{"en":"Claude Code skills and sub-agents for .NET Developers"},"features":{"zh":["设置 EF Core 项目","优化查询性能","管理数据库迁移","集成 EF Core 与 .NET","调试变更跟踪问题","高效加载导航集合"],"ja":["EF Core プロジェクトの設定","クエリパフォーマンスの最適化","データベース移行の管理","EF Core と .NET の統合","変更追跡の問題のデバッグ","ナビゲーションコレクションの効率的な読み込み"],"ko":["EF Core 프로젝트 설정","쿼리 성능 최적화","데이터베이스 마이그레이션 관리","EF Core 와 .NET 통합","변경 추적 문제 디버깅","네비게이션 컬렉션 효율적인 로딩"],"es":["Optimización del rendimiento de consultas","Gestión de migraciones de bases de datos","Integración con .NET Aspire","Depuración de problemas de seguimiento de cambios","Carga eficiente de colecciones de navegación múltiples"],"fr":["Optimisation des performances des requêtes","Gestion des migrations de bases de données","Intégration avec .NET Aspire","Débogage des problèmes de suivi des modifications","Chargement efficace de collections de navigation multiples"],"de":["Optimierung der Abfrageleistung","Verwaltung von Datenbankmigrationen","Integration mit .NET Aspire","Fehlerbehebung bei Änderungsnachverfolgungsproblemen","Effizientes Laden von mehreren Navigationskollektionen"],"pt":["Otimização de desempenho de consultas","Gerenciamento de migrações de banco de dados","Integração com .NET Aspire","Depuração de problemas de rastreamento de alterações","Carregamento eficiente de coleções de navegação múltiplas"],"ru":["Оптимизация производительности запросов","Управление миграциями базы данных","Интеграция с .NET Aspire","Отладка проблем отслеживания изменений","Эффективная загрузка множественных навигационных коллекций"],"ar":["تحسين أداء الاستعلامات","إدارة هجرات قاعدة البيانات","التكامل مع .NET Aspire","تصحيح أخطاء تتبع التغييرات","تحميل كفء لمجموعات الملاحة المتعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Entity Framework Core",".NET 开发","EF Core 模式","数据库迁移","查询性能","变更跟踪","导航集合","数据库设计"],"ja":["Entity Framework Core",".NET 開発","EF Core パターン","データベース移行","クエリパフォーマンス","変更追跡","ナビゲーションコレクション","データベース設計"],"ko":["Entity Framework Core",".NET 개발","EF Core 패턴","데이터베이스 마이그레이션","쿼리 성능","변경 추적","네비게이션 컬렉션","데이터베이스 설계"],"es":["Entity Framework Core","patrones de diseño","optimización de rendimiento","migraciones de bases de datos","desarrollo de aplicaciones .NET","consultas eficientes","seguimiento de cambios"],"fr":["Entity Framework Core","modèles de conception","optimisation des performances","migrations de bases de données","développement d''applications .NET","requêtes efficaces","suivi des modifications"],"de":["Entity Framework Core","Entwurfsmuster","Leistungsoptimierung","Datenbankmigrationen","Entwicklung von .NET-Anwendungen","effiziente Abfragen","Änderungsnachverfolgung"],"pt":["EF Core","Desenvolvimento .NET","Acesso a dados","Otimização de desempenho","Migrações de banco de dados","Integração com .NET Aspire"],"ru":["EF Core","Разработка .NET","Доступ к данным","Оптимизация производительности","Миграции базы данных","Интеграция с .NET Aspire"],"ar":["EF Core","التطوير .NET","الوصول إلى البيانات","تحسين الأداء","هجرات قاعدة البيانات","التكامل مع .NET Aspire"]}},"owner":"Aaronontheweb","repo":"dotnet-skills","repoPath":"Aaronontheweb/dotnet-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"efcore-patterns","description":"Entity Framework Core best practices including NoTracking by default, query splitting for navigation collections, migration management, dedicated migration services, and common pitfalls to avoid.","bodyPreview":"# Entity Framework Core Patterns\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Setting up EF Core in a new project\n- Optimizing query performance\n- Managing database migrations\n- Integrating EF Core with .NET Aspire\n- Debugging change tracking issues\n- Loading multiple navigation collections efficiently (query splitting)\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **NoTracking by Default** - Most queries are read-only; opt-in to tracking\n2. **Never Edit Migrations Manually** - Always use CLI commands\n3. **Dedi","body":"# Entity Framework Core Patterns\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Setting up EF Core in a new project\n- Optimizing query performance\n- Managing database migrations\n- Integrating EF Core with .NET Aspire\n- Debugging change tracking issues\n- Loading multiple navigation collections efficiently (query splitting)\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **NoTracking by Default** - Most queries are read-only; opt-in to tracking\n2. **Never Edit Migrations Manually** - Always use CLI commands\n3. **Dedicated Migration Service** - Separate migration execution from application startup\n4. **ExecutionStrategy for Retries** - Handle transient database failures\n5. **Explicit Updates** - When NoTracking, explicitly mark entities for update\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 1: NoTracking by Default\n\nConfigure your DbContext to disable change tracking by default. This improves performance for read-heavy workloads.\n\n```csharp\npublic class ApplicationDbContext : DbContext\n{\n    public ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options)\n        : base(options)\n    {\n        // Disable change tracking by default for better performance on read-only queries\n        // Use .AsTracking() explicitly for queries that need to track changes\n        ChangeTracker.QueryTrackingBehavior = QueryTrackingBehavior.NoTracking;\n    }\n\n    public DbSet<Order> Orders => Set<Order>();\n    public DbSet<Customer> Customers => Set<Customer>();\n}\n```\n\n### When NoTracking is Active\n\n**Read-only queries work normally:**\n```csharp\n// ✅ Fast read - no tracking overhead\nvar orders = await dbContext.Orders\n    .Where(o => o.Status == OrderStatus.Pending)\n    .ToListAsync();\n```\n\n**Writes require explicit handling:**\n```csharp\n// ❌ WRONG - Entity not tracked, SaveChanges does nothing\nvar order = await dbContext.Orders.FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == orderId);\norder.Status = OrderStatus.Shipped;\nawait dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(); // Nothing happens!\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Explicitly mark entity for update\nvar order = await dbContext.Orders.FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == orderId);\norder.Status = OrderStatus.Shipped;\ndbContext.Orders.Update(order); // Marks entire entity as modified\nawait dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();\n\n// ✅ ALSO CORRECT - Use AsTracking() for the query\nvar order = await dbContext.Orders\n    .AsTracking()\n    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == orderId);\norder.Status = OrderStatus.Shipped;\nawait dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(); // Works!\n```\n\n### When to Use Tracking\n\n| Scenario | Use Tracking? | Why |\n|----------|---------------|-----|\n| Display data in UI | No | Read-only, no updates |\n| API GET endpoints | No | Returning data, no mutations |\n| Update single entity | Yes or explicit Update() | Need to save changes |\n| Complex update with navigation | Yes | Tracking handles relationships |\n| Batch operations | No + ExecuteUpdate | More efficient |\n\n### Explicit Add/Update Pattern\n\n```csharp\npublic class OrderService\n{\n    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;\n\n    // CREATE - Always use Add (works regardless of tracking)\n    public async Task<Order> CreateOrderAsync(Order order)\n    {\n        _db.Orders.Add(order);\n        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();\n        return order;\n    }\n\n    // UPDATE - Explicitly mark as modified\n    public async Task UpdateOrderStatusAsync(Guid orderId, OrderStatus newStatus)\n    {\n        var order = await _db.Orders.FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == orderId)\n            ?? throw new NotFoundException($\"Order {orderId} not found\");\n\n        order.Status = newStatus;\n        order.UpdatedAt = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;\n\n        // Explicitly mark as modified since DbContext uses NoTracking by default\n        _db.Orders.Update(order);\n        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();\n    }\n\n    // DELETE - Attach and remove\n    public async Task DeleteOrderAsync(Guid orderId)\n    {\n        var order = new Order { Id = orderId };\n        _db.Orders.Remove(order);\n        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 2: Never Edit Migrations Manually\n\n**CRITICAL:** Always use EF Core CLI commands to manage migrations. Never:\n- Manually edit migration files (except for custom SQL in `Up()`/`Down()`)\n- Delete migration files directly\n- Rename migration files\n- Copy migrations between projects\n\n### Creating Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Create a new migration\ndotnet ef migrations add AddCustomerTable \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n\n# With a specific DbContext (if you have multiple)\ndotnet ef migrations add AddCustomerTable \\\n    --context ApplicationDbContext \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n```\n\n### Removing Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Remove the last migration (if not yet applied)\ndotnet ef migrations remove \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n\n# NEVER do this:\n# rm Migrations/20240101_AddCustomerTable.cs  # ❌ BAD!\n```\n\n### Applying Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Apply all pending migrations\ndotnet ef database update \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n\n# Apply to a specific migration\ndotnet ef database update AddCustomerTable \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n\n# Rollback to a previous migration\ndotnet ef database update PreviousMigrationName \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n```\n\n### Generating SQL Scripts\n\n```bash\n# Generate SQL script for all migrations\ndotnet ef migrations script \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api \\\n    --output migrations.sql\n\n# Generate idempotent script (safe to run multiple times)\ndotnet ef migrations script \\\n    --idempotent \\\n    --project src/MyApp.Infrastructure \\\n    --startup-project src/MyApp.Api\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 3: Dedicated Migration Service with Aspire\n\nSeparate migration execution from your main application using a dedicated migration service. This ensures:\n- Migrations complete before the app starts\n- Clean separation of concerns\n- Controlled seeding in test environments\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── MyApp.AppHost/           # Aspire orchestration\n├── MyApp.Api/               # Main application\n├── MyApp.Infrastructure/    # DbContext and migrations\n└── MyApp.MigrationService/  # Dedicated migration runner\n```\n\n### MigrationService Program.cs\n\n```csharp\nusing MyApp.Infrastructure.Data;\nusing MyApp.MigrationService;\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\n\nvar builder = Host.CreateApplicationBuilder(args);\n\n// Add Aspire service defaults\nbuilder.AddServiceDefaults();\n\n// Add PostgreSQL DbContext\nvar connectionString = builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\"appdb\")\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Connection string ''appdb'' not found.\");\n\nbuilder.Services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>\n    options.UseNpgsql(connectionString, npgsqlOptions =>\n        npgsqlOptions.MigrationsAssembly(\"MyApp.Infrastructure\")));\n\n// Add the migration worker\nbuilder.Services.AddHostedService<MigrationWorker>();\n\nvar host = builder.Build();\nhost.Run();\n```\n\n### MigrationWorker.cs\n\n```csharp\npublic class MigrationWorker : BackgroundService\n{\n    private readonly IServiceProvider _serviceProvider;\n    private readonly IHostApplicationLifetime _hostApplicationLifetime;\n    private readonly ILogger<MigrationWorker> _logger;\n\n    public MigrationWorker(\n        IServiceProvider serviceProvider,\n        IHostApplicationLifetime hostApplicationLifetime,\n        ILogger<MigrationWorker> logger)\n    {\n        _serviceProvider = serviceProvider;\n        _hostApplicationLifetime = hostApplicationLifetime;\n        _logger = logger;\n    }\n\n    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)\n    {\n        _logger.LogInformation(\"Migration service starting...\");\n\n        try\n        {\n            using var scope = _serviceProvider.CreateScope();\n            var dbContext = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();\n\n            await RunMigrationsAsync(dbContext, stoppingToken);\n\n            _logger.LogInformation(\"Migration service completed successfully.\");\n        }\n        catch (Exception ex)\n        {\n            _logger.LogError(ex, \"Migration service failed: {Error}\", ex.Message);\n            throw;\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            // Stop the application after migrations complete\n            _hostApplicationLifetime.StopApplication();\n        }\n    }\n\n    private async Task RunMigrationsAsync(ApplicationDbContext dbContext, CancellationToken ct)\n    {\n        // Use execution strategy for transient failure handling\n        var strategy = dbContext.Database.CreateExecutionStrategy();\n\n        await strategy.ExecuteAsync(async () =>\n        {\n            var pendingMigrations = await dbContext.Database.GetPendingMigrationsAsync(ct);\n\n            if (pendingMigrations.Any())\n            {\n                _logger.LogInformation(\"Applying {Count} pending migrations...\",\n                    pendingMigrations.Count());\n\n                await dbContext.Database.MigrateAsync(ct);\n\n                _logger.LogInformation(\"Migrations applied successfully.\");\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                _logger.LogInformation(\"No pending migrations. Database is up to date.\");\n            }\n        });\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### AppHost Configuration\n\n```csharp\nvar builder = DistributedApplication.CreateBuilder(args);\n\nvar postgres = builder.AddPostgres(\"postgres\");\nvar db = postgres.AddDatabase(\"appdb\");\n\n// Migrations run first, then exit\nvar migrations = builder.AddProject<Projects.MyApp_MigrationService>(\"migrations\")\n    .WaitFor(db)\n    .WithReference(db);\n\n// API waits for migrations to complete\nvar api = builder.AddProject<Projects.MyApp_Api>(\"api\")\n    .WaitForCompletion(migrations)  // Key: waits for migrations to finish\n    .WithReference(db);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 4: ExecutionStrategy for Transient Failures\n\nAlways use `CreateExecutionStrategy()` for operations that might fail transiently:\n\n```csharp\npublic async Task UpdateWithRetryAsync(Guid id, Action<Order> update)\n{\n    var strategy = _dbContext.Database.CreateExecutionStrategy();\n\n    await strategy.ExecuteAsync(async () =>\n    {\n        var order = await _dbContext.Orders\n            .AsTracking()\n            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == id);\n\n        if (order is null) return;\n\n        update(order);\n        await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();\n    });\n}\n```\n\n**Important:** You cannot use `CreateExecutionStrategy()` with user-initiated transactions. If you need transactions with retry:\n\n```csharp\nvar strategy = _dbContext.Database.CreateExecutionStrategy();\n\nawait strategy.ExecuteAsync(async () =>\n{\n    // Transaction must be INSIDE the strategy callback\n    await using var transaction = await _dbContext.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();\n\n    try\n    {\n        // ... your operations ...\n        await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();\n        await transaction.CommitAsync();\n    }\n    catch\n    {\n        await transaction.RollbackAsync();\n        throw;\n    }\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 5: Bulk Operations with ExecuteUpdate/ExecuteDelete\n\nFor bulk operations, use EF Core 7+ `ExecuteUpdateAsync` and `ExecuteDeleteAsync` instead of loading entities:\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ SLOW - Loads all entities into memory\nvar expiredOrders = await _db.Orders\n    .Where(o => o.ExpiresAt < DateTimeOffset.UtcNow)\n    .ToListAsync();\n\nforeach (var order in expiredOrders)\n{\n    order.Status = OrderStatus.Expired;\n}\nawait _db.SaveChangesAsync();\n\n// ✅ FAST - Single SQL UPDATE statement\nawait _db.Orders\n    .Where(o => o.ExpiresAt < DateTimeOffset.UtcNow)\n    .ExecuteUpdateAsync(setters => setters\n        .SetProperty(o => o.Status, OrderStatus.Expired)\n        .SetProperty(o => o.UpdatedAt, DateTimeOffset.UtcNow));\n\n// ✅ FAST - Single SQL DELETE statement\nawait _db.Orders\n    .Where(o => o.Status == OrderStatus.Cancelled && o.CreatedAt < cutoffDate)\n    .ExecuteDeleteAsync();\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### 1. Forgetting to Update When NoTracking\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ Silent failure - entity not tracked\nvar customer = await _db.Customers.FindAsync(id);\ncustomer.Name = \"New Name\";\nawait _db.SaveChangesAsync(); // Does nothing!\n\n// ✅ Explicit update\nvar customer = await _db.Customers.FindAsync(id);\ncustomer.Name = \"New Name\";\n_db.Customers.Update(customer);\nawait _db.SaveChangesAsync();\n```\n\n### 2. N+1 Query Problem\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ N+1 queries - one query per order\nvar customers = await _db.Customers.ToListAsync();\nforeach (var customer in customers)\n{\n    var orders = customer.Orders; // Lazy load triggers query\n}\n\n// ✅ Eager loading - single query\nvar customers = await _db.Customers\n    .Include(c => c.Orders)\n    .ToListAsync();\n```\n\n### 3. Tracking Conflicts with Multiple DbContext Instances\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ Tracking conflict - entity tracked by different context\nvar order1 = await _db1.Orders.AsTracking().FindAsync(id);\nvar order2 = await _db2.Orders.AsTracking().FindAsync(id);\norder2.Status = OrderStatus.Shipped;\nawait _db2.SaveChangesAsync(); // May throw or behave unexpectedly\n\n// ✅ Use single context or detach first\n_db1.Entry(order1).State = EntityState.Detached;\n```\n\n### 4. Not Using Async Consistently\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ Blocking call in async context\nvar orders = _db.Orders.ToList(); // Blocks thread\n\n// ✅ Async all the way\nvar orders = await _db.Orders.ToListAsync();\n```\n\n### 5. Querying Inside Loops\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ Query per iteration\nforeach (var orderId in orderIds)\n{\n    var order = await _db.Orders.FindAsync(orderId);\n    // process order\n}\n\n// ✅ Single query\nvar orders = await _db.Orders\n    .Where(o => orderIds.Contains(o.Id))\n    .ToListAsync();\n```\n\n---\n\n## DbContext Lifetime in DI\n\n### ASP.NET Core (Scoped by Default)\n\n```csharp\n// Scoped = one instance per HTTP request\nbuilder.Services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>\n    options.UseNpgsql(connectionString));\n```\n\n### Background Services (Create Scope)\n\n```csharp\npublic class MyBackgroundService : BackgroundService\n{\n    private readonly IServiceProvider _serviceProvider;\n\n    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)\n    {\n        // ✅ Create scope for each unit of work\n        using var scope = _serviceProvider.CreateScope();\n        var dbContext = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();\n\n        // ... use dbContext ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Actors / Long-Lived Objects (Factory Pattern)\n\n```csharp\npublic class OrderActor : ReceiveActor\n{\n    private readonly IDbContextFactory<ApplicationDbContext> _dbFactory;\n\n    public OrderActor(IDbContextFactory<ApplicationDbContext> dbFactory)\n    {\n        _dbFactory = dbFactory;\n\n        ReceiveAsync<GetOrder>(async msg =>\n        {\n            // Create fresh context for each operation\n            await using var db = await _dbFactory.CreateDbContextAsync();\n            var order = await db.Orders.FindAsync(msg.OrderId);\n            Sender.Tell(order);\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n// Registration\nbuilder.Services.AddDbContextFactory<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>\n    options.UseNpgsql(connectionString));\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 6: Query Splitting to Prevent Cartesian Explosion\n\nWhen you load multiple navigation collections via `Include()`, EF Core generates a single query that can cause cartesian explosion. If you have 10 orders with 10 items each, you get 100 rows instead of 10 + 10.\n\n### Global Configuration (Recommended for Most Cases)\n\nEnable query splitting globally in your DbContext configuration:\n\n```csharp\nservices.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>\n    options.UseNpgsql(connectionString, npgsqlOptions =>\n        {\n            npgsqlOptions.UseQuerySplittingBehavior(QuerySplittingBehavior.SplitQuery);\n        }));\n```\n\n### Per-Query Override\n\nUse single query when you know it''s more efficient:\n\n```csharp\n// Use single query when you know the structure is well-understood\nvar orders = await dbContext.Orders\n    .Include(o => o.Items)\n    .Include(o => o.Payments)\n    .AsSingleQuery()  // Override global split behavior\n    .ToListAsync();\n```\n\n### Trade-offs\n\n| Behavior | Pros | Cons |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| SplitQuery | No cartesian explosion, better for large collections | Multiple round-trips, potential consistency issues |\n| SingleQuery | Single round-trip, transactional consistency | Cartesian explosion with multiple collections |\n\n**Recommendation**: Default to `SplitQuery` globally, override with `AsSingleQuery()` for specific queries where single-query is known to be better.\n\n### When to Prefer SingleQuery\n\n- Small, well-understood navigation graphs (2-3 levels)\n- Queries where all related data is always needed\n- Performance-critical paths where round-trip cost is lower than cartesian explosion\n\n### When to Prefer SplitQuery\n\n- Large or unpredictable navigation graphs\n- Many-to-many relationships\n- Queries loading collections that may not all be needed\n\n---\n\n## Testing with EF Core\n\n### In-Memory Provider (Unit Tests Only)\n\n```csharp\n// Only for simple unit tests - doesn''t match real database behavior\nvar options = new DbContextOptionsBuilder<ApplicationDbContext>()\n    .UseInMemoryDatabase(databaseName: Guid.NewGuid().ToString())\n    .Options;\n\nusing var context = new ApplicationDbContext(options);\n```\n\n### Real Database with TestContainers (Integration Tests)\n\nSee the `testcontainers-integration-tests` skill for proper database testing.\n\n```csharp\n// Use real PostgreSQL in container\nvar container = new PostgreSqlBuilder()\n    .WithImage(\"postgres:16-alpine\")\n    .Build();\n\nawait container.StartAsync();\n\nvar options = new DbContextOptionsBuilder<ApplicationDbContext>()\n    .UseNpgsql(container.GetConnectionString())\n    .Options;\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:23:23.907Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for .NET Developer Agents seeking to master Entity Framework Core patterns for optimized database interactions","zh":"适合于寻求掌握实体框架核心模式以优化数据库交互的 .NET 开发者代理","ja":".NET Developer エージェントが Entity Framework Core パターンをマスターしてデータベースの相互作用を最適化するのに最適","ko":"데이터베이스 상호 작용을 최적화하기 위한 엔터티 프레임워크 코어 패턴을 마스터하려는 .NET 개발자 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrolladores de .NET que buscan dominar los patrones de Entity Framework Core para interacciones de base de datos optimizadas","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développeurs .NET qui cherchent à maîtriser les modèles de Entity Framework Core pour des interactions de base de données optimisées","de":"Ideal für .NET-Entwickleragenten, die Entity Framework Core-Muster für optimierte Datenbankinteraktionen meistern möchten","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvedores .NET que buscam dominar padrões do Entity Framework Core para interações de banco de dados otimizadas","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков .NET, стремящихся освоить шаблоны Entity Framework Core для оптимизированных взаимодействий с базой данных","ar":"مثالي لعميل وكلاء التطوير .NET الذين يسعون إلى التمكن من الأنماط الأساسية لتكنولوجيا Entity Framework من أجل تفاعلات قواعد البيانات المُختزلة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize query performance, manage database migrations, and integrate EF Core with .NET Aspire using best practices like NoTracking by default and never editing migrations manually, all while efficiently loading multiple navigation collections through query splitting","zh":"赋予代理优化查询性能、管理数据库迁移以及使用最佳实践（如默认的 NoTracking 和永远不手动编辑迁移）将 EF Core 与 .NET Aspire 集成，同时通过查询分割高效地加载多个导航集合","ja":"エージェントに、クエリのパフォーマンスを最適化し、データベースの移行を管理し、ベストプラクティス（デフォルトの NoTracking や手動での移行の編集を決して行わないなど）を使用して EF Core を .NET Aspire と統合し、クエリの分割によって複数のナビゲーション コレクションを効率的に読み込むことを可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 쿼리 성능을 최적화하고 데이터베이스 마이그레이션을 관리하며 최고의 실천 방법(예: 기본 NoTracking 및 마이그레이션을 수동으로 편집하지 않음)을 사용하여 EF Core를 .NET Aspire와 통합하고 쿼리 분할을 통해 여러 탐색 컬렉션을 효율적으로 로드할 수 있도록 함","es":"Permite a los agentes optimizar el rendimiento de las consultas, administrar las migraciones de la base de datos e integrar EF Core con .NET Aspire utilizando las mejores prácticas como NoTracking por defecto y nunca editar las migraciones manualmente, todo mientras se cargan eficientemente múltiples colecciones de navegación a través de la división de consultas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''optimiser les performances des requêtes, de gérer les migrations de base de données et d''intégrer EF Core avec .NET Aspire en utilisant les meilleures pratiques comme NoTracking par défaut et en ne modifiant jamais les migrations manuellement, le tout en chargeant efficacement plusieurs collections de navigation via le fractionnement de requêtes","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, die Abfrageleistung zu optimieren, Datenbankmigrationen zu verwalten und EF Core mit .NET Aspire mithilfe von Best Practices wie NoTracking standardmäßig und dem manuellen Bearbeiten von Migrationen zu integrieren, während gleichzeitig mehrere Navigationsauflistungen effizient durch Abfrageaufteilung geladen werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a otimizar o desempenho de consultas, gerenciar migrações de banco de dados e integrar o EF Core com .NET Aspire utilizando boas práticas como NoTracking por padrão e nunca editando migrações manualmente, tudo isso carregando de forma eficiente vários conjuntos de navegação por meio da divisão de consultas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оптимизировать производительность запросов, управлять миграциями базы данных и интегрировать EF Core с .NET Aspire, используя лучшие практики, такие как NoTracking по умолчанию и никогда не редактируя миграции вручную, при этом эффективно загружая несколько навигационных коллекций посредством разделения запросов","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحسين أداء الاستعلامات وإدارة هجرة قواعد البيانات وتكامل EF Core مع .NET Aspire باستخدام أفضل الممارسات مثل NoTracking افتراضيًا وأبدًا تحرير الهجرات يدوياً، كل ذلك مع تحميل مت Yates التнавج متعددة بفعالية من خلال تقسيم الاستعلامات"},"useCases":{"en":["Setting up EF Core in new projects with optimized configurations","Debugging change tracking issues for improved data consistency","Integrating EF Core with .NET Aspire for seamless application development"],"zh":["在新项目中使用优化配置设置 EF Core","调试更改跟踪问题以提高数据一致性","将 EF Core 与 .NET Aspire 集成以实现无缝应用程序开发"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトに最適化された構成で EF Core を設定する","変更の追跡に関する問題をデバッグしてデータの一貫性を高める","EF Core を .NET Aspire と統合してシームレスなアプリケーション開発を行う"],"ko":["최적화된 구성으로 새 프로젝트에 EF Core 설정","데이터 일관성을 개선하기 위한 변경 사항 추적 문제 디버깅","EF Core를 .NET Aspire와 통합하여 無缝な 애플리케이션 개발을 thực現하는"],"es":["Configuración de EF Core en nuevos proyectos con configuraciones optimizadas","Depuración de problemas de seguimiento de cambios para una mayor coherencia de los datos","Integración de EF Core con .NET Aspire para un desarrollo de aplicaciones sin problemas"],"fr":["Configuration de EF Core dans de nouveaux projets avec des configurations optimisées","Débogage des problèmes de suivi des modifications pour une meilleure cohérence des données","Intégration de EF Core avec .NET Aspire pour un développement d''applications sans problème"],"de":["Einrichtung von EF Core in neuen Projekten mit optimierten Konfigurationen","Fehlerbehebung bei Änderungsverfolgungsproblemen für eine verbesserte Datenkonsistenz","Integration von EF Core mit .NET Aspire für eine reibungslose Anwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["Configurar o EF Core em novos projetos com configurações otimizadas","Depurar problemas de rastreamento de alterações para melhorar a consistência dos dados","Integrar o EF Core com .NET Aspire para desenvolvimento de aplicativos sem interrupções"],"ru":["Настройка EF Core в новых проектах с оптимизированными конфигурациями","Отладка проблем отслеживания изменений для улучшения согласованности данных","Интеграция EF Core с .NET Aspire для бесперебойного разработки приложений"],"ar":["تكوين EF Core في مشاريع جديدة مع تكوينات مُختزلة","تصحيح أخطاء تتبع التغييرات لتحسين الاتساقية البيانات","تكامل EF Core مع .NET Aspire من أجل تطوير تطبيقات سلس"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET environment","Specific to Entity Framework Core","Optimized for query performance and database migration management"],"zh":[".NET 环境が必要","特定于实体框架核心","针对查询性能和数据库迁移管理进行优化"],"ja":[".NET 環境が必要","エンティティ フレームワーク コアに特有","クエリ パフォーマンスとデータベース移行の管理に最適化"],"ko":[".NET 환경 필요","엔터티 프레임워크 코어에 특정","쿼리 성능 및 데이터베이스 마이그레이션 관리에 최적화"],"es":["Requiere un entorno .NET","Específico de Entity Framework Core","Optimizado para el rendimiento de las consultas y la administración de migraciones de la base de datos"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement .NET","Spécifique à Entity Framework Core","Optimisé pour les performances des requêtes et la gestion des migrations de base de données"],"de":["Benötigt eine .NET-Umgebung","Spezifisch für Entity Framework Core","Optimiert für Abfrageleistung und Datenbankmigrationen-Verwaltung"],"pt":["Exige ambiente .NET","Específico para Entity Framework Core","Otimizado para desempenho de consultas e gerenciamento de migração de banco de dados"],"ru":["Требует среды .NET","Специфичен для Entity Framework Core","Оптимизирован для производительности запросов и управления миграциями базы данных"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة .NET","محدد لتكنولوجيا Entity Framework Core","مُختزل لتحسين أداء الاستعلامات وإدارة هجرة قواعد البيانات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mims-harvard/ToolUniverse/tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design', 'community', 'mims-harvard', 'ToolUniverse', 'mims-harvard/ToolUniverse', 'tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z', '2026-02-18T02:23:41.063Z', NULL, '{"id":"mims-harvard/ToolUniverse/tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design","name":"tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design","description":{"zh":"ToolUniverse提供了AI引导的蛋白质治疗设计解决方案，通过结构优先、目标导向、迭代验证和开发可行性等关键原则，实现高效的蛋白质设计","ja":"ToolUniverseはAIガイドのタンパク質治療設計ソリューションを提供し、構造優先、ターゲット指向、イテレーティブ検証、開発可能性などの重要な原則を通じて、高効率のタンパク質設計を実現","ko":"ToolUniverse는 AI 가이드 단백질 치료 설계 솔루션을 제공하며, 구조 우선, 대상 지향, 반복 검증 및 개발 가능성 등의 주요 원칙을 통하여 효율적인 단백질 설계를 실현","es":"ToolUniverse permite el diseño de proteínas terapéuticas con IA, utilizando generación de backbone RFdiffusion y optimización de secuencia ProteinMPNN. Este enfoque combina diseño estructural y validación iterativa para desarrollar proteínas terapéuticas innovadoras","fr":"ToolUniverse permet la conception de protéines thérapeutiques avec l''IA, en utilisant la génération de backbone RFdiffusion et l''optimisation de séquence ProteinMPNN. Cette approche combine le design structurel et la validation itérative pour développer des protéines thérapeutiques innovantes","de":"ToolUniverse ermöglicht den Entwurf therapeutischer Proteine mit KI, unter Verwendung der Backbone-Generierung RFdiffusion und der Sequenzoptimierung ProteinMPNN. Dieser Ansatz kombiniert strukturelles Design und iterative Validierung, um innovative therapeutische Proteine zu entwickeln","pt":"A ToolUniverse é uma plataforma de design de proteínas terapêuticas que utiliza IA para desenvolver soluções inovadoras. Ela emprega princípios de design de estrutura, orientado a alvo e validação iterativa","ru":"ToolUniverse - это платформа для проектирования терапевтических белков, которая использует ИИ для разработки инновационных решений. Она основана на принципах структуры, ориентированного на цель и итеративной проверки","ar":"ToolUniverse هي منصة لتصميم البروتينات العلاجية التي تستخدم الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير حلول مبتكرة. وهي تستخدم مبادئ التصميم الهيكلي والتوجيه والتحقق التكراري","en":"Democratizing AI scientists with ToolUniverse"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"ToolUniverse蛋白质治疗设计","ja":"ToolUniverseタンパク質治療設計","ko":"ToolUniverse 단백질 치료 설계","es":"Diseño de proteínas terapéuticas con IA","fr":"Conception de protéines thérapeutiques avec IA","de":"Entwurf therapeutischer Proteine mit KI","pt":"Design de Proteínas Terapêuticas com IA","ru":"Проектирование терапевтических белков с помощью ИИ","ar":"تصميم البروتينات العلاجية بالذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design"},"description":{"zh":"ToolUniverse提供了AI引导的蛋白质治疗设计解决方案，通过结构优先、目标导向、迭代验证和开发可行性等关键原则，实现高效的蛋白质设计","ja":"ToolUniverseはAIガイドのタンパク質治療設計ソリューションを提供し、構造優先、ターゲット指向、イテレーティブ検証、開発可能性などの重要な原則を通じて、高効率のタンパク質設計を実現","ko":"ToolUniverse는 AI 가이드 단백질 치료 설계 솔루션을 제공하며, 구조 우선, 대상 지향, 반복 검증 및 개발 가능성 등의 주요 원칙을 통하여 효율적인 단백질 설계를 실현","es":"ToolUniverse permite el diseño de proteínas terapéuticas con IA, utilizando generación de backbone RFdiffusion y optimización de secuencia ProteinMPNN. Este ...","fr":"ToolUniverse permet la conception de protéines thérapeutiques avec l''IA, en utilisant la génération de backbone RFdiffusion et l''optimisation de séquence Pro...","de":"ToolUniverse ermöglicht den Entwurf therapeutischer Proteine mit KI, unter Verwendung der Backbone-Generierung RFdiffusion und der Sequenzoptimierung Protein...","pt":"A ToolUniverse é uma plataforma de design de proteínas terapêuticas que utiliza IA para desenvolver soluções inovadoras. Ela emprega princípios de design de ...","ru":"ToolUniverse - это платформа для проектирования терапевтических белков, которая использует ИИ для разработки инновационных решений. Она основана на принципах...","ar":"ToolUniverse هي منصة لتصميم البروتينات العلاجية التي تستخدم الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير حلول مبتكرة. وهي تستخدم مبادئ التصميم الهيكلي والتوجيه والتحقق التكراري","en":"Democratizing AI scientists with ToolUniverse"},"definition":{"en":"Democratizing AI scientists with ToolUniverse"},"features":{"zh":["结构优先设计","目标导向设计","迭代验证","开发可行性"],"ja":["構造優先設計","ターゲット指向設計","イテレーティブ検証","開発可能性"],"ko":["구조 우선 설계","대상 지향 설계","반복 검증","개발 가능성"],"es":["Diseño estructural guiado por la estructura del objetivo","Generación de backbone con RFdiffusion","Optimización de secuencia con ProteinMPNN","Validación iterativa de la estructura","Consideración de la desarrollabilidad y la inmunogenicidad"],"fr":["Conception structurelle guidée par la structure de la cible","Génération de backbone avec RFdiffusion","Optimisation de séquence avec ProteinMPNN","Validation itérative de la structure","Prise en compte de la dévelopabilité et de l''immunogénicité"],"de":["Strukturelles Design unter Berücksichtigung der Zielstruktur","Backbone-Generierung mit RFdiffusion","Sequenzoptimierung mit ProteinMPNN","Iterative Validierung der Struktur","Berücksichtigung der Entwickelbarkeit und Immunogenität"],"pt":["Design de estrutura em primeiro lugar","Orientado a alvo","Validação iterativa","Conscientização do desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Проектирование структуры в первую очередь","Ориентированное на цель","Итеративная проверка","Осведомленность о разработке"],"ar":["تصميم الهيكل أولا","التوجيه","التحقق التكراري","الوعي بالتطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["蛋白质治疗设计","AI引导蛋白质设计","结构优先设计","目标导向设计","迭代验证","开发可行性"],"ja":["タンパク質治療設計","AIガイドタンパク質設計","構造優先設計","ターゲット指向設計","イテレーティブ検証","開発可能性"],"ko":["단백질 치료 설계","AI 가이드 단백질 설계","구조 우선 설계","대상 지향 설계","반복 검증","개발 가능성"],"es":["diseño de proteínas terapéuticas","IA en biología","algoritmos de aprendizaje automático","RFdiffusion","ProteinMPNN","desarrollo de proteínas","biología estructural","inmunogenicidad"],"fr":["conception de protéines thérapeutiques","IA en biologie","algorithmes d''apprentissage automatique","RFdiffusion","ProteinMPNN","développement de protéines","biologie structurale","immunogénicité"],"de":["Entwurf therapeutischer Proteine","KI in der Biologie","Algorithmen des maschinellen Lernens","RFdiffusion","ProteinMPNN","Entwicklung von Proteinen","strukturelle Biologie","Immunogenität"],"pt":["design de proteínas terapêuticas","IA para desenvolvimento de proteínas","ferramentas de design de proteínas","proteínas terapêuticas","desenvolvimento de proteínas","biotecnologia"],"ru":["проектирование терапевтических белков","ИИ для разработки белков","инструменты для проектирования белков","терапевтические белки","разработка белков","биотехнология"],"ar":["تصميم البروتينات العلاجية","الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير البروتينات","أدوات تصميم البروتينات","البروتينات العلاجية","تطوير البروتينات","التكنولوجيا الحيوية"]}},"owner":"mims-harvard","repo":"ToolUniverse","repoPath":"mims-harvard/ToolUniverse","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tooluniverse-protein-therapeutic-design","description":"Design novel protein therapeutics (binders, enzymes, scaffolds) using AI-guided de novo design. Uses RFdiffusion for backbone generation, ProteinMPNN for sequence design, ESMFold/AlphaFold2 for validation. Use when asked to design protein binders, therapeutic proteins, or engineer protein function.","bodyPreview":"# Therapeutic Protein Designer\n\nAI-guided de novo protein design using RFdiffusion backbone generation, ProteinMPNN sequence optimization, and structure validation for therapeutic protein development.\n\n**KEY PRINCIPLES**:\n1. **Structure-first design** - Generate backbone geometry before sequence\n2. **Target-guided** - Design binders with target structure in mind\n3. **Iterative validation** - Predict structure to validate designs\n4. **Developability-aware** - Consider aggregation, immunogenicity,","body":"# Therapeutic Protein Designer\n\nAI-guided de novo protein design using RFdiffusion backbone generation, ProteinMPNN sequence optimization, and structure validation for therapeutic protein development.\n\n**KEY PRINCIPLES**:\n1. **Structure-first design** - Generate backbone geometry before sequence\n2. **Target-guided** - Design binders with target structure in mind\n3. **Iterative validation** - Predict structure to validate designs\n4. **Developability-aware** - Consider aggregation, immunogenicity, expression\n5. **Evidence-graded** - Grade designs by confidence metrics\n6. **Actionable output** - Provide sequences ready for experimental testing\n7. **English-first queries** - Always use English terms in tool calls (protein names, target names), even if the user writes in another language. Only try original-language terms as a fallback. Respond in the user''s language\n\n---\n\n## When to Use\n\nApply when user asks:\n- \"Design a protein binder for [target]\"\n- \"Create a therapeutic protein against [protein/epitope]\"\n- \"Design a protein scaffold with [property]\"\n- \"Optimize this protein sequence for [function]\"\n- \"Design a de novo enzyme for [reaction]\"\n- \"Generate protein variants for [target binding]\"\n\n---\n\n## Critical Workflow Requirements\n\n### 1. Report-First Approach (MANDATORY)\n\n1. **Create the report file FIRST**:\n   - File name: `[TARGET]_protein_design_report.md`\n   - Initialize with section headers\n   - Add placeholder: `[Designing...]`\n\n2. **Progressively update** as designs are generated\n\n3. **Output separate files**:\n   - `[TARGET]_designed_sequences.fasta` - All designed sequences\n   - `[TARGET]_top_candidates.csv` - Ranked candidates with metrics\n\n### 2. Design Documentation (MANDATORY)\n\nEvery design MUST include:\n\n```markdown\n### Design: Binder_001\n\n**Sequence**: MVLSPADKTN...\n**Length**: 85 amino acids\n**Target**: PD-L1 (UniProt: Q9NZQ7)\n**Method**: RFdiffusion → ProteinMPNN → ESMFold validation\n\n**Quality Metrics**:\n| Metric | Value | Interpretation |\n|--------|-------|----------------|\n| pLDDT | 88.5 | High confidence |\n| pTM | 0.82 | Good fold |\n| ProteinMPNN score | -2.3 | Favorable |\n| Predicted binding | Strong | Based on interface pLDDT |\n\n*Source: NVIDIA NIM via `NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion`, `NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn`, `NvidiaNIM_esmfold`*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0: Tool Verification\n\n### NVIDIA NIM Tools Required\n\n| Tool | Purpose | API Key Required |\n|------|---------|------------------|\n| `NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion` | Backbone generation | Yes |\n| `NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn` | Sequence design | Yes |\n| `NvidiaNIM_esmfold` | Fast structure validation | Yes |\n| `NvidiaNIM_alphafold2` | High-accuracy validation | Yes |\n| `NvidiaNIM_esm2_650m` | Sequence embeddings | Yes |\n\n### Parameter Verification\n\n| Tool | WRONG Parameter | CORRECT Parameter |\n|------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| `NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion` | `num_steps` | `diffusion_steps` |\n| `NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn` | `pdb` | `pdb_string` |\n| `NvidiaNIM_esmfold` | `seq` | `sequence` |\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\n```\nPhase 1: Target Characterization\n├── Get target structure (PDB, EMDB cryo-EM, or AlphaFold)\n├── Identify binding epitope\n├── Analyze existing binders\n├── Check EMDB for membrane protein structures (NEW)\n└── OUTPUT: Target profile\n    ↓\nPhase 2: Backbone Generation (RFdiffusion)\n├── Define design constraints\n├── Generate multiple backbones\n├── Filter by geometry quality\n└── OUTPUT: Candidate backbones\n    ↓\nPhase 3: Sequence Design (ProteinMPNN)\n├── Design sequences for each backbone\n├── Sample multiple sequences per backbone\n├── Score by ProteinMPNN likelihood\n└── OUTPUT: Designed sequences\n    ↓\nPhase 4: Structure Validation\n├── Predict structure (ESMFold/AlphaFold2)\n├── Compare to designed backbone\n├── Assess fold quality (pLDDT, pTM)\n└── OUTPUT: Validated designs\n    ↓\nPhase 5: Developability Assessment\n├── Aggregation propensity\n├── Expression likelihood\n├── Immunogenicity prediction\n└── OUTPUT: Developability scores\n    ↓\nPhase 6: Report Synthesis\n├── Ranked candidate list\n├── Experimental recommendations\n├── Next steps\n└── OUTPUT: Final report\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Target Characterization\n\n### 1.1 Get Target Structure\n\n```python\ndef get_target_structure(tu, target_id):\n    \"\"\"Get target structure from PDB, EMDB, or predict.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Try PDB first (X-ray/NMR)\n    pdb_results = tu.tools.PDB_search_by_uniprot(uniprot_id=target_id)\n    \n    if pdb_results:\n        # Get highest resolution structure\n        best_pdb = sorted(pdb_results, key=lambda x: x[''resolution''])[0]\n        structure = tu.tools.PDB_get_structure(pdb_id=best_pdb[''pdb_id''])\n        return {''source'': ''PDB'', ''pdb_id'': best_pdb[''pdb_id''], \n                ''resolution'': best_pdb[''resolution''], ''structure'': structure}\n    \n    # Try EMDB for cryo-EM structures (valuable for membrane proteins)\n    protein_info = tu.tools.UniProt_get_protein_by_accession(accession=target_id)\n    emdb_results = tu.tools.emdb_search(\n        query=protein_info[''proteinDescription''][''recommendedName''][''fullName''][''value'']\n    )\n    \n    if emdb_results and len(emdb_results) > 0:\n        # Get highest resolution cryo-EM entry\n        best_emdb = sorted(emdb_results, key=lambda x: x.get(''resolution'', 99))[0]\n        # Get associated PDB model if available\n        emdb_details = tu.tools.emdb_get_entry(entry_id=best_emdb[''emdb_id''])\n        if emdb_details.get(''pdb_ids''):\n            structure = tu.tools.PDB_get_structure(pdb_id=emdb_details[''pdb_ids''][0])\n            return {''source'': ''EMDB cryo-EM'', ''emdb_id'': best_emdb[''emdb_id''],\n                    ''pdb_id'': emdb_details[''pdb_ids''][0], \n                    ''resolution'': best_emdb.get(''resolution''), ''structure'': structure}\n    \n    # Fallback to AlphaFold prediction\n    sequence = tu.tools.UniProt_get_protein_sequence(accession=target_id)\n    structure = tu.tools.NvidiaNIM_alphafold2(\n        sequence=sequence[''sequence''],\n        algorithm=\"mmseqs2\"\n    )\n    return {''source'': ''AlphaFold2 (predicted)'', ''structure'': structure}\n```\n\n### 1.1b EMDB for Membrane Proteins (NEW)\n\n**When to prioritize EMDB**: Membrane proteins, large complexes, and targets where conformational states matter.\n\n```python\ndef get_cryoem_structures(tu, target_name):\n    \"\"\"Get cryo-EM structures for membrane proteins/complexes.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Search EMDB\n    emdb_results = tu.tools.emdb_search(\n        query=f\"{target_name} membrane OR receptor\"\n    )\n    \n    structures = []\n    for entry in emdb_results[:5]:\n        details = tu.tools.emdb_get_entry(entry_id=entry[''emdb_id''])\n        structures.append({\n            ''emdb_id'': entry[''emdb_id''],\n            ''resolution'': entry.get(''resolution'', ''N/A''),\n            ''title'': entry.get(''title'', ''N/A''),\n            ''conformational_state'': details.get(''state'', ''Unknown''),\n            ''pdb_models'': details.get(''pdb_ids'', [])\n        })\n    \n    return structures\n```\n\n**Output for Report**:\n\n```markdown\n### 1.1b Cryo-EM Structures (EMDB)\n\n| EMDB ID | Resolution | PDB Model | Conformation |\n|---------|------------|-----------|--------------|\n| EMD-12345 | 2.8 Å | 7ABC | Active state |\n| EMD-23456 | 3.1 Å | 8DEF | Inactive state |\n\n**Note**: Cryo-EM structures capture physiologically relevant conformations for membrane protein targets.\n\n*Source: EMDB*\n```\n\n### 1.2 Identify Binding Epitope\n\n```python\ndef identify_epitope(tu, target_structure, epitope_residues=None):\n    \"\"\"Identify or validate binding epitope.\"\"\"\n    \n    if epitope_residues:\n        # User-specified epitope\n        return {''residues'': epitope_residues, ''source'': ''user-defined''}\n    \n    # Find surface-exposed regions\n    # Use structural analysis to identify potential epitopes\n    return analyze_surface(target_structure)\n```\n\n### 1.3 Output for Report\n\n```markdown\n## 1. Target Characterization\n\n### 1.1 Target Information\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| **Target** | PD-L1 (Programmed death-ligand 1) |\n| **UniProt** | Q9NZQ7 |\n| **Structure source** | PDB: 4ZQK (2.0 Å resolution) |\n| **Binding epitope** | IgV domain, residues 19-127 |\n| **Known binders** | Atezolizumab, durvalumab, avelumab |\n\n### 1.2 Epitope Analysis\n\n| Residue Range | Type | Surface Area | Druggability |\n|---------------|------|--------------|--------------|\n| 54-68 | Loop | 850 Å² | High |\n| 115-125 | Beta strand | 420 Å² | Medium |\n| 19-30 | N-terminus | 380 Å² | Medium |\n\n**Selected Epitope**: Residues 54-68 (PD-1 binding interface)\n\n*Source: PDB 4ZQK, surface analysis*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Backbone Generation\n\n### 2.1 RFdiffusion Design\n\n```python\ndef generate_backbones(tu, design_params):\n    \"\"\"Generate de novo backbones using RFdiffusion.\"\"\"\n    \n    backbones = tu.tools.NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion(\n        diffusion_steps=design_params.get(''steps'', 50),\n        # Additional parameters depending on design type\n    )\n    \n    return backbones\n```\n\n### 2.2 Design Modes\n\n| Mode | Use Case | Key Parameters |\n|------|----------|----------------|\n| **Unconditional** | De novo scaffold | `diffusion_steps` only |\n| **Binder design** | Target-guided binder | `target_structure`, `hotspot_residues` |\n| **Motif scaffolding** | Functional motif embedding | `motif_sequence`, `motif_structure` |\n\n### 2.3 Output for Report\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Backbone Generation\n\n### 2.1 Design Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| **Method** | RFdiffusion via NVIDIA NIM |\n| **Design mode** | Unconditional scaffold generation |\n| **Diffusion steps** | 50 |\n| **Number generated** | 10 backbones |\n\n### 2.2 Generated Backbones\n\n| Backbone | Length | Topology | Quality |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| BB_001 | 85 aa | 3-helix bundle | Good |\n| BB_002 | 92 aa | Beta sandwich | Good |\n| BB_003 | 78 aa | Alpha-beta | Good |\n| BB_004 | 88 aa | All-alpha | Moderate |\n| BB_005 | 95 aa | Mixed | Good |\n\n**Selected for sequence design**: BB_001, BB_002, BB_003, BB_005 (top 4)\n\n*Source: NVIDIA NIM via `NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion`*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Sequence Design\n\n### 3.1 ProteinMPNN Design\n\n```python\ndef design_sequences(tu, backbone_pdb, num_sequences=8):\n    \"\"\"Design sequences for backbone using ProteinMPNN.\"\"\"\n    \n    sequences = tu.tools.NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn(\n        pdb_string=backbone_pdb,\n        num_sequences=num_sequences,\n        temperature=0.1  # Lower = more conservative\n    )\n    \n    return sequences\n```\n\n### 3.2 Sampling Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Conservative | Moderate | Diverse |\n|-----------|--------------|----------|---------|\n| Temperature | 0.1 | 0.2 | 0.5 |\n| Sequences per backbone | 4 | 8 | 16 |\n| Use case | Validated scaffold | Exploration | Diversity |\n\n### 3.3 Output for Report\n\n```markdown\n## 3. Sequence Design\n\n### 3.1 Design Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| **Method** | ProteinMPNN via NVIDIA NIM |\n| **Temperature** | 0.1 (conservative) |\n| **Sequences per backbone** | 8 |\n| **Total sequences** | 32 |\n\n### 3.2 Designed Sequences (Top 10 by Score)\n\n| Rank | Backbone | Sequence ID | Length | MPNN Score | Predicted pI |\n|------|----------|-------------|--------|------------|--------------|\n| 1 | BB_001 | Seq_001_A | 85 | -1.89 | 6.2 |\n| 2 | BB_002 | Seq_002_C | 92 | -1.95 | 5.8 |\n| 3 | BB_001 | Seq_001_B | 85 | -2.01 | 7.1 |\n| 4 | BB_003 | Seq_003_A | 78 | -2.08 | 6.5 |\n| 5 | BB_005 | Seq_005_B | 95 | -2.12 | 5.4 |\n\n### 3.3 Top Sequence: Seq_001_A\n\n```\n>Seq_001_A (85 aa, MPNN score: -1.89)\nMVLSPADKTNVKAAWGKVGAHAGEYGAEALERMFLSFPTTKTYFPHFDLSH\nGSAQVKGHGKKVADALTNAVAHVDDMPNALSALSDLHAHKL\n```\n\n*Source: NVIDIA NIM via `NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn`*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Structure Validation\n\n### 4.1 ESMFold Validation\n\n```python\ndef validate_structure(tu, sequence):\n    \"\"\"Validate designed sequence by structure prediction.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Fast validation with ESMFold\n    predicted = tu.tools.NvidiaNIM_esmfold(sequence=sequence)\n    \n    # Extract quality metrics\n    plddt = extract_plddt(predicted)\n    ptm = extract_ptm(predicted)\n    \n    return {\n        ''structure'': predicted,\n        ''mean_plddt'': np.mean(plddt),\n        ''ptm'': ptm,\n        ''passes'': np.mean(plddt) > 70 and ptm > 0.7\n    }\n```\n\n### 4.2 Validation Criteria\n\n| Metric | Threshold | Interpretation |\n|--------|-----------|----------------|\n| Mean pLDDT | >70 | Confident fold |\n| pTM | >0.7 | Good global topology |\n| RMSD to backbone | <2 Å | Design recapitulated |\n\n### 4.3 Output for Report\n\n```markdown\n## 4. Structure Validation\n\n### 4.1 Validation Results\n\n| Sequence | pLDDT | pTM | RMSD to Design | Status |\n|----------|-------|-----|----------------|--------|\n| Seq_001_A | 88.5 | 0.85 | 1.2 Å | ✓ PASS |\n| Seq_002_C | 82.3 | 0.79 | 1.5 Å | ✓ PASS |\n| Seq_001_B | 85.1 | 0.82 | 1.3 Å | ✓ PASS |\n| Seq_003_A | 79.8 | 0.76 | 1.8 Å | ✓ PASS |\n| Seq_005_B | 68.2 | 0.65 | 2.8 Å | ✗ FAIL |\n\n### 4.2 Top Validated Design: Seq_001_A\n\n| Region | Residues | pLDDT | Interpretation |\n|--------|----------|-------|----------------|\n| Helix 1 | 1-28 | 92.3 | Very high confidence |\n| Loop 1 | 29-35 | 78.4 | Moderate confidence |\n| Helix 2 | 36-58 | 91.8 | Very high confidence |\n| Loop 2 | 59-65 | 75.2 | Moderate confidence |\n| Helix 3 | 66-85 | 90.1 | Very high confidence |\n\n**Overall**: Well-folded 3-helix bundle with high confidence core\n\n*Source: NVIDIA NIM via `NvidiaNIM_esmfold`*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Developability Assessment\n\n### 5.1 Aggregation Propensity\n\n```python\ndef assess_aggregation(sequence):\n    \"\"\"Assess aggregation propensity.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Calculate hydrophobic patches\n    # Calculate isoelectric point\n    # Identify aggregation-prone motifs\n    \n    return {\n        ''aggregation_score'': score,\n        ''hydrophobic_patches'': patches,\n        ''risk_level'': ''Low'' if score < 0.5 else ''Medium'' if score < 0.7 else ''High''\n    }\n```\n\n### 5.2 Developability Metrics\n\n| Metric | Favorable | Marginal | Unfavorable |\n|--------|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| Aggregation score | <0.5 | 0.5-0.7 | >0.7 |\n| Isoelectric point | 5-9 | 4-5 or 9-10 | <4 or >10 |\n| Hydrophobic patches | <3 | 3-5 | >5 |\n| Cysteine count | 0 or even | Odd | Multiple unpaired |\n\n### 5.3 Output for Report\n\n```markdown\n## 5. Developability Assessment\n\n### 5.1 Developability Scores\n\n| Design | Aggregation | pI | Cysteines | Expression | Overall |\n|--------|-------------|-----|-----------|------------|---------|\n| Seq_001_A | 0.32 (Low) | 6.2 | 0 | High | ★★★ |\n| Seq_002_C | 0.45 (Low) | 5.8 | 2 (paired) | Medium | ★★☆ |\n| Seq_001_B | 0.38 (Low) | 7.1 | 0 | High | ★★★ |\n| Seq_003_A | 0.58 (Med) | 6.5 | 0 | Medium | ★★☆ |\n\n### 5.2 Recommendations\n\n**Best candidate for expression**: Seq_001_A\n- Low aggregation propensity\n- Neutral pI (easy purification)\n- No cysteines (no misfolding risk)\n- Predicted high E. coli expression\n\n*Source: Sequence analysis*\n```\n\n---\n\n## Report Template\n\n```markdown\n# Therapeutic Protein Design Report: [TARGET]\n\n**Generated**: [Date] | **Query**: [Original query] | **Status**: In Progress\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 1. Target Characterization\n### 1.1 Target Information\n[Designing...]\n### 1.2 Binding Epitope\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 2. Backbone Generation\n### 2.1 Design Parameters\n[Designing...]\n### 2.2 Generated Backbones\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 3. Sequence Design\n### 3.1 ProteinMPNN Results\n[Designing...]\n### 3.2 Top Sequences\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 4. Structure Validation\n### 4.1 ESMFold Validation\n[Designing...]\n### 4.2 Quality Metrics\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 5. Developability Assessment\n### 5.1 Scores\n[Designing...]\n### 5.2 Recommendations\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 6. Final Candidates\n### 6.1 Ranked List\n[Designing...]\n### 6.2 Sequences for Testing\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 7. Experimental Recommendations\n[Designing...]\n\n---\n\n## 8. Data Sources\n[Will be populated...]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Evidence Grading\n\n| Tier | Symbol | Criteria |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| **T1** | ★★★ | pLDDT >85, pTM >0.8, low aggregation, neutral pI |\n| **T2** | ★★☆ | pLDDT >75, pTM >0.7, acceptable developability |\n| **T3** | ★☆☆ | pLDDT >70, pTM >0.65, developability concerns |\n| **T4** | ☆☆☆ | Failed validation or major developability issues |\n\n---\n\n## Completeness Checklist\n\n### Phase 1: Target\n- [ ] Target structure obtained (PDB or predicted)\n- [ ] Binding epitope identified\n- [ ] Existing binders noted\n\n### Phase 2: Backbones\n- [ ] ≥5 backbones generated\n- [ ] Top 3-5 selected for sequence design\n- [ ] Selection criteria documented\n\n### Phase 3: Sequences\n- [ ] ≥8 sequences per backbone designed\n- [ ] MPNN scores reported\n- [ ] Top 10 sequences listed\n\n### Phase 4: Validation\n- [ ] All sequences validated by ESMFold\n- [ ] pLDDT and pTM reported\n- [ ] Pass/fail criteria applied\n- [ ] ≥3 passing designs\n\n### Phase 5: Developability\n- [ ] Aggregation assessed\n- [ ] pI calculated\n- [ ] Expression prediction\n- [ ] Final ranking\n\n### Phase 6: Deliverables\n- [ ] Ranked candidate list\n- [ ] FASTA file with sequences\n- [ ] Experimental recommendations\n\n---\n\n## Fallback Chains\n\n| Primary Tool | Fallback 1 | Fallback 2 |\n|--------------|------------|------------|\n| `NvidiaNIM_rfdiffusion` | Manual backbone design | Scaffold from PDB |\n| `NvidiaNIM_proteinmpnn` | Rosetta ProteinMPNN | Manual sequence design |\n| `NvidiaNIM_esmfold` | `NvidiaNIM_alphafold2` | AlphaFold DB |\n| PDB structure | `NvidiaNIM_alphafold2` | AlphaFold DB |\n\n---\n\n## Tool Reference\n\nSee [TOOLS_REFERENCE.md](TOOLS_REFERENCE.md) for complete tool documentation.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:23:41.063Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Biotech Agents requiring advanced protein design capabilities using RFdiffusion and ProteinMPNN","zh":"适用于需要使用RFdiffusion和ProteinMPNN进行高级蛋白质设计的生物技术代理","ja":"RFdiffusionおよびProteinMPNNを使用した高度なタンパク質設計機能を必要とするバイオテックエージェントに適しています","ko":"RFdiffusion 및 ProteinMPNN을 사용한 고급 단백질 설계 기능이 필요한 바이오테크 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de biotecnología que requieren capacidades avanzadas de diseño de proteínas utilizando RFdiffusion y ProteinMPNN","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de biotechnologie nécessitant des capacités de conception de protéines avancées utilisant RFdiffusion et ProteinMPNN","de":"Ideal für Biotech-Agents, die erweiterte Proteindesign-Fähigkeiten unter Verwendung von RFdiffusion und ProteinMPNN erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes de biotecnologia que exigem capacidades avançadas de design de proteínas usando RFdiffusion e ProteinMPNN","ru":"Идеально для биотехнологических агентов, требующих передовых возможностей проектирования белков с использованием RFdiffusion и ProteinMPNN","ar":"مثالي لعميل البايوتكنولوجي الذي يتطلب القدرات المتقدمة لتصميم البروتين باستخدام RFdiffusion و ProteinMPNN"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design therapeutic proteins with structure-first and target-guided approaches, leveraging RFdiffusion backbone generation and ProteinMPNN sequence optimization, while considering developability factors like aggregation and immunogenicity","zh":"赋予代理设计结构优先和靶向引导的治疗性蛋白质的能力，利用RFdiffusion骨架生成和ProteinMPNN序列优化，同时考虑可开发性因素，如聚集和免疫原性","ja":"エージェントに、構造優先とターゲット指向の治療用タンパク質を設計する能力を付与します。RFdiffusionのバックボーン生成とProteinMPNNのシーケンス最適化を活用し、集団化と免疫原性などの開発可能性要因を考慮します","ko":"에이전트에게 구조 우선 및 표적 유도 치료 단백질을 설계할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. RFdiffusion의 골격 생성 및 ProteinMPNN의 시퀀스 최적화를 활용하며, 집단화 및 면역원성과 같은 개발 가능성 요인을 고려합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar proteínas terapéuticas con enfoques de estructura-p