ntégrations d''intelligence artificielle","Développement d''agents personnalisés"],"de":["Automatische Delegation von Aufgaben","Zugriff auf Tools wie Cloudflare, React und Tailwind v4","Benutzerdefiniertes Prompt-Design","Künstliche Intelligenz-Integrationen","Entwicklung benutzerdefinierter Agenten"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de agentes personalizados","Integração com Cloudflare","Utilização de React e Tailwind v4","Integrações de IA","Delegação adequada de tarefas","Acesso a ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Разработка пользовательских агентов","Интеграция с Cloudflare","Использование React и Tailwind v4","Интеграции ИИ","Правильная делегация задач","Доступ к инструментам разработки"],"ar":["تطوير وكلاء مخصصين","إدماج مع كلود فلير","استخدام ري액ت وتايل ويند 4","إدماج الذكاء الاصطناعي","تفويض مناسب للمهام","وصول إلى أدوات التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":[" Claude Code ","full stack dev","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4","AI"," Claude Code","agent-development"],"ja":[" Claude Code","full stack dev","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4","AI"," Claude Code","agent-development"],"ko":[" Claude Code ","full stack dev","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4","AI"," Claude Code ","agent-development"],"es":["desarrollo de agentes","Claude Code","automatización de tareas","inteligencia artificial","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4"],"fr":["développement d''agents","Claude Code","automatisation de tâches","intelligence artificielle","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4"],"de":["Entwicklung von Agenten","Claude Code","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","künstliche Intelligenz","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de agentes","Claude Code","full stack","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4","integrações de IA","desenvolvimento de software","programação"],"ru":["разработка агентов","Claude Code","полный стек","Cloudflare","React","Tailwind v4","интеграции ИИ","разработка программного обеспечения","программирование"],"ar":["تطوير الوكلاء","شفرة كلود","التطوير الكامل","كلود فلير","ري액ت","تايل ويند 4","إدماج الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير البرمجيات","البرمجة"]}},"owner":"jezweb","repo":"claude-skills","repoPath":"jezweb/claude-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-development","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Agent Development for Claude Code\n\nBuild effective custom agents for Claude Code with proper delegation, tool access, and prompt design.\n\n## Agent Description Pattern\n\nThe description field determines whether Claude will automatically delegate tasks.\n\n### Strong Trigger Pattern\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: agent-name\ndescription: |\n  [Role] specialist. MUST BE USED when [specific triggers].\n  Use PROACTIVELY for [task category].\n  Keywords: [trigger words]\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, Bash\nmode","body":"# Agent Development for Claude Code\n\nBuild effective custom agents for Claude Code with proper delegation, tool access, and prompt design.\n\n## Agent Description Pattern\n\nThe description field determines whether Claude will automatically delegate tasks.\n\n### Strong Trigger Pattern\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: agent-name\ndescription: |\n  [Role] specialist. MUST BE USED when [specific triggers].\n  Use PROACTIVELY for [task category].\n  Keywords: [trigger words]\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, Bash\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n```\n\n### Weak vs Strong Descriptions\n\n| Weak (won''t auto-delegate) | Strong (auto-delegates) |\n|---------------------------|-------------------------|\n| \"Analyzes screenshots for issues\" | \"Visual QA specialist. MUST BE USED when analyzing screenshots. Use PROACTIVELY for visual QA.\" |\n| \"Runs Playwright scripts\" | \"Playwright specialist. MUST BE USED when running Playwright scripts. Use PROACTIVELY for browser automation.\" |\n\n**Key phrases**:\n- \"MUST BE USED when...\"\n- \"Use PROACTIVELY for...\"\n- Include trigger keywords\n\n### Delegation Mechanisms\n\n1. **Explicit**: `Task tool subagent_type: \"agent-name\"` - always works\n2. **Automatic**: Claude matches task to agent description - requires strong phrasing\n\n**Session restart required** after creating/modifying agents.\n\n## Tool Access Principle\n\n**If an agent doesn''t need Bash, don''t give it Bash.**\n\n| Agent needs to... | Give tools | Don''t give |\n|-------------------|------------|------------|\n| Create files only | Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep | Bash |\n| Run scripts/CLIs | Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, Bash | — |\n| Read/audit only | Read, Glob, Grep | Write, Edit, Bash |\n\n**Why?** Models default to `cat > file << ''EOF''` heredocs instead of Write tool. Each bash command requires approval, causing dozens of prompts per agent run.\n\n### Allowlist Pattern\n\nInstead of restricting Bash, allowlist safe commands in `.claude/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"allow\": [\n      \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"WebFetch(domain:*)\",\n      \"Bash(cd *)\", \"Bash(cp *)\", \"Bash(mkdir *)\", \"Bash(ls *)\",\n      \"Bash(cat *)\", \"Bash(head *)\", \"Bash(tail *)\", \"Bash(grep *)\",\n      \"Bash(diff *)\", \"Bash(mv *)\", \"Bash(touch *)\", \"Bash(file *)\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Model Selection (Quality First)\n\nDon''t downgrade quality to work around issues - fix root causes instead.\n\n| Model | Use For |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Opus** | Creative work (page building, design, content) - quality matters |\n| **Sonnet** | Most agents - content, code, research (default) |\n| **Haiku** | Only script runners where quality doesn''t matter |\n\n## Memory Limits\n\n### Root Cause Fix (REQUIRED)\n\nAdd to `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`:\n```bash\nexport NODE_OPTIONS=\"--max-old-space-size=16384\"\n```\n\nIncreases Node.js heap from 4GB to 16GB.\n\n### Parallel Limits (Even With Fix)\n\n| Agent Type | Max Parallel | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|-------|\n| Any agents | 2-3 | Context accumulates; batch then pause |\n| Heavy creative (Opus) | 1-2 | Uses more memory |\n\n### Recovery\n\n1. `source ~/.bashrc` or restart terminal\n2. `NODE_OPTIONS=\"--max-old-space-size=16384\" claude`\n3. Check what files exist, continue from there\n\n## Sub-Agent vs Remote API\n\n**Always prefer Task sub-agents over remote API calls.**\n\n| Aspect | Remote API Call | Task Sub-Agent |\n|--------|-----------------|----------------|\n| Tool access | None | Full (Read, Grep, Write, Bash) |\n| File reading | Must pass all content in prompt | Can read files iteratively |\n| Cross-referencing | Single context window | Can reason across documents |\n| Decision quality | Generic suggestions | Specific decisions with rationale |\n| Output quality | ~100 lines typical | 600+ lines with specifics |\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Remote API call\nconst response = await fetch(''https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages'', {...})\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Use Task tool\n// Invoke Task with subagent_type: \"general-purpose\"\n```\n\n## Declarative Over Imperative\n\nDescribe **what** to accomplish, not **how** to use tools.\n\n### Wrong (Imperative)\n\n```markdown\n### Check for placeholders\n```bash\ngrep -r \"PLACEHOLDER:\" build/*.html\n```\n```\n\n### Right (Declarative)\n\n```markdown\n### Check for placeholders\nSearch all HTML files in build/ for:\n- PLACEHOLDER: comments\n- TODO or TBD markers\n- Template brackets like [Client Name]\n\nAny match = incomplete content.\n```\n\n### What to Include\n\n| Include | Skip |\n|---------|------|\n| Task goal and context | Explicit bash/tool commands |\n| Input file paths | \"Use X tool to...\" |\n| Output file paths and format | Step-by-step tool invocations |\n| Success/failure criteria | Shell pipeline syntax |\n| Blocking checks (prerequisites) | Micromanaged workflows |\n| Quality checklists | |\n\n## Self-Documentation Principle\n\n> \"Agents that won''t have your context must be able to reproduce the behaviour independently.\"\n\nEvery improvement must be encoded into the agent''s prompt, not left as implicit knowledge.\n\n### What to Encode\n\n| Discovery | Where to Capture |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| Bug fix pattern | Agent''s \"Corrections\" or \"Common Issues\" section |\n| Quality requirement | Agent''s \"Quality Checklist\" section |\n| File path convention | Agent''s \"Output\" section |\n| Tool usage pattern | Agent''s \"Process\" section |\n| Blocking prerequisite | Agent''s \"Blocking Check\" section |\n\n### Test: Would a Fresh Agent Succeed?\n\nBefore completing any agent improvement:\n1. Read the agent prompt as if you have no context\n2. Ask: Could a new session follow this and produce the same quality?\n3. If no: Add missing instructions, patterns, or references\n\n### Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why It Fails |\n|--------------|--------------|\n| \"As we discussed earlier...\" | No prior context exists |\n| Relying on files read during dev | Agent may not read same files |\n| Assuming knowledge from errors | Agent won''t see your debugging |\n| \"Just like the home page\" | Agent hasn''t built home page |\n\n## Flexibility vs Rigidity\n\nMatch specification level to task type. Over-specifying flexible agents makes them brittle.\n\n| Task Type | Specification Level | Example |\n|-----------|---------------------|---------|\n| **Mechanical/repetitive** | High (rigid steps) | Version checker, file copier |\n| **Judgment-based** | Low (guidelines) | Docs auditor, code reviewer |\n| **Creative** | Minimal (goals only) | Content writer, brainstormer |\n\n### Signs You''ve Over-Specified\n\n- Agent fills in template sections with \"N/A\"\n- Agent tries to complete all phases even when irrelevant\n- Scoring systems produce meaningless numbers\n- Agent fails when scope doesn''t match assumptions\n- Long agents (>150 lines) for simple tasks\n\n### Flexible Agent Guidelines\n\n**DO:**\n- Describe *what to look for*, not exact steps\n- Provide output *examples*, not rigid templates\n- Include scope control (\"if >30 items, ask user\")\n- Give escape hatches (\"if unsure, flag for review\")\n- Keep under 100 lines for judgment tasks\n\n**DON''T:**\n- Require filling every section of a template\n- Create elaborate weighted scoring systems\n- List every possible check exhaustively\n- Assume scope without asking\n\n### Example: Docs Auditor\n\n**Over-specified (bad):**\n```markdown\n## Phase 1: Discovery\nExecute Glob for all .md files...\n\n## Phase 6: Generate Report\n| Category | Weight | Score | Weighted |\n|----------|--------|-------|----------|\n| Links    | 20%    | X/100 | X        |\n```\n\n**Right-sized (good):**\n```markdown\n## What to Check\n- TODOs, broken links, stale versions\n\n## Output Format\nList issues by severity. Include file:line and fix.\n\n## Scope Control\nIf >30 files, ask user which to focus on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent Prompt Structure\n\nEffective agent prompts include:\n\n```markdown\n## Your Role\n[What the agent does]\n\n## Blocking Check\n[Prerequisites that must exist]\n\n## Input\n[What files to read]\n\n## Process\n[Step-by-step with encoded learnings]\n\n## Output\n[Exact file paths and formats]\n\n## Quality Checklist\n[Verification steps including learned gotchas]\n\n## Common Issues\n[Patterns discovered during development]\n```\n\n## Pipeline Agents\n\nWhen inserting a new agent into a numbered pipeline (e.g., `HTML-01` → `HTML-05` → `HTML-11`):\n\n| Must Update | What |\n|-------------|------|\n| New agent | \"Workflow Position\" diagram + \"Next\" field |\n| **Predecessor agent** | Its \"Next\" field to point to new agent |\n\n**Common bug**: New agent is \"orphaned\" because predecessor still points to old next agent.\n\n**Verification**:\n```bash\ngrep -n \"Next:.*→\\|Then.*runs next\" .claude/agents/*.md\n```\n\n## The Sweet Spot\n\n**Best use case**: Tasks that are **repetitive but require judgment**.\n\nExample: Auditing 70 skills manually = tedious. But each audit needs intelligence (check docs, compare versions, decide what to fix). Perfect for parallel agents with clear instructions.\n\n**Not good for**:\n- Simple tasks (just do them)\n- Highly creative tasks (need human direction)\n- Tasks requiring cross-file coordination (agents work independently)\n\n## Effective Prompt Template\n\n```\nFor each [item]:\n1. Read [source file]\n2. Verify with [external check - npm view, API call, etc.]\n3. Check [authoritative source]\n4. Score/evaluate\n5. FIX issues found ← Critical instruction\n```\n\n**Key elements**:\n- **\"FIX issues found\"** - Without this, agents only report. With it, they take action.\n- **Exact file paths** - Prevents ambiguity\n- **Output format template** - Ensures consistent, parseable reports\n- **Batch size ~5 items** - Enough work to be efficient, not so much that failures cascade\n\n## Workflow Pattern\n\n```\n1. ME: Launch 2-3 parallel agents with identical prompt, different item lists\n2. AGENTS: Work in parallel (read → verify → check → edit → report)\n3. AGENTS: Return structured reports (score, status, fixes applied, files modified)\n4. ME: Review changes (git status, spot-check diffs)\n5. ME: Commit in batches with meaningful changelog\n6. ME: Push and update progress tracking\n```\n\n**Why agents don''t commit**: Allows human review, batching, and clean commit history.\n\n## Signs a Task Fits This Pattern\n\n**Good fit**:\n- Same steps repeated for many items\n- Each item requires judgment (not just transformation)\n- Items are independent (no cross-item dependencies)\n- Clear success criteria (score, pass/fail, etc.)\n- Authoritative source exists to verify against\n\n**Bad fit**:\n- Items depend on each other''s results\n- Requires creative/subjective decisions\n- Single complex task (use regular agent instead)\n- Needs human input mid-process\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Agent Frontmatter Template\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: my-agent\ndescription: |\n  [Role] specialist. MUST BE USED when [triggers].\n  Use PROACTIVELY for [task category].\n  Keywords: [trigger words]\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, Bash\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n```\n\n### Fix Bash Approval Spam\n\n1. Remove Bash from tools if not needed\n2. Put critical instructions FIRST (right after frontmatter)\n3. Use allowlists in `.claude/settings.json`\n\n### Memory Crash Recovery\n\n```bash\nexport NODE_OPTIONS=\"--max-old-space-size=16384\"\nsource ~/.bashrc && claude\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:25:00.954Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Full Stack Developer Agents requiring advanced Claude Code CLI integrations with Cloudflare, React, and Tailwind v4.","zh":"适合需要高级 Claude Code CLI 集成的全栈开发者代理，包括 Cloudflare、React 和 Tailwind v4。","ja":"Cloudflare、React、Tailwind v4 との高度な Claude Code CLI 統合を必要とするフルスタック開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Cloudflare, React 및 Tailwind v4와의 고급 Claude Code CLI 통합을 필요로 하는 풀스택 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollador de Pilas Completa que requieren integraciones avanzadas de Claude Code CLI con Cloudflare, React y Tailwind v4.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développeur full-stack nécessitant des intégrations avancées de Claude Code CLI avec Cloudflare, React et Tailwind v4.","de":"Ideal für Full-Stack-Entwickler-Agenten, die erweiterte Claude Code CLI-Integrationen mit Cloudflare, React und Tailwind v4 benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvedor Full Stack que exigem integrações avançadas do Claude Code CLI com Cloudflare, React e Tailwind v4.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack Developer, требующих расширенных интеграций с Claude Code CLI, Cloudflare, React и Tailwind v4.","ar":"مثالي لعميل وكلاء تطوير الويب الكامل الذين يتطلبون تكاملات متقدمة لوصف Claude Code CLI مع Cloudflare و React و Tailwind v4."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build custom solutions with proper delegation, tool access, and prompt design using YAML, leveraging tools like Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, and Bash, and integrating with AI services.","zh":"赋予代理构建自定义解决方案的能力，具有适当的委托、工具访问和提示设计，使用 YAML，並利用诸如 Read、Write、Edit、Glob、Grep 和 Bash 等工具，并与 AI 服务集成。","ja":"YAML を使用して、Read、Write、Edit、Glob、Grep、Bash などのツールを利用し、AI サービスと統合することで、代理がカスタム ソリューションを構築し、適切な委任、ツール アクセス、プロンプト デザインを行うことができます。","ko":"YAML을 사용하여 Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep 및 Bash와 같은 도구를 활용하고 AI 서비스와 통합하여 에이전트가 맞춤형 솔루션을 구축하고 적절한 위임, 도구 액세스 및 프롬프트 디자인을 수행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir soluciones personalizadas con una delegación adecuada, acceso a herramientas y diseño de instrucciones utilizando YAML, aprovechando herramientas como Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep y Bash, e integrándose con servicios de inteligencia artificial.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des solutions personnalisées avec une délégation appropriée, un accès aux outils et une conception d''instructions en utilisant YAML, en exploitant des outils tels que Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep et Bash, et en s''intégrant avec des services d''intelligence artificielle.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, benutzerdefinierte Lösungen mit ordnungsgemäßer Delegation, Werkzeugzugriff und Prompt-Design unter Verwendung von YAML zu erstellen, indem es Tools wie Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep und Bash nutzt und sich in AI-Dienste integriert.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem soluções personalizadas com delegação adequada, acesso a ferramentas e design de prompt usando YAML, aproveitando ferramentas como Ler, Escrever, Editar, Glob, Grep e Bash, e integrando com serviços de IA.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать индивидуальные решения с правильной делегацией, доступом к инструментам и разработкой промпта с использованием YAML, используя инструменты như Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep и Bash, и интегрируя с сервисами ИИ.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء من إنشاء حلول مخصصة مع تفويض مناسب ووصول إلى أدوات وتصميم مؤشر باستخدام YAML، واستخدام أدوات مثل قراءة وكتابة وتحرير و Glob و Grep و Bash، وتكاملها مع خدمات الذكاء الاصطناعي."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing effective agent description patterns for automatic task delegation","Developing strong trigger patterns for proactive task execution","Building custom agents with Cloudflare, React, and Tailwind v4 integrations"],"zh":["为自动任务委托设计有效的代理描述模式","开发强大的触发模式以实现主动任务执行","使用 Cloudflare、React 和 Tailwind v4 集成构建自定义代理"],"ja":["自動タスク委任のための効果的なエージェント記述パターンを設計する","能動的なタスク実行のための強力なトリガーパターンを開発する","Cloudflare、React、Tailwind v4 統合を使用してカスタム エージェントを構築する"],"ko":["자동 작업 위임을 위한 효과적인 에이전트 설명 패턴 설계","능동적인 작업 실행을 위한 강력한 트리거 패턴 개발","Cloudflare, React 및 Tailwind v4 통합을 사용하여 맞춤형 에이전트 구축"],"es":["Diseñar patrones de descripción de agentes efectivos para la delegación automática de tareas","Desarrollar patrones de activación sólidos para la ejecución proactiva de tareas","Crear agentes personalizados con integraciones de Cloudflare, React y Tailwind v4"],"fr":["Concevoir des modèles de description d''agents efficaces pour la délégation automatique de tâches","Développer des modèles de déclenchement solides pour l''exécution proactive de tâches","Créer des agents personnalisés avec des intégrations de Cloudflare, React et Tailwind v4"],"de":["Entwerfen effektiver Agenten-Beschreibungs-Muster für die automatische Aufgabendelegation","Entwickeln starker Auslöser-Muster für die proaktive Aufgaben-Ausführung","Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Agenten mit Cloudflare-, React- und Tailwind-v4-Integrationen"],"pt":["Desenvolver padrões de descrição de agente eficazes para delegação automática de tarefas","Desenvolver padrões de gatilho fortes para execução proativa de tarefas","Construir agentes personalizados com integrações Cloudflare, React e Tailwind v4"],"ru":["Разработать эффективные шаблоны описания агентов для автоматической делегации задач","Разработать сильные шаблоны триггеров для проактивной выполнения задач","Создать индивидуальных агентов с интеграциями Cloudflare, React и Tailwind v4"],"ar":["تصميم أنماط وصف وكلاء فعّالة للتفويض التلقائي للمهام","تطوير أنماط هادفة قوية للتنفيذ الفعّال للمهام","بناء وكلاء مخصصين مع دمج Cloudflare و React و Tailwind v4"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code CLI setup"," YAML formatting knowledge necessary","Cloudflare, React, and Tailwind v4 compatibility required"],"zh":["需要 Claude Code CLI 设置","需要 YAML 格式知识","需要 Cloudflare、React 和 Tailwind v4 兼容性"],"ja":["Claude Code CLI の設定が必要","YAML フォーマットの知識が必要","Cloudflare、React、Tailwind v4 との互換性が必要"],"ko":["Claude Code CLI 설정이 필요합니다.","YAML 형식 지식이 필요합니다.","Cloudflare, React 및 Tailwind v4와의 호환성이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere configuración de Claude Code CLI","Conocimiento de formato YAML necesario","Compatibilidad con Cloudflare, React y Tailwind v4 requerida"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Claude Code CLI","Connaissances de formatage YAML nécessaires","Compatibilité avec Cloudflare, React et Tailwind v4 requise"],"de":["Erfordert Claude Code CLI-Setup","YAML-Formatierkenntnisse erforderlich","Cloudflare-, React- und Tailwind-v4-Kompatibilität erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige configuração do Claude Code CLI","Conhecimento de formatação YAML necessário","Compatibilidade com Cloudflare, React e Tailwind v4 exigida"],"ru":["Требует настройки Claude Code CLI","Необходимо знание форматирования YAML","Требуется совместимость с Cloudflare, React и Tailwind v4"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد وصف Claude Code CLI","معرفة تنسيق YAML ضرورية","متطلبات توافق Cloudflare و React و Tailwind v4"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
