ntwurfs- und Fehlerbehebungsleitfaden","pt":"Desenvolvimento Concorrente em Rust","ru":"Параллельное программирование в Rust","ar":"التطوير المتوازي في Rust","en":"m07-concurrency"},"description":{"zh":"Rust 并发性开发涉及选择合适的并发原语，考虑工作负载类型、数据共享和线程安全性","ja":"Rust 並行性開発では、適切な並行性原語を選択し、ワークロードの種類、データ共有、スレッドセーフティを考慮","ko":"Rust 동시성 개발은 적절한 동시성 원시를 선택하고 작업 유형, 데이터 공유, 스레드 안전성을 고려하는 것을 포함","es":"Concurrencia en Rust: Guía de diseño y resolución de errores. Aprende a identificar el tipo de carga de trabajo y a elegir los primitivos de concurrencia ade...","fr":"Concurrence en Rust : Guide de conception et de résolution d''erreurs. Apprenez à identifier le type de charge de travail et à choisir les primitifs de concur...","de":"Konkurrenz in Rust: Entwurfs- und Fehlerbehebungsleitfaden. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie den Arbeitslastentyp identifizieren und die geeigneten Konkurrenzprimitiven...","pt":"O sistema de assistência de desenvolvedor Rust para concorrência ajuda a determinar se um problema é limitado por CPU ou E/S e quais primitivas usar","ru":"Система помощи разработчику Rust для параллельного программирования помогает определить, является ли проблема ограничена CPU или вводом/выводом, и какие прим...","ar":"نظام مساعدة مطور Rust للتطوير المتوازي يساعد في تحديد ما إذا كان هناك problém محدود بالموارد الحاسوبية أو الإدخال/الإخراج وما هي البدائيات التي يجب استخدامها","en":"Rust Developer AI Assistance System — Meta-Problem-Driven Knowledge Indexing"},"definition":{"en":"Rust Developer AI Assistance System — Meta-Problem-Driven Knowledge Indexing"},"features":{"zh":["区分CPU-bound和I/O-bound工作负载","选择合适的并发原语","考虑数据共享和线程安全性","处理Send和Sync错误","优化程序性能和响应速度"],"ja":["CPUバウンドとI/Oバウンドのワークロードを区別","適切な並行性原語を選択","データ共有とスレッドセーフティを考慮","SendとSyncエラーを処理","プログラムのパフォーマンスとレスポンスを最適化"],"ko":["CPU 바운드와 I/O 바운드 작업을 구분","적절한 동시성 원시를 선택","데이터 공유와 스레드 안전성을 고려","Send와 Sync 에러를 처리","프로그램의 성능과 응답성을 최적화"],"es":["Identificación del tipo de carga de trabajo","Elección de primitivos de concurrencia adecuados","Resolución de errores comunes","Mejora del rendimiento y la eficiencia","Diseño de sistemas concurrentes escalables"],"fr":["Identification du type de charge de travail","Choix de primitifs de concurrence appropriés","Résolution d''erreurs courantes","Amélioration des performances et de l''efficacité","Conception de systèmes concurrents évolutifs"],"de":["Identifizierung des Arbeitslastentyps","Auswahl geeigneter Konkurrenzprimitiven","Behebung häufiger Fehler","Verbesserung der Leistung und Effizienz","Entwurf von skalierbaren Konkurrenzsystemen"],"pt":["Determinação do tipo de carga de trabalho","Escolha de primitivas de concorrência","Gerenciamento de segurança de thread","Otimização de desempenho","Resolução de erros comuns"],"ru":["Определение типа рабочей нагрузки","Выбор примитивов параллельного программирования","Управление безопасностью потоков","Оптимизация производительности","Решение общих ошибок"],"ar":["تحديد نوع الحمل العمل","اختيار البدائيات المتوازية","إدارة أمان الخيط","تحسين الأداء","حل الأخطاء الشائعة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust 并发性","CPU-bound","I/O-bound","数据共享","线程安全性","Send","Sync","并发原语"],"ja":["Rust 並行性","CPUバウンド","I/Oバウンド","データ共有","スレッドセーフティ","Send","Sync","並行性原語"],"ko":["Rust 동시성","CPU 바운드","I/O 바운드","데이터 공유","스레드 안전성","Send","Sync","동시성 원시"],"es":["concurrencia en Rust","diseño de concurrencia","resolución de errores","primitivos de concurrencia","rendimiento y eficiencia","sistemas concurrentes"],"fr":["concurrence en Rust","conception de concurrence","résolution d''erreurs","primitifs de concurrence","performances et efficacité","systèmes concurrents"],"de":["Konkurrenz in Rust","Entwurf von Konkurrenz","Fehlerbehebung","Konkurrenzprimitiven","Leistung und Effizienz","Konkurrenzsysteme"],"pt":["concorrência em Rust","desenvolvimento concorrente","primitivas de concorrência","segurança de thread","otimização de desempenho","Rust para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["параллельное программирование в Rust","параллельное развитие","примитивы параллельного программирования","безопасность потоков","оптимизация производительности","Rust для разработчиков"],"ar":["التطوير المتوازي في Rust","التطوير المتوازي","البدائيات المتوازية","أمان الخيط","تحسين الأداء","Rust للمطورين"]}},"owner":"actionbook","repo":"rust-skills","repoPath":"actionbook/rust-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.396Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m07-concurrency","description":"CRITICAL: Use for concurrency/async. Triggers: E0277 Send Sync, cannot be sent between threads, thread, spawn, channel, mpsc, Mutex, RwLock, Atomic, async, await, Future, tokio, deadlock, race condition, 并发, 线程, 异步, 死锁","bodyPreview":"# Concurrency\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Is this CPU-bound or I/O-bound, and what''s the sharing model?**\n\nBefore choosing concurrency primitives:\n- What''s the workload type?\n- What data needs to be shared?\n- What''s the thread safety requirement?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 Send | \"Add Send bound\" | Should this type cross threads? |\n| E0277 Sync | \"Wrap in Mutex\" | Is share","body":"# Concurrency\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Is this CPU-bound or I/O-bound, and what''s the sharing model?**\n\nBefore choosing concurrency primitives:\n- What''s the workload type?\n- What data needs to be shared?\n- What''s the thread safety requirement?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 Send | \"Add Send bound\" | Should this type cross threads? |\n| E0277 Sync | \"Wrap in Mutex\" | Is shared access really needed? |\n| Future not Send | \"Use spawn_local\" | Is async the right choice? |\n| Deadlock | \"Reorder locks\" | Is the locking design correct? |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore adding concurrency:\n\n1. **What''s the workload?**\n   - CPU-bound → threads (std::thread, rayon)\n   - I/O-bound → async (tokio, async-std)\n   - Mixed → hybrid approach\n\n2. **What''s the sharing model?**\n   - No sharing → message passing (channels)\n   - Immutable sharing → Arc<T>\n   - Mutable sharing → Arc<Mutex<T>> or Arc<RwLock<T>>\n\n3. **What are the Send/Sync requirements?**\n   - Cross-thread ownership → Send\n   - Cross-thread references → Sync\n   - Single-thread async → spawn_local\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑ (MANDATORY)\n\n**CRITICAL**: Don''t just fix the error. Trace UP to find domain constraints.\n\n### Domain Detection Table\n\n| Context Keywords | Load Domain Skill | Key Constraint |\n|-----------------|-------------------|----------------|\n| Web API, HTTP, axum, actix, handler | **domain-web** | Handlers run on any thread |\n| 交易, 支付, trading, payment | **domain-fintech** | Audit + thread safety |\n| gRPC, kubernetes, microservice | **domain-cloud-native** | Distributed tracing |\n| CLI, terminal, clap | **domain-cli** | Usually single-thread OK |\n\n### Example: Web API + Rc Error\n\n```\n\"Rc cannot be sent between threads\" in Web API context\n    ↑ DETECT: \"Web API\" → Load domain-web\n    ↑ FIND: domain-web says \"Shared state must be thread-safe\"\n    ↑ FIND: domain-web says \"Rc in state\" is Common Mistake\n    ↓ DESIGN: Use Arc<T> with State extractor\n    ↓ IMPL: axum::extract::State<Arc<AppConfig>>\n```\n\n### Generic Trace\n\n```\n\"Send not satisfied for my type\"\n    ↑ Ask: What domain is this? Load domain-* skill\n    ↑ Ask: Does this type need to cross thread boundaries?\n    ↑ Check: m09-domain (is the data model correct?)\n```\n\n| Situation | Trace To | Question |\n|-----------|----------|----------|\n| Send/Sync in Web | **domain-web** | What''s the state management pattern? |\n| Send/Sync in CLI | **domain-cli** | Is multi-thread really needed? |\n| Mutex vs channels | m09-domain | Shared state or message passing? |\n| Async vs threads | m10-performance | What''s the workload profile? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nFrom design to implementation:\n\n```\n\"Need parallelism for CPU work\"\n    ↓ Use: std::thread or rayon\n\n\"Need concurrency for I/O\"\n    ↓ Use: async/await with tokio\n\n\"Need to share immutable data across threads\"\n    ↓ Use: Arc<T>\n\n\"Need to share mutable data across threads\"\n    ↓ Use: Arc<Mutex<T>> or Arc<RwLock<T>>\n    ↓ Or: channels for message passing\n\n\"Need simple atomic operations\"\n    ↓ Use: AtomicBool, AtomicUsize, etc.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Send/Sync Markers\n\n| Marker | Meaning | Example |\n|--------|---------|---------|\n| `Send` | Can transfer ownership between threads | Most types |\n| `Sync` | Can share references between threads | `Arc<T>` |\n| `!Send` | Must stay on one thread | `Rc<T>` |\n| `!Sync` | No shared refs across threads | `RefCell<T>` |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Thread-Safe | Blocking | Use When |\n|---------|-------------|----------|----------|\n| `std::thread` | Yes | Yes | CPU-bound parallelism |\n| `async/await` | Yes | No | I/O-bound concurrency |\n| `Mutex<T>` | Yes | Yes | Shared mutable state |\n| `RwLock<T>` | Yes | Yes | Read-heavy shared state |\n| `mpsc::channel` | Yes | Optional | Message passing |\n| `Arc<Mutex<T>>` | Yes | Yes | Shared mutable across threads |\n\n## Decision Flowchart\n\n```\nWhat type of work?\n├─ CPU-bound → std::thread or rayon\n├─ I/O-bound → async/await\n└─ Mixed → hybrid (spawn_blocking)\n\nNeed to share data?\n├─ No → message passing (channels)\n├─ Immutable → Arc<T>\n└─ Mutable →\n   ├─ Read-heavy → Arc<RwLock<T>>\n   └─ Write-heavy → Arc<Mutex<T>>\n   └─ Simple counter → AtomicUsize\n\nAsync context?\n├─ Type is Send → tokio::spawn\n├─ Type is !Send → spawn_local\n└─ Blocking code → spawn_blocking\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Errors\n\n| Error | Cause | Fix |\n|-------|-------|-----|\n| E0277 `Send` not satisfied | Non-Send in async | Use Arc or spawn_local |\n| E0277 `Sync` not satisfied | Non-Sync shared | Wrap with Mutex |\n| Deadlock | Lock ordering | Consistent lock order |\n| `future is not Send` | Non-Send across await | Drop before await |\n| `MutexGuard` across await | Guard held during suspend | Scope guard properly |\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| Arc<Mutex<T>> everywhere | Contention, complexity | Message passing |\n| thread::sleep in async | Blocks executor | tokio::time::sleep |\n| Holding locks across await | Blocks other tasks | Scope locks tightly |\n| Ignoring deadlock risk | Hard to debug | Lock ordering, try_lock |\n\n---\n\n## Async-Specific Patterns\n\n### Avoid MutexGuard Across Await\n\n```rust\n// Bad: guard held across await\nlet guard = mutex.lock().await;\ndo_async().await;  // guard still held!\n\n// Good: scope the lock\n{\n    let guard = mutex.lock().await;\n    // use guard\n}  // guard dropped\ndo_async().await;\n```\n\n### Non-Send Types in Async\n\n```rust\n// Rc is !Send, can''t cross await in spawned task\n// Option 1: use Arc instead\n// Option 2: use spawn_local (single-thread runtime)\n// Option 3: ensure Rc is dropped before .await\n```\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Smart pointer choice | m02-resource |\n| Interior mutability | m03-mutability |\n| Performance tuning | m10-performance |\n| Domain concurrency needs | domain-* |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:24:44.038Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust Developer AI Agents needing advanced concurrency control and thread safety management.","zh":"非常适合需要高级并发控制和线程安全管理的Rust开发者AI代理。","ja":"Rust開発者向けの高級な並行性制御とスレッドセーフティ管理が必要なAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 병렬성 제어 및 스레드 안전성 관리가 필요한 Rust 개발자 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de inteligencia artificial de Rust que necesitan un control de concurrencia avanzado y una gestión de seguridad de subprocesos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle de Rust qui nécessitent un contrôle de concurrence avancé et une gestion de sécurité de threads.","de":"Perfekt für Rust-Entwickler-KI-Agents, die erweiterte Konkurrenzkontrolle und Thread-Sicherheitsverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA de Desenvolvedores Rust que necessitam de controle de concorrência avançado e gerenciamento de segurança de thread.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ-разработчиков Rust, которым требуется продвинутый контроль согласованности и управление безопасностью потоков.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوكيل الذكي لمطوري روست الذين يحتاجون إلى تحكم متقدم في التزامن وإدارة سلامة الخيط."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to determine workload types, identify shared data, and apply appropriate concurrency primitives, ensuring thread safety and efficient execution, all while handling errors like E0277 Send and Sync by applying Send bounds and Mutex wrapping.","zh":"赋予代理人确定工作负载类型、识别共享数据并应用适当的并发原语的能力，确保线程安全和高效执行，同时通过应用Send边界和Mutex包装来处理E0277 Send和Sync等错误。","ja":"エージェントがワークロードの種類を決定し、共有データを識別し、適切な並行性プリミティブを適用してスレッドセーフティと効率的な実行を保証する能力を付与し、Send境界とMutexラッピングを適用してE0277 SendとSyncなどのエラーを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 작업 부하 유형을 결정하고 공유 데이터를 식별하고 적절한 병렬성 원시값을 적용하여 스레드 안전성과 효율적인 실행을 보장하는 기능을 부여하며 Send 경계와 Mutex 래핑을 적용하여 E0277 Send 및 Sync와 같은 오류를 처리합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes determinar los tipos de cargas de trabajo, identificar datos compartidos y aplicar primitivas de concurrencia adecuadas, garantizando la seguridad de los threads y una ejecución eficiente, todo mientras se manejan errores como E0277 Send y Sync aplicando límites Send y envoltura Mutex.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déterminer les types de charges de travail, d''identifier les données partagées et d''appliquer des primitives de concurrence appropriées, garantissant la sécurité des threads et une exécution efficace, tout en gérant les erreurs comme E0277 Send et Sync en appliquant des limites Send et un emballage Mutex.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Workload-Typen zu bestimmen, gemeinsame Daten zu identifizieren und geeignete Konkurrenzsprimitiven anzuwenden, wodurch Thread-Sicherheit und effiziente Ausführung gewährleistet werden, während Fehler wie E0277 Send und Sync durch Anwenden von Send-Grenzen und Mutex-Verpackung behandelt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a determinar os tipos de carga de trabalho, identificar dados compartilhados e aplicar primitivas de concorrência apropriadas, garantindo a segurança do thread e a execução eficiente, tudo isso lidando com erros como E0277 Send e Sync aplicando limites Send e envoltório Mutex.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью определять типы рабочей нагрузки, выявлять общие данные и применять соответствующие примитивы согласованности, обеспечивая безопасность потоков и эффективное выполнение, все это при обработке ошибок, таких как E0277 Send и Sync, путем применения ограничений Send и обертывания Mutex.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحديد أنواع حمولة العمل، وتحديد البيانات المشتركة، وتطبيق البدائيات المناسبة للتزامن، مما يضمن سلامة الخيط والتنفيذ الفعال، مع التعامل مع الأخطاء مثل E0277 Send و Sync من خلال تطبيق حدود الإرسال وغلاف Mutex."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging concurrency-related errors like E0277","Choosing optimal concurrency primitives for CPU-bound or I/O-bound workloads","Ensuring thread safety for shared data in Rust applications"],"zh":["调试与并发性相关的错误，如E0277","为CPU绑定或I/O绑定的工作负载选择最优的并发原语","确保Rust应用程序中共享数据的线程安全性"],"ja":["E0277などの並行性関連のエラーをデバッグする","CPUバウンドまたはI/Oバウンドのワークロードに最適な並行性プリミティブを選択する","Rustアプリケーションで共有データのスレッドセーフティを確保する"],"ko":["E0277과 같은 병렬성 관련 오류를 디버깅하는 것","CPU 바운드 또는 I/O 바운드 작업 부하에 최적의 병렬성 원시값을 선택하는 것","Rust 애플리케이션에서 공유 데이터의 스레드 안전성을 보장하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de errores relacionados con la concurrencia como E0277","Elección de primitivas de concurrencia óptimas para cargas de trabajo limitadas por CPU o E/S","Garantizar la seguridad de los threads para datos compartidos en aplicaciones de Rust"],"fr":["Débogage des erreurs liées à la concurrence comme E0277","Choix de primitives de concurrence optimales pour les charges de travail limitées par le CPU ou l''E/S","Assurer la sécurité des threads pour les données partagées dans les applications Rust"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Konkurrenzfehlern wie E0277","Auswahl optimaler Konkurrenzsprimitiven für CPU- oder E/A-begrenzte Workloads","Sicherstellung der Thread-Sicherheit für gemeinsame Daten in Rust-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Depuração de erros relacionados à concorrência, como E0277","Escolha de primitivas de concorrência ótimas para cargas de trabalho limitadas por CPU ou E/S","Garantia de segurança de thread para dados compartilhados em aplicações Rust"],"ru":["Отладка ошибок, связанных с согласованностью, таких как E0277","Выбор оптимальных примитивов согласованности для рабочих нагрузок, ограниченных CPU или вводом/выводом","Обеспечение безопасности потоков для общих данных в приложениях Rust"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء متعلقة بالتزامن مثل E0277","اختيار البدائيات المثالية للتزامن لتحميل العمل المحدد بواسطة وحدة المعالجة المركزية أو الإدخال/الإخراج","ضمان سلامة الخيط للبيانات المشتركة في تطبيقات روست"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Rust language mechanics","Limited to Rust programming language","Needs consideration of thread safety requirements"],"zh":["需要理解Rust语言机制","仅限Rust编程语言","需要考虑线程安全性要求"],"ja":["Rust言語のメカニズムを理解する必要がある","Rustプログラミング言語に限定される","スレッドセーフティの要件を考慮する必要がある"],"ko":["Rust 언어 메커니즘을 이해해야 함","Rust 프로그래밍 언어에만 국한됨","스레드 안전성 요구 사항을 고려해야 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los mecanismos del lenguaje Rust","Limitado al lenguaje de programación Rust","Requiere consideración de los requisitos de seguridad de los threads"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des mécanismes du langage Rust","Limité au langage de programmation Rust","Nécessite une prise en compte des exigences de sécurité des threads"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der Rust-Sprachmechanik","Begrenzt auf die Rust-Programmiersprache","Benötigt Berücksichtigung der Thread-Sicherheitsanforderungen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos mecanismos de linguagem Rust","Limitado à linguagem de programação Rust","Necessita consideração dos requisitos de segurança do thread"],"ru":["Требует понимания механизмов языка Rust","Ограничен языком программирования Rust","Требует учета требований безопасности потоков"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم ميكانيكا لغة روست","محدود بلغة برمجة روست","يحتاج إلى مراعاة متطلبات سلامة الخيط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
