写测试脚本","提高开发效率","减少维护成本"],"ja":["構造化ログ","リアルタイムモニタリング","テストスクリプトの作成不要","開発効率の向上","メンテナンスコストの削減"],"ko":["구조화된 로그","실시간 모니터링","테스트 스크립트 작성 필요 없음","개발 효율성 향상","유지 보수 비용 절감"],"es":["Registros estructurados","Monitoreo en tiempo real","Análisis de logs AI","Detección automática de problemas","Desarrollo de aplicaciones AI-nativas"],"fr":["Journaux structurés","Monitoring en temps réel","Analyse de logs AI","Détection automatique de problèmes","Développement d''applications AI-natives"],"de":["Strukturierte Protokolle","Echtzeit-Überwachung","AI-Log-Analyse","Automatische Problemerkennung","Entwicklung von AI-nativen Anwendungen"],"pt":["Logs estruturados","Monitoramento em tempo real","Análise de logs por IA","Detecção automática de problemas","Desenvolvimento de QA sem scripts"],"ru":["Структурированные логи","Мониторинг в реальном времени","Анализ логов с помощью ИИ","Автоматическое обнаружение проблем","Разработка QA без скриптов"],"ar":["سجلات منظمة","مراقبة في الوقت الفعلي","تحليل السجلات بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي","اكتشاف تلقائي للمشاكل","تطوير QA بدون سكريبتات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["零脚本QA","AI原生开发","PDCA方法","结构化日志","实时监控","开发效率","维护成本"],"ja":["ゼロスクリプトQA","AIネイティブ開発","PDCA手法","構造化ログ","リアルタイムモニタリング","開発効率","メンテナンスコスト"],"ko":["제로 스크립트 QA","AI 네이티브 개발","PDCA 방법","구조화된 로그","실시간 모니터링","개발 효율성","유지 보수 비용"],"es":["Zero Script QA","pruebas de software","desarrollo de aplicaciones","AI nativa","registros estructurados","monitoreo en tiempo real"],"fr":["Zero Script QA","tests de logiciel","développement d''applications","AI native","journaux structurés","monitoring en temps réel"],"de":["Zero Script QA","Software-Tests","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","AI-nativ","strukturierte Protokolle","Echtzeit-Überwachung"],"pt":["Zero Script QA","desenvolvimento de QA","logs estruturados","monitoramento em tempo real","análise de logs por IA","detecção automática de problemas","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Zero Script QA","разработка QA","структурированные логи","мониторинг в реальном времени","анализ логов с помощью ИИ","автоматическое обнаружение проблем","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Zero Script QA","تطوير QA","سجلات منظمة","مراقبة في الوقت الفعلي","تحليل السجلات بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي","اكتشاف تلقائي للمشاكل","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"popup-studio-ai","repo":"bkit-claude-code","repoPath":"popup-studio-ai/bkit-claude-code","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.397Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zero-script-qa","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Zero Script QA Expert Knowledge\n\n## Overview\n\nZero Script QA is a methodology that verifies features through **structured logs** and **real-time monitoring** without writing test scripts.\n\n```\nTraditional: Write test code → Execute → Check results → Maintain\nZero Script: Build log infrastructure → Manual UX test → AI log analysis → Auto issue detection\n```\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Log Everything\n- All API calls (including 200 OK)\n- All errors\n- All important business events\n- Entire flow tr","body":"# Zero Script QA Expert Knowledge\n\n## Overview\n\nZero Script QA is a methodology that verifies features through **structured logs** and **real-time monitoring** without writing test scripts.\n\n```\nTraditional: Write test code → Execute → Check results → Maintain\nZero Script: Build log infrastructure → Manual UX test → AI log analysis → Auto issue detection\n```\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Log Everything\n- All API calls (including 200 OK)\n- All errors\n- All important business events\n- Entire flow trackable via Request ID\n\n### 2. Structured JSON Logs\n- Parseable JSON format\n- Consistent fields (timestamp, level, request_id, message, data)\n- Different log levels per environment\n\n### 3. Real-time Monitoring\n- Docker log streaming\n- Claude Code analyzes in real-time\n- Immediate issue detection and documentation\n\n---\n\n## Logging Architecture\n\n### JSON Log Format Standard\n\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-08T10:30:00.000Z\",\n  \"level\": \"INFO\",\n  \"service\": \"api\",\n  \"request_id\": \"req_abc123\",\n  \"message\": \"API Request completed\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"method\": \"POST\",\n    \"path\": \"/api/users\",\n    \"status\": 200,\n    \"duration_ms\": 45\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Required Log Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| timestamp | ISO 8601 | Time of occurrence |\n| level | string | DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR |\n| service | string | Service name (api, web, worker, etc.) |\n| request_id | string | Request tracking ID |\n| message | string | Log message |\n| data | object | Additional data (optional) |\n\n### Log Level Policy\n\n| Environment | Minimum Level | Purpose |\n|-------------|---------------|---------|\n| Local | DEBUG | Development and QA |\n| Staging | DEBUG | QA and integration testing |\n| Production | INFO | Operations monitoring |\n\n---\n\n## Request ID Propagation\n\n### Concept\n\n```\nClient → API Gateway → Backend → Database\n   ↓         ↓           ↓          ↓\nreq_abc   req_abc     req_abc    req_abc\n\nTrackable with same Request ID across all layers\n```\n\n### Implementation Patterns\n\n#### 1. Request ID Generation (Entry Point)\n```typescript\n// middleware.ts\nimport { v4 as uuidv4 } from ''uuid'';\n\nexport function generateRequestId(): string {\n  return `req_${uuidv4().slice(0, 8)}`;\n}\n\n// Propagate via header\nheaders[''X-Request-ID''] = requestId;\n```\n\n#### 2. Request ID Extraction and Propagation\n```typescript\n// API client\nconst requestId = headers[''X-Request-ID''] || generateRequestId();\n\n// Include in all logs\nlogger.info(''Processing request'', { request_id: requestId });\n\n// Include in header when calling downstream services\nawait fetch(url, {\n  headers: { ''X-Request-ID'': requestId }\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Backend Logging (FastAPI)\n\n### Logging Middleware\n\n```python\n# middleware/logging.py\nimport logging\nimport time\nimport uuid\nimport json\nfrom fastapi import Request\n\nclass JsonFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    def format(self, record):\n        log_record = {\n            \"timestamp\": self.formatTime(record),\n            \"level\": record.levelname,\n            \"service\": \"api\",\n            \"request_id\": getattr(record, ''request_id'', ''N/A''),\n            \"message\": record.getMessage(),\n        }\n        if hasattr(record, ''data''):\n            log_record[\"data\"] = record.data\n        return json.dumps(log_record)\n\nclass LoggingMiddleware:\n    async def __call__(self, request: Request, call_next):\n        request_id = request.headers.get(''X-Request-ID'', f''req_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}'')\n        request.state.request_id = request_id\n\n        start_time = time.time()\n\n        # Request logging\n        logger.info(\n            f\"Request started\",\n            extra={\n                ''request_id'': request_id,\n                ''data'': {\n                    ''method'': request.method,\n                    ''path'': request.url.path,\n                    ''query'': str(request.query_params)\n                }\n            }\n        )\n\n        response = await call_next(request)\n\n        duration = (time.time() - start_time) * 1000\n\n        # Response logging (including 200 OK!)\n        logger.info(\n            f\"Request completed\",\n            extra={\n                ''request_id'': request_id,\n                ''data'': {\n                    ''status'': response.status_code,\n                    ''duration_ms'': round(duration, 2)\n                }\n            }\n        )\n\n        response.headers[''X-Request-ID''] = request_id\n        return response\n```\n\n### Business Logic Logging\n\n```python\n# services/user_service.py\ndef create_user(data: dict, request_id: str):\n    logger.info(\"Creating user\", extra={\n        ''request_id'': request_id,\n        ''data'': {''email'': data[''email'']}\n    })\n\n    # Business logic\n    user = User(**data)\n    db.add(user)\n    db.commit()\n\n    logger.info(\"User created\", extra={\n        ''request_id'': request_id,\n        ''data'': {''user_id'': user.id}\n    })\n\n    return user\n```\n\n---\n\n## Frontend Logging (Next.js)\n\n### Logger Module\n\n```typescript\n// lib/logger.ts\ntype LogLevel = ''DEBUG'' | ''INFO'' | ''WARNING'' | ''ERROR'';\n\ninterface LogData {\n  request_id?: string;\n  [key: string]: any;\n}\n\nconst LOG_LEVELS: Record<LogLevel, number> = {\n  DEBUG: 0,\n  INFO: 1,\n  WARNING: 2,\n  ERROR: 3,\n};\n\nconst MIN_LEVEL = process.env.NODE_ENV === ''production'' ? ''INFO'' : ''DEBUG'';\n\nfunction log(level: LogLevel, message: string, data?: LogData) {\n  if (LOG_LEVELS[level] < LOG_LEVELS[MIN_LEVEL]) return;\n\n  const logEntry = {\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    level,\n    service: ''web'',\n    request_id: data?.request_id || ''N/A'',\n    message,\n    data: data ? { ...data, request_id: undefined } : undefined,\n  };\n\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(logEntry));\n}\n\nexport const logger = {\n  debug: (msg: string, data?: LogData) => log(''DEBUG'', msg, data),\n  info: (msg: string, data?: LogData) => log(''INFO'', msg, data),\n  warning: (msg: string, data?: LogData) => log(''WARNING'', msg, data),\n  error: (msg: string, data?: LogData) => log(''ERROR'', msg, data),\n};\n```\n\n### API Client Integration\n\n```typescript\n// lib/api-client.ts\nimport { logger } from ''./logger'';\nimport { v4 as uuidv4 } from ''uuid'';\n\nexport async function apiClient<T>(\n  endpoint: string,\n  options: RequestInit = {}\n): Promise<T> {\n  const requestId = `req_${uuidv4().slice(0, 8)}`;\n  const startTime = Date.now();\n\n  logger.info(''API Request started'', {\n    request_id: requestId,\n    method: options.method || ''GET'',\n    endpoint,\n  });\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api${endpoint}`, {\n      ...options,\n      headers: {\n        ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n        ''X-Request-ID'': requestId,\n        ...options.headers,\n      },\n    });\n\n    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;\n    const data = await response.json();\n\n    // Log 200 OK too!\n    logger.info(''API Request completed'', {\n      request_id: requestId,\n      status: response.status,\n      duration_ms: duration,\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      logger.error(''API Request failed'', {\n        request_id: requestId,\n        status: response.status,\n        error: data.error,\n      });\n      throw new ApiError(data.error);\n    }\n\n    return data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error(''API Request error'', {\n      request_id: requestId,\n      error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : ''Unknown error'',\n    });\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Nginx JSON Logging\n\n### nginx.conf Configuration\n\n```nginx\nhttp {\n    log_format json_combined escape=json ''{''\n        ''\"timestamp\":\"$time_iso8601\",''\n        ''\"level\":\"INFO\",''\n        ''\"service\":\"nginx\",''\n        ''\"request_id\":\"$http_x_request_id\",''\n        ''\"message\":\"HTTP Request\",''\n        ''\"data\":{''\n            ''\"remote_addr\":\"$remote_addr\",''\n            ''\"method\":\"$request_method\",''\n            ''\"uri\":\"$request_uri\",''\n            ''\"status\":$status,''\n            ''\"body_bytes_sent\":$body_bytes_sent,''\n            ''\"request_time\":$request_time,''\n            ''\"upstream_response_time\":\"$upstream_response_time\",''\n            ''\"http_referer\":\"$http_referer\",''\n            ''\"http_user_agent\":\"$http_user_agent\"''\n        ''}''\n    ''}'';\n\n    access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log json_combined;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Docker-Based QA Workflow\n\n### docker-compose.yml Configuration\n\n```yaml\nversion: ''3.8''\nservices:\n  api:\n    build: ./backend\n    environment:\n      - LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG\n      - LOG_FORMAT=json\n    logging:\n      driver: json-file\n      options:\n        max-size: \"10m\"\n        max-file: \"3\"\n\n  web:\n    build: ./frontend\n    environment:\n      - NODE_ENV=development\n    depends_on:\n      - api\n\n  nginx:\n    image: nginx:alpine\n    volumes:\n      - ./nginx/nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n    ports:\n      - \"80:80\"\n    depends_on:\n      - api\n      - web\n```\n\n### Real-time Log Monitoring\n\n```bash\n# Stream all service logs\ndocker compose logs -f\n\n# Specific service only\ndocker compose logs -f api\n\n# Filter errors only\ndocker compose logs -f | grep ''\"level\":\"ERROR\"''\n\n# Track specific Request ID\ndocker compose logs -f | grep ''req_abc123''\n```\n\n---\n\n## QA Automation Workflow\n\n### 1. Start Environment\n```bash\n# Start development environment\ndocker compose up -d\n\n# Start log monitoring (Claude Code monitors)\ndocker compose logs -f\n```\n\n### 2. Manual UX Testing\n```\nUser tests actual features in browser:\n1. Sign up attempt\n2. Login attempt\n3. Use core features\n4. Test edge cases\n```\n\n### 3. Claude Code Log Analysis\n```\nClaude Code in real-time:\n1. Monitor log stream\n2. Detect error patterns\n3. Detect abnormal response times\n4. Track entire flow via Request ID\n5. Auto-document issues\n```\n\n### 4. Issue Documentation\n```markdown\n# QA Issue Report\n\n## Issues Found\n\n### ISSUE-001: Insufficient error handling on login failure\n- **Request ID**: req_abc123\n- **Severity**: Medium\n- **Reproduction path**: Login → Wrong password\n- **Log**:\n  ```json\n  {\"level\":\"ERROR\",\"message\":\"Login failed\",\"data\":{\"error\":\"Invalid credentials\"}}\n  ```\n- **Problem**: Error message not user-friendly\n- **Recommended fix**: Add error code to message mapping\n```\n\n---\n\n## Issue Detection Patterns\n\n### 1. Error Detection\n```json\n{\"level\":\"ERROR\",\"message\":\"...\"}\n```\n→ Report immediately\n\n### 2. Slow Response Detection\n```json\n{\"data\":{\"duration_ms\":3000}}\n```\n→ Warning when exceeding 1000ms\n\n### 3. Consecutive Failure Detection\n```\n3+ consecutive failures on same endpoint\n```\n→ Report potential system issue\n\n### 4. Abnormal Status Codes\n```json\n{\"data\":{\"status\":500}}\n```\n→ Report 5xx errors immediately\n\n---\n\n## Phase Integration\n\n| Phase | Zero Script QA Integration |\n|-------|---------------------------|\n| Phase 4 (API) | API response logging verification |\n| Phase 6 (UI) | Frontend logging verification |\n| Phase 7 (Security) | Security event logging verification |\n| Phase 8 (Review) | Log quality review |\n| Phase 9 (Deployment) | Production log level configuration |\n\n---\n\n## Iterative Test Cycle Pattern\n\nBased on bkamp.ai notification feature development:\n\n### Example: 8-Cycle Test Process\n\n| Cycle | Pass Rate | Bug Found | Fix Applied |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1st | 30% | DB schema mismatch | Schema migration |\n| 2nd | 45% | NULL handling missing | Add null checks |\n| 3rd | 55% | Routing error | Fix deeplinks |\n| 4th | 65% | Type mismatch | Fix enum types |\n| 5th | 70% | Calculation error | Fix count logic |\n| 6th | 75% | Event missing | Add event triggers |\n| 7th | 82% | Cache sync issue | Fix cache invalidation |\n| 8th | **89%** | Stable | Final polish |\n\n### Cycle Workflow\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   Iterative Test Cycle                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Cycle N:                                                   │\n│  1. Run test script (E2E or manual)                         │\n│  2. Claude monitors logs in real-time                       │\n│  3. Record pass/fail results                                │\n│  4. Claude identifies root cause of failures                │\n│  5. Fix code immediately (hot reload)                       │\n│  6. Document: Cycle N → Bug → Fix                           │\n│                                                             │\n│  Repeat until acceptable pass rate (>85%)                   │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### E2E Test Script Template\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# E2E Test Script Template\n\nAPI_URL=\"http://localhost:8000\"\nTOKEN=\"your-test-token\"\n\nPASS_COUNT=0\nFAIL_COUNT=0\nSKIP_COUNT=0\n\nGREEN=''\\033[0;32m''\nRED=''\\033[0;31m''\nYELLOW=''\\033[0;33m''\nNC=''\\033[0m''\n\ntest_feature_action() {\n    echo -n \"Testing: Feature action... \"\n\n    response=$(curl -s -X POST \"$API_URL/api/v1/feature/action\" \\\n        -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n        -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n        -d ''{\"param\": \"value\"}'')\n\n    if [[ \"$response\" == *\"expected_result\"* ]]; then\n        echo -e \"${GREEN}✅ PASS${NC}\"\n        ((PASS_COUNT++))\n    else\n        echo -e \"${RED}❌ FAIL${NC}\"\n        echo \"Response: $response\"\n        ((FAIL_COUNT++))\n    fi\n}\n\n# Run all tests\ntest_feature_action\n# ... more tests\n\n# Summary\necho \"\"\necho \"═══════════════════════════════════════\"\necho \"Test Results:\"\necho -e \"  ${GREEN}✅ PASS: $PASS_COUNT${NC}\"\necho -e \"  ${RED}❌ FAIL: $FAIL_COUNT${NC}\"\necho -e \"  ${YELLOW}⏭️  SKIP: $SKIP_COUNT${NC}\"\necho \"═══════════════════════════════════════\"\n```\n\n### Test Cycle Documentation Template\n\n```markdown\n# Feature Test Results - Cycle N\n\n## Summary\n- **Date**: YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Feature**: {feature name}\n- **Pass Rate**: N%\n- **Tests**: X passed / Y total\n\n## Results\n\n| Test Case | Status | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Test 1 | ✅ | |\n| Test 2 | ❌ | {error description} |\n| Test 3 | ⏭️ | {skip reason} |\n\n## Bugs Found\n\n### BUG-001: {Title}\n- **Root Cause**: {description}\n- **Fix**: {what was changed}\n- **Files**: `path/to/file.py:123`\n\n## Next Cycle Plan\n- {what to test next}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n### Logging Infrastructure\n- [ ] JSON log format applied\n- [ ] Request ID generation and propagation\n- [ ] Log level settings per environment\n- [ ] Docker logging configuration\n\n### Backend Logging\n- [ ] Logging middleware implemented\n- [ ] All API calls logged (including 200 OK)\n- [ ] Business logic logging\n- [ ] Detailed error logging\n\n### Frontend Logging\n- [ ] Logger module implemented\n- [ ] API client integration\n- [ ] Error boundary logging\n\n### QA Workflow\n- [ ] Docker Compose configured\n- [ ] Real-time monitoring ready\n- [ ] Issue documentation template ready\n\n---\n\n## Auto-Apply Rules\n\n### When Building Logging Infrastructure\n\nWhen implementing API/Backend:\n1. Suggest logging middleware creation\n2. Suggest JSON format logger setup\n3. Add Request ID generation/propagation logic\n\nWhen implementing Frontend:\n1. Suggest Logger module creation\n2. Suggest logging integration with API client\n3. Suggest including Request ID header\n\n### When Performing QA\n\nOn test request:\n1. Guide to run `docker compose logs -f`\n2. Request manual UX testing from user\n3. Real-time log monitoring\n4. Document issues immediately when detected\n5. Provide fix suggestions\n\n### Issue Detection Thresholds\n\n| Severity | Condition | Action |\n|----------|-----------|--------|\n| Critical | `level: ERROR` or `status: 5xx` | Immediate report |\n| Critical | `duration_ms > 3000` | Immediate report |\n| Critical | 3+ consecutive failures | Immediate report |\n| Warning | `status: 401, 403` | Warning report |\n| Warning | `duration_ms > 1000` | Warning report |\n| Info | Missing log fields | Note for improvement |\n| Info | Request ID not propagated | Note for improvement |\n\n### Required Logging Locations\n\n#### Backend (FastAPI/Express)\n```\n✅ Request start (method, path, params)\n✅ Request complete (status, duration_ms)\n✅ Major business logic steps\n✅ Detailed info on errors\n✅ Before/after external API calls\n✅ DB queries (in development)\n```\n\n#### Frontend (Next.js/React)\n```\n✅ API call start\n✅ API response received (status, duration)\n✅ Detailed info on errors\n✅ Important user actions\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:28:22.088Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing advanced log analysis and real-time monitoring for AI-native development","zh":"非常适合像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，需要高级日志分析和实时监控的 AI 原生开发","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの AI エージェントが高度なログ分析とリアルタイム監視を必要とする AI ネイティブ開発に最適","ko":"클라우드 코드와 오토지피티 같은 AI 에이전트가 고급 로그 분석과 실시간 모니터링을 필요로 하는 AI 네이티브 개발에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que necesitan un análisis de registros avanzado y un monitoreo en tiempo real para el desarrollo nativo de IA","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant une analyse de journaux avancée et un monitoring en temps réel pour le développement natif IA","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine erweiterte Log-Analyse und Echtzeit-Überwachung für die KI-native Entwicklung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que necessitam de análise de log avançada e monitoramento em tempo real para desenvolvimento nativo de IA","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, которым требуются продвинутый анализ журналов и мониторинг в реальном времени для разработки, родной для ИИ","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوسائط الذكية مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT التي تحتاج إلى تحليل سجل متقدم ومراقبة في الوقت الفعلي لتطوير ذكاء الاصطناع الأصلي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify features through structured logs and real-time monitoring without writing test scripts, leveraging PDCA methodology and AI log analysis for auto issue detection, utilizing protocols like API call logging and error tracking","zh":"赋予代理人通过结构化日志和实时监控而无需编写测试脚本来验证功能的能力，利用 PDCA 方法论和 AI 日志分析进行自动问题检测，利用诸如 API 调用日志记录和错误跟踪等协议","ja":"エージェントがテストスクリプトを書かずに構造化ログとリアルタイム監視を使用して機能を検証できるようにし、PDCA 方法論と AI ログ分析を使用して自動的に問題を検出することを可能にし、API コールのログ記録やエラートラッキングなどのプロトコルを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 테스트 스크립트를 작성하지 않고 구조화된 로그와 실시간 모니터링을 사용하여 기능을 검증할 수 있도록 하며, PDCA 방법론과 AI 로그 분석을 사용하여 자동으로 문제를 발견하는 것을 가능하게 하며, API 호출 로깅 및 오류 추적과 같은 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar características a través de registros estructurados y monitoreo en tiempo real sin escribir scripts de prueba, aprovechando la metodología PDCA y el análisis de registros de IA para la detección automática de problemas, utilizando protocolos como el registro de llamadas de API y el seguimiento de errores","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier les fonctionnalités via des journaux structurés et un monitoring en temps réel sans écrire de scripts de test, en exploitant la méthodologie PDCA et l''analyse de journaux IA pour la détection automatique de problèmes, en utilisant des protocoles tels que le journalisation d''appels d''API et le suivi d''erreurs","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Funktionen durch strukturierte Logs und Echtzeit-Überwachung zu überprüfen, ohne Testskripte zu schreiben, indem es die PDCA-Methodik und die KI-Log-Analyse für die automatische Fehlererkennung nutzt, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie API-Aufruf-Protokollierung und Fehlernachverfolgung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar recursos por meio de logs estruturados e monitoramento em tempo real sem escrever scripts de teste, aproveitando a metodologia PDCA e análise de log de IA para detecção automática de problemas, utilizando protocolos como registro de chamadas de API e acompanhamento de erros","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять функции посредством структурированных журналов и мониторинга в реальном времени без написания тестовых сценариев, используя методологию PDCA и анализ журналов ИИ для автоматического обнаружения проблем, используя протоколы, такие как журналирование вызовов API и отслеживание ошибок","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من التحقق من الميزات من خلال سجلات منظمة ومراقبة في الوقت الفعلي دون كتابة سكريبتات الاختبار، مستفيدا من منهجية PDCA وتحليل سجل الوسائط الذكية لكشف المشكلات تلقائيا، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل تسجيل مكالمات البروتوكول ومراقبة الأخطاء"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating QA testing with log infrastructure","Generating real-time monitoring dashboards for UX testing","Debugging issues with AI-powered log analysis"],"zh":["使用日志基础设施自动化 QA 测试","为 UX 测试生成实时监控仪表盘","使用 AI驱动的日志分析调试问题"],"ja":["ログインフラストラクチャを使用した QA テストの自動化","UX テスト用のリアルタイム監視ダッシュボードの生成","AI ドライブのログ分析を使用した問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["로그 인프라를 사용한 QA 테스트 자동화","UX 테스트를 위한 실시간 모니터링 대시보드 생성","AI 구동 로그 분석을 사용한 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas de QA con infraestructura de registros","Generación de paneles de monitoreo en tiempo real para pruebas de UX","Depuración de problemas con análisis de registros impulsado por IA"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests de QA avec une infrastructure de journaux","Génération de tableaux de bord de monitoring en temps réel pour les tests UX","Débogage de problèmes avec une analyse de journaux propulsée par l''IA"],"de":["Automatisierung von QA-Tests mit Log-Infrastruktur","Erzeugung von Echtzeit-Überwachungsdashboards für UX-Tests","Fehlerbehebung mit KI-gesteuerter Log-Analyse"],"pt":["Automatizar testes de QA com infraestrutura de log","Gerar painéis de monitoramento em tempo real para testes de UX","Depurar problemas com análise de log impulsionada por IA"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тестирование QA с инфраструктурой журналов","Генерировать панели мониторинга в реальном времени для тестирования UX","Отлаживать проблемы с помощью анализа журналов, основанного на ИИ"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبار جودة الأمان مع بنية سجل","توليد لوحات مراقبة في الوقت الفعلي لاختبار UX","تصحيح الأخطاء مع تحليل سجل مدفوع بالذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires log infrastructure setup","Dependent on quality of logs for accurate analysis"],"zh":["需要日志基础设施设置","依赖于日志质量以进行准确分析"],"ja":["ログインフラストラクチャの設定が必要","ログの品質に依存して正確な分析を行う"],"ko":["로그 인프라 설정이 필요","로그 품질에 따라 정확한 분석에 의존"],"es":["Requiere configuración de infraestructura de registros","Depende de la calidad de los registros para un análisis preciso"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de l''infrastructure de journaux","Dépend de la qualité des journaux pour une analyse précise"],"de":["Benötigt eine Einrichtung der Log-Infrastruktur","Hängt von der Qualität der Logs für eine genaue Analyse ab"],"pt":["Requer configuração de infraestrutura de log","Depende da qualidade dos logs para análise precisa"],"ru":["Требует настройки инфраструктуры журналов","Зависит от качества журналов для точного анализа"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد بنية سجل","يعتمد على جودة السجلات لتحليل دقيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rmyndharis/antigravity-skills/business-analyst', 'community', 'rmyndharis', 'antigravity-skills', 'rmyndharis/antigravity-skills', 'business-analyst', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.397Z', '2026-02-18T02:28:27.050Z', NULL, '{"id":"rmyndharis/antigravity-skills/business-analyst","name":"business-analyst","description":{"zh":"Business Analyst 技能是一套用于谷歌反重力（Google Antigravity）的Agent技能集合，提供业务分析任务和工作流的指导和最佳实践。","ja":"ビジネスアナリストスキルは、Google Antigravity用のエージェントスキルのカリキュラムコレクションであり、ビジネスアナリストタスクとワークフローのガイダンスとベストプラクティスを提供します。","ko":"비즈니스 분석가 기술은 구글 안티그라비티（Google Antigravity）용 에이전트 기술의 커리큘럼 컬렉션으로, 비즈니스 분석 작업 및 워크플로우에 대한 가이드와 모범 사례를 제공합니다.","es":"El skill de analista de negocios es una colección curada de habilidades para mejorar tus procesos y tomar decisiones informadas","fr":"Le skill d''analyste commercial est une collection soigneusement sélectionnée de compétences pour améliorer vos processus et prendre des décisions éclairées","de":"Das Business-Analyst-Skill ist eine sorgfältig ausgewählte Sammlung von Fähigkeiten, um Ihre Prozesse zu verbessern und fundierte Entscheidungen zu treffen","pt":"O analista de negócios é uma habilidade que fornece orientação e melhores práticas para tarefas de análise de negócios","ru":"Бизнес-аналитик - это навык, который предоставляет руководство и лучшие практики для задач бизнес-анализа","ar":"محلل الأعمال هو مهارة توفر إرشادات وأفضل الممارسات للوظائف التحليلية التجارية","en":"A curated collection of Agent Skills for Google Antigravity"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Business Analyst 技能","ja":"ビジネスアナリストスキル","ko":"비즈니스 분석가 기술","es":"Analista de Negocios: Mejora tus Procesos","fr":"Analyste Commercial: Améliorez vos Processus","de":"Business-Analyst: Optimieren Sie Ihre Prozesse","pt":"Analista de Negócios: Ferramentas e Melhores Práticas","ru":"Бизнес-аналитик: Инструменты и Лучшие Практики