pment. Point your AI agent here to get started."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Ralph Wiggum: 自主AI编码与规格驱动开发","ja":"Ralph Wiggum: 自動AIコーディングと仕様駆動開発","ko":"Ralph Wiggum: 자율적인 AI 코딩 및 사양 주도 개발","es":"Ralph Wiggum: Desarrollo de software autónomo","fr":"Ralph Wiggum: Développement de logiciel autonome","de":"Ralph Wiggum: Autonomes Software-Entwicklung","pt":"Ralph Wiggum: Desenvolvimento Autônomo de AI","ru":"Ральф Виггум: Автономальное Кодирование AI","ar":"رالف وايغوم: تنمية آي آي ذاتية","en":"ralph-wiggum"},"description":{"zh":"Ralph Wiggum是一种自主AI编码技术，结合Geoffrey Huntley的迭代bash循环和规格驱动开发","ja":"Ralph Wiggumは、Geoffrey Huntleyのイテレーティブbashループと仕様駆動開発を組み合わせた自動AIコーディング技術です","ko":"Ralph Wiggum은 Geoffrey Huntley의 반복 bash 루프와 사양 주도 개발을 결합한 자율적인 AI 코딩 기술입니다","es":"Ralph Wiggum es una habilidad de codificación autónoma que permite el desarrollo de software asistido por IA de manera autónoma. Combina el desarrollo impuls...","fr":"Ralph Wiggum est une compétence de codage autonome qui permet le développement de logiciels assisté par IA de manière autonome. Elle combine le développement...","de":"Ralph Wiggum ist eine Fähigkeit zum autonomen Codieren, die die Entwicklung von Software asistiert von KI auf autonome Weise ermöglicht. Sie kombiniert die s...","pt":"Ralph Wiggum combina laço de bash iterativo com desenvolvimento orientado a especificações para desenvolvimento de software autônomo assistido por AI.","ru":"Ральф Виггум объединяет итеративный цикл bash с разработкой, управляемой спецификациями, для полностью автономного разработки программного обеспечения с помо...","ar":"رالف وايغوم ي 结ب حلقة/bash المتكررة مع التطوير الموجه للمواصفات من أجل تطوير البرمجيات المكتبي الذاتي بمساعدة الآي آي.","en":"Ralph Wiggum: Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development. Point your AI agent here to get started."},"definition":{"en":"Ralph Wiggum: Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development. Point your AI agent here to get started."},"features":{"zh":["自主AI编码","规格驱动开发","Geoffrey Huntley的迭代bash循环","每次迭代都有新的上下文","防止上下文溢出和劣化"],"ja":["自動AIコーディング","仕様駆動開発","Geoffrey Huntleyのイテレーティブbashループ","毎回のイテレーションで新しいコンテキスト","コンテキストオーバーフローと劣化を防止"],"ko":["자율적인 AI 코딩","사양 주도 개발","Geoffrey Huntley의 반복 bash 루프","각 반복에서 새로운 컨텍스트","컨텍스트 오버플로와 열화 방지"],"es":["Desarrollo de software autónomo","Codificación asistida por IA","Desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","Iteraciones de bash para una creación de software más eficiente","Prevenir la sobrecarga y degradación del contexto"],"fr":["Développement de logiciel autonome","Codage assisté par IA","Développement piloté par des spécifications","Itérations de bash pour une création de logiciels plus efficace","Prévenir la surcharge et la dégradation du contexte"],"de":["Autonomes Software-Entwicklung","Codieren asistiert von KI","Spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung","Bash-Iterierungen für eine effizientere Softwareerstellung","Verhindern von Kontextüberlastung und -degradation"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento autônomo de AI","Desenvolvimento orientado a especificações","Laço de bash iterativo","Prevenção de transbordamento de contexto","Degradção de contexto evitada"],"ru":["Автономальное кодирование AI","Разработка, управляемая спецификациями","Итеративный цикл bash","Предотвращение переполнения контекста","Избежание деградации контекста"],"ar":["تنمية آي آي ذاتية","التطوير الموجه للمواصفات","حلقة/bash المتكررة","منع فيضان السياق","تجنب تدهور السياق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["自主AI编码","规格驱动开发","Geoffrey Huntley","迭代bash循环","自动化软件开发","AI辅助开发"],"ja":["自動AIコーディング","仕様駆動開発","Geoffrey Huntley","イテレーティブbashループ","自動化ソフトウェア開発","AI辅助開発"],"ko":["자율적인 AI 코딩","사양 주도 개발","Geoffrey Huntley","반복 bash 루프","자동화 소프트웨어 개발","AI 보조 개발"],"es":["desarrollo de software autónomo","codificación asistida por IA","desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","iteraciones de bash","creación de software eficiente","prevenir sobrecarga de contexto"],"fr":["développement de logiciel autonome","codage assisté par IA","développement piloté par des spécifications","itérations de bash","création de logiciels efficace","prévenir surcharge de contexte"],"de":["autonomes Software-Entwicklung","Codieren asistiert von KI","spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung","Bash-Iterierungen","effiziente Softwareerstellung","Verhindern von Kontextüberlastung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento autônomo de AI","desenvolvimento orientado a especificações","codificação autônoma de AI","laço de bash iterativo","prevenção de transbordamento de contexto","desenvolvimento de software assistido por AI"],"ru":["автономальное кодирование AI","разработка, управляемая спецификациями","автономальное кодирование AI","итеративный цикл bash","предотвращение переполнения контекста","разработка программного обеспечения с помощью AI"],"ar":["تنمية آي آي ذاتية","التطوير الموجه للمواصفات","ترميز آي آي ذاتي","حلقة/bash المتكررة","منع فيضان السياق","تطوير البرمجيات بمساعدة الآي آي"]}},"owner":"fstandhartinger","repo":"ralph-wiggum","repoPath":"fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.397Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ralph-wiggum","description":"Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development. Implements Geoffrey Huntleys iterative bash loop methodology where agents work through specs one at a time, outputting a completion signal only when acceptance criteria are 100% met.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Ralph Wiggum\n\n> Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development\n\n## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n\nRalph Wiggum combines **Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop** with **spec-driven development** for fully autonomous AI-assisted software development.\n\nThe key insight: **Fresh context each iteration**. Each loop starts a new agent process with a clean context window, preventing context overflow and degradation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse Ralph Wiggum when:\n\n- You have multiple specifications/fe","body":"# Ralph Wiggum\n\n> Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development\n\n## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n\nRalph Wiggum combines **Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop** with **spec-driven development** for fully autonomous AI-assisted software development.\n\nThe key insight: **Fresh context each iteration**. Each loop starts a new agent process with a clean context window, preventing context overflow and degradation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse Ralph Wiggum when:\n\n- You have multiple specifications/features to implement\n- You want the AI to work autonomously through tasks\n- You need consistent, verifiable completion of acceptance criteria\n- You want to avoid context window problems in long sessions\n\n## How It Works\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     RALPH LOOP                              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Loop 1: Pick spec A → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  Loop 2: Pick spec B → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  Loop 3: Pick spec C → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  ...                                                        │\n│                                                             │\n│  Each iteration = Fresh context window                      │\n│  Shared state = Files on disk (specs, plan, history)        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Installation\n\n### Quick Install (via Skill Installers)\n\n```bash\n# Using Vercel''s add-skill\nnpx add-skill fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n\n# Using OpenSkills\nopenskills install fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n```\n\n### Full Setup (Recommended)\n\nFor full Ralph Wiggum setup with constitution and interview:\n\n```bash\n# Tell your AI agent:\n\"Set up Ralph Wiggum using https://github.com/fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\"\n```\n\nThe agent will guide you through a **lightweight, pleasant setup**:\n\n1. **Quick Setup** (~1 min) — Create directories, download scripts\n2. **Project Interview** — Focus on your **vision and goals** (not tech details)\n3. **Constitution** — Create a guiding document for all sessions\n4. **Next Steps** — Clear guidance on creating specs and starting Ralph\n\nFor existing projects, the agent detects your tech stack automatically. The interview prioritizes understanding *what you''re building and why*.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Fresh Context Each Loop\n\nEach iteration of the Ralph loop starts a new AI agent process. This means:\n- No context window overflow\n- No degradation over time\n- Clean slate for each task\n\n### 2. Shared State on Disk\n\nState persists between loops via files:\n- `specs/` — Feature specifications with acceptance criteria\n- `ralph_history.txt` — Log of breakthroughs, blockers, learnings\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — Optional detailed task breakdown\n\n### 3. Completion Signal\n\nThe agent outputs `<promise>DONE</promise>` **ONLY** when:\n- All acceptance criteria are verified\n- Tests pass\n- Changes are committed and pushed\n\nThe bash loop checks for this phrase. If not found, it retries.\n\n### 4. Backpressure via Tests\n\nTests, lints, and builds act as guardrails. The agent must fix issues before outputting the completion signal.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Creating Specifications\n\n**The key to success:** Each spec needs **clear, testable acceptance criteria**. This is what tells Ralph when a task is truly \"done.\"\n\n```markdown\n# Feature: User Authentication\n\n## Requirements\n- OAuth login with Google\n- Session management\n- Logout functionality\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] User can log in with Google\n- [ ] Session persists across page reloads\n- [ ] User can log out\n- [ ] Tests pass\n\n**Output when complete:** `<promise>DONE</promise>`\n```\n\n**Good criteria:** \"User can log in with Google and session persists\"\n**Bad criteria:** \"Auth works correctly\"\n\nThe more specific your acceptance criteria, the better Ralph performs.\n\n### Running the Loop\n\n```bash\n# Start building (Claude Code)\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh\n\n# With max iterations\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh 20\n\n# Using Codex CLI\n./scripts/ralph-loop-codex.sh\n```\n\n### Logging (All Output Captured)\n\nEvery loop run writes **all output** to log files in `logs/`:\n\n- **Session log:** `logs/ralph_*_session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log` (entire run, including CLI output)\n- **Iteration logs:** `logs/ralph_*_iter_N_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log` (per-iteration CLI output)\n- **Codex last message:** `logs/ralph_codex_output_iter_N_*.txt`\n\n### RLM Mode (Experimental)\n\nProvide a large context file and the agent will treat it as external environment.\nThis is **optional and experimental** — it does not implement the full recursive runtime from the paper, but it **does** preserve all loop outputs on disk and guides the agent to query them as needed.\n\n```bash\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh --rlm-context ./rlm/context.txt\n./scripts/ralph-loop-codex.sh --rlm-context ./rlm/context.txt\n```\n\nRLM workspace (when enabled):\n- `rlm/trace/` — Prompt snapshots per iteration\n- `rlm/index.tsv` — Index of all iterations\n- `logs/` — Full CLI output per iteration\n\nOptional recursive subcalls:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/rlm-subcall.sh --query rlm/queries/q1.md\n```\n\nThis mirrors the Recursive Language Model (RLM) idea: handle huge prompts by inspecting only the slices you need.\n\n## Two Modes\n\n| Mode | Purpose | Command |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| **build** (default) | Pick spec, implement, test, commit | `./scripts/ralph-loop.sh` |\n| **plan** (optional) | Create detailed task breakdown | `./scripts/ralph-loop.sh plan` |\n\n## Key Principles\n\n### Let Ralph Ralph\n\nTrust the AI to self-identify, self-correct, and self-improve. Observe patterns and adjust prompts.\n\n### YOLO Mode\n\nFor Ralph to work effectively, enable full autonomy:\n- Claude Code: `--dangerously-skip-permissions`\n- Codex: `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`\n\n⚠️ **Use at your own risk.** Only in sandboxed environments.\n\n## Links\n\n- **GitHub:** https://github.com/fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n- **Website:** https://ralph-wiggum.ai\n- **Original methodology:** [Geoffrey Huntley''s how-to-ralph-wiggum](https://github.com/ghuntley/how-to-ralph-wiggum)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:31:45.887Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous AI Agents needing spec-driven development and iterative bash loop capabilities for fully autonomous AI-assisted software development.","zh":"非常适合需要基于规格驱动开发和迭代bash循环功能的自主AI代理，实现完全自主的AI辅助软件开发。","ja":"規格駆動開発と反復的bashループ機能を必要とする自律的なAIエージェントに最適で、完全に自律的なAI支援ソフトウェア開発を実現します。","ko":"규격 주도 개발 및 반복적인 bash 루프 기능이 필요한 자율적인 AI 에이전트에게 적합하여 완전히 자율적인 AI 보조 소프트웨어 개발을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA Autónomos que necesitan desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones y capacidades de bucle bash iterativo para el desarrollo de software asistido por IA completamente autónomo.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de IA Autonomes ayant besoin d''un développement piloté par des spécifications et de capacités de boucle bash itérative pour le développement de logiciels assistés par IA entièrement autonomes.","de":"Perfekt für autonome KI-Agents, die spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung und iterative Bash-Schleifenfunktionen für vollständig autonome KI-gestützte Softwareentwicklung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Autônomos que precisam de desenvolvimento baseado em especificações e capacidades de loop de bash iterativo para desenvolvimento de software de IA totalmente autônomo.","ru":"Идеально для автономных агентов ИИ, которым требуется разработка, управляемая спецификациями, и итеративные возможности цикла bash для полностью автономного разработки программного обеспечения с помощью ИИ.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المستقلة التي تحتاج إلى تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات وقدرات حلقة باش التكرارية لبرمجيات كاملة الذكاء الاصطناعي-مसاعدة تطوير البرمجيات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop with spec-driven development, ensuring fresh context each iteration and preventing context overflow and degradation, utilizing spec-driven development for autonomous AI coding.","zh":"赋予代理能够利用Geoffrey Huntley的迭代bash循环与规格驱动开发，确保每次迭代都有最新的上下文，并防止上下文溢出和退化，利用规格驱动开发实现自主AI编码。","ja":"Geoffrey Huntleyの反復的bashループと規格駆動開発を利用できるようにエージェントを強化し、各反復ごとに新しいコンテキストを保証し、コンテキストオーバーフローと劣化を防ぎ、規格駆動開発を使用して自律的なAIコーディングを実現します。","ko":"Geoffrey Huntley의 반복 bash 루프와 규격 주도 개발을 활용할 수 있도록 에이전트를 강화하여, 각 반복마다 새로운 컨텍스트를 보장하고, 컨텍스트 오버플로 및 열화退化를 방지하며, 규격 주도 개발을 사용하여 자율적인 AI 코딩을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar el bucle bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley con desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones, asegurando un contexto fresco en cada iteración y evitando el desbordamiento y la degradación del contexto, utilizando el desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones para la codificación de IA autónoma.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter la boucle bash itérative de Geoffrey Huntley avec un développement piloté par des spécifications, assurant un contexte frais à chaque itération et empêchant le débordement et la dégradation du contexte, en utilisant le développement piloté par des spécifications pour la codification de l''IA autonome.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Geoffrey Huntleys iterativen Bash-Schleifen mit spezifikationsgetriebener Entwicklung zu nutzen, um bei jeder Iteration einen frischen Kontext sicherzustellen und Kontextüberlauf und -verschlechterung zu verhindern, indem spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung für autonome KI-Codierung verwendet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitarem o loop de bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley com desenvolvimento baseado em especificações, garantindo um contexto fresco a cada iteração e prevenindo o transbordamento e degradação de contexto, utilizando o desenvolvimento baseado em especificações para codificação de IA autônoma.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать итеративный цикл bash Джофри Хантли с разработкой, управляемой спецификациями, обеспечивая свежий контекст на каждой итерации и предотвращая переполнение и деградацию контекста, используя разработку, управляемую спецификациями, для автономного кодирования ИИ.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على استخدام حلقة باش التكرارية لجوفري هانتلي مع التطوير الذي يقوده المواصفات، مما يضمن سياقًا جديدًا في كل تكرار ويتجنب فيضان السياق وتدهوره، باستخدام التطوير الذي يقوده المواصفات للتدوين الذكاء الاصطناعي المستقلة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating software development with spec-driven development","Generating clean context windows for each iteration","Preventing context overflow and degradation in AI-assisted development"],"zh":["使用规格驱动开发自动化软件开发","为每次迭代生成干净的上下文窗口","防止AI辅助开发中的上下文溢出和退化"],"ja":["規格駆動開発を使用したソフトウェア開発の自動化","各反復ごとのクリーンなコンテキストウィンドウの生成","AI支援開発におけるコンテキストオーバーフローと劣化の防止"],"ko":["규격 주도 개발을 사용한 소프트웨어 개발 자동화","각 반복마다 깨끗한 컨텍스트 창을 생성","AI 보조 개발에서 컨텍스트 오버플로 및 열화방지"],"es":["Automatizar el desarrollo de software con desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","Generar ventanas de contexto limpias para cada iteración","Prevenir el desbordamiento y la degradación del contexto en el desarrollo asistido por IA"],"fr":["Automatiser le développement de logiciels avec un développement piloté par des spécifications","Générer des fenêtres de contexte propres pour chaque itération","Prévenir le débordement et la dégradation du contexte dans le développement assisté par IA"],"de":["Automatisierung der Softwareentwicklung mit spezifikationsgetriebener Entwicklung","Erzeugen von sauberen Kontextfenstern für jede Iteration","Verhindern von Kontextüberlauf und -verschlechterung in der KI-gestützten Entwicklung"],"pt":["Automatizar o desenvolvimento de software com desenvolvimento baseado em especificações","Gerar janelas de contexto limpas para cada iteração","Prevenir o transbordamento e degradação de contexto no desenvolvimento auxiliado por IA"],"ru":["Автоматизировать разработку программного обеспечения с помощью разработки, управляемой спецификациями","Генерировать чистые контекстные окна для каждой итерации","Предотвращать переполнение и деградацию контекста в разработке программного обеспечения с помощью ИИ"],"ar":["تحسين تطوير البرمجيات مع التطوير الذي يقوده المواصفات","توليد نوافذ سياق نظيفة لكل تكرار","منع فيضان السياق وتدهوره في تطوير البرمجيات بمساعدة الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires multiple specifications or features to function effectively"],"zh":["需要多个规格或功能才能有效工作"],"ja":["有効に機能するには複数の仕様または機能が必要"],"ko":["효과적으로 작동하려면 여러 개의 사양 또는 기능이 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere múltiples especificaciones o características para funcionar de manera efectiva"],"fr":["Nécessite plusieurs spécifications ou fonctionnalités pour fonctionner de manière efficace"],"de":["Benötigt mehrere Spezifikationen oder Funktionen, um effektiv zu funktionieren"],"pt":["Requer múltiplas especificações ou recursos para funcionar de forma eficaz"],"ru":["Требует нескольких спецификаций или функций для эффективного функционирования"],"ar":["يتطلب مواصفات أو ميزات متعددة للعمل بشكل فعال"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('w-winter/dot314/surf', 'community', 'w-winter', 'dot314', 'w-winter/dot314', 'surf', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.397Z', '2026-02-18T02:31:56.331Z', NULL, '{"id":"w-winter/dot314/surf","name":"surf","description":{"zh":"Surf 浏览器自动化控制是一种命令行工具，用于控制 Chrome 浏览器。它提供了大量的命令和选项，用于自动化浏览器操作","ja":"Surf ブラウザ自動化制御は、Chrome ブラウザを制御するためのコマンドラインツールです。ブラウザ操作を自動化するための多数のコマンドとオプションを提供しています","ko":"Surf 브라우저 자동화 제어는 Chrome 브라우저를 제어하기 위한 명령줄 툴입니다. 브라우저 동작을 자동화하기 위한 많은 명령어와 옵션을 제공합니다","es":"Surf es una herramienta de automatización de navegador que permite controlar Chrome desde la línea de comandos o socket de Unix. Ofrece una variedad de comandos y opciones para personalizar el flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Surf est un outil d''automatisation de navigateur qui permet de contrôler Chrome depuis la ligne de commande ou le socket Unix. Il offre une variété de commandes et d''options pour personnaliser le flux de travail.","de":"Surf ist ein Browser-Automatisierungstool, das es ermöglicht, Chrome über die Kommandozeile oder das Unix-Socket zu steuern. Es bietet eine Vielzahl von Befehlen und Optionen, um den Arbeitsablauf anzupassen.","pt":"O Surf é uma ferramenta de automação de navegador que permite controlar o Chrome via CLI ou soquete Unix","ru":"Surf - это инструмент автоматизации браузера, позволяющий контролировать Chrome через CLI или Unix-сокет","ar":"سف هو أداة للتحكم في المتصفح التي تمكنك من التحكم في متصفح Chrome عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر أو сокيت Unix","en":"Extensions, commands, themes for Pi"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Surf 浏览器自动化控制","ja":"Surf ブラウザ自動化制御","ko":"Surf 브라우저 자동화 제어","es":"Automatización de navegador con Surf","fr":"Automatisation du navigateur avec Surf","de":"Browser-Automatisierung mit Surf","pt":"Controle de Navegador Surf","ru":"Автоматизация браузера Surf","ar":"سيطرة متصفح سف","en":"surf"},"description":{"zh":"Surf 浏览器自动化控制是一种命令行工具，用于控制 Chrome 浏览器。它提供了大量的命令和选项，用于自动化浏览器操作","ja":"Surf ブラウザ自動化制御は、Chrome ブラウザを制御するためのコマンドラインツールです。ブラウザ操作を自動化するための多数のコマンドとオプションを提供しています","ko":"Surf 브라우저 자동화 제어는 Chrome 브라우저를 제어하기 위한 명령줄 툴입니다. 브라우저 동작을 자동화하기 위한 많은 명령어와 옵션을 제공합니다","es":"Surf es una herramienta de automatización de navegador que permite controlar Chrome desde la línea de comandos o socket de Unix. Ofrece una variedad de coman...","fr":"Surf est un outil d''automatisation de navigateur qui permet de contrôler Chrome depuis la ligne de commande ou le socket Unix. Il offre une variété de comman...","de":"Surf ist ein Browser-Automatisierungstool, das es ermöglicht, Chrome über die Kommandozeile oder das Unix-Socket zu steuern. Es bietet eine Vielzahl von Befe...","pt":"O Surf é uma ferramenta de automação de navegador que permite controlar o Chrome via CLI ou soquete Unix","ru":"Surf - это инструмент автоматизации браузера, позволяющий контролировать Chrome через CLI или Unix-сокет","ar":"سف هو أداة للتحكم في المتصفح التي تمكنك من التحكم في متصفح Chrome عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر أو сокيت Unix","en":"Extensions, commands, themes for Pi"},"definition":{"en":"Extensions, commands, themes for Pi"},"features":{"zh":["CLI 控制","Unix socket 支持","自动化浏览器操作","大量命令和选项","支持主题和扩展"],"ja":["CLI 制御","Unix ソケット対応","ブラウザ操作の自動化","多数のコマンドとオプション","テーマと拡張機能のサポート"],"ko":["CLI 제어","Unix 소켓 지원","브라우저 동작 자동화","많은 명령어와 옵션","테마와 확장 기능 지원"],"es":["Control de Chrome desde la línea de comandos","Conexión a través de socket de Unix","Variados comandos para personalizar el flujo de trabajo","Búsqueda de herramientas y ayuda integrada","Guías de temas y referencias detalladas"],"fr":["Contrôle de Chrome depuis la ligne de commande","Connexion via le socket Unix","Commandes variées pour personnaliser le flux de travail","Recherche d''outils et aide intégrée","Guides de sujets et références détaillées"],"de":["Steuerung von Chrome über die Kommandozeile","Verbindung über das Unix-Socket","Vielfältige Befehle für die Anpassung des Arbeitsablaufs","Suche nach Tools und integrierte Hilfe","Themenführer und detaillierte Referenzen"],"pt":["Controle de navegador via CLI","Controle de navegador via soquete Unix","Comandos para navegação e interação","Suporte a temas e extensões","Comandos para busca e ajuda"],"ru":["Контроль браузера через CLI","Контроль браузера через Unix-сокет","Команды для навигации и взаимодействия","Поддержка тем и расширений","Команды для поиска и помощи"],"ar":["التحكم في المتصفح عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر","التحكم في المتصفح عبر сокيت Unix","أوامر للتنقل والتفاعل","دعم للمواضيع والامتدادات","أوامر للبحث والمساعدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Surf 浏览器自动化","Chrome 浏览器控制","CLI 工具","Unix socket","浏览器自动化","命令行工具"],"ja":["Surf ブラウザ自動化","Chrome ブラウザ制御","CLI ツール","Unix ソケット","ブラウザ自動化","コマンドラインツール"],"ko":["Surf 브라우저 자동화","Chrome 브라우저 제어","CLI 툴","Unix 소켓","브라우저 자동화","명령줄 툴"],"es":["automatización de navegador","control de Chrome","línea de comandos","socket de Unix","personalización de flujo de trabajo","búsqueda de herramientas","guías de temas","referencias detalladas","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["automatisation de navigateur","contrôle de Chrome","ligne de commande","socket Unix","personnalisation de flux de travail","recherche d''outils","guides de sujets","références détaillées","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Browser-Automatisierung","Steuerung von Chrome","Kommandozeile","Unix-Socket","Anpassung des Arbeitsablaufs","Suche nach Tools","Themenführer","detaillierte Referenzen","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["automação de navegador","controle de navegador","CLI","soquete Unix","temas","extensões","navegação","interação","busca","ajuda"],"ru":["автоматизация браузера","контроль браузера","CLI","Unix-сокет","темы","расширения","навигация","взаимодействие","поиск","помощь"],"ar":["التحكم في المتصفح","التنقل","التفاعل","واجهة سطر الأوامر","сокيت Unix","المواضيع","الامتدادات","البحث","المساعدة","أداة التحكم في المتصفح"]}},"owner":"w-winter","repo":"dot314","repoPath":"w-winter/dot314","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.397Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"surf","description":"Control Chrome browser via CLI for testing, automation, and debugging. Use when the user needs browser automation, screenshots, form filling, page inspection, network/CPU emulation, DevTools streaming, or AI queries via ChatGPT/Gemini/Perplexity/Grok.","bodyPreview":"# Surf Browser Automation\n\nControl Chrome browser via CLI or Unix socket.\n\n## CLI Quick Reference\n\n```bash\nsurf --help                    # Full help\nsurf <group>                   # Group help (tab, scroll, page, wait, dialog, emulate, form, perf, ai)\nsurf --help-full               # All commands\nsurf --find <term>             # Search tools\nsurf --help-topic <topic>      # Topic guide (refs, semantic, frames, devices, windows)\n```\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n```bash\n# 1. Navigate to page\nsurf navigate","body":"# Surf Browser Automation\n\nControl Chrome browser via CLI or Unix socket.\n\n## CLI Quick Reference\n\n```bash\nsurf --help                    # Full help\nsurf <group>                   # Group help (tab, scroll, page, wait, dialog, emulate, form, perf, ai)\nsurf --help-full               # All commands\nsurf --find <term>             # Search tools\nsurf --help-topic <topic>      # Topic guide (refs, semantic, frames, devices, windows)\n```\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n```bash\n# 1. Navigate to page\nsurf navigate \"https://example.com\"\n\n# 2. Read page to get element refs\nsurf page.read\n\n# 3. Click by ref or coordinates\nsurf click --ref \"e1\"\nsurf click --x 100 --y 200\n\n# 4. Type text\nsurf type --text \"hello\"\n\n# 5. Screenshot\nsurf screenshot --output /tmp/shot.png\n```\n\n## AI Assistants (No API Keys)\n\nQuery AI models using your browser''s logged-in session. Must be logged into the respective service in Chrome.\n\n### ChatGPT\n```bash\nsurf chatgpt \"explain this code\"\nsurf chatgpt \"summarize\" --with-page              # Include current page context\nsurf chatgpt \"review\" --model gpt-4o              # Specify model\nsurf chatgpt \"analyze\" --file document.pdf        # With file attachment\n```\n\n### Gemini\n```bash\nsurf gemini \"explain quantum computing\"\nsurf gemini \"summarize\" --with-page               # Include page context\nsurf gemini \"analyze\" --file data.csv             # Attach file\nsurf gemini \"a robot surfing\" --generate-image /tmp/robot.png\nsurf gemini \"add sunglasses\" --edit-image photo.jpg --output out.jpg\nsurf gemini \"summarize\" --youtube \"https://youtube.com/...\"\nsurf gemini \"hello\" --model gemini-2.5-flash      # Models: gemini-3-pro (default), gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-2.5-flash\nsurf gemini \"wide banner\" --generate-image /tmp/banner.png --aspect-ratio 16:9\n```\n\n### Perplexity\n```bash\nsurf perplexity \"what is quantum computing\"\nsurf perplexity \"explain this page\" --with-page   # Include page context\nsurf perplexity \"deep dive\" --mode research       # Research mode (Pro)\nsurf perplexity \"latest news\" --model sonar       # Model selection (Pro)\n```\n\n### Grok (via x.com - requires X.com login in Chrome)\n```bash\nsurf grok \"what are the latest AI trends on X\"    # Search X posts\nsurf grok \"analyze @username recent activity\"     # Profile analysis\nsurf grok \"summarize this page\" --with-page       # Include page context\nsurf grok \"find viral AI posts\" --deep-search     # DeepSearch mode\nsurf grok \"quick question\" --model fast           # Models: auto, fast, expert, thinking (default)\n```\n\n**Grok Validation & Troubleshooting:**\n```bash\n# Validate Grok UI and check available models (no query sent)\nsurf grok --validate\n\n# If models changed, save discovered models to surf.json config\nsurf grok --validate --save-models\n```\n\n### AI Tool Troubleshooting\n\nWhen AI queries fail, check these common issues:\n\n1. **Not logged in**: The error \"login required\" means you need to log into the service in Chrome\n2. **Model selection failed**: The UI may have changed. Run `surf grok --validate` to check\n3. **Response timeout**: Thinking models (ChatGPT o1, Grok thinking) can take 45+ seconds\n4. **Element not found**: The service''s UI changed. Check for surf-cli updates\n\n**Debugging workflow for agents:**\n```bash\n# 1. Check if the service is accessible and UI is valid\nsurf grok --validate\n\n# 2. If models mismatch, update the local settings\nsurf grok --validate --save-models\n\n# 3. Retry with explicit model name from validation output\nsurf grok \"query\" --model <model-from-validation>\n\n# 4. If still failing, try with longer timeout\nsurf grok \"query\" --timeout 600\n```\n\n## Tab Management\n\n```bash\nsurf tab.list\nsurf tab.new \"https://google.com\"\nsurf tab.switch 12345\nsurf tab.close 12345\nsurf tab.reload                # Reload current tab\n\n# Named tabs (aliases)\nsurf tab.name myapp            # Name current tab\nsurf tab.switch myapp          # Switch by name\nsurf tab.named                 # List named tabs\nsurf tab.unname myapp          # Remove name\n\n# Tab groups\nsurf tab.group                 # Create/add to tab group\nsurf tab.ungroup               # Remove from group\nsurf tab.groups                # List all tab groups\n```\n\n## Window Management\n\n```bash\nsurf window.list                              # List all windows\nsurf window.list --tabs                       # Include tab details\nsurf window.new                               # New window\nsurf window.new --url \"https://example.com\"   # New window with URL\nsurf window.new --incognito                   # New incognito window\nsurf window.new --unfocused                   # Don''t focus new window\nsurf window.focus 12345                       # Focus window by ID\nsurf window.close 12345                       # Close window\nsurf window.resize --id 123 --width 1920 --height 1080\nsurf window.resize --id 123 --state maximized # States: normal, minimized, maximized, fullscreen\n```\n\n**Window isolation for agents:**\n```bash\n# Create isolated window for agent work\nsurf window.new \"https://example.com\"\n# Returns window ID, use with subsequent commands:\nsurf --window-id 123 tab.list\nsurf --window-id 123 go \"https://other.com\"\n```\n\n## Input Methods\n\n```bash\n# CDP method (real events) - default\nsurf type --text \"hello\"\nsurf click --x 100 --y 200\n\n# JS method (DOM manipulation) - for contenteditable\nsurf type --text \"hello\" --selector \"#input\" --method js\n\n# Keys\nsurf key Enter\nsurf key \"cmd+a\"\nsurf key.repeat --key Tab --count 5           # Repeat key presses\n\n# Hover and drag\nsurf hover --ref e5\nsurf drag --from-x 100 --from-y 100 --to-x 200 --to-y 200\n```\n\n## Page Inspection\n\n```bash\nsurf page.read                 # Accessibility tree with refs + page text\nsurf page.read --no-text       # Interactive elements only (no text content)\nsurf page.read --ref e5        # Get specific element details\nsurf page.read --depth 3       # Limit tree depth\nsurf page.read --compact       # Minimal output for LLM efficiency\nsurf page.text                 # Plain text content only\nsurf page.state                # Modals, loading state, scroll info\n```\n\n## Semantic Element Location\n\nFind and act on elements by role, text, or label instead of refs:\n\n```bash\n# Find by ARIA role\nsurf locate.role button --name \"Submit\" --action click\nsurf locate.role textbox --name \"Email\" --action fill --value \"test@example.com\"\nsurf locate.role link --all                    # Return all matches\n\n# Find by text content\nsurf locate.text \"Sign In\" --action click\nsurf locate.text \"Accept\" --exact --action click\n\n# Find form field by label\nsurf locate.label \"Username\" --action fill --value \"john\"\nsurf locate.label \"Password\" --action fill --value \"secret\"\n```\n\n**Actions:** `click`, `fill`, `hover`, `text` (get text content)\n\n## Text Search\n\n```bash\nsurf search \"login\"                    # Find text in page\nsurf search \"Error\" --case-sensitive   # Case-sensitive\nsurf search \"button\" --limit 5         # Limit results\nsurf find \"login\"                      # Alias for search\n```\n\n## Element Inspection\n\n```bash\nsurf element.styles e5                 # Get computed styles by ref\nsurf element.styles \".card\"            # Or by CSS selector\n# Returns: font, color, background, border, padding, bounding box\n```\n\n## Scrolling\n\n```bash\nsurf scroll.bottom\nsurf scroll.top\nsurf scroll.to --y 500         # Scroll to Y position\nsurf scroll.to --ref e5        # Scroll element into view\nsurf scroll.by --y 200         # Scroll by amount\nsurf scroll.info               # Get scroll position\n```\n\n## Waiting\n\n```bash\nsurf wait 2                    # Wait 2 seconds\nsurf wait.element \".loaded\"    # Wait for element\nsurf wait.network              # Wait for network idle\nsurf wait.url \"/success\"       # Wait for URL pattern\nsurf wait.dom --stable 100     # Wait for DOM stability\nsurf wait.load                 # Wait for page load complete\n```\n\n## Dialog Handling\n\n```bash\nsurf dialog.info               # Get current dialog type/message\nsurf dialog.accept             # Accept (OK)\nsurf dialog.accept --text \"response\"  # Accept prompt with text\nsurf dialog.dismiss            # Dismiss (Cancel)\n```\n\n## Device/Network Emulation\n\n```bash\n# Network throttling\nsurf emulate.network slow-3g   # Presets: slow-3g, fast-3g, 4g, offline\nsurf emulate.network reset     # Disable throttling\n\n# CPU throttling\nsurf emulate.cpu 4             # 4x slower\nsurf emulate.cpu 1             # Reset\n\n# Device emulation (19 presets)\nsurf emulate.device \"iPhone 14\"\nsurf emulate.device \"Pixel 7\"\nsurf emulate.device --list     # List available devices\n\n# Custom viewport\nsurf emulate.viewport --width 1280 --height 720\nsurf emulate.touch --enable    # Enable touch emulation\n\n# Geolocation\nsurf emulate.geo --lat 37.7749 --lon -122.4194\nsurf emulate.geo --clear\n```\n\n## Form Automation\n\n```bash\nsurf page.read                 # Get element refs first\n\n# Fill by ref\nsurf form.fill --data ''[{\"ref\":\"e1\",\"value\":\"John\"},{\"ref\":\"e2\",\"value\":\"john@example.com\"}]''\n\n# Checkboxes: true/false\nsurf form.fill --data ''[{\"ref\":\"e7\",\"value\":true}]''\n\n# Dropdown selection\nsurf select e5 \"Option A\"                    # By value (default)\nsurf select e5 \"Option A\" \"Option B\"         # Multi-select\nsurf select e5 --by label \"Display Text\"     # By visible label\nsurf select e5 --by index 2                  # By index (0-based)\n```\n\n## File Upload\n\n```bash\nsurf upload --ref e5 --files \"/path/to/file.txt\"\nsurf upload --ref e5 --files \"/path/file1.txt,/path/file2.txt\"\n```\n\n## Iframe Handling\n\n```bash\nsurf frame.list                # List frames with IDs\nsurf frame.switch \"FRAME_ID\"   # Switch to iframe context\nsurf frame.main                # Return to main frame\nsurf frame.js --id \"FRAME_ID\" --code \"return document.title\"\n\n# After frame.switch, subsequent commands target that frame:\nsurf frame.switch \"iframe-1\"\nsurf page.read                 # Reads iframe content\nsurf click e5                  # Clicks in iframe\nsurf frame.main                # Back to main page\n```\n\n## Network Inspection\n\n```bash\nsurf network                   # List captured requests\nsurf network --stream          # Real-time network events\nsurf network.get --id \"req-123\"   # Full request details\nsurf network.body --id \"req-123\"  # Get response body\nsurf network.curl --id \"req-123\"  # Generate curl command\nsurf network.origins           # List origins with stats\nsurf network.stats             # Capture statistics\nsurf network.export            # Export all requests\nsurf network.clear             # Clear captured requests\n```\n\n## Console\n\n```bash\nsurf console                   # Get console messages\nsurf console --stream          # Real-time console\nsurf console --stream --level error  # Errors only\n```\n\n## JavaScript Execution\n\n```bash\nsurf js \"return document.title\"\nsurf js \"document.querySelector(''.btn'').click()\"\n```\n\n## Performance\n\n```bash\nsurf perf.metrics              # Current metrics snapshot\nsurf perf.start                # Start trace\nsurf perf.stop                 # Stop and get results\n```\n\n## Screenshots\n\n```bash\nsurf screenshot                           # Auto-saves to /tmp/surf-snap-*.png\nsurf screenshot --output /tmp/shot.png    # Save to specific file\nsurf screenshot --selector \".card\"        # Element only\nsurf screenshot --full-page               # Full page scroll capture\nsurf screenshot --no-save                 # Return base64 only, don''t save file\n```\n\n## Zoom\n\n```bash\nsurf zoom                      # Get current zoom level\nsurf zoom 1.5                  # Set zoom to 150%\nsurf zoom 1                    # Reset to 100%\n```\n\n## Cookies & Storage\n\n```bash\nsurf cookie.list               # List cookies for current page\nsurf cookie.list --domain .google.com\nsurf cookie.set --name \"token\" --value \"abc123\"\nsurf cookie.get --name \"token\"\nsurf cookie.clear              # Clear all cookies\n```\n\n## History & Bookmarks\n\n```bash\nsurf history --query \"github\" --max 20\nsurf bookmarks --query \"docs\"\nsurf bookmark.add --url \"https://...\" --title \"My Bookmark\"\nsurf bookmark.remove\n```\n\n## Health Checks & Smoke Tests\n\n```bash\nsurf health --url \"http://localhost:3000\"\nsurf smoke --urls \"http://localhost:3000\" \"http://localhost:3000/about\"\nsurf smoke --urls \"...\" --screenshot /tmp/smoke\n```\n\n## Workflows\n\nExecute multi-step browser automation as a single command with smart auto-waits.\n\n### Inline Workflows\n\n```bash\n# Pipe-separated commands\nsurf do ''go \"https://example.com\" | click e5 | screenshot''\n\n# Multi-step login flow\nsurf do ''go \"https://example.com/login\" | type \"user@example.com\" --selector \"#email\" | type \"pass\" --selector \"#password\" | click --selector \"button[type=submit]\"''\n\n# Validate without executing\nsurf do ''go \"url\" | click e5'' --dry-run\n```\n\n### Named Workflows\n\nSave workflows as JSON files in `~/.surf/workflows/` (user) or `./.surf/workflows/` (project):\n\n```bash\n# List available workflows\nsurf workflow.list\n\n# Show workflow details\nsurf workflow.info my-workflow\n\n# Run by name with arguments\nsurf do my-workflow --email \"user@example.com\" --password \"secret\"\n\n# Validate workflow file\nsurf workflow.validate workflow.json\n```\n\n### Workflow JSON Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Login Flow\",\n  \"description\": \"Automate login process\",\n  \"args\": {\n    \"email\": { \"required\": true },\n    \"password\": { \"required\": true },\n    \"url\": { \"default\": \"https://example.com/login\" }\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"tool\": \"navigate\", \"args\": { \"url\": \"%{url}\" } },\n    { \"tool\": \"type\", \"args\": { \"text\": \"%{email}\", \"selector\": \"input[name=email]\" } },\n    { \"tool\": \"type\", \"args\": { \"text\": \"%{password}\", \"selector\": \"input[name=password]\" } },\n    { \"tool\": \"click\", \"args\": { \"selector\": \"button[type=submit]\" } },\n    { \"tool\": \"screenshot\", \"args\": {}, \"as\": \"result\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Loops and Step Outputs\n\n```json\n{\n  \"steps\": [\n    // Capture step output for later use\n    { \"tool\": \"js\", \"args\": { \"code\": \"return [1,2,3]\" }, \"as\": \"items\" },\n\n    // Fixed iterations\n    { \"repeat\": 5, \"steps\": [\n      { \"tool\": \"click\", \"args\": { \"ref\": \"e5\" } }\n    ]},\n\n    // Iterate over array\n    { \"each\": \"%{items}\", \"as\": \"item\", \"steps\": [\n      { \"tool\": \"js\", \"args\": { \"code\": \"console.log(''%{item}'')\" } }\n    ]},\n\n    // Repeat until condition\n    { \"repeat\": 20, \"until\": { \"tool\": \"js\", \"args\": { \"code\": \"return done\" } }, \"steps\": [...] }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Workflow Options\n\n```bash\n--file, -f <path>     # Load from JSON file\n--dry-run             # Parse and validate without executing\n--on-error stop|continue  # Error handling (default: stop)\n--step-delay <ms>     # Delay between steps (default: 100, 0 to disable)\n--no-auto-wait        # Disable automatic waits\n--json                # Structured JSON output\n```\n\n**Auto-waits:** Commands automatically wait for completion:\n- Navigation (`go`, `back`, `forward`) → waits for page load\n- Clicks, key presses, form fills → waits for DOM stability\n- Tab switches → waits for tab to load\n\n**Why use `do`?** Instead of 6-8 separate CLI calls with LLM orchestration between each, a workflow executes deterministically. Faster, cheaper, and more reliable.\n\n## Error Diagnostics\n\n```bash\n# Auto-capture screenshot + console on failure\nsurf wait.element \".missing\" --auto-capture --timeout 2000\n# Saves to /tmp/surf-error-*.png\n```\n\n## Common Options\n\n```bash\n--tab-id <id>         # Target specific tab\n--window-id <id>      # Target specific window\n--json                # Raw JSON output\n--auto-capture        # Screenshot + console on error\n--timeout <ms>        # Override default timeout\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n1. **First CDP operation is slow** (~5-8s) - debugger attachment overhead, subsequent calls fast\n2. **Use refs from page.read** for reliable element targeting over CSS selectors\n3. **JS method for contenteditable** - Modern editors (ChatGPT, Claude, Notion) need `--method js`\n4. **Named tabs for workflows** - `tab.name app` then `tab.switch app`\n5. **Auto-capture for debugging** - `--auto-capture` saves diagnostics on failure\n6. **AI tools use browser session** - Must be logged into the service, no API keys needed\n7. **Grok validation** - Run `surf grok --validate` if queries fail to check UI changes\n8. **Long timeouts for thinking models** - ChatGPT o1, Grok thinking can take 60+ seconds\n9. **Use `surf do` for multi-step tasks** - Reduces token overhead and improves reliability\n10. **Dry-run workflows first** - `surf do ''...'' --dry-run` validates without executing\n11. **Window isolation** - Use `window.new` + `--window-id` to keep agent work separate from your browsing\n12. **Semantic locators** - `locate.role`, `locate.text`, `locate.label` for more robust element finding\n13. **Frame context** - Use `frame.switch` before interacting with iframe content\n\n## Socket API\n\nFor programmatic access:\n\n```bash\necho ''{\"type\":\"tool_request\",\"method\":\"execute_tool\",\"params\":{\"tool\":\"tab.list\",\"args\":{}},\"id\":\"1\"}'' | nc -U /tmp/surf.sock\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:31:56.331Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automation Agents needing advanced browser control via CLI or Unix socket.","zh":"适用于需要通过CLI或Unix套接字进行高级浏览器控制的自动化代理。","ja":"CLIまたはUnixソケットを介した高度なブラウザ制御が必要な自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"CLI 또는 Unix 소켓을 통해 고급 브라우저 제어가 필요한 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de automatización que necesitan control avanzado del navegador mediante CLI o socket Unix.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''automatisation nécessitant un contrôle avancé du navigateur via CLI ou socket Unix.","de":"Ideal für Automatisierungs-Agents, die eine erweiterte Browsersteuerung über CLI oder Unix-Socket benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Automação que necessitam de controlo avançado do navegador via CLI ou soquete Unix.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, которым требуется расширенное управление браузером через CLI или Unix-сокет.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الأتمتة الذين يحتاجون إلى تحكم متقدم في المتصفح عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) أو مقبس يونكس (Unix socket)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to control Chrome browser programmatically using Unix socket or CLI commands, enabling automation of tasks like navigation, scrolling, and form filling via protocols and tools like CLI and Unix socket.","zh":"赋予代理程序通过Unix套接字或CLI命令以编程方式控制Chrome浏览器的能力，使得可以通过协议和工具（如CLI和Unix套接字）自动执行导航、滚动和表单填充等任务。","ja":"エージェントがUnixソケットまたはCLIコマンドを使用してChromeブラウザをプログラム的に制御できるようにし、CLIおよびUnixソケットなどのプロトコルおよびツールを使用して、ナビゲーション、スクロール、フォーム入力などのタスクを自動化できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 Unix 소켓 또는 CLI 명령을 사용하여 Chrome 브라우저를 프로그래밍 방식으로 제어할 수 있도록 해주어, CLI 및 Unix 소켓과 같은 프로토콜 및 도구를 사용하여 네비게이션, 스크롤, 폼 입력 등과 같은 작업을 자동화할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes controlar el navegador Chrome de forma programática utilizando socket Unix o comandos CLI, lo que posibilita la automatización de tareas como navegación, desplazamiento y llenado de formularios mediante protocolos y herramientas como CLI y socket Unix.","fr":"Permet aux agents de contrôler le navigateur Chrome par programmation en utilisant un socket Unix ou des commandes CLI, permettant l''automatisation de tâches telles que la navigation, le défilement et le remplissage de formulaires via des protocoles et des outils comme CLI et socket Unix.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, den Chrome-Browser programmgesteuert über Unix-Socket oder CLI-Befehle zu steuern, was die Automatisierung von Aufgaben wie Navigation, Scrollen und Formularausfüllen über Protokolle und Tools wie CLI und Unix-Socket ermöglicht.","pt":"Permite que os agentes controlem o navegador Chrome programaticamente usando soquete Unix ou comandos CLI, possibilitando a automação de tarefas como navegação, rolagem e preenchimento de formulários através de protocolos e ferramentas como CLI e soquete Unix.","ru":"Позволяет агентам программно управлять браузером Chrome с использованием Unix-сокета или команд CLI, обеспечивая автоматизацию таких задач, как навигация, прокрутка и заполнение форм, с помощью протоколов и инструментов, таких как CLI и Unix-сокет.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من التحكم في متصفح Chrome برمجياً باستخدام مقبس يونكس (Unix socket) أو أوامر واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI)، مما يتيح أتمتة مهام مثل التنقل والتمرير وملء النماذج عبر البروتوكولات وأدوات مثل CLI ومقبس يونكس."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating browser navigation and interaction","Generating automated tests for web applications","Controlling browser performance and debugging"],"zh":["自动化浏览器导航和交互","为Web应用程序生成自动化测试","控制浏览器性能和调试"],"ja":["ブラウザのナビゲーションとインタラクションの自動化","Webアプリケーションの自動テストの生成","ブラウザのパフォーマンスとデバッグの制御"],"ko":["브라우저 네비게이션 및 상호 작용 자동화","웹 애플리케이션 자동 테스트 생성","브라우저 성능 및 디버깅 제어"],"es":["Automatización de navegación e interacción del navegador","Generación de pruebas automatizadas para aplicaciones web","Control del rendimiento y depuración del navegador"],"fr":["Automatisation de la navigation et de l''interaction du navigateur","Génération de tests automatisés pour applications web","Contrôle des performances et débogage du navigateur"],"de":["Automatisierung der Browser-Navigation und -Interaktion","Erstellung automatisierter Tests für Webanwendungen","Steuerung der Browserleistung und Debugging"],"pt":["Automatização de navegação e interação no navegador","Geração de testes automatizados para aplicações web","Controlo de desempenho e depuração do navegador"],"ru":["Автоматизация навигации и взаимодействия в браузере","Создание автоматизированных тестов для веб-приложений","Управление производительностью браузера и отладка"],"ar":["أتمتة التنقل والتفاعل في المتصفح","إنشاء اختبارات آلية للتطبيقات الويب","التحكم في أداء المتصفح وتصحيح الأخطاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Chrome browser installation","Limited to Chrome browser control"],"zh":["需要安装Chrome浏览器","仅限于Chrome浏览器控制"],"ja":["Chromeブラウザのインストールが必要","Chromeブラウザの制御のみ"],"ko":["Chrome 브라우저 설치 필요","Chrome 브라우저 제어만 가능"],"es":["Requiere la instalación del navegador Chrome","Limitado al control del navegador Chrome"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation du navigateur Chrome","Limité au contrôle du navigateur Chrome"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation des Chrome-Browsers","Beschränkt auf die Steuerung des Chrome-Browsers"],"pt":["Requer a instalação do navegador Chrome","Limitado ao controlo do navegador Chrome"],"ru":["Требует установки браузера Chrome","Ограничено управлением браузером Chrome"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت مت