"prowler-commit 是一个代码提交规范，确保您的 Git 提交清晰、简洁、易于理解。","ja":"prowler-commit は、Git コミットを明確で簡潔で理解しやすいものにするためのコミット規約です。","ko":"prowler-commit 은 Git 커밋을 명확하고 간결하며 이해하기 쉬운 형태로 유지하기 위한 코드 커밋 규칙입니다.","es":"Prowler Commit es un conjunto de reglas para commits convencionales que mejoran la calidad y la claridad del código","fr":"Prowler Commit est un ensemble de règles pour les commits conventionnels qui améliorent la qualité et la clarté du code","de":"Prowler Commit ist eine Sammlung von Regeln für konventionelle Commits, die die Qualität und Klarheit des Codes verbessern","pt":"O prowler-commit é uma habilidade que fornece as melhores práticas para commits, garantindo que o seu código seja claro e conciso.","ru":"prowler-commit — это навык, который предоставляет лучшие практики для коммитов, гарантируя, что ваш код будет ясным и кратким.","ar":"prowler-commit هو مهارة تقدم أفضل الممارسات للاستحواذ، مما يضمن وضوح كودك ووضوحه","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["使用 conventional-commits 格式","保持第一行在 72 个字符以内","在提交前询问用户确认","避免过度具体的描述","不包含实现细节在标题中"],"ja":["conventional-commits フォーマットを使用","最初の行を 72 文字以内に保つ","コミット前にユーザーに確認する","詳細すぎる説明を避ける","タイトルに実装詳細を含めない"],"ko":["conventional-commits 형식을 사용","첫 번째 줄을 72 자 이내로 유지","커밋 전 사용자 확인을 요청","과도한 자세한 설명을避免","제목에 구현 세부 정보를 포함하지 않음"],"es":["Uso de formato de commits convencionales","Límite de 72 caracteres en la primera línea","Solicitud de confirmación del usuario antes de commitear","Evitación de detalles de implementación en el título","Prohibición del uso de `-n` y `git push --force`"],"fr":["Utilisation du format de commits conventionnels","Limite de 72 caractères dans la première ligne","Demande de confirmation de l''utilisateur avant de commiter","Évitement des détails d''implémentation dans le titre","Interdiction de l''utilisation de `-n` et `git push --force`"],"de":["Verwendung des Formats für konventionelle Commits","Begrenzung auf 72 Zeichen in der ersten Zeile","Anfrage der Benutzerbestätigung vor dem Committen","Vermeidung von Implementierungsdetails im Titel","Verbot der Verwendung von `-n` und `git push --force`"],"pt":["Uso de formato conventional-commits","Manutenção da primeira linha under 72 caracteres","Solicitação de confirmação do usuário antes de commitar","Evitar detalhes de implementação no título","Evitar uso de flags destrutivas"],"ru":["Использование формата conventional-commits","Сохранение первой строки под 72 символами","Запрос подтверждения пользователя перед коммитом","Избегание деталей реализации в заголовке","Избегание использования флагов с разрушительным эффектом"],"ar":["استخدام تنسيق conventional-commits","الحفاظ على السطر الأول أقل من 72 حرف","طلب تأكيد المستخدم قبل الاستحواذ","تجنب التفاصيل التنفيذية في العنوان","تجنب استخدام أعلام مدمرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码提交规范","Git 提交最佳实践","conventional-commits","代码格式化","提交前确认","避免过度具体的描述"],"ja":["コミット規約","Git コミットベストプラクティス","conventional-commits","コードフォーマット","コミット前確認","詳細すぎる説明の避け方"],"ko":["코드 커밋 규칙","Git 커밋 모범 사례","conventional-commits","코드 형식화","커밋 전 확인","과도한 자세한 설명 피하기"],"es":["commits convencionales","mejores prácticas de desarrollo","git","desarrollo de software","calidad del código","claridad del código"],"fr":["commits conventionnels","meilleures pratiques de développement","git","développement de logiciels","qualité du code","clarté du code"],"de":["konventionelle Commits","Best Practices für die Entwicklung","git","Softwareentwicklung","Codequalität","Codeklarheit"],"pt":["prowler-commit","conventional-commits","melhores práticas para commits","qualidade de código","desenvolvimento de software","git"],"ru":["prowler-commit","conventional-commits","лучшие практики для коммитов","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения","git"],"ar":["prowler-commit","conventional-commits","أفضل الممارسات للاستحواذ","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","git"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.398Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prowler-commit","description":">","version":"1.1.0","bodyPreview":"## Critical Rules\n\n- ALWAYS use conventional-commits format: `type(scope): description`\n- ALWAYS keep the first line under 72 characters\n- ALWAYS ask for user confirmation before committing\n- NEVER be overly specific (avoid counts like \"6 subsections\", \"3 files\")\n- NEVER include implementation details in the title\n- NEVER use `-n` flag unless user explicitly requests it\n- NEVER use `git push --force` or `git push -f` (destructive, rewrites history)\n- NEVER proactively offer to commit - wait for","body":"## Critical Rules\n\n- ALWAYS use conventional-commits format: `type(scope): description`\n- ALWAYS keep the first line under 72 characters\n- ALWAYS ask for user confirmation before committing\n- NEVER be overly specific (avoid counts like \"6 subsections\", \"3 files\")\n- NEVER include implementation details in the title\n- NEVER use `-n` flag unless user explicitly requests it\n- NEVER use `git push --force` or `git push -f` (destructive, rewrites history)\n- NEVER proactively offer to commit - wait for user to explicitly request it\n\n---\n\n## Commit Format\n\n```\ntype(scope): concise description\n\n- Key change 1\n- Key change 2\n- Key change 3\n```\n\n### Types\n\n| Type | Use When |\n|------|----------|\n| `feat` | New feature or functionality |\n| `fix` | Bug fix |\n| `docs` | Documentation only |\n| `chore` | Maintenance, dependencies, configs |\n| `refactor` | Code change without feature/fix |\n| `test` | Adding or updating tests |\n| `perf` | Performance improvement |\n| `style` | Formatting, no code change |\n\n### Scopes\n\n| Scope | When |\n|-------|------|\n| `api` | Changes in `api/` |\n| `ui` | Changes in `ui/` |\n| `sdk` | Changes in `prowler/` |\n| `mcp` | Changes in `mcp_server/` |\n| `skills` | Changes in `skills/` |\n| `ci` | Changes in `.github/` |\n| `docs` | Changes in `docs/` |\n| *omit* | Multiple scopes or root-level |\n\n---\n\n## Good vs Bad Examples\n\n### Title Line\n\n```\n# GOOD - Concise and clear\nfeat(api): add provider connection retry logic\nfix(ui): resolve dashboard loading state\nchore(skills): add Celery documentation\ndocs: update installation guide\n\n# BAD - Too specific or verbose\nfeat(api): add provider connection retry logic with exponential backoff and jitter (3 retries max)\nchore(skills): add comprehensive Celery documentation covering 8 topics\nfix(ui): fix the bug in dashboard component on line 45\n```\n\n### Body (Bullet Points)\n\n```\n# GOOD - High-level changes\n- Add retry mechanism for failed connections\n- Document task composition patterns\n- Expand configuration reference\n\n# BAD - Too detailed\n- Add retry with max_retries=3, backoff=True, jitter=True\n- Add 6 subsections covering chain, group, chord\n- Update lines 45-67 in dashboard.tsx\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Analyze changes**\n   ```bash\n   git status\n   git diff --stat HEAD\n   git log -3 --oneline  # Check recent commit style\n   ```\n\n2. **Draft commit message**\n   - Choose appropriate type and scope\n   - Write concise title (< 72 chars)\n   - Add 2-5 bullet points for significant changes\n\n3. **Present to user for confirmation**\n   - Show files to be committed\n   - Show proposed message\n   - Wait for explicit confirmation\n\n4. **Execute commit**\n   ```bash\n   git add <files>\n   git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n   type(scope): description\n\n   - Change 1\n   - Change 2\n   EOF\n   )\"\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```\nSingle file changed?\n├─ Yes → May omit body, title only\n└─ No → Include body with key changes\n\nMultiple scopes affected?\n├─ Yes → Omit scope: `feat: description`\n└─ No → Include scope: `feat(api): description`\n\nFixing a bug?\n├─ User-facing → fix(scope): description\n└─ Internal/dev → chore(scope): fix description\n\nAdding documentation?\n├─ Code docs (docstrings) → Part of feat/fix\n└─ Standalone docs → docs: or docs(scope):\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\n# Check current state\ngit status\ngit diff --stat HEAD\n\n# Standard commit\ngit add <files>\ngit commit -m \"type(scope): description\"\n\n# Multi-line commit\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ntype(scope): description\n\n- Change 1\n- Change 2\nEOF\n)\"\n\n# Amend last commit (same message)\ngit commit --amend --no-edit\n\n# Amend with new message\ngit commit --amend -m \"new message\"\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:34:19.845Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Git-based AI Agents requiring standardized commit formatting and history management.","zh":"适用于基于 Git 的 AI Agent，需要标准化的提交格式和历史管理。","ja":"Git ベースの AI エージェントに適しており、標準化されたコミット形式と履歴管理を必要とする。","ko":"Git 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 표준화된 커밋 형식 및 기록 관리가 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA basados en Git que requieren un formato de confirmación estandarizado y gestión de historial.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA basés sur Git nécessitant un format de commit standardisé et une gestion d''historique.","de":"Ideal für Git-basierte KI-Agents, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Format und eine Historienverwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA baseados em Git que exigem formatação de commit padronizada e gerenciamento de histórico.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе Git, требующих стандартизированного форматирования коммитов и управления историей.","ar":"مثالي للأعضاء الذكية القائمة على Git التي تتطلب تنسيقًا قياسيًا للالتزام وتحكمًا في التاريخ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce conventional-commits format, ensuring descriptive commit titles and preventing destructive git push operations, all while maintaining a clean history through strict adherence to rules like avoiding `-n` flags and `git push --force` commands.","zh":"赋予代理人执行 conventional-commits 格式的权力，确保描述性的提交标题，并防止破坏性的 Git 推送操作，同时通过严格遵守规则（如避免 `-n` 标志和 `git push --force` 命令）保持干净的历史记录。","ja":"conventional-commits 形式の適用をエージェントに可能にし、記述的なコミットタイトルを保証し、破壊的な Git プッシュ操作を防ぎ、同時に規則（例： `-n` フラグと `git push --force` コマンドの回避）を厳密に遵守することでクリーンな履歴を維持する。","ko":"에이전트가 conventional-commits 형식을 강제하여 설명적인 커밋 제목을 보장하고, 파괴적인 Git 푸시 연산을 방지하면서 규칙을 엄격히 준수함으로써 깨끗한 기록을 유지할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar el formato conventional-commits, garantizando títulos de commit descriptivos y evitando operaciones de git push destructivas, todo mientras mantiene una historia limpia a través de una estricta adhesión a reglas como evitar las banderas `-n` y los comandos `git push --force`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer le format conventional-commits, garantissant des titres de commit descriptifs et évitant les opérations de git push destructrices, le tout en maintenant une histoire propre grâce à une stricte adhésion à des règles comme l''évitement des drapeaux `-n` et des commandes `git push --force`.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das conventional-commits-Format durchzusetzen, wodurch beschreibende Commit-Titel sichergestellt und destruktive git push-Vorgänge verhindert werden, während gleichzeitig eine saubere Historie durch strikte Einhaltung von Regeln wie dem Vermeiden von `-n`-Flags und `git push --force`-Befehlen aufrechterhalten wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes imponham o formato conventional-commits, garantindo títulos de commit descritivos e prevenindo operações de git push destrutivas, mantendo ao mesmo tempo um histórico limpo por meio da adesão estrita a regras como evitar sinalizadores `-n` e comandos `git push --force`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить формат conventional-commits, гарантируя описательные названия коммитов и предотвращая разрушительные операции git push, а также поддерживая чистую историю посредством строгого соблюдения правил, таких как избежание флагов `-n` и команд `git push --force`.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء فرض تنسيق conventional-commits، مما يضمن عناوين الالتزام الوصفية ومنع عمليات git push التدميرية، مع الحفاظ في الوقت نفسه على سجل نظيف من خلال الالتزام الصارم بقواعد مثل تجنب أعلام `-n` وأوامر `git push --force`."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing commit messages with type and scope","Preventing accidental force pushes","Automating commit validation for adherence to critical rules"],"zh":["以类型和范围标准化提交消息","防止意外的强制推送","自动验证提交以遵守关键规则"],"ja":["種類とスコープによるコミットメッセージの標準化","事故的な強制プッシュの防止","重要な規則への準拠を自動的に検証するためのコミットの検証"],"ko":["유형 및 범위로 커밋 메시지를 표준화","사고적인 강제 푸시 방지","중요한 규칙을 준수하기 위한 커밋 자동 검증"],"es":["Estandarizar los mensajes de commit con tipo y alcance","Prevenir empujes forzados accidentales","Automatizar la validación de commits para la adhesión a reglas críticas"],"fr":["Standardiser les messages de commit avec type et portée","Prévenir les poussées forcées accidentelles","Automatiser la validation des commits pour l''adhésion aux règles critiques"],"de":["Standardisieren von Commit-Nachrichten mit Typ und Umfang","Verhindern von unbeabsichtigten force pushes","Automatisieren der Commit-Validierung für die Einhaltung kritischer Regeln"],"pt":["Padronizar mensagens de commit com tipo e escopo","Prevenir pushes forçados acidentais","Automatizar validação de commit para aderência a regras críticas"],"ru":["Стандартизировать сообщения коммитов с типом и объемом","Предотвратить случайные принудительные 푸ши","Автоматизировать проверку коммитов на соблюдение критических правил"],"ar":["تقييس رسائل الالتزام بنوعها ونطاقها","منع عمليات الدفع القسرية العرضية","توفير التحقق التلقائي من الالتزامات لامتثالها للقواعد الحرجة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git integration","Adheres to conventional-commits format strictly","Needs user confirmation for commits"],"zh":["需要 Git 集成","严格遵守 conventional-commits 格式","需要用户确认提交"],"ja":["Git 統合の必要性","conventional-commits 形式の厳格な遵守","コミットのユーザー確認の必要性"],"ko":["Git 통합 필요","conventional-commits 형식의 엄격한 준수","커밋 사용자 확인 필요"],"es":["Requiere integración con Git","Se adhiere estrictamente al formato conventional-commits","Necesita confirmación del usuario para los commits"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Git","Adhère strictement au format conventional-commits","Nécessite une confirmation de l''utilisateur pour les commits"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Integration","Hält sich streng an das conventional-commits-Format","Benötigt Benutzerbestätigung für Commits"],"pt":["Exige integração com o Git","Adere estritamente ao formato conventional-commits","Necessita confirmação do usuário para commits"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Git","Соблюдает формат conventional-commits строго","Требует подтверждения пользователя для коммитов"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع Git","يلتزم بتنسيق conventional-commits بشكل صارم","يحتاج إلى تأكيد المستخدم للالتزامات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
