"Asignación de controles de cumplimiento","Soporte para AWS, Azure y GCP"],"fr":["Création de cadres de conformité pour les fournisseurs de cloud","Ajout de exigences aux cadres existants","Mapping des contrôles de conformité","Prise en charge d''AWS, Azure et GCP"],"de":["Erstellung von Compliance-Frameworks für Cloud-Anbieter","Hinzufügen von Anforderungen zu bestehenden Frameworks","Zuweisung von Compliance-Controllen","Unterstützung für AWS, Azure und GCP"],"pt":["Criação de estruturas de conformidade para provedores de nuvem","Adição de requisitos a estruturas de conformidade existentes","Mapeamento de verificações para controles de conformidade","Suporte a provedores como AWS, Azure e GCP"],"ru":["Создание структур соответствия для провайдеров облачных услуг","Добавление требований к существующим структурам соответствия","Сопоставление проверок с контролями соответствия","Поддержка провайдеров AWS, Azure и GCP"],"ar":["إنشاء هياكل مطابقة لموفري خدمات السحابة","إضافة متطلبات إلى هياكل مطابقة موجودة","ربط الفحوصات بضوابط المطابقة","دعم موفري خدمات مثل AWS و Azure و GCP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Prowler 合规性框架","云服务提供商","合规性要求","JSON 文件","AWS","Azure","GCP"],"ja":["Prowler コンプライアンス フレームワーク","クラウドサービス プロバイダー","コンプライアンス要件","JSON ファイル","AWS","Azure","GCP"],"ko":["Prowler 컴플라이언스 프레임워크","클라우드 서비스 공급자","컴플라이언스 요구 사항","JSON 파일","AWS","Azure","GCP"],"es":["Prowler Compliance","marco de cumplimiento","proveedores cloud","AWS","Azure","GCP","compliance cloud"],"fr":["Prowler Compliance","cadre de conformité","fournisseurs de cloud","AWS","Azure","GCP","conformité cloud"],"de":["Prowler Compliance","Compliance-Framework","Cloud-Anbieter","AWS","Azure","GCP","Cloud-Compliance"],"pt":["conformidade de nuvem","prowler compliance","estruturas de conformidade","provedores de nuvem","AWS","Azure","GCP"],"ru":["облачная соответствие","prowler compliance","структуры соответствия","провайдеры облачных услуг","AWS","Azure","GCP"],"ar":["مطابقة السحابة","prowler compliance","هياكل مطابقة","موفرو خدمات السحابة","AWS","Azure","GCP"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.398Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prowler-compliance","description":">","version":"1.1","bodyPreview":"## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Creating a new compliance framework for any provider\n- Adding requirements to existing frameworks\n- Mapping checks to compliance controls\n- Understanding compliance framework structures and attributes\n\n## Compliance Framework Location\n\nFrameworks are JSON files located in: `prowler/compliance/{provider}/{framework_name}_{provider}.json`\n\n**Supported Providers:**\n- `aws` - Amazon Web Services\n- `azure` - Microsoft Azure\n- `gcp` - Google Cloud Platform\n- `kub","body":"## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Creating a new compliance framework for any provider\n- Adding requirements to existing frameworks\n- Mapping checks to compliance controls\n- Understanding compliance framework structures and attributes\n\n## Compliance Framework Location\n\nFrameworks are JSON files located in: `prowler/compliance/{provider}/{framework_name}_{provider}.json`\n\n**Supported Providers:**\n- `aws` - Amazon Web Services\n- `azure` - Microsoft Azure\n- `gcp` - Google Cloud Platform\n- `kubernetes` - Kubernetes\n- `github` - GitHub\n- `m365` - Microsoft 365\n- `alibabacloud` - Alibaba Cloud\n- `cloudflare` - Cloudflare\n- `oraclecloud` - Oracle Cloud\n- `oci` - Oracle Cloud Infrastructure\n- `nhn` - NHN Cloud\n- `mongodbatlas` - MongoDB Atlas\n- `iac` - Infrastructure as Code\n- `llm` - Large Language Models\n\n## Base Framework Structure\n\nAll compliance frameworks share this base structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Framework\": \"FRAMEWORK_NAME\",\n  \"Name\": \"Full Framework Name with Version\",\n  \"Version\": \"X.X\",\n  \"Provider\": \"PROVIDER\",\n  \"Description\": \"Framework description...\",\n  \"Requirements\": [\n    {\n      \"Id\": \"requirement_id\",\n      \"Description\": \"Requirement description\",\n      \"Name\": \"Optional requirement name\",\n      \"Attributes\": [...],\n      \"Checks\": [\"check_name_1\", \"check_name_2\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Framework-Specific Attribute Structures\n\nEach framework type has its own attribute model. Below are the exact structures used by Prowler:\n\n### CIS (Center for Internet Security)\n\n**Framework ID format:** `cis_{version}_{provider}` (e.g., `cis_5.0_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"1.1\",\n  \"Description\": \"Maintain current contact details\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"account_maintain_current_contact_details\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Section\": \"1 Identity and Access Management\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"Optional subsection\",\n      \"Profile\": \"Level 1\",\n      \"AssessmentStatus\": \"Automated\",\n      \"Description\": \"Detailed attribute description\",\n      \"RationaleStatement\": \"Why this control matters\",\n      \"ImpactStatement\": \"Impact of implementing this control\",\n      \"RemediationProcedure\": \"Steps to fix the issue\",\n      \"AuditProcedure\": \"Steps to verify compliance\",\n      \"AdditionalInformation\": \"Extra notes\",\n      \"DefaultValue\": \"Default configuration value\",\n      \"References\": \"https://docs.example.com/reference\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Profile values:** `Level 1`, `Level 2`, `E3 Level 1`, `E3 Level 2`, `E5 Level 1`, `E5 Level 2`\n**AssessmentStatus values:** `Automated`, `Manual`\n\n---\n\n### ISO 27001\n\n**Framework ID format:** `iso27001_{year}_{provider}` (e.g., `iso27001_2022_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"A.5.1\",\n  \"Description\": \"Policies for information security should be defined...\",\n  \"Name\": \"Policies for information security\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"securityhub_enabled\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Category\": \"A.5 Organizational controls\",\n      \"Objetive_ID\": \"A.5.1\",\n      \"Objetive_Name\": \"Policies for information security\",\n      \"Check_Summary\": \"Summary of what is being checked\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** `Objetive_ID` and `Objetive_Name` use this exact spelling (not \"Objective\").\n\n---\n\n### ENS (Esquema Nacional de Seguridad - Spain)\n\n**Framework ID format:** `ens_rd2022_{provider}` (e.g., `ens_rd2022_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"op.acc.1.aws.iam.2\",\n  \"Description\": \"Proveedor de identidad centralizado\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"iam_check_saml_providers_sts\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"IdGrupoControl\": \"op.acc.1\",\n      \"Marco\": \"operacional\",\n      \"Categoria\": \"control de acceso\",\n      \"DescripcionControl\": \"Detailed control description in Spanish\",\n      \"Nivel\": \"alto\",\n      \"Tipo\": \"requisito\",\n      \"Dimensiones\": [\"trazabilidad\", \"autenticidad\"],\n      \"ModoEjecucion\": \"automatico\",\n      \"Dependencias\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Nivel values:** `opcional`, `bajo`, `medio`, `alto`\n**Tipo values:** `refuerzo`, `requisito`, `recomendacion`, `medida`\n**Dimensiones values:** `confidencialidad`, `integridad`, `trazabilidad`, `autenticidad`, `disponibilidad`\n\n---\n\n### MITRE ATT&CK\n\n**Framework ID format:** `mitre_attack_{provider}` (e.g., `mitre_attack_aws`)\n\nMITRE uses a different requirement structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Name\": \"Exploit Public-Facing Application\",\n  \"Id\": \"T1190\",\n  \"Tactics\": [\"Initial Access\"],\n  \"SubTechniques\": [],\n  \"Platforms\": [\"Containers\", \"IaaS\", \"Linux\", \"Network\", \"Windows\", \"macOS\"],\n  \"Description\": \"Adversaries may attempt to exploit a weakness...\",\n  \"TechniqueURL\": \"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"guardduty_is_enabled\", \"inspector2_is_enabled\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"AWSService\": \"Amazon GuardDuty\",\n      \"Category\": \"Detect\",\n      \"Value\": \"Minimal\",\n      \"Comment\": \"Explanation of how this service helps...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**For Azure:** Use `AzureService` instead of `AWSService`\n**For GCP:** Use `GCPService` instead of `AWSService`\n**Category values:** `Detect`, `Protect`, `Respond`\n**Value values:** `Minimal`, `Partial`, `Significant`\n\n---\n\n### NIST 800-53\n\n**Framework ID format:** `nist_800_53_revision_{version}_{provider}` (e.g., `nist_800_53_revision_5_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"ac_2_1\",\n  \"Name\": \"AC-2(1) Automated System Account Management\",\n  \"Description\": \"Support the management of system accounts...\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"iam_password_policy_minimum_length_14\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"ItemId\": \"ac_2_1\",\n      \"Section\": \"Access Control (AC)\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"Account Management (AC-2)\",\n      \"SubGroup\": \"AC-2(3) Disable Accounts\",\n      \"Service\": \"iam\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Generic Compliance (Fallback)\n\nFor frameworks without specific attribute models:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"requirement_id\",\n  \"Description\": \"Requirement description\",\n  \"Name\": \"Optional name\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"check_name\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"ItemId\": \"item_id\",\n      \"Section\": \"Section name\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"Subsection name\",\n      \"SubGroup\": \"Subgroup name\",\n      \"Service\": \"service_name\",\n      \"Type\": \"type\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### AWS Well-Architected Framework\n\n**Framework ID format:** `aws_well_architected_framework_{pillar}_pillar_aws`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"SEC01-BP01\",\n  \"Description\": \"Establish common guardrails...\",\n  \"Name\": \"Establish common guardrails\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"account_part_of_organizations\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Name\": \"Establish common guardrails\",\n      \"WellArchitectedQuestionId\": \"securely-operate\",\n      \"WellArchitectedPracticeId\": \"sec_securely_operate_multi_accounts\",\n      \"Section\": \"Security\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"Security foundations\",\n      \"LevelOfRisk\": \"High\",\n      \"AssessmentMethod\": \"Automated\",\n      \"Description\": \"Detailed description\",\n      \"ImplementationGuidanceUrl\": \"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### KISA ISMS-P (Korea)\n\n**Framework ID format:** `kisa_isms_p_{year}_{provider}` (e.g., `kisa_isms_p_2023_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"1.1.1\",\n  \"Description\": \"Requirement description\",\n  \"Name\": \"Requirement name\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"check_name\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Domain\": \"1. Management System\",\n      \"Subdomain\": \"1.1 Management System Establishment\",\n      \"Section\": \"1.1.1 Section Name\",\n      \"AuditChecklist\": [\"Checklist item 1\", \"Checklist item 2\"],\n      \"RelatedRegulations\": [\"Regulation 1\"],\n      \"AuditEvidence\": [\"Evidence type 1\"],\n      \"NonComplianceCases\": [\"Non-compliance example\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### C5 (Germany Cloud Computing Compliance Criteria Catalogue)\n\n**Framework ID format:** `c5_{provider}` (e.g., `c5_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"BCM-01\",\n  \"Description\": \"Requirement description\",\n  \"Name\": \"Requirement name\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"check_name\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Section\": \"BCM Business Continuity Management\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"BCM-01\",\n      \"Type\": \"Basic Criteria\",\n      \"AboutCriteria\": \"Description of criteria\",\n      \"ComplementaryCriteria\": \"Additional criteria\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### CCC (Cloud Computing Compliance)\n\n**Framework ID format:** `ccc_{provider}` (e.g., `ccc_aws`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"CCC.C01\",\n  \"Description\": \"Requirement description\",\n  \"Name\": \"Requirement name\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"check_name\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"FamilyName\": \"Cryptography & Key Management\",\n      \"FamilyDescription\": \"Family description\",\n      \"Section\": \"CCC.C01\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"Key Management\",\n      \"SubSectionObjective\": \"Objective description\",\n      \"Applicability\": [\"IaaS\", \"PaaS\", \"SaaS\"],\n      \"Recommendation\": \"Recommended action\",\n      \"SectionThreatMappings\": [{\"threat\": \"T1190\"}],\n      \"SectionGuidelineMappings\": [{\"guideline\": \"NIST\"}]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Prowler ThreatScore\n\n**Framework ID format:** `prowler_threatscore_{provider}` (e.g., `prowler_threatscore_aws`)\n\nProwler ThreatScore is a custom security scoring framework developed by Prowler that evaluates AWS account security based on **four main pillars**:\n\n| Pillar | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| **1. IAM** | Identity and Access Management controls (authentication, authorization, credentials) |\n| **2. Attack Surface** | Network exposure, public resources, security group rules |\n| **3. Logging and Monitoring** | Audit logging, threat detection, forensic readiness |\n| **4. Encryption** | Data at rest and in transit encryption |\n\n**Scoring System:**\n- **LevelOfRisk** (1-5): Severity of the security issue\n  - `5` = Critical (e.g., root MFA, public S3 buckets)\n  - `4` = High (e.g., user MFA, public EC2)\n  - `3` = Medium (e.g., password policies, encryption)\n  - `2` = Low\n  - `1` = Informational\n- **Weight**: Impact multiplier for score calculation\n  - `1000` = Critical controls (root security, public exposure)\n  - `100` = High-impact controls (user authentication, monitoring)\n  - `10` = Standard controls (password policies, encryption)\n  - `1` = Low-impact controls (best practices)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Id\": \"1.1.1\",\n  \"Description\": \"Ensure MFA is enabled for the ''root'' user account\",\n  \"Checks\": [\"iam_root_mfa_enabled\"],\n  \"Attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"Title\": \"MFA enabled for ''root''\",\n      \"Section\": \"1. IAM\",\n      \"SubSection\": \"1.1 Authentication\",\n      \"AttributeDescription\": \"The root user account holds the highest level of privileges within an AWS account. Enabling MFA enhances security by adding an additional layer of protection.\",\n      \"AdditionalInformation\": \"Enabling MFA enhances console security by requiring the authenticating user to both possess a time-sensitive key-generating device and have knowledge of their credentials.\",\n      \"LevelOfRisk\": 5,\n      \"Weight\": 1000\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Available for providers:** AWS, Kubernetes, M365\n\n---\n\n## Available Compliance Frameworks\n\n### AWS (41 frameworks)\n| Framework | File Name |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| CIS 1.4, 1.5, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0 | `cis_{version}_aws.json` |\n| ISO 27001:2013, 2022 | `iso27001_{year}_aws.json` |\n| NIST 800-53 Rev 4, 5 | `nist_800_53_revision_{version}_aws.json` |\n| NIST 800-171 Rev 2 | `nist_800_171_revision_2_aws.json` |\n| NIST CSF 1.1, 2.0 | `nist_csf_{version}_aws.json` |\n| PCI DSS 3.2.1, 4.0 | `pci_{version}_aws.json` |\n| HIPAA | `hipaa_aws.json` |\n| GDPR | `gdpr_aws.json` |\n| SOC 2 | `soc2_aws.json` |\n| FedRAMP Low/Moderate | `fedramp_{level}_revision_4_aws.json` |\n| ENS RD2022 | `ens_rd2022_aws.json` |\n| MITRE ATT&CK | `mitre_attack_aws.json` |\n| C5 Germany | `c5_aws.json` |\n| CISA | `cisa_aws.json` |\n| FFIEC | `ffiec_aws.json` |\n| RBI Cyber Security | `rbi_cyber_security_framework_aws.json` |\n| AWS Well-Architected | `aws_well_architected_framework_{pillar}_pillar_aws.json` |\n| AWS FTR | `aws_foundational_technical_review_aws.json` |\n| GxP 21 CFR Part 11, EU Annex 11 | `gxp_{standard}_aws.json` |\n| KISA ISMS-P 2023 | `kisa_isms_p_2023_aws.json` |\n| NIS2 | `nis2_aws.json` |\n\n### Azure (15+ frameworks)\n| Framework | File Name |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| CIS 2.0, 2.1, 3.0, 4.0 | `cis_{version}_azure.json` |\n| ISO 27001:2022 | `iso27001_2022_azure.json` |\n| ENS RD2022 | `ens_rd2022_azure.json` |\n| MITRE ATT&CK | `mitre_attack_azure.json` |\n| PCI DSS 4.0 | `pci_4.0_azure.json` |\n| NIST CSF 2.0 | `nist_csf_2.0_azure.json` |\n\n### GCP (15+ frameworks)\n| Framework | File Name |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| CIS 2.0, 3.0, 4.0 | `cis_{version}_gcp.json` |\n| ISO 27001:2022 | `iso27001_2022_gcp.json` |\n| HIPAA | `hipaa_gcp.json` |\n| MITRE ATT&CK | `mitre_attack_gcp.json` |\n| PCI DSS 4.0 | `pci_4.0_gcp.json` |\n| NIST CSF 2.0 | `nist_csf_2.0_gcp.json` |\n\n### Kubernetes (6 frameworks)\n| Framework | File Name |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| CIS 1.8, 1.10, 1.11 | `cis_{version}_kubernetes.json` |\n| ISO 27001:2022 | `iso27001_2022_kubernetes.json` |\n| PCI DSS 4.0 | `pci_4.0_kubernetes.json` |\n\n### Other Providers\n- **GitHub:** `cis_1.0_github.json`\n- **M365:** `cis_4.0_m365.json`, `iso27001_2022_m365.json`\n- **NHN:** `iso27001_2022_nhn.json`\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Requirement IDs**: Follow the original framework numbering exactly (e.g., \"1.1\", \"A.5.1\", \"T1190\", \"ac_2_1\")\n2. **Check Mapping**: Map to existing checks when possible. Use `Checks: []` for manual-only requirements\n3. **Completeness**: Include all framework requirements, even those without automated checks\n4. **Version Control**: Include framework version in `Name` and `Version` fields\n5. **File Naming**: Use format `{framework}_{version}_{provider}.json`\n6. **Validation**: Prowler validates JSON against Pydantic models at startup - invalid JSON will cause errors\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\n# List available frameworks for a provider\nprowler {provider} --list-compliance\n\n# Run scan with specific compliance framework\nprowler aws --compliance cis_5.0_aws\n\n# Run scan with multiple frameworks\nprowler aws --compliance cis_5.0_aws pci_4.0_aws\n\n# Output compliance report in multiple formats\nprowler aws --compliance cis_5.0_aws -M csv json html\n```\n\n## Code References\n\n- **Compliance Models:** `prowler/lib/check/compliance_models.py`\n- **Compliance Processing:** `prowler/lib/check/compliance.py`\n- **Compliance Output:** `prowler/lib/outputs/compliance/`\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Templates:** See [assets/](assets/) for framework JSON templates\n- **Documentation:** See [references/compliance-docs.md](references/compliance-docs.md) for additional resources\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:35:11.339Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Security Agents requiring comprehensive compliance framework management for AWS, Azure, and GCP providers.","zh":"适用于需要对AWS、Azure和GCP提供商进行全面合规框架管理的云安全代理的理想选择。","ja":"AWS、Azure、GCPプロバイダーに対する包括的なコンプライアンスフレームワーク管理を必要とするクラウドセキュリティエージェントに最適です。","ko":"AWS, Azure, GCP 제공업체에 대한 포괄적인 규정 준수 프레임워크 관리가 필요한 클라우드 보안 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Seguridad en la Nube que requieren una gestión de marco de cumplimiento integral para los proveedores AWS, Azure y GCP.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Sécurité Cloud nécessitant une gestion complète du cadre de conformité pour les fournisseurs AWS, Azure et GCP.","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Sicherheitsagenten, die eine umfassende Verwaltung des Compliance-Frameworks für die Anbieter AWS, Azure und GCP erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Segurança em Nuvem que exigem gestão abrangente de estruturas de conformidade para provedores AWS, Azure e GCP.","ru":"Идеально для агентов безопасности облака, требующих всестороннего управления каркасами соответствия для провайдеров AWS, Azure и GCP.","ar":"مثالية لأجهزة العميل أمن السحابة التي تتطلب إدارة شاملة لإطار uygunluk لمزودي AWS و Azure و GCP."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create, modify, and map compliance frameworks using JSON files, supporting structured compliance attributes and controls for major cloud providers like AWS, Azure, and GCP, leveraging the prowler-compliance skill.","zh":"赋予代理创建、修改和映射合规框架的能力，使用JSON文件支持主要云提供商（如AWS、Azure和GCP）结构化的合规属性和控制，利用prowler-compliance技能。","ja":"エージェントがJSONファイルを使用してコンプライアンスフレームワークを作成、変更、管理できるようにし、AWS、Azure、GCPなどの主要クラウドプロバイダーで構造化されたコンプライアンス属性とコントロールをサポートし、prowler-complianceスキルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 JSON 파일을 사용하여 규정 준수 프레임워크를 생성, 수정 및 매핑할 수 있도록 하며 주요 클라우드 제공업체(AWS, Azure, GCP 등)에서 구조화된 규정 준수 속성 및 제어를 지원하며 prowler-compliance 기술을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear, modificar y asignar marcos de cumplimiento utilizando archivos JSON, que admiten atributos y controles de cumplimiento estructurados para los principales proveedores de la nube como AWS, Azure y GCP, aprovechando la habilidad de prowler-compliance.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer, de modifier et de mapper des cadres de conformité en utilisant des fichiers JSON, qui prennent en charge les attributs et les contrôles de conformité structurés pour les principaux fournisseurs de cloud tels que AWS, Azure et GCP, en exploitant la compétence prowler-compliance.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Compliance-Frameworks mithilfe von JSON-Dateien zu erstellen, zu ändern und zuzuordnen, die strukturierte Compliance-Attribute und -kontrollen für große Cloud-Anbieter wie AWS, Azure und GCP unterstützen, indem die prowler-Compliance-Fähigkeit genutzt wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem, modifiquem e mapeiem estruturas de conformidade usando arquivos JSON, suportando atributos e controles de conformidade estruturados para principais provedores de nuvem como AWS, Azure e GCP, aproveitando a habilidade prowler-compliance.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать, изменять и сопоставлять каркасы соответствия с помощью файлов JSON, поддерживающих структурированные атрибуты и контроли соответствия для основных облачных провайдеров, таких как AWS, Azure и GCP, используя навык prowler-compliance.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء و تعديل و تعيين إطارات uygunluk باستخدام ملفات JSON، و دعم سمات وضوابط التأهيل المنظّمة للمزودين الرئيسيين لسحابة مثل AWS و Azure و GCP، و الاستفادة من مهارة prowler-compliance."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new compliance frameworks for cloud providers","Mapping checks to existing compliance controls in JSON files","Understanding and modifying compliance framework structures for AWS, Azure, or GCP"],"zh":["为云提供商创建新的合规框架","将检查映射到JSON文件中的现有合规控制","了解和修改AWS、Azure或GCP的合规框架结构"],"ja":["クラウドプロバイダー用の新しいコンプライアンスフレームワークを作成する","JSONファイル内の既存のコンプライアンスコントロールにチェックをマッピングする","AWS、Azure、またはGCPのコンプライアンスフレームワーク構造を理解し、変更する"],"ko":["클라우드 제공업체를 위한 새로운 규정 준수 프레임워크를 생성하는 것","JSON 파일 내의 기존 규정 준수 제어에 대한 검사를 매핑하는 것","AWS, Azure 또는 GCP의 규정 준수 프레임워크 구조를 이해하고 수정하는 것"],"es":["Crear nuevos marcos de cumplimiento para proveedores de la nube","Asignar comprobaciones a controles de cumplimiento existentes en archivos JSON","Comprender y modificar estructuras de marcos de cumplimiento para AWS, Azure o GCP"],"fr":["Créer de nouveaux cadres de conformité pour les fournisseurs de cloud","Mapper les vérifications aux contrôles de conformité existants dans les fichiers JSON","Comprendre et modifier les structures de cadres de conformité pour AWS, Azure ou GCP"],"de":["Erstellen neuer Compliance-Frameworks für Cloud-Anbieter","Zuordnen von Prüfungen zu bestehenden Compliance-Kontrollen in JSON-Dateien","Verstehen und Ändern von Compliance-Framework-Strukturen für AWS, Azure oder GCP"],"pt":["Criar novas estruturas de conformidade para provedores de nuvem","Mapear verificações para controles de conformidade existentes em arquivos JSON","Entender e modificar estruturas de conformidade para AWS, Azure ou GCP"],"ru":["Создание новых каркасов соответствия для облачных провайдеров","Сопоставление проверок с существующими контролями соответствия в файлах JSON","Понимание и изменение каркасов соответствия для AWS, Azure или GCP"],"ar":["إنشاء إطارات جديدة من التأهيل للمزودين السحABIة","تعيين الفحوصات إلى ضوابط التأهيل الحالية في ملفات JSON","فهم وتعديل هياكل التأهيل لـ AWS و Azure و GCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires specific provider support (currently AWS, Azure, GCP, and Kubernetes)","Framework files must be in JSON format and located in the prowler/compliance directory"],"zh":["需要特定提供商的支持（目前支持AWS、Azure、GCP和Kubernetes）","框架文件必须是JSON格式并位于prowler/compliance目录中"],"ja":["特定プロバイダーのサポートが必要（現在はAWS、Azure、GCP、Kubernetesがサポート対象）","フレームワークファイルはJSON形式で、prowler/complianceディレクトリに配置する必要がある"],"ko":["특정 제공업체의 지원이 필요함(현재 AWS, Azure, GCP 및 Kubernetes가 지원됨)","프레임워크 파일은 JSON 형식이어야 하며 prowler/compliance 디렉토리에 위치해야 함"],"es":["Requiere soporte específico del proveedor (actualmente AWS, Azure, GCP y Kubernetes)","Los archivos de marco deben estar en formato JSON y ubicados en el directorio prowler/compliance"],"fr":["Nécessite un support spécifique du fournisseur (actuellement AWS, Azure, GCP et Kubernetes)","Les fichiers de cadre doivent être au format JSON et situés dans le répertoire prowler/compliance"],"de":["Benötigt spezifische Anbieterunterstützung (derzeit AWS, Azure, GCP und Kubernetes)","Framework-Dateien müssen im JSON-Format vorliegen und sich im Verzeichnis prowler/compliance befinden"],"pt":["Exige suporte específico do provedor (atualmente AWS, Azure, GCP e Kubernetes)","Arquivos de estrutura devem estar no formato JSON e localizados no diretório prowler/compliance"],"ru":["Требует специальной поддержки провайдера (в настоящее время AWS, Azure, GCP и Kubernetes)","Файлы каркаса должны быть в формате JSON и находиться в каталоге prowler/compliance"],"ar":["يتطلب دعمًا محددًا من المزود (حاليًا AWS و Azure و GCP و Kubernetes)","يجب أن تكون ملفات الإطار في تنسيق JSON و تقع في الدليل prowler/compliance"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":85}');
