do con R2","Límite de namespace aumentado","Compatibilidad con wrangler@4.59.2 y @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0"],"fr":["Stockage clé-valeur pour Cloudflare Workers","Améliorations des performances et de la latence","Lectures massives de l''API","Stockage hybride avec R2","Limite de namespace augmentée","Compatibilité avec wrangler@4.59.2 et @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0"],"de":["Schlüssel-Wert-Speicher für Cloudflare Workers","Leistungs- und Latenzverbesserungen","Massenlesungen von API","Hybrid-Speicher mit R2","Erhöhte Namespace-Grenze","Kompatibilität mit wrangler@4.59.2 und @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0"],"pt":["Armazenamento de chave-valor na nuvem","Desempenho melhorado com arquitetura redesenhada","Leitura em massa de até 100 chaves em uma solicitação","Aumento do limite de namespace","Latência reduzida com menos de 5ms de p99","Suporte a armazenamento híbrido com R2"],"ru":["Облачное хранилище ключ-значение","Улучшенная производительность с переработанной архитектурой","Массовое чтение до 100 ключей в одном запросе","Увеличение лимита namespace","Снижение задержки с менее 5мс p99","Поддержка гибридного хранилища с R2"],"ar":["تخزين القيم المفتاحية السحابي","تحسين الأداء مع هندسة معمارية معاد تصميمها","قراءة بالجملة تصل إلى 100 مفتاح في طلب واحد","زيادة حد Namespace","تقليل الكفاءة مع أقل من 5 ميلي ثانية من p99","دعم تخزين هجين مع R2"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","Workers","KV","R2","Namespace","Bulk reads API","Architecture redesign","Performance optimization"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","Workers","KV","R2","Namespace","Bulk reads API","Architecture redesign","Performance optimization"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","Workers","KV","R2","Namespace","Bulk reads API","Architecture redesign","Performance optimization"],"es":["Cloudflare KV","almacenamiento de clave-valor","Cloudflare Workers","desarrollo de aplicaciones","rendimiento y latencia","API de lecturas masivas","almacenamiento híbrido","namespace"],"fr":["Cloudflare KV","stockage clé-valeur","Cloudflare Workers","développement d''applications","performances et latence","API de lectures massives","stockage hybride","namespace"],"de":["Cloudflare KV","Schlüssel-Wert-Speicher","Cloudflare Workers","Anwendungsentwicklung","Leistung und Latenz","API-Massenlesungen","Hybrid-Speicher","Namespace"],"pt":["Cloudflare KV","armazenamento de chave-valor na nuvem","desenvolvedores","solução de armazenamento","escalabilidade","desempenho","arquitetura redesenhada","leitura em massa","limite de namespace"],"ru":["Cloudflare KV","облачное хранилище ключ-значение","разработчики","решение для хранения","масштабируемость","производительность","переработанная архитектура","массовое чтение","лимит namespace"],"ar":["Cloudflare KV","تخزين القيم المفتاحية السحابي","المطورين","حل لتخزين","التمكين","الأداء","الهندسة المعمارية المعاد تصميمها","قراءة بالجملة","حد Namespace"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloudflare-kv","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Cloudflare Workers KV\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **August 2025**: Architecture redesign (40x performance gain, <5ms p99 latency, hybrid storage with R2)\n- **April 2025**: Bulk reads API (retrieve up to 100 keys in single request, counts as 1 operation)\n- **January 2025**: Namespace limit increase","body":"# Cloudflare Workers KV\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **August 2025**: Architecture redesign (40x performance gain, <5ms p99 latency, hybrid storage with R2)\n- **April 2025**: Bulk reads API (retrieve up to 100 keys in single request, counts as 1 operation)\n- **January 2025**: Namespace limit increased (200 → 1,000 namespaces per account for Free and Paid plans)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nnpx wrangler kv namespace create MY_NAMESPACE\n# Output: [[kv_namespaces]] binding = \"MY_NAMESPACE\" id = \"<UUID>\"\n```\n\n**wrangler.jsonc:**\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [{\n    \"binding\": \"MY_NAMESPACE\",  // Access as env.MY_NAMESPACE\n    \"id\": \"<production-uuid>\",\n    \"preview_id\": \"<preview-uuid>\"  // Optional: local dev\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n```typescript\ntype Bindings = { MY_NAMESPACE: KVNamespace };\n\napp.post(''/set/:key'', async (c) => {\n  await c.env.MY_NAMESPACE.put(c.req.param(''key''), await c.req.text());\n  return c.json({ success: true });\n});\n\napp.get(''/get/:key'', async (c) => {\n  const value = await c.env.MY_NAMESPACE.get(c.req.param(''key''));\n  return value ? c.json({ value }) : c.json({ error: ''Not found'' }, 404);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## KV API Reference\n\n### Read Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Get single key\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'');  // string | null\nconst data = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''json'' });  // object | null\nconst buffer = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''arrayBuffer'' });\nconst stream = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''stream'' });\n\n// Get with cache (minimum 60s)\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 300 });  // 5 min edge cache\n\n// Bulk read (counts as 1 operation)\nconst values = await env.MY_KV.get([''key1'', ''key2'']);  // Map<string, string | null>\n\n// With metadata\nconst { value, metadata } = await env.MY_KV.getWithMetadata(''key'');\nconst result = await env.MY_KV.getWithMetadata([''key1'', ''key2'']);  // Bulk with metadata\n```\n\n### Write Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Basic write (max 1/second per key)\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''key'', ''value'');\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''user:123'', JSON.stringify({ name: ''John'' }));\n\n// With expiration\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''session'', data, { expirationTtl: 3600 });  // 1 hour\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''token'', value, { expiration: Math.floor(Date.now()/1000) + 86400 });\n\n// With metadata (max 1024 bytes)\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''config'', ''dark'', {\n  metadata: { updatedAt: Date.now(), version: 2 }\n});\n```\n\n**Critical Limits:**\n- Key: 512 bytes max\n- Value: 25 MiB max\n- Metadata: 1024 bytes max\n- Write rate: 1/second per key (429 error if exceeded)\n- Expiration: 60 seconds minimum\n\n### List Operations\n\n```typescript\n// List with pagination\nconst result = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'', limit: 1000, cursor });\n// result: { keys: [], list_complete: boolean, cursor?: string }\n\n// CRITICAL: Always check list_complete, not keys.length === 0\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'', cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n### Delete Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Delete single key\nawait env.MY_KV.delete(''key'');  // Always succeeds\n\n// Bulk delete (CLI only, up to 10,000 keys)\n// npx wrangler kv bulk delete --binding=MY_KV keys.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Caching Pattern with CacheTtl\n\n```typescript\nasync function getCachedData(kv: KVNamespace, key: string, fetchFn: () => Promise<any>, ttl = 300) {\n  const cached = await kv.get(key, { type: ''json'', cacheTtl: ttl });\n  if (cached) return cached;\n\n  const data = await fetchFn();\n  await kv.put(key, JSON.stringify(data), { expirationTtl: ttl * 2 });\n  return data;\n}\n```\n\n**Guidelines**: Minimum 60s, use for read-heavy workloads (100:1 read/write ratio)\n\n### Metadata Optimization\n\n```typescript\n// Store small values (<1024 bytes) in metadata to avoid separate get() calls\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''user:123'', '''', {\n  metadata: { status: ''active'', plan: ''pro'', lastSeen: Date.now() }\n});\n\n// list() returns metadata automatically (no additional get() calls)\nconst users = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'' });\nusers.keys.forEach(({ name, metadata }) => console.log(name, metadata.status));\n```\n\n### Understanding Hot vs Cold Keys\n\nKV performance varies based on key temperature:\n\n| Type | Response Time | When It Happens |\n|------|---------------|-----------------|\n| **Hot keys** | 6-8ms | Read 2+ times/minute per datacenter |\n| **Cold keys** | 100-300ms | Infrequently accessed, fetched from central storage |\n\n**Post-August 2025 Improvements**:\n- P90 for all KV Worker invocations: <12ms (was 22ms before)\n- Hot reads up to 3x faster\n- All operations faster by up to 20ms\n\n**Optimization**: Use key coalescing to make cold keys benefit from hot key caching:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: Many cold keys (300ms each)\nawait kv.put(''user:123:name'', ''John'');\nawait kv.put(''user:123:email'', ''john@example.com'');\nawait kv.put(''user:123:plan'', ''pro'');\n\n// Each read of a cold key: ~100-300ms\nconst name = await kv.get(''user:123:name'');    // Cold\nconst email = await kv.get(''user:123:email'');  // Cold\nconst plan = await kv.get(''user:123:plan'');    // Cold\n\n// ✅ Good: Single hot key (6-8ms)\nawait kv.put(''user:123'', JSON.stringify({\n  name: ''John'',\n  email: ''john@example.com'',\n  plan: ''pro''\n}));\n\n// Single read, cached as hot key: ~6-8ms\nconst user = JSON.parse(await kv.get(''user:123''));\n```\n\n**CacheTtl helps cold keys**: For infrequently-read data, `cacheTtl` reduces cold read latency.\n\n**Trade-off**: Coalescing requires read-modify-write for updates\n\n### Pagination Helper\n\n```typescript\nasync function* paginateKV(kv: KVNamespace, options: { prefix?: string } = {}) {\n  let cursor: string | undefined;\n  do {\n    const result = await kv.list({ ...options, cursor });\n    yield result.keys;\n    cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n  } while (cursor);\n}\n\n// Usage\nfor await (const keys of paginateKV(env.MY_KV, { prefix: ''user:'' })) {\n  processKeys(keys);\n}\n```\n\n### Rate Limit Retry with Exponential Backoff\n\n```typescript\nasync function putWithRetry(kv: KVNamespace, key: string, value: string, opts?: KVPutOptions) {\n  let attempts = 0, delay = 1000;\n  while (attempts < 5) {\n    try {\n      await kv.put(key, value, opts);\n      return;\n    } catch (error) {\n      if ((error as Error).message.includes(''429'')) {\n        attempts++;\n        if (attempts >= 5) throw new Error(''Max retry attempts'');\n        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));\n        delay *= 2;  // Exponential backoff\n      } else throw error;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Understanding Eventual Consistency\n\nKV is **eventually consistent** across Cloudflare''s global network (Aug 2025 redesign: hybrid storage, <5ms p99 latency):\n\n**How It Works:**\n1. Writes immediately visible in same location (read-your-own-write consistency within same POP)\n2. Other locations see update within ~60 seconds (or cacheTtl value)\n3. Cached reads may return stale data during propagation\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\n// Tokyo: Write\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''1'');\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''counter''); // \"1\" ✅ (same POP, RYOW)\n\n// London (within 60s): May be stale ⚠️\nconst value2 = await env.MY_KV.get(''counter''); // Might be old value\n\n// After 60+ seconds: Consistent ✅\n```\n\n**Read-Your-Own-Write (RYOW) Guarantee**: Since August 2025 redesign, requests routed through the **same Cloudflare point of presence** see their own writes immediately. Global consistency across different POPs still takes up to 60 seconds.\n\n**Timestamp Mitigation Pattern** (for critical consistency needs):\n```typescript\n// Use timestamp in key structure to avoid consistency issues\nconst timestamp = Date.now();\nawait kv.put(`user:123:${timestamp}`, userData);\n\n// Find latest using list with prefix\nconst result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:123:'' });\nconst latestKey = result.keys.sort((a, b) =>\n  parseInt(b.name.split('':'')[2]) - parseInt(a.name.split('':'')[2])\n).at(0);\n```\n\n**Use KV for**: Read-heavy workloads (100:1 ratio), config, feature flags, caching, user preferences\n**Don''t use KV for**: Financial transactions, strong consistency, >1/second writes per key, critical data\n\n**Need strong consistency?** Use [Durable Objects](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/)\n\n**Source**: [Redesigning Workers KV](https://blog.cloudflare.com/rearchitecting-workers-kv-for-redundancy/)\n\n---\n\n## Wrangler CLI Essentials\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nnpx wrangler kv namespace create MY_NAMESPACE [--preview]\n\n# Manage keys (add --remote flag to access production data)\nnpx wrangler kv key put --binding=MY_KV \"key\" \"value\" [--ttl=3600] [--metadata=''{}'']\nnpx wrangler kv key get --binding=MY_KV \"key\" [--remote]\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV [--prefix=\"user:\"] [--remote]\nnpx wrangler kv key delete --binding=MY_KV \"key\"\n\n# Bulk operations (up to 10,000 keys)\nnpx wrangler kv bulk put --binding=MY_KV data.json\nnpx wrangler kv bulk delete --binding=MY_KV keys.json\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT**: CLI commands default to **local storage**. Add `--remote` flag to access production/remote data.\n\n---\n\n## Development vs Production\n\n### Remote Bindings for Local Development (Wrangler 4.37+)\n\nConnect local Workers to production KV namespaces during development:\n\n**wrangler.jsonc:**\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [{\n    \"binding\": \"MY_KV\",\n    \"id\": \"production-uuid\",\n    \"remote\": true  // Connect to live KV\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n**How It Works:**\n- Local Worker code executes locally (fast iteration)\n- KV operations route to production namespace through proxy\n- No manual data seeding required\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Test against real production data without deploying\n- Fast local code execution with production data access\n- Faster feedback loop (no deploy-test cycle)\n\n**⚠️ Warning**: Writes affect production data. Consider using a staging namespace with `remote: true` instead of production.\n\n**Version Support:**\n- Wrangler 4.37.0+\n- @cloudflare/vite-plugin 1.13.0+\n- @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers 0.9.0+\n\n**Source**: [Remote bindings architecture](https://blog.cloudflare.com/connecting-to-production-the-architecture-of-remote-bindings/)\n\n---\n\n## Limits & Quotas\n\n| Feature | Free Plan | Paid Plan |\n|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| Reads per day | 100,000 | Unlimited |\n| Writes per day (different keys) | 1,000 | Unlimited |\n| **Writes per key per second** | **1** | **1** |\n| Operations per Worker invocation | 1,000 | 1,000 |\n| **Namespaces per account** | **1,000** | **1,000** |\n| Storage per account | 1 GB | Unlimited |\n| Key size | 512 bytes | 512 bytes |\n| Metadata size | 1024 bytes | 1024 bytes |\n| Value size | 25 MiB | 25 MiB |\n| Minimum cacheTtl | 60 seconds | 60 seconds |\n\n**Critical**: 1 write/second per key (429 if exceeded), bulk operations count as 1 operation, namespace limit increased from 200 → 1,000 (Jan 2025)\n\n---\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### 1. Rate Limit (429 Too Many Requests)\n**Cause**: Writing to same key >1/second\n**Solution**: Use retry with exponential backoff (see Advanced Patterns)\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''1'');\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''2''); // 429 error!\n\n// ✅ Good\nawait putWithRetry(env.MY_KV, ''counter'', ''2'');\n```\n\n### 2. Value Too Large\n**Cause**: Value exceeds 25 MiB\n**Solution**: Validate size before writing\n\n```typescript\nif (value.length > 25 * 1024 * 1024) throw new Error(''Value exceeds 25 MiB'');\n```\n\n### 3. Metadata Too Large\n**Cause**: Metadata exceeds 1024 bytes when serialized\n**Solution**: Validate serialized size\n\n```typescript\nconst serialized = JSON.stringify(metadata);\nif (serialized.length > 1024) throw new Error(''Metadata exceeds 1024 bytes'');\n```\n\n### 4. Invalid CacheTtl\n**Cause**: cacheTtl <60 seconds\n**Solution**: Use minimum 60\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Error\nawait env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 30 });\n\n// ✅ Correct\nawait env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 60 });\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### Always Do ✅\n\n1. Use bulk operations when reading multiple keys (counts as 1 operation)\n2. Set cacheTtl for frequently-read, infrequently-updated data (min 60s)\n3. Store small values (<1024 bytes) in metadata when using `list()` frequently\n4. Check `list_complete` when paginating, not `keys.length === 0`\n5. Use retry logic with exponential backoff for write operations\n6. Validate sizes before writing (key 512B, value 25MiB, metadata 1KB)\n7. Coalesce related keys for better caching performance\n8. Use KV for read-heavy workloads (100:1 read/write ratio ideal)\n\n### Never Do ❌\n\n1. Never write to same key >1/second (causes 429 rate limit errors)\n2. Never assume immediate global consistency (takes ~60 seconds to propagate)\n3. Never use KV for atomic operations (use Durable Objects instead)\n4. Never set cacheTtl <60 seconds (will fail)\n5. Never commit namespace IDs to public repos (use environment variables)\n6. Never exceed 1000 operations per invocation (use bulk operations)\n7. Never rely on write order (eventual consistency = no guarantees)\n8. Never forget to handle null values (`get()` returns `null` if key doesn''t exist)\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue 1: \"429 Too Many Requests\" on writes\n**Cause**: Writing to same key >1/second\n**Solution**: Consolidate writes or use retry with exponential backoff\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: Rate limit\nfor (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) await kv.put(''counter'', String(i));\n\n// ✅ Good: Single write\nawait kv.put(''counter'', ''9'');\n\n// ✅ Good: Retry with backoff\nawait putWithRetry(kv, ''counter'', String(i));\n```\n\n### Issue 2: Stale reads after write\n**Cause**: Eventual consistency (~60 seconds propagation)\n**Solution**: Accept stale reads, use Durable Objects for strong consistency, or implement app-level cache invalidation\n\n### Issue 3: \"Operations limit exceeded\"\n**Cause**: >1000 KV operations in single Worker invocation\n**Solution**: Use bulk operations\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: 5000 operations\nfor (const key of 5000keys) await kv.get(key);\n\n// ✅ Good: 1 operation\nconst values = await kv.get(keys);  // Bulk read\n```\n\n### Issue 4: List returns empty but cursor exists\n**Cause**: Deleted/expired keys create \"tombstones\" that must be iterated through\n**Solution**: Always check `list_complete`, not `keys.length`\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Correct pagination\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await kv.list({ cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);  // Even if empty\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n**CRITICAL**: When using `prefix`, you **must include it in all paginated calls**:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Loses prefix on subsequent pages\nlet result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:'' });\nresult = await kv.list({ cursor: result.cursor });  // Missing prefix!\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Include prefix on every call\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:'', cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n**Source**: [List keys documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/api/list-keys/)\n\n### Issue 5: `wrangler types` Does Not Generate Types for Environment-Nested KV Bindings\n\n**Cause**: KV namespaces defined within environment configurations (e.g., `[env.feature.kv_namespaces]`) are not included in generated TypeScript types\n**Impact**: Loss of TypeScript autocomplete and type checking for KV bindings\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #9709](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/9709)\n\n**Example Configuration:**\n```toml\n# wrangler.toml\n[env.feature]\nname = \"my-worker-feature\"\n[[env.feature.kv_namespaces]]\nbinding = \"MY_STORAGE_FEATURE\"\nid = \"xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n```\n\nRunning `npx wrangler types` creates type definitions for environment variables but not for the KV namespace bindings.\n\n**Workaround:**\n```bash\n# Generate types for specific environment\nnpx wrangler types -e feature\n```\n\nOr define KV namespaces at top level instead of nested in environments:\n```toml\n# Top-level (types generated correctly)\n[[kv_namespaces]]\nbinding = \"MY_STORAGE\"\nid = \"xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n```\n\n**Note**: Runtime bindings still work correctly; this only affects type generation.\n\n### Issue 6: `wrangler kv key list` Returns Empty Array for Remote Data\n\n**Cause**: CLI commands default to **local storage**, not remote/production KV\n**Impact**: Users expect to see production data but get empty array from local storage\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10395](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10395)\n\n**Solution**: Use `--remote` flag to access production/remote data\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Shows local storage (likely empty)\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV\n\n# ✅ Shows remote/production data\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV --remote\n```\n\n**Why This Happens**: By design, `wrangler dev` uses local KV storage to avoid interfering with production data. CLI commands follow the same default for consistency.\n\n**Applies to**: All `wrangler kv key` commands (get, list, delete, put)\n\n---\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] Environment-specific namespaces configured (`id` vs `preview_id`)\n- [ ] Namespace IDs stored in environment variables (not hardcoded)\n- [ ] Rate limit retry logic implemented for writes\n- [ ] Appropriate `cacheTtl` values set for reads (min 60s)\n- [ ] Sizes validated (key 512B, value 25MiB, metadata 1KB)\n- [ ] Bulk operations used where possible\n- [ ] Pagination with `list_complete` check (not `keys.length`)\n- [ ] Error handling for null values\n- [ ] Monitoring/alerting for rate limits\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [Cloudflare KV Docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/)\n- [KV API Reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/api/)\n- [KV Limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/platform/limits/)\n- [How KV Works](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/concepts/how-kv-works/)\n- [Wrangler KV Commands](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/commands/#kv)\n\n---\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Package Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n**Changes**: Added 6 research findings - hot/cold key performance patterns, remote bindings (Wrangler 4.37+), wrangler types environment issue, CLI --remote flag requirement, RYOW consistency details, prefix persistence in pagination\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:52:47.443Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Edge Computing Agents requiring high-performance, low-latency key-value storage with Cloudflare Workers KV.","zh":"适用于需要高性能、低延迟键值存储的 Edge Computing Agents，特别是与 Cloudflare Workers KV 配合使用。","ja":"Cloudflare Workers KV を使用する高性能、低遅延のキー値ストレージを必要とする Edge Computing エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Cloudflare Workers KV를 사용하는 고성능, 저지연 키-값 저장소가 필요한 에지 컴퓨팅 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de Edge Computing que requieren un almacenamiento de clave-valor de alto rendimiento y baja latencia con Cloudflare Workers KV.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de calcul de bord nécessitant un stockage de clés-valeurs à haute performance et à faible latence avec Cloudflare Workers KV.","de":"Ideal für Edge-Computing-Agents, die ein hochleistungs- und niedrigverzögertes Schlüssel-Wert-Speicher mit Cloudflare Workers KV erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Computação de Borda que exigem armazenamento de chave-valor de alto desempenho e baixa latência com Cloudflare Workers KV.","ru":"Идеально подходит для एजентых вычислений на краю, требующих высокопроизводительного, низкозадержного хранилища ключ-значение с Cloudflare Workers KV.","ar":"مثالي لعميل حوسبة الحافة الذي يتطلب تخزين قيم المفتاح عالي الأداء ووقت استجابة منخفض مع Cloudflare Workers KV."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Cloudflare''s hybrid storage with R2, enabling 40x performance gain and <5ms p99 latency, while utilizing the bulk reads API for efficient data retrieval, all through the wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types libraries.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Cloudflare 的混合存储 R2，实现 40 倍的性能提升和 <5ms p99 延迟，同时利用批量读取 API 进行高效的数据检索，所有这些都通过 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 库来实现。","ja":"エージェントに Cloudflare のハイブリッドストレージ R2 を使用させることで、40 倍のパフォーマンス向上と <5ms p99 待ち時間を実現し、同時にバルク読み取り API を使用して効率的なデータ取得を実現します。すべての機能は、wrangler と @cloudflare/workers-types ライブラリを通じて提供されます。","ko":"에이전트가 Cloudflare의 하이브리드 스토리지 R2를 사용하여 40배의 성능 향상과 <5ms p99 지연을实现할 수 있도록 하며, 또한 대량 읽기 API를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터检索를 thực現합니다. 모든 기능은 wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types 라이브러리를 통해 제공됩니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar el almacenamiento híbrido de Cloudflare con R2, lo que permite una mejora del rendimiento 40 veces mayor y una latencia p99 <5 ms, al mismo tiempo que utiliza la API de lecturas masivas para una recuperación de datos eficiente, todo a través de las bibliotecas wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter le stockage hybride de Cloudflare avec R2, permettant un gain de performances 40 fois supérieur et une latence p99 <5 ms, tout en utilisant l''API de lectures massives pour une récupération de données efficace, le tout via les bibliothèques wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Cloudflares Hybrid-Speicher mit R2 zu nutzen, wodurch eine 40-fache Leistungssteigerung und eine p99-Latenz <5 ms ermöglicht wird, während die Bulk-Reads-API für eine effiziente Datenerfassung verwendet wird, und dies alles über die Bibliotheken wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar o armazenamento híbrido da Cloudflare com R2, permitindo um ganho de desempenho 40x e latência p99 <5ms, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza a API de leituras em massa para recuperação de dados eficiente, tudo por meio das bibliotecas wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать гибридное хранилище Cloudflare с R2, обеспечивая 40-кратное увеличение производительности и задержку p99 <5мс, а также использует массовый API чтения для эффективного извлечения данных, все через библиотеки wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من الاستفادة من التخزين الهجين من Cloudflare مع R2، مما يتيح تحقيق مكاسب أداء 40 ضعفا وتأخير p99 أقل من 5 مللي ثانية، مع الاستفادة من واجهة برمجة التطبيقات للقراءة بالجملة لاسترجاع البيانات بكفاءة، وكل ذلك من خلال مكتبات wrangler و@cloudflare/workers-types."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing high-performance caching mechanisms for web applications","Storing and retrieving sensitive data with Cloudflare''s secure key-value storage","Optimizing data storage and retrieval for edge computing applications with Cloudflare Workers"],"zh":["为 Web 应用程序实现高性能缓存机制","使用 Cloudflare 的安全键值存储存储和检索敏感数据","为 Edge Computing 应用程序与 Cloudflare Workers 优化数据存储和检索"],"ja":["Web アプリケーションのための高性能キャッシュメカニズムを実装する","Cloudflare の安全なキー値ストレージを使用して機密データを格納および取得する","Edge Computing アプリケーション用に Cloudflare Workers とデータのストレージと取得を最適化する"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션을 위한 고성능 캐싱 메커니즘 구현","Cloudflare의 보안 키-값 저장소를 사용하여 민감한 데이터를 저장 및检索","에지 컴퓨팅 애플리케이션을 위한 Cloudflare Workers와 데이터 저장 및检索 최적화"],"es":["Implementar mecanismos de caché de alto rendimiento para aplicaciones web","Almacenar y recuperar datos sensibles con el almacenamiento de clave-valor seguro de Cloudflare","Optimizar el almacenamiento y la recuperación de datos para aplicaciones de edge computing con Cloudflare Workers"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des mécanismes de mise en cache à haute performance pour les applications Web","Stockage et récupération de données sensibles avec le stockage de clés-valeurs sécurisé de Cloudflare","Optimisation du stockage et de la récupération de données pour les applications de calcul de bord avec Cloudflare Workers"],"de":["Implementierung von Hochleistungs-Caching-Mechanismen für Webanwendungen","Speichern und Abrufen von sensiblen Daten mit Cloudflares sicherem Schlüssel-Wert-Speicher","Optimierung des Speicher- und Abrufverhaltens für Edge-Computing-Anwendungen mit Cloudflare Workers"],"pt":["Implementação de mecanismos de cache de alto desempenho para aplicações web","Armazenamento e recuperação de dados sensíveis com armazenamento de chave-valor seguro da Cloudflare","Otimização do armazenamento e recuperação de dados para aplicações de computação de borda com Cloudflare Workers"],"ru":["Реализация высокопроизводительных механизмов кэширования для веб-приложений","Хранение и извлечение конфиденциальных данных с использованием безопасного хранилища ключ-значение от Cloudflare","Оптимизация хранения и извлечения данных для приложений вычислений на краю с Cloudflare Workers"],"ar":["تنفيذ آليات ذاكرة暂存 عالية الأداء للتطبيقات الويب","تخزين واسترجاع البيانات الحساسة مع تخزين قيم المفتاح الآمن من Cloudflare","تحسين تخزين واسترجاع البيانات للتطبيقات حوسبة الحافة مع Cloudflare Workers"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare Workers setup with cloudflare-worker-base dependency","Dependent on wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types libraries for functionality"],"zh":["需要 Cloudflare Workers 设置并依赖 cloudflare-worker-base 依赖项","依赖 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 库来实现功能"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers の設定と cloudflare-worker-base 依存関係が必要","機能を実現するために wrangler と @cloudflare/workers-types ライブラリに依存する"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers 설정 및 cloudflare-worker-base 종속성이 필요","기능을實現하기 위해 wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types 라이브러리에 종속"],"es":["Requiere una configuración de Cloudflare Workers con la dependencia cloudflare-worker-base","Dependiente de las bibliotecas wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types para la funcionalidad"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Cloudflare Workers avec la dépendance cloudflare-worker-base","Dépend des bibliothèques wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types pour la fonctionnalité"],"de":["Benötigt eine Cloudflare-Workers-Konfiguration mit der Abhängigkeit cloudflare-worker-base","Abhängig von den Bibliotheken wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types für die Funktionalität"],"pt":["Exige configuração do Cloudflare Workers com dependência cloudflare-worker-base","Dependente das bibliotecas wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types para funcionalidade"],"ru":["Требует настройки Cloudflare Workers с зависимостью cloudflare-worker-base","Зависит от библиотек wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types для функциональности"],"ar":["يتطلب إعدادات Cloudflare Workers مع اعتماد cloudflare-worker-base","يعتمد على مكتبات wrangler و@cloudflare/workers-types للوظيفة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/cloudflare-kv', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'cloudflare-kv', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:53:04.286Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/cloudflare-kv","name":"cloudflare-kv","description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","ja":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","ko":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","es":"Cloudflare Workers KV es una solución de almacenamiento de datos en la nube para desarrolladores, que ofrece un rendimiento rápido y una baja latencia. Permite lecturas masivas y cuenta con una arquitectura de almacenamiento híbrida","fr":"Cloudflare Workers KV est une solution de stockage de données dans le cloud pour les développeurs, qui offre des performances rapides et une faible latence. Elle permet des lectures massives et dispose d''une architecture de stockage hybride","de":"Cloudflare Workers KV ist eine Cloud-Datenspeicherlösung für Entwickler, die ein schnelles Rendering und eine geringe Latenz bietet. Sie ermöglicht Massenlesevorgänge und verfügt über eine hybride Speicherarchitektur","pt":"O Cloudflare Workers KV é um serviço de armazenamento de dados na nuvem que oferece baixa latência e alta performance","ru":"Cloudflare Workers KV — облачное хранилище данных с низкой задержкой и высокой производительностью","ar":"Cloudflare Workers KV هو خدمة تخزين البيانات السحابي التي توفر زمن منخفض وسرعة عالية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Cloudflare Workers KV","ja":"Cloudflare Workers KV","ko":"Cloudflare Workers KV","es":"Cloudflare Workers KV: Almacenamiento de datos en la nube","fr":"Cloudflare Workers KV : Stockage de données dans le cloud","de":"Cloudflare Workers KV: Cloud-Datenspeicher","pt":"Cloudflare KV: Armazenamento de Dados na Nuvem","ru":"Cloudflare KV: Облачное Хранилище Данных","ar":"Cloudflare KV: تخزين البيانات السحابي","en":"cloudflare-kv"},"description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","ja":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","ko":"Cloudflare Workers KV, 40, 5ms p99 ","es":"Cloudflare Workers KV es una solución de almacenamiento de datos en la nube para desarrolladores, que ofrece un rendimiento rápido y una baja latencia. Permi...","fr":"Cloudflare Workers KV est une solution de stockage de données dans le cloud pour les développeurs, qui offre des performances rapides et une faible latence. ...","de":"Cloudflare Workers KV ist eine Cloud-Datenspeicherlösung für Entwickler, die ein schnelles Rendering und eine geringe Latenz bietet. Sie ermöglicht Massenles...","pt":"O Cloudflare Workers KV é um serviço de armazenamento de dados na nuvem que oferece baixa latência e alta performance","ru":"Cloudflare Workers KV — облачное хранилище данных с низкой задержкой и высокой производительностью","ar":"Cloudflare Workers KV هو خدمة تخزين البيانات السحابي التي توفر زمن منخفض وسرعة عالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["40","5ms p99 ","R2","100","2025","Namespace "],"ja":["40","5ms p99 ","R2","100","2025","Namespace "],"ko":["40","5ms p99 ","R2","100","2025","Namespace "],"es":["Lecturas masivas de hasta 100 claves en una sola solicitud","Arquitectura de almacenamiento híbrida con R2","Baja latencia de menos de 5 ms","Límite de namespace aumentado","Compatibilidad con cloudflare-worker-base para la configuración de Workers","Actualizaciones recientes para mejorar el rendimiento"],"fr":["Lectures massives de jusqu''à 100 clés en une seule requête","Architecture de stockage hybride avec R2","Faible latence de moins de 5 ms","Limite de namespace augmenté","Compatibilité avec cloudflare-worker-base pour la configuration des Workers","Mises à jour récentes pour améliorer les performances"],"de":["Massenlesevorgänge von bis zu 100 Schlüsseln in einer einzigen Anfrage","Hybride Speicherarchitektur mit R2","Geringe Latenz von weniger als 5 ms","Erhöhter Namensraum-Limit","Kompatibilität mit cloudflare-worker-base für die Worker-Konfiguration","Aktuelle Updates für verbesserte Leistung"],"pt":["Baixa latência (<5ms p99)","Alta performance (40x ganho de desempenho)","Armazenamento híbrido com R2","Leituras em massa (até 100 chaves por solicitação)","Aumento do limite de namespace"],"ru":["Низкая задержка (<5ms p99)","Высокая производительность (40-кратный прирост производительности)","Гибридное хранилище с R2","Массовые чтения (до 100 ключей в одном запросе)","Увеличение лимита namespace"],"ar":["زمن منخفض (<5ms p99)","سرعة عالية (زيادة أداء 40 مرة)","تخزين هجين مع R2","قراءات بالجملة (حتى 100 مفتاح في طلب واحد)","زيادة حد المساحة التخزينية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","KV","Workers","Cloud","Storage","Performance","Latency","R2","Namespace"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","KV","Workers","Cloud","Storage","Performance","Latency","R2","Namespace"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloudflare","KV","Workers","Cloud","Storage","Performance","Latency","R2","Namespace"],"es":["Cloudflare Workers KV","almacenamiento de datos en la nube","lecturas masivas","baja latencia","arquitectura de almacenamiento híbrida","desarrollo de aplicaciones en la nube","soluciones de almacenamiento de datos","tecnologías de cloud computing","herramientas de desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["Cloudflare Workers KV","stockage de données dans le cloud","lectures massives","faible latence","architecture de stockage hybride","développement d''applications dans le cloud","solutions de stockage de données","technologies de cloud computing","outils de développement d''applications"],"de":["Cloudflare Workers KV","Cloud-Datenspeicher","Massenlesevorgänge","geringe Latenz","hybride Speicherarchitektur","Entwicklung von Cloud-Anwendungen","Cloud-Datenspeicherlösungen","Cloud-Computing-Technologien","Entwicklungstools für Cloud-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Cloudflare KV","armazenamento de dados na nuvem","baixa latência","alta performance","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","Cloudflare Workers"],"ru":["Cloudflare KV","облачное хранилище данных","низкая задержка","высокая производительность","разработка приложений","Cloudflare Workers"],"ar":["Cloudflare KV","تخزين البيانات السحابي","زمن منخفض","سرعة عالية","تطوير التطبيقات","Cloudflare Workers"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloudflare-kv","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Cloudflare Workers KV\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **August 2025**: Architecture redesign (40x performance gain, <5ms p99 latency, hybrid storage with R2)\n- **April 2025**: Bulk reads API (retrieve up to 100 keys in single request, counts as 1 operation)\n- **January 2025**: Namespace limit increase","body":"# Cloudflare Workers KV\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **August 2025**: Architecture redesign (40x performance gain, <5ms p99 latency, hybrid storage with R2)\n- **April 2025**: Bulk reads API (retrieve up to 100 keys in single request, counts as 1 operation)\n- **January 2025**: Namespace limit increased (200 → 1,000 namespaces per account for Free and Paid plans)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nnpx wrangler kv namespace create MY_NAMESPACE\n# Output: [[kv_namespaces]] binding = \"MY_NAMESPACE\" id = \"<UUID>\"\n```\n\n**wrangler.jsonc:**\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [{\n    \"binding\": \"MY_NAMESPACE\",  // Access as env.MY_NAMESPACE\n    \"id\": \"<production-uuid>\",\n    \"preview_id\": \"<preview-uuid>\"  // Optional: local dev\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n```typescript\ntype Bindings = { MY_NAMESPACE: KVNamespace };\n\napp.post(''/set/:key'', async (c) => {\n  await c.env.MY_NAMESPACE.put(c.req.param(''key''), await c.req.text());\n  return c.json({ success: true });\n});\n\napp.get(''/get/:key'', async (c) => {\n  const value = await c.env.MY_NAMESPACE.get(c.req.param(''key''));\n  return value ? c.json({ value }) : c.json({ error: ''Not found'' }, 404);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## KV API Reference\n\n### Read Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Get single key\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'');  // string | null\nconst data = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''json'' });  // object | null\nconst buffer = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''arrayBuffer'' });\nconst stream = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { type: ''stream'' });\n\n// Get with cache (minimum 60s)\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 300 });  // 5 min edge cache\n\n// Bulk read (counts as 1 operation)\nconst values = await env.MY_KV.get([''key1'', ''key2'']);  // Map<string, string | null>\n\n// With metadata\nconst { value, metadata } = await env.MY_KV.getWithMetadata(''key'');\nconst result = await env.MY_KV.getWithMetadata([''key1'', ''key2'']);  // Bulk with metadata\n```\n\n### Write Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Basic write (max 1/second per key)\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''key'', ''value'');\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''user:123'', JSON.stringify({ name: ''John'' }));\n\n// With expiration\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''session'', data, { expirationTtl: 3600 });  // 1 hour\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''token'', value, { expiration: Math.floor(Date.now()/1000) + 86400 });\n\n// With metadata (max 1024 bytes)\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''config'', ''dark'', {\n  metadata: { updatedAt: Date.now(), version: 2 }\n});\n```\n\n**Critical Limits:**\n- Key: 512 bytes max\n- Value: 25 MiB max\n- Metadata: 1024 bytes max\n- Write rate: 1/second per key (429 error if exceeded)\n- Expiration: 60 seconds minimum\n\n### List Operations\n\n```typescript\n// List with pagination\nconst result = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'', limit: 1000, cursor });\n// result: { keys: [], list_complete: boolean, cursor?: string }\n\n// CRITICAL: Always check list_complete, not keys.length === 0\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'', cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n### Delete Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Delete single key\nawait env.MY_KV.delete(''key'');  // Always succeeds\n\n// Bulk delete (CLI only, up to 10,000 keys)\n// npx wrangler kv bulk delete --binding=MY_KV keys.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Caching Pattern with CacheTtl\n\n```typescript\nasync function getCachedData(kv: KVNamespace, key: string, fetchFn: () => Promise<any>, ttl = 300) {\n  const cached = await kv.get(key, { type: ''json'', cacheTtl: ttl });\n  if (cached) return cached;\n\n  const data = await fetchFn();\n  await kv.put(key, JSON.stringify(data), { expirationTtl: ttl * 2 });\n  return data;\n}\n```\n\n**Guidelines**: Minimum 60s, use for read-heavy workloads (100:1 read/write ratio)\n\n### Metadata Optimization\n\n```typescript\n// Store small values (<1024 bytes) in metadata to avoid separate get() calls\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''user:123'', '''', {\n  metadata: { status: ''active'', plan: ''pro'', lastSeen: Date.now() }\n});\n\n// list() returns metadata automatically (no additional get() calls)\nconst users = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: ''user:'' });\nusers.keys.forEach(({ name, metadata }) => console.log(name, metadata.status));\n```\n\n### Understanding Hot vs Cold Keys\n\nKV performance varies based on key temperature:\n\n| Type | Response Time | When It Happens |\n|------|---------------|-----------------|\n| **Hot keys** | 6-8ms | Read 2+ times/minute per datacenter |\n| **Cold keys** | 100-300ms | Infrequently accessed, fetched from central storage |\n\n**Post-August 2025 Improvements**:\n- P90 for all KV Worker invocations: <12ms (was 22ms before)\n- Hot reads up to 3x faster\n- All operations faster by up to 20ms\n\n**Optimization**: Use key coalescing to make cold keys benefit from hot key caching:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: Many cold keys (300ms each)\nawait kv.put(''user:123:name'', ''John'');\nawait kv.put(''user:123:email'', ''john@example.com'');\nawait kv.put(''user:123:plan'', ''pro'');\n\n// Each read of a cold key: ~100-300ms\nconst name = await kv.get(''user:123:name'');    // Cold\nconst email = await kv.get(''user:123:email'');  // Cold\nconst plan = await kv.get(''user:123:plan'');    // Cold\n\n// ✅ Good: Single hot key (6-8ms)\nawait kv.put(''user:123'', JSON.stringify({\n  name: ''John'',\n  email: ''john@example.com'',\n  plan: ''pro''\n}));\n\n// Single read, cached as hot key: ~6-8ms\nconst user = JSON.parse(await kv.get(''user:123''));\n```\n\n**CacheTtl helps cold keys**: For infrequently-read data, `cacheTtl` reduces cold read latency.\n\n**Trade-off**: Coalescing requires read-modify-write for updates\n\n### Pagination Helper\n\n```typescript\nasync function* paginateKV(kv: KVNamespace, options: { prefix?: string } = {}) {\n  let cursor: string | undefined;\n  do {\n    const result = await kv.list({ ...options, cursor });\n    yield result.keys;\n    cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n  } while (cursor);\n}\n\n// Usage\nfor await (const keys of paginateKV(env.MY_KV, { prefix: ''user:'' })) {\n  processKeys(keys);\n}\n```\n\n### Rate Limit Retry with Exponential Backoff\n\n```typescript\nasync function putWithRetry(kv: KVNamespace, key: string, value: string, opts?: KVPutOptions) {\n  let attempts = 0, delay = 1000;\n  while (attempts < 5) {\n    try {\n      await kv.put(key, value, opts);\n      return;\n    } catch (error) {\n      if ((error as Error).message.includes(''429'')) {\n        attempts++;\n        if (attempts >= 5) throw new Error(''Max retry attempts'');\n        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));\n        delay *= 2;  // Exponential backoff\n      } else throw error;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Understanding Eventual Consistency\n\nKV is **eventually consistent** across Cloudflare''s global network (Aug 2025 redesign: hybrid storage, <5ms p99 latency):\n\n**How It Works:**\n1. Writes immediately visible in same location (read-your-own-write consistency within same POP)\n2. Other locations see update within ~60 seconds (or cacheTtl value)\n3. Cached reads may return stale data during propagation\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\n// Tokyo: Write\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''1'');\nconst value = await env.MY_KV.get(''counter''); // \"1\" ✅ (same POP, RYOW)\n\n// London (within 60s): May be stale ⚠️\nconst value2 = await env.MY_KV.get(''counter''); // Might be old value\n\n// After 60+ seconds: Consistent ✅\n```\n\n**Read-Your-Own-Write (RYOW) Guarantee**: Since August 2025 redesign, requests routed through the **same Cloudflare point of presence** see their own writes immediately. Global consistency across different POPs still takes up to 60 seconds.\n\n**Timestamp Mitigation Pattern** (for critical consistency needs):\n```typescript\n// Use timestamp in key structure to avoid consistency issues\nconst timestamp = Date.now();\nawait kv.put(`user:123:${timestamp}`, userData);\n\n// Find latest using list with prefix\nconst result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:123:'' });\nconst latestKey = result.keys.sort((a, b) =>\n  parseInt(b.name.split('':'')[2]) - parseInt(a.name.split('':'')[2])\n).at(0);\n```\n\n**Use KV for**: Read-heavy workloads (100:1 ratio), config, feature flags, caching, user preferences\n**Don''t use KV for**: Financial transactions, strong consistency, >1/second writes per key, critical data\n\n**Need strong consistency?** Use [Durable Objects](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/)\n\n**Source**: [Redesigning Workers KV](https://blog.cloudflare.com/rearchitecting-workers-kv-for-redundancy/)\n\n---\n\n## Wrangler CLI Essentials\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nnpx wrangler kv namespace create MY_NAMESPACE [--preview]\n\n# Manage keys (add --remote flag to access production data)\nnpx wrangler kv key put --binding=MY_KV \"key\" \"value\" [--ttl=3600] [--metadata=''{}'']\nnpx wrangler kv key get --binding=MY_KV \"key\" [--remote]\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV [--prefix=\"user:\"] [--remote]\nnpx wrangler kv key delete --binding=MY_KV \"key\"\n\n# Bulk operations (up to 10,000 keys)\nnpx wrangler kv bulk put --binding=MY_KV data.json\nnpx wrangler kv bulk delete --binding=MY_KV keys.json\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT**: CLI commands default to **local storage**. Add `--remote` flag to access production/remote data.\n\n---\n\n## Development vs Production\n\n### Remote Bindings for Local Development (Wrangler 4.37+)\n\nConnect local Workers to production KV namespaces during development:\n\n**wrangler.jsonc:**\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [{\n    \"binding\": \"MY_KV\",\n    \"id\": \"production-uuid\",\n    \"remote\": true  // Connect to live KV\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n**How It Works:**\n- Local Worker code executes locally (fast iteration)\n- KV operations route to production namespace through proxy\n- No manual data seeding required\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Test against real production data without deploying\n- Fast local code execution with production data access\n- Faster feedback loop (no deploy-test cycle)\n\n**⚠️ Warning**: Writes affect production data. Consider using a staging namespace with `remote: true` instead of production.\n\n**Version Support:**\n- Wrangler 4.37.0+\n- @cloudflare/vite-plugin 1.13.0+\n- @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers 0.9.0+\n\n**Source**: [Remote bindings architecture](https://blog.cloudflare.com/connecting-to-production-the-architecture-of-remote-bindings/)\n\n---\n\n## Limits & Quotas\n\n| Feature | Free Plan | Paid Plan |\n|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| Reads per day | 100,000 | Unlimited |\n| Writes per day (different keys) | 1,000 | Unlimited |\n| **Writes per key per second** | **1** | **1** |\n| Operations per Worker invocation | 1,000 | 1,000 |\n| **Namespaces per account** | **1,000** | **1,000** |\n| Storage per account | 1 GB | Unlimited |\n| Key size | 512 bytes | 512 bytes |\n| Metadata size | 1024 bytes | 1024 bytes |\n| Value size | 25 MiB | 25 MiB |\n| Minimum cacheTtl | 60 seconds | 60 seconds |\n\n**Critical**: 1 write/second per key (429 if exceeded), bulk operations count as 1 operation, namespace limit increased from 200 → 1,000 (Jan 2025)\n\n---\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### 1. Rate Limit (429 Too Many Requests)\n**Cause**: Writing to same key >1/second\n**Solution**: Use retry with exponential backoff (see Advanced Patterns)\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''1'');\nawait env.MY_KV.put(''counter'', ''2''); // 429 error!\n\n// ✅ Good\nawait putWithRetry(env.MY_KV, ''counter'', ''2'');\n```\n\n### 2. Value Too Large\n**Cause**: Value exceeds 25 MiB\n**Solution**: Validate size before writing\n\n```typescript\nif (value.length > 25 * 1024 * 1024) throw new Error(''Value exceeds 25 MiB'');\n```\n\n### 3. Metadata Too Large\n**Cause**: Metadata exceeds 1024 bytes when serialized\n**Solution**: Validate serialized size\n\n```typescript\nconst serialized = JSON.stringify(metadata);\nif (serialized.length > 1024) throw new Error(''Metadata exceeds 1024 bytes'');\n```\n\n### 4. Invalid CacheTtl\n**Cause**: cacheTtl <60 seconds\n**Solution**: Use minimum 60\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Error\nawait env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 30 });\n\n// ✅ Correct\nawait env.MY_KV.get(''key'', { cacheTtl: 60 });\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### Always Do ✅\n\n1. Use bulk operations when reading multiple keys (counts as 1 operation)\n2. Set cacheTtl for frequently-read, infrequently-updated data (min 60s)\n3. Store small values (<1024 bytes) in metadata when using `list()` frequently\n4. Check `list_complete` when paginating, not `keys.length === 0`\n5. Use retry logic with exponential backoff for write operations\n6. Validate sizes before writing (key 512B, value 25MiB, metadata 1KB)\n7. Coalesce related keys for better caching performance\n8. Use KV for read-heavy workloads (100:1 read/write ratio ideal)\n\n### Never Do ❌\n\n1. Never write to same key >1/second (causes 429 rate limit errors)\n2. Never assume immediate global consistency (takes ~60 seconds to propagate)\n3. Never use KV for atomic operations (use Durable Objects instead)\n4. Never set cacheTtl <60 seconds (will fail)\n5. Never commit namespace IDs to public repos (use environment variables)\n6. Never exceed 1000 operations per invocation (use bulk operations)\n7. Never rely on write order (eventual consistency = no guarantees)\n8. Never forget to handle null values (`get()` returns `null` if key doesn''t exist)\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue 1: \"429 Too Many Requests\" on writes\n**Cause**: Writing to same key >1/second\n**Solution**: Consolidate writes or use retry with exponential backoff\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: Rate limit\nfor (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) await kv.put(''counter'', String(i));\n\n// ✅ Good: Single write\nawait kv.put(''counter'', ''9'');\n\n// ✅ Good: Retry with backoff\nawait putWithRetry(kv, ''counter'', String(i));\n```\n\n### Issue 2: Stale reads after write\n**Cause**: Eventual consistency (~60 seconds propagation)\n**Solution**: Accept stale reads, use Durable Objects for strong consistency, or implement app-level cache invalidation\n\n### Issue 3: \"Operations limit exceeded\"\n**Cause**: >1000 KV operations in single Worker invocation\n**Solution**: Use bulk operations\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad: 5000 operations\nfor (const key of 5000keys) await kv.get(key);\n\n// ✅ Good: 1 operation\nconst values = await kv.get(keys);  // Bulk read\n```\n\n### Issue 4: List returns empty but cursor exists\n**Cause**: Deleted/expired keys create \"tombstones\" that must be iterated through\n**Solution**: Always check `list_complete`, not `keys.length`\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Correct pagination\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await kv.list({ cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);  // Even if empty\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n**CRITICAL**: When using `prefix`, you **must include it in all paginated calls**:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Loses prefix on subsequent pages\nlet result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:'' });\nresult = await kv.list({ cursor: result.cursor });  // Missing prefix!\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Include prefix on every call\nlet cursor: string | undefined;\ndo {\n  const result = await kv.list({ prefix: ''user:'', cursor });\n  processKeys(result.keys);\n  cursor = result.list_complete ? undefined : result.cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n```\n\n**Source**: [List keys documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/api/list-keys/)\n\n### Issue 5: `wrangler types` Does Not Generate Types for Environment-Nested KV Bindings\n\n**Cause**: KV namespaces defined within environment configurations (e.g., `[env.feature.kv_namespaces]`) are not included in generated TypeScript types\n**Impact**: Loss of TypeScript autocomplete and type checking for KV bindings\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #9709](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/9709)\n\n**Example Configuration:**\n```toml\n# wrangler.toml\n[env.feature]\nname = \"my-worker-feature\"\n[[env.feature.kv_namespaces]]\nbinding = \"MY_STORAGE_FEATURE\"\nid = \"xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n```\n\nRunning `npx wrangler types` creates type definitions for environment variables but not for the KV namespace bindings.\n\n**Workaround:**\n```bash\n# Generate types for specific environment\nnpx wrangler types -e feature\n```\n\nOr define KV namespaces at top level instead of nested in environments:\n```toml\n# Top-level (types generated correctly)\n[[kv_namespaces]]\nbinding = \"MY_STORAGE\"\nid = \"xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n```\n\n**Note**: Runtime bindings still work correctly; this only affects type generation.\n\n### Issue 6: `wrangler kv key list` Returns Empty Array for Remote Data\n\n**Cause**: CLI commands default to **local storage**, not remote/production KV\n**Impact**: Users expect to see production data but get empty array from local storage\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10395](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10395)\n\n**Solution**: Use `--remote` flag to access production/remote data\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Shows local storage (likely empty)\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV\n\n# ✅ Shows remote/production data\nnpx wrangler kv key list --binding=MY_KV --remote\n```\n\n**Why This Happens**: By design, `wrangler dev` uses local KV storage to avoid interfering with production data. CLI commands follow the same default for consistency.\n\n**Applies to**: All `wrangler kv key` commands (get, list, delete, put)\n\n---\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] Environment-specific namespaces configured (`id` vs `preview_id`)\n- [ ] Namespace IDs stored in environment variables (not hardcoded)\n- [ ] Rate limit retry logic implemented for writes\n- [ ] Appropriate `cacheTtl` values set for reads (min 60s)\n- [ ] Sizes validated (key 512B, value 25MiB, metadata 1KB)\n- [ ] Bulk operations used where possible\n- [ ] Pagination with `list_complete` check (not `keys.length`)\n- [ ] Error handling for null values\n- [ ] Monitoring/alerting for rate limits\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [Cloudflare KV Docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/)\n- [KV API Reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/api/)\n- [KV Limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/platform/limits/)\n- [How KV Works](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/concepts/how-kv-works/)\n- [Wrangler KV Commands](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/commands/#kv)\n\n---\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Package Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n**Changes**: Added 6 research findings - hot/cold key performance patterns, remote bindings (Wrangler 4.37+), wrangler types environment issue, CLI --remote flag requirement, RYOW consistency details, prefix persistence in pagination\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:53:04.286Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Edge Computing Agents requiring low-latency, high-performance key-value storage with Cloudflare Workers KV.","zh":"适用于需要低延迟、高性能键值存储的 Edge Computing 代理，特别是与 Cloudflare Workers KV 配合使用。","ja":"Cloudflare Workers KV を使用して低遅延、高パフォーマンスのキーバリューストレージを必要とする Edge Computing エージェントに適しています。","ko":"Cloudflare Workers KV와 함께 사용하여 낮은 지연 시간과 높은 성능의 키-값 저장소가 필요한 에지 컴퓨팅 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Edge Computing que requieren almacenamiento de clave-valor de baja latencia y alto rendimiento con Cloudflare Workers KV.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de calcul de bord nécessitant un stockage de clés-valeurs à faible latence et à haute performance avec Cloudflare Workers KV.","de":"Ideal für Edge-Computing-Agents, die ein niedriglatentes, hochleistungskey-wert-Speicher mit Cloudflare Workers KV erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Computação de Borda que exigem armazenamento de chave-valor de baixa latência e alto desempenho com Cloudflare Workers KV.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов вычислений на краю сети, требующих хранилища ключ-значение с низкой задержкой и высокой производительностью с Cloudflare Workers KV.","ar":"مثالي لعميل حوسبة الحافة الذي يتطلب تخزين قيمة المفتاح منخفض الاتصال وال أداء العالي مع Cloudflare Workers KV."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Cloudflare''s hybrid storage with R2, enabling bulk reads and writes with ultra-low latency, and providing a 40x performance gain through its redesigned architecture, all while utilizing the latest versions of wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Cloudflare 的混合存储（R2），实现批量读写，超低延迟，并通过重新设计的架构提供 40 倍的性能提升，同时利用 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 的最新版本。","ja":"Cloudflare のハイブリッドストレージ (R2) を使用して、エージェントがバルク読み取りと書き込みを行い、超低遅延を実現し、再設計されたアーキテクチャを通じて 40 倍のパフォーマンスの向上を提供し、wrangler と @cloudflare/workers-types の最新バージョンを利用します。","ko":"Cloudflare의 하이브리드 저장소(R2)를 사용하여 에이전트가 대량 읽기/쓰기를 수행하고 cực저지연을 달성하며, 재설계된 아키텍처를 통해 40배의 성능 향상을 제공하고, wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types의 최신 버전을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar el almacenamiento híbrido de Cloudflare con R2, lo que permite lecturas y escrituras masivas con una latencia ultrabaja y proporciona una ganancia de rendimiento de 40 veces a través de su arquitectura rediseñada, todo mientras utiliza las versiones más recientes de wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter le stockage hybride de Cloudflare avec R2, ce qui permet des lectures et des écritures massives avec une latence ultrabasse et fournit un gain de performances de 40 fois grâce à son architecture repensée, le tout en utilisant les dernières versions de wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Cloudflares Hybrid-Speicher mit R2 zu nutzen, wodurch Massenlese- und -schreibvorgänge mit ultraniedriger Latenz ermöglicht werden und durch die neugestaltete Architektur eine 40-fache Leistungssteigerung erzielt wird, während die neuesten Versionen von wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitarem o armazenamento híbrido da Cloudflare com R2, permitindo leituras e gravações em massa com latência ultra-baixa e fornecendo um ganho de desempenho de 40 vezes por meio de sua arquitetura redesenhada, tudo isso utilizando as versões mais recentes do wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать гибридное хранилище Cloudflare с R2, что позволяет выполнять операции чтения и записи в большом объеме с сверхнизкой задержкой и обеспечивает 40-кратное увеличение производительности за счет переработанной архитектуры, все это при использовании последних версий wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء إمكانية الاستفادة من التخزين الهجين من Cloudflare مع R2، مما يتيح عمليات القراءة والكتابة بالجملة مع انخفاض زمن الوصول إلى أدنى حد، و يوفر مكسبا في الأداء 40 ضعفا من خلال هيكله المصممใหมا، و كل ذلك باستخدام أحدث إصدارات wrangler و @cloudflare/workers-types."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing high-performance caching mechanisms with Cloudflare Workers","Storing and retrieving sensitive data with Cloudflare''s secure key-value storage","Optimizing application performance with Cloudflare KV''s bulk reads API"],"zh":["使用 Cloudflare Workers 实现高性能缓存机制","使用 Cloudflare 的安全键值存储存储和检索敏感数据","使用 Cloudflare KV 的批量读取 API 优化应用程序性能"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers を使用して高パフォーマンスのキャッシュメカニズムを実装する","Cloudflare のセキュアキーバリューストレージを使用して機密データを保存および取得する","Cloudflare KV のバルク読み取り API を使用してアプリケーションのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers를 사용하여 고성능 캐싱 메커니즘을 구현합니다.","Cloudflare의 보안 키-값 저장소를 사용하여 민감한 데이터를 저장 및 검색합니다.","Cloudflare KV의 대량 읽기 API를 사용하여 애플리케이션 성능을 최적화합니다."],"es":["Implementar mecanismos de caché de alto rendimiento con Cloudflare Workers","Almacenar y recuperar datos sensibles con el almacenamiento de clave-valor seguro de Cloudflare","Optimizar el rendimiento de la aplicación con la API de lecturas masivas de Cloudflare KV"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des mécanismes de mise en cache à haute performance avec Cloudflare Workers","Stockage et récupération de données sensibles avec le stockage de clés-valeurs sécurisé de Cloudflare","Optimiser les performances de l''application avec l''API de lectures massives de Cloudflare KV"],"de":["Implementierung von Hochleistungs-Caching-Mechanismen mit Cloudflare Workers","Speichern und Abrufen von sensiblen Daten mit Cloudflares sicherem Key-Wert-Speicher","Optimieren der Anwendungsleistung mit der Massenlese-API von Cloudflare KV"],"pt":["Implementação de mecanismos de cache de alto desempenho com Cloudflare Workers","Armazenamento e recuperação de dados sensíveis com armazenamento de chave-valor seguro da Cloudflare","Otimização do desempenho da aplicação com API de leituras em massa do Cloudflare KV"],"ru":["Реализация механизмов кэширования высокого уровня производительности с Cloudflare Workers","Хранение и извлечение конфиденциальных данных с помощью безопасного хранилища ключ-значение Cloudflare","Оптимизация производительности приложения с помощью API массового чтения Cloudflare KV"],"ar":["تنفيذ آليات ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت عالية الأداء مع Cloudflare Workers","تخزين واسترجاع البيانات الحساسة مع تخزين قيمة المفتاح الآمن من Cloudflare","تحسين أداء التطبيق مع واجهة برمجة تطبيقات القراءة بالجملة من Cloudflare KV"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare Worker setup with cloudflare-worker-base","Dependent on wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types libraries","Namespace limits apply, although recently increased"],"zh":["需要 Cloudflare Worker 设置与 cloudflare-worker-base","依赖于 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 库","命名空间限制适用，尽管最近增加"],"ja":["Cloudflare Worker の設定と cloudflare-worker-base が必要","wrangler と @cloudflare/workers-types ライブラリに依存","名前空間の制限が適用されますが、最近増加しました"],"ko":["Cloudflare Worker 설정 및 cloudflare-worker-base가 필요합니다.","wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types 라이브러리에 종속됩니다.","네임스페이스 제한이 적용되지만 최근 증가했습니다."],"es":["Requiere configuración de Cloudflare Worker con cloudflare-worker-base","Dependiente de las bibliotecas wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types","Se aplican límites de espacio de nombres, aunque se han aumentado recientemente"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Cloudflare Worker avec cloudflare-worker-base","Dépendant des bibliothèques wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types","Les limites d''espace de noms s''appliquent, bien qu''elles aient été récemment augmentées"],"de":["Benötigt eine Cloudflare-Worker-Konfiguration mit cloudflare-worker-base","Abhängig von den Bibliotheken wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types","Namensraum-Beschränkungen gelten, obwohl sie kürzlich erhöht wurden"],"pt":["Exige configuração do Cloudflare Worker com cloudflare-worker-base","Depende das bibliotecas wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types","Limites de namespace se aplicam, embora tenham sido recentemente aumentados"],"ru":["Требует настройки Cloudflare Worker с cloudflare-worker-base","Зависит от библиотек wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types","Применяются ограничения namespace, хотя они были недавно увеличены"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد عميل Cloudflare مع cloudflare-worker-base","يعتمد على مكتبات wrangler و @cloudflare/workers-types","تطبق حدود مساحة الاسم، على الرغم من أنها تم زيادتها مؤخرا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
