r":"Mise à jour quotidienne de réunions","de":"Täglicher Meeting-Update","pt":"Atualização de Reunião Diária - Ferramenta de Desenvolvim...","ru":"Ежедневное обновление встречи - Инструмент для разработчиков","ar":"تحديث اجتماع يومي - أداة تطوير","en":"daily-meeting-update"},"description":{"zh":"每日会议更新技能通过交互式访谈生成每日站立会议/会议更新，支持开发、文档、规划和专业工作流程。","ja":"デイリー ミーティング アップデート スキルは、インタラクティブなインタビューを通じて毎日のスタンドアップ会議/ミーティングの更新を生成し、開発、ドキュメント、計画、プロのワークフローをサポートします。","ko":"일일 회의 업데이트 스킬은 대화형 인터뷰를 통해 일일 스탠드업 회의/미팅 업데이트를 생성하며 개발, 문서, 계획 및 전문 워크플로우를 지원합니다.","es":"La actualización diaria de reuniones es una colección de habilidades y comandos que extienden las capacidades de los agentes de codificación de IA.","fr":"La mise à jour quotidienne de réunions est une collection de compétences et de commandes qui étendent les capacités des agents de codage IA.","de":"Das tägliche Meeting-Update ist eine Sammlung von Fähigkeiten und Befehlen, die die Fähigkeiten der AI-Coding-Agenten erweitern.","pt":"A atualização de reunião diária é uma ferramenta que gera relatórios personalizados através de entrevistas interativas, integrando-se com GitHub e Jira.","ru":"Ежедневное обновление встречи - это инструмент, который генерирует пользовательские отчеты через интерактивные интервью, интегрируясь с GitHub и Jira.","ar":"تحديث اجتماع يومي هو أداة لتوليد تقارير مخصصة من خلال مقابلات تفاعلية، متكامل مع GitHub و Jira.","en":"A curated collection of skills, commands and role based agents for AI coding agents. they are packaged instructions and scripts that extend agent capabilitie..."},"definition":{"en":"A curated collection of skills, commands and role based agents for AI coding agents. they are packaged instructions and scripts that extend agent capabilities across development, documentation, planning, and professional workflows."},"features":{"zh":["交互式访谈","每日站立会议/会议更新","开发工作流程支持","文档工作流程支持","规划工作流程支持","专业工作流程支持"],"ja":["インタラクティブなインタビュー","毎日のスタンドアップ会議/ミーティングの更新","開発ワークフローのサポート","ドキュメントワークフローのサポート","計画ワークフローのサポート","プロのワークフローのサポート"],"ko":["대화형 인터뷰","일일 스탠드업 회의/미팅 업데이트","개발 워크플로우 지원","문서 워크플로우 지원","계획 워크플로우 지원","전문 워크플로우 지원"],"es":["Entrevista interactiva para generar actualizaciones diarias","Integración con GitHub y Jira","Compatibilidad con Claude Code","Selección de elementos relevantes a través de multiSelect","Resumen de la sesión del día anterior"],"fr":["Entretien interactif pour générer des mises à jour quotidiennes","Intégration avec GitHub et Jira","Compatibilité avec Claude Code","Sélection d''éléments pertinents via multiSelect","Résumé de la session de la veille"],"de":["Interaktives Interview zur Generierung von täglichen Updates","Integration mit GitHub und Jira","Kompatibilität mit Claude Code","Auswahl von relevanten Elementen über multiSelect","Zusammenfassung der Sitzung vom Vortag"],"pt":["Geração de relatórios personalizados","Integração com GitHub e Jira","Entrevistas interativas para coleta de dados","Relatórios diários automatizados","Customização de itens relevantes"],"ru":["Генерация пользовательских отчетов","Интеграция с GitHub и Jira","Интерактивные интервью для сбора данных","Автоматические ежедневные отчеты","Настройка актуальных пунктов"],"ar":["توليد تقارير مخصصة","التكامل مع GitHub و Jira","مقابلات تفاعلية لجمع البيانات","تقارير يومية آلية","تخصيص العناصر ذات الصلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 编码助手","每日会议更新","交互式访谈","开发工作流程","文档工作流程","规划工作流程","专业工作流程","AI 编码"],"ja":["AI コーディング エージェント","デイリー ミーティング アップデート","インタラクティブなインタビュー","開発ワークフロー","ドキュメントワークフロー","計画ワークフロー","プロのワークフロー","AI コーディング"],"ko":["AI 코딩 에이전트","일일 회의 업데이트","대화형 인터뷰","개발 워크플로우","문서 워크플로우","계획 워크플로우","전문 워크플로우","AI 코딩"],"es":["actualización diaria de reuniones","agentes de codificación de IA","integración con GitHub","integración con Jira","Claude Code","desarrollo de software","gestión de proyectos"],"fr":["mise à jour quotidienne de réunions","agents de codage IA","intégration avec GitHub","intégration avec Jira","Claude Code","développement de logiciels","gestion de projets"],"de":["tägliches Meeting-Update","AI-Coding-Agenten","Integration mit GitHub","Integration mit Jira","Claude Code","Softwareentwicklung","Projektmanagement"],"pt":["atualização de reunião diária","ferramenta de desenvolvimento","relatórios personalizados","integração com GitHub","integração com Jira","entrevistas interativas"],"ru":["ежедневное обновление встречи","инструмент для разработчиков","пользовательские отчеты","интеграция с GitHub","интеграция с Jira","интерактивные интервью"],"ar":["تحديث اجتماع يومي","أداة تطوير","تقارير مخصصة","التكامل مع GitHub","التكامل مع Jira","مقابلات تفاعلية"]}},"owner":"albertms22","repo":"agent-toolkit","repoPath":"albertms22/agent-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"daily-meeting-update","description":"Interactive daily standup/meeting update generator. Use when user says daily, standup, scrum update, status update, what did I do yesterday, prepare for meeting, morning update, or team sync. Pulls activity from GitHub, Jira, and Claude Code session history. Conducts 4-question interview (yesterday, today, blockers, discussion topics) and generates formatted Markdown update.","bodyPreview":"# Daily Meeting Update\n\nGenerate a daily standup/meeting update through an **interactive interview**. Never assume tools are configured—ask first.\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\nSTART\n  │\n  ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Phase 1: DETECT & OFFER INTEGRATIONS                │\n│ • Check: Claude Code history? gh CLI? jira CLI?     │\n│ • Claude Code → Pull yesterday''s session digest     │\n│   → User selects relevant items via multiSelect     │\n│ • GitHub/Jira → Ask user, pull if","body":"# Daily Meeting Update\n\nGenerate a daily standup/meeting update through an **interactive interview**. Never assume tools are configured—ask first.\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\nSTART\n  │\n  ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Phase 1: DETECT & OFFER INTEGRATIONS                │\n│ • Check: Claude Code history? gh CLI? jira CLI?     │\n│ • Claude Code → Pull yesterday''s session digest     │\n│   → User selects relevant items via multiSelect     │\n│ • GitHub/Jira → Ask user, pull if approved          │\n│ • Pull data NOW (before interview)                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 2: INTERVIEW (with insights)                  │\n│ • Show pulled data as context                       │\n│ • Yesterday: \"I see you merged PR #123, what else?\" │\n│ • Today: What will you work on?                     │\n│ • Blockers: Anything blocking you?                  │\n│ • Topics: Anything to discuss at end of meeting?    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 3: GENERATE UPDATE                            │\n│ • Combine interview answers + tool data             │\n│ • Format as clean Markdown                          │\n│ • Present to user                                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Detect & Offer Integrations\n\n### Step 1: Silent Detection\n\nCheck for available integrations **silently** (suppress errors, don''t show to user):\n\n| Integration | Detection |\n|-------------|-----------|\n| **Claude Code History** | `~/.claude/projects` directory exists with `.jsonl` files |\n| GitHub CLI | `gh auth status` succeeds |\n| Jira CLI | `jira` command exists |\n| Atlassian MCP | `mcp__atlassian__*` tools available |\n| Git | Inside a git repository |\n\n### Step 2: Offer GitHub/Jira Integrations (if available)\n\n> **Claude Code users:** Use `AskUserQuestionTool` tool for all questions in this phase.\n\n**GitHub/Git:**\n\nIf `HAS_GH` or `HAS_GIT`:\n\n```\n\"I detected you have GitHub/Git configured. Want me to pull your recent activity (commits, PRs, reviews)?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"Yes, pull the info\"\n- \"No, I''ll provide everything manually\"\n```\n\nIf yes:\n\n```\n\"Which repositories/projects should I check?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"Just the current directory\" (if in a git repo)\n- \"I''ll list the repos\" → user provides list\n```\n\n**Jira:**\n\nIf `HAS_JIRA_CLI` or `HAS_ATLASSIAN_MCP`:\n\n```\n\"I detected you have Jira configured. Want me to pull your tickets?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"Yes, pull my tickets\"\n- \"No, I''ll provide everything manually\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Pull GitHub/Jira Data (if approved)\n\n**GitHub/Git** — For each approved repo:\n- Commits by user since yesterday\n- PRs opened/merged by user\n- Reviews done by user\n\n**Jira** — Tickets assigned to user, updated in last 24h\n\n**Key insight**: Store results to use as context in Phase 2 interview.\n\n### Step 4: Offer Claude Code History\n\nThis integration captures everything you worked on with Claude Code — useful for recalling work that isn''t in git or Jira.\n\n**Detection:**\n```bash\nls ~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl 2>/dev/null | head -1\n```\n\n**If Claude Code history exists, ask:**\n\n```\n\"I can also pull your Claude Code session history from yesterday. This can help recall work that isn''t in git/Jira (research, debugging, planning). Want me to check?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"Yes, pull my Claude Code sessions\"\n- \"No, I have everything I need\"\n```\n\n**If yes, run the digest script:**\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/daily-meeting-update/scripts/claude_digest.py --format json\n```\n\n**Then present sessions with multiSelect:**\n\nUse `AskUserQuestionTool` with `multiSelect: true` to let user pick relevant items:\n\n```\n\"Here are your Claude Code sessions from yesterday. Select the ones relevant to your standup:\"\n\nOptions (multiSelect):\n- \"Fix authentication bug (backend-api)\"\n- \"Implement OAuth flow (backend-api)\"\n- \"Update homepage styles (frontend-app)\"\n- \"Research payment providers (docs)\"\n```\n\n**Key insight:** User selects which sessions are work-related. Personal projects or experiments can be excluded.\n\n**Do NOT run digest script when:**\n- User explicitly says \"No\" to Claude Code history\n- User says they''ll provide everything manually\n- `~/.claude/projects` directory doesn''t exist\n\n**If digest script fails:**\n- Fallback: Skip Claude Code integration silently, proceed with interview\n- Common issues: Python not installed, no sessions from yesterday, permission errors\n- Do NOT block the standup flow — the script is supplemental, not required\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Interview (with insights)\n\n> **Claude Code users:** Use `AskUserQuestionTool` tool to conduct the interview. This provides a better UX with structured options.\n\n**Use pulled data as context** to make questions smarter.\n\n### Question 1: Yesterday\n\n**If data was pulled**, show it first:\n\n```\n\"Here''s what I found from your activity:\n- Merged PR #123: fix login timeout\n- 3 commits in backend-api\n- Reviewed PR #456 (approved)\n\nAnything else you worked on yesterday that I missed?\"\n```\n\n**If no data pulled:**\n\n```\n\"What did you work on yesterday/since the last standup?\"\n```\n\nIf user response is vague, ask follow-up:\n- \"Can you give more details about X?\"\n- \"Did you complete anything specific?\"\n\n### Question 2: Today\n\n```\n\"What will you work on today?\"\n\nOptions:\n- [Text input - user types freely]\n```\n\n**If Jira data was pulled**, you can suggest:\n\n```\n\"I see you have these tickets assigned:\n- PROJ-123: Implement OAuth flow (In Progress)\n- PROJ-456: Fix payment bug (To Do)\n\nWill you work on any of these today?\"\n```\n\n### Question 3: Blockers\n\n```\n\"Do you have any blockers or impediments?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"No blockers\"\n- \"Yes, I have blockers\" → follow-up for details\n```\n\n### Question 4: Topics for Discussion\n\n```\n\"Any topic you want to bring up at the end of the daily?\"\n\nOptions:\n- \"No, nothing to discuss\"\n- \"Yes\" → follow-up for details\n\nExamples of topics:\n- Technical decision that needs input\n- Alignment with another team\n- Question about prioritization\n- Announcement or info for the team\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Generate Update\n\nCombine all information into clean Markdown:\n\n```markdown\n# Daily Update - [DATE]\n\n## Yesterday\n- [Items from interview]\n- [Items from GitHub/Jira if pulled]\n\n## Today\n- [Items from interview]\n\n## Blockers\n- [Blockers or \"No blockers\"]\n\n## PRs & Reviews (if pulled from GitHub)\n- [PRs opened]\n- [PRs merged]\n- [Reviews done]\n\n## Jira (if pulled from Jira)\n- [Tickets updated]\n\n## Topics for Discussion\n- [Topics or \"None\"]\n\n---\n*Links:*\n- [PR links]\n- [Ticket links]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Interview is primary** — Tools supplement, they don''t replace human context\n2. **Consent before access** — Always ask before pulling from any integration\n3. **Context-aware questions** — Show pulled data during interview to trigger memory (\"I see you merged PR #123...\")\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Action | Tool |\n|-------|--------|------|\n| 1. Detect & Offer | Check gh/jira/claude history, ask user, pull data | Bash (silent), AskUserQuestionTool* |\n| 2. Interview | Ask 4 questions with insights | AskUserQuestionTool* |\n| 3. Generate | Format Markdown | Output text |\n\n*Claude Code only: Use `AskUserQuestionTool` tool for structured questions.\n\n### Claude Code Digest Script\n\n```bash\n# Get yesterday''s sessions as JSON\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/daily-meeting-update/scripts/claude_digest.py --format json\n\n# Get today''s sessions\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/daily-meeting-update/scripts/claude_digest.py --date today --format json\n\n# Filter to specific project\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/daily-meeting-update/scripts/claude_digest.py --project ~/my-app --format json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Example Session\n\n```\nClaude: \"Let''s prepare your daily! I detected GitHub configured. Want me to pull your recent activity?\"\nUser: \"Yes\"\n\nClaude: \"Which repos should I check?\"\nUser: \"backend-api and frontend-app\"\n\n[Claude pulls GitHub data silently]\n\nClaude: \"I can also pull your Claude Code session history from yesterday. Want me to check?\"\nUser: \"Yes\"\n\n[Claude runs digest script, gets 5 sessions]\n\nClaude: \"Here are your Claude Code sessions from yesterday. Select the ones relevant to your standup:\"\n  ☑ Fix authentication timeout bug (backend-api)\n  ☑ Implement OAuth flow (backend-api)\n  ☐ Update personal blog (blog) - [user unchecks personal project]\n  ☑ Research payment providers (docs)\n  ☐ Debugging test failures (experiments)\n\nUser: [selects 3 relevant items]\n\nClaude: \"Here''s what I found from your activity:\n- Merged PR #120: fix login timeout\n- Opened PR #125: feat: add OAuth flow\n- Reviewed PR #123 (approved), PR #456 (changes requested)\n- 5 commits in backend-api\n- [From Claude Code] Fix authentication timeout bug\n- [From Claude Code] Implement OAuth flow\n- [From Claude Code] Research payment providers\n\nAnything else you worked on yesterday that I missed?\"\nUser: \"No, that covers it\"\n\nClaude: \"What will you work on today?\"\nUser: \"Continue the OAuth feature and deploy to staging\"\n\nClaude: \"Any blockers?\"\nUser: \"No\"\n\nClaude: \"Any topic to bring up at the end of the daily?\"\nUser: \"Yes, I want to discuss the architecture of the new payments module\"\n\n[Claude generates update]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Output Example\n\n```markdown\n# Daily Update - 2026-01-22\n\n## Yesterday\n- Worked on authentication feature\n- Research on payment providers\n- Merged PR #120 (fix: login timeout)\n- Opened PR #125 (feat: add OAuth flow)\n\n## Today\n- Continue OAuth feature\n- Deploy to staging\n\n## Blockers\n- No blockers\n\n## PRs & Reviews\n- **Opened:** PR #125 - feat: add OAuth flow\n- **Merged:** PR #120 - fix: login timeout\n- **Reviews:** PR #123 (approved), PR #456 (changes requested)\n\n## Topics for Discussion\n- Architecture of the new payments module\n\n---\n*Links:*\n- https://github.com/org/repo/pull/125\n- https://github.com/org/repo/pull/120\n```\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Avoid | Why (Expert Knowledge) | Instead |\n|-------|------------------------|---------|\n| Run gh/jira without asking | Users may have personal repos visible, or be in a sensitive project context they don''t want exposed | Always ask first, let user choose repos |\n| Assume current directory is the only project | Developers often work on 2-5 repos simultaneously (frontend, backend, infra) | Ask \"Which projects are you working on?\" |\n| Skip interview even with tool data | Tools capture WHAT happened but miss WHY and context (research, meetings, planning) | Interview is primary, tools supplement |\n| Generate update before all 4 questions | User might have critical blocker or discussion topic that changes the narrative | Complete interview, then generate |\n| Include raw commit messages | Commit messages are often cryptic (\"fix\", \"wip\") and don''t tell the story | Summarize into human-readable outcomes |\n| Ask for data after interview | Showing insights during interview makes questions smarter (\"I see you merged PR #123, anything else?\") | Pull data first, then interview with context |\n\n---\n\n## NEVER\n\n- **NEVER assume tools are configured** — Many devs have gh installed but not authenticated, or jira CLI pointing to wrong instance\n- **NEVER skip the \"Topics for Discussion\" question** — This is often the most valuable part of standup that tools can''t capture\n- **NEVER generate more than 15 bullets** — Standup should be <2 minutes to read; long updates lose the audience\n- **NEVER include ticket/PR numbers without context** — \"PROJ-123\" means nothing; always include title or summary\n- **NEVER pull data from repos user didn''t explicitly approve** — Even if you can see other repos, respect boundaries\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:53:28.802Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring streamlined meeting updates through interactive interviews and integrations with tools like GitHub and Jira.","zh":"适用于需要通过交互式访谈和与GitHub和Jira等工具集成来简化会议更新的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントがインタラクティブなインタビューとGitHubやJiraなどのツールとの統合を通じて会議の更新をストリームライン化する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 인터랙티브 인터뷰와 GitHub 및 Jira와 같은 도구와의 통합을 통해 회의 업데이트를 스트림 라인화해야 하는 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren actualizaciones de reuniones optimizadas a través de entrevistas interactivas y integraciones con herramientas como GitHub y Jira.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant des mises à jour de réunions rationalisées via des interviews interactives et des intégrations avec des outils comme GitHub et Jira.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die optimierte Besprechungsaktualisierungen durch interaktive Interviews und Integrationen mit Tools wie GitHub und Jira erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem atualizações de reuniões simplificadas por meio de entrevistas interativas e integrações com ferramentas como GitHub e Jira.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих упрощенных обновлений встреч через интерактивные интервью и интеграцию с инструментами seperti GitHub и Jira.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تحديثات اجتماعات مبسطة من خلال مقابلات تفاعلية ودمج أدوات مثل GitHub وJira."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate daily standup meeting updates by leveraging Claude Code history, GitHub CLI, and Jira CLI, facilitating multi-select item choices and seamless workflow integration across development and planning phases.","zh":"赋予代理人通过利用Claude Code历史记录、GitHub CLI和Jira CLI来生成每日站立会议更新的能力，促进跨开发和规划阶段的多选项选择和无缝的工作流集成。","ja":"Claude Codeの履歴、GitHub CLI、Jira CLIを利用して毎日のスタンドアップ会議の更新を生成する機能をエージェントに与え、開発と計画の各段階でマルチセレクトアイテムの選択とシームレスなワークフローの統合を促進します。","ko":"클로드 코드 기록, 깃허브 CLI, 지라 CLI를 활용하여 일일 스탠드업 미팅 업데이트를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에게 부여하여 개발 및 계획 단계에서 멀티 선택 항목 및 무결점 워크플로 통합을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar actualizaciones de reuniones diarias mediante la explotación de la historia de Claude Code, GitHub CLI y Jira CLI, facilitando elecciones de elementos multi-selección y una integración de flujo de trabajo sin problemas en las fases de desarrollo y planificación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des mises à jour de réunions quotidiennes en exploitant l''historique de Claude Code, GitHub CLI et Jira CLI, facilitant les choix d''éléments multi-sélection et une intégration de flux de travail transparente dans les phases de développement et de planification.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, tägliche Besprechungsaktualisierungen zu generieren, indem es die Geschichte von Claude Code, GitHub CLI und Jira CLI nutzt, und erleichtert so die Auswahl von Multi-Elementen und eine nahtlose Arbeitsabflussintegration in den Entwicklungs- und Planungsphasen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar atualizações de reuniões diárias standup aproveitando o histórico do Claude Code, GitHub CLI e Jira CLI, facilitando escolhas de itens multi-seleção e integração de fluxo de trabalho sem interrupções em fases de desenvolvimento e planejamento.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать ежедневные обновления встреч standup, используя историю Claude Code, GitHub CLI и Jira CLI, облегчая выбор пунктов многовыбор и бесперебойную интеграцию рабочего процесса на стадиях разработки и планирования.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على توليد تحديثات اجتماعات يومية من خلال استخدام سجل كلود كود، واجهة سطر أوامر جيثب، وواجهة سطر أوامر جيرا، و تسهل اختيار عناصر متعددة ودمج سير العمل دون انقطاع خلال مراحل التطوير والتخطيط."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating daily meeting updates through interactive user interviews","Generating yesterday''s session digests using Claude Code","Pulling relevant items from GitHub or Jira for meeting updates"],"zh":["通过交互式用户访谈自动执行每日会议更新","使用Claude Code生成昨天的会议摘要","从GitHub或Jira中提取相关项目以进行会议更新"],"ja":["インタラクティブなユーザーインタビューを通じて毎日の会議更新を自動化する","Claude Codeを使用して昨日の会議の要約を生成する","GitHubまたはJiraから会議更新のために関連アイテムを取得する"],"ko":["인터랙티브 사용자 인터뷰를 통해 일일 미팅 업데이트를 자동화하는 것","클라우드 코드를 사용하여 어제의 세션 요약을 생성하는 것","깃허브 또는 지라에서 미팅 업데이트를 위해 관련 항목을 가져오는 것"],"es":["Automatización de actualizaciones de reuniones diarias a través de entrevistas de usuario interactivas","Generación de resúmenes de sesiones de ayer mediante Claude Code","Obtención de elementos relevantes de GitHub o Jira para actualizaciones de reuniones"],"fr":["Automatisation des mises à jour de réunions quotidiennes via des interviews utilisateur interactives","Génération des résumés de sessions d''hier à l''aide de Claude Code","Récupération d''éléments pertinents de GitHub ou Jira pour les mises à jour de réunions"],"de":["Automatisierung von täglichen Besprechungsaktualisierungen durch interaktive Benutzerschnittstellen","Erzeugung von Sitzungsprotokollen von gestern mit Claude Code","Abruf von relevanten Elementen aus GitHub oder Jira für Besprechungsaktualisierungen"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de reuniões diárias por meio de entrevistas interativas de usuário","Gerar resumos da sessão de ontem usando o Claude Code","Puxar itens relevantes do GitHub ou Jira para atualizações de reuniões"],"ru":["Автоматизировать ежедневные обновления встреч через интерактивные интервью пользователей","Генерировать сводки вчерашней сессии, используя Claude Code","Извлекать соответствующие элементы из GitHub или Jira для обновлений встреч"],"ar":["توفير تحديثات اجتماعات آلية يومية من خلال مقابلات تفاعلية للمستخدم","توليد ملخصات جلستي الأمس باستخدام كلود كود","سحب عناصر ذات صلة من جيثب أو جيرا لتحديثات الاجتماعات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code, GitHub CLI, or Jira CLI setup and configuration","Needs user input for integration and item selection","Assumes access to relevant development and project management tools"],"zh":["需要Claude Code、GitHub CLI或Jira CLI的设置和配置","需要用户输入以进行集成和项目选择","假设可以访问相关的开发和项目管理工具"],"ja":["Claude Code、GitHub CLI、またはJira CLIの設定と構成が必要","統合とアイテムの選択のためにユーザー入力が必要","関連する開発ツールとプロジェクト管理ツールへのアクセスが可能であることが前提"],"ko":["클라우드 코드, 깃허브 CLI 또는 지라 CLI의 설정 및 구성이 필요하다.","통합 및 항목 선택을 위해 사용자 입력이 필요하다.","관련 개발 도구 및 프로젝트 관리 도구에 대한 액세스가 가능하다고 가정한다."],"es":["Requiere configuración y configuración de Claude Code, GitHub CLI o Jira CLI","Necesita la entrada del usuario para la integración y la selección de elementos","Supone el acceso a herramientas de desarrollo y gestión de proyectos relevantes"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration et une configuration de Claude Code, GitHub CLI ou Jira CLI","Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour l''intégration et la sélection d''éléments","Suppose l''accès à des outils de développement et de gestion de projet pertinents"],"de":["Erfordert Einrichtung und Konfiguration von Claude Code, GitHub CLI oder Jira CLI","Benötigt Benutzereingaben für die Integration und die Auswahl von Elementen","Geht davon aus, dass auf relevante Entwicklungsmittel und Projektmanagement-Tools zugegriffen wird"],"pt":["Requer configuração e instalação do Claude Code, GitHub CLI ou Jira CLI","Necessita de entrada do usuário para integração e seleção de itens","Pressupõe acesso a ferramentas de desenvolvimento e gestão de projetos relevantes"],"ru":["Требует настройки и конфигурации Claude Code, GitHub CLI или Jira CLI","Требует ввода пользователя для интеграции и выбора пунктов","Предполагает доступ к соответствующим инструментам разработки и управления проектами"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد وتكوين كلود كود، واجهة سطر أوامر جيثب أو واجهة سطر أوامر جيرا","يحتاج إلى إدخال المستخدم من أجل التكامل واختيار العناصر","يفترض الوصول إلى أدوات تطوير وإدارة المشاريع ذات الصلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fierzone/agent-skills-standard/Language', 'community', 'fierzone', 'agent-skills-standard', 'fierzone/agent-skills-standard', 'Language', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:53:48.908Z', NULL, '{"id":"fierzone/agent-skills-standard/Language","name":"Language","description":{"zh":"Golang 语言标准提供了代码格式、命名、包和错误处理等方面的指南","ja":"Go 言語スタンダードでは、コード形式、命名、パッケージ、エラーハンドリングなどについてのガイドラインを提供します","ko":"고랭 언어 표준은 코드 형식,命名, 패키지, 오류 처리 등에 대한 가이드라인을 제공합니다","es":"Estándares de lenguaje para Golang que mejoran la legibilidad y el rendimiento del código","fr":"Normes de langage pour Golang qui améliorent la lisibilité et les performances du code","de":"Sprachstandards für Golang, die die Lesbarkeit und Leistung des Codes verbessern","pt":"As diretrizes de linguagem Golang fornecem um conjunto de regras para escrever código limpo e eficiente. Aprenda sobre as melhores práticas para codificação em Golang","ru":"Руководства по языку Golang предоставляют набор правил для написания чистого и эффективного кода. Узнайте о лучших практиках для кодирования на Golang","ar":"توفر معايير لغة جولانج مجموعة من القواعد لكتابة رمز نظيف وفعال. تعلم عن أفضل الممارسات لترميز جولانج","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Golang 语言标准","ja":"Go 言語スタンダード","ko":"고랭 언어 표준","es":"Estándares de Lenguaje de Golang","fr":"Normes de Langage Golang","de":"Golang-Sprachstandards","pt":"Padrões de Linguagem Golang","ru":"Стандарты языка Golang","ar":"معايير لغة جولانج","en":"Language"},"description":{"zh":"Golang 语言标准提供了代码格式、命名、包和错误处理等方面的指南","ja":"Go 言語スタンダードでは、コード形式、命名、パッケージ、エラーハンドリングなどについてのガイドラインを提供します","ko":"고랭 언어 표준은 코드 형식,命名, 패키지, 오류 처리 등에 대한 가이드라인을 제공합니다","es":"Estándares de lenguaje para Golang que mejoran la legibilidad y el rendimiento del código","fr":"Normes de langage pour Golang qui améliorent la lisibilité et les performances du code","de":"Sprachstandards für Golang, die die Lesbarkeit und Leistung des Codes verbessern","pt":"As diretrizes de linguagem Golang fornecem um conjunto de regras para escrever código limpo e eficiente. Aprenda sobre as melhores práticas para codificação ...","ru":"Руководства по языку Golang предоставляют набор правил для написания чистого и эффективного кода. Узнайте о лучших практиках для кодирования на Golang","ar":"توفر معايير لغة جولانج مجموعة من القواعد لكتابة رمز نظيف وفعال. تعلم عن أفضل الممارسات لترميز جولانج","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["代码格式化","命名约定","包管理","错误处理","接口定义"],"ja":["コード形式","命名規則","パッケージ管理","エラーハンドリング","インターフェース定義"],"ko":["코드 형식","命名 규칙","패키지 관리","오류 처리","인터페이스 정의"],"es":["Uso de camelCase para variables internas","Uso de PascalCase para variables exportadas","Paquetes cortos y en minúsculas","Definición de interfaces donde se utilizan","Manejo de errores como último valor de retorno"],"fr":["Utilisation de camelCase pour les variables internes","Utilisation de PascalCase pour les variables exportées","Paquets courts et en minuscules","Définition des interfaces où elles sont utilisées","Gestion des erreurs comme dernière valeur de retour"],"de":["Verwendung von camelCase für interne Variablen","Verwendung von PascalCase für exportierte Variablen","Kurze und kleinschreibungspackages","Definition von Schnittstellen, wo sie verwendet werden","Fehlerbehandlung als letzter Rückgabewert"],"pt":["Formatação automática com gofmt ou goimports","Nomenclatura em camelCase para variáveis internas","Nomenclatura em PascalCase para variáveis exportadas","Tratamento de erros com retorno de erro como último valor","Definição de interfaces onde são usadas"],"ru":["Автоматическая форматирование с помощью gofmt или goimports","Именование в camelCase для внутренних переменных","Именование в PascalCase для экспортируемых переменных","Обработка ошибок с возвратом ошибки как последнее значение","Определение интерфейсов там, где они используются"],"ar":["تنسيق تلقائي باستخدام gofmt أو goimports","تسمية بالحالة الهجائية لتحويل الحروف إلى صغيرة لملفات داخلية","تسمية بالحالة الهجائية لتحويل الحروف إلى كبيرة لملفات مستوردة","معالجة الأخطاء بإرجاع الخطأ كقيمة أخيرة","تعريف الواجهات حيث يتم استخدامها"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Golang","语言标准","代码格式","命名约定","包管理","错误处理","接口定义"],"ja":["Go","言語スタンダード","コード形式","命名規則","パッケージ管理","エラーハンドリング","インターフェース定義"],"ko":["고랭","언어 표준","코드 형식","命名 규칙","패키지 관리","오류 처리","인터페이스 정의"],"es":["Golang","estándares de lenguaje","mejores prácticas","codificación","legibilidad","rendimiento","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Golang","normes de langage","meilleures pratiques","codage","lisibilité","performances","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Golang","Sprachstandards","beste Praktiken","Codierung","Lesbarkeit","Leistung","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["Golang","linguagem de programação","codificação","formatação","nomenclatura","tratamento de erros","interfaces","variáveis","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Golang","язык программирования","кодирование","форматирование","именование","обработка ошибок","интерфейсы","переменные","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["جولانج","لغة برمجة","ترميز","تنسيق","تسمية","معالجة الأخطاء","واجهات","متغيرات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"fierzone","repo":"agent-skills-standard","repoPath":"fierzone/agent-skills-standard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Language","description":"Core idioms, style guides, and best practices for writing idiomatic Go code.","bodyPreview":"# Golang Language Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0 (CRITICAL)**\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- **Fmt**: Run `gofmt` or `goimports` on save.\n- **Naming**: Use `camelCase` for internal, `PascalCase` for exported.\n- **Packages**: Short, lowercase, singular, no underscores (e.g., `net/http` not `net_http`).\n- **Interfaces**: Define where used, not where implemented. Small interfaces (1-2 methods).\n- **Errors**: Return error as last return value. Handle immediately.\n- **Variables**: Short names for small scope (`i`,","body":"# Golang Language Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0 (CRITICAL)**\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- **Fmt**: Run `gofmt` or `goimports` on save.\n- **Naming**: Use `camelCase` for internal, `PascalCase` for exported.\n- **Packages**: Short, lowercase, singular, no underscores (e.g., `net/http` not `net_http`).\n- **Interfaces**: Define where used, not where implemented. Small interfaces (1-2 methods).\n- **Errors**: Return error as last return value. Handle immediately.\n- **Variables**: Short names for small scope (`i`, `ctx`), descriptive for large scope.\n- **Slices**: Prefer slices over arrays. Use `make()` for capacity.\n- **Const**: Use `iota` for enums.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- **No `init`**: Use constructors, not `init()`.\n- **No Globals**: Use DI, not global mutable state.\n- **No `panic`**: Return errors, don''t panic.\n- **No `_` ignored errors**: Always check and handle errors.\n- **No stutter**: `log.Error`, not `log.LogError`.\n\n## references\n\n- [Idioms](references/idioms.md)\n- [Effective Go Summary](references/effective-go-summary.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:53:48.908Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing adherence to Golang language standards and best practices.","zh":"非常适合需要遵守Golang语言标准和最佳实践的代码分析代理。","ja":"Golang言語の標準とベストプラクティスに従う必要があるコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Golang 언어 표준 및 모범 사례를 준수해야 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan adherirse a los estándares y las mejores prácticas del lenguaje Golang.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code ayant besoin de respecter les normes et les meilleures pratiques du langage Golang.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die die Einhaltung der Golang-Sprachstandards und -bestpraktiken benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de aderência aos padrões e às melhores práticas da linguagem Golang.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов Анализа Кодов, требующих соблюдения стандартов и лучших практик языка Golang.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحللين للرمز الذي يحتاجون إلى الالتزام بمعايير وافضل الممارسات لمعايير لغة Golang."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce coding standards with gofmt and goimports, utilizing camelCase and PascalCase naming conventions, and handling errors immediately with small interfaces and short variable names, all while following package naming guidelines like net/http.","zh":"赋予代理人使用gofmt和goimports强制执行编码标准的能力，利用camelCase和PascalCase命名约定，并使用小接口和短变量名立即处理错误，同时遵循net/http等包命名指南。","ja":"gofmtとgoimportsを使用してコード規範を強制適用するエージェントを可能にし、camelCaseとPascalCaseの命名規約を使用し、小さなインターフェースと短い変数名でエラーをすぐに処理し、net/httpなどのパッケージ命名規約に従う。","ko":"gofmt와 goimports를 사용하여 코딩 표준을 강제 적용하는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, camelCase와 PascalCase命名 규칙을 사용하며, 작은 인터페이스와 짧은 변수 이름으로 즉시 오류를 처리하며, net/http 등의 패키지 이름 지침을 따릅니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación con gofmt y goimports, utilizando convenciones de nomenclatura camelCase y PascalCase, y manejando errores de inmediato con interfaces pequeñas y nombres de variables cortos, siguiendo todas las pautas de nomenclatura de paquetes como net/http.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faire respecter les normes de codage avec gofmt et goimports, en utilisant les conventions de dénomination camelCase et PascalCase, et en gérant les erreurs immédiatement avec de petites interfaces et de courts noms de variables, en suivant toutes les directives de dénomination de packages comme net/http.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Codierungsstandards mit gofmt und goimports durchzusetzen, indem sie camelCase- und PascalCase-Namenskonventionen verwenden und Fehler sofort mit kleinen Schnittstellen und kurzen Variablennamen behandeln, während sie alle Richtlinien für Paketnamen wie net/http befolgen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor normas de codificação com gofmt e goimports, utilizando convenções de nomenclatura camelCase e PascalCase, e lidando com erros imediatamente com interfaces pequenas e nomes de variáveis curtos, tudo isso seguindo diretrizes de nomenclatura de pacotes como net/http.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов кодирования с помощью gofmt и goimports, используя конвенции именования camelCase и PascalCase, и обрабатывая ошибки немедленно с помощью небольших интерфейсов и коротких имен переменных, все это при соблюдении руководящих принципов по именованию пакетов, таких как net/http.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فرض معايير الترميز باستخدام gofmt و goimports ، باستخدام اتفاقيات تسمية camelCase و PascalCase ، ومعالجة الأخطاء على الفور باستخدام واجهات صغيرة وأسماء متغيرات قصيرة ، كل ذلك مع اتباع إرشادات تسمية الحزم مثل net/http."},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing Golang coding standards on save","Generating error-handling code snippets","Validating package naming conventions"],"zh":["保存时强制执行Golang编码标准","生成错误处理代码片段","验证包命名约定"],"ja":["保存時にGolangのコーディング規範を強制適用する","エラーハンドリングのコードスニペットを生成する","パッケージ命名規約を検証する"],"ko":["저장 시 Golang 코딩 표준 강제 적용","오류 처리 코드 조각 생성","패키지 이름 규칙 검증"],"es":["Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación de Golang al guardar","Generar fragmentos de código de manejo de errores","Validar convenciones de nomenclatura de paquetes"],"fr":["Faire respecter les normes de codage Golang à l''enregistrement","Générer des extraits de code de gestion des erreurs","Valider les conventions de dénomination de packages"],"de":["Durchsetzen der Golang-Codierungsstandards beim Speichern","Erzeugen von Fehlerbehandlungs-Code-Snippets","Überprüfen von Paketbenennungskonventionen"],"pt":["Impor padrões de codificação Golang na hora de salvar","Gerar trechos de código de tratamento de erros","Validar convenções de nomenclatura de pacotes"],"ru":["Обеспечение соблюдения стандартов кодирования Golang при сохранении","Генерация фрагментов кода для обработки ошибок","Проверка конвенций по именованию пакетов"],"ar":["فرض معايير الترميز Golang عند الحفظ","توليد شفرات تعامل الأخطاء","التحقق من اتفاقيات تسمية الحزم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Golang environment","Specific to Golang language standards"],"zh":["需要Golang环境","特定于Golang语言标准"],"ja":["Golang環境が必要","Golang言語の規範に特有"],"ko":["Golang 환경 필요","Golang 언어 표준에 특정"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Golang","Específico para los estándares del lenguaje Golang"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Golang","Spécifique aux normes du langage Golang"],"de":["Benötigt Golang-Umgebung","Spezifisch für die Golang-Sprachstandards"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Golang","Específico para padrões de linguagem Golang"],"ru":["Требует среды Golang","Специфичен для стандартов языка Golang"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Golang","محدد لمعايير لغة Golang"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
