nterstützung für LSP-Operationen","Integration mit dem Claude Code-Fähigkeitsregister"],"pt":["Descubra implementações de traços","Entenda projetos polimórficos","Use a sintaxe /rust-trait-explorer","Encontre implementadores de traços","Encontre traços implementados por structs"],"ru":["Найдите реализации трейтов","Понимайте полиморфные проекты","Используйте синтаксис /rust-trait-explorer","Найдите реализаторы трейтов","Найдите трейты, реализованные структурами"],"ar":["اكتشف تطبيقات السمات","افهم التصميمات المتعددة الشكل","استخدم الصياغة /rust-trait-explorer","ابحث عن منفذين للسمات","ابحث عن السمات التي يتم تنفيذها بواسطة الهياكل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust","特征探索器","多态设计","特征实现","LSP 操作","Rust 语言开发"],"ja":["Rust","トレイトエクスプローラー","多相設計","トレイト実装","LSP 操作","Rust 言語開発"],"ko":["러스트","특성 탐색기","다형성 디자인","특성 구현","LSP 연산","러스트 언어 개발"],"es":["Rust","traits","diseños polimórficos","explorador de traits","desarrollo de software","programación en Rust","registros de habilidades","Claude Code"],"fr":["Rust","traits","conceptions polymorphes","explorateur de traits","développement de logiciels","programmation en Rust","registres de compétences","Claude Code"],"de":["Rust","Traits","polymorphe Designs","Trait-Explorer","Softwareentwicklung","Rust-Programmierung","Fähigkeitsregister","Claude Code"],"pt":["Rust","Trait","Explorer","Implementações de traços","Projetos polimórficos","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Rust","Трейт","Эксплорер","Реализации трейтов","Полиморфные проекты","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["رست","سمة","مستكشف","تطبيقات السمات","التصاميم المتعددة الشكل","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-trait-explorer","description":"Explore Rust trait implementations using LSP. Triggers on: /trait-impl, find implementations, who implements, trait 实现, 谁实现了, 实现了哪些trait","bodyPreview":"# Rust Trait Explorer\n\nDiscover trait implementations and understand polymorphic designs.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/rust-trait-explorer <TraitName|StructName>\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- `/rust-trait-explorer Handler` - Find all implementors of Handler trait\n- `/rust-trait-explorer MyStruct` - Find all traits implemented by MyStruct\n\n## LSP Operations\n\n### Go to Implementation\n\nFind all implementations of a trait.\n\n```\nLSP(\n  operation: \"goToImplementation\",\n  filePath: \"src/traits.rs\",\n  line: 10,\n  character:","body":"# Rust Trait Explorer\n\nDiscover trait implementations and understand polymorphic designs.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/rust-trait-explorer <TraitName|StructName>\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- `/rust-trait-explorer Handler` - Find all implementors of Handler trait\n- `/rust-trait-explorer MyStruct` - Find all traits implemented by MyStruct\n\n## LSP Operations\n\n### Go to Implementation\n\nFind all implementations of a trait.\n\n```\nLSP(\n  operation: \"goToImplementation\",\n  filePath: \"src/traits.rs\",\n  line: 10,\n  character: 11\n)\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- Trait name is known\n- Want to find all implementors\n- Understanding polymorphic code\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Find Trait Implementors\n\n```\nUser: \"Who implements the Handler trait?\"\n    │\n    ▼\n[1] Find trait definition\n    LSP(goToDefinition) or workspaceSymbol\n    │\n    ▼\n[2] Get implementations\n    LSP(goToImplementation)\n    │\n    ▼\n[3] For each impl, get details\n    LSP(documentSymbol) for methods\n    │\n    ▼\n[4] Generate implementation map\n```\n\n### Find Traits for a Type\n\n```\nUser: \"What traits does MyStruct implement?\"\n    │\n    ▼\n[1] Find struct definition\n    │\n    ▼\n[2] Search for \"impl * for MyStruct\"\n    Grep pattern matching\n    │\n    ▼\n[3] Get trait details for each\n    │\n    ▼\n[4] Generate trait list\n```\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Trait Implementors\n\n```\n## Implementations of `Handler`\n\n**Trait defined at:** src/traits.rs:15\n\n​```rust\npub trait Handler {\n    fn handle(&self, request: Request) -> Response;\n    fn name(&self) -> &str;\n}\n​```\n\n### Implementors (4)\n\n| Type | Location | Notes |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| AuthHandler | src/handlers/auth.rs:20 | Handles authentication |\n| ApiHandler | src/handlers/api.rs:15 | REST API endpoints |\n| WebSocketHandler | src/handlers/ws.rs:10 | WebSocket connections |\n| MockHandler | tests/mocks.rs:5 | Test mock |\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n#### AuthHandler\n​```rust\nimpl Handler for AuthHandler {\n    fn handle(&self, request: Request) -> Response {\n        // Authentication logic\n    }\n\n    fn name(&self) -> &str {\n        \"auth\"\n    }\n}\n​```\n\n#### ApiHandler\n​```rust\nimpl Handler for ApiHandler {\n    fn handle(&self, request: Request) -> Response {\n        // API routing logic\n    }\n\n    fn name(&self) -> &str {\n        \"api\"\n    }\n}\n​```\n```\n\n### Traits for a Type\n\n```\n## Traits implemented by `User`\n\n**Struct defined at:** src/models/user.rs:10\n\n### Standard Library Traits\n| Trait | Derived/Manual | Notes |\n|-------|----------------|-------|\n| Debug | #[derive] | Auto-generated |\n| Clone | #[derive] | Auto-generated |\n| Default | manual | Custom defaults |\n| Display | manual | User-friendly output |\n\n### Serde Traits\n| Trait | Location |\n|-------|----------|\n| Serialize | #[derive] |\n| Deserialize | #[derive] |\n\n### Project Traits\n| Trait | Location | Methods |\n|-------|----------|---------|\n| Entity | src/db/entity.rs:30 | id(), created_at() |\n| Validatable | src/validation.rs:15 | validate() |\n\n### Implementation Hierarchy\n\n​```\nUser\n├── derive\n│   ├── Debug\n│   ├── Clone\n│   ├── Serialize\n│   └── Deserialize\n└── impl\n    ├── Default (src/models/user.rs:50)\n    ├── Display (src/models/user.rs:60)\n    ├── Entity (src/models/user.rs:70)\n    └── Validatable (src/models/user.rs:85)\n​```\n```\n\n## Trait Hierarchy Visualization\n\n```\n## Trait Hierarchy\n\n                    ┌─────────────┐\n                    │    Error    │ (std)\n                    └──────┬──────┘\n                           │\n              ┌────────────┼────────────┐\n              │            │            │\n      ┌───────▼───────┐ ┌──▼──┐ ┌───────▼───────┐\n      │  AppError     │ │ ... │ │  DbError      │\n      └───────┬───────┘ └─────┘ └───────┬───────┘\n              │                         │\n      ┌───────▼───────┐         ┌───────▼───────┐\n      │ AuthError     │         │ QueryError    │\n      └───────────────┘         └───────────────┘\n```\n\n## Analysis Features\n\n### Coverage Check\n\n```\n## Trait Implementation Coverage\n\nTrait: Handler (3 required methods)\n\n| Implementor | handle() | name() | priority() | Complete |\n|-------------|----------|--------|------------|----------|\n| AuthHandler | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Yes |\n| ApiHandler | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ default | Yes |\n| MockHandler | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Yes |\n```\n\n### Blanket Implementations\n\n```\n## Blanket Implementations\n\nThe following blanket impls may apply to your types:\n\n| Trait | Blanket Impl | Applies To |\n|-------|--------------|------------|\n| From<T> | `impl<T> From<T> for T` | All types |\n| Into<U> | `impl<T, U> Into<U> for T where U: From<T>` | Types with From |\n| ToString | `impl<T: Display> ToString for T` | Types with Display |\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n| User Says | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| \"Who implements X?\" | goToImplementation on trait |\n| \"What traits does Y impl?\" | Grep for `impl * for Y` |\n| \"Show trait hierarchy\" | Find super-traits recursively |\n| \"Is X: Send + Sync?\" | Check std trait impls |\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Navigate to impl | rust-code-navigator |\n| Call relationships | rust-call-graph |\n| Project structure | rust-symbol-analyzer |\n| Safe refactoring | rust-refactor-helper |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:53:44.294Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust-focused AI Agents needing advanced trait exploration and polymorphic design analysis.","zh":"适用于需要高级特征探索和多态设计分析的Rust专注AI代理。","ja":"Rustを中心としたAIエージェントが高度なトレイトの探索と多相的な設計分析を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 특성 탐색 및 다형성 설계 분석이 필요한 러스트(Rust) 중심의 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA centrados en Rust que necesitan una exploración avanzada de rasgos y análisis de diseño polimórfico.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA axés sur Rust nécessitant une exploration avancée de traits et une analyse de conception polymorphique.","de":"Perfekt für rust-fokussierte KI-Agenten, die eine erweiterte Eigenschaftserkundung und eine polymorphe Designanalyse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA focados em Rust que precisam de exploração avançada de traits e análise de design polimórfico.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Rust, которым необходима продвинутая эксплуатация черт и анализ полиморфного дизайна.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي ذي التركيز على روست والذي يحتاج إلى استكشاف متقدم للسمات وتحليل التصميم متعدد الشكل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover trait implementations and understand complex polymorphic designs using LSP operations, facilitating efficient go-to-implementation functionality and trait-struct analysis with Rust-specific syntax.","zh":"赋予代理发现特征实现并理解复杂的多态设计的能力，使用LSP操作，方便高效的转到实现功能和特征-结构分析，支持Rust特定的语法。","ja":"LSP操作を使用して、トレイトの実装を発見し、複雑な多相的な設計を理解する能力をエージェントに与え、効率的な実装への移動機能とトレイト-構造の分析をRust特有の構文でサポートします。","ko":"LSP 연산을 사용하여 특성 구현을 발견하고 복잡한 다형성 설계를 이해하는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여하여 효율적인 구현으로 이동 기능과 특성-구조 분석을 러스트 특유의 구문으로 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a descubrir implementaciones de rasgos y comprender diseños polimórficos complejos utilizando operaciones LSP, facilitando una funcionalidad de ir a la implementación eficiente y un análisis de rasgo-struct con sintaxis específica de Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir des implémentations de traits et de comprendre des conceptions polymorphiques complexes en utilisant des opérations LSP, facilitant une fonctionnalité d''aller à l''implémentation efficace et une analyse de trait-struct avec une syntaxe spécifique à Rust.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Trait-Implementierungen zu entdecken und komplexe polymorphe Designs unter Verwendung von LSP-Operationen zu verstehen, wodurch eine effiziente Go-to-Implementation-Funktionalität und eine Trait-Struct-Analyse mit Rust-spezifischer Syntax ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrirem implementações de traits e compreenderem projetos polimórficos complexos usando operações LSP, facilitando a funcionalidade de ir para a implementação eficiente e a análise de trait-struct com sintaxe específica do Rust.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать реализации черт и понимать сложные полиморфные конструкции с помощью операций LSP, обеспечивая эффективную функциональность перехода к реализации и анализ trait-struct с синтаксисом, специфичным для Rust.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من اكتشاف عمليات تنفيذ السمات وفهم التصميمات متعددة الشكل المعقدة باستخدام عمليات بروتوكول خادم اللغة، وتسهيل وظيفة الانتقال إلى التنفيذ بكفاءة وتحليل هيكل-سمة مع بناء الجملة المحدد لروست."},"useCases":{"en":["Exploring trait implementations for specific structs","Finding all traits implemented by a given struct","Debugging polymorphic designs using LSP go-to-implementation operations"],"zh":["探索特定结构的特征实现","查找给定结构实现的所有特征","使用LSP转到实现操作调试多态设计"],"ja":["特定構造のトレイトの実装を探索する","特定の構造が実装するすべてのトレイトを検索する","LSPの実装への移動操作を使用して多相的な設計をデバッグする"],"ko":["특정 구조의 특성 구현 탐색","특정 구조가 구현하는 모든 특성을 찾기","LSP 구현으로 이동 연산을 사용하여 다형성 설계 디버깅"],"es":["Explorar implementaciones de rasgos para structs específicos","Encontrar todos los rasgos implementados por un struct determinado","Depurar diseños polimórficos utilizando operaciones LSP de ir a la implementación"],"fr":["Explorer les implémentations de traits pour des structs spécifiques","Trouver tous les traits implémentés par un struct donné","Déboguer les conceptions polymorphiques en utilisant des opérations LSP d''aller à l''implémentation"],"de":["Erkunden von Trait-Implementierungen für spezifische Structs","Alle von einem bestimmten Struct implementierten Traits finden","Polymorphe Designs mithilfe von LSP-Go-to-Implementation-Operationen debuggen"],"pt":["Explorar implementações de traits para structs específicos","Encontrar todos os traits implementados por um struct determinado","Depurar projetos polimórficos usando operações LSP de ir para a implementação"],"ru":["Изучать реализации черт для конкретных structs","Найти все черты, реализованные данным struct","Отлаживать полиморфные конструкции с помощью операций LSP перехода к реализации"],"ar":["استكشاف عمليات تنفيذ السمات لل structs المحددة","العثور على جميع السمات المنفذة من قبل هيكل معين","تصحيح تصميمات متعددة الشكل باستخدام عمليات بروتوكول خادم اللغة للانتقال إلى التنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust codebase access","Limited to Rust programming language","Dependent on Language Server Protocol (LSP) operations"],"zh":["需要访问Rust代码库","仅限于Rust编程语言","依赖于语言服务器协议（LSP）操作"],"ja":["Rustコードベースへのアクセスが必要","Rustプログラミング言語のみに限定される","言語サーバープロトコル（LSP）操作に依存する"],"ko":["러스트 코드베이스 액세스가 필요","러스트 프로그래밍 언어에만 제한","언어 서버 프로토콜(LSP) 연산에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código de Rust","Limitado al lenguaje de programación Rust","Dependiente de las operaciones del Protocolo de servidor de lenguaje (LSP)"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code Rust","Limité au langage de programmation Rust","Dépendant des opérations du Protocole de serveur de langage (LSP)"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Rust-Codebasis","Begrenzt auf die Rust-Programmiersprache","Abhängig von den Operationen des Language-Server-Protokolls (LSP)"],"pt":["Requer acesso à base de código Rust","Limitado à linguagem de programação Rust","Dependente das operações do Protocolo de Servidor de Linguagem (LSP)"],"ru":["Требует доступа к базе кода Rust","Ограничен языком программирования Rust","Зависит от операций Протокола сервера языка (LSP)"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة روست","محدود بلغة البرمجة روست","يعتمد على عمليات بروتوكول خادم اللغة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('harikiran138/lumina-ai-learning/skill-creator', 'community', 'harikiran138', 'lumina-ai-learning', 'harikiran138/lumina-ai-learning', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:54:03.066Z', NULL, '{"id":"harikiran138/lumina-ai-learning/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"Skill Creator是一种适应性AI学习伴侣，通过认知分析和预测智能，提供个性化的教育体验。","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、認知分析と予測インテリジェンスによって、個別化された教育を提供する適応型AI学習コンパニオンです。","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 인지 분석과 예측 지능을 통해 개인화된 교육을 제공하는 적응형 AI 학습 동반자입니다.","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es un compañero de aprendizaje AI que ofrece educación personalizada a través del análisis cognitivo y la inteligencia predictiva","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un compagnon d''apprentissage IA qui propose une éducation personnalisée grâce à l''analyse cognitive et à l''intelligence prédictive","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Lernbegleiter AI, der eine personalisierte Ausbildung durch kognitive Analyse und prädiktive Intelligenz bietet","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é um companheiro de aprendizado de IA que personaliza a educação através da análise cognitiva e inteligência preditiva.","ru":"Создатель Навыков - это адаптивный компаньон для обучения, который персонализирует образование через когнитивный анализ и предиктивную интеллекту.","ar":"مُبدع المهارات هو رفيق التعلم الذكي الذي يُقدم تعليمًا مُصممًا وفقًا لتحليل إدراكي وذكاء تنبؤي.","en":"Adaptive AI learning companion that personalizes education through cognitive analysis and predictive intelligence. Offline-first, multilingual, and designed to make quality learning accessible to all."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Skill Creator：个性化AI学习伴侣","ja":"スキルクリエイター：適応型AI学習コンパニオン","ko":"스킬 크리에이터: 개인화된 AI 학습 동반자","es":"Creador de Habilidades: Aprendizaje Personalizado","fr":"Créateur de Compétences: Apprentissage Adaptatif","de":"Fähigkeits-Ersteller: Adaptive Lernunterstützung","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Aprenda com o Companion de IA","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Адаптивный компаньон для обучения","ar":"مُبدع المهارات: رفيق التعلم الذكي","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"Skill Creator是一种适应性AI学习伴侣，通过认知分析和预测智能，提供个性化的教育体验。","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、認知分析と予測インテリジェンスによって、個別化された教育を提供する適応型AI学習コンパニオンです。","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 인지 분석과 예측 지능을 통해 개인화된 교육을 제공하는 적응형 AI 학습 동반자입니다.","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es un compañero de aprendizaje AI que ofrece educación personalizada a través del análisis cognitivo y la inteligencia predictiva","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un compagnon d''apprentissage IA qui propose une éducation personnalisée grâce à l''analyse cognitive et à l''intelligence prédic...","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Lernbegleiter AI, der eine personalisierte Ausbildung durch kognitive Analyse und prädiktive Intelligenz bietet","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é um companheiro de aprendizado de IA que personaliza a educação através da análise cognitiva e inteligência preditiva.","ru":"Создатель Навыков - это адаптивный компаньон для обучения, который персонализирует образование через когнитивный анализ и предиктивную интеллекту.","ar":"مُبدع المهارات هو رفيق التعلم الذكي الذي يُقدم تعليمًا مُصممًا وفقًا لتحليل إدراكي وذكاء تنبؤي.","en":"Adaptive AI learning companion that personalizes education through cognitive analysis and predictive intelligence. Offline-first, multilingual, and designed ..."},"definition":{"en":"Adaptive AI learning companion that personalizes education through cognitive analysis and predictive intelligence. Offline-first, multilingual, and designed to make quality learning accessible to all."},"features":{"zh":["个性化教育","认知分析","预测智能","离线优先","多语言支持"],"ja":["個別化された教育","認知分析","予測インテリジェンス","オフライン優先","多言語対応"],"ko":["개인화된 교육","인지 분석","예측 지능","오프라인 우선","다국어 지원"],"es":["Aprendizaje personalizado","Análisis cognitivo","Inteligencia predictiva","Accesibilidad offline","Multilingüe"],"fr":["Apprentissage personnalisé","Analyse cognitive","Intelligence prédictive","Accessibilité hors ligne","Multilingue"],"de":["Personalisiertes Lernen","Kognitive Analyse","Prädiktive Intelligenz","Offline-Zugänglichkeit","Mehrsprachig"],"pt":["Aprendizado adaptativo","Análise cognitiva","Inteligência preditiva","Acesso offline","Suporte multilíngue"],"ru":["Адаптивное обучение","Когнитивный анализ","Предиктивная интеллект","Доступ без интернета","Мультяшный поддержка"],"ar":["التعلم التكيفي","التحليل الإدراكي","الذكاء التنبؤي","الوصول دون اتصال","الدعم اللغوي المتعدد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI学习","个性化教育","认知分析","预测智能","离线优先","多语言支持"],"ja":["AI学習","個別化された教育","認知分析","予測インテリジェンス","オフライン優先","多言語対応"],"ko":["AI 학습","개인화된 교육","인지 분석","예측 지능","오프라인 우선","다국어 지원"],"es":["aprendizaje personalizado","inteligencia artificial","análisis cognitivo","educación en línea","desarrollo de habilidades","IA para educación"],"fr":["apprentissage personnalisé","intelligence artificielle","analyse cognitive","éducation en ligne","développement de compétences","IA pour l''éducation"],"de":["personalisiertes Lernen","künstliche Intelligenz","kognitive Analyse","Online-Ausbildung","Fähigkeitsentwicklung","KI für Bildung"],"pt":["aprendizado de máquina","inteligência artificial","educação personalizada","companheiro de aprendizado","análise cognitiva","inteligência preditiva"],"ru":["машинообучение","искусственный интеллект","персонализированное образование","компаньон для обучения","когнитивный анализ","предиктивная интеллект"],"ar":["التعلم الآلي","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التعليم المُصمم","رفيق التعلم","التحليل الإدراكي","الذكاء التنبؤي"]}},"owner":"harikiran138","repo":"lumina-ai-learning","repoPath":"harikiran138/lumina-ai-learning","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:03.066Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills.","zh":"非常适合需要专门知识和工作流扩展的AI代理，如Claude，通过模块化技能实现。","ja":"Claudeのような専門知識とワークフローの拡張が必要なAIエージェントに最適であり、モジュラーなスキルを通じて実現される。","ko":"클로드 같은 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 모듈러 스킬을 통해 구현된다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo a través de habilidades modulares.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude ayant besoin de connaissances spécialisées et d''extensions de flux de travail via des compétences modulaires.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen durch modulare Fähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho por meio de habilidades modulares.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса через модульные навыки.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيعات سير العمل من خلال مهارات مودULAR"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage modular, self-contained packages extending their capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, utilizing procedural knowledge and multi-language support.","zh":"赋予代理创建和管理模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，通过专门的知识、工作流和工具来扩展其能力，并利用程序化知识和多语言支持。","ja":"エージェントがモジュラー化された自己完結型パッケージを作成して管理する能力を提供し、専門知識、ワークフロー、ツールを利用して能力を拡張し、手続き知識とマルチ言語サポートを利用する。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 자체 완결형 패키지를 생성하고 관리할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여, 전문 지식, 워크플로, 도구를 이용하여 능력을 확장하고, 절차 지식과 다중 언어 지원을 활용한다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y gestionar paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían sus capacidades con conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, utilizando conocimiento procedural y soporte multilenguaje.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent leurs capacités avec des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, en utilisant des connaissances procédurales et un support multilingue.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen und zu verwalten, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen, Arbeitsabläufen und Werkzeugen erweitern, unter Nutzung von prozeduralem Wissen und Mehrsprachigkeitsunterstützung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e gerenciar pacotes modulares, autocontidos que estendem suas capacidades com conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, utilizando conhecimento procedural e suporte a vários idiomas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и управлять модульными, самодостаточными пакетами, расширяющими их возможности специализированными знаниями, рабочими процессами и инструментами, используя процедурные знания и поддержку нескольких языков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء وإدارة حزم مودULAR، مكتفية ذاتيًا تعزز قدراتهم مع المعرفة المتخصصة وسير العمل والأدوات، باستخدام المعرفة الإجرائية ودعم اللغة المتعددة"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing specialized workflows for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["创建特定领域的入门指南","开发特定任务的专用工作流","使用程序化知识来扩展代理能力"],"ja":["ドメイン固有のオンボーディングガイドを作成する","タスク固有のワークフローを開発する","手続き知識を使用してエージェントの能力を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인별 온보딩 가이드 생성","특정 작업을 위한 전문 워크플로 개발","절차 지식을 사용하여 에이전트 능력 확장"],"es":["Creación de guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollo de flujos de trabajo especializados para tareas","Ampliación de las capacidades del agente con conocimiento procedural"],"fr":["Création de guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développement de flux de travail spécialisés pour les tâches","Élargissement des capacités de l''agent avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Erstellung von domänenspezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden","Entwicklung spezialisierter Workflows für Aufgaben","Erweiterung der Agentenfähigkeiten mit prozeduralem Wissen"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolver fluxos de trabalho especializados para tarefas","Estender as capacidades do agente com conhecimento procedural"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных доменов","Разработка специализированных рабочих процессов для задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء دليل إرشادي لدمج المجال النوعي","تطوير سير عمل متخصصة للمهام","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء باستخدام المعرفة الإجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s agent framework","Offline-first functionality may have limitations in online-only environments"],"zh":["需要Claude的代理框架","离线优先功能在仅在线环境中可能存在限制"],"ja":["Claudeのエージェントフレームワークが必要","オフライン優先機能はオンラインのみの環境では制限がある可能性がある"],"ko":["클로드 에이전트 프레임워크가 필요","오프라인 우선 기능은 온라인만의 환경에서 제한이 있을 수 있다"],"es":["Requiere el marco de agente de Claude","La funcionalidad offline-first puede tener limitaciones en entornos solo en línea"],"fr":["Nécessite le cadre d''agent de Claude","La fonctionnalité offline-first peut avoir des limites dans les environnements en ligne uniquement"],"de":["Benötigt das Agenten-Framework von Claude","Die Offline-first-Funktionalität kann in reinen Online-Umgebungen Einschränkungen haben"],"pt":["Requer a estrutura de agente do Claude","A funcionalidade offline-first pode ter limitações em ambientes online-only"],"ru":["Требует框架 агента Claude","Функциональность offline-first может иметь ограничения в средах только для онлайн"],"ar":["يتطلب إطار وكيل Claude","يمكن أن يكون للوظيفة الأولى离线 قيود في بيئات فقط عبر الإنترنت"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('stephenhuo-code/sunnyagent/skill-creator', 'community', 'stephenhuo-code', 'sunnyagent', 'stephenhuo-code/sunnyagent', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:54:29.163Z', NULL, '{"id":"stephenhuo-code/sunnyagent/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建器提供创建有效技能的指南，扩展Claude的能力并提供专业知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、クラウドの能力を拡張し、専門知識やワークフローを提供するスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 클라우드의 능력을 확장하고 전문 지식 및 워크플로우를 제공하는 스킬을 생성하기 위한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear skills efectivos que amplían las capacidades de Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des skills efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude.","de":"Der Skill-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zum Erstellen effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades de Claude com conhecimento especializado","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, позволяя разработчикам расширить возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний","ar":"يوفّر Skill Creator إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建器：为Claude打造专属技能","ja":"スキルクリエーター：クラウドの専用スキルを作成する","ko":"스킬 생성기: 클라우드의 전문 스킬 구축","es":"Creador de Habilidades: Desarrolla Skills Efectivos","fr":"Créateur de Compétences: Développez des Skills Efficaces","de":"Skill-Ersteller: Erstellen Sie Effektive Fähigkeiten","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Создатель навыков: руководство для разработчиков","ar":"مصمم المهارات: دليل للمطورين","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建器提供创建有效技能的指南，扩展Claude的能力并提供专业知识和工作流程","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、クラウドの能力を拡張し、専門知識やワークフローを提供するスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供する","ko":"스킬 생성기는 클라우드의 능력을 확장하고 전문 지식 및 워크플로우를 제공하는 스킬을 생성하기 위한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear skills efectivos que amplían las capacidades de Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des skills efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude.","de":"Der Skill-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zum Erstellen effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades de Claude com conhecimen...","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, позволяя разработчикам расширить возможности Claude с помощью специализированных зн...","ar":"يوفّر Skill Creator إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供专业知识和工作流程","扩展Claude的能力","创建模块化技能","支持多种工作流程","提供技能创建指南"],"ja":["専門知識やワークフローを提供する","クラウドの能力を拡張する","モジュール化されたスキルを作成する","複数のワークフローをサポートする","スキル作成のガイダンスを提供する"],"ko":["전문 지식 및 워크플로우 제공","클라우드의 능력을 확장","모듈화된 스킬 생성","다중 워크플로우 지원","스킬 생성 가이드 제공"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimiento procedural","Herramientas y workflows personalizables","Creación de skills modulares","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissance procédurale","Outils et workflows personnalisables","Création de skills modulaires","Étendre les capacités de Claude"],"de":["Spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","Prozedurales Wissen","Anpassbare Tools und Arbeitsabläufe","Erstellung modularen Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes","Permite a extensão das capacidades de Claude com conhecimento especializado","Oferece fluxos de trabalho especializados para tarefas específicas","Transforma Claude em um agente especializado","Fornece conhecimento procedural que nenhum modelo pode possuir"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков","Позволяет расширить возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний","Предлагает специализированные рабочие процессы для конкретных задач","Преобразует Claude в специализированного агента","Предоставляет процедурные знания, которых нет у никакой модели"],"ar":["يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","يسمح بتوسيع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة","يقدم عمليات عاملة متخصصة لمهام محددة","يحول Claude إلى وكيل متخصص","يوفر معرفة إجرائية لا تملكها أي نموذج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建器","Claude技能","专业知识","工作流程","模块化技能","AI能力扩展","技能开发"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","クラウドスキル","専門知識","ワークフロー","モジュール化されたスキル","AI能力拡張","スキル開発"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","클라우드 스킬","전문 지식","워크플로우","모듈화된 스킬","AI 능력 확장","스킬 개발"],"es":["desarrollo de skills","creador de habilidades","ampliación de capacidades","conocimiento procedural","flujos de trabajo especializados","herramientas personalizables"],"fr":["développement de skills","créateur de compétences","étendre les capacités","connaissance procédurale","flux de travail spécialisés","outils personnalisables"],"de":["Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Skill-Ersteller","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten","prozedurales Wissen","spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","anpassbare Tools"],"pt":["Skill Creator","criação de habilidades","desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensão de capacidades","conhecimento especializado","fluxos de trabalho","desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Skill Creator","создание навыков","разработка навыков","расширение возможностей","специализированные знания","рабочие процессы","разработчики"],"ar":["Skill Creator","إنشاء مهارات","تطوير المهارات","توسيع القدرات","المعرفة المتخصصة","العمليات العاملة","المطورون"]}},"owner":"stephenhuo-code","repo":"sunnyagent","repoPath":"stephenhuo-code/sunnyagent","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:29.163Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflows to extend their capabilities.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude 这样的高级 AI 代理，它需要专门的知识和工作流来扩展其功能。","ja":"Claude のような高度な AI エージェントに特別な知識とワークフローが必要な場合に最適です。","ko":"클로드와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트가 기능을 확장하기 위해 전문 지식과 워크플ロー가 필요할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude que necesitan conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados para ampliar sus capacidades.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA avancés comme Claude nécessitant des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés pour étendre leurs capacités.","de":"Perfekt für fortschrittliche KI-Agents wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Arbeitsabläufe benötigen, um ihre Fähigkeiten zu erweitern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho para estender suas capacidades.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, которые требуют специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов для расширения их возможностей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم مثل Claude الذي يحتاج إلى معرفة متخصصة وسلسلة من الإجراءات لتعزيز قدراته."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained packages that provide specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, effectively transforming them into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge using multi-step workflows.","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，这些软件包提供专门的知识、工作流和工具，有效地将它们转化为具有过程知识的专用代理，使用多步骤工作流。","ja":"エージェントがモジュール化されたセルフコンテインドパッケージを作成できるようにし、専門知識、ワークフロー、ツールを提供して、実質的に多段階のワークフローを使用する手順知識を持つ専門エージェントに変換します。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 셀프 컨테이닝 패키지를 생성할 수 있도록하여 전문 지식, 워크플로 및 도구를 제공하고, 실제적으로 멀티 스텝 워크플로를 사용하는 절차 지식을 가진 전문 에이전트로 변환합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que proporcionan conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, transformándolos efectivamente en agentes especializados equipados con conocimientos procedimentales utilizando flujos de trabajo multietapa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des paquets modulaires et autocontenus qui fournissent des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, les transformant effectivement en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales utilisant des flux de travail multietapas.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse, Arbeitsabläufe und Tools bereitstellen, und verwandelt sie damit effektiv in spezialisierte Agenten, die mit prozeduralem Wissen ausgestattet sind und mehrstufige Arbeitsabläufe verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar pacotes modulares, autossuficientes que fornecem conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, transformando-os efetivamente em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural usando fluxos de trabalho em várias etapas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, которые предоставляют специализированные знания, рабочие процессы и инструменты, эффективно превращая их в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями с помощью многоступенчатых рабочих процессов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من إنشاء حزم متجانسة وذاتية الحدوث توفر معرفة متخصصة وإجراءات وأدوات، مما يؤدي إلى تحويلها بشكل فعال إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بالمعرفة الإجرائية باستخدام سلاسل إجراءات متعددة المراحل."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing procedural knowledge for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with specialized tools"],"zh":["创建领域特定入门指南","开发任务的程序知识","使用专用工具扩展代理功能"],"ja":["ドメイン固有のオンボーディングガイドを作成する","タスクの手順知識を開発する","専用ツールでエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인별 온보딩 가이드 만들기","작업을 위한 절차 지식 개발","전용 도구를 사용하여 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Crear guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollar conocimientos procedimentales para tareas","Ampliar las capacidades del agente con herramientas especializadas"],"fr":["Créer des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développer des connaissances procédurales pour les tâches","Étendre les capacités de l''agent avec des outils spécialisés"],"de":["Erstellen von domänenspezifischen Onboardingleitfäden","Entwickeln von prozeduralem Wissen für Aufgaben","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Tools"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para tarefas","Estender as capacidades do agente com ferramentas especializadas"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции, специфичных для домена","Разработка процедурных знаний для задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью специализированных инструментов"],"ar":["إنشاء أدلة إعداد متخصصة في المجال","تطوير معرفة إجرائية للمهام","تمديد قدرات الوكيل بأدوات متخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"zh":["需要了解 Claude 的体系结构和技能开发框架"],"ja":["Claude のアーキテクチャとスキル開発フレームワークを理解する必要がある"],"ko":["클로드의 아키텍처와 스킬 개발 프레임워크를 이해해야 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la arquitectura de Claude y del marco de desarrollo de habilidades"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de l''architecture de Claude et du cadre de développement de compétences"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Architektur von Claude und des Skill-Entwicklungsframeworks"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da arquitetura do Claude e do quadro de desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["Требует понимания архитектуры Claude и рамках разработки навыков"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لهيكل وكيل Claude وأطر إطار تطوير المهارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fierzone/agent-skills-standard/iOS Performance', 'community', 'fierzone', 'agent-skills-standard', 'fierzone/agent-skills-standard', 'iOS Performance', 0, 0, 20, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:54:01.508Z', NULL, '{"id":"fierzone/agent-skills-standard/iOS Performance","name":"iOS Performance","description":{"zh":"iOS ","ja":"iOS ","ko":"iOS ","es":"Optimiza el rendimiento de tus aplicaciones iOS con técnicas y herramientas especializadas","fr":"Optimisez les performances de vos applications iOS avec des techniques et des outils spécialisés","de":"Optimieren Sie die Leistung Ihrer iOS-Anwendungen mit spezialisierten Techniken und Tools","pt":"Otimize o desempenho do seu aplicativo iOS com técnicas de diagnóstico e otimização","ru":"Оптимизируйте производительность вашего приложения iOS с помощью методов диагностики и оптимизации","ar":"احسن أداء تطبيق آيفون الخاص بك باستخدام تقنيات التشخيص والتحسين","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"iOS","ja":"iOS","ko":"iOS ","es":"Mejora del Rendimiento en iOS","fr":"Amélioration des Performances iOS","de":"iOS Leistungsverbesserung","pt":"Otimização de Desempenho iOS","ru":"Оптимизация Производительности iOS","ar":"تحسين أداء آيفون","en":"iOS Performance"},"description":{"zh":"iOS ","ja":"iOS ","ko":"iOS ","es":"Optimiza el rendimiento de tus aplicaciones iOS con técnicas y herramientas especializadas","fr":"Optimisez les performances de vos applications iOS avec des techniques et des outils spécialisés","de":"Optimieren Sie die Leistung Ihrer iOS-Anwendungen mit spezialisierten Techniken und Tools","pt":"Otimize o desempenho do seu aplicativo iOS com técnicas de diagnóstico e otimização","ru":"Оптимизируйте производительность вашего приложения iOS с помощью методов диагностики и оптимизации","ar":"احسن أداء تطبيق آيفون الخاص بك باستخدام تقنيات التشخيص والتحسين","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","Table/Collection Views","Image Caching","SDWebImage"],"ja":["Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","Table/Collection Views","Image Caching","SDWebImage"],"ko":["Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","Table/Collection Views","Image Caching","SDWebImage"],"es":["Uso de Instruments para detectar problemas de memoria","Optimización de Table/Collection Views","Uso de Image Caching con SDWebImage o Kingfisher","Análisis de request payload sizes y frequency","Identificación de tareas pesadas de CPU y Main Thread stalls"],"fr":["Utilisation d''Instruments pour détecter les problèmes de mémoire","Optimisation de Table/Collection Views","Utilisation de Image Caching avec SDWebImage ou Kingfisher","Analyse des tailles et fréquences des requêtes","Identification des tâches lourdes de CPU et des blocages du thread principal"],"de":["Verwendung von Instruments zur Erkennung von Speicherproblemen","Optimierung von Table/Collection Views","Verwendung von Image Caching mit SDWebImage oder Kingfisher","Analyse der Anforderungspayload-Größen und -Häufigkeit","Identifizierung von CPU-intensiven Aufgaben und Main-Thread-Blockaden"],"pt":["Uso de Instruments para detectar problemas de memória","Otimização de Table/Collection Views","Uso de Image Caching com SDWebImage ou Kingfisher","Análise de request payload sizes e frequency com Network instrument","Identificação de tarefas pesadas de CPU e stalls de Main Thread com Time Profiler"],"ru":["Использование Instruments для обнаружения проблем с памятью","Оптимизация Table/Collection Views","Использование кэширования изображений с SDWebImage или Kingfisher","Анализ размеров и частоты запросов с помощью Network instrument","Определение тяжёлых задач CPU и зависаний основного потока с помощью Time Profiler"],"ar":["استخدام Instruments للكشف عن مشاكل الذاكرة","تحسين Views الجدول / المجموعة","استخدام ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت للصور مع SDWebImage أو Kingfisher","تحليل أحجام وحوادث الطلبات باستخدام أداة الشبكة","تحديد المهام الكثيرة من CPU وآثار المعالج الرئيسي باستخدام Time Profiler"]},"keywords":{"zh":["iOS ","iOS ","Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","iOS "],"ja":["iOS ","iOS ","Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","iOS "],"ko":["iOS ","iOS ","Instruments","Time Profiler","Network ","iOS "],"es":["rendimiento iOS","optimización de aplicaciones","Instruments","Image Caching","Table/Collection Views","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles"],"fr":["performances iOS","optimisation des applications","Instruments","mise en cache d''images","Table/Collection Views","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["iOS-Leistung","Optimierung von Anwendungen","Instruments","Bild-Caching","Table/Collection Views","Entwicklung von mobilen Anwendungen"],"pt":["otimização de desempenho iOS","desempenho de aplicativos","instruments","table view","image caching","network instrument","time profiler"],"ru":["оптимизация производительности ios","производительность приложений","инструменты","tableView","кэширование изображений","сетевой инструмент","профилировщик времени"],"ar":["تحسين أداء آيفون","أداء التطبيقات","أدوات","مشاهدة الجدول","ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت للصور","أداة الشبكة","مُحلل الوقت"]}},"owner":"fierzone","repo":"agent-skills-standard","repoPath":"fierzone/agent-skills-standard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"iOS Performance","description":"Standards for Instruments, Memory Management, and Optimization.","bodyPreview":"# iOS Performance Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0**\n\n## Implementation Guidelines\n\n### Diagnostic Tools\n\n- **Instruments**: Regularly use **Allocations** and **Leaks** to detect memory issues.\n- **Time Profiler**: Identify heavy CPU tasks and Main Thread stalls.\n- **Network instrument**: Analyze request payload sizes and frequency.\n\n### Optimization\n\n- **Table/Collection Views**: Always use `dequeueReusableCell` and keep `cellForRowAt` logic lightweight.\n- **Image Caching**: Use `SDWebImage` or `Ki","body":"# iOS Performance Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0**\n\n## Implementation Guidelines\n\n### Diagnostic Tools\n\n- **Instruments**: Regularly use **Allocations** and **Leaks** to detect memory issues.\n- **Time Profiler**: Identify heavy CPU tasks and Main Thread stalls.\n- **Network instrument**: Analyze request payload sizes and frequency.\n\n### Optimization\n\n- **Table/Collection Views**: Always use `dequeueReusableCell` and keep `cellForRowAt` logic lightweight.\n- **Image Caching**: Use `SDWebImage` or `Kingfisher` for remote assets to prevent redundant fetching and main-thread decoding. (Note: `AsyncImage` lacks built-in caching; prioritize third-party for lists).\n- **Background threads**: Offload expensive work (parsing, encryption) from the Main thread using GCD or Tasks.\n\n### Diagnostics\n\n- **Compiler Warnings**: Enable `SWIFT_TREAT_WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS` in Release builds.\n- **Static Analyzer**: Use Xcode''s \"Analyze\" (Product > Analyze) to find logic errors.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- **CPU work on Main Thread**: `**No parsing/processing on Main**: Use background thread.`\n- **Force Cache Flushes**: `**No redundant cache clears**: Let the system handle low-memory warnings via AppDelegate.`\n- **Retain Cycles**: `**Check for cycles in Instruments**: Use the Leaks instrument frequently.`\n\n## References\n\n- [Profiling & Optimization](references/implementation.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:01.508Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile Agents specializing in iOS app development needing expert performance optimization techniques.","zh":"适用于专注于iOS应用开发的移动代理，需要专家级性能优化技术的代理。","ja":"iOSアプリ開発におけるパフォーマンス最適化の専門技術が必要なモバイルエージェントに最適。","ko":"iOS 앱 개발을 전문으로 하는 모바일 에이전트에게 성능 최적화 기술이 필요한 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes móviles especializados en el desarrollo de aplicaciones de iOS que necesitan técnicas de optimización de rendimiento expertas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents mobiles spécialisés dans le développement d''applications iOS nécessitant des techniques d''optimisation de performances expertes.","de":"Perfekt für Mobile Agents, die auf die Entwicklung von iOS-Apps spezialisiert sind und Experten-Techniken zur Leistungsoptimierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Móveis especializados em desenvolvimento de aplicativos iOS que necessitam de técnicas de otimização de desempenho especializadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для мобильных агентов, специализирующихся на разработке приложений для iOS, требующих экспертных техник оптимизации производительности.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الهاتف المحمول المتخصص في تطوير تطبيقات iOS التي تحتاج إلى تقنيات تحسين الأداء الخبير."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to detect memory leaks and CPU-intensive tasks using Instruments, while optimizing table and collection views with dequeueReusableCell and leveraging image caching libraries like SDWebImage, ultimately enhancing overall iOS app performance.","zh":"使代理能够使用Instruments检测内存泄漏和CPU密集型任务，同时使用dequeueReusableCell优化表格和集合视图，并利用像SDWebImage这样的图像缓存库， 궁극上提高整个iOS应用的性能。","ja":"エージェントがInstrumentsを使用してメモリ漏れとCPU集中タスクを検出できるようにし、dequeueReusableCellを使用してテーブルとコレクションビューを最適化し、SDWebImageのようなイメージキャッシュライブラリを活用して、最終的に全体のiOSアプリのパフォーマンスを向上させる。","ko":"에이전트가 Instruments를 사용하여 메모리 누수와 CPU 집중적인 작업을 감지할 수 있도록 하며, dequeueReusableCell를 사용하여 테이블 및 컬렉션 뷰를 최적화하고, SDWebImage와 같은 이미지 캐싱 라이브러리를 활용하여 궁극적으로 전체 iOS 앱의 성능을 향상시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a detectar fugas de memoria y tareas intensivas de CPU utilizando Instruments, mientras se optimizan las vistas de tabla y colección con dequeueReusableCell y se aprovechan las bibliotecas de caché de imágenes como SDWebImage, lo que mejora en última instancia el rendimiento general de la aplicación de iOS.","fr":"Permet aux agents de détecter les fuites de mémoire et les tâches intensives en CPU à l''aide d''Instruments, tout en optimisant les vues de tableau et de collection avec dequeueReusableCell et en exploitant les bibliothèques de mise en cache d''images comme SDWebImage, ce qui améliore en fin de compte les performances globales de l''application iOS.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Speicherverluste und CPU-intensiven Aufgaben mithilfe von Instruments zu erkennen, während Tabellen- und Sammlungsansichten mit dequeueReusableCell optimiert und Bild-Cache-Bibliotheken wie SDWebImage genutzt werden, um letztendlich die Gesamtleistung der iOS-App zu verbessern.","pt":"Permite que os agentes detectem vazamentos de memória e tarefas intensivas de CPU usando Instruments, ao mesmo tempo em que otimizam tabelas e visualizações de coleção com dequeueReusableCell e aproveitam bibliotecas de cache de imagens como SDWebImage, melhorando assim o desempenho geral do aplicativo iOS.","ru":"Позволяет агентам обнаруживать утечки памяти и задачи, требующие больших затрат процессора, с помощью Instruments, а также оптимизировать таблицы и коллекции с dequeueReusableCell и использовать библиотеки кэширования изображений, такие как SDWebImage, в конечном итоге повышая общую производительность приложения для iOS.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء اكتشاف تسربات الذاكرة والمهام الكثيفة لاستخدام وحدة المعالجة المركزية باستخدام أدوات ، وفي الوقت نفسه تحسين العرض والمتحف مع dequeueReusableCell واستخدام مكتبات ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت للصور مثل SDWebImage ، مما يحسن الأداء العام لتطبيق iOS في النهاية."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging memory issues with Allocations and Leaks","Optimizing table and collection views for smoother user interaction","Analyzing network request payloads and frequency with Network instrument"],"zh":["使用分配和泄漏调试内存问题","优化表格和集合视图以实现更流畅的用户交互","使用网络仪表分析网络请求有效载荷和频率"],"ja":["AllocationsとLeaksを使用してメモリの問題をデバッグする","テーブルとコレクションビューを最適化してユーザーインタラクションをスムーズにする","Network instrumentを使用してネットワークリクエストのペイロードと頻度を分析する"],"ko":["할당 및 누수를 사용하여 메모리 문제를 디버깅합니다.","테이블 및 컬렉션 뷰를 최적화하여 사용자 상호 작용을 더 원활하게 만듭니다.","네트워크 악기를 사용하여 네트워크 요청의 페이로드 및 빈도를 분석합니다."],"es":["Depuración de problemas de memoria con Allocations y Leaks","Optimización de vistas de tabla y colección para una interacción del usuario más fluida","Análisis de la carga útil y frecuencia de solicitudes de red con el instrumento de red"],"fr":["Débogage des problèmes de mémoire avec Allocations et Leaks","Optimisation des vues de tableau et de collection pour une interaction utilisateur plus fluide","Analyse de la charge utile et de la fréquence des requêtes réseau avec l''instrument de réseau"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von Speicherproblemen mit Allocations und Leaks","Optimierung von Tabellen- und Sammlungsansichten für eine reibungslosere Benutzerinteraktion","Analyse von Netzwerkanforderungen und -häufigkeit mit dem Netzwerkinstrument"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas de memória com Allocations e Leaks","Otimização de tabelas e visualizações de coleção para interação do usuário mais suave","Análise de payloads e frequência de solicitações de rede com o instrumento Network"],"ru":["Отладка проблем с памятью с помощью Allocations и Leaks","Оптимизация таблиц и коллекций для более гладкого взаимодействия с пользователем","Анализ полезных нагрузок и частоты сетевых запросов с помощью инструмента Network"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء الذاكرة باستخدام Allocations و Leaks","تحسين العرض والمتحف لتفاعل المستخدم الأملس","تحليل حمولات و تكرار الطلبات الشبكية مع أداة الشبكة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Xcode and Instruments for diagnostic tools","Limited to iOS platform development","Familiarity with Swift or Objective-C programming languages necessary"],"zh":["需要Xcode和Instruments进行诊断","仅限于iOS平台开发","需要熟悉Swift或Objective-C编程语言"],"ja":["診断ツールとしてXcodeとInstrumentsが必要","iOSプラットフォーム開発のみ","SwiftまたはObjective-Cプログラミング言語の知識が必要"],"ko":["진단 도구로서 Xcode 및 Instruments가 필요합니다.","iOS 플랫폼 개발만 해당됩니다.","Swift 또는 Objective-C 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 지식이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere Xcode e Instruments para herramientas de diagnóstico","Limitado al desarrollo de plataforma de iOS","Se requiere familiaridad con los lenguajes de programación Swift o Objective-C"],"fr":["Nécessite Xcode et Instruments pour les outils de diagnostic","Limité au développement de plate-forme iOS","Exige une connaissance des langages de programmation Swift ou Objective-C"],"de":["Benötigt Xcode und Instruments für Diagnosetools","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung der iOS-Plattform","Benötigt Kenntnisse in den Programmiersprachen Swift oder Objective-C"],"pt":["Requer Xcode e Instruments para ferramentas de diagnóstico","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de plataforma iOS","Familiaridade com as linguagens de programação Swift ou Objective-C necessária"],"ru":["Требуется Xcode и Instruments для диагностических инструментов","Ограничен разработкой платформы iOS","Необходимо знание языков программирования Swift или Objective-C"],"ar":["يتطلب Xcode و Instruments لأدوات التشخيص","محدود بتطوير منصة iOS","الاطلاع على لغات البرمجة Swift أو Objective-C ضروري"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":20}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('illogical/InstructionLibrary/skill-creator', 'community', 'illogical', 'InstructionLibrary', 'illogical/InstructionLibrary', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:54:11.570Z', NULL, '{"id":"illogical/InstructionLibrary/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建者提供了开发高效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展 Claude 的功能并提供专业知识","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者が効果的なスキルを作成し、Claude の機能を拡張し、専門知識を提供するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 효율적인 스킬을 개발하고 Claude의 기능을 확장하며 전문 지식을 제공하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es una herramienta para desarrollar habilidades personalizadas que amplían las capacidades de Claude","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un outil pour développer des compétences sur mesure qui étendent les capacités de Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Werkzeug zum Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern","pt":"O Skill Creator é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas que estendem as capacidades de Claude. Ele fornece conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho para domínios e tarefas específicos.","ru":"Skill Creator — это инструмент для создания пользовательских навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude. Он предоставляет специализированное знание и рабочие процессы для конкретных доменов и задач.","ar":"Skill Creator هو أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة لتوسيع قدرات برنامج Claude. يوفر معرفة متخصصة وعمليات عمل لمجالات ومهام محددة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建者：开发高效技能的指南","ja":"スキルクリエーター：効果的なスキルの作成ガイド","ko":"스킬 생성기: 효율적인 스킬 개발 가이드","es":"Creador de Habilidades: Desarrolla habilidades personaliz...","fr":"Créateur de Compétences: Développez des compétences sur m...","de":"Fähigkeits-Ersteller: Erstellen Sie benutzerdefinierte Fä...","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Desenvolvimento de Skills Persona...","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Разработка Пользовательских Навыков","ar":"مُبدع المهارات: تطوير مهارات مخصصة","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建者提供了开发高效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展 Claude 的功能并提供专业知识","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者が効果的なスキルを作成し、Claude の機能を拡張し、専門知識を提供するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 효율적인 스킬을 개발하고 Claude의 기능을 확장하며 전문 지식을 제공하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es una herramienta para desarrollar habilidades personalizadas que amplían las capacidades de Claude","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un outil pour développer des compétences sur mesure qui étendent les capacités de Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Werkzeug zum Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern","pt":"O Skill Creator é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas que estendem as capacidades de Claude. Ele fornece conhecimento especializado e fluxos...","ru":"Skill Creator — это инструмент для создания пользовательских навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude. Он предоставляет специализированное знание и рабо...","ar":"Skill Creator هو أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة لتوسيع قدرات برنامج Claude. يوفر معرفة متخصصة وعمليات عمل لمجالات ومهام محددة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供开发高效技能的指南","帮助开发者扩展 Claude 的功能","提供专业知识和工作流程","支持多种技能开发","简化技能开发流程"],"ja":["効果的なスキルの作成ガイドを提供","開発者が Claude の機能を拡張するのに役立つ","専門知識とワークフローを提供","複数のスキル開発をサポート","スキル開発プロセスを簡素化"],"ko":["효율적인 스킬 개발 가이드 제공","개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장하는 데 도움","전문 지식과 워크플로우 제공","다중 스킬 개발 지원","스킬 개발 프로세스简化"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Herramientas y conocimientos personalizados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Desarrollo de habilidades personalizadas","Integración con la plataforma de Claude"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Outils et connaissances sur mesure","Élargissement des capacités de Claude","Développement de compétences sur mesure","Intégration avec la plateforme de Claude"],"de":["Spezialisierte Workflows","Benutzerdefinierte Tools und Kenntnisse","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten","Integration mit der Claude-Plattform"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Conhecimento especializado para domínios e tarefas","Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Integração com Claude","Desenvolvimento de soluções mustomizadas"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских навыков","Специализированное знание для доменов и задач","Специализированные рабочие процессы","Интеграция с Claude","Разработка индивидуальных решений"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","معرفة متخصصة لمجالات ومهام","عمليات عمل مخصصة","التكامل مع برنامج Claude","تطوير حلول مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建者","开发高效技能","扩展 Claude 的功能","专业知识","工作流程","技能开发","开发工具"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","効果的なスキルの作成","Claude の機能拡張","専門知識","ワークフロー","スキル開発","開発ツール"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","효율적인 스킬 개발","Claude의 기능 확장","전문 지식","워크플로우","스킬 개발","개발 도구"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","agentes de inteligencia artificial","flujos de trabajo especializados","herramientas personalizadas","ampliación de capacidades","inteligencia artificial","desarrollo de software","tecnología de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","agents d''intelligence artificielle","flux de travail spécialisés","outils sur mesure","élargissement des capacités","intelligence artificielle","développement de logiciels","technologie d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","KI-Agenten","spezialisierte Workflows","benutzerdefinierte Tools","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten","Künstliche Intelligenz","Software-Entwicklung","KI-Technologie"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades","criação de skills","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","tecnologia de inteligência artificial","soluções personalizadas","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["разработка навыков","создание навыков","инструменты разработки","технология искусственного интеллекта","индивидуальные решения","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تطوير المهارات","إنشاء المهارات","أدوات التطوير","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي","حلول مخصصة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"illogical","repo":"InstructionLibrary","repoPath":"illogical/InstructionLibrary","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:11.570Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Language Agents seeking to create specialized knowledge domains and workflows","zh":"适合高级语言代理创建专用知识领域和工作流","ja":"高度な言語エージェントが専用の知識ドメインとワークフローを作成するのに適しています","ko":"고급 언어 에이전트가 전문 지식 도메인 및 워크플ロー 생성에 적합함","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que buscan crear dominios de conocimiento especializados y flujos de trabajo","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de langage avancés qui cherchent à créer des domaines de connaissances spécialisés et des flux de travail","de":"Ideal für fortgeschrittene Sprachagenten, die spezialisierte Wissensbereiche und Workflows erstellen möchten","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que buscam criar domínios de conhecimento especializados e fluxos de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых языковых агентов, стремящихся создать специализированные области знаний и рабочие процессы","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة متقدم يبحث عن إنشاء مجالات معرفة متخصصة وسلاسل عمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge, providing modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities through specialized workflows and tools, leveraging multi-step workflows","zh":"使代理能够转变为配备程序化知识的专用代理，提供模块化和自包含的软件包，通过专用工作流和工具扩展功能，利用多步骤工作流","ja":"エージェントが手順きょうか知識を備えた専用エージェントに変化することを可能にし、モジュール化およびセルフコンテインドパッケージを提供し、専用ワークフローおよびツールを利用して機能を拡張し、マルチステップワークフローを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 절차 지식이 포함된 전문 에이전트로 변신할 수 있도록 하며, 모듈화되고 자체 포함된 패키지를 제공하여 전문 워크플로 및 도구를 통해 기능을 확장하고 다단계 워크플로를 활용함","es":"Permite a los agentes transformarse en agentes especializados equipados con conocimiento procedimental, proporcionando paquetes modulares y autosuficientes que amplían las capacidades a través de flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, aprovechando flujos de trabajo multietapa","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des packages modulaires et autonomes qui étendent les capacités grâce à des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, en exploitant des flux de travail multietapas","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Agenten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem sie modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitstellen, die die Fähigkeiten durch spezialisierte Workflows und Tools erweitern, indem sie mehrstufige Workflows nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades por meio de fluxos de trabalho especializados e ferramentas, aproveitando fluxos de trabalho em várias etapas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированные агенты, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности посредством специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя многоступенчатые рабочие процессы","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التحول إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بمعرفة إجرائية ، وتوفير حزم مودULAR ومتكاملة توفر امتدادات للقدرات من خلال سلاسل عمل متخصصة وأدوات ، واستخدام سلاسل عمل متعددة المراحل"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing procedural knowledge for niche tasks","Extending agent capabilities with modular packages"],"zh":["创建特定领域的入门指南","开发针对细分任务的程序化知识","使用模块化包扩展代理功能"],"ja":["ドメイン固有のオンボーディングガイドを作成する","ニッチタスクの手順きょうか知識を開発する","モジュール化パッケージを使用してエージェント機能を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인별 온보딩 가이드 생성","니치 작업을 위한 절차 지식 개발","모듈화된 패키지를 사용하여 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Creación de guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollo de conocimiento procedimental para tareas de nicho","Ampliación de las capacidades de los agentes con paquetes modulares"],"fr":["Création de guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développement de connaissances procédurales pour des tâches de niche","Extension des capacités des agents avec des packages modulaires"],"de":["Erstellung von domänenspezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden","Entwicklung von prozeduralem Wissen für Nischenaufgaben","Erweiterung der Agentenfähigkeiten mit modularen Paketen"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para tarefas de nicho","Estender as capacidades do agente com pacotes modulares"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных областей","Разработка процедурных знаний для нишевых задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью модульных пакетов"],"ar":["إنشاء أدلة إعدادเฉพาะ بالمجال","تطوير معرفة إجرائية لأعمال محددة","تمديد قدرات العميل باستخدام حزم مودULAR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s capabilities and limitations","Dependent on the agent''s ability to integrate new knowledge and workflows"],"zh":["需要了解Claude的能力和局限性","依赖于代理整合新知识和工作流的能力"],"ja":["Claudeの能力と制約を理解する必要がある","新しい知識とワークフローを統合するエージェントの能力に依存する"],"ko":["Claude의 능력 및 한계를 이해해야 함","새로운 지식 및 워크플로를 통합하는 에이전트의 능력에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión de las capacidades y limitaciones de Claude","Depende de la capacidad del agente para integrar nuevos conocimientos y flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des capacités et des limites de Claude","Dépend de la capacité de l''agent à intégrer de nouveaux connaissances et flux de travail"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis für die Fähigkeiten und Einschränkungen von Claude","Hängt von der Fähigkeit des Agents ab, neue Kenntnisse und Workflows zu integrieren"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das capacidades e limitações do Claude","Depende da capacidade do agente de integrar novos conhecimentos e fluxos de trabalho"],"ru":["Требует понимания возможностей и ограничений Claude","Зависит от способности агента интегрировать новые знания и рабочие процессы"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم إمكانيات وقيود كلود","يعتمد على قدرة العميل على دمج معرفة وجديد وسلاسل عمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/Android Persistence', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'Android Persistence', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:54:29.079Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/Android Persistence","name":"Android Persistence","description":{"zh":"Android 持久化标准提供了优化应用数据存储的指南","ja":"Android パーシステンスはアプリケーションデータの保存を最適化する","ko":"안드로이드 지속성은 애플리케이션 데이터 저장을 최적화합니다","es":"La persistencia en Android se refiere a la capacidad de almacenar y recuperar datos de manera eficiente. Room y DataStore son dos opciones populares","fr":"La persistance Android fait référence à la capacité de stocker et de récupérer des données de manière efficace. Room et DataStore sont deux options populaires","de":"Die Persistenz in Android bezieht sich auf die Fähigkeit, Daten effizient zu speichern und wiederzuerlangen. Room und DataStore sind zwei beliebte Optionen","pt":"Os padrões de persistência Android fornecem diretrizes para armazenar e gerenciar dados de forma eficiente. Aprenda sobre Room e DataStore","ru":"Стандарты персистенции Android предоставляют рекомендации для хранения и управления данными эффективным образом. Узнайте о Room и DataStore","ar":"تقدم معايير استمرارية أندرويد إرشادات لتخزين وإدارة البيانات بفعالية. تعرف على Room و DataStore","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Android 持久化技术","ja":"Android パーシステンス","ko":"안드로이드 지속성","es":"Persistencia en Android","fr":"Persistance Android","de":"Android Persistence","pt":"Padrões de Persistência Android","ru":"Стандарты персистенции Android","ar":"معايير استمرارية أندرويد","en":"Android Persistence"},"description":{"zh":"Android 持久化标准提供了优化应用数据存储的指南","ja":"Android パーシステンスはアプリケーションデータの保存を最適化する","ko":"안드로이드 지속성은 애플리케이션 데이터 저장을 최적화합니다","es":"La persistencia en Android se refiere a la capacidad de almacenar y recuperar datos de manera eficiente. Room y DataStore son dos opciones populares","fr":"La persistance Android fait référence à la capacité de stocker et de récupérer des données de manière efficace. Room et DataStore sont deux options populaires","de":"Die Persistenz in Android bezieht sich auf die Fähigkeit, Daten effizient zu speichern und wiederzuerlangen. Room und DataStore sind zwei beliebte Optionen","pt":"Os padrões de persistência Android fornecem diretrizes para armazenar e gerenciar dados de forma eficiente. Aprenda sobre Room e DataStore","ru":"Стандарты персистенции Android предоставляют рекомендации для хранения и управления данными эффективным образом. Узнайте о Room и DataStore","ar":"تقدم معايير استمرارية أندرويد إرشادات لتخزين وإدارة البيانات بفعالية. تعرف على Room و DataStore","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["Room 持久化库","DataStore 替代 SharedPreferences","事务支持","异步查询","实体映射"],"ja":["Room パーシステンスライブラリ","DataStore を使用した SharedPreferences の置き換え","トランザクションのサポート","非同期クエリ","エンティティマッピング"],"ko":["Room 지속성 라이브러리","DataStore로 SharedPreferences 대체","트랜잭션 지원","비동기 쿼리","엔티티 매핑"],"es":["Implementación de Room para consultas y escrituras","Uso de DataStore para reemplazar SharedPreferences","Soporte para transacciones con @Transaction","Compatibilidad con Flow y suspend para operaciones asíncronas","Mapeo de entidades a modelos de dominio en el repositorio","Inyección de instancias singleton de DataStore"],"fr":["Implémentation de Room pour les requêtes et les écritures","Utilisation de DataStore pour remplacer SharedPreferences","Prise en charge des transactions avec @Transaction","Compatibilité avec Flow et suspend pour les opérations asynchrones","Mappage des entités aux modèles de domaine dans le référentiel","Injection d''instances singleton de DataStore"],"de":["Implementierung von Room für Abfragen und Schreibvorgänge","Verwendung von DataStore zum Ersetzen von SharedPreferences","Unterstützung für Transaktionen mit @Transaction","Kompatibilität mit Flow und suspend für asynchrone Vorgänge","Zuordnung von Entitäten zu Domain-Modellen im Repository","Einjektion von Singleton-Instanzen von DataStore"],"pt":["Uso de Room para consultas assíncronas","Uso de DataStore para substituir SharedPreferences","Implementação de transações com @Transaction","Mapeamento de entidades para modelos de domínio","Injeção de instâncias singleton via Scope"],"ru":["Использование Room для асинхронных запросов","Использование DataStore для замены SharedPreferences","Реализация транзакций с @Transaction","Отображение сущностей на модели домена","Внедрение singleton-экземпляров через Scope"],"ar":["استخدام Room للاستفسارات غير المتزامنة","استخدام DataStore لاستبدال SharedPreferences","تنفيذ المعاملات مع @Transaction","تعيين الكيانات إلى نماذج المجال","حقن مثيلات Singleton عبر Scope"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Android 持久化","Room","DataStore","SharedPreferences","异步查询","事务","实体映射"],"ja":["Android パーシステンス","Room","DataStore","SharedPreferences","非同期クエリ","トランザクション","エンティティマッピング"],"ko":["안드로이드 지속성","Room","DataStore","SharedPreferences","비동기 쿼리","트랜잭션","엔티티 매핑"],"es":["persistencia en android","room android","datastore android","android desarrollo","programación android","almacenamiento de datos android","gestión de datos android","android persistence","android room"],"fr":["persistance android","room android","datastore android","développement android","programmation android","stockage de données android","gestion de données android","android persistance","android room"],"de":["persistenz in android","room android","datastore android","android entwickeln","programmieren android","datenspeicherung android","datenverwaltung android","android persistenz","android room"],"pt":["persistência android","room android","datastore android","desenvolvimento android","padrões de persistência","armazenamento de dados android"],"ru":["персистенция android","room android","datastore android","разработка android","стандарты персистенции","хранение данных android"],"ar":["استمرارية أندرويد","room أندرويد","datastore أندرويد","تطوير أندرويد","معايير استمرارية","تخزين البيانات أندرويد"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Android Persistence","description":"Standards for Room Database and DataStore","bodyPreview":"# Android Persistence Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0**\n\n## Implementation Guidelines\n\n### Room\n\n- **Async**: Return `Flow<List<T>>` for queries, use `suspend` for Write/Insert.\n- **Entities**: Keep simple `@Entity` data classes. Map to Domain models in Repository.\n- **Transactions**: Use `@Transaction` for multi-table queries (Relations).\n\n### DataStore\n\n- **Usage**: Replace `SharedPreferences` with `ProtoDataStore` (Type-safe) or `PreferencesDataStore`.\n- **Scope**: Inject singleton instance via","body":"# Android Persistence Standards\n\n## **Priority: P0**\n\n## Implementation Guidelines\n\n### Room\n\n- **Async**: Return `Flow<List<T>>` for queries, use `suspend` for Write/Insert.\n- **Entities**: Keep simple `@Entity` data classes. Map to Domain models in Repository.\n- **Transactions**: Use `@Transaction` for multi-table queries (Relations).\n\n### DataStore\n\n- **Usage**: Replace `SharedPreferences` with `ProtoDataStore` (Type-safe) or `PreferencesDataStore`.\n- **Scope**: Inject singleton instance via Hilt.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- **Main Thread**: `**No IO on Main**: Use Dispatchers.IO (Room helper does this, but verify flow collection).`\n- **Domain Leak**: `**No Entities in UI**: Map to Domain/UI Models.`\n\n## References\n\n- [DAO Templates](references/implementation.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:29.079Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile Agents needing robust Android data storage solutions using Room and DataStore","zh":"非常适合需要使用 Room 和 DataStore 实现强大的 Android 数据存储解决方案的移动代理","ja":"Room と DataStore を使用した堅牢な Android データストレージ ソリューションを必要とするモバイル エージェントに最適","ko":"Room과 DataStore를 사용하여 강력한 안드로이드 데이터 저장 솔루션을 필요로 하는 모바일 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Móviles que necesitan soluciones de almacenamiento de datos de Android robustas utilizando Room y DataStore","fr":"Parfait pour les agents mobiles ayant besoin de solutions de stockage de données Android robustes utilisant Room et DataStore","de":"Perfekt für Mobile Agenten, die robuste Android-Datenspeicherlösungen mit Room und DataStore benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Móveis que precisam de soluções robustas de armazenamento de dados Android usando Room e DataStore","ru":"Идеально подходит для мобильных агентов, которым требуются прочные решения для хранения данных Android с помощью Room и DataStore","ar":"مثالي لعميل المحمول الذي يحتاج إلى حلول تخزين بيانات أندرويد قوية باستخدام Room و DataStore"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage complex data transactions using @Transaction for multi-table queries and replace SharedPreferences with ProtoDataStore for type-safe data storage, leveraging Flow and suspend for asynchronous operations","zh":"赋予代理管理复杂数据事务的能力，使用 @Transaction 处理多表查询，并使用 ProtoDataStore 替代 SharedPreferences 实现类型安全的数据存储，利用 Flow 和 suspend 实现异步操作","ja":"@Transaction を使用して多表クエリを処理し、ProtoDataStore を使用して SharedPreferences を置き換えて型安全なデータストレージを実現し、Flow と suspend を使用して非同期操作を可能にすることで、複雑なデータトランザクションを管理するためのエージェントを強化","ko":"@Transaction을 사용하여 다중 테이블 쿼리를 처리하고 ProtoDataStore를 사용하여 SharedPreferences를 대체하여 유형 안전한 데이터 저장소를实现하며 Flow와 suspend를 사용하여 비동기 연산을 가능하게 함으로써 복잡한 데이터 트랜젝션을 관리할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar transacciones de datos complejas utilizando @Transaction para consultas de varias tablas y reemplazar SharedPreferences con ProtoDataStore para un almacenamiento de datos seguro y con tipos, aprovechando Flow y suspend para operaciones asíncronas","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des transactions de données complexes en utilisant @Transaction pour des requêtes multi-tables et de remplacer SharedPreferences par ProtoDataStore pour un stockage de données sécurisé et typé, en exploitant Flow et suspend pour les opérations asynchrones","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, komplexe Datentransaktionen mithilfe von @Transaction für Multitabellenabfragen zu verwalten und SharedPreferences durch ProtoDataStore für typsicheres Datenspeichern zu ersetzen, wobei Flow und suspend für asynchrone Operationen genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar transações de dados complexas usando @Transaction para consultas de multi-tabela e substituir SharedPreferences por ProtoDataStore para armazenamento de dados de tipo seguro, aproveitando Flow e suspend para operações assíncronas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять сложными транзакциями данных с помощью @Transaction для многотабличных запросов и заменять SharedPreferences на ProtoDataStore для безопасного хранения данных с типовым контролем, используя Flow и suspend для асинхронных операций","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة معاملات البيانات المعقدة باستخدام @Transaction لاستفسارات الجداول المتعددة واستبدال SharedPreferences بـ ProtoDataStore لتخزين البيانات بأمان مع التحكم في النوع، واستغلال Flow و suspend للعمليات غير المتزامنة"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing data persistence in Android apps using Room","Migrating from SharedPreferences to DataStore for secure data storage","Optimizing data transactions with @Transaction"],"zh":["在 Android 应用中使用 Room 实现数据持久化","从 SharedPreferences 迁移到 DataStore 以实现安全的数据存储","使用 @Transaction 优化数据事务"],"ja":["Room を使用して Android アプリでデータ永続化を実現","SharedPreferences から DataStore への移行によるセキュアなデータストレージの実現","@Transaction を使用したデータトランザクションの最適化"],"ko":["Room을 사용하여 안드로이드 애플리케이션에서 데이터 지속성을 구현","SharedPreferences에서 DataStore로의 마이그레이션을 통해 안전한 데이터 저장을 구현","@Transaction을 사용하여 데이터 트랜잭션을 최적화"],"es":["Implementar la persistencia de datos en aplicaciones de Android utilizando Room","Migrar de SharedPreferences a DataStore para un almacenamiento de datos seguro","Optimizar las transacciones de datos con @Transaction"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre la persistance des données dans les applications Android à l''aide de Room","Migrer de SharedPreferences vers DataStore pour un stockage de données sécurisé","Optimiser les transactions de données avec @Transaction"],"de":["Implementierung der Datenspeicherung in Android-Apps mit Room","Migration von SharedPreferences zu DataStore für sicheres Datenspeichern","Optimierung von Datentransaktionen mit @Transaction"],"pt":["Implementar persistência de dados em aplicativos Android usando Room","Migrar de SharedPreferences para DataStore para armazenamento de dados seguro","Otimizar transações de dados com @Transaction"],"ru":["Реализация персистентности данных в приложениях Android с помощью Room","Миграция с SharedPreferences на DataStore для безопасного хранения данных","Оптимизация транзакций данных с помощью @Transaction"],"ar":["تنفيذ استمرارية البيانات في تطبيقات أندرويد باستخدام Room","الانتقال من SharedPreferences إلى DataStore لتخزين البيانات بشكل آمن","تحسين معاملات البيانات باستخدام @Transaction"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Kotlin Coroutines for asynchronous operations","Android-specific implementation"],"zh":["需要 Kotlin Coroutines 来支持异步操作","Android 特定的实现"],"ja":["非同期操作をサポートするために Kotlin Coroutines が必要","Android 専用の実装"],"ko":["비동기 연산을 지원하기 위해 Kotlin Coroutines가 필요","안드로이드 전용 구현"],"es":["Requiere Kotlin Coroutines para operaciones asíncronas","Implementación específica de Android"],"fr":["Nécessite Kotlin Coroutines pour les opérations asynchrones","Implémentation spécifique à Android"],"de":["Erfordert Kotlin Coroutines für asynchrone Operationen","Android-spezifische Implementierung"],"pt":["Requer Kotlin Coroutines para operações assíncronas","Implementação específica do Android"],"ru":["Требует Kotlin Coroutines для асинхронных операций","Реализация специфичная для Android"],"ar":["يتطلب Kotlin Coroutines للعمليات غير المتزامنة","تنفيذ محدد لمنصة أندرويد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
