,"description":{"zh":"桌面应用开发指南，使用Web技术同时支持Windows、macOS和Linux","ja":"デスクトップアプリ開発ガイド、Web技術を使用してWindows、macOS、Linuxを同時にサポート","ko":"데스크톱 앱 개발 가이드, Web 기술을 사용하여 Windows, macOS, Linux를 동시에 지원","es":"Guía para desarrollar aplicaciones de escritorio utilizando tecnologías web como HTML, CSS y JavaScript, soportando Windows, macOS y Linux simultáneamente","fr":"Guide pour développer des applications de bureau en utilisant des technologies web comme HTML, CSS et JavaScript, prenant en charge Windows, macOS et Linux s...","de":"Anleitung zum Erstellen von Desktop-Anwendungen mit Web-Technologien wie HTML, CSS und JavaScript, die Windows, macOS und Linux gleichzeitig unterstützen","pt":"Desenvolva aplicativos de desktop cross-plataforma usando tecnologias web. Suporte a Windows, macOS e Linux com uma única base de código","ru":"Разрабатывайте кроссплатформенные десктоп-приложения, используя веб-технологии. Поддержка Windows, macOS и Linux с помощью единой кодовой базы","ar":"تطوير تطبيقات سطح المكتب متعددة المنصات باستخدام تقنيات الويب. دعم لويندوز و ماك و لينكس مع قاعدة код واحدة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用Web技术（HTML、CSS、JavaScript）","同时支持Windows、macOS和Linux","轻量级（3MB）","Rust安全性","成熟的生态系统"],"ja":["Web技術（HTML、CSS、JavaScript）を使用","Windows、macOS、Linuxを同時にサポート","軽量（3MB）","Rustのセキュリティ","成熟したエコシステム"],"ko":["Web 기술(HTML, CSS, JavaScript)을 사용","Windows, macOS, Linux를 동시에 지원","軽量(3MB)","Rust 보안","성숙한 에코시스템"],"es":["Soporte para Windows, macOS y Linux","Desarrollo con tecnologías web como HTML, CSS y JavaScript","Selección de frameworks como Tauri y Electron","Seguridad con Rust","Tamaño de archivo ligero de 3MB"],"fr":["Prise en charge de Windows, macOS et Linux","Développement avec des technologies web comme HTML, CSS et JavaScript","Sélection de frameworks comme Tauri et Electron","Sécurité avec Rust","Taille de fichier légère de 3Mo"],"de":["Unterstützung für Windows, macOS und Linux","Entwicklung mit Web-Technologien wie HTML, CSS und JavaScript","Framework-Auswahl wie Tauri und Electron","Sicherheit mit Rust","Geringe Dateigröße von 3MB"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento cross-plataforma","Suporte a Windows, macOS e Linux","Uso de tecnologias web como HTML, CSS e JavaScript","Criação de aplicativos leves e seguros","Compatibilidade com frameworks como Tauri e Electron"],"ru":["Кроссплатформенная разработка","Поддержка Windows, macOS и Linux","Использование веб-технологий, таких как HTML, CSS и JavaScript","Создание легких и безопасных приложений","Совместимость с фреймворками, такими как Tauri и Electron"],"ar":["التطوير متعدد المنصات","دعم لويندوز و ماك و لينكس","استخدام تقنيات الويب مثل HTML و CSS و JavaScript","إنشاء تطبيقات خفيفة وآمنة","التوافق مع الإطارات مثل Tauri و Electron"]},"keywords":{"zh":["桌面应用开发","Web技术","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Windows","macOS","Linux","Tauri","Electron"],"ja":["デスクトップアプリ開発","Web技術","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Windows","macOS","Linux","Tauri","Electron"],"ko":["데스크톱 앱 개발","Web 기술","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Windows","macOS","Linux","Tauri","Electron"],"es":["desarrollo de aplicaciones de escritorio","tecnologías web","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron","seguridad con Rust"],"fr":["développement d''applications de bureau","technologies web","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron","sécurité avec Rust"],"de":["Desktop-Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Web-Technologien","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron","Sicherheit mit Rust"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de aplicativos de desktop","tecnologias web","cross-plataforma","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron"],"ru":["разработка десктоп-приложений","веб-технологии","кроссплатформенная разработка","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات سطح المكتب","تقنيات الويب","متعدد المنصات","HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Tauri","Electron"]}},"owner":"suhwan","repo":"claude-registry","repoPath":"suhwan/claude-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"desktop-app","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Desktop App Development Expertise\n\n## Overview\n\nA guide for developing desktop apps using web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript).\nSupport Windows, macOS, and Linux simultaneously with a single codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Framework Selection Guide\n\n### Framework Selection by Tier (v1.3.0)\n\n| Framework | Tier | Recommendation | Use Case |\n|-----------|------|----------------|----------|\n| **Tauri** | Tier 2 | ⭐ Primary | Lightweight (3MB), Rust security |\n| **Electron** | Tier 3 | Supported | Mature ec","body":"# Desktop App Development Expertise\n\n## Overview\n\nA guide for developing desktop apps using web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript).\nSupport Windows, macOS, and Linux simultaneously with a single codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Framework Selection Guide\n\n### Framework Selection by Tier (v1.3.0)\n\n| Framework | Tier | Recommendation | Use Case |\n|-----------|------|----------------|----------|\n| **Tauri** | Tier 2 | ⭐ Primary | Lightweight (3MB), Rust security |\n| **Electron** | Tier 3 | Supported | Mature ecosystem, VS Code-like apps |\n\n> **AI-Native Recommendation**: Tauri\n> - 35% YoY growth\n> - 20-40MB memory vs Electron''s 200-400MB\n> - Mobile support (iOS/Android) via Tauri 2.0\n> - Rust backend = memory safety\n\n> **Ecosystem Recommendation**: Electron\n> - Mature tooling\n> - Node.js integration\n> - Proven at scale (VS Code, Slack)\n\n### Level-wise Recommendations\n\n```\nStarter → Tauri (v2) [Tier 2]\n  - Simpler setup than Electron\n  - Smaller output bundles (~3MB vs ~150MB)\n\nDynamic → Tauri + auto-update [Tier 2]\n  - Includes server integration, auto-update\n  - Lower memory footprint\n\nEnterprise → Tauri [Tier 2] or Electron [Tier 3]\n  - Tauri for performance and security\n  - Electron for complex Node.js integration\n```\n\n---\n\n## Electron Guide\n\n### Project Creation\n\n```bash\n# Create with electron-vite (recommended)\nnpm create @electron-vite/create my-electron-app\ncd my-electron-app\n\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# Start development server\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n### Folder Structure\n\n```\nmy-electron-app/\n├── src/\n│   ├── main/               # Main process (Node.js)\n│   │   └── index.ts        # App entry point, window management\n│   ├── preload/            # Preload script\n│   │   └── index.ts        # Renderer↔Main bridge\n│   └── renderer/           # Renderer process (Web)\n│       ├── src/            # React/Vue code\n│       └── index.html      # HTML entry point\n├── resources/              # App icons, assets\n├── electron.vite.config.ts # Build configuration\n├── electron-builder.yml    # Deployment configuration\n└── package.json\n```\n\n### Core Concept: Process Separation\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    Electron App                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Main Process (Node.js)                             │\n│  - System API access (files, network, etc.)         │\n│  - Window creation/management                       │\n│  - Menu, tray management                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Preload Script (Bridge)                            │\n│  - Safe main↔renderer communication                 │\n│  - Expose only specific APIs                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Renderer Process (Chromium)                        │\n│  - Web UI (React, Vue, etc.)                        │\n│  - DOM access                                       │\n│  - No direct Node.js API access (security)          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Main Process\n\n```typescript\n// src/main/index.ts\nimport { app, BrowserWindow, ipcMain } from ''electron'';\nimport { join } from ''path'';\n\nlet mainWindow: BrowserWindow | null = null;\n\nfunction createWindow() {\n  mainWindow = new BrowserWindow({\n    width: 1200,\n    height: 800,\n    webPreferences: {\n      preload: join(__dirname, ''../preload/index.js''),\n      sandbox: false,\n    },\n  });\n\n  // Dev mode: Load Vite server\n  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === ''development'') {\n    mainWindow.loadURL(''http://localhost:5173'');\n    mainWindow.webContents.openDevTools();\n  } else {\n    // Production: Load built files\n    mainWindow.loadFile(join(__dirname, ''../renderer/index.html''));\n  }\n}\n\napp.whenReady().then(createWindow);\n\napp.on(''window-all-closed'', () => {\n  if (process.platform !== ''darwin'') {\n    app.quit();\n  }\n});\n\n// IPC: Handle requests from renderer\nipcMain.handle(''read-file'', async (event, filePath) => {\n  const fs = await import(''fs/promises'');\n  return fs.readFile(filePath, ''utf-8'');\n});\n```\n\n### Preload Script\n\n```typescript\n// src/preload/index.ts\nimport { contextBridge, ipcRenderer } from ''electron'';\n\n// APIs to safely expose to renderer\ncontextBridge.exposeInMainWorld(''electronAPI'', {\n  // Read file\n  readFile: (filePath: string) => ipcRenderer.invoke(''read-file'', filePath),\n\n  // Save file dialog\n  saveFile: (content: string) => ipcRenderer.invoke(''save-file'', content),\n\n  // App version\n  getVersion: () => process.env.npm_package_version,\n\n  // Platform\n  platform: process.platform,\n});\n\n// Type definitions (for use in renderer)\ndeclare global {\n  interface Window {\n    electronAPI: {\n      readFile: (path: string) => Promise<string>;\n      saveFile: (content: string) => Promise<void>;\n      getVersion: () => string;\n      platform: NodeJS.Platform;\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Renderer Process\n\n```typescript\n// src/renderer/src/App.tsx\nimport { useState } from ''react'';\n\nfunction App() {\n  const [content, setContent] = useState('''');\n\n  const handleOpenFile = async () => {\n    const result = await window.electronAPI.readFile(''/path/to/file.txt'');\n    setContent(result);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"app\">\n      <h1>My Electron App</h1>\n      <p>Platform: {window.electronAPI.platform}</p>\n      <button onClick={handleOpenFile}>Open File</button>\n      <pre>{content}</pre>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default App;\n```\n\n### Creating Menus\n\n```typescript\n// src/main/menu.ts\nimport { Menu, app, shell } from ''electron'';\n\nconst template: Electron.MenuItemConstructorOptions[] = [\n  {\n    label: ''File'',\n    submenu: [\n      { label: ''New File'', accelerator: ''CmdOrCtrl+N'', click: () => {} },\n      { label: ''Open'', accelerator: ''CmdOrCtrl+O'', click: () => {} },\n      { type: ''separator'' },\n      { label: ''Quit'', role: ''quit'' },\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    label: ''Edit'',\n    submenu: [\n      { label: ''Undo'', role: ''undo'' },\n      { label: ''Redo'', role: ''redo'' },\n      { type: ''separator'' },\n      { label: ''Cut'', role: ''cut'' },\n      { label: ''Copy'', role: ''copy'' },\n      { label: ''Paste'', role: ''paste'' },\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    label: ''Help'',\n    submenu: [\n      {\n        label: ''Documentation'',\n        click: () => shell.openExternal(''https://docs.example.com''),\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n];\n\n// Add macOS app menu\nif (process.platform === ''darwin'') {\n  template.unshift({\n    label: app.getName(),\n    submenu: [\n      { role: ''about'' },\n      { type: ''separator'' },\n      { role: ''services'' },\n      { type: ''separator'' },\n      { role: ''hide'' },\n      { role: ''unhide'' },\n      { type: ''separator'' },\n      { role: ''quit'' },\n    ],\n  });\n}\n\nexport const menu = Menu.buildFromTemplate(template);\n```\n\n### System Tray\n\n```typescript\n// src/main/tray.ts\nimport { Tray, Menu, nativeImage } from ''electron'';\nimport { join } from ''path'';\n\nlet tray: Tray | null = null;\n\nexport function createTray() {\n  const icon = nativeImage.createFromPath(join(__dirname, ''../../resources/icon.png''));\n  tray = new Tray(icon.resize({ width: 16, height: 16 }));\n\n  const contextMenu = Menu.buildFromTemplate([\n    { label: ''Open'', click: () => {} },\n    { type: ''separator'' },\n    { label: ''Quit'', role: ''quit'' },\n  ]);\n\n  tray.setToolTip(''My App'');\n  tray.setContextMenu(contextMenu);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tauri Guide\n\n### Project Creation\n\n```bash\n# Prerequisite: Rust installation required\n# Install from https://rustup.rs\n\n# Create Tauri project\nnpm create tauri-app my-tauri-app\ncd my-tauri-app\n\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# Start development server\nnpm run tauri dev\n```\n\n### Folder Structure\n\n```\nmy-tauri-app/\n├── src/                    # Frontend (React, Vue, etc.)\n│   ├── App.tsx\n│   └── main.tsx\n├── src-tauri/              # Tauri backend (Rust)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── main.rs         # Main entry point\n│   │   └── lib.rs          # Command definitions\n│   ├── tauri.conf.json     # Tauri configuration\n│   └── Cargo.toml          # Rust dependencies\n├── public/\n└── package.json\n```\n\n### Command Definition (Rust)\n\n```rust\n// src-tauri/src/lib.rs\nuse tauri::command;\n\n#[command]\nfn greet(name: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"Hello, {}!\", name)\n}\n\n#[command]\nasync fn read_file(path: &str) -> Result<String, String> {\n    std::fs::read_to_string(path)\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n}\n\n#[cfg_attr(mobile, tauri::mobile_entry_point)]\npub fn run() {\n    tauri::Builder::default()\n        .invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![greet, read_file])\n        .run(tauri::generate_context!())\n        .expect(\"error while running tauri application\");\n}\n```\n\n### Calling from Frontend\n\n```typescript\n// src/App.tsx\nimport { invoke } from ''@tauri-apps/api/core'';\n\nfunction App() {\n  const [greeting, setGreeting] = useState('''');\n\n  const handleGreet = async () => {\n    const result = await invoke(''greet'', { name: ''World'' });\n    setGreeting(result as string);\n  };\n\n  const handleReadFile = async () => {\n    try {\n      const content = await invoke(''read_file'', { path: ''/path/to/file.txt'' });\n      console.log(content);\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(error);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={handleGreet}>Greet</button>\n      <p>{greeting}</p>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Web vs Desktop Differences\n\n### File System Access\n\n```typescript\n// Web: Not possible (user must select directly)\n// Desktop: Free access\n\n// Electron\nconst fs = require(''fs'');\nfs.writeFileSync(''/path/to/file.txt'', ''content'');\n\n// Tauri\nawait invoke(''write_file'', { path: ''/path/to/file.txt'', content: ''content'' });\n```\n\n### System Integration\n\n```\nThings impossible on web but possible on desktop:\n- System tray icon\n- Global shortcuts\n- Native notifications\n- Drag and drop (file path access)\n- Full clipboard control\n- Native menus\n```\n\n### Offline Support\n\n```\nWeb: Requires Service Worker, limited\nDesktop: Works offline by default\n\n⚠️ Server integration features must handle offline!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Build & Deployment\n\n### Electron Build\n\n```yaml\n# electron-builder.yml\nappId: com.example.myapp\nproductName: My App\ndirectories:\n  buildResources: resources\nfiles:\n  - ''!**/.vscode/*''\n  - ''!src/*''\n  - ''!electron.vite.config.*''\nmac:\n  artifactName: ${name}-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\n  target:\n    - dmg\n    - zip\n  icon: resources/icon.icns\nwin:\n  artifactName: ${name}-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\n  target:\n    - nsis\n  icon: resources/icon.ico\nlinux:\n  target:\n    - AppImage\n    - deb\n```\n\n```bash\n# Execute build\nnpm run build:mac\nnpm run build:win\nnpm run build:linux\n```\n\n### Auto-update\n\n```typescript\n// src/main/updater.ts\nimport { autoUpdater } from ''electron-updater'';\n\nautoUpdater.checkForUpdatesAndNotify();\n\nautoUpdater.on(''update-available'', () => {\n  // Notify update available\n});\n\nautoUpdater.on(''update-downloaded'', () => {\n  // Restart to apply update\n  autoUpdater.quitAndInstall();\n});\n```\n\n### Tauri Build\n\n```bash\n# Build for current platform\nnpm run tauri build\n\n# Output locations\n# macOS: src-tauri/target/release/bundle/dmg/\n# Windows: src-tauri/target/release/bundle/msi/\n# Linux: src-tauri/target/release/bundle/appimage/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Desktop PDCA Checklist\n\n### Phase 1: Schema\n```\n□ Decide local data storage method (SQLite, JSON file, etc.)\n□ Decide if cloud sync is needed\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Mockup\n```\n□ Consider platform-specific UI guidelines (macOS, Windows)\n□ Plan keyboard shortcuts\n□ Design menu structure\n```\n\n### Phase 6: UI\n```\n□ Support dark/light mode\n□ Handle window resizing\n□ Handle platform-specific UI differences (window control positions, etc.)\n```\n\n### Phase 7: Security\n```\n□ Don''t expose Node.js APIs directly (use contextBridge)\n□ Security handling when loading external URLs\n□ Encrypt sensitive data storage\n```\n\n### Phase 9: Deployment\n```\n□ Code signing (macOS Notarization, Windows Signing)\n□ Set up auto-update\n□ App Store submission (if needed)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Useful Libraries\n\n### Electron\n\n| Library | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| electron-store | Local settings/data storage |\n| electron-updater | Auto-update |\n| electron-log | Logging |\n| better-sqlite3 | SQLite database |\n\n### Tauri\n\n| Library | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| tauri-plugin-store | Settings storage |\n| tauri-plugin-sql | SQLite support |\n| tauri-plugin-log | Logging |\n| tauri-plugin-updater | Auto-update |\n\n---\n\n## Requesting from Claude\n\n### Project Creation\n```\n\"Set up a [app description] app project with Electron + React.\n- Use electron-vite\n- Support system tray\n- Set up auto-update\"\n```\n\n### Feature Implementation\n```\n\"Implement file open/save functionality.\n- Use native file dialogs\n- Save recent file list\n- Support drag and drop\"\n```\n\n### Build Configuration\n```\n\"Create electron-builder configuration.\n- macOS: DMG + notarization\n- Windows: NSIS installer\n- Auto-update server integration\"\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:54:56.584Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cross-Platform Agents needing simultaneous Windows, macOS, and Linux support with a single codebase using web technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.","zh":"适用于需要在Windows、macOS和Linux上同时支持的跨平台代理，使用单一代码库和Web技术，如HTML、CSS和JavaScript。","ja":"Windows、macOS、Linuxを同時にサポートするクロスプラットフォームエージェントに適しています。単一のコードベースとHTML、CSS、JavaScriptなどのWeb技術を使用します。","ko":"Windows, macOS, Linux를 동시에 지원하는 크로스 플랫폼 에이전트에 적합합니다. 단일 코드베이스와 HTML, CSS, JavaScript 등의 웹 기술을 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de plataforma cruzada que necesitan soporte simultáneo para Windows, macOS y Linux con una sola base de código utilizando tecnologías web como HTML, CSS y JavaScript.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de plateforme croisée nécessitant un support simultané pour Windows, macOS et Linux avec une seule base de code utilisant des technologies Web comme HTML, CSS et JavaScript.","de":"Perfekt für Cross-Platform-Agents, die gleichzeitige Unterstützung für Windows, macOS und Linux mit einer einzigen Codebasis benötigen, die Webtechnologien wie HTML, CSS und JavaScript verwendet.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Cross-Platform que necessitam de suporte simultâneo para Windows, macOS e Linux com uma única base de código usando tecnologias web como HTML, CSS e JavaScript.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов с поддержкой нескольких платформ, которым требуется одновременная поддержка Windows, macOS и Linux с единой базой кода, использующей веб-технологии, такие как HTML, CSS и JavaScript.","ar":"مثالي لعميل متعدد المنصات الذي يحتاج إلى دعم متزامن لنظامي Windows و macOS و Linux مع قاعدة код واحدة باستخدام تقنيات الويب مثل HTML و CSS و JavaScript."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build lightweight desktop applications with Rust security using Tauri, or leverage the mature ecosystem of Electron, supporting various use cases with a single codebase, utilizing frameworks like Tauri and Electron.","zh":"赋予代理构建轻量级桌面应用的能力，使用Rust安全性和Tauri，或利用Electron的成熟生态系统，支持各种用例，使用单一代码库和Tauri、Electron等框架。","ja":"エージェントがTauriを使用して軽量のデスクトップアプリケーションを構築したり、Electronの成熟したエコシステムを利用して、単一のコードベースを使用してさまざまなユースケースをサポートしたりすることができます。","ko":"에이전트가 러스트 보안과 타우리(Tauri)를 사용하여 가벼운 데스크톱 애플리케이션을 구축하거나 일렉트론의 성숙한 생태계를 활용하여 단일 코드베이스를 사용하여 다양한 사용 사례를 지원할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear aplicaciones de escritorio ligeras con seguridad de Rust utilizando Tauri, o aprovechar el ecosistema maduro de Electron, que admite varios casos de uso con una sola base de código, utilizando frameworks como Tauri y Electron.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications de bureau légères avec une sécurité Rust en utilisant Tauri, ou de tirer parti de l''écosystème mature d''Electron, qui prend en charge divers cas d''utilisation avec une seule base de code, en utilisant des frameworks comme Tauri et Electron.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, leichte Desktop-Anwendungen mit Rust-Sicherheit unter Verwendung von Tauri zu erstellen oder das etablierte Ökosystem von Electron zu nutzen, das verschiedene Anwendungsfälle mit einer einzigen Codebasis unterstützt, indem Frameworks wie Tauri und Electron verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações de área de trabalho leves com segurança Rust usando Tauri, ou aproveitar o ecossistema maduro do Electron, que suporta vários casos de uso com uma única base de código, utilizando frameworks como Tauri e Electron.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать легкие настольные приложения с безопасностью Rust, используя Tauri, или использовать зрелый экосистему Electron, поддерживающий различные сценарии использования с единой базой кода, используя фреймворки, такие как Tauri и Electron.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء تطبيقات سطح المكتب خفيفة الوزن مع أمان Rust باستخدام Tauri، أو الاستفادة من النظام البيئي الناضج للكترون، الذي يدعم حالات استخدام متعددة مع قاعدة код واحدة، باستخدام إطار 