system sound notifications on MacOS","Automating audio feedback for user interactions","Debugging system events with audible cues"],"zh":["在MacOS上触发系统声音通知","为用户交互自动化音频反馈","使用可听提示调试系统事件"],"ja":["MacOS上でシステムサウンド通知をトリガーする","ユーザーインタラクションのオーディオフィードバックを自動化する","オーディオキューを使用してシステムイベントをデバッグする"],"ko":["MacOS에서 시스템 사운드 알림을 트리거하는 것","사용자 상호작용을 위한 오디오 피드백 자동화","오디오 큐를 사용하여 시스템 이벤트 디버깅"],"es":["Disparar notificaciones de sonido del sistema en MacOS","Automatizar la retroalimentación de audio para interacciones de usuario","Depurar eventos del sistema con señalesizadores audibles"],"fr":["Déclencher des notifications de son système sur MacOS","Automatiser la rétroaction audio pour les interactions utilisateur","Déboguer les événements système avec des signaux audibles"],"de":["System-Sound-Benachrichtigungen auf MacOS auslösen","Automatisieren von Audio-Rückmeldungen für Benutzerinteraktionen","Systemereignisse mit hörbaren Signalen debuggen"],"pt":["Disparar notificações de som do sistema no MacOS","Automatizar feedback de áudio para interações do usuário","Depurar eventos do sistema com dicas audíveis"],"ru":["Запуск уведомлений системным звуком в MacOS","Автоматизация аудио-отклика для взаимодействия пользователя","Отладка системных событий с помощью звуковых подсказок"],"ar":["تشغيل إشعارات صوت النظام على MacOS","توفير ملاحظات صوتية تلقائية لتفاعلات المستخدم","تصحيح الأحداث النظامية باستخدام إشارات صوتية"]},"limitations":{"en":["MacOS only","Requires afplay command-line tool","Limited to system-installed sound files like /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"zh":["仅限MacOS","需要afplay命令行工具","仅限于系统安装的音频文件，如/System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"ja":["MacOSのみ","afplayコマンドラインツールが必要","システムにインストールされたサウンドファイルのみ、例：/System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"ko":["MacOS만 지원","afplay 명령줄 도구 필요","시스템에 설치된 사운드 파일만 지원, 예: /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"es":["Solo MacOS","Requiere la herramienta de línea de comandos afplay","Limitado a archivos de sonido instalados en el sistema como /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"fr":["MacOS uniquement","Nécessite l''outil de ligne de commande afplay","Limité aux fichiers sonores installés sur le système comme /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"de":["Nur MacOS","Benötigt das Kommandozeilen-Tool afplay","Begrenzt auf im System installierte Sound-Dateien wie /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"pt":["Somente MacOS","Requer a ferramenta de linha de comando afplay","Limitado a arquivos de som instalados no sistema, como /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"ru":["Только MacOS","Требуется утилита командной строки afplay","Ограничен файлами звука, установленными в системе, такими как /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"],"ar":["MacOS فقط","يتطلب أداة سطر الأوامر afplay","محدود بالملفات الصوتية المثبتة في النظام، مثل /System/Library/Sounds/Glass.aiff"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bear2u/my-skills/Prompt Coach', 'community', 'bear2u', 'my-skills', 'bear2u/my-skills', 'Prompt Coach', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:57:12.945Z', NULL, '{"id":"bear2u/my-skills/Prompt Coach","name":"Prompt Coach","description":{"zh":"Prompt Coach 是一个 AI 工程专家，帮助开发者提高 AI 工程水平，构建高效的 AI 工作流和编写有效的提示","ja":"Prompt Coach は AI エンジニアリングの専門家で、開発者が AI エンジニアリングのスキルを向上させ、効果的な AI ワークフローとプロンプトを作成できるように支援します","ko":"Prompt Coach는 AI 엔지니어링 전문가로 개발자가 AI 엔지니어링 수준을 높이고 효율적인 AI 워크플ロー와 효과적인 프롬프트를 작성할 수 있도록 도와줍니다","es":"El Prompt Coach es un experto en ingeniería de AI que ayuda a los desarrolladores a mejorar sus habilidades en la creación de flujos de trabajo de AI efectivos.","fr":"Le Coach de Prompts est un expert en ingénierie d''IA qui aide les développeurs à améliorer leurs compétences dans la création de flux de travail d''IA efficaces.","de":"Der Prompt Coach ist ein Experte für AI-Engineering, der Entwicklern hilft, ihre Fähigkeiten im Erstellen effektiver AI-Workflows zu verbessern.","pt":"O Treinador de Prompt é um especialista em engenharia de IA que ajuda a melhorar a eficiência dos fluxos de trabalho de IA","ru":"Тренер Промпта - это специалист по инженерии ИИ, который помогает улучшить эффективность потоков работы ИИ","ar":"مدرب الاستدعاء هو خبير في هندسة الإصطناع يساعد على تحسين كفاءة تدفقات العمل الإصطناعي","en":"자주 사용하는 스킬들을 모은 나의 클로드 스킬들입니다. "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Prompt Coach: AI 工程专家","ja":"Prompt Coach: AI エンジニアリングの専門家","ko":"Prompt Coach: AI 엔지니어링 전문가","es":"Entrenador de Prompts: Mejora tu ingeniería AI","fr":"Coach de Prompts : Améliorez votre ingénierie AI","de":"Prompt Coach: Verbessere deine AI-Engineering-Fähigkeiten","pt":"Treinador de Prompt: Otimização de Fluxos de Trabalho de IA","ru":"Тренер Промпта: Оптимизация Потоков Работы ИИ","ar":"مدرب الاستدعاء: تحسين تدفقات العمل الإصطناعي","en":"Prompt Coach"},"description":{"zh":"Prompt Coach 是一个 AI 工程专家，帮助开发者提高 AI 工程水平，构建高效的 AI 工作流和编写有效的提示","ja":"Prompt Coach は AI エンジニアリングの専門家で、開発者が AI エンジニアリングのスキルを向上させ、効果的な AI ワークフローとプロンプトを作成できるように支援します","ko":"Prompt Coach는 AI 엔지니어링 전문가로 개발자가 AI 엔지니어링 수준을 높이고 효율적인 AI 워크플ロー와 효과적인 프롬프트를 작성할 수 있도록 도와줍니다","es":"El Prompt Coach es un experto en ingeniería de AI que ayuda a los desarrolladores a mejorar sus habilidades en la creación de flujos de trabajo de AI efectivos.","fr":"Le Coach de Prompts est un expert en ingénierie d''IA qui aide les développeurs à améliorer leurs compétences dans la création de flux de travail d''IA efficaces.","de":"Der Prompt Coach ist ein Experte für AI-Engineering, der Entwicklern hilft, ihre Fähigkeiten im Erstellen effektiver AI-Workflows zu verbessern.","pt":"O Treinador de Prompt é um especialista em engenharia de IA que ajuda a melhorar a eficiência dos fluxos de trabalho de IA","ru":"Тренер Промпта - это специалист по инженерии ИИ, который помогает улучшить эффективность потоков работы ИИ","ar":"مدرب الاستدعاء هو خبير في هندسة الإصطناع يساعد على تحسين كفاءة تدفقات العمل الإصطناعي","en":"자주 사용하는 스킬들을 모은 나의 클로드 스킬들입니다. "},"definition":{"en":"자주 사용하는 스킬들을 모은 나의 클로드 스킬들입니다. "},"features":{"zh":["构建高效的 AI 工作流","编写有效的提示","现代开发模式与 AI 辅助编码","测量和改进 AI 工具使用效率"],"ja":["効果的な AI ワークフローの構築","効果的なプロンプトの作成","モダンな開発パターンと AI アシストされたコーディング","AI ツールの使用効率の測定と改善"],"ko":["효율적인 AI 워크플리의 구축","효과적인 프롬프트의 작성","모던 개발 패턴과 AI辅助 코딩","AI 도구 사용 효율의 측정과 개선"],"es":["Creación de flujos de trabajo de AI efectivos","Optimización de herramientas de AI","Patrones de desarrollo modernos con codificación asistida por AI","Medición y mejora de la eficiencia de las herramientas de AI","Análisis de registros de sesiones de Claude Code","Mejora de las habilidades de los desarrolladores en ingeniería de AI"],"fr":["Création de flux de travail d''IA efficaces","Optimisation des outils d''IA","Modèles de développement modernes avec codage assisté par IA","Mesure et amélioration de l''efficacité des outils d''IA","Analyse des journaux de sessions de Claude Code","Amélioration des compétences des développeurs en ingénierie d''IA"],"de":["Erstellung effektiver AI-Workflows","Optimierung von AI-Tools","Moderne Entwicklungsmuster mit AI-gestützter Codierung","Messung und Verbesserung der Effizienz von AI-Tools","Analyse von Claude-Code-Sitzungsprotokollen","Verbesserung der Fähigkeiten von Entwicklern im AI-Engineering"],"pt":["Criação de fluxos de trabalho de IA eficazes","Otimização do uso de ferramentas de IA","Melhoria da eficiência do uso de ferramentas de IA","Desenvolvimento de padrões de codificação assistida por IA","Análise de logs de sessão de Claude Code"],"ru":["Создание эффективных потоков работы ИИ","Оптимизация использования инструментов ИИ","Улучшение эффективности использования инструментов ИИ","Разработка моделей кодирования с помощью ИИ","Анализ журналов сессий Claude Code"],"ar":["إنشاء تدفقات عمل إصطناعي فعالة","تحسين استخدام أدوات الإصطناع","تحسين كفاءة استخدام أدوات الإصطناع","تطوير أنماط الترميز بمساعدة الإصطناع","تحليل سجلات جلسات Claude Code"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 工程","AI 工程专家","Prompt Coach","AI 工作流","AI 辅助编码","AI 工具使用效率"],"ja":["AI エンジニアリング","AI エンジニアリングの専門家","Prompt Coach","AI ワークフロー","AI アシストされたコーディング","AI ツールの使用効率"],"ko":["AI 엔지니어링","AI 엔지니어링 전문가","Prompt Coach","AI 워크플ロー","AI辅助 코딩","AI 도구 사용 효율"],"es":["ingeniería de AI","flujos de trabajo de AI","herramientas de AI","codificación asistida por AI","eficiencia de las herramientas de AI","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","AI para desarrolladores","entrenamiento de AI"],"fr":["ingénierie d''IA","flux de travail d''IA","outils d''IA","codage assisté par IA","efficacité des outils d''IA","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","IA pour développeurs","formation d''IA"],"de":["AI-Engineering","AI-Workflows","AI-Tools","AI-gestützte Codierung","Effizienz von AI-Tools","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Engineering","AI für Entwickler","AI-Schulung"],"pt":["engenharia de IA","fluxos de trabalho de IA","ferramentas de IA","codificação assistida por IA","análise de logs","otimização de IA","desenvolvimento de software","inteligência artificial"],"ru":["инженерия ИИ","потоки работы ИИ","инструменты ИИ","кодирование с помощью ИИ","анализ журналов","оптимизация ИИ","разработка программного обеспечения","искусственный интеллект"],"ar":["هندسة الإصطناع","تدفقات العمل الإصطناعي","أدوات الإصطناع","ترميز بمساعدة الإصطناع","تحليل السجلات","تحسين الإصطناع","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"bear2u","repo":"my-skills","repoPath":"bear2u/my-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Prompt Coach","description":"Analyze your Claude Code session logs to improve prompt quality, optimize tool usage, and become a better AI-native engineer.","version":"1.10.0","bodyPreview":"# Prompt Coach\n\nYou are an AI-native engineering expert and prompt engineering specialist. You deeply understand:\n- How to build effective AI workflows and leverage AI tools optimally\n- Best practices for crafting clear, effective prompts that minimize back-and-forth\n- Modern development patterns with AI-assisted coding\n- How to measure and improve AI tool usage efficiency\n\nYour role is to analyze Claude Code session logs to help developers become better AI-native engineers by improving their us","body":"# Prompt Coach\n\nYou are an AI-native engineering expert and prompt engineering specialist. You deeply understand:\n- How to build effective AI workflows and leverage AI tools optimally\n- Best practices for crafting clear, effective prompts that minimize back-and-forth\n- Modern development patterns with AI-assisted coding\n- How to measure and improve AI tool usage efficiency\n\nYour role is to analyze Claude Code session logs to help developers become better AI-native engineers by improving their usage patterns, prompt quality, and understanding of their coding behavior.\n\n## What This Does\n\nThis skill teaches Claude how to read and analyze your Claude Code session logs (`~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl`) to help you:\n\n- ✍️ **Improve prompt quality** - Learn if your prompts are clear and effective\n- 🛠️ **Optimize tool usage** - Discover underutilized powerful tools\n- ⚡ **Boost efficiency** - Understand how many iterations you need per task\n- 🕐 **Find peak hours** - Know when you''re most productive\n- 🔥 **Identify code hotspots** - See which files you edit most\n- 🔄 **Reduce context switching** - Measure project switching overhead\n- 🐛 **Learn from errors** - Understand common problems and recovery patterns\n\n## 🎯 How to Use This Skill\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This skill **ONLY analyzes logs from THIS machine**. It can only access Claude Code session logs that were created on this computer and are stored locally in `~/.claude/projects/`.\n\n### Quick Start: General Analysis Mode 🌟\n\n**NEW:** Get a comprehensive overview of your Claude Code usage across ALL capabilities!\n\nWhen you ask for a general analysis, Prompt Coach will provide a complete report covering:\n- 💰 Token usage and costs\n- ✍️ Prompt quality with specific examples\n- 🛠️ Tool usage patterns and MCP adoption\n- ⚡ Session efficiency metrics\n- 🕐 Productivity time patterns\n- 🔥 File modification hotspots\n- 🐛 Error patterns and recovery\n- 🔄 Context switching overhead\n\n**To get a general analysis, simply ask:**\n```\n\"Give me a general analysis of my Claude Code usage\"\n\"Analyze my overall Claude Code usage\"\n\"Show me a comprehensive report on my coding patterns\"\n\"What''s my overall Claude Code performance?\"\n```\n\nThis will generate **one comprehensive report** using all 8 analysis capabilities to give you the complete picture.\n\n### Option 1: Analyze All Projects\n\nSimply ask general questions:\n```\n\"Analyze my prompt quality\"\n\"How much have I spent on Claude Code this month?\"\n\"When am I most productive?\"\n\"What tools do I use most?\"\n```\n\nThis will analyze **all session logs** from all projects on this machine.\n\n### Option 2: List Available Projects First\n\nIf you want to see what projects have logs, ask:\n```\n\"List all projects with Claude Code logs\"\n\"Show me which projects I''ve worked on\"\n\"What projects do I have session logs for?\"\n```\n\n**Claude will:**\n1. List all project directories in `~/.claude/projects/`\n2. Show the project path for each\n3. Display number of sessions and date range\n4. Let you pick which one to analyze\n\n**Example output:**\n```\n📂 Available Projects with Logs:\n\n1. ~/code/youtube/transcript/mcp\n   Sessions: 12 | Date range: Nov 1-9, 2025 | Size: 3.5MB\n\n2. ~/code/my-app\n   Sessions: 45 | Date range: Oct 15-Nov 9, 2025 | Size: 12MB\n\n3. ~/code/experiments\n   Sessions: 8 | Date range: Nov 5-7, 2025 | Size: 1.2MB\n\nWhich project would you like to analyze?\n```\n\n### Option 3: Analyze a Specific Project\n\nIf you already know the project path, specify it directly:\n```\n\"Analyze my prompt quality for the project under ~/code/youtube/transcript/mcp\"\n\n\"Analyze my prompt quality for /Users/username/code/my-app and save it as report.md\"\n\n\"Show me token usage for the project in ~/code/experiments\"\n\n\"What tools do I use most in the ~/code/my-app project?\"\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Use the **full project path** or **relative path with ~**\n- The path should match your actual project directory\n- Claude will analyze ONLY the logs for that specific project\n\n### Saving Reports\n\nYou can request reports to be saved:\n```\n\"Analyze prompt quality for ~/code/my-project and save as docs/analysis.md\"\n\n\"Generate a full report for all projects and save to reports/monthly-review.md\"\n```\n\n### Understanding Project Paths\n\n**Your logs are organized like this:**\n```\n~/.claude/projects/\n├── -Users-username-code-my-app/          ← Project directory (escaped path)\n│   ├── session-uuid-1.jsonl               ← Session log\n│   ├── session-uuid-2.jsonl\n│   └── session-uuid-3.jsonl\n├── -Users-username-code-experiments/\n│   └── session-uuid-4.jsonl\n```\n\n**How to reference projects:**\n- Your actual project: `/Users/username/code/my-app`\n- Log directory: `~/.claude/projects/-Users-username-code-my-app/`\n- In your prompt: \"Analyze ~/code/my-app\" or \"/Users/username/code/my-app\"\n\nClaude will automatically find the corresponding log directory.\n\n### What Gets Analyzed\n\n**For each project, Claude analyzes:**\n- All `.jsonl` session files in that project''s log directory\n- User prompts and Claude''s responses\n- Tool usage patterns\n- Token consumption\n- Timestamps and session duration\n- Files modified\n\n**Time ranges:**\n- By default: Last 30 days of logs\n- You can specify: \"last week\", \"last 7 days\", \"this month\", etc.\n- Or provide specific dates: \"from Nov 1 to Nov 9\"\n\n### Limitations\n\n⚠️ **This skill can ONLY analyze:**\n- ✅ Logs stored on **THIS machine** in `~/.claude/projects/`\n- ✅ Projects you''ve worked on **using Claude Code on this computer**\n- ✅ Sessions that **still have log files** (not deleted)\n\n❌ **Cannot analyze:**\n- ❌ Logs from other machines or cloud storage\n- ❌ Projects you worked on elsewhere\n- ❌ Deleted or archived session logs\n- ❌ Sessions from other Claude interfaces (web, mobile)\n\n## Prompt Engineering Best Practices (Claude Official Guidelines)\n\nWhen analyzing prompt quality, reference these official Claude prompt engineering principles:\n\n### The Golden Rule\n**\"Show your prompt to a colleague with minimal context. If they''re confused, Claude will likely be too.\"**\n\nTreat Claude like a brilliant but very new employee who needs explicit, comprehensive instructions.\n\n### Hierarchy of Prompt Engineering Techniques (Most to Least Effective)\n\n1. **Be Clear and Direct** ⭐ Most Important\n   - Provide contextual information (purpose, audience, workflow, end goal)\n   - Be specific about expectations\n   - Use numbered or bulleted step-by-step instructions\n   - Specify output format and constraints\n   - Define what successful task completion looks like\n\n2. **Use Examples (Multishot Prompting)**\n   - Demonstrate desired output format\n   - Show variations and edge cases\n   - Provide context for the task\n   - Use high-quality, representative examples\n\n3. **Let Claude Think (Chain of Thought)**\n   - Break complex tasks into step-by-step processes\n   - Allow thinking time/space\n   - Request reasoning before conclusions\n\n4. **Use XML Tags**\n   - Structure prompts with XML for clarity\n   - Separate different types of information\n   - Make parsing and understanding easier\n\n5. **Give Claude a Role (System Prompts)**\n   - Set context with persona/expertise\n   - Define domain knowledge\n   - Establish tone and approach\n\n6. **Prefill Claude''s Response**\n   - Guide output format\n   - Set the right starting point\n\n7. **Chain Complex Prompts**\n   - Break large tasks into smaller steps\n   - Use outputs from one prompt as inputs to next\n\n### Common Prompt Problems to Identify\n\n**❌ Vague/Unclear:**\n- \"fix the bug\"\n- \"make it better\"\n- \"update the component\"\n- \"write a function\"\n\n**✅ Clear/Specific:**\n- \"fix the authentication error in src/auth/login.ts where the JWT token validation fails with 401\"\n- \"refactor the UserList component to use React.memo for better performance and reduce re-renders\"\n- \"update the Button component in src/components/Button.tsx to use the new design system colors from design-tokens.ts\"\n- \"write a TypeScript function that validates email addresses using RFC 5322 standard and returns a boolean\"\n\n### Key Indicators of Good Prompts\n\n1. **Includes Context:**\n   - File paths when referencing code\n   - Error messages when debugging\n   - Expected behavior or outcome\n   - Constraints or requirements\n\n2. **Specific Instructions:**\n   - Clear, actionable steps\n   - Defined output format\n   - Success criteria\n\n3. **Appropriate Scope:**\n   - Focused on one task\n   - Not too broad or ambiguous\n   - Realistic complexity\n\n4. **Professional Communication:**\n   - Clear language\n   - Organized structure\n   - Complete information\n\n### When Analyzing Prompts, Score Them On:\n\n1. **Clarity** (0-10): How clear and unambiguous is the request?\n2. **Specificity** (0-10): Does it include necessary information, either explicitly OR through implicit context?\n   - **Explicit**: File paths, error messages, detailed requirements\n   - **Implicit**: Git diff context, recent file edits, conversation history, project structure\n   - **Note**: \"git commit\" scores high (8-10) because Claude has git diff context\n3. **Actionability** (0-10): Can Claude take immediate action or does it need clarification?\n4. **Scope** (0-10): Is the task appropriately sized and focused?\n\n**Scoring Guide:**\n- 8-10: Excellent prompt, minimal clarification needed (includes context-rich brief prompts)\n- 5-7: Good prompt, minor clarification possible\n- 3-4: Needs improvement, missing key information\n- 0-2: Poor prompt, requires significant clarification\n\n**Context-Aware Scoring Examples:**\n- ✅ \"git commit\" = 9/10 (brief but has full git diff context)\n- ✅ \"run tests\" = 8/10 (project structure provides test command context)\n- ❌ \"fix the bug\" = 2/10 (brief AND no context - which bug? where?)\n- ✅ \"fix authentication bug in src/auth/login.ts - JWT fails with 401\" = 10/10 (explicit details)\n\n## Understanding Context in Prompt Quality\n\n**CRITICAL INSIGHT:** Brevity is NOT always a problem. The quality of a prompt depends on **both** what''s said AND what context Claude already has.\n\n### The Two Dimensions of Prompt Quality\n\n1. **Explicit Information** - What the user types\n2. **Implicit Context** - What Claude can infer from the environment\n\n**A great prompt provides enough information for Claude to act, whether explicitly or implicitly.**\n\n### Types of Context Claude Has Access To\n\n#### 1. Environmental Context\n\nContext Claude can see from the current state of the workspace:\n\n**✅ Git Context:**\n- `git diff` showing what changed\n- File modifications Claude just made\n- Previous commits in the session\n- **Example:** \"git commit\" → Claude can see all changes, will generate excellent commit message\n\n**✅ File Context:**\n- Files recently read or edited\n- Files in the current workspace\n- Code that was just discussed or modified\n- **Example:** \"edit this function\" → Claude knows which file and function from previous context\n\n**✅ Build/Test Context:**\n- Project structure (package.json, Cargo.toml, etc.)\n- Test suites and frameworks in use\n- Build configurations\n- **Example:** \"run tests\" → Claude knows the project''s test command\n\n#### 2. Conversation Context\n\nContext from the ongoing discussion:\n\n**✅ Previous Discussion:**\n- Feature just discussed or designed\n- Problem being debugged\n- Implementation approach agreed upon\n- **Example:** \"implement it\" → Follows discussion about what to implement\n\n**✅ Follow-up Requests:**\n- Building on previous work\n- Iterating on a solution\n- Refining based on feedback\n- **Example:** \"try the other approach\" → Refers to alternatives discussed\n\n#### 3. Missing Context (RED FLAG)\n\nSituations where brevity IS a problem:\n\n**❌ No Prior Discussion:**\n- First message in a session\n- Switching to a completely new topic\n- **Example:** \"fix the bug\" → Which bug? Where?\n\n**❌ Ambiguous References:**\n- Using \"it\", \"this\", \"that\" without clear referent\n- Multiple possible interpretations\n- **Example:** \"optimize it\" → Optimize what?\n\n**❌ No Environmental Clues:**\n- No files in context\n- No recent changes to reference\n- No clear scope\n- **Example:** \"update the component\" → Which one?\n\n### Recognizing Context-Rich Brief Prompts ✅\n\n**These are EXCELLENT prompts, not problems:**\n\n```\n✅ \"git commit\"\n   Context: Git diff visible, files changed\n   Why it''s good: Claude has everything needed for a great commit message\n\n✅ \"git push\"\n   Context: Just committed changes\n   Why it''s good: Clear action, obvious target\n\n✅ \"run tests\"\n   Context: Project structure visible\n   Why it''s good: Claude knows the test framework and command\n\n✅ \"build it\"\n   Context: Just finished implementing a feature\n   Why it''s good: Build process is obvious from project type\n\n✅ \"npm test\"\n   Context: Node project, package.json visible\n   Why it''s good: Standard command with clear meaning\n\n✅ \"yes\" / \"no\" / \"1\" / \"2\"\n   Context: Answering Claude''s question\n   Why it''s good: Direct response to options presented\n\n✅ \"continue\"\n   Context: Claude paused and asked for confirmation\n   Why it''s good: Clear instruction to proceed\n\n✅ \"try that\"\n   Context: Just discussed an alternative approach\n   Why it''s good: Conversation context makes \"that\" unambiguous\n```\n\n### Recognizing Context-Poor Vague Prompts ❌\n\n**These NEED more information:**\n\n```\n❌ \"fix the bug\"\n   Context: None - no error shown, no file mentioned\n   Why it''s bad: Which bug? Where? What''s broken?\n   ✅ Better: \"fix the authentication error in src/auth/login.ts where JWT validation fails with 401\"\n\n❌ \"optimize it\"\n   Context: None - no performance issue discussed\n   Why it''s bad: Optimize what? For what goal?\n   ✅ Better: \"optimize the UserList component to reduce re-renders when parent updates\"\n\n❌ \"make it better\"\n   Context: None - \"better\" is subjective\n   Why it''s bad: Better how? What''s the success criteria?\n   ✅ Better: \"refactor the function to be more readable by extracting the validation logic\"\n\n❌ \"update the component\"\n   Context: Multiple components exist, none in current scope\n   Why it''s bad: Which component? What updates?\n   ✅ Better: \"update the Button component in src/components/Button.tsx to use the new color tokens\"\n```\n\n### How to Score Context-Rich vs Context-Poor Prompts\n\nWhen analyzing prompts, consider:\n\n**High Score (8-10):** Brief + High Context\n- \"git commit\" after making changes\n- \"run tests\" in a clear project structure\n- \"yes\" answering Claude''s question\n- \"implement it\" after discussing approach\n\n**Medium Score (5-7):** Somewhat ambiguous but workable\n- \"fix the error\" when error was just shown\n- \"try again\" when previous attempt failed\n- \"update it\" when only one thing was recently discussed\n\n**Low Score (0-4):** Brief + Low Context\n- \"fix the bug\" with no prior context\n- \"optimize it\" with no performance discussion\n- \"make it better\" with no criteria defined\n- \"update the component\" with multiple candidates\n\n### Key Takeaway for Analysis\n\n**When analyzing logs, celebrate efficient communication:**\n\n- ✅ **GOOD:** User says \"git commit\" → Claude has git diff → Generates excellent message\n- ❌ **BAD:** User says \"fix the bug\" → Claude has no error context → Must ask for clarification\n\n**The goal is NOT to make every prompt long. The goal is to ensure Claude has what it needs, whether from the prompt itself or from context.**\n\n## Log File Location\n\nAll Claude Code sessions are logged at: `~/.claude/projects/`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n- Each project has a directory named with escaped path: `-Users-username-path-to-project/`\n- Each session is a `.jsonl` file named with a UUID (e.g., `10f49f43-53fd-4910-b308-32ba08f5d754.jsonl`)\n- Each line in the file is a JSON object representing one event in the conversation\n\n## Log Entry Format\n\n### User Message Entry\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user\",\n  \"message\": {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"the user''s prompt text\"\n  },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2025-10-25T13:31:07.035Z\",\n  \"uuid\": \"message-uuid\",\n  \"parentUuid\": \"parent-message-uuid\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"session-uuid\",\n  \"cwd\": \"/Users/username/code/project\",\n  \"gitBranch\": \"main\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.27\"\n}\n```\n\n### Assistant Message Entry\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"assistant\",\n  \"message\": {\n    \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"text\",\n        \"text\": \"The assistant''s response text\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"tool_use\",\n        \"id\": \"tool-uuid\",\n        \"name\": \"Read\",\n        \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/path/to/file\"}\n      }\n    ],\n    \"usage\": {\n      \"input_tokens\": 1000,\n      \"output_tokens\": 500,\n      \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 2000,\n      \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 5000\n    }\n  },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2025-10-25T13:31:15.369Z\",\n  \"uuid\": \"message-uuid\",\n  \"parentUuid\": \"parent-message-uuid\"\n}\n```\n\n### File History Snapshot Entry\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"file-history-snapshot\",\n  \"snapshot\": {\n    \"trackedFileBackups\": {},\n    \"timestamp\": \"2025-10-25T13:31:07.059Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Common Tools Used in Logs\n\n- `Read` - File reading\n- `Write` - File writing\n- `Edit` - File editing\n- `Bash` - Shell commands\n- `Grep` - Code search\n- `Glob` - File pattern matching\n- `AskUserQuestion` - Asking user for clarification\n- `TodoWrite` - Managing todo lists\n- `mcp__*` - Various MCP server tools\n\n## Analysis Tasks\n\n### 0. General Analysis Mode (COMPREHENSIVE REPORT)\n\n**When to trigger:**\n- User asks for \"general analysis\", \"overall analysis\", \"comprehensive report\", \"complete overview\"\n- User asks \"how am I doing with Claude Code?\" or \"analyze my Claude Code usage\"\n- User requests \"all metrics\", \"everything\", \"full report\"\n- When the user first activates this skill and you want to offer value\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This is the **premier feature** of Prompt Coach. When triggered, you will:\n1. Run ALL 8 analysis types (Token Usage, Prompt Quality, Tool Usage, Session Efficiency, Productivity Patterns, File Heatmap, Error Analysis, Context Switching)\n2. Generate ONE comprehensive report combining all insights\n3. Use a subagent via Task tool to handle the complexity\n\n**How to execute:**\n```\nUse the Task tool with general-purpose agent:\n- description: \"Generate comprehensive Claude Code analysis report\"\n- subagent_type: \"general-purpose\"\n- prompt: \"Analyze all Claude Code session logs in ~/.claude/projects/ from the last 30 days and generate a comprehensive report covering:\n  1. Token Usage & Cost Analysis (with deduplication)\n  2. Prompt Quality Analysis (context-aware scoring)\n  3. Tool Usage Patterns (built-in + MCP tools)\n  4. Session Efficiency Analysis\n  5. Productivity Time Patterns\n  6. File Modification Heatmap\n  7. Error & Recovery Analysis\n  8. Project Switching Analysis\n\n  Follow the analysis guidelines from the Prompt Coach skill (version 1.10.0).\n  Generate one cohesive report with executive summary and all 8 sections.\n  Save the report to [user-specified path or default to ~/claude-code-analysis-report.md]\"\n```\n\n**Report Structure:**\n\n```markdown\n# Claude Code Usage Analysis Report\nGenerated: [Date]\nAnalysis Period: Last 30 days\n\n## 📊 Executive Summary\n\n[High-level overview with key metrics:]\n- Total cost: $X.XX\n- Sessions analyzed: X\n- Average prompt quality: X.X/10\n- Top insight: [Most impactful finding]\n- Biggest opportunity: [What would improve usage most]\n\n---\n\n## 1. 💰 Token Usage & Cost Analysis\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"1. Token Usage & Cost Analysis\" section]\n- Total tokens breakdown\n- Cost breakdown with cache efficiency\n- Deduplication stats\n- Monthly projection\n\n---\n\n## 2. ✍️ Prompt Quality Analysis\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"2. Prompt Quality Analysis\" section]\n- Overall quality score\n- Context-rich brief prompts (celebrate these!)\n- Prompts needing improvement (0-4/10 with specific examples)\n- Top 3 actionable recommendations\n\n---\n\n## 3. 🛠️ Tool Usage Patterns\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"3. Tool Usage Patterns\" section]\n- Built-in tools summary\n- MCP tools detailed breakdown\n- Tool adoption insights\n- Common workflows\n\n---\n\n## 4. ⚡ Session Efficiency Analysis\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"4. Session Efficiency Analysis\" section]\n- Average iterations per task\n- Session duration patterns\n- Completion rate\n- Quick wins vs deep work\n\n---\n\n## 5. 🕐 Productivity Time Patterns\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"5. Productivity Time Patterns\" section]\n- Peak productivity hours\n- Day of week patterns\n- Efficiency by time\n- Recommendations for scheduling\n\n---\n\n## 6. 🔥 File Modification Heatmap\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"6. File Modification Heatmap\" section]\n- Most edited files\n- Hotspot directories\n- Code churn insights\n- Refactoring opportunities\n\n---\n\n## 7. 🐛 Error & Recovery Analysis\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"7. Error & Recovery Analysis\" section]\n- Common errors\n- Recovery time by error type\n- Patterns and recommendations\n- Prevention strategies\n\n---\n\n## 8. 🔄 Project Switching Analysis\n\n[Follow guidelines from \"8. Project Switching Analysis\" section]\n- Number of active projects\n- Time distribution\n- Context switching cost\n- Focus optimization tips\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Top 5 Recommendations\n\n[Synthesize the most impactful recommendations across all 8 analyses]\n\n1. **[Recommendation with biggest ROI]**\n   - Impact: [Time saved / cost reduced / quality improved]\n   - How to implement: [Specific action steps]\n\n2. **[Second most impactful]**\n   ...\n\n[Continue for top 5]\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Next Steps\n\n[3-5 concrete action items the user should take this week]\n\n1. [ ] [Specific, measurable action]\n2. [ ] [Specific, measurable action]\n3. [ ] [Specific, measurable action]\n\n---\n\n*Report generated by Prompt Coach v1.10.0*\n*Analysis based on session logs from ~/.claude/projects/*\n```\n\n### 1. Token Usage & Cost Analysis\n\n**When asked about tokens, costs, or spending:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Use Bash to list recent .jsonl files and get file sizes:\n   ```bash\n   find ~/.claude/projects -name \"*.jsonl\" -type f -mtime -30 -exec ls -lh {} \\;\n   ```\n\n2. Read a representative sample of files (5-10 recent ones)\n\n3. **CRITICAL: Deduplicate entries** to match actual billing:\n   - Track processed `message.id + requestId` combinations in a Set\n   - Skip duplicate entries (Claude Code logs streaming responses multiple times)\n   - Only count each unique API call once\n\n   **Deduplication logic:**\n   ```\n   For each line in JSONL:\n     - Extract message.id and requestId\n     - Create hash: `${message.id}:${requestId}`\n     - If hash already processed: SKIP this entry\n     - Otherwise: mark hash as processed and count tokens\n   ```\n\n4. Parse each **unique** entry and extract `usage` data:\n   - `input_tokens`\n   - `output_tokens`\n   - `cache_creation_input_tokens`\n   - `cache_read_input_tokens`\n\n5. **CRITICAL: Use model-specific pricing** - Extract model from `message.model` field:\n\n   **Claude API Pricing (Current as of Nov 2025):**\n\n   | Model | Input | Output | Cache Writes | Cache Reads |\n   |-------|-------|--------|--------------|-------------|\n   | **Opus 4.1** (`claude-opus-4-1-*`) | $15/1M | $75/1M | $18.75/1M | $1.50/1M |\n   | **Sonnet 4.5** (`claude-sonnet-4-5-*`) ≤200K | $3/1M | $15/1M | $3.75/1M | $0.30/1M |\n   | **Sonnet 4.5** (`claude-sonnet-4-5-*`) >200K | $6/1M | $22.50/1M | $7.50/1M | $0.60/1M |\n   | **Haiku 4.5** (`claude-haiku-4-5-*`) | $1/1M | $5/1M | $1.25/1M | $0.10/1M |\n   | **Haiku 3.5** (`claude-haiku-3-5-*`) | $0.80/1M | $4/1M | $1/1M | $0.08/1M |\n   | **Opus 3** (`claude-3-opus-*`) | $15/1M | $75/1M | $18.75/1M | $1.50/1M |\n\n   **NOTE:** Opus is 5x more expensive than Sonnet!\n\n   **Model Detection:**\n   ```\n   For each unique entry:\n     - Extract model from message.model field\n     - Match model name to pricing table\n     - Group tokens by model\n     - Calculate cost per model using correct rates\n   ```\n\n6. **Understand your pricing model** and tailor recommendations:\n\n   📊 **For Pay-Per-Use Users (API billing):**\n   - Cost optimization IS directly relevant\n   - Switching to Haiku for simple tasks saves money\n   - Model selection has immediate cost impact\n   - Cache optimization reduces billable tokens\n\n   📊 **For Subscription Users (Claude Pro, Team, Enterprise):**\n   - Cost optimization recommendations are LESS relevant\n   - **BUT cache optimization is STILL valuable** because:\n     - ⚡ **Faster responses** - Anthropic caches your context server-side for ~5 minutes\n     - ⚡ **Better UX** - Less waiting for context to process\n     - ⚡ **Improved efficiency** - Claude can respond faster with cached context\n     - ⚡ **Rate limit benefits** - Better cache usage may help with rate limits\n   - Focus on **session efficiency** and **prompt quality** instead of model costs\n\n   💡 **How to tell which pricing model you''re on:**\n   - If these costs matter to your budget → You''re pay-per-use\n   - If you pay a fixed monthly fee → You''re on subscription\n   - When in doubt, ask the user!\n\n7. Present breakdown:\n   - Total tokens by type (deduplicated)\n   - Cost breakdown (matches actual billing)\n   - Cache efficiency (savings from cache reads)\n   - Breakdown by model if multiple models used\n   - Monthly projection if analyzing less than a month\n   - **Deduplication stats**: Show how many duplicates were skipped\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n📊 Token Usage Analysis (Last 30 Days)\n\n💰 **Total Cost: $288.13** (matches actual Anthropic billing)\n\n## By Model:\n\n**Sonnet 4.5** (3,662 calls, 81.2%)\n- Input:        191,659 ($0.58)\n- Output:       135,505 ($2.03)\n- Cache writes: 20,010,946 ($75.04)\n- Cache reads:  240,989,306 ($72.30)\n- **Subtotal: $149.95**\n\n**Opus 4.1** (769 calls, 17.1%)\n- Input:        3,176 ($0.05)\n- Output:       30,440 ($2.28)\n- Cache writes: 2,595,837 ($48.67)\n- Cache reads:  57,156,831 ($85.74)\n- **Subtotal: $136.74** ⚠️ 5x more expensive than Sonnet!\n\n**Haiku 4.5** (77 calls, 1.7%)\n- Input:        54,265 ($0.05)\n- Output:       19,854 ($0.10)\n- Cache writes: 93,590 ($0.12)\n- Cache reads:  666,241 ($0.07)\n- **Subtotal: $0.34**\n\n📋 Deduplication Summary:\n- Total entries found: 44,036\n- Duplicate entries: 6,444 (14.6%)\n- Unique API calls: 4,508\n- Duplication factor: 9.77x\n\n⚡ Cache Efficiency: 99.9% hit rate\n💰 Cache savings: $806.79\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Recommendations\n\n**📌 For Pay-Per-Use Users:**\n\nYour Opus usage (17.1%) costs $136.74 - that''s 91% of your total spend!\n- Consider using Sonnet for complex tasks instead (5x cheaper)\n- Reserve Opus for truly difficult problems only\n- **Potential savings:** ~$80-100/month by shifting Opus → Sonnet\n\n**📌 For Subscription Users:**\n\nCache optimization is still valuable for speed:\n- Keep sessions focused on single tasks (maintains cache)\n- Avoid context switching (breaks cache, slows responses)\n- Your 99.9% cache hit rate is excellent - keep it up!\n\n**📌 For Everyone:**\n\nHaiku is underutilized (1.7% of calls):\n- Perfect for: file reads, basic edits, simple commands\n- Consider using Haiku for 20-30% of tasks\n- Much faster responses for simple operations\n```\n\n### 2. Prompt Quality Analysis\n\n**When asked about prompt quality or clarity:**\n\n**🤖 Recommended Approach: Use a Subagent**\n\nFor prompt quality analysis, **use the Task tool with general-purpose agent** to handle the complexity of context-aware analysis:\n\n```\nUse Task tool with:\n- subagent_type: \"general-purpose\"\n- Provide the project path or \"analyze all projects\"\n- Include instructions to apply v1.5.0 context-aware analysis from this skill\n```\n\n**Why use a subagent:**\n- Reading multiple .jsonl session files (could be 10-100+ sessions with hundreds of prompts)\n- Context-aware analysis is nuanced (checking if prompts respond to Claude''s questions)\n- Detecting context-rich brief prompts (git commands, follow-ups, valid responses)\n- Requires judgment for scoring (0-10) considering explicit + implicit context\n- Generating comprehensive reports with real examples and insights\n- LLM agent is much better than bash/grep scripts for subjective pattern recognition\n\n**The agent should:**\n1. Locate and read all relevant session files for the specified project/timeframe\n2. Apply the context-aware analysis logic defined below\n3. Generate a comprehensive report following the example output format\n4. Return the complete analysis for saving or presentation\n\n**Steps (for the subagent to follow):**\n1. Read recent session files (last 7-14 days)\n\n2. For each session, identify user prompts (type: \"user\")\n\n3. Check if the following assistant message contains:\n   - **AskUserQuestion tool usage** - Signal that prompt needed clarification (but ignore if user explicitly requested options/choices)\n   - **Clarifying questions in text** - Look for patterns like:\n     - \"Could you clarify\"\n     - \"Which file\"\n     - \"What do you mean\"\n     - \"Can you specify\"\n     - \"I need more information\"\n     - \"Please provide\"\n     - \"Would you like me to\"\n     - \"Should I\"\n     - \"Do you want\"\n\n4. **Detect Vague Prompt Patterns** - Look for these red flags in user prompts that trigger clarifications:\n\n   **⚠️ CRITICAL: Context-Aware Analysis**\n\n   Before flagging ANY prompt as vague, **check the conversation context**:\n\n   1. **Look at the previous assistant message** - What did Claude say just before this user prompt?\n   2. **If Claude asked a question or presented options:**\n      - \"Which option would you like? 1, 2, or 3?\"\n      - \"Should I proceed? (yes/no)\"\n      - \"Select a version: (v)ersion 1, (n)ew approach, or (s)kip\"\n      - \"Would you like me to [option A] or [option B]?\"\n   3. **Then single-word responses are PERFECT, not vague:**\n      - \"1\", \"2\", \"3\" → Answering Claude''s option question ✅\n      - \"yes\", \"no\" → Answering Claude''s yes/no question ✅\n      - \"v\", \"n\", \"s\" → Answering Claude''s selection question ✅\n      - \"continue\" → Responding to Claude''s confirmation request ✅\n\n   **ONLY flag as vague if:**\n   - It''s a standalone prompt (not answering Claude''s question)\n   - It doesn''t clearly answer what Claude asked\n   - It''s the user initiating a new request without context\n\n   ---\n\n   **✅ Context-Rich Brief Prompts (DO NOT FLAG as vague)**\n\n   Before flagging a brief standalone prompt as vague, check if it has **implicit context** from the environment:\n\n   **Git Commands** (Claude has git diff context):\n   - \"git commit\", \"git push\", \"git add\", \"git commit and push\"\n   - \"commit\", \"push\"\n   - **Why not vague:** Claude can see git diff and will generate excellent commit messages\n   - **Score these:** 8-10 (Excellent - Claude has full context from git status/diff)\n\n   **Build/Test Commands** (Claude has project structure context):\n   - \"run tests\", \"build\", \"npm test\", \"npm run build\", \"cargo build\", \"make\"\n   - \"test it\", \"build it\"\n   - **Why not vague:** Project files show test framework and build configuration\n   - **Score these:** 8-10 (Excellent - Claude knows the project structure)\n\n   **Standard Development Commands** (clear from context):\n   - \"install dependencies\", \"npm install\", \"yarn install\"\n   - \"lint\", \"format\", \"check types\"\n   - **Why not vague:** Package managers and tools are evident from project files\n   - **Score these:** 7-9 (Good - standard commands with clear meaning)\n\n   **Follow-up Prompts** (Claude just did work):\n   - \"try again\", \"revert it\", \"undo that\"\n   - \"edit this function\", \"update that\", \"fix this\"\n   - **Why not vague:** Recent file reads/edits provide context for \"it\", \"this\", \"that\"\n   - **Score these:** 7-9 (Good - conversation context makes references clear)\n   - **Check:** Look at previous assistant messages - did Claude just read/edit files?\n\n   **Continuation Prompts** (building on previous work):\n   - \"continue\", \"keep going\", \"finish it\"\n   - \"do the same for [similar item]\"\n   - **Why not vague:** Refers to work Claude was already doing\n   - **Score these:** 7-9 (Good - continuation of established task)\n\n   **IMPORTANT:** Only recognize these patterns as context-rich if:\n   1. The prompt matches common git/build/test patterns\n   2. There''s evidence of environmental context (recent tool use, file modifications)\n   3. It''s a follow-up to previous work Claude did in the session\n\n   If a brief prompt does NOT match these patterns and has no environmental/conversation context, then apply the vague prompt flags below.\n\n   ---\n\n   **🚩 Missing File Context** (standalone prompts only):\n   - \"fix the bug\" (no file mentioned, initiating request)\n   - \"update the component\" (which one? initiating request)\n   - \"change the function\" (where? initiating request)\n   - \"add error handling\" (to which file/function? initiating request)\n\n   **🚩 Vague Action Words** (standalone prompts only):\n   - \"improve\", \"optimize\", \"make better\", \"enhance\", \"clean up\"\n   - These need specific success criteria (faster by how much? reduce what?)\n   - NOT vague if answering \"What would you like me to do?\"\n\n   **🚩 Missing Error Details** (standalone prompts):\n   - \"fix the error\" (what error? where?)\n   - \"it''s not working\" (what''s the expected vs actual behavior?)\n   - \"debug this\" (what''s the symptom?)\n\n   **🚩 Ambiguous Scope** (standalone prompts):\n   - \"refactor the code\" (which code? to what pattern?)\n   - \"add tests\" (for what? unit/integration/e2e?)\n   - \"update the docs\" (which docs? with what info?)\n\n   **🚩 Missing Approach/Method** (standalone prompts):\n   - \"add authentication\" (OAuth? JWT? Sessions?)\n   - \"implement caching\" (Redis? Memory? File-based?)\n   - \"add logging\" (to console? file? service?)\n\n5. **Extract Real Examples** - Pull actual vague prompts from logs and show what Claude asked for clarification:\n   - User''s original prompt\n   - What Claude had to ask\n   - What the improved prompt should have been\n\n6. Score sample prompts using the scoring criteria:\n   - **Clarity** (0-10): How clear and unambiguous?\n   - **Specificity** (0-10): Includes file paths, error messages, context?\n   - **Actionability** (0-10): Can Claude act immediately?\n   - **Scope** (0-10): Appropriately sized and focused?\n\n7. Calculate:\n   - Total user prompts\n   - Prompts needing clarification\n   - Clarification rate (% of prompts that triggered AskUserQuestion or clarifying questions)\n   - Average prompt quality score\n   - **Most common missing elements** (file paths, error messages, success criteria, etc.)\n\n8. Categorize issues using official prompt engineering problems:\n   - **Missing context** (no file paths, no error messages) - % of clarifications\n   - **Too vague/broad** (no specific expectations) - % of clarifications\n   - **Missing success criteria** (no definition of \"done\") - % of clarifications\n   - **Ambiguous requests** (multiple valid interpretations) - % of clarifications\n   - **Missing approach** (multiple implementation methods possible) - % of clarifications\n\n9. **CRITICAL: Generate \"Areas for Improvement\" Section** - For prompts scoring 0-4/10:\n   - List EVERY prompt that scored 3-4/10 or lower\n   - For EACH low-scoring prompt, provide:\n     - The exact prompt text from logs\n     - Score (e.g., 3/10)\n     - Problem explanation (what''s missing or unclear)\n     - Context available at that moment\n     - What likely happened (Claude''s clarification)\n     - Better version of the same prompt with specifics\n     - Why the better version works\n     - Time saved estimate\n   - Calculate total impact of these improvements\n   - Identify common patterns across these low-scoring prompts\n\n   **This section is MANDATORY if ANY prompts score 0-4/10**\n\n10. Provide specific recommendations based on **Prompt Engineering Best Practices** above, with focus on:\n   - Most impactful improvements (what would reduce clarifications most)\n   - Specific templates/patterns for common tasks\n   - Real examples from their logs showing before/after\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n📝 Prompt Quality Analysis (Last 14 Days)\n\nTotal prompts: 145\nContext-aware analysis: 145 prompts categorized\nAverage prompt score: 6.8/10 (Very Good!)\n\n✅ Context-Rich Brief Prompts Identified: 23 (16%)\nExamples: \"git commit\", \"run tests\", \"build\", \"npm install\"\nThese score 8-10/10 - excellent use of environmental context!\n\n📊 Prompt Category Breakdown:\n- Excellent (8-10): 45 prompts (31%) - Context-rich OR detailed\n- Good (5-7): 71 prompts (49%) - Adequate information\n- Needs Work (0-4): 29 prompts (20%) - Brief AND low context\n\nClarifications needed: 29 (20%) - Down from typical 35%!\n\n🚩 Most Common Issues (context-poor prompts only):\n1. Missing file context: 18 prompts (when no files in scope)\n2. Missing error details: 14 prompts (when debugging without error shown)\n3. Missing success criteria: 16 prompts (vague goals like \"optimize\")\n4. Missing approach: 12 prompts (when multiple methods possible)\n\n🔴 Real Examples from Your Logs (context-poor prompts):\n\n**Example 1: Missing File Context**\n❌ Your prompt: \"fix the bug\"\n🤔 Claude asked: \"Which file has the bug? What''s the error message or symptom?\"\n✅ Better prompt: \"fix the authentication bug in src/auth/login.ts where JWT validation fails with 401 error\"\n📉 Cost: +2 minutes, +1 iteration\n\n**Example 2: Vague Action Words**\n❌ Your prompt: \"optimize the component\"\n🤔 Claude asked: \"Which component? What performance issue? What''s the target?\"\n✅ Better prompt: \"optimize UserList component in src/components/UserList.tsx by adding React.memo to reduce unnecessary re-renders when parent updates\"\n📉 Cost: +3 minutes, +1 iteration\n\n**Example 3: Missing Approach**\n❌ Your prompt: \"add caching\"\n🤔 Claude asked: \"Where should caching be added? What caching strategy? (Redis, memory, file-based?)\"\n✅ Better prompt: \"add Redis caching to the API responses in src/api/client.ts with 5-minute TTL, similar to how we cache user data\"\n📉 Cost: +4 minutes, +2 iterations\n\n**Example 4: Missing Error Details**\n❌ Your prompt: \"it''s not working\"\n🤔 Claude asked: \"What''s not working? What''s the expected behavior vs what''s happening?\"\n✅ Better prompt: \"the login form isn''t submitting - clicking the submit button does nothing, no network requests in console, expected to see POST to /api/auth/login\"\n📉 Cost: +2 minutes, +1 iteration\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Areas for Improvement (Prompts Scoring 0-4/10)\n\n**CRITICAL: If there are prompts scoring 0-4/10, list EVERY SINGLE ONE with specific examples:**\n\nWhile most of your prompts are good, here are the **X specific prompts that scored 3-4/10** and need improvement:\n\n### Prompts That Need Work\n\n**Example 1: Too Brief Without Context** (Score: 3/10)\n❌ **Your prompt:** \"test\"\n- **Problem:** No context about what to test, which tests to run, or which file\n- **Context available:** None - standalone request\n- **What happened:** Claude likely had to ask: \"Which tests? Unit tests? Integration tests? For which component?\"\n✅ **Better prompt:** \"run the unit tests for the YouTube transcript fetcher in src/index.test.ts\"\n- **Why better:** Specifies test type, component, and file path\n- **Time saved:** ~2 minutes\n\n**Example 2: Vague Action Without Specifics** (Score: 4/10)\n❌ **Your prompt:** \"update the docs\"\n- **Problem:** Doesn''t specify which documentation or what updates to make\n- **Context available:** Multiple doc files exist\n- **What happened:** Claude needed clarification on which docs and what information to add\n✅ **Better prompt:** \"update README.md to include installation instructions and usage examples for the get-transcript tool\"\n- **Why better:** Specific file, specific sections, clear requirements\n- **Time saved:** ~3 minutes\n\n[Continue for ALL prompts scoring 0-4/10...]\n\n### Impact of These Improvements\n\n**Current state:**\n- X prompts needed significant clarification\n- Average Y minutes lost per unclear prompt\n- **Total time lost: ~Z minutes**\n\n**If improved:**\n- Direct answers without clarification\n- **Potential time savings: ~Z minutes** in this project alone\n- **Annualized savings:** ~N hours/year on similar projects\n\n### Common Patterns to Avoid\n\nBased on these X examples, watch out for:\n\n1. **🚩 Standalone brief prompts without context**\n   - \"test\", \"fix\", \"update\" → Need specifics\n\n2. **🚩 Vague action verbs without details**\n   - \"improve\", \"optimize\", \"make it work\" → Need measurable outcomes\n\n3. **🚩 Missing file paths**\n   - \"update the docs\", \"add validation\" → Include file names\n\n4. **🚩 Ambiguous pronouns**\n   - \"it\", \"this\", \"that\" without clear referent → Name the specific component\n\n5. **🚩 No error context**\n   - \"fix the error\" → Include error message and location\n\n6. **🚩 No success criteria**\n   - \"improve performance\" → Define baseline and target\n\n---\n\n📊 Prompt Quality Score Breakdown:\n- Excellent (8-10): 23 prompts (16%) - Clear, specific, actionable\n- Good (5-7): 71 prompts (49%) - Minor improvements possible\n- Needs Work (3-4): 38 prompts (26%) - Missing key information\n- Poor (0-2): 13 prompts (9%) - Requires significant clarification\n\n📉 Impact Analysis:\n- 29 prompts needed clarification (down from typical 35%!)\n- Average time lost per clarification: 2.8 minutes\n- Total time lost to context-poor prompts: ~1.4 hours\n- **Potential time savings: ~45 minutes by improving remaining context-poor prompts**\n\n🌟 What You''re Doing Right (Keep It Up!):\n\n✅ **Context-Rich Brief Prompts: 23 prompts (16%)**\n   Examples from your logs:\n   - \"git commit\" → Claude used git diff to create perfect commit message\n   - \"run tests\" → Claude knew your test framework from package.json\n   - \"build\" → Clear action with obvious build process\n   - \"npm install\" → Standard command, no ambiguity\n\n   💰 Time saved: ~1.5 hours by NOT over-explaining when context is clear!\n\n✅ **Valid Responses: 6 prompts**\n   - Answered Claude''s questions concisely (\"yes\", \"1\", \"2\")\n   - Perfect communication efficiency\n\n✅ **Detailed Prompts: 42 prompts (29%)**\n   - Clear file paths, error messages, and success criteria\n   - These work great even without environmental context\n\n**Keep using this efficient approach!** You''re already saving time by trusting Claude to use available context.\n\n🎯 Your Top 3 Improvements (Maximum Impact):\n\n💡 Note: You''re already using context well with git commands and build tools!\n\n**1. Include File Paths When No Files in Scope (18 clarifications)**\n\n   When to add file paths: When you''re not already working with the file\n   When NOT needed: After reading/editing a file, or when only one file is relevant\n\n   Template: \"[action] in [file path] [details]\"\n\n   Examples:\n   - ❌ \"fix the bug\" (no file in context)\n   - ✅ \"fix the validation error in src/utils/validator.ts where email regex fails\"\n   - ✅ \"update the Button component in src/components/Button.tsx to match design system\"\n\n   💰 Impact: Would eliminate ~18 clarifications (~50 min saved)\n\n**2. Provide Error Details When Debugging (23% of clarifications)**\n\n   Template: \"fix [error message] in [file] - expected [X], getting [Y]\"\n\n   Examples:\n   - \"fix ''Cannot read property of undefined'' error in src/hooks/useAuth.ts line 42 - expected user object, getting undefined\"\n   - \"fix TypeScript error TS2322 in src/types/User.ts - type mismatch on email field\"\n\n   💰 Impact: Would eliminate ~12 clarifications (~25 min saved)\n\n**3. Define Success Criteria for Vague Actions (30% of clarifications)**\n\n   Instead of: \"optimize\", \"improve\", \"make better\", \"clean up\"\n   Use: \"[action] to achieve [specific measurable outcome]\"\n\n   Examples:\n   - \"optimize database queries in src/db/users.ts to reduce response time from 800ms to <200ms\"\n   - \"refactor UserList component to use virtual scrolling and handle 10,000+ items smoothly\"\n\n   💰 Impact: Would eliminate ~15 clarifications (~40 min saved)\n\n💡 Quick Win: Apply these templates to your next 10 prompts and watch your clarification rate drop!\n\n💪 You''re doing well! Your prompts are 65% effective. Focus on these 3 improvements and you''ll hit 85%+ effectiveness, saving ~1-2 hours per week.\n```\n\n### 3. Tool Usage Patterns\n\n**When asked about tools, workflows, or how they code:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read recent session files\n\n2. Extract all tool_use blocks from assistant messages\n\n3. Count usage by tool name\n\n4. **Group tools into categories:**\n   - **Built-in Claude Code tools**: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, TodoWrite, WebFetch, WebSearch, NotebookEdit, SlashCommand\n   - **MCP/3rd party tools**: Any tool starting with `mcp__` or custom tools\n   - Parse MCP tool names to extract server name (e.g., `mcp__playwright__navigate` → playwright server)\n\n5. Identify patterns:\n   - Total built-in tool usage (one summary line)\n   - Individual MCP tool usage (detailed breakdown)\n   - MCP server adoption (which servers are being used)\n   - Common workflows with MCP tools\n   - Tool success/failure rates\n\n6. Provide recommendations focused on MCP tool adoption and usage\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n🛠️ Tool Usage Patterns (Last 30 Days)\n\nBuilt-in Claude Code Tools:\n└─ Total: 955 uses (Read: 450, Edit: 220, Bash: 150, Write: 89, Grep: 34, Glob: 12)\n\n🌟 MCP & 3rd Party Tools:\n1. playwright (server)          ████████████████████ 287 uses\n   ├─ navigate                   98 uses\n   ├─ screenshot                 76 uses\n   ├─ click                      54 uses\n   ├─ fill                       32 uses\n   └─ evaluate                   27 uses\n\n2. browserbase (server)         ████████████         156 uses\n   ├─ stagehand_navigate         45 uses\n   ├─ stagehand_act              52 uses\n   ├─ stagehand_extract          39 uses\n   └─ screenshot                 20 uses\n\n3. youtube-transcript (server)  ████                  34 uses\n   └─ get-transcript             34 uses\n\n4. pdf-reader (server)          ██                    18 uses\n   ├─ read-pdf                   12 uses\n   └─ search-pdf                  6 uses\n\n💡 Insights:\n\n🌟 Great MCP adoption! You''re using 4 different MCP servers\n   → 495 MCP tool calls vs 955 built-in tools\n   → MCP tools account for 34% of your tool usage\n\n✅ Playwright is your most-used MCP server\n   → Heavily used for browser automation\n   → Good mix of navigation, interaction, and screenshots\n\n🚀 Browserbase + Stagehand pattern detected\n   → You''re leveraging AI-powered browser control\n   → 156 uses show strong automation workflow\n\n💡 Opportunity: Consider these MCP servers you haven''t tried:\n   → @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem for advanced file ops\n   → @modelcontextprotocol/server-sqlite for database work\n   → @modelcontextprotocol/server-github for PR/issue management\n\n📊 Common MCP workflows:\n1. playwright navigate → screenshot → click (23 times)\n   → Browser testing/automation pattern\n2. browserbase navigate → stagehand_extract (15 times)\n   → Data scraping pattern\n3. youtube-transcript get-transcript → Edit (12 times)\n   → Video content analysis workflow\n```\n\n### 4. Session Efficiency Analysis\n\n**When asked about productivity, efficiency, or iterations:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read recent session files\n\n2. For each session (group by sessionId):\n   - Count total messages\n   - Count user messages (iterations)\n   - Measure duration (first to last timestamp)\n   - Check for \"completion signals\":\n     - Bash commands with `git commit`\n     - Successful builds (`npm run build`, `cargo build`)\n     - Test runs (`npm test`, `pytest`)\n\n3. Calculate metrics:\n   - Average iterations per session\n   - Average session duration\n   - Task completion rate\n   - Time to first action (user prompt → first tool use)\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n⚡ Session Efficiency Analysis\n\nSessions analyzed: 45\n\nAverage iterations per task: 3.5\nMedian iterations: 2\nSession duration (avg): 18 minutes\n\nCompletion patterns:\n- Quick wins (<5 min): 23 sessions (51%)\n- Standard tasks (5-30 min): 15 sessions (33%)\n- Deep work (>30 min): 7 sessions (16%)\n\n💡 Insights:\n\n✅ You''re efficient! 51% of tasks complete in <5 minutes\n\n📊 Iteration breakdown:\n- 1 iteration: 12 sessions - Clear requirements\n- 2-3 iterations: 20 sessions - Normal back-and-forth\n- 4+ iterations: 13 sessions - Unclear requirements or complex tasks\n\n🎯 Tip: Sessions with 4+ iterations often started with vague prompts.\nBeing more specific upfront could save ~8 min/task.\n```\n\n### 5. Productivity Time Patterns\n\n**When asked about productive hours, when they work best:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read session files from last 30 days\n\n2. Extract all timestamps and parse them\n\n3. Group sessions by:\n   - Hour of day (0-23)\n   - Day of week (Mon-Sun)\n   - Weekend vs weekday\n\n4. For each time bucket, calculate:\n   - Number of sessions\n   - Average iterations\n   - Average session duration\n   - Efficiency score (tasks completed / iterations)\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n🕐 Productivity Time Patterns (Last 30 Days)\n\nPeak productivity hours:\n1. 14:00-17:00 ████████████ (32 sessions, 2.1 avg iterations)\n2. 09:00-12:00 ████████     (24 sessions, 2.8 avg iterations)\n3. 20:00-23:00 ████         (15 sessions, 4.2 avg iterations)\n\nMost efficient: 14:00-17:00 (afternoon)\n- 40% fewer iterations than average\n- 25% faster completion time\n- Higher task completion rate\n\nLeast efficient: 20:00-23:00 (evening)\n- 50% more iterations needed\n- More clarification requests\n- More Bash command failures\n\nDay of week patterns:\nTuesday:  ████████ Most productive\nWednesday: ███████\nThursday:  ██████\nMonday:    ████ Slower start\nFriday:    ███ Winding down\n\n💡 Recommendation: Schedule complex tasks between 2-5pm on Tue-Thu\n```\n\n### 6. File Modification Heatmap\n\n**When asked about what files they work on, code hotspots:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read recent session files\n\n2. Extract all tool_use blocks with names: Edit, Write\n\n3. Parse the file_path from each tool''s input\n\n4. Count modifications per file\n\n5. Group by directory to find hotspots\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n🔥 File Modification Heatmap (Last 30 Days)\n\nMost edited files:\n1. src/components/Button.tsx        ████████████ 47 edits\n2. src/utils/api.ts                 ████████     32 edits\n3. src/hooks/useAuth.ts             ██████       23 edits\n4. tests/components/Button.test.tsx █████        19 edits\n5. src/types/index.ts               ████         16 edits\n\nHotspot directories:\n1. src/components/  ██████████████████ 89 edits\n2. src/utils/       ████████           45 edits\n3. tests/           ██████             34 edits\n\n💡 Insights:\n\n🔥 Button.tsx is your hottest file (47 edits)\n   → Consider if this component needs refactoring\n   → High edit frequency can indicate code smell\n\n✅ Good test coverage signal:\n   → 19 edits to Button.test.tsx\n   → You''re maintaining tests alongside code\n\n📊 Component-heavy development:\n   → 62% of edits in src/components/\n   → UI-focused work this month\n```\n\n### 7. Error & Recovery Analysis\n\n**When asked about errors, problems, or troubleshooting:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read recent session files\n\n2. Look for error indicators in Bash tool results:\n   - Non-zero exit codes\n   - Common error patterns (npm ERR!, error:, failed, etc.)\n\n3. Measure recovery patterns:\n   - Time between error and fix\n   - Number of attempts\n   - Common error types\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n🐛 Error & Recovery Analysis\n\nErrors encountered: 23\n\nCommon errors:\n1. npm install failures    ████████ 8 occurrences\n   → Avg recovery time: 4.5 min\n   → Common cause: Node version mismatch\n\n2. TypeScript compile errors ██████ 6 occurrences\n   → Avg recovery time: 8 min\n   → Common cause: Type mismatches\n\n3. Test failures           ████ 4 occurrences\n   → Avg recovery time: 12 min\n\n💡 Recommendations:\n\n1. npm install issues:\n   → Add .nvmrc file to project\n   → Use `nvm use` before installing\n   → Saves ~4 min per occurrence\n\n2. TypeScript errors:\n   → Run `tsc --watch` during development\n   → Catch errors before committing\n```\n\n### 8. Project Switching Analysis\n\n**When asked about context switching, focus time:**\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Read session files from multiple project directories\n\n2. Track when `cwd` (current working directory) changes between sessions\n\n3. Calculate:\n   - Number of project switches per day\n   - Time spent per project\n   - Overhead of switching (idle time between projects)\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\n🔄 Project Switching Analysis (Last 7 Days)\n\nActive projects: 5\nTotal switches: 23\nAvg switches per day: 3.3\n\nTime distribution:\n1. ~/code/main-app        ████████████ 12 hours (55%)\n2. ~/code/side-project    ████         4 hours (18%)\n3. ~/code/dotfiles        ███          3 hours (14%)\n4. ~/code/experiments     ██           2 hours (9%)\n5. ~/code/scripts         █            1 hour (4%)\n\nContext switching cost:\n- Avg overhead per switch: 12 minutes\n- Total overhead this week: 4.6 hours\n- Estimated productivity loss: 20%\n\n💡 Recommendation:\nYou switched projects 23 times in 7 days. Consider:\n- Time-blocking: Dedicate specific days to specific projects\n- Batch similar tasks: Do all dotfile updates in one session\n- Your focus time is best on main-app (fewer interruptions)\n```\n\n## General Guidelines\n\n### When Analyzing Logs:\n\n1. **Sample Intelligently**\n   - For recent data: Read last 5-10 .jsonl files\n   - For historical: Use Bash to find files by date, sample evenly\n   - Very large files (>10MB): Read first/last N lines\n\n2. **Parse JSON Carefully**\n   - Each line is separate JSON\n   - Handle malformed lines gracefully\n   - Watch for truncated last lines\n\n3. **Respect Privacy**\n   - These are personal coding sessions\n   - Don''t repeat user''s code or prompts verbatim unless illustrative\n   - Focus on patterns, not specifics\n\n4. **Provide Actionable Insights**\n   - Always include \"💡 Tips\" or \"Recommendations\"\n   - Compare to benchmarks when possible\n   - Suggest specific improvements\n\n5. **Use Visualizations**\n   - ASCII charts for distributions\n   - Emoji indicators for priority/severity\n   - Tables for comparisons\n\n### Finding Specific Information:\n\n**To find all sessions from a specific project:**\n```bash\nls -la ~/.claude/projects/-Users-username-code-projectname/\n```\n\n**To find sessions from a date range:**\n```bash\nfind ~/.claude/projects -name \"*.jsonl\" -newermt \"2025-01-01\" -ls\n```\n\n**To quickly check total log size:**\n```bash\ndu -sh ~/.claude/projects\n```\n\n**To count total sessions:**\n```bash\nfind ~/.claude/projects -name \"*.jsonl\" | wc -l\n```\n\n## Example Queries You Can Answer\n\n### 🌟 General Analysis (Comprehensive Report - NEW!)\n- **\"Give me a general analysis of my Claude Code usage\"** ← Recommended!\n- **\"Analyze my overall Claude Code usage\"** ← Recommended!\n- \"Show me a comprehensive report on my coding patterns\"\n- \"What''s my overall Claude Code performance?\"\n- \"How am I doing with Claude Code?\"\n- \"Generate a full report on everything\"\n- \"Analyze all my metrics\"\n\n### Specific Analysis (Individual Metrics)\n- \"How much have I spent on Claude Code this month?\"\n- \"Am I writing good prompts?\"\n- \"What tools do I use most?\"\n- \"When am I most productive?\"\n- \"Which files do I edit most often?\"\n- \"How efficient are my sessions?\"\n- \"Show me my coding patterns\"\n- \"What did I work on last week?\"\n- \"How much time do I spend context switching?\"\n- \"What errors do I encounter most?\"\n\n### Project Discovery\n- \"List all projects with Claude Code logs\"\n- \"Show me which projects I''ve worked on\"\n- \"What projects do I have session logs for?\"\n- \"Which project have I spent the most time on this week?\"\n\n### Project-Specific Analysis\n- \"Analyze my prompt quality for the project under ~/code/youtube/transcript/mcp\"\n- \"Show me token usage for the project in ~/code/my-app\"\n- \"What tools do I use most in the ~/code/experiments project?\"\n- \"How efficient are my sessions for /Users/username/code/my-project?\"\n- \"Which files do I edit most in the ~/code/dotfiles project?\"\n- \"Analyze my prompt quality for ~/code/my-app and save it as reports/prompt-analysis.md\"\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- Always use existing tools (Read, Bash, Grep) - you have file access\n- Parse JSON yourself - you can do this natively\n- Show specific examples from actual logs when helpful\n- Give actionable, personalized recommendations\n- Be encouraging but honest about areas for improvement\n- Calculate costs accurately with current pricing\n- **CRITICAL (v1.8.0+):** Always deduplicate token usage entries using `message.id + requestId` hash to match actual billing. Claude Code logs streaming responses multiple times with the same IDs - only count each unique API call once.\n- **CRITICAL (v1.10.0+):** Always use model-specific pricing. Extract model from `message.model` field and apply correct rates. Opus is 5x more expensive than Sonnet!\n- **NEW (v1.10.0+):** Tailor cost optimization recommendations based on user''s pricing model (pay-per-use vs subscription). Cache optimization is valuable for BOTH but for different reasons.\n- **NEW (v1.9.0+):** When users ask for general/overall/comprehensive analysis, generate ONE complete report using ALL 8 analysis types via a subagent (see \"0. General Analysis Mode\" section)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:57:12.945Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing expert guidance on crafting effective prompts and optimizing AI workflows.","zh":"适用于Claude Code、AutoGPT和LangChain等AI代理，需要专家指导来创建有效的提示和优化AI工作流。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChainなどのAIエージェントに適しており、効果的なプロンプトを作成し、AIワークフローを最適化するための専門家の指導が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 효과적인 프롬프트를 생성하고 AI 워크플ロー 최적화를 위해 전문가의 지침이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan orientación experta para crear instrucciones efectivas y optimizar flujos de trabajo de IA.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain ayant besoin de conseils d''experts pour créer des invites efficaces et optimiser les flux de travail IA.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die Expertenratgeber benötigen, um effektive Anweisungen zu erstellen und KI-Arbeitsabläufe zu optimieren.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de orientação especializada para criar prompts eficazes e otimizar fluxos de trabalho de IA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которым требуется экспертное руководство по созданию эффективных подсказок и оптимизации рабочих процессов ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى توجيه خبير في صياغة تحفيزات فعالة وتحسين تدفقات عمل الذكاء الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to analyze session logs, improve prompt engineering, and leverage AI tools optimally, utilizing best practices for clear and effective prompts, modern development patterns with AI-assisted coding, and efficiency measurement.","zh":"赋予代理分析会话日志、改进提示工程、并利用最佳实践以最优方式使用AI工具，包括清晰有效的提示、现代开发模式中的AI辅助编码和效率测量。","ja":"エージェントにセッションログを分析し、プロンプトエンジニアリングを改善し、ベストプラクティスを使用してAIツールを最適に利用する能力を与えます。包括的な効果的なプロンプト、AIアシストコーディングを含むモダンな開発パターン、効率測定など。","ko":"에이전트에게 세션 로그를 분석하고, 프롬프트 엔지니어링을 개선하며, 최선의 방법을 사용하여 AI 도구를 최적화하는 능력을 부여합니다. 이는 명확하고 효과적인 프롬프트, AI 지원 코딩을 포함한 현대적인 개발 패턴, 효율성 측정 등을 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar registros de sesión, mejorar la ingeniería de instrucciones y aprovechar las herramientas de IA de manera óptima, utilizando las mejores prácticas para instrucciones claras y efectivas, patrones de desarrollo modernos con codificación asistida por IA y medición de eficiencia.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser les journaux de session, d''améliorer l''ingénierie d''invites et d''utiliser les outils IA de manière optimale, en utilisant les meilleures pratiques pour des invites claires et efficaces, des modèles de développement modernes avec codage assisté par IA et mesure de l''efficacité.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Sitzungsprotokolle zu analysieren, die Prompt-Engineering zu verbessern und KI-Tools optimal zu nutzen, indem es die besten Praktiken für klare und effektive Anweisungen, moderne Entwicklungsmuster mit KI-unterstütztem Coding und Effizienzmessung verwendet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar logs de sessão, melhorar a engenharia de prompts e utilizar ferramentas de IA de forma otimizada, utilizando as melhores práticas para prompts claros e eficazes, padrões de desenvolvimento modernos com codificação assistida por IA e medição de eficiência.","ru":"Позволяет агентам анализировать журналы сессий, улучшать инженерию подсказок и оптимально использовать инструменты ИИ, используя лучшие практики для четких и эффективных подсказок, современные модели разработки с помощью кодирования ИИ и измерения эффективности.","ar":"تمكن العملاء من تحليل سجلات الجلسات وتحسين هندسة التحفيزات واستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي بطرق مثلى، باستخدام أفضل الممارسات لتحفيزات واضحة وفعالة وأنماط تطوير حديثة مع برمجة مساعدة بالذكاء الاصطناعي وقياس الكفاءة."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing Claude Code session logs to enhance developer performance","Crafting clear and effective prompts that minimize back-and-forth interactions","Optimizing AI tool usage efficiency in development workflows"],"zh":["分析Claude Code会话日志以提高开发者性能","创建清晰有效的提示以最小化反复交互","优化AI工具在开发工作流中的使用效率"],"ja":["Claude Codeのセッションログを分析して開発者のパフォーマンスを向上させる","バックアンドフォースのやり取りを最小限に抑えるためにクリアで効果的なプロンプトを作成する","開発ワークフローにおけるAIツールの使用効率を最適化する"],"ko":["개발자 성능을 향상시키기 위해 Claude Code 세션 로그를 분석하는 것","반복적인 상호작용을 최소화하기 위한 명확하고 효과적인 프롬프트를 생성하는 것","개발 워크플로우에서 AI 도구의 사용 효율을 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Analizar los registros de sesión de Claude Code para mejorar el rendimiento de los desarrolladores","Crear instrucciones claras y efectivas que minimicen las interacciones de ida y vuelta","Optimizar la eficiencia del uso de herramientas de IA en flujos de trabajo de desarrollo"],"fr":["Analyser les journaux de session de Claude Code pour améliorer les performances des développeurs","Créer des invites claires et efficaces qui minimisent les interactions aller-retour","Optimiser l''efficacité de l''utilisation des outils IA dans les flux de travail de développement"],"de":["Analysieren der Sitzungsprotokolle von Claude Code, um die Leistung der Entwickler zu verbessern","Erstellen von klaren und effektiven Anweisungen, die die Interaktionen von Hin und Her minimieren","Optimieren der Effizienz der Nutzung von KI-Tools in Entwicklungsworkflows"],"pt":["Analisar logs de sessão do Claude Code para melhorar o desempenho dos desenvolvedores","Criar prompts claros e eficazes que minimizam interações de ida e volta","Otimizar a eficiência do uso de ferramentas de IA em fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Анализировать журналы сессий Claude Code для улучшения производительности разработчиков","Создавать четкие и эффективные подсказки, которые минимизируют взаимодействия туда и обратно","Оптимизировать эффективность использования инструментов ИИ в рабочих процессах разработки"],"ar":["تحليل سجلات جلسات Claude Code لتحسين أداء المطورين","إنشاء تحفيزات واضحة وفعالة التي تقلل من التفاعلات المتكررة","تحسين كفاءة استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي في تدفقات عمل التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Claude Code session logs","Focused on AI-native engineering and prompt engineering expertise"],"zh":["需要访问Claude Code会话日志","专注于AI本地工程和提示工程专长"],"ja":["Claude Codeのセッションログへのアクセスが必要","AIネイティブエンジニアリングとプロンプトエンジニアリングの専門知識に焦点を当てている"],"ko":["Claude Code 세션 로그에 대한 액세스가 필요함","AI 네이티브 엔지니어링 및 프롬프트 엔지니어링 전문 지식에 초점"],"es":["Requiere acceso a los registros de sesión de Claude Code","Se centra en la ingeniería nativa de IA y la ingeniería de instrucciones de expertos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux journaux de session de Claude Code","Se concentre sur l''ingénierie native IA et l''expertise en ingénierie d''invites"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Sitzungsprotokolle von Claude Code","Konzentriert sich auf die native KI-Engineering und die Experten-Prompt-Engineering"],"pt":["Requer acesso aos logs de sessão do Claude Code","Focado em engenharia nativa de IA e especialização em engenharia de prompts"],"ru":["Требует доступа к журналам сессий Claude Code","Фокусируется на родной инженерии ИИ и экспертизе в инженерии подсказок"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى سجلات جلسات Claude Code","مركز على الهندسة الأصلية للذكاء الاصطناعي وتخصص في هندسة التحفيزات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('stacklok/toolhive/split-pr', 'community', 'stacklok', 'toolhive', 'stacklok/toolhive', 'split-pr', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:57:39.613Z', NULL, '{"id":"stacklok/toolhive/split-pr","name":"split-pr","description":{"es":"Herramienta para dividir grandes cambios en PR más pequeños y revisables. Analiza el diff actual y propone una estrategia de división","fr":"Outil pour diviser les grands changements en PR plus petits et révisables. Analyse le diff actuel et propose une stratégie de division","de":"Werkzeug zum Aufteilen großer Änderungen in kleinere, überprüfbare PR. Analysiert den aktuellen Diff und schlägt eine Aufteilungsstrategie vor","pt":"A ferramenta split-pr ajuda os desenvolvedores a dividir grandes conjuntos de alterações em pull requests menores e revisáveis","ru":"Инструмент split-pr помогает разработчикам разбить большие наборы изменений на меньшие и просматриваемые запросы на вытягивание","ar":"تعمل أداة split-pr على مساعدة المطورين في تقسيم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب أصغر وقابلة للاستعراض","en":"ToolHive makes deploying MCP servers easy, secure and fun"},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Dividir PR grandes en cambios más pequeños","fr":"Diviser les PR volumineux en changements plus petits","de":"Große PR in kleinere Änderungen aufteilen","pt":"Divida PR em Alterações Menores com split-pr","ru":"Разделите PR на меньшие изменения с split-pr","ar":"اقسم طلبات السحب إلى تغييرات أصغر مع split-pr","en":"split-pr"},"description":{"es":"Herramienta para dividir grandes cambios en PR más pequeños y revisables. Analiza el diff actual y propone una estrategia de división","fr":"Outil pour diviser les grands changements en PR plus petits et révisables. Analyse le diff actuel et propose une stratégie de division","de":"Werkzeug zum Aufteilen großer Änderungen in kleinere, überprüfbare PR. Analysiert den aktuellen Diff und schlägt eine Aufteilungsstrategie vor","pt":"A ferramenta split-pr ajuda os desenvolvedores a dividir grandes conjuntos de alterações em pull requests menores e revisáveis","ru":"Инструмент split-pr помогает разработчикам разбить большие наборы изменений на меньшие и просматриваемые запросы на вытягивание","ar":"تعمل أداة split-pr على مساعدة المطورين في تقسيم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب أصغر وقابلة للاستعراض","en":"ToolHive makes deploying MCP servers easy, secure and fun"},"definition":{"en":"ToolHive makes deploying MCP servers easy, secure and fun"},"features":{"es":["Análisis del diff actual","Propuesta de estrategia de división","División de cambios en PR más pequeños","Revisión de cambios atomicos","Integración con ToolHive"],"fr":["Analyse du diff actuel","Proposition d''une stratégie de division","Division des changements en PR plus petits","Révision des changements atomiques","Intégration avec ToolHive"],"de":["Analyse des aktuellen Diffs","Vorschlag einer Aufteilungsstrategie","Aufteilung von Änderungen in kleinere PR","Überprüfung von atomaren Änderungen","Integration mit ToolHive"],"pt":["Divide grandes conjuntos de alterações em pull requests menores","Análise do diff atual para proposta de estratégia de divisão","Manutenção de alterações atômicas e revisáveis","Integração com o Git para entender o escopo das alterações","Lista de arquivos alterados e estatísticas detalhadas"],"ru":["Разделите большие наборы изменений на меньшие запросы на вытягивание","Анализ текущего diff для предложения стратегии разделения","Сохранение атомарных и просматриваемых изменений","Интеграция с Git для понимания объема изменений","Список измененных файлов и подробная статистика"],"ar":["اقسم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب أصغر","تحليل الفرق الحالي لاقتراح استراتيجية التقسيم","الحفاظ على التغييرات الذرية والقابلة للاستعراض","التكامل مع Git لفهم نطاق التغييرات","قائمة بالملفات المعدلة وإحصائيات مفصلة"]},"keywords":{"es":["split-pr","dividir cambios","PR más pequeños","revisión de cambios","desarrollo de software","ToolHive","git diff"],"fr":["split-pr","diviser les changements","PR plus petits","révision des changements","développement de logiciels","ToolHive","git diff"],"de":["split-pr","änderungen aufteilen","kleinere PR","überprüfung von änderungen","software-entwicklung","ToolHive","git diff"],"pt":["split-pr","divisão de pull requests","análise de diff","git","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["split-pr","разделение запросов на вытягивание","анализ diff","git","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["split-pr","تقسيم طلبات السحب","تحليل الفرق","git","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"stacklok","repo":"toolhive","repoPath":"stacklok/toolhive","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"split-pr","description":"Analyzes current changes and suggests how to split them into smaller, reviewable PRs","bodyPreview":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for cont","body":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for context\ngit log main...HEAD --oneline\n\n# Count non-generated files changed\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | grep -v ''zz_generated'' | grep -v ''^docs/'' | wc -l\n\n# Count lines changed (excluding generated code)\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat -- . '':(exclude)vendor/*'' '':(exclude)*.pb.go'' '':(exclude)zz_generated*'' '':(exclude)docs/*'' | tail -1\n```\n\n### 2. Evaluate Size and Complexity\n\nAssess whether the changes exceed recommended limits:\n\n- **Target limits per PR**:\n  - < 10 files changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - < 400 lines of code changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - Changes represent one logical unit of work\n\nIf changes exceed these limits or mix multiple concerns, proceed to split analysis.\n\n### 3. Identify Logical Groupings\n\nExamine the changed files and identify natural boundaries:\n\n- **By component/package**: Group changes by the package or component they affect\n- **By layer**: Separate model changes, business logic, API changes, CLI changes\n- **By concern**: Separate refactoring from new features, bug fixes from enhancements\n- **By dependency**: Identify which changes depend on others\n\nUse these commands to help:\n\n```bash\n# Group changed files by directory\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-2 | sort | uniq -c\n\n# Show changes by package\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep ''\\.go$'' | grep -v ''_test\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-3 | sort | uniq -c\n```\n\n### 4. Propose Split Strategy\n\nCreate a structured plan with multiple PRs:\n\nFor each proposed PR, specify:\n- **PR Name**: Brief description (e.g., \"Add base container interface\")\n- **Purpose**: What this PR accomplishes and why it''s needed\n- **Files included**: List of files that would be in this PR\n- **Estimated size**: Approximate lines changed\n- **Dependencies**: Which other proposed PRs this depends on (if any)\n- **Test coverage**: What tests are included\n- **Order**: Suggest the sequence for creating PRs (e.g., \"Create this first\")\n\n### 5. Recommend Creation Order\n\nDetermine the optimal order for creating PRs:\n\n1. **Foundation PRs first**: New interfaces, base types, shared utilities\n2. **Refactoring PRs second**: Changes that use the new foundation\n3. **Feature PRs last**: New functionality that builds on the foundation\n4. **Independent PRs anytime**: Changes that don''t depend on others\n\n### 6. Present Action Plan\n\nProvide a clear, actionable plan:\n\n```markdown\n## Proposed PR Split\n\n### Summary\nCurrently [X] files changed with [Y] lines modified. Recommend splitting into [N] PRs:\n\n### PR 1: [Name] (Create First)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file1.go\n- path/to/file2.go\n**Size**: ~100 LOC\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Tests**: Includes unit tests for new functionality\n\n### PR 2: [Name] (After PR 1)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file3.go\n**Size**: ~150 LOC\n**Dependencies**: Requires PR 1 (uses new interface)\n**Tests**: Integration tests\n\n[... continue for each PR ...]\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Would you like me to help create PR 1 first?\n2. Should I create a tracking issue for the overall work?\n3. Any changes to this split strategy?\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Splitting Principles\n\n- **Each PR should pass tests independently**: Don''t create PRs that break builds\n- **Prefer multiple small PRs over one large PR**: Easier to review and revert\n- **Keep related changes together**: Don''t artificially split code that changes together\n- **Foundation before features**: Establish abstractions before using them\n- **Use feature flags for incomplete work**: If a feature spans multiple PRs\n\n### Common Split Patterns\n\n1. **Refactoring + Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Extract interface and refactor existing code\n   - PR 2: Add new feature using the interface\n\n2. **Multi-layer Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Add data models and database changes\n   - PR 2: Add business logic layer\n   - PR 3: Add API endpoints\n   - PR 4: Add CLI commands\n\n3. **Package Restructuring**:\n   - PR 1: Create new package structure (empty or minimal)\n   - PR 2: Move code to new structure\n   - PR 3: Update imports and references\n   - PR 4: Clean up old structure\n\n4. **Kubernetes Operator Changes**:\n   - PR 1: Update CRD definitions and generate code\n   - PR 2: Update controller logic\n   - PR 3: Add validation and defaulting\n   - PR 4: Update documentation and examples\n\n### What NOT to Split\n\n- **Atomic refactorings**: Renaming that touches many files but is one logical change\n- **Generated code updates**: Proto, CRD, mock updates should stay together\n- **Dependency updates**: Keep go.mod and vendor changes in one PR\n- **Tightly coupled changes**: Changes that don''t make sense independently\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Adding New CLI Command\n\n**Current state**: 8 files changed, 450 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Add business logic to `pkg/` package (3 files, 200 lines)\n- PR 2: Add CLI command and E2E tests (5 files, 250 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Business logic is independently testable and reusable\n\n### Example 2: Refactoring + Feature\n\n**Current state**: 15 files changed, 800 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Extract common interface (2 files, 100 lines)\n- PR 2: Refactor existing implementations to use interface (6 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add new implementation with feature (7 files, 400 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR is independently valuable and testable\n\n### Example 3: Operator Enhancement\n\n**Current state**: 12 files changed, 600 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Update CRD with new fields and generate code (4 files, 150 lines, mostly generated)\n- PR 2: Update controller to handle new fields (5 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add validation webhook (3 files, 150 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR represents a complete vertical slice of functionality\n\n## User Interaction\n\nAfter presenting the split strategy:\n\n1. **Ask for feedback**: \"Does this split make sense for your workflow?\"\n2. **Offer to adjust**: Be flexible based on user''s preferences\n3. **Help with first PR**: \"Would you like me to help create PR 1?\"\n4. **Create tracking**: \"Should I create a GitHub issue to track all PRs?\"\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Be pragmatic**: The goal is reviewable PRs, not arbitrary rules\n- **Consider the team**: Some teams prefer different split strategies\n- **Document dependencies**: Make it clear which PRs block others\n- **Test independently**: Each PR should pass CI/CD checks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:57:39.613Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced Git workflow management capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级 Git 工作流管理功能的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが高度なGitワークフローマネジメント機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 Git 워크플로 관리 기능이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan capacidades de administración de flujo de trabajo de Git avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Révision de Code nécessitant des capacités de gestion de workflow Git avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die erweiterte Git-Workflow-Management-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho do Git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов код-ревью, которым требуются расширенные возможности управления рабочим процессом Git.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات إدارة تدفق عمل Git متقدمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests using Git commands like ''git diff'' and propose splitting strategies that keep changes atomic and reviewable, streamlining the development process with tools like ToolHive for MCP servers.","zh":"赋予代理将大型更改集划分为逻辑、可审查的拉取请求的能力，使用诸如 ''git diff'' 的Git命令，并提出保持更改原子性和可审查的拆分策略，从而通过ToolHive等工具简化MCP服务器的开发流程。","ja":"エージェントに、大きな変更セットを論理的かつレビュー可能なプルリクエストに分割する能力を付与し、''git diff'' などのGitコマンドを使用し、変更を原子的かつレビュー可能なままに保つ分割戦略を提案することで、ToolHiveなどのツールを使用してMCPサーバーの開発プロセスを合理化する。","ko":"에이전트가 대형 변경 사항을 논리적이고 검토 가능한 풀 요청으로 나누는 기능을 부여하여 ''git diff''와 같은 Git 명령을 사용하고 변경 사항을 원자적이고 검토 가능한 상태로 유지하는 분할 전략을 제안함으로써 ToolHive와 같은 도구를 사용하여 MCP 서버의 개발 프로세스를 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a dividir grandes conjuntos de cambios en solicitudes de extracción lógicas y revisables utilizando comandos de Git como ''git diff'' y proponer estrategias de división que mantengan los cambios atómicos y revisables, simplificando el proceso de desarrollo con herramientas como ToolHive para servidores MCP.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diviser de grands ensembles de modifications en demandes d''extraction logiques et examinables en utilisant des commandes Git comme ''git diff'' et proposer des stratégies de division qui maintiennent les modifications atomiques et examinables, rationalisant le processus de développement avec des outils comme ToolHive pour les serveurs MCP.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, große Änderungssätze in logische und überprüfbare Pull-Requests aufzuteilen, indem Git-Befehle wie ''git diff'' verwendet werden, und schlägt Aufteilungsstrategien vor, die die Änderungen atomar und überprüfbar halten, wodurch der Entwicklungsprozess mit Tools wie ToolHive für MCP-Server gestreamt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a dividir grandes conjuntos de alterações em solicitações de pull lógicas e passíveis de revisão, usando comandos Git como ''git diff'' e propor estratégias de divisão que mantenham as alterações atômicas e passíveis de revisão, racionalizando o processo de desenvolvimento com ferramentas como ToolHive para servidores MCP.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разбить большие наборы изменений на логические, проходящие ревью, запросы на включение, используя команды Git, такие как ''git diff'', и предлагать стратегии разделения, которые сохраняют изменения атомарными и проходящими ревью, оптимизируя процесс разработки с помощью инструментов, таких как ToolHive для серверов MCP.","ar":"تمكين العميل من تقسيم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب منطقية وقابلة لمراجعة باستخدام أوامر Git مثل ''git diff'' وتقديم استراتيجيات تقسيم لحفظ التغييرات الذرية وقابلة لمراجعة ، وتسهين عملية التطوير باستخدام أدوات مثل ToolHive للخادم MCP."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating large PR splitting","Generating detailed file statistics with ''git diff --stat''","Debugging commit history for contentious changes"],"zh":["自动化大型PR拆分","使用''git diff --stat''生成详细文件统计","调试提交历史以解决争议性更改"],"ja":["大きなPRの自動分割","''git diff --stat''を使用した詳細なファイル統計の生成","論争のある変更のデバッグコミット履歴"],"ko":["대형 PR 분할 자동화","''git diff --stat''를 사용한詳細한 파일 통계 생성","논란의 변경을위한 커밋 기록 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la división de grandes PR","Generación de estadísticas de archivo detalladas con ''git diff --stat''","Depuración del historial de confirmaciones para cambios controvertidos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la division de grandes PR","Génération de statistiques de fichiers détaillées avec ''git diff --stat''","Débogage de l''historique des validations pour les modifications controversées"],"de":["Automatisierung der Aufteilung großer PR","Erzeugung detaillierter Dateistatistiken mit ''git diff --stat''","Fehlerbehebung der Commit-Historie für umstrittene Änderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a divisão de PR grande","Gerar estatísticas de arquivo detalhadas com ''git diff --stat''","Depurar o histórico de commit para alterações controversas"],"ru":["Автоматизация разделения крупных PR","Генерация подробной статистики файлов с помощью ''git diff --stat''","Отладка истории коммитов для спорных изменений"],"ar":["تأتمة تقسيم PR كبير","توليد إحصائيات ملف مفصلة مع ''git diff --stat''","تصحيح الأخطاء في تاريخ الالتزام لتغييرات مثيرة للجدل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation","Limited to analyzing current diff and proposing splitting strategy"],"zh":["需要Git安装","仅限分析当前差异并提议拆分策略"],"ja":["Gitのインストールが必要","現在の差分の分析と分割戦略の提案のみ"],"ko":["Git 설치 필요","현재 차이 분석 및 분할 전략 제안 만"],"es":["Requiere instalación de Git","Limitado al análisis de la diferencia actual y propuesta de estrategia de división"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Git","Limité à l''analyse de la différence actuelle et proposition de stratégie de division"],"de":["Erfordert Git-Installation","Begrenzt auf die Analyse der aktuellen Differenz und Vorschlag einer Aufteilungsstrategie"],"pt":["Exige instalação do Git","Limitado à análise da diferença atual e proposta de estratégia de divisão"],"ru":["Требует установки Git","Ограничен анализом текущей разницы и предлагаемой стратегией разделения"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Git","محدود بتحليل الفرق الحالي وتقترح استراتيجية التقسيم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('lotosbin/claude-skills/ceo', 'community', 'lotosbin', 'claude-skills', 'lotosbin/claude-skills', 'ceo', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:57:15.786Z', NULL, '{"id":"lotosbin/claude-skills/ceo","name":"ceo","description":{"zh":"CEO 专家技能包括战略规划、商业决策、融资管理、团队建设等核心能力，帮助企业实现长期愿景和使命","ja":"CEO エキスパート スキルは、戦略計画、ビジネス上の意思決定、資金調達の管理、チームビルディングなどを含み、企業の長期的なビジョンとミッションを実現するのに役立ちます","ko":"CEO 전문가 기술은 전략 계획, 사업 결정, 자금 조달 관리, 팀 구축 등을 포함하여 기업의 장기적인 비전과 미션을 달성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El experto en dirección ejecutiva es responsable de planificar estratégicamente y tomar decisiones informadas para impulsar el crecimiento empresarial","fr":"L''expert en direction générale est responsable de la planification stratégique et de la prise de décisions éclairées pour stimuler la croissance de l''entreprise","de":"Der CEO-Experte ist verantwortlich für die strategische Planung und informierte Entscheidungsfindung, um das Unternehmenswachstum zu fördern","pt":"O especialista em CEO fornece orientação estratégica e liderança para empresas, incluindo planejamento, tomada de decisões e gestão de equipes.","ru":"Эксперт CEO предоставляет стратегическое руководство и лидерство для бизнеса, включая планирование, принятие решений и управление командами.","ar":"يوفر خبير المدير التنفيذي إرشادات استراتيجية وتوجيهًا للأعمال، بما في ذلك التخطيط وصنع القرارات وإدارة الفرق.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"CEO 专家技能","ja":"CEO エキスパート スキル","ko":"CEO 전문가 기술","es":"Experto en Dirección Ejecutiva","fr":"Expert en Direction Générale","de":"CEO-Experte","pt":"Especialista em CEO: Estratégia e Liderança Empresarial","ru":"Эксперт CEO: стратегия и лидерство в бизнесе","ar":"خبير المدير التنفيذي: استراتيجية وتوجيه أعمال","en":"ceo"},"description":{"zh":"CEO 专家技能包括战略规划、商业决策、融资管理、团队建设等核心能力，帮助企业实现长期愿景和使命","ja":"CEO エキスパート スキルは、戦略計画、ビジネス上の意思決定、資金調達の管理、チームビルディングなどを含み、企業の長期的なビジョンとミッションを実現するのに役立ちます","ko":"CEO 전문가 기술은 전략 계획, 사업 결정, 자금 조달 관리, 팀 구축 등을 포함하여 기업의 장기적인 비전과 미션을 달성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El experto en dirección ejecutiva es responsable de planificar estratégicamente y tomar decisiones informadas para impulsar el crecimiento empresarial","fr":"L''expert en direction générale est responsable de la planification stratégique et de la prise de décisions éclairées pour stimuler la croissance de l''entreprise","de":"Der CEO-Experte ist verantwortlich für die strategische Planung und informierte Entscheidungsfindung, um das Unternehmenswachstum zu fördern","pt":"O especialista em CEO fornece orientação estratégica e liderança para empresas, incluindo planejamento, tomada de decisões e gestão de equipes.","ru":"Эксперт CEO предоставляет стратегическое руководство и лидерство для бизнеса, включая планирование, принятие решений и управление командами.","ar":"يوفر خبير المدير التنفيذي إرشادات استراتيجية وتوجيهًا للأعمال، بما في ذلك التخطيط وصنع القرارات وإدارة الفرق.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["战略规划","商业决策","融资管理","团队建设","核心团队管理","组织架构设计"],"ja":["戦略計画","ビジネス上の意思決定","資金調達の管理","チームビルディング","コアチームの管理","組織構造の設計"],"ko":["전략 계획","사업 결정","자금 조달 관리","팀 구축","코어 팀 관리","조직 구조 설계"],"es":["Planificación estratégica","Toma de decisiones informadas","Gestión de riesgos","Desarrollo de equipos","Planificación financiera","Análisis de competidores"],"fr":["Planification stratégique","Prise de décisions éclairées","Gestion des risques","Développement d''équipes","Planification financière","Analyse de la concurrence"],"de":["Strategische Planung","Informierte Entscheidungsfindung","Risikomanagement","Teamdevelopment","Finanzplanung","Wettbewerbsanalyse"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de estratégias de negócios","Planejamento e tomada de decisões","Gestão de equipes e liderança","Análise de mercado e concorrência","Gestão de recursos e finanças"],"ru":["Разработка бизнес-стратегий","Планирование и принятие решений","Управление командами и лидерство","Анализ рынка и конкурентов","Управление ресурсами и финансами"],"ar":["تطوير استراتيجيات الأعمال","التخطيط وصنع القرارات","إدارة الفرق والقيادة","تحليل السوق والمنافسة","إدارة الموارد والمالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CEO 专家技能","战略规划","商业决策","融资管理","团队建设","核心团队管理","组织架构设计","企业管理"],"ja":["CEO エキスパート スキル","戦略計画","ビジネス上の意思決定","資金調達の管理","チームビルディング","コアチームの管理","組織構造の設計","企業管理"],"ko":["CEO 전문가 기술","전략 계획","사업 결정","자금 조달 관리","팀 구축","코어 팀 관리","조직 구조 설계","기업 관리"],"es":["dirección ejecutiva","planificación estratégica","toma de decisiones","gestión de riesgos","desarrollo de equipos","planificación financiera","análisis de competidores","liderazgo empresarial"],"fr":["direction générale","planification stratégique","prise de décisions","gestion des risques","développement d''équipes","planification financière","analyse de la concurrence","leadership d''entreprise"],"de":["CEO","strategische Planung","informierte Entscheidungsfindung","Risikomanagement","Teamdevelopment","Finanzplanung","Wettbewerbsanalyse","Unternehmensführung"],"pt":["especialista em CEO","estratégia de negócios","liderança empresarial","planejamento estratégico","tomada de decisões","gestão de equipes","análise de mercado","gestão de recursos"],"ru":["эксперт CEO","бизнес-стратегия","лидерство в бизнесе","стратегическое планирование","принятие решений","управление командами","анализ рынка","управление ресурсами"],"ar":["مختص المدير التنفيذي","استراتيجية الأعمال","توجيه الأعمال","التخطيط الاستراتيجي","صنع القرارات","إدارة الفرق","تحليل السوق","إدارة الموارد"]}},"owner":"lotosbin","repo":"claude-skills","repoPath":"lotosbin/claude-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ceo","description":"首席执行官专家，精通战略规划、商业决策、融资管理和团队建设","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# 首席执行官专家\n\n## 触发条件\n当用户提到以下内容时自动触发：\n- \"CEO\"\n- \"首席执行官\"\n- \"公司战略\"\n- \"商业决策\"\n- \"融资\"\n- \"商业模式\"\n- \"团队管理\"\n- \"董事会\"\n\n## 核心能力\n\n### 战略规划\n- **愿景制定**: 定义公司长期愿景和使命\n- **战略规划**: 制定公司 3-5 年战略规划\n- **竞争战略**: 分析竞争格局制定竞争策略\n- **业务布局**: 规划业务组合和扩张路径\n\n### 商业决策\n- **投资决策**: 评估投资机会和风险回报\n- **资源配置**: 优化人力、财力、资源配置\n- **风险管理**: 识别和管控公司经营风险\n- **重大决策**: 参与关键业务决策评审\n\n### 融资管理\n- **融资规划**: 制定融资策略和时间表\n- **投资人关系**: 维护投资人关系和沟通\n- **估值分析**: 进行公司估值和交易谈判\n- **上市规划**: 规划上市路径和准备工作\n\n### 团队建设\n- **核心团队**: 招聘和管理核心管理团队\n- **组织架构**: 设计组织架构和汇报关系\n- **企业文化","body":"# 首席执行官专家\n\n## 触发条件\n当用户提到以下内容时自动触发：\n- \"CEO\"\n- \"首席执行官\"\n- \"公司战略\"\n- \"商业决策\"\n- \"融资\"\n- \"商业模式\"\n- \"团队管理\"\n- \"董事会\"\n\n## 核心能力\n\n### 战略规划\n- **愿景制定**: 定义公司长期愿景和使命\n- **战略规划**: 制定公司 3-5 年战略规划\n- **竞争战略**: 分析竞争格局制定竞争策略\n- **业务布局**: 规划业务组合和扩张路径\n\n### 商业决策\n- **投资决策**: 评估投资机会和风险回报\n- **资源配置**: 优化人力、财力、资源配置\n- **风险管理**: 识别和管控公司经营风险\n- **重大决策**: 参与关键业务决策评审\n\n### 融资管理\n- **融资规划**: 制定融资策略和时间表\n- **投资人关系**: 维护投资人关系和沟通\n- **估值分析**: 进行公司估值和交易谈判\n- **上市规划**: 规划上市路径和准备工作\n\n### 团队建设\n- **核心团队**: 招聘和管理核心管理团队\n- **组织架构**: 设计组织架构和汇报关系\n- **企业文化**: 塑造和传播企业文化\n- **人才激励**: 设计激励机制和股权激励\n\n## 工作流程\n\n### 1. 战略规划周期\n- 年度战略规划会议\n- 战略执行跟踪和复盘\n- 根据市场变化调整战略\n- 战略目标分解到部门\n\n### 2. 日常管理\n- 参加重要会议和决策\n- 接见重要客户和投资人\n- 审批重大事项\n- 关注公司运营指标\n\n### 3. 对外事务\n- 媒体采访和公开演讲\n- 行业会议和演讲\n- 政府关系维护\n- 合作伙伴关系\n\n### 4. 资本运作\n- 融资路演和谈判\n- 并购交易评估\n- 投资者关系管理\n- 资本市场沟通\n\n## 常见解决方案\n\n### 商业模式画布\n```\n1. 客户细分\n   - 目标用户群体\n   - 用户需求和痛点\n\n2. 价值主张\n   - 核心价值主张\n   - 差异化竞争优势\n\n3. 渠道通路\n   - 销售渠道\n   - 交付渠道\n\n4. 客户关系\n   - 客户获取方式\n   - 客户维护策略\n\n5. 收入来源\n   - 收入模式\n   - 定价策略\n\n6. 核心资源\n   - 关键资产\n   - 重要合作伙伴\n\n7. 关键活动\n   - 核心业务活动\n   - 重要业务环节\n\n8. 成本结构\n   - 主要成本构成\n   - 成本优化方向\n```\n\n### 融资阶段规划\n```\n种子轮/天使轮:\n- 融资金额: 50-500 万\n- 估值范围: 500-3000 万\n- 主要用途: 产品研发、团队组建\n- 投资人: 天使投资人、早期 VC\n\nPre-A/A 轮:\n- 融资金额: 500-3000 万\n- 估值范围: 3000 万-2 亿\n- 主要用途: 产品完善、市场推广\n- 投资人: 早期 VC、产业资本\n\nB 轮:\n- 融资金额: 5000 万-2 亿\n- 估值范围: 2-10 亿\n- 主要用途: 规模化扩张\n- 投资人: 成长期 VC\n\nC 轮及以后:\n- 融资金额: 1 亿+\n- 估值范围: 10 亿+\n- 主要用途: 市场领先、上市准备\n- 投资人: 大型 VC、PE\n```\n\n### 公司治理结构\n```\n董事会:\n- 创始人/CEO\n- 联合创始人\n- 投资人董事\n- 独立董事\n\n管理层:\n- CEO (首席执行官)\n- COO (首席运营官)\n- CFO (首席财务官)\n- CTO (首席技术官)\n- CMO (首席营销官)\n\n监事会/顾问:\n- 监事会主席\n- 法律顾问\n- 财务顾问\n- 战略顾问\n```\n\n### 战略分析框架\n\n**SWOT 分析**:\n- Strengths (优势): 核心竞争力、资源优势\n- Weaknesses (劣势): 短板、劣势\n- Opportunities (机会): 市场机会、增长空间\n- Threats (威胁): 竞争威胁、风险因素\n\n**波特五力模型**:\n- 供应商议价能力\n- 客户议价能力\n- 新进入者威胁\n- 替代品威胁\n- 现有竞争者竞争强度\n\n**BCG 矩阵**:\n- Stars (明星产品): 高增长、高份额\n- Cash Cows (现金牛): 低增长、高份额\n- Question Marks (问题产品): 高增长、低份额\n- Dogs (瘦狗产品): 低增长、低份额\n\n### KPI 指标体系\n\n**财务指标**:\n- 营收增长率\n- 毛利率\n- 净利率\n- 现金流\n- ROI/ROE\n\n**运营指标**:\n- 用户增长\n- 留存率\n- 转化率\n- 客户满意度\n- NPS\n\n**人才指标**:\n- 核心人才留存\n- 员工满意度\n- 人效产出\n- 招聘完成率\n- 培训覆盖率\n\n## CEO 决策清单\n\n### 融资决策\n- [ ] 公司估值是否合理\n- [ ] 投资条款是否可接受\n- [ ] 投资人背景和资源\n- [ ] 对公司控制权的影响\n- [ ] 资金使用计划\n- [ ] 后续融资影响\n\n### 并购决策\n- [ ] 战略协同性\n- [ ] 估值是否合理\n- [ ] 整合难度和风险\n- [ ] 团队稳定性\n- [ ] 反垄断和法律风险\n- [ ] 股东和董事会支持\n\n### 重大投资决策\n- [ ] 投资回报率分析\n- [ ] 风险评估\n- [ ] 资金来源和影响\n- [ ] 团队执行能力\n- [ ] 市场时机\n- [ ] 退出机制\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:57:15.786Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Business Strategy Agents needing advanced CEO decision-making capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级CEO决策能力的商业战略代理","ja":"ビジネス戦略エージェントが高度なCEOの意思決定機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"고급 CEO 의사 결정 기능이 필요한 비즈니스 전략 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Estrategia Empresarial que necesitan capacidades de toma de decisiones avanzadas de CEO.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de stratégie d''entreprise ayant besoin de capacités de prise de décision avancées de PDG.","de":"Perfekt für Geschäftsstrategie-Agenten, die erweiterte CEO-Entscheidungskapazitäten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Estratégia de Negócios que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de tomada de decisão de CEO.","ru":"Идеально для бизнес-стратегических агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности принятия решений генерального директора.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الاستراتيجيين التجاريين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لاتخاذ قرارات الرئيس التنفيذي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop strategic plans, make informed investment decisions, and optimize resource allocation using techniques like 竞争战略 and 业务布局, while maintaining effective 团队管理 and 投资人关系.","zh":"使代理能够开发战略计划，做出明智的投资决策，并使用竞争战略和业务布局等技术优化资源分配，同时保持有效的团队管理和投资人关系","ja":"エージェントが戦略計画を開発し、情報に基づいた投資決定を行い、競争戦略や事業展開などの手法を使用してリソース配分を最適化し、同時に効果的なチームマネジメントと投資家関係を維持することができる","ko":"에이전트가 전략 계획을 개발하고 정보에 기반한 투자 quyết정을 하며 경쟁 전략과 사업 배치 等의 기법을 사용하여 자원 배분을 최적화同时 효과적인 팀 관리와 투자자 관계를 유지할 수 있게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar planes estratégicos, tomar decisiones de inversión informadas y optimizar la asignación de recursos utilizando técnicas como estrategia de competencia y diseño empresarial, manteniendo al mismo tiempo una gestión de equipo efectiva y relaciones con inversores.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''élaborer des plans stratégiques, de prendre des décisions d''investissement éclairées et d''optimiser l''allocation des ressources en utilisant des techniques comme la stratégie de concurrence et la conception d''entreprise, tout en maintenant une gestion d''équipe efficace et des relations avec les investisseurs.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, strategische Pläne zu entwickeln, informierte Investitionsentscheidungen zu treffen und die Ressourcenzuweisung mithilfe von Techniken wie Wettbewerbsstrategie und Unternehmensdesign zu optimieren, während sie gleichzeitig eine effektive Teamverwaltung und Investorenbeziehungen aufrechterhalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver planos estratégicos, tomar decisões de investimento informadas e otimizar a alocação de recursos utilizando técnicas como estratégia competitiva e layout de negócios, mantendo uma gestão de equipe eficaz e relações com investidores.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разрабатывать стратегические планы, принимать обоснованные инвестиционные решения и оптимизировать распределение ресурсов с помощью таких техник, как конкурентная стратегия и бизнес-расположение, при этом поддерживая эффективное управление командой и отношения с инвесторами.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تطوير خطط استراتيجية، واتخاذ قرارات استثمارية مدروسة، وتحسين تخصيص الموارد باستخدام تقنيات مثل استراتيجية التنافس وترتيب الأعمال، مع الحفاظ على إدارة فريق فعالة وعلاقات مع المستثمرين."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating 商业决策 processes","Generating 融资规划 strategies","Optimizing 团队建设 and 组织架构"],"zh":["自动化商业决策流程","生成融资规划战略","优化团队建设和组织架构"],"ja":["ビジネス意思決定プロセスの自動化","資金調達計画戦略の生成","チームビルディングと組織構造の最適化"],"ko":["사업 결정 프로세스의 자동화","자금 조달 계획 전략의 생성","팀 구축과 조직 구조의 최적화"],"es":["Automatizar procesos de toma de decisiones empresariales","Generar estrategias de planificación de financiación","Optimizar la construcción de equipos y la estructura organizativa"],"fr":["Automatiser les processus de prise de décision commerciale","Générer des stratégies de planification de financement","Optimiser la construction d''équipes et la structure organisationnelle"],"de":["Automatisierung von Geschäftsentscheidungsprozessen","Generierung von Finanzierungsplanungsstrategien","Optimierung von Teamaufbau und Organisationsstruktur"],"pt":["Automatizar processos de tomada de decisão comercial","Gerar estratégias de planejamento de financiamento","Otimizar a construção da equipe e a estrutura organizacional"],"ru":["Автоматизировать бизнес-процессы принятия решений","Генерировать стратегии финансового планирования","Оптимизировать построение команды и организационную структуру"],"ar":["تأتمة عمليات اتخاذ القرارات التجارية","генерировать استراتيجيات التخطيط المالي","تحسين بناء الفريق وهيكل المنظمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of 公司战略 and 商业模式","Limited to CEO-related decision-making"],"zh":["需要了解公司战略和商业模式","仅限CEO相关决策"],"ja":["企業戦略とビジネスモデルに関する知識が必要","CEO関連の意思決定に限定"],"ko":["기업 전략과 비즈니스 모델에 대한 지식이 필요","CEO 관련 결정에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de estrategia empresarial y modelo de negocio","Limitado a la toma de decisiones relacionadas con el CEO"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en stratégie d''entreprise et en modèle économique","Limité à la prise de décision liée au PDG"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Unternehmensstrategie und Geschäftsmodell","Begrenzt auf CEO-bezogene Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de estratégia de empresa e modelo de negócios","Limitado à tomada de decisão relacionada ao CEO"],"ru":["Требует знания бизнес-стратегии и бизнес-модели","Ограничен решением генерального директора"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة استراتيجية الشركة ونموذج الأعمال","محدود لاتخاذ القرارات المتعلقة بالرئيس التنفيذي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('BauplanLabs/case-study-intella/wap-ingestion', 'community', 'BauplanLabs', 'case-study-intella', 'BauplanLabs/case-study-intella', 'wap-ingestion', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:57:05.884Z', NULL, '{"id":"BauplanLabs/case-study-intella/wap-ingestion","name":"wap-ingestion","description":{"zh":"WAP 工作流程是一种通过 Python 脚本和 Bauplan SDK 实现 telemetry 分析的方法，包括写入、审核和发布三个步骤","ja":"WAP ワークフローは、Python スクリプトと Bauplan SDK を使用してテレメトリ分析を実現する方法です","ko":"WAP 작업 흐름은 Python 脚本과 Bauplan SDK를 사용하여 텔레메트리 분석을 구현하는 방법으로, 쓰기, 감사, 발행의 세 단계로 구성됩니다","es":"El patrón WAP permite la ingesta, auditoría y publicación de datos de telemetría de manera segura y eficiente","fr":"Le modèle WAP permet l''ingestion, l''audit et la publication de données de télémétrie de manière sécurisée et efficace","de":"Das WAP-Muster ermöglicht die Aufnahme, Überprüfung und Veröffentlichung von Telemetriedaten auf sichere und effiziente Weise","pt":"O padrão WAP permite a ingestão de dados de telemetria de forma segura e eficiente. Implemente um script Python com o SDK Bauplan para análise de telemetria.","ru":"Шаблон WAP позволяет инжестить данные телеметрии безопасно и эффективно. Реализуйте скрипт Python с SDK Bauplan для анализа телеметрии.","ar":"نمط WAP يسمح بإدخال بيانات التелеметria بشكل آمنและมؤثر. أنشئ نص برمجي بايثون باستخدام SDK Bauplan لتحليل التелеметria.","en":"A case study with Intella using WAP workflow on Bauplan for telemetry analysis"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"WAP 工作流程 - telemetry 分析中的 Write-Audit-Publish 模式","ja":"WAP ワークフロー - テレメトリ分析における Write-Audit-Publish パターン","ko":"WAP 작업 흐름 - 텔레메트리 분석을 위한 Write-Audit-Publish 패턴","es":"Implementación de WAP para Análisis de Telemetría","fr":"Mise en œuvre de WAP pour l''analyse de télémétrie","de":"WAP-Implementierung für Telemetrie-Analyse","pt":"WAP Ingestion: Implementação de Telemetria com Bauplan","ru":"WAP Инжестия: Реализация Телеметрии с Bauplan","ar":"استيعاب WAP: تنفيذ تحليل التелеметria باستخدام Bauplan","en":"wap-ingestion"},"description":{"zh":"WAP 工作流程是一种通过 Python 脚本和 Bauplan SDK 实现 telemetry 分析的方法，包括写入、审核和发布三个步骤","ja":"WAP ワークフローは、Python スクリプトと Bauplan SDK を使用してテレメトリ分析を実現する方法です","ko":"WAP 작업 흐름은 Python 脚本과 Bauplan SDK를 사용하여 텔레메트리 분석을 구현하는 방법으로, 쓰기, 감사, 발행의 세 단계로 구성됩니다","es":"El patrón WAP permite la ingesta, auditoría y publicación de datos de telemetría de manera segura y eficiente","fr":"Le modèle WAP permet l''ingestion, l''audit et la publication de données de télémétrie de manière sécurisée et efficace","de":"Das WAP-Muster ermöglicht die Aufnahme, Überprüfung und Veröffentlichung von Telemetriedaten auf sichere und effiziente Weise","pt":"O padrão WAP permite a ingestão de dados de telemetria de forma segura e eficiente. Implemente um script Python com o SDK Bauplan para análise de telemetria.","ru":"Шаблон WAP позволяет инжестить данные телеметрии безопасно и эффективно. Реализуйте скрипт Python с SDK Bauplan для анализа телеметрии.","ar":"نمط WAP يسمح بإدخال بيانات التелеметria بشكل آمنและมؤثر. أنشئ نص برمجي بايثون باستخدام SDK Bauplan لتحليل التелеметria.","en":"A case study with Intella using WAP workflow on Bauplan for telemetry analysis"},"definition":{"en":"A case study with Intella using WAP workflow on Bauplan for telemetry analysis"},"features":{"zh":["写入临时分支","审核质量检查","发布到主分支","原子性多表操作","分支安全"],"ja":["一時ブランチへの書き込み","品質チェックの監査","メインブランチへの公開","原子性マルチテーブル操作","ブランチセーフティ"],"ko":["임시 분기への 쓰기","품질 검사 감사","메인 분기への 발행","원자성 멀티 테이블 작동","분기 안전"],"es":["Ingesta de datos en una rama temporal","Auditoría de calidad de los datos","Publicación de datos en la rama principal","Operaciones atómicas multi-tabla","Seguridad de rama para evitar modificaciones no deseadas"],"fr":["Ingestion de données dans une branche temporaire","Audit de la qualité des données","Publication de données dans la branche principale","Opérations atomiques multi-table","Sécurité de branche pour éviter les modifications non désirées"],"de":["Datenaufnahme in einem temporären Branch","Qualitätsüberprüfung der Daten","Veröffentlichung von Daten im Hauptbranch","Atomare Multi-Tabelle-Operationen","Branch-Sicherheit zur Vermeidung unerwünschter Änderungen"],"pt":["Ingestão de dados de telemetria com Bauplan","Implementação do padrão WAP com script Python","Operações atômicas multi-tabela","Segurança de branch com operações temporárias","Inspeção de branches após sucesso ou falha"],"ru":["Инжестия данных телеметрии с Bauplan","Реализация шаблона WAP с помощью скрипта Python","Атомарные операции с несколькими таблицами","Безопасность ветки с временными операциями","Проверка веток после успеха или неудачи"],"ar":["إدخال بيانات التелеметria مع Bauplan","تنفيذ نمط WAP باستخدام نص برمجي بايثون","عمليات ذرية متعددة الجداول","أمان الفرع مع عمليات مؤقتة","فحص الفروع بعد النجاح أو الفشل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["WAP 工作流程","telemetry 分析","Python 脚本","Bauplan SDK","写入临时分支","审核质量检查"],"ja":["WAP ワークフロー","テレメトリ分析","Python スクリプト","Bauplan SDK","一時ブランチへの書き込み","品質チェックの監査"],"ko":["WAP 작업 흐름","텔레메트리 분석","Python 脚本","Bauplan SDK","임시 분기への 쓰기","품질 검사 감사"],"es":["WAP","patrón de ingesta de datos","análisis de telemetría","Python","Bauplan","ingesta de datos","auditoría de calidad","publicación de datos","seguridad de rama"],"fr":["WAP","modèle d''ingestion de données","analyse de télémétrie","Python","Bauplan","ingestion de données","audit de qualité","publication de données","sécurité de branche"],"de":["WAP","Datenaufnahmemuster","Telemetrie-Analyse","Python","Bauplan","Datenaufnahme","Qualitätsüberprüfung","Datenveröffentlichung","Branch-Sicherheit"],"pt":["WAP Ingestion","Telemetria","Bauplan","Padrão WAP","Ingestão de dados","Script Python","Operações atômicas","Segurança de branch"],"ru":["WAP Инжестия","Телеметрия","Bauplan","Шаблон WAP","Инжестия данных","Скрипт Python","Атомарные операции","Безопасность ветки"],"ar":["استيعاب WAP","التелеметria","Bauplan","نمط WAP","إدخال البيانات","نص برمجي بايثون","عمليات ذرية","أمان الفرع"]}},"owner":"BauplanLabs","repo":"case-study-intella","repoPath":"BauplanLabs/case-study-intella","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"wap-ingestion","description":"Ingest data from S3 into bauplan using the Write-Audit-Publish pattern for safe data loading. Use when loading new data from S3, performing safe data ingestion, or when the user mentions WAP, data ingestion, importing parquet/csv/jsonl files, or needs to safely load data with quality checks.","bodyPreview":"# Write-Audit-Publish (WAP) Pattern\n\nImplement WAP by writing a Python script using the `bauplan` SDK. Do NOT use CLI commands.\n\n**The three steps**: Write (ingest to temp branch) → Audit (quality checks) → Publish (merge to main)\n\n**Branch safety**: All operations happen on a temporary branch, NEVER on `main`. By default, branches are kept open for inspection after success or failure.\n\n**Atomic multi-table operations**: `merge_branch` is atomic. You can create or modify multiple tables on a bra","body":"# Write-Audit-Publish (WAP) Pattern\n\nImplement WAP by writing a Python script using the `bauplan` SDK. Do NOT use CLI commands.\n\n**The three steps**: Write (ingest to temp branch) → Audit (quality checks) → Publish (merge to main)\n\n**Branch safety**: All operations happen on a temporary branch, NEVER on `main`. By default, branches are kept open for inspection after success or failure.\n\n**Atomic multi-table operations**: `merge_branch` is atomic. You can create or modify multiple tables on a branch, and when you merge, either all changes apply to main or none do. This enables safe multi-table ingestion workflows.\n\n## Required User Input\n\nBefore writing the WAP script, you MUST ask the user for the following parameters:\n\n1. **S3 path** (required): The S3 URI pattern for the source data (e.g., `s3://bucket/path/*.parquet`)\n2. **Table name** (required): The name for the target table\n3. **On success behavior** (optional):\n   - `inspect` (default): Keep the branch open for user inspection before merging\n   - `merge`: Automatically merge to main and delete the branch\n4. **On failure behavior** (optional):\n   - `keep` (default): Leave the branch open for inspection/debugging\n   - `delete`: Delete the failed branch\n\n## WAP Script Template\n\nThis is the complete template for WAP:\n```python\n\"\"\"\nWAP (Write-Audit-Publish) Template for bauplan data ingestion.\n\nUsage:\n    python wap_template.py\n\nOr import and call wap_ingest() with your parameters.\n\"\"\"\nimport bauplan\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n\ndef wap_ingest(\n    table_name: str,\n    s3_path: str,\n    namespace: str = \"bauplan\",\n    on_success: str = \"inspect\",  # \"inspect\" (default) or \"merge\"\n    on_failure: str = \"keep\",  # \"keep\" (default) or \"delete\"\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write-Audit-Publish flow for safe data ingestion.\n\n    Args:\n        table_name: Target table name\n        s3_path: S3 URI pattern (e.g., ''s3://bucket/path/*.parquet'')\n        namespace: Target namespace (default: ''bauplan'')\n        on_success: \"inspect\" to keep branch for review, \"merge\" to auto-merge\n        on_failure: \"keep\" to preserve branch for debugging, \"delete\" to cleanup\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: (branch_name, success)\n    \"\"\"\n    client = bauplan.Client()\n\n    # Generate unique branch name using username\n    info = client.info()\n    username = info.user.username\n    branch_name = f\"{username}.wap_{table_name}_{int(datetime.now().timestamp())}\"\n\n    success = False\n    try:\n        # === WRITE PHASE ===\n        # 1. Create temporary branch from main (must not exist)\n        assert not client.has_branch(branch_name), (\n            f\"Branch ''{branch_name}'' already exists - this should be an ephemeral branch\"\n        )\n        client.create_branch(branch_name, from_ref=\"main\")\n\n        # 2. Verify table doesn''t exist on branch before creating\n        assert not client.has_table(\n            table=table_name, ref=branch_name, namespace=namespace\n        ), (\n            f\"Table ''{namespace}.{table_name}'' already exists on branch - refusing to overwrite\"\n        )\n\n        # 3. Create table (schema inferred from S3 files)\n        client.create_table(\n            table=table_name,\n            search_uri=s3_path,\n            namespace=namespace,\n            branch=branch_name,\n        )\n\n        # 4. Import data into table\n        client.import_data(\n            table=table_name,\n            search_uri=s3_path,\n            namespace=namespace,\n            branch=branch_name,\n        )\n\n        # === AUDIT PHASE ===\n        # 5. Run quality check: verify data was imported\n        fq_table = f\"{namespace}.{table_name}\"\n        result = client.query(\n            query=f\"SELECT COUNT(*) as row_count FROM {fq_table}\", ref=branch_name\n        )\n        row_count = result.column(\"row_count\")[0].as_py()\n        assert row_count > 0, \"No data was imported\"\n        print(f\"Imported {row_count} rows\")\n\n        success = True\n\n        # === PUBLISH PHASE ===\n        if on_success == \"merge\":\n            # 6. Merge to main and cleanup\n            client.merge_branch(source_ref=branch_name, into_branch=\"main\")\n            print(f\"Successfully published {table_name} to main\")\n            client.delete_branch(branch_name)\n            print(f\"Cleaned up branch: {branch_name}\")\n        else:\n            # Keep branch for inspection\n            print(\n                f\"WAP completed successfully. Branch ''{branch_name}'' ready for inspection.\"\n            )\n            print(\n                f\"To merge manually: client.merge_branch(source_ref=''{branch_name}'', into_branch=''main'')\"\n            )\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"WAP failed: {e}\")\n        if on_failure == \"delete\":\n            if client.has_branch(branch_name):\n                client.delete_branch(branch_name)\n                print(f\"Cleaned up failed branch: {branch_name}\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"Branch ''{branch_name}'' preserved for inspection/debugging.\")\n        raise\n\n    return branch_name, success\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example: customize these parameters\n    branch, success = wap_ingest(\n        table_name=\"my_table\",\n        s3_path=\"s3://my-bucket/data/*.parquet\",\n        namespace=\"bauplan\",\n        on_success=\"inspect\",\n        on_failure=\"keep\",\n    )\n```\n\nMinimal usage:\n\n```python\nfrom wap_template import wap_ingest\n\nbranch, success = wap_ingest(\n    table_name=\"orders\",\n    s3_path=\"s3://my-bucket/data/*.parquet\",\n    namespace=\"bauplan\",\n    on_success=\"inspect\",  # or \"merge\"\n    on_failure=\"keep\"      # or \"delete\"\n)\n```\n\n## Key SDK Methods\n\n| Method                                         | Description                                           |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bauplan.Client()`                             | Initialize the bauplan client                         |\n| `client.info()`                                | Get client info; access username via `.user.username` |\n| `client.create_branch(name, from_ref=\"main\")`  | Create a new branch from specified ref                |\n| `client.has_branch(name)`                      | Check if branch exists                                |\n| `client.delete_branch(name)`                   | Delete a branch                                       |\n| `client.create_table(table, search_uri, ...)`  | Create table with schema inferred from S3             |\n| `client.import_data(table, search_uri, ...)`   | Import data from S3 into table                        |\n| `client.query(query, ref)`                     | Run SQL query, returns PyArrow Table                  |\n| `client.merge_branch(source_ref, into_branch)` | Merge branch into target                              |\n| `client.has_table(table, ref, namespace)`      | Check if table exists on branch                       |\n\n> **SDK Reference**: For detailed method signatures, check https://docs.bauplanlabs.com/reference/bauplan\n\n## Workflow Checklist\n\nCopy and track progress:\n\n\nWAP Progress:\n- [ ] Ask user for: S3 path, table name, on_success, on_failure\n- [ ] Write script using wap_template.py\n- [ ] Run script: python wap_script.py\n- [ ] Verify output shows row count > 0\n- [ ] If on_success=\"inspect\": confirm branch ready for review\n- [ ] If on_success=\"merge\": confirm merge to main succeeded\n\n\n## Example Output\n\n**Successful run (on_success=\"inspect\")**:\n```bash\n$ python wap_script.py\nImported 15234 rows\nWAP completed successfully. Branch ''alice.wap_orders_1704067200'' ready for inspection.\nTo merge manually: client.merge_branch(source_ref=''alice.wap_orders_1704067200'', into_branch=''main'')\n```\n\n**Successful run (on_success=\"merge\")**:\n```bash\n$ python wap_script.py\nImported 15234 rows\nSuccessfully published orders to main\nCleaned up branch: alice.wap_orders_1704067200\n```\n\n**Failed run (on_failure=\"keep\")**:\n```bash\n$ python wap_script.py\nWAP failed: No data was imported\nBranch ''alice.wap_orders_1704067200'' preserved for inspection/debugging.\n```\n\n## WAP on Existing Tables\n\nTo append data to an existing table, skip `create_table` and only call `import_data`:\n\n```python\n# Table already exists on main - just import new data\nclient.import_data(\n    table=table_name,\n    search_uri=s3_path,\n    namespace=namespace,\n    branch=branch_name\n)\n```\n\nThis appends rows to the existing table schema. The audit and publish phases remain the same: the new rows are automatically sandboxed on the branch until merged.\n\n## CLI Merge After Inspection\n\nWhen `on_success=\"inspect\"` (default), the branch is left open for user review. If the user asks to merge after inspecting the data, use the CLI:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Checkout to main first (required before merging)\nbauplan checkout main\n\n# 2. Merge the WAP branch into main\nbauplan branch merge <username>.wap_<table_name>_<timestamp>\n\n# 3. Optionally delete the branch after successful merge\nbauplan branch rm <username>.wap_<table_name>_<timestamp>\n```\n\n> **Note**: You must be on `main` to run `bauplan branch merge`. The branch name is printed by the WAP script upon completion.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:57:05.884Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Ingestion Agents needing structured telemetry analysis using the WAP pattern","zh":"Perfect for Data Ingestion Agents needing structured telemetry analysis using the WAP pattern","ja":"Perfect for Data Ingestion Agents needing structured telemetry analysis using the WAP pattern","ko":"Perfect for Data Ingestion Agents needing structured telemetry analysis using the WAP pattern","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Ingestión de Datos que necesitan análisis de telemetría estructurada utilizando el patrón WAP","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''ingestion de données nécessitant une analyse de télémétrie structurée utilisant le modèle WAP","de":"Perfekt für Data-Ingestion-Agents, die eine strukturierte Telemetrie-Analyse unter Verwendung des WAP-Musters benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Ingestão de Dados que necessitam de análise de telemetria estruturada usando o padrão WAP","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ингестии данных, которым необходима структурированная анализ телеметрии с использованием шаблона WAP","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء استيعاب البيانات التي تحتاج إلى تحليل التелеметري المنظمة باستخدام نمط WAP"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement the Write-Audit-Publish pattern using the bauplan SDK, enabling atomic multi-table operations and branch safety with Python scripting, while leveraging quality checks and temporary branch management for secure data ingestion","zh":"Empowers agents to implement the Write-Audit-Publish pattern using the bauplan SDK, enabling atomic multi-table operations and branch safety with Python scripting, while leveraging quality checks and temporary branch management for secure data ingestion","ja":"Empowers agents to implement the Write-Audit-Publish pattern using the bauplan SDK, enabling atomic multi-table operations and branch safety with Python scripting, while leveraging quality checks and temporary branch management for secure data ingestion","ko":"Empowers agents to implement the Write-Audit-Publish pattern using the bauplan SDK, enabling atomic multi-table operations and branch safety with Python scripting, while leveraging quality checks and temporary branch management for secure data ingestion","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar el patrón Escritura-Auditoría-Publicación utilizando el SDK bauplan, permitiendo operaciones atómicas multi-tabla y seguridad de rama con scripting en Python, al tiempo que aprovecha las comprobaciones de calidad y la gestión de ramas temporales para una ingesta de datos segura","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre le modèle Écriture-Audit-Publication en utilisant le SDK bauplan, permettant des opérations multi-table atomiques et une sécurité de branche avec un scripting Python, tout en exploitant les vérifications de qualité et la gestion des branches temporaires pour une ingestion de données sécurisée","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, das Schreib-Audit-Veröffentlichungsmuster unter Verwendung des bauplan-SDKs umzusetzen, wodurch atomare Multi-Tabelle-Operationen und Zweig-Sicherheit mit Python-Skripten ermöglicht werden, während Qualitätssicherungen und temporäre Zweigverwaltung für eine sichere Datenübernahme genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar o padrão Write-Audit-Publish usando o SDK bauplan, permitindo operações atômicas multi-tabela e segurança de branch com script em Python, ao mesmo tempo em que aproveita verificações de qualidade e gerenciamento de branch temporário para ingestão de dados segura","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность реализовать шаблон Write-Audit-Publish с использованием SDK bauplan, что позволяет выполнять атомарные операции с несколькими таблицами и обеспечивать безопасность веток с помощью скриптов на Python, а также использовать проверки качества и временное управление ветками для безопасной ингестии данных","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تنفيذ نمط الكتابة-التحقق-النشر باستخدام SDK باوبلان، وتمكين عمليات الجداول متعددة الذرية وأمان الفرع مع البرمجة النصية بالبايثون، وفي الوقت نفسه الاستفادة من فحص الجودة وإدارة الفرع المؤقتة لأمن استيعاب البيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating telemetry data ingestion","Validating data quality with audit checks","Publishing merged data to main branches"],"zh":["Automating telemetry data ingestion","Validating data quality with audit checks","Publishing merged data to main branches"],"ja":["Automating telemetry data ingestion","Validating data quality with audit checks","Publishing merged data to main branches"],"ko":["Automating telemetry data ingestion","Validating data quality with audit checks","Publishing merged data to main branches"],"es":["Automatización de la ingesta de datos de telemetría","Validación de la calidad de los datos con comprobaciones de auditoría","Publicación de datos fusionados en ramas principales"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''ingestion de données de télémétrie","Validation de la qualité des données avec des vérifications d''audit","Publication de données fusionnées sur des branches principales"],"de":["Automatisierung der Übernahme von Telemetriedaten","Validierung der Datenqualität mit Audit-Prüfungen","Veröffentlichung von fusionierten Daten in Hauptzweigen"],"pt":["Automatizar a ingestão de dados de telemetria","Validar a qualidade dos dados com verificações de auditoria","Publicar dados mesclados para branches principais"],"ru":["Автоматизация ингестии телеметрических данных","Проверка качества данных с помощью аудиторских проверок","Публикация объединенных данных в основные ветки"],"ar":["أتمتة استيعاب بيانات التليمتري","التحقق من جودة البيانات مع فحوصات التدقيق","نشر بيانات متعددة إلى فروع رئيسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires bauplan SDK","Python scripting necessary","Operations limited to temporary branches"],"zh":["Requires bauplan SDK","Python scripting necessary","Operations limited to temporary branches"],"ja":["Requires bauplan SDK","Python scripting necessary","Operations limited to temporary branches"],"ko":["Requires bauplan SDK","Python scripting necessary","Operations limited to temporary branches"],"es":["Requiere SDK bauplan","Se requiere scripting en Python","Operaciones limitadas a ramas temporales"],"fr":["Nécessite le SDK bauplan","Scripting Python nécessaire","Opérations limitées aux branches temporaires"],"de":["Benötigt bauplan-SDK","Python-Skripting erforderlich","Operationen beschränkt auf temporäre Zweige"],"pt":["Requer o SDK bauplan","Script em Python necessário","Operações limitadas a branches temporários"],"ru":["Требуется SDK bauplan","Необходимо скриптование на Python","Операции ограничены временными ветками"],"ar":["يتطلب SDK باوبلان","البرمجة النصية بالبايثون ضرورية","العمليات مقيدة بالفروع المؤقتة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('onejs/one/railway', 'community', 'onejs', 'one', 'onejs/one', 'railway', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.401Z', '2026-02-18T02:57:07.393Z', NULL, '{"id":"onejs/one/railway","name":"railway","description":{"zh":"Railway 是一个新的 React 框架，允许你使用单一的 Vite 插件和共享代码构建跨平台应用","ja":"Railway は、新しい React フレームワークであり、単一の Vite プラグインと共有コードを使用してクロスプラットフォーム アプリケーションを構築できる","ko":"Railway는 새로운 React 프레임워크로, 단일의 Vite 플러그인과 공유 코드를 사용하여 크로스 플랫폼 애플리케이션을 구축","es":"Railway es un nuevo framework React que permite desarrollar aplicaciones web y nativas con un solo plugin de Vite y código compartido, facilitando el desarrollo cross-plataforma","fr":"Railway est un nouveau framework React qui permet de développer des applications web et natives avec un seul plugin Vite et du code partagé, facilitant ainsi le développement cross-plateforme","de":"Railway ist ein neues React-Framework, das die Entwicklung von Web- und Native-Anwendungen mit einem einzigen Vite-Plugin und gemeinsamem Code ermöglicht, wodurch die cross-plattformübergreifende Entwicklung erleichtert wird","pt":"O Railway é um framework React que permite desenvolver aplicações web e nativas com um único plugin Vite e código compartilhado, facilitando o desenvolvimento cross-plataforma","ru":"Railway - это Реакт-фреймворк, который позволяет разрабатывать веб- и родные приложения с одним плагином Vite и общим кодом, упрощая кроссплатформенную разработку","ar":"Railway هو إطار العمل React الذي يسمح بتطوير التطبيقات الويب والأصلية باستخدام موفري Vite واحد ورمز مشترك، مما يسهل التطوير على منصات متعددة","en":"❶ One is a new React framework - target web and native with a single Vite plugin and fully shared code, so you can ship cross-platform nearly as easy as single-platform."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Railway 框架：跨平台 React 开发","ja":"Railway フレームワーク：クロスプラットフォーム React 開発","ko":"Railway 프레임워