 패널 디자인"],"es":["Diseño de dashboards","Creación de paneles de administración","Desarrollo de aplicaciones SaaS","Diseño de interfaces de datos","Creación de páginas de configuración"],"fr":["Conception de tableaux de bord","Création de panneaux d''administration","Développement d''applications SaaS","Conception d''interfaces de données","Création de pages de configuration"],"de":["Dashboard-Design","Erstellung von Admin-Panel","Entwicklung von SaaS-Anwendungen","Design von Dateninterfaces","Erstellung von Konfigurationsseiten"],"pt":["Criação de dashboards personalizados","Design de painéis de administração","Desenvolvimento de aplicativos SaaS","Otimização de interfaces de usuário","Criação de layouts responsivos"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных панелей управления","Дизайн административных панелей","Разработка приложений SaaS","Оптимизация интерфейсов пользователя","Создание адаптивных макетов"],"ar":["إنشاء داشبورد مخصص","تصميم لوحات التحكم والإدارة","تطوير تطبيقات SaaS","تحسين واجهات المستخدم","إنشاء تصاميم واجهة مستخدم مرنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["界面设计","交互界面","用户体验","一致性设计","工艺设计","dashboard 设计","admin 面板设计","SaaS 应用程序设计"],"ja":["インターフェース設計","インタラクティブなインターフェース","ユーザー体験","一貫性設計","工芸性設計","ダッシュボード設計","アドミンパネル設計","SaaS アプリケーション設計"],"ko":["인터페이스 디자인","상호 작용 인터페이스","사용자 경험","일관성 디자인","공예적 설계","대시보드 디자인","관리자 패널 디자인","SaaS 애플리케이션 디자인"],"es":["diseño de interfaces de usuario","interfaces de usuario","dashboards","paneles de administración","aplicaciones SaaS","diseño de interfaces","experiencia de usuario","usabilidad"],"fr":["conception d''interface utilisateur","interfaces utilisateur","tableaux de bord","panneaux d''administration","applications SaaS","conception d''interface","expérience utilisateur","ergonomie"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächendesign","Benutzeroberflächen","Dashboards","Admin-Panel","SaaS-Anwendungen","Benutzeroberflächendesign","Benutzererfahrung","Benutzerfreundlichkeit"],"pt":["design de interface","dashboards personalizados","painéis de administração","aplicativos SaaS","otimização de interfaces","layouts responsivos","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["дизайн интерфейса","индивидуальные панели управления","административные панели","приложения SaaS","оптимизация интерфейсов","адаптивные макеты","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة","داشبورد مخصص","لوحات التحكم والإدارة","تطبيقات SaaS","تحسين واجهات المستخدم","تصاميم واجهة مستخدم مرنة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"thiagobraddock","repo":"gealdebara","repoPath":"thiagobraddock/gealdebara","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"interface-design","description":"This skill is for interface design — dashboards, admin panels, apps, tools, and interactive products. NOT for marketing design (landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns).","bodyPreview":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and","body":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and still produce a template. Warm colors on cold structures. Friendly fonts on generic layouts. \"Kitchen feel\" that looks like every other app.\n\nThis happens because intent lives in prose, but code generation pulls from patterns. The gap between them is where defaults win.\n\nThe process below helps. But process alone doesn''t guarantee craft. You have to catch yourself.\n\n---\n\n# Where Defaults Hide\n\nDefaults don''t announce themselves. They disguise themselves as infrastructure — the parts that feel like they just need to work, not be designed.\n\n**Typography feels like a container.** Pick something readable, move on. But typography isn''t holding your design — it IS your design. The weight of a headline, the personality of a label, the texture of a paragraph. These shape how the product feels before anyone reads a word. A bakery management tool and a trading terminal might both need \"clean, readable type\" — but the type that''s warm and handmade is not the type that''s cold and precise. If you''re reaching for your usual font, you''re not designing.\n\n**Navigation feels like scaffolding.** Build the sidebar, add the links, get to the real work. But navigation isn''t around your product — it IS your product. Where you are, where you can go, what matters most. A page floating in space is a component demo, not software. The navigation teaches people how to think about the space they''re in.\n\n**Data feels like presentation.** You have numbers, show numbers. But a number on screen is not design. The question is: what does this number mean to the person looking at it? What will they do with it? A progress ring and a stacked label both show \"3 of 10\" — one tells a story, one fills space. If you''re reaching for number-on-label, you''re not designing.\n\n**Token names feel like implementation detail.** But your CSS variables are design decisions. `--ink` and `--parchment` evoke a world. `--gray-700` and `--surface-2` evoke a template. Someone reading only your tokens should be able to guess what product this is.\n\nThe trap is thinking some decisions are creative and others are structural. There are no structural decisions. Everything is design. The moment you stop asking \"why this?\" is the moment defaults take over.\n\n---\n\n# Intent First\n\nBefore touching code, answer these. Not in your head — out loud, to yourself or the user.\n\n**Who is this human?**\nNot \"users.\" The actual person. Where are they when they open this? What''s on their mind? What did they do 5 minutes ago, what will they do 5 minutes after? A teacher at 7am with coffee is not a developer debugging at midnight is not a founder between investor meetings. Their world shapes the interface.\n\n**What must they accomplish?**\nNot \"use the dashboard.\" The verb. Grade these submissions. Find the broken deployment. Approve the payment. The answer determines what leads, what follows, what hides.\n\n**What should this feel like?**\nSay it in words that mean something. \"Clean and modern\" means nothing — every AI says that. Warm like a notebook? Cold like a terminal? Dense like a trading floor? Calm like a reading app? The answer shapes color, type, spacing, density — everything.\n\nIf you cannot answer these with specifics, stop. Ask the user. Do not guess. Do not default.\n\n## Every Choice Must Be A Choice\n\nFor every decision, you must be able to explain WHY.\n\n- Why this layout and not another?\n- Why this color temperature?\n- Why this typeface?\n- Why this spacing scale?\n- Why this information hierarchy?\n\nIf your answer is \"it''s common\" or \"it''s clean\" or \"it works\" — you haven''t chosen. You''ve defaulted. Defaults are invisible. Invisible choices compound into generic output.\n\n**The test:** If you swapped your choices for the most common alternatives and the design didn''t feel meaningfully different, you never made real choices.\n\n## Sameness Is Failure\n\nIf another AI, given a similar prompt, would produce substantially the same output — you have failed.\n\nThis is not about being different for its own sake. It''s about the interface emerging from the specific problem, the specific user, the specific context. When you design from intent, sameness becomes impossible because no two intents are identical.\n\nWhen you design from defaults, everything looks the same because defaults are shared.\n\n## Intent Must Be Systemic\n\nSaying \"warm\" and using cold colors is not following through. Intent is not a label — it''s a constraint that shapes every decision.\n\nIf the intent is warm: surfaces, text, borders, accents, semantic colors, typography — all warm. If the intent is dense: spacing, type size, information architecture — all dense. If the intent is calm: motion, contrast, color saturation — all calm.\n\nCheck your output against your stated intent. Does every token reinforce it? Or did you state an intent and then default anyway?\n\n---\n\n# Product Domain Exploration\n\nThis is where defaults get caught — or don''t.\n\nGeneric output: Task type → Visual template → Theme\nCrafted output: Task type → Product domain → Signature → Structure + Expression\n\nThe difference: time in the product''s world before any visual or structural thinking.\n\n## Required Outputs\n\n**Do not propose any direction until you produce all four:**\n\n**Domain:** Concepts, metaphors, vocabulary from this product''s world. Not features — territory. Minimum 5.\n\n**Color world:** What colors exist naturally in this product''s domain? Not \"warm\" or \"cool\" — go to the actual world. If this product were a physical space, what would you see? What colors belong there that don''t belong elsewhere? List 5+.\n\n**Signature:** One element — visual, structural, or interaction — that could only exist for THIS product. If you can''t name one, keep exploring.\n\n**Defaults:** 3 obvious choices for this interface type — visual AND structural. You can''t avoid patterns you haven''t named.\n\n## Proposal Requirements\n\nYour direction must explicitly reference:\n- Domain concepts you explored\n- Colors from your color world exploration\n- Your signature element\n- What replaces each default\n\n**The test:** Read your proposal. Remove the product name. Could someone identify what this is for? If not, it''s generic. Explore deeper.\n\n---\n\n# The Mandate\n\n**Before showing the user, look at what you made.**\n\nAsk yourself: \"If they said this lacks craft, what would they mean?\"\n\nThat thing you just thought of — fix it first.\n\nYour first output is probably generic. That''s normal. The work is catching it before the user has to.\n\n## The Checks\n\nRun these against your output before presenting:\n\n- **The swap test:** If you swapped the typeface for your usual one, would anyone notice? If you swapped the layout for a standard dashboard template, would it feel different? The places where swapping wouldn''t matter are the places you defaulted.\n\n- **The squint test:** Blur your eyes. Can you still perceive hierarchy? Is anything jumping out harshly? Craft whispers.\n\n- **The signature test:** Can you point to five specific elements where your signature appears? Not \"the overall feel\" — actual components. A signature you can''t locate doesn''t exist.\n\n- **The token test:** Read your CSS variables out loud. Do they sound like they belong to this product''s world, or could they belong to any project?\n\nIf any check fails, iterate before showing.\n\n---\n\n# Craft Foundations\n\n## Subtle Layering\n\nThis is the backbone of craft. Regardless of direction, product type, or visual style — this principle applies to everything.\n\n**Surfaces must be barely different but still distinguishable.** Study Vercel, Supabase, Linear. Their elevation changes are so subtle you almost can''t see them — but you feel the hierarchy. Not dramatic jumps. Not obviously different colors. Whisper-quiet shifts.\n\n**Borders must be light but not invisible.** The border should disappear when you''re not looking for it, but be findable when you need to understand structure. If borders are the first thing you notice, they''re too strong. If you can''t tell where regions begin and end, they''re too weak.\n\n**The squint test:** Blur your eyes at the interface. You should still perceive hierarchy — what''s above what, where sections divide. But nothing should jump out. No harsh lines. No jarring color shifts. Just quiet structure.\n\nThis separates professional interfaces from amateur ones. Get this wrong and nothing else matters.\n\n## Infinite Expression\n\nEvery pattern has infinite expressions. **No interface should look the same.**\n\nA metric display could be a hero number, inline stat, sparkline, gauge, progress bar, comparison delta, trend badge, or something new. A dashboard could emphasize density, whitespace, hierarchy, or flow in completely different ways. Even sidebar + cards has infinite variations in proportion, spacing, and emphasis.\n\n**Before building, ask:**\n- What''s the ONE thing users do most here?\n- What products solve similar problems brilliantly? Study them.\n- Why would this interface feel designed for its purpose, not templated?\n\n**NEVER produce identical output.** Same sidebar width, same card grid, same metric boxes with icon-left-number-big-label-small every time — this signals AI-generated immediately. It''s forgettable.\n\nThe architecture and components should emerge from the task and data, executed in a way that feels fresh. Linear''s cards don''t look like Notion''s. Vercel''s metrics don''t look like Stripe''s. Same concepts, infinite expressions.\n\n## Color Lives Somewhere\n\nEvery product exists in a world. That world has colors.\n\nBefore you reach for a palette, spend time in the product''s world. What would you see if you walked into the physical version of this space? What materials? What light? What objects?\n\nYour palette should feel like it came FROM somewhere — not like it was applied TO something.\n\n**Beyond Warm and Cold:** Temperature is one axis. Is this quiet or loud? Dense or spacious? Serious or playful? Geometric or organic? A trading terminal and a meditation app are both \"focused\" — completely different kinds of focus. Find the specific quality, not the generic label.\n\n**Color Carries Meaning:** Gray builds structure. Color communicates — status, action, emphasis, identity. Unmotivated color is noise. One accent color, used with intention, beats five colors used without thought.\n\n---\n\n# Design Principles\n\n## Spacing\nPick a base unit and stick to multiples. Consistency matters more than the specific number. Random values signal no system.\n\n## Padding\nKeep it symmetrical. If one side is 16px, others should match unless there''s a clear reason.\n\n## Depth\nChoose ONE approach and commit:\n- **Borders-only** — Clean, technical. For dense tools.\n- **Subtle shadows** — Soft lift. For approachable products.\n- **Layered shadows** — Premium, dimensional. For cards that need presence.\n\nDon''t mix approaches.\n\n## Border Radius\nSharper feels technical. Rounder feels friendly. Pick a scale and apply consistently.\n\n## Typography\nHeadlines need weight and tight tracking. Body needs readability. Data needs monospace. Build a hierarchy.\n\n## Color & Surfaces\nBuild from primitives: foreground (text hierarchy), background (surface elevation), border (separation hierarchy), brand, and semantic (destructive, warning, success). Every color should trace back to these. No random hex values — everything maps to the system.\n\n## Animation\nFast micro-interactions (~150ms), smooth easing. No bouncy/spring effects.\n\n## States\nEvery interactive element needs states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled. Data needs states too: loading, empty, error. Missing states feel broken.\n\n## Controls\nNative `<select>` and `<input type=\"date\">` can''t be styled. Build custom components.\n\n---\n\n# Avoid\n\n- **Harsh borders** — if borders are the first thing you see, they''re too strong\n- **Dramatic surface jumps** — elevation changes should be whisper-quiet\n- **Inconsistent spacing** — the clearest sign of no system\n- **Mixed depth strategies** — pick one approach and commit\n- **Missing interaction states** — hover, focus, disabled, loading, error\n- **Dramatic drop shadows** — shadows should be subtle, not attention-grabbing\n- **Large radius on small elements**\n- **Pure white cards on colored backgrounds**\n- **Thick decorative borders**\n- **Gradients and color for decoration** — color should mean something\n- **Multiple accent colors** — dilutes focus\n\n---\n\n# Workflow\n\n## Communication\nBe invisible. Don''t announce modes or narrate process.\n\n**Never say:** \"I''m in ESTABLISH MODE\", \"Let me check system.md...\"\n\n**Instead:** Jump into work. State suggestions with reasoning.\n\n## Suggest + Ask\nLead with your exploration and recommendation, then confirm:\n```\n\"Domain: [5+ concepts from the product''s world]\nColor world: [5+ colors that exist in this domain]\nSignature: [one element unique to this product]\nRejecting: [default 1] → [alternative], [default 2] → [alternative], [default 3] → [alternative]\n\nDirection: [approach that connects to the above]\"\n\n[AskUserQuestion: \"Does that direction feel right?\"]\n```\n\n## If Project Has system.md\nRead `.interface-design/system.md` and apply. Decisions are made.\n\n## If No system.md\n1. Explore domain — Produce all four required outputs\n2. Propose — Direction must reference all four\n3. Confirm — Get user buy-in\n4. Build — Apply principles\n5. **Evaluate** — Run the mandate checks before showing\n6. Offer to save\n\n---\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:57:51.954Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI-focused Agents needing advanced dashboard design and data interface creation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级仪表盘设计和数据接口创建能力的UI专注代理。","ja":"UI に焦点を当てたエージェントが高度なダッシュボード設計とデータインターフェイス作成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 대시보드 디자인 및 데이터 인터페이스 생성 기능이 필요한 UI 중심 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes enfocados en la interfaz de usuario que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de diseño de panel y creación de interfaz de datos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur l''interface utilisateur nécessitant des capacités avancées de conception de tableau de bord et de création d''interface de données.","de":"Perfekt für benutzeroberflächenorientierte Agenten, die erweiterte Dashboard-Design- und Daten-Schnittstellen-Erstellungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em UI que necessitam de design de dashboard avançado e capacidades de criação de interface de dados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на UI, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности проектирования панелей управления и создания интерфейсов данных.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التركيز على واجهة المستخدم التي تحتاج إلى تصميم لوحة القيادة المتقدمة وإنشاء واجهة بيانات القدرات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft consistent and user-friendly interfaces for dashboards, admin panels, and SaaS apps using design principles and patterns, while generating generic output and following established protocols for settings pages and data interfaces.","zh":"赋予代理创建仪表盘、管理员面板和SaaS应用程序的一致且用户友好的界面能力，使用设计原则和模式，同时生成通用输出并遵循设置页面和数据接口的既定协议。","ja":"エージェントが設計原則とパターンを使用してダッシュボード、管理パネル、SaaS アプリケーションに一貫性とユーザーフレンドリーなインターフェイスを作成できるようにし、汎用的な出力生成と設定ページおよびデータインターフェイスの既定のプロトコルに従う。","ko":"에이전트가 디자인 원칙과 패턴을 사용하여 대시보드, 관리자 패널 및 SaaS 애플리케이션에 일관성과 사용자 친화적인 인터페이스를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 일반 출력을 생성하고 설정 페이지 및 데이터 인터페이스의 확립된 프로토콜을 따릅니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces coherentes y fáciles de usar para paneles de control, paneles de administración y aplicaciones SaaS utilizando principios y patrones de diseño, mientras genera una salida genérica y sigue protocolos establecidos para páginas de configuración e interfaces de datos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces cohérentes et conviviales pour les tableaux de bord, les panneaux d''administration et les applications SaaS en utilisant des principes et des modèles de conception, tout en générant une sortie générique et en suivant les protocoles établis pour les pages de paramètres et les interfaces de données.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, konsistente und benutzerfreundliche Schnittstellen für Dashboards, Administrationspanele und SaaS-Apps zu erstellen, indem sie Designprinzipien und -muster verwenden, während sie generische Ausgaben erzeugen und etablierte Protokolle für Einstellungsseiten und Datenschnittstellen befolgen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar interfaces consistentes e amigáveis para dashboards, painéis de administração e aplicativos SaaS usando princípios e padrões de design, enquanto gera saída genérica e segue protocolos estabelecidos para páginas de configurações e interfaces de dados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать последовательные и удобные интерфейсы для панелей управления, административных панелей и приложений SaaS, используя принципы и шаблоны проектирования, при этом генерируя общий вывод и следуя установленным протоколам для страниц настроек и интерфейсов данных.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من إنشاء واجهات متسقة وسهلة الاستخدام للوحات القيادة وألواح الإدارة وتطبيقات SaaS باستخدام مبادئ وأنماط التصميم، مع توليد مخرجات عامة والامتثال لبروتوكولات محددة للصفحات الإعدادات وواجهات البيانات."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing responsive dashboards","Creating intuitive admin panels","Developing user-friendly SaaS app interfaces"],"zh":["设计响应式仪表盘","创建直观的管理员面板","开发用户友好的SaaS应用程序接口"],"ja":["レスポンシブダッシュボードの設計","直感的な管理パネルの作成","ユーザーフレンドリーなSaaSアプリケーションインターフェイスの開発"],"ko":["반응형 대시보드 설계","직관적인 관리자 패널 생성","사용자 친화적인 SaaS 애플리케이션 인터페이스 개발"],"es":["Diseñar paneles de control responsivos","Crear paneles de administración intuitivos","Desarrollar interfaces de aplicaciones SaaS de fácil uso"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux de bord réactifs","Créer des panneaux d''administration intuitifs","Développer des interfaces d''applications SaaS conviviales"],"de":["Reaktive Dashboards entwerfen","Intuitive Administrationspanele erstellen","Benutzerfreundliche SaaS-App-Schnittstellen entwickeln"],"pt":["Projeto de dashboards responsivos","Criação de painéis de administração intuitivos","Desenvolvimento de interfaces de aplicativos SaaS amigáveis"],"ru":["Проектирование адаптивных панелей управления","Создание интуитивных административных панелей","Разработка удобных интерфейсов для приложений SaaS"],"ar":["تصميم لوحات القيادة المستجيبة","إنشاء ألواح إدارة直觉ية","تطوير واجهات تطبيقات SaaS سهلة الاستخدام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for landing pages or marketing sites","Redirects campaigns to frontend design"],"zh":["不适合登陆页面或营销网站","重定向活动到前端设计"],"ja":["ランディングページやマーケティングサイトには不適","キャンペーンをフロントエンド設計にリダイレクト"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지 또는 마케팅 사이트에 적합하지 않음","캠페인을 프론트엔드 디자인으로 리디렉션"],"es":["No apto para páginas de destino o sitios de marketing","Redirige campañas al diseño frontend"],"fr":["Non adapté pour les pages de destination ou les sites de marketing","Redirige les campagnes vers la conception frontend"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für Zielseiten oder Marketing-Websites","Leitet Kampagnen zur Frontend-Design"],"pt":["Não adequado para páginas de destino ou sites de marketing","Redireciona campanhas para design de frontend"],"ru":["Не подходит для посадочных страниц или маркетинговых сайтов","Перенаправляет кампании на проектирование frontend"],"ar":["غير مناسب للصفحات الهبوطية أو المواقع التسويقية","تحويل الحملات إلى تصميم واجهة المستخدم الأمامية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cloudposse/docs/docs-styles', 'community', 'cloudposse', 'docs', 'cloudposse/docs', 'docs-styles', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T02:58:30.504Z', NULL, '{"id":"cloudposse/docs/docs-styles","name":"docs-styles","description":{"zh":"Terraform Reference Architecture为AWS、Datadog和GitHub Actions提供了一种集成的方式，用于简化基础设施管理","ja":"Terraformリファレンスアーキテクチャは、AWS、Datadog、GitHub Actionsの統合を提供し、インフラストラクチャの管理を簡素化します","ko":"Terraform 참조 아키텍처는 AWS, Datadog 및 GitHub Actions의 통합을 제공하여 인프라 관리를 간소화합니다","es":"La referencia de arquitectura de Terraform para AWS, Datadog y GitHub Actions, con estilos de documentación para mejorar la legibilidad y la comprensión","fr":"La référence d''architecture Terraform pour AWS, Datadog et GitHub Actions, avec des styles de documentation pour améliorer la lisibilité et la compréhension","de":"Die Referenzarchitektur von Terraform für AWS, Datadog und GitHub Actions, mit Dokumentationsstilen für eine verbesserte Lesbarkeit und Verständlichkeit","en":"Terraform Reference Architecture for AWS, Datadog and GitHub Actions"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Terraform参考架构：AWS、Datadog和GitHub Actions","ja":"Terraformリファレンスアーキテクチャ：AWS、Datadog、GitHub Actions","ko":"Terraform 참조 아키텍처: AWS, Datadog 및 GitHub Actions","es":"Estilos de Documentación para Desarrolladores","fr":"Styles de Documentation pour Développeurs","de":"Dokumentationsstile für Entwickler","en":"docs-styles"},"description":{"zh":"Terraform Reference Architecture为AWS、Datadog和GitHub Actions提供了一种集成的方式，用于简化基础设施管理","ja":"Terraformリファレンスアーキテクチャは、AWS、Datadog、GitHub Actionsの統合を提供し、インフラストラクチャの管理を簡素化します","ko":"Terraform 참조 아키텍처는 AWS, Datadog 및 GitHub Actions의 통합을 제공하여 인프라 관리를 간소화합니다","es":"La referencia de arquitectura de Terraform para AWS, Datadog y GitHub Actions, con estilos de documentación para mejorar la legibilidad y la comprensión","fr":"La référence d''architecture Terraform pour AWS, Datadog et GitHub Actions, avec des styles de documentation pour améliorer la lisibilité et la compréhension","de":"Die Referenzarchitektur von Terraform für AWS, Datadog und GitHub Actions, mit Dokumentationsstilen für eine verbesserte Lesbarkeit und Verständlichkeit","en":"Terraform Reference Architecture for AWS, Datadog and GitHub Actions"},"definition":{"en":"Terraform Reference Architecture for AWS, Datadog and GitHub Actions"},"features":{"zh":["Terraform Reference Architecture","AWS集成","Datadog集成","GitHub Actions集成","基础设施管理简化","CSS样式和颜色约定"],"ja":["Terraformリファレンスアーキテクチャ","AWS統合","Datadog統合","GitHub Actions統合","インフラストラクチャ管理の簡素化","CSSスタイルとカラーコン벤ション"],"ko":["Terraform 참조 아키텍처","AWS 통합","Datadog 통합","GitHub Actions 통합","인프라 관리 간소화","CSS 스타일 및 색상 규칙"],"es":["Paleta de colores personalizada","Convenciones de CSS para una mejor legibilidad","Integración con Terraform y GitHub Actions","Compatibilidad con AWS y Datadog","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Palette de couleurs personnalisée","Conventions CSS pour une meilleure lisibilité","Intégration avec Terraform et GitHub Actions","Compatibilité avec AWS et Datadog","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte Farbpalette","CSS-Konventionen für eine verbesserte Lesbarkeit","Integration mit Terraform und GitHub Actions","Kompatibilität mit AWS und Datadog","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","基础设施管理","集成","CSS样式","颜色约定","云计算"],"ja":["Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","インフラストラクチャ管理","統合","CSSスタイル","カラーコン벤ション","クラウドコンピューティング"],"ko":["Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","인프라 관리","통합","CSS 스타일","색상 규칙","클라우드 컴퓨팅"],"es":["estilos de documentación","Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","convenciones de CSS","paleta de colores","experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["styles de documentation","Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","conventions CSS","palette de couleurs","expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Dokumentationsstile","Terraform","AWS","Datadog","GitHub Actions","CSS-Konventionen","Farbpalette","Benutzererfahrung"]}},"owner":"cloudposse","repo":"docs","repoPath":"cloudposse/docs","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"docs-styles","description":"CSS styles, color themes, and visual conventions for docs.cloudposse.com. Use when styling components, mermaid diagrams, or working with site theming.","bodyPreview":"# Documentation Styles\n\nCSS styles and color conventions for docs.cloudposse.com.\n\n## Color Palette\n\n### Site Primary Colors\n\nDefined in `src/css/custom.css`:\n\n| Variable | Light | Dark | Usage |\n|----------|-------|------|-------|\n| `--ifm-color-primary` | `#3578e5` | `#3578e5` | Primary blue, links, buttons |\n| `--ifm-color-primary-dark` | `#306cce` | `#306cce` | Hover states |\n| `--ifm-color-primary-darkest` | `#2554a0` | `#2554a0` | Active states |\n| `--ifm-background-color` | default | `#03","body":"# Documentation Styles\n\nCSS styles and color conventions for docs.cloudposse.com.\n\n## Color Palette\n\n### Site Primary Colors\n\nDefined in `src/css/custom.css`:\n\n| Variable | Light | Dark | Usage |\n|----------|-------|------|-------|\n| `--ifm-color-primary` | `#3578e5` | `#3578e5` | Primary blue, links, buttons |\n| `--ifm-color-primary-dark` | `#306cce` | `#306cce` | Hover states |\n| `--ifm-color-primary-darkest` | `#2554a0` | `#2554a0` | Active states |\n| `--ifm-background-color` | default | `#030711` | Page background |\n\n### Mermaid Diagram Colors\n\nDefined in `src/css/mermaid.css`:\n\n| Variable | Hex | Usage |\n|----------|-----|-------|\n| `--mermaid-primary` | `#3578e5` | Primary elements, read-only access |\n| `--mermaid-primary-dark` | `#2554a0` | Darker blue variant |\n| `--mermaid-secondary` | `#6c757d` | Gray, neutral elements |\n| `--mermaid-success` | `#28a745` | Green, write/apply access |\n| `--mermaid-danger` | `#dc3545` | Red, destructive/admin |\n| `--mermaid-warning` | `#e67e22` | Orange, caution/IdP |\n| `--mermaid-info` | `#17a2b8` | Teal, informational |\n| `--mermaid-user` | `#9b59b6` | Purple, user/identity |\n| `--mermaid-account` | `#2c3e50` | Dark slate, AWS accounts |\n\n### Using Colors in Mermaid Diagrams\n\nMermaid doesn''t support CSS variables directly. Use hex values with `style`:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    user[\"User\"] --> service[\"Service\"]\n\n    style user fill:#9b59b6,color:#fff\n    style service fill:#3578e5,color:#fff\n```\n\n### Semantic Color Meanings\n\n| Color | Meaning | Example Usage |\n|-------|---------|---------------|\n| Blue (`#3578e5`) | Read-only, plan, info | TerraformPlanAccess |\n| Green (`#28a745`) | Write, apply, success | TerraformApplyAccess |\n| Orange (`#e67e22`) | Identity, IdP, warning | Identity Center |\n| Purple (`#9b59b6`) | User, human identity | User nodes |\n| Dark slate (`#2c3e50`) | AWS accounts, infrastructure | Account nodes |\n| Red (`#dc3545`) | Destructive, admin, danger | RootAccess |\n\n## CSS File Locations\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/css/custom.css` | Global styles, Infima overrides |\n| `src/css/mermaid.css` | Mermaid diagram styling |\n| `src/css/admonitions.css` | Admonition/callout styling |\n| `src/css/sidebar.css` | Navigation sidebar |\n| `src/css/navbar.css` | Top navigation |\n| `src/css/footer.css` | Footer styling |\n\n## Dark Mode\n\nUse `[data-theme=''dark'']` or `html[data-theme=''dark'']` selectors:\n\n```css\n[data-theme=''dark''] .my-element {\n    background: #21262d;\n    color: #fff;\n}\n```\n\n## Component Styling\n\nReact components have co-located CSS modules:\n\n```\nsrc/components/\n├── Steps/\n│   ├── index.js\n│   └── index.module.css\n├── ActionCard/\n│   ├── index.js\n│   └── index.module.css\n```\n\nUse `clsx` for conditional class names:\n\n```jsx\nimport clsx from ''clsx'';\nimport styles from ''./index.module.css'';\n\n<div className={clsx(styles.container, isActive && styles.active)} />\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:58:30.504Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing standardized CSS styling for documentation and reference architectures, particularly those working with Terraform, AWS, Datadog, and GitHub Actions.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化CSS样式的开发人员代理，特别是用于文档和参考架构的代理，例如那些使用Terraform、AWS、Datadog和GitHub Actions的代理。","ja":"Terraform、AWS、Datadog、GitHub Actionsなどのドキュメントやリファレンスアーキテクチャで標準化されたCSSスタイリングが必要な開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Terraform, AWS, Datadog, GitHub Actions 등의 문서 및 참조 아키텍처에서 표준화된 CSS 스타일링이 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan estilos de CSS estandarizados para documentación y arquitecturas de referencia, particularmente aquellos que trabajan con Terraform, AWS, Datadog y GitHub Actions.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de styles CSS standardisés pour la documentation et les architectures de référence, en particulier ceux qui travaillent avec Terraform, AWS, Datadog et GitHub Actions.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsagenten, die standardisierte CSS-Stile für Dokumentationen und Referenzarchitekturen benötigen, insbesondere für diejenigen, die mit Terraform, AWS, Datadog und GitHub Actions arbeiten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que necessitam de estilização de CSS padronizada para documentação e arquiteturas de referência, particularmente aqueles que trabalham com Terraform, AWS, Datadog e GitHub Actions.","ru":"Идеально для агентов-разработчиков, которым необходима стандартизированная стилизация CSS для документации и эталонных архитектур, особенно для тех, кто работает с Terraform, AWS, Datadog и GitHub Actions.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق موحد لغة CSS للوثائق وهندسة المراجع، ولا سيما أولئك الذين يعملون مع Terraform و AWS و Datadog و GitHub Actions."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to consistently apply a defined color palette and CSS styles, such as primary blue, hover states, and active states, directly utilizing variables like `--ifm-color-primary` and `--ifm-background-color` in their documentation generation, ensuring visual cohesion across docs.cloudposse.com.","zh":"赋予代理应用一致的颜色调色板和CSS样式的能力，例如主要蓝色、悬停状态和活动状态，直接在文档生成中使用诸如`--ifm-color-primary`和`--ifm-background-color`的变量，确保docs.cloudposse.com上的文档在视觉上的一致性。","ja":"エージェントに一貫した色のパレットとCSSスタイル、たとえばプライマリーブルー、ホバーステート、アクティブステートを適用する能力を付与し、`--ifm-color-primary`と`--ifm-background-color`などの変数を直接文書生成に利用し、docs.cloudposse.comの文書に視覚的一貫性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 일관된 색상 팔레트와 CSS 스타일, 예를 들어 주색, 호버 상태 및 활성 상태를 적용할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 `--ifm-color-primary` 및 `--ifm-background-color`와 같은 변수를 직접 문서 생성에 사용함으로써 docs.cloudposse.com의 문서에 대한 시각적 일관성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar de forma consistente una paleta de colores definida y estilos CSS, como azul primario, estados de desplazamiento y estados activos, utilizando directamente variables como `--ifm-color-primary` y `--ifm-background-color` en la generación de documentación, garantizando la cohesión visual en toda la documentación de docs.cloudposse.com.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer de manière cohérente une palette de couleurs définie et des styles CSS, tels que le bleu principal, les états de survol et les états actifs, en utilisant directement des variables comme `--ifm-color-primary` et `--ifm-background-color` dans la génération de documentation, assurant ainsi une cohérence visuelle à travers tout docs.cloudposse.com.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, eine definierte Farbpalette und CSS-Stile, wie primäres Blau, Hover-Zustände und aktive Zustände, konsistent anzuwenden, indem sie direkt Variablen wie `--ifm-color-primary` und `--ifm-background-color` in der Dokumentenerstellung verwenden, was eine visuelle Kohärenz über die gesamte Dokumentation von docs.cloudposse.com gewährleistet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar consistentemente uma paleta de cores definida e estilos CSS, como azul primário, estados de hover e estados ativos, utilizando diretamente variáveis como `--ifm-color-primary` e `--ifm-background-color` na geração de documentação, garantindo coesão visual em todo o docs.cloudposse.com.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью последовательно применять определённую цветовую палитру и стили CSS, такие как основной синий, состояния наведения и активные состояния, напрямую используя переменные как `--ifm-color-primary` и `--ifm-background-color` при генерации документации, обеспечивая визуальную сплочённость на всем сайте docs.cloudposse.com.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تطبيق لون موحد ومحدد وأسلوب CSS، مثل الأزرق الأساسي وحالات التمرير والحالات النشطة، باستخدام متغيرات مثل `--ifm-color-primary` و `--ifm-background-color` مباشرة في توليد الوثائق، مما يضمن الاتساق المرئي عبر docs.cloudposse.com."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing documentation themes across multiple projects","Automating CSS style application for Terraform reference architectures","Generating consistent color schemes for AWS and Datadog integrations"],"zh":["跨多个项目标准化文档主题","自动应用Terraform参考架构的CSS样式","为AWS和Datadog集成生成一致的颜色方案"],"ja":["複数のプロジェクトにわたるドキュメントのテーマを標準化する","TerraformのリファレンスアーキテクチャのCSSスタイルを自動的に適用する","AWSとDatadogの統合のための一貫した色のスキームを生成する"],"ko":["다수의 프로젝트에 걸친 문서 테마를 표준화하는 것","Terraform 참조 아키텍처의 CSS 스타일 자동 적용","AWS 및 Datadog 통합을 위한 일관된 색상 스키마 생성"],"es":["Estandarizar temas de documentación en varios proyectos","Automatizar la aplicación de estilos CSS para arquitecturas de referencia de Terraform","Generar esquemas de colores coherentes para integraciones de AWS y Datadog"],"fr":["Standardiser les thèmes de documentation sur plusieurs projets","Automatiser l''application des styles CSS pour les architectures de référence de Terraform","Générer des schémas de couleurs cohérents pour les intégrations AWS et Datadog"],"de":["Dokumentationsthemen über mehrere Projekte hinweg standardisieren","Automatisierung der CSS-Stil-Anwendung für Terraform-Referenzarchitekturen","Erzeugen konsistenter Farbschemata für AWS- und Datadog-Integrationen"],"pt":["Padronizar temas de documentação em vários projetos","Automatizar a aplicação de estilos CSS para arquiteturas de referência do Terraform","Gerar esquemas de cores consistentes para integrações do AWS e Datadog"],"ru":["Стандартизировать темы документации в нескольких проектах","Автоматизировать применение стилей CSS для эталонных архитектур Terraform","Генерировать последовательные цветовые схемы для интеграций AWS и Datadog"],"ar":["موحدات مواضيع الوثائق عبر عدة مشاريع","توفير تطبيق أسلوب CSS آلي لمعماريات مرجعية Terraform","إنتاج مخططات ألوان متسقة للتكاملات من AWS و Datadog"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to CSS customization files like `src/css/custom.css`","Limited to documentation styling, not applicable for general web development"],"zh":["需要访问CSS自定义文件，如`src/css/custom.css`","仅限于文档样式，不适用于一般的Web开发"],"ja":["CSSのカスタマイズファイル、たとえば`src/css/custom.css`へのアクセスが必要","ドキュメントのスタイリングにのみ限定され、一般的なWeb開発には適用されない"],"ko":["CSS 사용자 정의 파일인 `src/css/custom.css`에 대한 액세스가 필요함","문서 스타일링에만 한정되어 일반적인 웹 개발에는 적용되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de personalización de CSS como `src/css/custom.css`","Limitado a la estilización de documentación, no aplicable para el desarrollo web general"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à des fichiers de personnalisation de CSS tels que `src/css/custom.css`","Limité à la personnalisation de la documentation, non applicable pour le développement web général"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf CSS-Anpassungsdateien wie `src/css/custom.css`","Begrenzt auf die Stilisisierung von Dokumentationen, nicht anwendbar für die allgemeine Webentwicklung"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de personalização de CSS como `src/css/custom.css`","Limitado à estilização de documentação, não se aplica ao desenvolvimento web geral"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам настройки CSS, таким как `src/css/custom.css`","Ограничен стилизацией документации, не применимо для общего веб-разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات تخصيص لغة CSS مثل `src/css/custom.css`","محدود bằngestyling الوثائق، لا ينطبق على تطوير الويب العام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('llama-farm/llamafarm/fix-ci', 'community', 'llama-farm', 'llamafarm', 'llama-farm/llamafarm', 'fix-ci', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T02:58:05.726Z', NULL, '{"id":"llama-farm/llamafarm/fix-ci","name":"fix-ci","description":{"zh":"Fix CI技能自动化CI故障排除，通过获取GitHub Actions失败日志，分析问题并创建解决计划","ja":"Fix CIスキルは、CIトラブルシューティングを自動化することで、GitHub Actionsの失敗ログを取得し、問題を分析して解決計画を作成します","ko":"Fix CI 기술은 CI 문제를 자동으로 해결하며 GitHub Actions 실패 로그를 가져와 문제를 분석하고 해결 계획을 생성합니다","es":"Fix CI es una habilidad que automatiza la resolución de problemas de CI. Permite deployar modelos AI, agentes y bases de datos de forma local o remota en minutos.","fr":"Fix CI est une compétence qui automatise la résolution des problèmes de CI. Elle permet de déployer des modèles AI, des agents et des bases de données de manière locale ou distante en quelques minutes.","de":"Fix CI ist eine Fähigkeit, die die Fehlerbehebung von CI automatisiert. Sie ermöglicht die Bereitstellung von AI-Modellen, Agenten und Datenbanken lokal oder remote in Minuten.","pt":"O Fix CI é uma habilidade que automatiza a solução de problemas de integração contínua, detectando falhas no GitHub Actions e criando planos de solução.","ru":"Fix CI — это навык, который автоматизирует решение проблем непрерывной интеграции, обнаруживая сбои в GitHub Actions и создавая планы решения.","ar":"Fix CI هو مهارة يأتمتة حل مشاكل التكامل المستمر، ويكتشف الأعطال في GitHub Actions وينشئ خطط الحل.","en":"Deploy any AI model, agent, database, RAG, and pipeline locally or remotely in minutes"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Fix CI技能：自动化CI故障排除","ja":"Fix CIスキル：CIトラブルシューティングの自動化","ko":"Fix CI 기술: CI 문제 자동 해결","es":"Soluciona CI: Deploy de modelos AI en minutos","fr":"Fix CI : Déployez des modèles AI en quelques minutes","de":"Fix CI: AI-Modelle in Minuten bereitstellen","pt":"Fix CI: Automatize Solução de Problemas de Integração Con...","ru":"Fix CI: Автоматизация устранения неполадок в непрерывной ...","ar":"Fix CI: أتمتة حل مشاكل التكامل المستمر","en":"fix-ci"},"description":{"zh":"Fix CI技能自动化CI故障排除，通过获取GitHub Actions失败日志，分析问题并创建解决计划","ja":"Fix CIスキルは、CIトラブルシューティングを自動化することで、GitHub Actionsの失敗ログを取得し、問題を分析して解決計画を作成します","ko":"Fix CI 기술은 CI 문제를 자동으로 해결하며 GitHub Actions 실패 로그를 가져와 문제를 분석하고 해결 계획을 생성합니다","es":"Fix CI es una habilidad que automatiza la resolución de problemas de CI. Permite deployar modelos AI, agentes y bases de datos de forma local o remota en min...","fr":"Fix CI est une compétence qui automatise la résolution des problèmes de CI. Elle permet de déployer des modèles AI, des agents et des bases de données de man...","de":"Fix CI ist eine Fähigkeit, die die Fehlerbehebung von CI automatisiert. Sie ermöglicht die Bereitstellung von AI-Modellen, Agenten und Datenbanken lokal oder...","pt":"O Fix CI é uma habilidade que automatiza a solução de problemas de integração contínua, detectando falhas no GitHub Actions e criando planos de solução.","ru":"Fix CI — это навык, который автоматизирует решение проблем непрерывной интеграции, обнаруживая сбои в GitHub Actions и создавая планы решения.","ar":"Fix CI هو مهارة يأتمتة حل مشاكل التكامل المستمر، ويكتشف الأعطال في GitHub Actions وينشئ خطط الحل.","en":"Deploy any AI model, agent, database, RAG, and pipeline locally or remotely in minutes"},"definition":{"en":"Deploy any AI model, agent, database, RAG, and pipeline locally or remotely in minutes"},"features":{"zh":["自动化CI故障排除","获取GitHub Actions失败日志","分析问题并创建解决计划","支持本地和远程部署","提高开发效率"],"ja":["CIトラブルシューティングの自動化","GitHub Actionsの失敗ログの取得","問題の分析と解決計画の作成","ローカルとリモートの両方のデプロイをサポート","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["CI 문제 자동 해결","GitHub Actions 실패 로그 가져오기","문제 분석 및 해결 계획 생성","로컬 및 리모트 배포 지원","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Deploy de modelos AI en minutos","Resolución automática de problemas de CI","Compatibilidad con GitHub Actions","Análisis de registros y reproducción de errores","Creación de un plan de solución para la aprobación del usuario"],"fr":["Déployez des modèles AI en quelques minutes","Résolution automatique des problèmes de CI","Compatibilité avec GitHub Actions","Analyse des journaux et reproduction des erreurs","Création d''un plan de solution pour l''approbation de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Bereitstellung von AI-Modellen in Minuten","Automatische Fehlerbehebung von CI","Kompatibilität mit GitHub Actions","Analyse von Protokollen und Wiederholung von Fehlern","Erstellung eines Lösungsplans für die Benutzerfreigabe"],"pt":["Automação de solução de problemas de integração contínua","Detecção de falhas no GitHub Actions","Criação de planos de solução personalizados","Integração com GitHub CLI","Suporte à execução local e remota"],"ru":["Автоматизация решения проблем непрерывной интеграции","Обнаружение сбоев в GitHub Actions","Создание индивидуальных планов решения","Интеграция с GitHub CLI","Поддержка локального и удаленного выполнения"],"ar":["أتمتة حل مشاكل التكامل المستمر","اكتشاف الأعطال في GitHub Actions","إنشاء خطط حل مخصصة","التكامل مع GitHub CLI","دعم التنفيذ المحلي والعن بعد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CI故障排除","自动化CI","GitHub Actions","开发效率","CI问题解决","自动化测试"],"ja":["CIトラブルシューティング","自動化CI","GitHub Actions","開発効率","CI問題解決","自動化テスト"],"ko":["CI 문제 해결","自動化 CI","GitHub Actions","개발 효율성","CI 문제 자동 해결","自動化 테스트"],"es":["Fix CI","Integración Continua","Modelos AI","GitHub Actions","Resolución de problemas","Deploy de modelos","Automatización de CI","Desarrollo de software","Herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Fix CI","Intégration Continue","Modèles AI","GitHub Actions","Résolution de problèmes","Déployez des modèles","Automatisation de CI","Développement de logiciels","Outils de développement"],"de":["Fix CI","Continuous Integration","AI-Modelle","GitHub Actions","Fehlerbehebung","Bereitstellung von Modellen","Automatisierung von CI","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklertools"],"pt":["integração contínua","GitHub Actions","automação de solução de problemas","Fix CI","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["непрерывная интеграция","GitHub Actions","автоматизация решения проблем","Fix CI","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التكامل المستمر","GitHub Actions","أتمتة حل المشاكل","Fix CI","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"llama-farm","repo":"llamafarm","repoPath":"llama-farm/llamafarm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix-ci","description":"Fetch GitHub CI failure information, analyze root causes, reproduce locally, and propose a fix plan. Use `/fix-ci` for current branch or `/fix-ci <run-id>` for a specific run.","bodyPreview":"# Fix CI Skill\n\nAutomates CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan for user approval.\n\n---\n\n## Execution Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Prerequisites Check\n\nVerify the GitHub CLI is installed and authenticated:\n\n```bash\ngh --version && gh auth status\n```\n\n**If gh is not installed:**\n- Inform user: \"GitHub CLI is required. Install with: `brew install gh`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n**If not authenticated:**\n- Inform user: \"Please a","body":"# Fix CI Skill\n\nAutomates CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan for user approval.\n\n---\n\n## Execution Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Prerequisites Check\n\nVerify the GitHub CLI is installed and authenticated:\n\n```bash\ngh --version && gh auth status\n```\n\n**If gh is not installed:**\n- Inform user: \"GitHub CLI is required. Install with: `brew install gh`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n**If not authenticated:**\n- Inform user: \"Please authenticate with: `gh auth login`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n### Step 2: Parse Arguments\n\nDetermine the mode based on arguments:\n\n- **No arguments** (`/fix-ci`): Fetch failures for the current branch only\n- **With run-id** (`/fix-ci <run-id>`): Fetch specific run (bypasses branch scoping)\n\n### Step 3: Fetch Failed Run\n\n**Default mode (current branch):**\n\n```bash\nBRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\ngh run list --branch \"$BRANCH\" --status failure --limit 1 --json databaseId,name,headBranch,workflowName,createdAt\n```\n\n**Specific run mode:**\n\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --json databaseId,name,headBranch,workflowName,jobs,conclusion\n```\n\n**If no failures found:**\n- Report: \"No failed runs found for branch `$BRANCH`. CI is green!\"\n- Optionally show recent successful runs:\n```bash\ngh run list --branch \"$BRANCH\" --limit 3 --json databaseId,conclusion,workflowName,createdAt\n```\n- Exit gracefully\n\n### Step 4: Get Failure Details\n\nOnce a failed run is identified, gather comprehensive details:\n\n```bash\nRUN_ID=<the-run-id>\n\n# Get failed jobs with their steps\ngh run view $RUN_ID --json jobs --jq ''.jobs[] | select(.conclusion == \"failure\") | {name, conclusion, steps: [.steps[] | select(.conclusion == \"failure\")]}''\n\n# Get failed step logs (critical for debugging)\ngh run view $RUN_ID --log-failed 2>&1 | head -500\n\n# Get verbose run info\ngh run view $RUN_ID --verbose\n```\n\n**Log handling:**\n- Truncate logs to 500 lines to avoid context overflow\n- Note to user: \"Showing first 500 lines of failed logs. Full logs available on GitHub.\"\n\n### Step 5: Download Artifacts (if available)\n\nAttempt to download any debug artifacts:\n\n```bash\n# Try common artifact names - failures are OK (not all runs have artifacts)\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"coverage\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"test-results\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"logs\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\n```\n\nIf artifacts downloaded, read them for additional context.\n\n### Step 6: Analyze Failure Type\n\nCategorize the failure based on log patterns:\n\n| Pattern | Failure Type | Root Cause Area |\n|---------|--------------|-----------------|\n| `FAIL:`, `--- FAIL`, `FAILED` | Test Failure | Specific test case |\n| `ruff check`, `ruff format` | Lint Error | Code style/formatting |\n| `ModuleNotFoundError`, `ImportError` | Import Error | Missing dependency |\n| `TypeError`, `AttributeError` | Runtime Error | Type mismatch |\n| `SyntaxError` | Syntax Error | Invalid code |\n| `AssertionError` | Assertion Failure | Test expectation mismatch |\n| `TimeoutError`, `timed out` | Timeout | Performance/hang |\n| `PermissionError`, `EACCES` | Permission Error | File/resource access |\n| `ConnectionError`, `ECONNREFUSED` | Network Error | External service |\n\nExtract key information:\n- Failed test name/file (if applicable)\n- Error message\n- Stack trace location (file:line)\n- Environment variables or config issues\n\n### Step 7: Map to Local Test Commands\n\nDetermine the appropriate local command based on the CI job:\n\n| CI Workflow/Job | Local Command |\n|-----------------|---------------|\n| `test-cli` | `cd cli && go test ./...` |\n| `test-python` (server) | `cd server && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (rag) | `cd rag && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (config) | `cd config && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (runtime) | `cd runtimes/universal && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `lint` (python) | `uv run ruff check .` |\n| `lint` (go) | `cd cli && golangci-lint run` |\n| `type-check` | `uv run mypy .` |\n| `build-cli` | `nx build cli` |\n| `build-designer` | `cd designer && npm run build` |\n\n**For specific test failures**, narrow down the command:\n- Python: `cd <dir> && uv run pytest -v <test_file>::<test_name>`\n- Go: `cd cli && go test -v -run <TestName> ./...`\n\n### Step 8: Reproduce Locally\n\nRun the mapped local command to confirm the failure reproduces:\n\n```bash\n# Example for Python test\ncd server && uv run pytest -v tests/test_api.py::test_health_check\n```\n\n**Outcome A - Failure reproduces locally:**\n- Good! Continue to fix plan\n- Report: \"Successfully reproduced failure locally\"\n\n**Outcome B - Failure does NOT reproduce locally:**\n- Note: \"Could not reproduce locally. Possible causes:\"\n  - Flaky test (timing-dependent)\n  - Environment difference (CI has different deps/config)\n  - Race condition\n- Suggest: \"Consider re-running CI with `gh run rerun $RUN_ID`\"\n- Ask user how to proceed (investigate further or skip)\n\n### Step 9: Analyze Root Cause\n\nBased on the failure type and logs, identify:\n\n1. **What failed**: Specific test, lint rule, or build step\n2. **Why it failed**: The actual error condition\n3. **Where to fix**: File(s) and line(s) that need changes\n4. **How to fix**: Proposed changes\n\nUse available tools to explore:\n- Read the failing test file\n- Read the code being tested\n- Search for related patterns in the codebase\n- Check recent changes that might have caused the failure\n\n### Step 10: Enter Plan Mode\n\nUse `EnterPlanMode` to create a formal fix plan. The plan should include:\n\n```markdown\n# CI Fix Plan\n\n## Problem Statement\n[Summary of the CI failure from logs]\n\n## Failure Details\n- **Run ID**: <run-id>\n- **Workflow**: <workflow-name>\n- **Job**: <job-name>\n- **Error Type**: <categorized-type>\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n[Explanation of why the failure occurred]\n\n## Affected Files\n- `path/to/file1.py` (line X)\n- `path/to/file2.py` (line Y)\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Change 1: [Brief description]\n[Specific edit to make]\n\n### Change 2: [Brief description]\n[Specific edit to make]\n\n## Verification Steps\n1. Run: `<local-test-command>`\n2. Expected: All tests pass\n3. Optional: Run full test suite with `<full-suite-command>`\n\n## Notes\n- [Any caveats or considerations]\n```\n\n### Step 11: User Approval Gate\n\nPresent the plan and wait for explicit user approval:\n- User approves: Proceed to execute fixes\n- User modifies: Incorporate feedback, update plan\n- User rejects: Exit gracefully without changes\n\n**CRITICAL**: Never make code changes without user approval.\n\n### Step 12: Execute Fix (after approval only)\n\n1. Make the proposed code changes using Edit tool\n2. Run local tests to verify the fix:\n```bash\n<local-test-command>\n```\n3. Report results:\n   - Success: \"Fix verified locally. Tests pass.\"\n   - Failure: \"Fix did not resolve the issue. [details]\"\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT auto-commit changes. Leave committing to the user or `/commit-push-pr` skill.\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Scenario | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| gh CLI not installed | Direct user to install: `brew install gh` |\n| gh not authenticated | Direct user to: `gh auth login` |\n| No failures found | Report CI is green, exit gracefully |\n| Rate limit exceeded | Suggest waiting or using `gh auth refresh` |\n| Run not found | Verify run ID, suggest `gh run list` to find valid IDs |\n| Large logs (>500 lines) | Truncate, note full logs on GitHub |\n| Local reproduction fails | Note as flaky/env issue, offer re-run option |\n| Network errors | Suggest retry, check connection |\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n**On finding a failure:**\n```\nCI Failure Found\nRun: #12345 (workflow-name)\nBranch: feature-branch\nFailed Job: test-python\nError Type: Test Failure\n\nAnalyzing logs...\n[Summary of failure]\n\nReproducing locally...\n[Result]\n\nEntering plan mode to propose fix...\n```\n\n**On success (after fix):**\n```\nFix Applied\n- Modified: path/to/file.py\n- Verification: Tests pass locally\n\nNext steps:\n- Review the changes\n- Run `/commit-push-pr` to commit and push\n- CI will re-run automatically on push\n```\n\n---\n\n## Notes for the Agent\n\n1. **Always scope to current branch by default** - Users expect `/fix-ci` to fix their current work, not random failures\n2. **Truncate logs wisely** - CI logs can be huge; extract the relevant error sections\n3. **Reproduce before fixing** - Don''t propose fixes for issues that can''t be reproduced\n4. **Plan mode is mandatory** - Always use EnterPlanMode before making changes\n5. **Never auto-commit** - The user controls when changes are committed\n6. **Be specific in analysis** - Generic advice isn''t helpful; identify exact files and lines\n7. **Handle flaky tests** - If reproduction fails, acknowledge it might be flaky\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:58:05.726Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing automated CI troubleshooting and GitHub Actions failure analysis.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化CI故障排除和GitHub Actions故障分析的DevOps代理。","ja":"DevOpsエージェントが自動化されたCIのトラブルシューティングとGitHub Actionsの故障分析を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 CI 문제 해결 및 GitHub Actions 오류 분석이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan solucionar problemas de CI automatizados y análisis de fallos de GitHub Actions.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin d''une résolution automatique des problèmes de CI et d''analyse des échecs de GitHub Actions.","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die eine automatisierte CI-Fehlerbehebung und eine Analyse von GitHub-Actions-Fehlern benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes DevOps que necessitam de solução de problemas de CI automatizados e análise de falhas de GitHub Actions.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым необходима автоматизированная устранение неполадок CI и анализ сбоев GitHub Actions.","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذي يحتاج إلى تشخيص العيوب التلقائي ل CI وتحليل فشل إجراءات GitHub."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan using GitHub CLI and authentication protocols like gh auth status.","zh":"赋予代理自动化CI故障排除的能力，通过获取GitHub Actions故障，分析日志，在本地重现问题，并使用GitHub CLI和身份验证协议（如gh auth status）创建修复计划。","ja":"エージェントにCIのトラブルシューティングを自動化する力を与え、GitHub Actionsの故障を取得し、ログを分析し、ローカルで問題を再現し、GitHub CLIと認証プロトコル（gh auth statusなど）を使用して修復計画を作成します。","ko":"에이전트가 CI 문제 해결을 자동화할 수 있도록 해주며, GitHub Actions 오류를 가져와 로그를 분석하고 로컬에서 문제를 재현하며, GitHub CLI 및 인증 프로토콜(예: gh auth status)을 사용하여 수정 계획을 생성합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes automatizar la solución de problemas de CI al recuperar los fallos de GitHub Actions, analizar los registros, reproducir los problemas de forma local y crear un plan de solución utilizando GitHub CLI y protocolos de autenticación como gh auth status.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser la résolution des problèmes de CI en récupérant les échecs de GitHub Actions, en analysant les journaux, en reproduisant les problèmes localement et en créant un plan de correction à l''aide de GitHub CLI et de protocoles d''authentification tels que gh auth status.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, die Fehlerbehebung von CI zu automatisieren, indem GitHub-Actions-Fehler abgerufen, Protokolle analysiert, Probleme lokal reproduziert und ein Behebungsplan mithilfe von GitHub CLI und Authentifizierungsprotokollen wie gh auth status erstellt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a solução de problemas de CI, buscando falhas de GitHub Actions, analisando logs, reproduzindo problemas localmente e criando um plano de solução usando GitHub CLI e protocolos de autenticação como gh auth status.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать устранение неполадок CI, получая сбои GitHub Actions, анализируя журналы, воспроизводя проблемы локально и создавая план исправления с помощью GitHub CLI и протоколов аутентификации, таких как gh auth status.","ar":"يمكّن الوكيل من توفير تشخيص عيوب CI التلقائي من خلال استرجاع فشل إجراءات GitHub، و تحليل السجلات، و إعادة إنتاج المشكلات محليًا، و创建 خطة إصلاح باستخدام GitHub CLI وبروتوكولات المصادقة مثل حالة المصادقة gh."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating CI failure analysis","Reproducing GitHub Actions issues locally","Generating fix plans for user approval"],"zh":["自动化CI故障分析","在本地重现GitHub Actions问题","为用户生成修复计划"],"ja":["CIの故障分析の自動化","GitHub Actionsの問題のローカルでの再現","ユーザー承認用の修復計画の生成"],"ko":["CI 오류 분석 자동화","GitHub Actions 문제를 로컬에서 재현","사용자 승인용 수정 계획 생성"],"es":["Automatización del análisis de fallos de CI","Reproducción de problemas de GitHub Actions de forma local","Generación de planes de solución para la aprobación del usuario"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''analyse des échecs de CI","Reproduction des problèmes de GitHub Actions localement","Génération de plans de correction pour l''approbation de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Automatisierung der Analyse von CI-Fehlern","Lokale Reproduktion von GitHub-Actions-Problemen","Erstellung von Behebungsplänen für die Benutzerfreigabe"],"pt":["Automatizar análise de falha de CI","Reproduzir problemas de GitHub Actions localmente","Gerar planos de solução para aprovação do usuário"],"ru":["Автоматизировать анализ сбоев CI","Воспроизводить проблемы GitHub Actions локально","Генерировать планы исправления для одобрения пользователем"],"ar":["التشغيل الآلي لتحليل الفشل CI","إعادة إنتاج مشاكل GitHub Actions محليًا","توليد خطط الإصلاح للموافقة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub CLI installation","Needs authentication with GitHub via gh auth"],"zh":["需要安装GitHub CLI","需要通过gh auth与GitHub进行身份验证"],"ja":["GitHub CLIのインストールが必要","gh authを使用してGitHubとの認証が必要"],"ko":["GitHub CLI 설치가 필요","gh auth를 사용하여 GitHub와 인증이 필요"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de GitHub CLI","Necesita autenticación con GitHub a través de gh auth"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de GitHub CLI","Nécessite une authentification avec GitHub via gh auth"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von GitHub CLI","Benötigt eine Authentifizierung mit GitHub über gh auth"],"pt":["Requer instalação do GitHub CLI","Necessita autenticação com GitHub via gh auth"],"ru":["Требует安装 GitHub CLI","Требует аутентификации с GitHub через gh auth"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت GitHub CLI","يحتاج إلى مصادقة مع GitHub من خلال حالة المصادقة gh"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
