uild Tools.","de":"Tools zum Erstellen und Bearbeiten von Skyrim-Mods mit SKSE. Benötigt CMake und MSVC Build Tools.","pt":"O módulo SKSE fornece ferramentas para criar e gerenciar projetos de plugins C++ para Skyrim. Requisitos de compilação incluem CMake e MSVC.","ru":"Модуль SKSE предоставляет инструменты для создания и управления проектами плагинов C++ для Skyrim. Требования к сборке включают CMake и MSVC.","ar":"يوفر المكون الإضافي SKSE أدوات لإنشاء وإدارة مشاريع الإضافات C++ لSkyrim. تشمل متطلبات البناء CMake و MSVC.","en":"Tools to assist LLMs with creating and editing Skyrim mods."},"definition":{"en":"Tools to assist LLMs with creating and editing Skyrim mods."},"features":{"zh":["SKSE ","C++ ","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake 3.21+","MSVC ","Skyrim "],"ja":["SKSE","C++","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake 3.21+","MSVC","Skyrim"],"ko":["SKSE ","C++ ","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake 3.21+","MSVC ","Skyrim "],"es":["Creación de proyectos de plugins C++ para SKSE","Gestión de proyectos con Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Compatibilidad con CMake 3.21+","Requisitos de compilación con MSVC Build Tools","Herramientas para la edición de mods de Skyrim"],"fr":["Création de projets de plugins C++ pour SKSE","Gestion de projets avec Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Compatibilité avec CMake 3.21+","Exigences de compilation avec MSVC Build Tools","Outils pour l''édition de mods de Skyrim"],"de":["Erstellung von C++-Plugin-Projekten für SKSE","Projektverwaltung mit Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Kompatibilität mit CMake 3.21+","Build-Anforderungen mit MSVC Build Tools","Tools zum Bearbeiten von Skyrim-Mods"],"pt":["Crie e edite plugins C++ para Skyrim","Use o Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit para gerenciar projetos","Requisitos de compilação incluem CMake e MSVC","Desenvolva mods de Skyrim com facilidade","Extensão de scripts no jogo"],"ru":["Создавайте и редактируйте плагины C++ для Skyrim","Используйте Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit для управления проектами","Требования к сборке включают CMake и MSVC","Разрабатывайте моды Skyrim с легкостью","Расширение скриптов в игре"],"ar":["أنشئ وتحرر إضافات C++ لSkyrim","استخدم Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit لإدارة المشاريع","تشمل متطلبات البناء CMake و MSVC","طور تعديلات Skyrim بسهولة","امتداد البرامج النصية في اللعبة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Skyrim SKSE","SKSE ","C++ ","Skyrim ","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","Skyrim "],"ja":["Skyrim SKSE","SKSE","C++","Skyrim","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","Skyrim"],"ko":["Skyrim SKSE","SKSE ","C++ ","Skyrim ","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","Skyrim "],"es":["SKSE","Skyrim","mods","C++","CMake","MSVC Build Tools","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","desarrollo de mods","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["SKSE","Skyrim","mods","C++","CMake","MSVC Build Tools","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","développement de mods","outils de développement"],"de":["SKSE","Skyrim","Mods","C++","CMake","MSVC Build Tools","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Mod-Entwicklung","Entwicklertools"],"pt":["SKSE","Skyrim","mods","C++","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","desenvolvimento de mods","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["SKSE","Skyrim","моды","C++","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","разработка модов","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["SKSE","Skyrim","تعديلات","C++","Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","CMake","MSVC","تطوير التعديلات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"SpookyPirate","repo":"spookys-automod-toolkit","repoPath":"SpookyPirate/spookys-automod-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skyrim-skse","description":"Create and manage SKSE C++ plugin projects. Use when the user wants to create native plugins, add Papyrus native functions, or extend Skyrims functionality at the native level.","bodyPreview":"# Skyrim SKSE Module\n\nCreate and manage SKSE (Skyrim Script Extender) C++ plugin projects using Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nRun all commands from the toolkit directory:\n```bash\ncd \"<TOOLKIT_PATH>\"\n# Example: cd \"C:\\Tools\\spookys-automod-toolkit\"\n```\n\n### Build Requirements\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Building SKSE plugins requires:\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Installation |\n|------|---------|--------------|\n| **CMake 3.21+** | Build system | [Download](https://cmake.org/download/) |\n| **MSVC Build","body":"# Skyrim SKSE Module\n\nCreate and manage SKSE (Skyrim Script Extender) C++ plugin projects using Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nRun all commands from the toolkit directory:\n```bash\ncd \"<TOOLKIT_PATH>\"\n# Example: cd \"C:\\Tools\\spookys-automod-toolkit\"\n```\n\n### Build Requirements\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Building SKSE plugins requires:\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Installation |\n|------|---------|--------------|\n| **CMake 3.21+** | Build system | [Download](https://cmake.org/download/) |\n| **MSVC Build Tools** | C++ compiler | [MSVC Build Tools](https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/#build-tools-for-visual-studio-2022) |\n| vcpkg | Dependencies | Auto-bootstrapped by project |\n\n**Note:** You do NOT need the full Visual Studio IDE - only the MSVC Build Tools (C++ compiler). The Build Tools can be installed standalone without Visual Studio.\n\n## Overview\n\nSKSE plugins are DLL files that extend Skyrim''s functionality at a native level. This module generates project scaffolding using **CommonLibSSE-NG**, which supports Skyrim SE, AE, GOG, and VR from a single codebase.\n\n## Command Reference\n\n### List Available Templates\n```bash\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse templates\n```\n\n**Available Templates:**\n| Template | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `basic` | Minimal SKSE plugin with logging |\n| `papyrus-native` | Plugin with Papyrus native function support |\n\n### Create SKSE Project\n```bash\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse create \"<name>\" [options]\n```\n| Option | Default | Description |\n|--------|---------|-------------|\n| `--template` | `basic` | Template to use |\n| `--output` | `.` | Output directory |\n| `--author` | `Unknown` | Author name |\n| `--description` | - | Project description |\n\n### Get Project Info\n```bash\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse info \"<path>\"\n```\n| Option | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `<path>` | Project directory (default: current) |\n\n### Add Papyrus Native Function\n```bash\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse add-function \"<project>\" --name \"<name>\" [options]\n```\n| Option | Default | Description |\n|--------|---------|-------------|\n| `--name` | Required | Function name |\n| `--return` | `void` | Return type |\n| `--param` | - | Parameters (format: `type:name`, repeatable) |\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Create Basic SKSE Plugin\n```bash\n# 1. Create project\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse create \"MyPlugin\" --output \"./\" --author \"YourName\"\n\n# 2. Build (requires CMake and MSVC)\ncd MyPlugin\ncmake -B build -S .\ncmake --build build --config Release\n\n# Output: build/Release/MyPlugin.dll\n```\n\n### Create Plugin with Papyrus Functions\n```bash\n# 1. Create project with papyrus-native template\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse create \"MyNativePlugin\" --template papyrus-native --author \"YourName\" --output \"./\"\n\n# 2. Add custom functions\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse add-function \"./MyNativePlugin\" --name \"GetActorSpeed\" --return \"Float\" --param \"Actor:target\"\n\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse add-function \"./MyNativePlugin\" --name \"SetActorSpeed\" --return \"void\" --param \"Actor:target\" --param \"Float:speed\"\n\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse add-function \"./MyNativePlugin\" --name \"GetPluginVersion\" --return \"Int\"\n\n# 3. Build\ncd MyNativePlugin\ncmake -B build -S .\ncmake --build build --config Release\n```\n\n### Check Existing Project\n```bash\n# Get project info\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse info \"./MyPlugin\"\n```\n\n## Papyrus Type Mapping\n\n| Papyrus Type | C++ Type | Notes |\n|--------------|----------|-------|\n| Int | int | 32-bit integer |\n| Float | float | 32-bit float |\n| Bool | bool | Boolean |\n| String | std::string | Text string |\n| Actor | RE::Actor* | Actor reference |\n| ObjectReference | RE::TESObjectREFR* | Object reference |\n| Form | RE::TESForm* | Any form |\n\n### Function Parameter Format\n```\n--param \"Type:name\"\n```\n\nExamples:\n- `--param \"Actor:target\"` - Actor parameter named \"target\"\n- `--param \"Float:speed\"` - Float parameter named \"speed\"\n- `--param \"Int:count\"` - Integer parameter named \"count\"\n- `--param \"String:message\"` - String parameter named \"message\"\n\n## Generated Project Structure\n\n```\nMyPlugin/\n  CMakeLists.txt          # CMake build configuration\n  vcpkg.json              # C++ dependencies\n  skse_config.json        # Toolkit configuration\n  src/\n    main.cpp              # SKSE plugin entry point\n    plugin.cpp            # Plugin implementation\n    plugin.h              # Plugin header\n  cmake/\n    CommonLibSSE.cmake    # CommonLibSSE-NG integration\n```\n\n## Template Details\n\n### basic Template\nMinimal plugin with:\n- Modern C++20 plugin metadata (`.RuntimeCompatibility()`)\n- Precompiled headers (PCH) for fast builds\n- Comprehensive event handler examples (OnHit, OnEquip)\n- Safe NiPointer and Actor casting patterns\n- Correct form lookup methods (EditorID vs FormID)\n- Logging setup\n- Message handler for game events\n\n**Modern API Features:**\n```cpp\n// Modern plugin version declaration\nextern \"C\" __declspec(dllexport) constinit SKSE::PluginVersionData SKSEPlugin_Version = [] {\n    SKSE::PluginVersionData data{};\n    data.RuntimeCompatibility(SKSE::RuntimeCompatibility::Independent);\n    return data;\n}();\n\n// Safe NiPointer handling\nauto target = event->target.get();  // Get raw pointer\nauto actor = target->As<RE::Actor>();  // Safe cast\n\n// Correct form lookup\nauto form = RE::TESForm::LookupByEditorID(\"MyForm\"sv);  // By EditorID\nauto form = RE::TESForm::LookupByID(0x00012EB7);  // By FormID\n```\n\n**Build Options:**\n- VCPKG (automatic dependency management)\n- Manual vendor/ folder (no VCPKG required)\n- Windows CMD build script included (`build.bat`)\n\n### papyrus-native Template\nIncludes everything in `basic` plus:\n- Papyrus native function registration\n- Script interface\n- Example function\n\n```cpp\n// Register functions\nbool RegisterFunctions(RE::BSScript::IVirtualMachine* vm) {\n    vm->RegisterFunction(\"MyFunction\", \"MyScript\", MyFunction);\n    return true;\n}\n\n// Example native function\nint MyFunction(RE::StaticFunctionTag*) {\n    return 42;\n}\n```\n\n## Using Native Functions in Papyrus\n\nAfter building the plugin, call native functions from Papyrus:\n```papyrus\nScriptName MyScript\n\n; Declare native functions\nInt Function GetPluginVersion() global native\nFloat Function GetActorSpeed(Actor target) global native\nFunction SetActorSpeed(Actor target, Float speed) global native\n\n; Usage\nEvent OnInit()\n    Int version = GetPluginVersion()\n    Debug.Notification(\"Plugin version: \" + version)\n\n    Actor player = Game.GetPlayer()\n    Float speed = GetActorSpeed(player)\n    SetActorSpeed(player, speed * 1.5)\nEndEvent\n```\n\n## CommonLibSSE-NG\n\nThis toolkit uses **CommonLibSSE-NG** (Next Generation), which provides:\n\n- **Multi-version support**: Single DLL works on SE, AE, GOG, VR\n- **Address independence**: No hardcoded addresses\n- **Modern C++**: Uses C++20 features\n- **Complete API**: Covers most game functions\n\n### Supported Skyrim Versions\n| Version | Support |\n|---------|---------|\n| Skyrim SE 1.5.x | Full |\n| Skyrim SE 1.6.x (AE) | Full |\n| Skyrim GOG | Full |\n| Skyrim VR | Partial |\n\n## Building Projects\n\n### Standard Build\n```bash\ncd MyPlugin\ncmake -B build -S .\ncmake --build build --config Release\n```\n\n### Debug Build\n```bash\ncmake --build build --config Debug\n```\n\n### Clean Rebuild\n```bash\nrm -rf build\ncmake -B build -S .\ncmake --build build --config Release\n```\n\n### Output Location\n- Release: `build/Release/MyPlugin.dll`\n- Debug: `build/Debug/MyPlugin.dll`\n\n## Installing SKSE Plugins\n\n1. Copy DLL to `Data/SKSE/Plugins/`\n2. Copy any config files to same folder\n3. Launch game with SKSE loader\n\n## Limitations\n\nThis module **CAN**:\n- Generate project scaffolding\n- Add Papyrus native function stubs\n- Manage project configuration\n\nThis module **CANNOT**:\n- Write custom C++ logic\n- Compile projects (requires local build tools)\n- Debug plugins\n- Generate complex game hooks\n\nFor advanced SKSE development:\n- [CommonLibSSE-NG Wiki](https://github.com/CharmedBaryon/CommonLibSSE-NG/wiki)\n- [SKSE Plugin Development Guide](https://www.creationkit.com/index.php?title=Category:SKSE)\n\n## Important Notes\n\n1. **Build tools required** - CMake and MSVC Build Tools needed (NOT full Visual Studio IDE)\n2. **Single codebase, all versions** - CommonLibSSE-NG handles version differences\n3. **vcpkg auto-bootstraps** - Dependencies downloaded on first build (~5 minutes first time)\n4. **Native functions need matching Papyrus declarations** - Script must declare functions as `native`\n5. **Use `--json` flag** for machine-readable output when scripting\n6. **LLMs can build plugins** - Use Bash tool to invoke CMake commands for end-to-end workflow\n\n## JSON Output\n\nAll commands support `--json` for structured output:\n```bash\ndotnet run --project src/SpookysAutomod.Cli -- skse info \"./MyPlugin\" --json\n```\n\nExample response:\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"result\": {\n    \"name\": \"MyPlugin\",\n    \"author\": \"YourName\",\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"template\": \"papyrus-native\",\n    \"description\": \"My SKSE Plugin\",\n    \"targetVersions\": [\"SE\", \"AE\"],\n    \"papyrusFunctions\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"GetActorSpeed\",\n        \"returnType\": \"Float\",\n        \"parameters\": [\n          { \"type\": \"Actor\", \"name\": \"target\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:59:20.034Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Gaming Agents focused on Skyrim mod development needing C++ plugin management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合专注于上古卷轴模组开发并需要C++插件管理能力的游戏代理。","ja":"Skyrimモッド開発に焦点を当て、C++プラグイン管理機能を必要とするゲームエージェントに最適。","ko":"스카이림 모드 개발에 중점을 둔 게임 에이전트에게 적합하며, C++ 플러그인 관리 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de juego centrados en el desarrollo de mods de Skyrim que necesitan capacidades de administración de plugins de C++.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de jeu axés sur le développement de mods Skyrim nécessitant des capacités de gestion de plugins C++.","de":"Perfekt für Gaming-Agents, die auf Skyrim-Mod-Entwicklung mit C++-Plugin-Management-Funktionen fokussiert sind.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de jogos focados no desenvolvimento de mods do Skyrim que necessitam de capacidades de gerenciamento de plugins em C++.","ru":"Идеально подходит для игровых агентов, ориентированных на разработку модов Skyrim, требующих возможностей управления плагинами C++.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يركزون على تطوير mods Skyrim والذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات إدارة الإضافات C++."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage SKSE plugins using Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit, leveraging CMake 3.21+ for build system management and MSVC for compilation, while working with Skyrim Script Extender projects.","zh":"赋予代理创建和管理SKSE插件的能力，利用Spooky的AutoMod Toolkit，并使用CMake 3.21+进行构建系统管理，使用MSVC进行编译，同时处理Skyrim Script Extender项目。","ja":"エージェントがSKSEプラグインを作成・管理できるようにし、SpookyのAutoMod Toolkitを利用し、CMake 3.21+でビルドシステムを管理し、MSVCでコンパイルを行い、Skyrim Script Extenderプロジェクトで作業する。","ko":"에이전트가 SKSE 플러그인을 생성하고 관리할 수 있도록하며, Spooky의 AutoMod Toolkit을 사용하고, CMake 3.21+를 사용하여 빌드 시스템을 관리하며, MSVC로 컴파일을 수행하며, 스카이림 스크립트 확장자 프로젝트에서 작업합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y administrar plugins de SKSE utilizando el kit de herramientas AutoMod de Spooky, aprovechando CMake 3.21+ para la administración del sistema de compilación y MSVC para la compilación, mientras trabaja con proyectos de Skyrim Script Extender.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des plugins SKSE en utilisant le kit d''outils AutoMod de Spooky, en exploitant CMake 3.21+ pour la gestion du système de build et MSVC pour la compilation, tout en travaillant sur des projets d''extension de script Skyrim.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, SKSE-Plugins mit dem Spooky-AutoMod-Toolkit zu erstellen und zu verwalten, indem CMake 3.21+ für die Build-System-Verwaltung und MSVC für die Kompilierung genutzt wird, während an Skyrim-Script-Extender-Projekten gearbeitet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e gerenciar plugins SKSE usando a Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit, aproveitando o CMake 3.21+ para gerenciamento do sistema de build e o MSVC para compilação, enquanto trabalham com projetos do Skyrim Script Extender.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и управлять плагинами SKSE, используя Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit, используя CMake 3.21+ для управления системой сборки и MSVC для компиляции, работая с проектами Skyrim Script Extender.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء وإدارة الإضافات SKSE باستخدام Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit، واستخدام CMake 3.21+ لإدارة نظام البناء وMSVC للترجمة، أثناء العمل على مشاريع Skyrim Script Extender."},"useCases":{"en":["Building custom SKSE plugins","Managing Skyrim mod projects with Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Debugging C++ code for Skyrim mods"],"zh":["构建自定义SKSE插件","使用Spooky的AutoMod Toolkit管理Skyrim模组项目","调试Skyrim模组的C++代码"],"ja":["カスタムSKSEプラグインの構築","SpookyのAutoMod Toolkitを使用したSkyrimモッドプロジェクトの管理","SkyrimモッドのC++コードのデバッグ"],"ko":["사용자 정의 SKSE 플러그인 빌드","Spooky의 AutoMod Toolkit을 사용한 스카이림 모드 프로젝트 관리","스카이림 모드의 C++ 코드 디버깅"],"es":["Creación de plugins de SKSE personalizados","Administración de proyectos de mods de Skyrim con el kit de herramientas AutoMod de Spooky","Depuración de código C++ para mods de Skyrim"],"fr":["Création de plugins SKSE personnalisés","Gestion de projets de mods Skyrim avec le kit d''outils AutoMod de Spooky","Débogage de code C++ pour les mods Skyrim"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter SKSE-Plugins","Verwaltung von Skyrim-Mod-Projekten mit dem Spooky-AutoMod-Toolkit","Fehlerbehebung von C++-Code für Skyrim-Mods"],"pt":["Construção de plugins SKSE personalizados","Gerenciamento de projetos de mods do Skyrim com a Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Depuração de código C++ para mods do Skyrim"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских плагинов SKSE","Управление проектами модов Skyrim с помощью Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","Отладка кода C++ для модов Skyrim"],"ar":["إنشاء إضافات SKSE مخصصة","إدارة مشاريع mods Skyrim باستخدام Spooky''s AutoMod Toolkit","تصحيح أخطاء في كود C++ لمودس Skyrim"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CMake 3.21+ installation","Needs MSVC build tools","Limited to Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE) plugin development"],"zh":["需要CMake 3.21+安装","需要MSVC构建工具","仅限Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)插件开发"],"ja":["CMake 3.21+のインストールが必要","MSVCビルドツールが必要","Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)プラグイン開発のみ"],"ko":["CMake 3.21+ 설치가 필요합니다.","MSVC 빌드 도구가 필요합니다.","스카이림 스크립트 확장자 (SKSE) 플러그인 개발만 가능"],"es":["Requiere instalación de CMake 3.21+","Necesita herramientas de compilación de MSVC","Limitado al desarrollo de plugins de Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de CMake 3.21+","A besoin d''outils de build MSVC","Limité au développement de plugins d''extension de script Skyrim (SKSE)"],"de":["Benötigt CMake 3.21+-Installation","Benötigt MSVC-Build-Tools","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Skyrim-Script-Extender-(SKSE)-Plugins"],"pt":["Requer instalação do CMake 3.21+","Necessita de ferramentas de build do MSVC","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de plugins do Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)"],"ru":["Требует установку CMake 3.21+","Требует инструментов сборки MSVC","Ограничен разработкой плагинов Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت CMake 3.21+","يحتاج إلى أدوات بناء MSVC","محدود بتطوير إضافات Skyrim Script Extender (SKSE)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Gerstep/cybos/gtd', 'community', 'Gerstep', 'cybos', 'Gerstep/cybos', 'gtd', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T02:59:43.896Z', NULL, '{"id":"Gerstep/cybos/gtd","name":"gtd","description":{"zh":"GTD Runner Skill 实现了从 GTD.md 项到自动任务执行的工作流","ja":"GTD Runner Skill は、GTD.md 項目から自動タスク実行までのワークフローを実現","ko":"GTD Runner Skill은 GTD.md 항목에서 자동 작업 실행까지의 워크플ロー를 구현합니다","es":"GTD Runner es una habilidad que ejecuta tareas de forma autónoma a partir de elementos de GTD.md, clasificándolos y planificando acciones para mejorar la productividad","fr":"GTD Runner est une compétence qui exécute des tâches de manière autonome à partir d''éléments de GTD.md, les classifiant et planifiant des actions pour améliorer la productivité","de":"GTD Runner ist eine Fähigkeit, die Aufgaben automatisch aus GTD.md-Elementen ausführt, sie klassifiziert und Aktionen plant, um die Produktivität zu steigern","pt":"O GTD Runner é uma ferramenta que executa tarefas de forma autônoma a partir de itens do GTD.md. Ele classifica e planeja ações para execução.","ru":"GTD Runner - это инструмент, который выполняет задачи автоматически из элементов GTD.md. Он классифицирует и планирует действия для выполнения.","ar":"GTD Runner هو أداة تقوم بتنفيذ المهام تلقائيًا من عناصر GTD.md. يقوم بتصنيف و تخطيط الإجراءات للتنفيذ.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"GTD 自动任务执行","ja":"GTD オートメーション タスク実行","ko":"GTD 자동 작업 실행","es":"GTD Runner: Ejecución Autónoma de Tareas","fr":"GTD Runner : Exécution Autonome de Tâches","de":"GTD Runner: Autonome Aufgabenausführung","pt":"GTD Runner: Automação de Tarefas com GTD.md","ru":"GTD Runner: Автоматизация задач из GTD.md","ar":"GTD Runner: تشغيل تلقائي للمهام من GTD.md","en":"gtd"},"description":{"zh":"GTD Runner Skill 实现了从 GTD.md 项到自动任务执行的工作流","ja":"GTD Runner Skill は、GTD.md 項目から自動タスク実行までのワークフローを実現","ko":"GTD Runner Skill은 GTD.md 항목에서 자동 작업 실행까지의 워크플ロー를 구현합니다","es":"GTD Runner es una habilidad que ejecuta tareas de forma autónoma a partir de elementos de GTD.md, clasificándolos y planificando acciones para mejorar la pro...","fr":"GTD Runner est une compétence qui exécute des tâches de manière autonome à partir d''éléments de GTD.md, les classifiant et planifiant des actions pour amélio...","de":"GTD Runner ist eine Fähigkeit, die Aufgaben automatisch aus GTD.md-Elementen ausführt, sie klassifiziert und Aktionen plant, um die Produktivität zu steigern","pt":"O GTD Runner é uma ferramenta que executa tarefas de forma autônoma a partir de itens do GTD.md. Ele classifica e planeja ações para execução.","ru":"GTD Runner - это инструмент, который выполняет задачи автоматически из элементов GTD.md. Он классифицирует и планирует действия для выполнения.","ar":"GTD Runner هو أداة تقوم بتنفيذ المهام تلقائيًا من عناصر GTD.md. يقوم بتصنيف و تخطيط الإجراءات للتنفيذ.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动任务执行","工作流分类","实体查找","计划和执行","输出结果"],"ja":["自動タスク実行","ワークフロー分類","エンティティ検索","計画と実行","出力結果"],"ko":["자동 작업 실행","워크플ロー 분류","엔티티 조회","계획 및 실행","출력 결과"],"es":["Ejecución autónoma de tareas","Clasificación de elementos de GTD.md","Planificación de acciones","Ejecución secuencial de tareas","Integración con bases de datos"],"fr":["Exécution autonome de tâches","Classification d''éléments de GTD.md","Planification d''actions","Exécution séquentielle de tâches","Intégration avec des bases de données"],"de":["Automatische Ausführung von Aufgaben","Klassifizierung von GTD.md-Elementen","Planung von Aktionen","Sequentielle Ausführung von Aufgaben","Integration mit Datenbanken"],"pt":["Execução autônoma de tarefas","Classificação e planejamento de ações","Integração com banco de dados","Suporte a comandos personalizados","Saída de resultados em formato de arquivo"],"ru":["Автоматическое выполнение задач","Классификация и планирование действий","Интеграция с базой данных","Поддержка пользовательских команд","Выходные результаты в формате файла"],"ar":["تنفيذ تلقائي للمهام","تصنيف و تخطيط الإجراءات","التكامل مع قاعدة البيانات","دعم أوامر مخصصة","خرج النتائج في شكل ملف"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GTD","自动任务执行","工作流","开发效率","任务管理","自动化"],"ja":["GTD","自動タスク実行","ワークフロー","開発効率","タスク管理","自動化"],"ko":["GTD","自動 작업 실행","워크플ロー","개발 효율성","작업 관리","자동화"],"es":["GTD Runner","ejecución autónoma de tareas","GTD.md","productividad","automatización de tareas","clasificación de tareas","planificación de acciones"],"fr":["GTD Runner","exécution autonome de tâches","GTD.md","productivité","automatisation de tâches","classification de tâches","planification d''actions"],"de":["GTD Runner","automatische Ausführung von Aufgaben","GTD.md","Produktivität","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Klassifizierung von Aufgaben","Planung von Aktionen"],"pt":["GTD Runner","automação de tarefas","GTD.md","classificação de tarefas","planejamento de ações","integração com banco de dados","comandos personalizados","saída de resultados"],"ru":["GTD Runner","автоматизация задач","GTD.md","классификация задач","планирование действий","интеграция с базой данных","пользовательские команды","выходные результаты"],"ar":["GTD Runner","تشغيل تلقائي للمهام","GTD.md","تصنيف المهام","تخطيط الإجراءات","التكامل مع قاعدة البيانات","أوامر مخصصة","خرج النتائج"]}},"owner":"Gerstep","repo":"cybos","repoPath":"Gerstep/cybos","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"gtd","description":"Autonomous task execution from GTD.md items. Use when processing GTD tasks, call prep, outreach, or podcast preparation.","bodyPreview":"# GTD Runner Skill\n\nAutonomous task execution from GTD.md items.\n\n## Trigger\n\n- Command: `/cyber-gtd`\n- Default: plan-first (show before execute)\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Read `@GTD.md` → extract items from `# Next`\n2. For each item:\n   - Classify → match pattern to workflow\n   - Lookup entities via database: `bun scripts/db/query.ts find-entity \"<name>\"`\n   - Plan actions\n3. Show plan → ask to execute\n4. Execute approved items sequentially (one at a time)\n5. Output: `~/CybosVault/private/content/work/M","body":"# GTD Runner Skill\n\nAutonomous task execution from GTD.md items.\n\n## Trigger\n\n- Command: `/cyber-gtd`\n- Default: plan-first (show before execute)\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Read `@GTD.md` → extract items from `# Next`\n2. For each item:\n   - Classify → match pattern to workflow\n   - Lookup entities via database: `bun scripts/db/query.ts find-entity \"<name>\"`\n   - Plan actions\n3. Show plan → ask to execute\n4. Execute approved items sequentially (one at a time)\n5. Output: `~/CybosVault/private/content/work/MMDD-<slug>.md`\n\n## Classification → Routing\n\n| Pattern | Confidence | Workflow |\n|---------|------------|----------|\n| \"ask for call\", \"message\", \"email\", \"reach out\" | High | → workflows/outreach.md |\n| \"call with\", \"meeting\", \"X <> Y\", \"sync\" | High | → workflows/call-prep.md |\n| \"podcast\" | High | → workflows/podcast.md |\n| company name, \"research\", \"DD\", \"look into\" | Medium | → workflows/research.md |\n| **no match** | Low | Best judgment → log to learnings.md |\n\n## Entity Lookup\n\nQuery database for entity context:\n\n1. Parse item for names (people, companies)\n2. Run: `bun scripts/db/query.ts find-entity \"<name>\" --json`\n3. If found, get full context: `bun scripts/db/query.ts entity <slug> --json`\n4. Entity context includes:\n   - Recent interactions (calls, emails, telegram)\n   - Deal associations\n   - Pending items\n5. If not found + confident it''s an entity:\n   - High confidence (company with domain) → auto-create stub\n   - Medium confidence → ask: \"Create entity file for X?\"\n\n## Output Format\n\nAll outputs to `~/CybosVault/private/content/work/MMDD-<slug>.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Task: [Task Description]\n\n**Status:** Pending Approval | Completed | Incomplete\n**Created:** YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\n**GTD Item:** [Original text from GTD.md]\n**Workflow:** [Which workflow handled this]\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n**Entity:** [Name]\n- Type: [person/org]\n- Deal: [link if exists]\n- Previous calls: [N calls found]\n\n**Key Info:**\n[Relevant context from calls, deals, entity files]\n\n---\n\n## Draft\n\n[Message/agenda/questions/etc]\n\n---\n\n## Pending Actions\n\n- [ ] Send via Gmail to email@example.com\n- [ ] Alternative: Telegram @handle\n\n---\n\n## Execution Log\n\n- HH:MM - [action taken]\n```\n\n## Staged Execution\n\nAgent completes what it can autonomously:\n- Research and context gathering\n- Draft creation\n- Preparation work\n\nThen queues actions requiring approval:\n- Sending messages (Gmail, Telegram)\n- Scheduling meetings\n- Any external action\n\n## Suggestions\n\nWhen processing tasks, if you notice 3+ similar patterns that don''t have\na dedicated workflow, suggest: \"I''ve seen ''[pattern]'' multiple times.\nWant me to create a workflow for it?\"\n\n## Self-Improvement\n\nLog all task executions to `@learnings.md` for pattern analysis.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:59:43.896Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Task Management Agents requiring autonomous execution of GTD.md items.","zh":"适用于需要自治执行GTD.md项目的任务管理代理。","ja":"GTD.mdアイテムの自治実行を必要とするタスク管理エージェントに適しています。","ko":"GTD.md 항목의 자율 실행을 요구하는 태스크 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Gestión de Tareas que requieren ejecución autónoma de elementos de GTD.md.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de tâches nécessitant une exécution autonome des éléments de GTD.md.","de":"Ideal für Task-Management-Agents, die eine autonome Ausführung von GTD.md-Elementen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Tarefas que exigem execução autônoma de itens do GTD.md.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по управлению задачами, требующих автономного выполнения элементов GTD.md.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة المهام الذي يتطلب تنفيذًا مستقلًا لعناصر GTD.md."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute tasks from GTD.md files, utilizing pattern matching and database entity lookup via bun scripts, to plan and sequentially execute approved items, leveraging workflow automation and entity management through protocols like `/cyber-gtd` commands.","zh":"赋予代理执行GTD.md文件中的任务的能力，使用模式匹配和通过bun脚本的数据库实体查找，来计划和顺序执行批准的项目，利用工作流自动化和实体管理通过像 `/cyber-gtd` 命令这样的协议。","ja":"GTD.mdファイルからのタスクの実行を可能にし、bunスクリプトによるデータベースエンティティの検索とパターンマッチングを利用して、承認されたアイテムを計画して順序的に実行し、 `/cyber-gtd` コマンドなどのプロトコルを介したワークフローオートメーションとエンティティ管理を利用します。","ko":"GTD.md 파일에서 작업을 실행할 수 있도록 에이전트에 권한을 부여하여 bun 스크립트를 통한 데이터베이스 엔티티 조회 및 패턴 매칭을 사용하여 승인된 항목을 계획하고 순차적으로 실행하며 `/cyber-gtd` 명령과 같은 프로토콜을 통해 워크플로 자동화 및 엔티티 관리를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar tareas desde archivos GTD.md, utilizando coincidencia de patrones y búsqueda de entidades de base de datos a través de scripts de bun, para planificar y ejecutar secuencialmente elementos aprobados, aprovechando la automatización de flujos de trabajo y la gestión de entidades a través de protocolos como comandos `/cyber-gtd`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des tâches à partir de fichiers GTD.md, en utilisant la correspondance de modèles et la recherche d''entités de base de données via des scripts bun, pour planifier et exécuter séquentiellement des éléments approuvés, en exploitant l''automatisation des flux de travail et la gestion des entités via des protocoles tels que les commandes `/cyber-gtd`.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Aufgaben aus GTD.md-Dateien auszuführen, indem Musterabgleich und Datenbankentitätsabfrage über bun-Skripte verwendet werden, um genehmigte Elemente zu planen und sequenziell auszuführen, wobei die Workflow-Automatisierung und Entitätsverwaltung durch Protokolle wie `/cyber-gtd`-Befehle genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar tarefas de arquivos GTD.md, utilizando correspondência de padrões e lookup de entidades de banco de dados via scripts bun, para planejar e executar sequencialmente itens aprovados, aproveitando a automação de fluxo de trabalho e gerenciamento de entidades por meio de protocolos como comandos `/cyber-gtd`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять задачи из файлов GTD.md, используя сопоставление с образцом и поиск сущностей базы данных через скрипты bun, для планирования и последовательного выполнения одобренных элементов, используя автоматизацию рабочего процесса и управление сущностями через протоколы типа команд `/cyber-gtd`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تنفيذ المهام من ملفات GTD.md، باستخدام مطابقة النمط والبحث عن كيانات قاعدة البيانات عبر نصوص bun، لتخطيط وتنفيذ العناصر المعتمدة بشكل متسلسل، واستغلال آليّة سير العمل وإدارة الكيانات من خلال بروتوكولات مثل أوامر `/cyber-gtd`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating task execution from GTD.md","Classifying and planning actions for workflow items","Executing approved tasks sequentially with output to ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"zh":["自动执行GTD.md中的任务","对工作流项目进行分类和规划","顺序执行批准的任务，输出到 ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"ja":["GTD.mdからのタスクの自動実行","ワークフロー項目の分類と計画","承認されたタスクの順序実行、出力先: ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"ko":["GTD.md의 태스크 자동 실행","워크플ロー 항목의 분류 및 계획","승인된 태스크의 순차적 실행, 출력 위치: ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"es":["Automatizar la ejecución de tareas desde GTD.md","Clasificar y planificar acciones para elementos de flujo de trabajo","Ejecutar tareas aprobadas secuencialmente con salida a ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"fr":["Automatiser l''exécution de tâches à partir de GTD.md","Classer et planifier des actions pour les éléments de flux de travail","Exécuter des tâches approuvées séquentiellement avec sortie à ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"de":["Automatisieren der Ausführung von Aufgaben aus GTD.md","Klassifizieren und Planen von Aktionen für Workflow-Elemente","Ausführen von genehmigten Aufgaben sequenziell mit Ausgabe an ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"pt":["Automatizar a execução de tarefas do GTD.md","Classificar e planejar ações para itens de fluxo de trabalho","Executar tarefas aprovadas sequencialmente com saída para ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"ru":["Автоматизировать выполнение задач из GTD.md","Классифицировать и планировать действия для элементов рабочего процесса","Выполнять одобренные задачи последовательно с выводом в ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"],"ar":["تأطير تنفيذ المهام من GTD.md","تصنيف وتخطيط الإجراءات لمهام سير العمل","تنفيذ المهام المعتمدة بشكل متسلسل مع إخراج إلى ~/CybosVault/private/content/work/"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to GTD.md files","Dependent on bun scripts for database entity lookup","Limited to sequential execution of approved items"],"zh":["需要访问GTD.md文件","依赖bun脚本进行数据库实体查找","仅限顺序执行批准的项目"],"ja":["GTD.mdファイルへのアクセスが必要","bunスクリプトによるデータベースエンティティの検索に依存","承認されたアイテムの順序実行のみ"],"ko":["GTD.md 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","데이터베이스 엔티티 조회를 위한 bun 스크립트에 의존합니다.","승인된 항목의 순차적 실행만 가능합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos GTD.md","Depende de scripts de bun para la búsqueda de entidades de base de datos","Limitado a la ejecución secuencial de elementos aprobados"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux fichiers GTD.md","Dépend des scripts bun pour la recherche d''entités de base de données","Limité à l''exécution séquentielle des éléments approuvés"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf GTD.md-Dateien","Hängt von bun-Skripten für die Datenbankentitätsabfrage ab","Begrenzt auf die sequenzielle Ausführung von genehmigten Elementen"],"pt":["Exige acesso a arquivos GTD.md","Dependente de scripts bun para lookup de entidades de banco de dados","Limitado à execução sequencial de itens aprovados"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам GTD.md","Зависит от скриптов bun для поиска сущностей базы данных","Ограничен последовательным выполнением одобренных элементов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات GTD.md","يعتمد على نصوص bun للبحث عن كيانات قاعدة البيانات","محدود بالتنفيذ المتسلسل للعناصر المعتمدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('commontoolsinc/labs/ct', 'community', 'commontoolsinc', 'labs', 'commontoolsinc/labs', 'ct', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T03:00:08.533Z', NULL, '{"id":"commontoolsinc/labs/ct","name":"ct","description":{"zh":"CT CLI ","ja":"CT CLI","ko":"CT CLI ","es":"El comando ct es la interfaz de línea de comandos de CommonTools, que permite a los desarrolladores realizar operaciones y configurar el entorno de manera eficiente","fr":"La commande ct est l''interface de ligne de commande de CommonTools, qui permet aux développeurs d''effectuer des opérations et de configurer l''environnement de manière efficace","de":"Der Befehl ct ist die Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle von CommonTools, die es Entwicklern ermöglicht, Operationen auszuführen und die Umgebung effizient zu konfigurieren","pt":"A ferramenta CT é uma CLI para CommonTools, permitindo que os desenvolvedores executem tarefas com facilidade","ru":"Инструмент CT является CLI для CommonTools, позволяя разработчикам выполнять задачи с легкостью","ar":"أداة CT هي CLI ل CommonTools، مما يسمح للمطورين بتنفيذ المهام بسهولة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"CT CLI ","ja":"CT CLI","ko":"CT CLI ","es":"CommonTools CLI: Guía de ct para desarrolladores","fr":"CommonTools CLI : Guide de ct pour les développeurs","de":"CommonTools CLI: Anleitung für ct-Entwickler","pt":"Ferramenta CT: CLI para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Инструмент CT: CLI для Разработчиков","ar":"أداة CT: CLI للمطورين","en":"ct"},"description":{"zh":"CT CLI ","ja":"CT CLI","ko":"CT CLI ","es":"El comando ct es la interfaz de línea de comandos de CommonTools, que permite a los desarrolladores realizar operaciones y configurar el entorno de manera ef...","fr":"La commande ct est l''interface de ligne de commande de CommonTools, qui permet aux développeurs d''effectuer des opérations et de configurer l''environnement d...","de":"Der Befehl ct ist die Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle von CommonTools, die es Entwicklern ermöglicht, Operationen auszuführen und die Umgebung effizient zu konf...","pt":"A ferramenta CT é uma CLI para CommonTools, permitindo que os desenvolvedores executem tarefas com facilidade","ru":"Инструмент CT является CLI для CommonTools, позволяя разработчикам выполнять задачи с легкостью","ar":"أداة CT هي CLI ل CommonTools، مما يسمح للمطورين بتنفيذ المهام بسهولة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["CT CLI","CLI","",""],"ja":["CT CLI","CLI","",""],"ko":["CT CLI","CLI","",""],"es":["Soporte para operaciones de piezas","Comprobación de tipos","Configuración del entorno","Uso de variables de entorno","Generación de claves de identidad"],"fr":["Prise en charge des opérations de pièces","Vérification des types","Configuration de l''environnement","Utilisation de variables d''environnement","Génération de clés d''identité"],"de":["Unterstützung für Teiloperationen","Typüberprüfung","Umgebungssetup","Verwendung von Umgebungsvariablen","Generierung von Identitätschlüsseln"],"pt":["Comandos para operações de código","Configuração de ambiente com variáveis","Criação de chaves de identidade","Suporte a tarefas de verificação de tipo"],"ru":["Команды для операций с кодом","Настройка среды с переменными","Создание ключей идентификации","Поддержка задач проверки типа"],"ar":["أوامر لعمليات الكود","إعداد البيئة مع متغيرات","إنشاء مفاتيح الهوية","دعم مهام فحص النوع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CT CLI","CLI","CommonTools","Deno","Type Checking","Identity Key"],"ja":["CT CLI","CLI","CommonTools","Deno","Type Checking","Identity Key"],"ko":["CT CLI","CLI","CommonTools","Deno","Type Checking","Identity Key"],"es":["CommonTools","ct","CLI","desarrollo de software","operaciones de piezas","comprobación de tipos","configuración del entorno"],"fr":["CommonTools","ct","CLI","développement de logiciels","opérations de pièces","vérification des types","configuration de l''environnement"],"de":["CommonTools","ct","CLI","Softwareentwicklung","Teiloperationen","Typüberprüfung","Umgebungssetup"],"pt":["ferramenta ct","cli para desenvolvedores","comandos de código","configuração de ambiente","chaves de identidade","verificação de tipo"],"ru":["инструмент ct","cli для разработчиков","команды кода","настройка среды","ключи идентификации","проверка типа"],"ar":["أداة ct","cli للمطورين","أوامر الكود","إعداد البيئة","مفاتيح الهوية","فحص النوع"]}},"owner":"commontoolsinc","repo":"labs","repoPath":"commontoolsinc/labs","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ct","description":"Guide for using the ct (CommonTools) binary to interact with pieces,","bodyPreview":"# CT CLI\n\nThe `ct` binary is the CLI for CommonTools. **Use `--help` for current commands:**\n\n```bash\ndeno task ct --help           # Top-level commands\ndeno task ct piece --help     # Piece operations\ndeno task ct check --help     # Type checking\n```\n\n## Environment Setup\n\n**Identity key** (required for most operations):\n```bash\nls -la claude.key              # Check for existing\ndeno task ct id new > claude.key  # Create if missing\n```\n\n**Environment variables** (avoid repeating flags):\n```bas","body":"# CT CLI\n\nThe `ct` binary is the CLI for CommonTools. **Use `--help` for current commands:**\n\n```bash\ndeno task ct --help           # Top-level commands\ndeno task ct piece --help     # Piece operations\ndeno task ct check --help     # Type checking\n```\n\n## Environment Setup\n\n**Identity key** (required for most operations):\n```bash\nls -la claude.key              # Check for existing\ndeno task ct id new > claude.key  # Create if missing\n```\n\n**Environment variables** (avoid repeating flags):\n```bash\nexport CT_API_URL=http://localhost:8000  # or https://toolshed.saga-castor.ts.net/\nexport CT_IDENTITY=./claude.key\n```\n\n**Local servers**: See `docs/development/LOCAL_DEV_SERVERS.md`\n\n## Quick Command Reference\n\n| Operation | Command |\n|-----------|---------|\n| Type check | `deno task ct check pattern.tsx --no-run` |\n| Deploy new | `deno task ct piece new pattern.tsx -i key -a url -s space` |\n| Update existing | `deno task ct piece setsrc pattern.tsx --piece ID -i key -a url -s space` |\n| Inspect state | `deno task ct piece inspect --piece ID ...` |\n| Get field | `deno task ct piece get --piece ID fieldPath ...` |\n| Set field | `echo ''{\"data\":...}'' \\| deno task ct piece set --piece ID path ...` |\n| Call handler | `deno task ct piece call --piece ID handlerName ...` |\n| Trigger recompute | `deno task ct piece step --piece ID ...` |\n| List pieces | `deno task ct piece ls -i key -a url -s space` |\n| Visualize | `deno task ct piece map ...` |\n\n## Core Workflow: setsrc vs new\n\n**Critical pattern:** After initial deployment, use `setsrc` to iterate:\n\n```bash\n# First time only\ndeno task ct piece new pattern.tsx ...\n# Output: Created piece bafyreia... <- Save this ID!\n\n# ALL subsequent iterations\ndeno task ct piece setsrc pattern.tsx --piece bafyreia... ...\n```\n\n**Why:** `new` creates duplicate pieces. `setsrc` updates in-place.\n\n## JSON Input Format\n\nAll values to `set` and `call` must be valid JSON:\n\n```bash\n# Strings need nested quotes\necho ''\"hello world\"'' | deno task ct piece set ... title\n\n# Numbers are bare\necho ''42'' | deno task ct piece set ... count\n\n# Objects\necho ''{\"name\": \"John\"}'' | deno task ct piece set ... user\n```\n\n## Gotcha: Stale Computed Values\n\n`piece set` does NOT trigger recompute. Run `piece step` after:\n\n```bash\necho ''[...]'' | deno task ct piece set --piece ID expenses ...\ndeno task ct piece step --piece ID ...  # Required!\ndeno task ct piece get --piece ID totalSpent ...\n```\n\nSee `docs/development/debugging/cli-debugging.md` for debugging patterns.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Issue | Fix |\n|-------|-----|\n| Commands hang | Check Tailnet connection for `*.ts.net` URLs |\n| Permission denied | `chmod 600 claude.key` |\n| JSON parse error | Check nested quotes, no trailing commas |\n| Local servers not responding | `./scripts/check-local-dev.sh` then `./scripts/restart-local-dev.sh --force` |\n\n## References\n\n- `packages/patterns/system/default-app.tsx` - System pieces (allCharms list lives here)\n- `docs/common/workflows/handlers-cli-testing.md` - Handler testing\n- `docs/development/debugging/cli-debugging.md` - CLI debugging\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:00:08.533Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for CLI-centric AI Agents requiring efficient task automation and type checking via the CommonTools framework.","zh":"适用于基于CLI的AI代理，需要通过CommonTools框架实现高效的任务自动化和类型检查。","ja":"CLI中心のAIエージェントに適しており、CommonToolsフレームワークを介したタスクの自動化とタイプチェックに最適です。","ko":"CLI 중심의 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, CommonTools 프레임워크를 통해 효율적인 작업 자동화 및 타입 확인에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA centrados en CLI que requieren una automatización de tareas eficiente y comprobación de tipos a través del marco de CommonTools.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA centrés sur CLI nécessitant une automatisation de tâches efficace et une vérification de types via le cadre de CommonTools.","de":"Ideal für CLI-zentrierte KI-Agents, die eine effiziente Aufgabenautomatisierung und Typüberprüfung über das CommonTools-Framework erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA centrados em CLI que exigem automação de tarefas eficiente e verificação de tipo via framework CommonTools.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на CLI, требующих эффективной автоматизации задач и проверки типов через фреймворк CommonTools.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المعتمد على واجهة سطر الأوامر الذي يتطلب آليّة مهمة فعالة وفحص نوع عبر إطار العمل CommonTools."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage the `ct` binary for streamlined command-line interactions, including piece operations and type checking using Deno tasks, while utilizing identity keys for secure authentication and environment variables for seamless integration.","zh":"赋予代理使用`ct`二进制文件进行流线化的命令行交互的能力，包括使用Deno任务的碎片操作和类型检查，同时利用身份密钥进行安全身份验证和环境变量进行无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントは、Denoタスクを使用したピース操作とタイプチェックを含む、ストリームライン化されたコマンドラインインタラクションのために`ct`バイナリを利用できるようになり、同時に、セキュアな認証のためにアイデンティティキーとシームレスな統合のために環境変数を利用できます。","ko":"에이전트는 Deno 태스크를 사용한 조각 작업 및 타입 확인을 포함한 스트림 라인화 된 명령줄 상호 작용을 위해 `ct` 바이너리를 사용할 수 있으며, 동시에 보안 인증을 위한 ID 키 및無縫な統合을 위한 환경 변수를 활용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar el binario `ct` para interacciones de línea de comandos optimizadas, incluyendo operaciones de piezas y verificación de tipos utilizando tareas de Deno, mientras que utiliza claves de identidad para una autenticación segura y variables de entorno para una integración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser le binaire `ct` pour des interactions de ligne de commande optimisées, notamment des opérations de pièces et de vérification de types à l''aide de tâches Deno, tout en utilisant des clés d''identité pour une authentification sécurisée et des variables d''environnement pour une intégration transparente.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, das `ct`-Binär für optimierte Kommandozeileninteraktionen zu nutzen, einschließlich Stückoperationen und Typüberprüfung unter Verwendung von Deno-Aufgaben, während sie Identitätsschlüssel für sichere Authentifizierung und Umgebungsvariablen für eine nahtlose Integration nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a utilizarem o binário `ct` para interações de linha de comando otimizadas, incluindo operações de peça e verificação de tipo usando tarefas Deno, ao mesmo tempo em que utilizam chaves de identidade para autenticação segura e variáveis de ambiente para integração transparente.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать бинарный файл `ct` для оптимизированных взаимодействий командной строки, включая операции с фрагментами и проверку типов с помощью задач Deno, а также использовать идентификационные ключи для безопасной аутентификации и переменные среды для бесшовной интеграции.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من استخدام الثنائي `ct` لم互одействات سطر أوامر محسّنة، بما في ذلك عمليات القطع وفحص النوع باستخدام مهام Deno، وفي الوقت نفسه استخدام مفتاح الهوية للتحقق الآمن وتغييرات بيئة لدمج متكامل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating CommonTools workflows with `ct` commands","Performing type checking on code snippets using `deno task ct check`","Generating new identity keys for secure operations with `deno task ct id new`"],"zh":["使用`ct`命令自动化CommonTools工作流程","使用`deno task ct check`对代码片段执行类型检查","使用`deno task ct id new`为安全操作生成新身份密钥"],"ja":["`ct`コマンドを使用してCommonToolsワークフローを自動化する","`deno task ct check`を使用してコードスニペットに対してタイプチェックを行う","`deno task ct id new`を使用してセキュア操作用の新しいアイデンティティキーを生成する"],"ko":["`ct` 명령을 사용하여 CommonTools 워크플로우를 자동화하는 것","`deno task ct check`를 사용하여 코드 조각에 대한 타입 확인을 수행하는 것","`deno task ct id new`를 사용하여 보안 작업을 위한 새로운 ID 키를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de CommonTools con comandos `ct`","Realización de comprobaciones de tipo en fragmentos de código con `deno task ct check`","Generación de nuevas claves de identidad para operaciones seguras con `deno task ct id new`"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de CommonTools avec des commandes `ct`","Réalisation de vérifications de type sur des extraits de code avec `deno task ct check`","Génération de nouvelles clés d''identité pour des opérations sécurisées avec `deno task ct id new`"],"de":["Automatisierung von CommonTools-Workflows mit `ct`-Befehlen","Durchführung von Typüberprüfungen auf Code-Fragmenten mit `deno task ct check`","Generierung neuer Identitätsschlüssel für sichere Operationen mit `deno task ct id new`"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho CommonTools com comandos `ct`","Realizar verificação de tipo em trechos de código usando `deno task ct check`","Gerar novas chaves de identidade para operações seguras com `deno task ct id new`"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие процессы CommonTools с помощью команд `ct`","Выполнять проверку типов на фрагментах кода с помощью `deno task ct check`","Генерировать новые идентификационные ключи для безопасных операций с помощью `deno task ct id new`"],"ar":["آليّة عمليات العمل CommonTools باستخدام أوامر `ct`","إجراء فحص نوع على مقاطع الشفرة باستخدام `deno task ct check`","توليد مفاتيح هوية جديدة لعمليات آمنة باستخدام `deno task ct id new`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Deno task setup","Needs an identity key for most operations","Limited to CommonTools framework compatibility"],"zh":["需要Deno任务设置","需要身份密钥才能进行大多数操作","仅限CommonTools框架兼容性"],"ja":["Denoタスクの設定が必要","大多数の操作にはアイデンティティキーが必要","CommonToolsフレームワークとの互換性のみ"],"ko":["Deno 태스크 설정이 필요합니다.","대부분의 작업을 수행하려면 ID 키가 필요합니다.","CommonTools 프레임워크와의 호환성만으로 제한됩니다."],"es":["Requiere configuración de tareas de Deno","Necesita una clave de identidad para la mayoría de las operaciones","Limitado a la compatibilidad del marco de CommonTools"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de tâches Deno","Nécessite une clé d''identité pour la plupart des opérations","Limité à la compatibilité du cadre de CommonTools"],"de":["Erfordert Deno-Aufgabeneinrichtung","Benötigt einen Identitätsschlüssel für die meisten Operationen","Begrenzt auf die Kompatibilität des CommonTools-Frameworks"],"pt":["Exige configuração de tarefa Deno","Necessita de uma chave de identidade para a maioria das operações","Limitado à compatibilidade do framework CommonTools"],"ru":["Требует настройки задачи Deno","Требует идентификационного ключа для большинства операций","Ограничен совместимостью фреймворка CommonTools"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مهمة Deno","يحتاج إلى مفتاح هوية لمعظم العمليات","محدود بالتوافق مع إطار العمل CommonTools"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Synthesys-Lab/assassyn/open-pr', 'community', 'Synthesys-Lab', 'assassyn', 'Synthesys-Lab/assassyn', 'open-pr', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T02:59:51.857Z', NULL, '{"id":"Synthesys-Lab/assassyn/open-pr","name":"open-pr","description":{"zh":"Open PR 技术允许 AI 代理从对话上下文创建 GitHub 拉取请求，具有有意义的标题、正确的格式和适当的标签选择","ja":"Open PR 技術は、AI エージェントが会話のコンテキストから GitHub プルリクエストを作成できるようにします。有意義なタイトル、正しいフォーマット、適切なタグ選択を備えています","ko":"Open PR 기술은 AI 에이전트가 대화의 맥락에서 GitHub 풀 리퀘스트를 생성할 수 있게 해줍니다. 의미 있는 제목, 올바른 형식 및 적절한 태그 선택을 제공합니다","es":"Open-pr es una habilidad que permite a los agentes de IA crear solicitudes de extracción en GitHub con títulos significativos y formato adecuado.","fr":"Open-pr est une compétence qui permet aux agents IA de créer des demandes d''extraction GitHub avec des titres significatifs et un format approprié.","de":"Open-pr ist eine Fähigkeit, die es IA-Agenten ermöglicht, GitHub-Pull-Requests mit bedeutungsvollen Titeln und geeigneter Formatierung zu erstellen.","pt":"Open PR é uma habilidade que permite criar PRs no GitHub de forma automatizada. Ela analisa o contexto da conversa e cria PRs com títulos significativos e formatação adequada.","ru":"Open PR — это навык, который позволяет создавать PR в GitHub автоматически. Он анализирует контекст разговора и создает PR с осмысленными названиями и правильным форматированием.","ar":"Open PR هو مهارة يسمح بإنشاء طلبات السحب المفتوحة على GitHub تلقائيًا. يقوم بتحليل سياق المحادثة وإنشاء طلبات السحب مع عناوين ذات معنى وتنسيق مناسب.","en":"Asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Open PR 技术：自动创建 GitHub 拉取请求","ja":"Open PR 技術：GitHub プルリクエストの自動作成","ko":"Open PR 기술: GitHub 풀 리퀘스트 자동 생성","es":"Creación de solicitudes de extracción en GitHub con open-pr","fr":"Créer des demandes d''extraction GitHub avec open-pr","de":"Erstellen von GitHub-Pull-Requests mit open-pr","pt":"Crie PRs no GitHub com Open PR","ru":"Создание PR в GitHub с Open PR","ar":"إنشاء طلبات السحب المفتوحة على GitHub مع Open PR","en":"open-pr"},"description":{"zh":"Open PR 技术允许 AI 代理从对话上下文创建 GitHub 拉取请求，具有有意义的标题、正确的格式和适当的标签选择","ja":"Open PR 技術は、AI エージェントが会話のコンテキストから GitHub プルリクエストを作成できるようにします。有意義なタイトル、正しいフォーマット、適切なタグ選択を備えています","ko":"Open PR 기술은 AI 에이전트가 대화의 맥락에서 GitHub 풀 리퀘스트를 생성할 수 있게 해줍니다. 의미 있는 제목, 올바른 형식 및 적절한 태그 선택을 제공합니다","es":"Open-pr es una habilidad que permite a los agentes de IA crear solicitudes de extracción en GitHub con títulos significativos y formato adecuado.","fr":"Open-pr est une compétence qui permet aux agents IA de créer des demandes d''extraction GitHub avec des titres significatifs et un format approprié.","de":"Open-pr ist eine Fähigkeit, die es IA-Agenten ermöglicht, GitHub-Pull-Requests mit bedeutungsvollen Titeln und geeigneter Formatierung zu erstellen.","pt":"Open PR é uma habilidade que permite criar PRs no GitHub de forma automatizada. Ela analisa o contexto da conversa e cria PRs com títulos significativos e fo...","ru":"Open PR — это навык, который позволяет создавать PR в GitHub автоматически. Он анализирует контекст разговора и создает PR с осмысленными названиями и правил...","ar":"Open PR هو مهارة يسمح بإنشاء طلبات السحب المفتوحة على GitHub تلقائيًا. يقوم بتحليل سياق المحادثة وإنشاء طلبات السحب مع عناوين ذات معنى وتنسيق مناسب.","en":"Asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis."},"definition":{"en":"Asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis."},"features":{"zh":["自动创建 GitHub 拉取请求","有意义的标题和正确的格式","适当的标签选择","从对话上下文提取 PR 详情","与用户确认后创建拉取请求"],"ja":["GitHub プルリクエストの自動作成","有意義なタイトルと正しいフォーマット","適切なタグ選択","会話のコンテキストから PR の詳細を抽出","ユーザーと確認した後プルリクエストを作成"],"ko":["GitHub 풀 리퀘스트 자동 생성","의미 있는 제목과 올바른 형식","적절한 태그 선택","대화의 맥락에서 PR 세부 정보 추출","사용자와 확인 후 풀 리퀘스트 생성"],"es":["Creación de solicitudes de extracción en GitHub","Títulos significativos y formato adecuado","Análisis de contexto de conversación","Confirmación con el usuario antes de crear la solicitud","Selección de etiquetas adecuadas","Resumen detallado de la solicitud"],"fr":["Création de demandes d''extraction GitHub","Titres significatifs et format approprié","Analyse du contexte de conversation","Confirmation avec l''utilisateur avant de créer la demande","Sélection d''étiquettes appropriées","Résumé détaillé de la demande"],"de":["Erstellung von GitHub-Pull-Requests","Bedeutungsvolle Titel und geeignete Formatierung","Analyse des Konversationskontexts","Bestätigung mit dem Benutzer vor der Erstellung der Anfrage","Auswahl geeigneter Schlagwörter","Detaillierte Zusammenfassung der Anfrage"],"pt":["Criação automática de PRs no GitHub","Análise do contexto da conversa para extrair detalhes do PR","Confirmação com o usuário antes da criação do PR","Títulos significativos e formatação adequada para PRs","Seleção apropriada de tags para PRs","Melhoria da produtividade do time de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Автоматическое создание PR в GitHub","Анализ контекста разговора для извлечения деталей PR","Подтверждение с пользователем перед созданием PR","Осмысленные названия и правильное форматирование для PR","Прямое выделение тегов для PR","Повышение производительности команды разработки"],"ar":["إنشاء تلقائي لطلبات السحب المفتوحة على GitHub","تحليل سياق المحادثة لاستخراج تفاصيل طلب السحب","التأكيد مع المستخدم قبل إنشاء طلب السحب","أسماء ذات معنى وتنسيق مناسب لطلبات السحب","اختيار مناسب للعلامات لطلبات السحب","تحسين إنتاجية فريق التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Open PR","GitHub 拉取请求","AI 代理","自动创建","开发效率","对话上下文"],"ja":["Open PR","GitHub プルリクエスト","AI エージェント","自動作成","開発効率","会話のコンテキスト"],"ko":["Open PR","GitHub 풀 리퀘스트","AI 에이전트","자동 생성","개발 효율성","대화의 맥락"],"es":["open-pr","solicitudes de extracción","GitHub","agentes de IA","automatización","desarrollo de software","colaboración en código","integración continua"],"fr":["open-pr","demandes d''extraction","GitHub","agents IA","automatisation","développement de logiciels","collaboration de code","intégration continue"],"de":["open-pr","Pull-Requests","GitHub","IA-Agenten","Automatisierung","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Kollaboration","kontinuierliche Integration"],"pt":["Open PR","Criação de PRs","GitHub","Automatização","Desenvolvimento de software","Produtividade","Equipes de desenvolvimento","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Open PR","Создание PR","GitHub","Автоматизация","Разработка программного обеспечения","Производительность","Команды разработки","Инструменты разработки"],"ar":["Open PR","إنشاء طلبات السحب","GitHub","التلقائية","تطوير البرمجيات","الإنتاجية","فرق التطوير","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"Synthesys-Lab","repo":"assassyn","repoPath":"Synthesys-Lab/assassyn","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"open-pr","description":"Create GitHub pull requests from conversation context with proper formatting and tag selection","bodyPreview":"# Open PR\n\nThis skill instructs AI agents on how to create GitHub pull requests from conversation context\nwith meaningful titles, proper formatting, and appropriate tag selection. The AI agent\nshould analyze the conversation, extract PR details, and confirm with the user before\ncreating the pull request.\n\n## PR Format\n\nGitHub pull requests created by this skill must follow this exact structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [tag][#issue-number] Brief description of what was achieved\n\n## Summary\n\nProvide a conc","body":"# Open PR\n\nThis skill instructs AI agents on how to create GitHub pull requests from conversation context\nwith meaningful titles, proper formatting, and appropriate tag selection. The AI agent\nshould analyze the conversation, extract PR details, and confirm with the user before\ncreating the pull request.\n\n## PR Format\n\nGitHub pull requests created by this skill must follow this exact structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [tag][#issue-number] Brief description of what was achieved\n\n## Summary\n\nProvide a concise summary of what has been achieved in this PR. Focus on the\ncompleted work and the value it delivers.\n\n## Changes\n\nProvide a detailed list of changes made in this PR:\n- Modified `file_path:line_range` to implement X\n- Added `new_file.py` for Y functionality\n- Updated `config.json` to support Z\n- Removed deprecated code from `old_file.py:line_range`\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe what was tested and how:\n- Added `tests/test_feature.py` to verify behavior A\n- Modified `tests/test_existing.py:line_range` to cover edge case B\n- Manually tested scenario C with the following steps:\n  1. Step 1\n  2. Step 2\n  3. Expected result\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #issue-number\n\n(Or \"Part of #issue-number\" if this PR partially addresses the issue)\n```\n\n## Tag Selection\n\nA `git-msg-tags.md` file should appear in `{ROOT_PROJ}/docs/git-msg-tags.md` which\ndefines the tags related to the corresponding modules or modifications. The AI agent\n**MUST** refer to this file to select the appropriate tag for the PR title.\n\nIf the file does not exist, reject the PR creation and ask the user to provide a\nlist of tags in `docs/git-msg-tags.md`.\n\n### Tag Logic\n\nThe AI agent must determine which tag to use based on the PR type by reading\n`docs/git-msg-tags.md` which contains the project''s tag definitions.\n\n**Selection guidelines:**\n- Read `docs/git-msg-tags.md` to understand available tags and their meanings\n- Choose the most specific tag that describes the primary change\n- If multiple tags could apply, choose the one that best represents the core purpose\n- If the tag is ambiguous, ask the user to select from 2-3 most relevant options\n\n## Workflow for AI Agents\n\nWhen this skill is invoked, the AI agent **MUST** follow these steps:\n\n### 1. Context Analysis Phase\n\nReview the entire conversation history and git changes to extract PR details:\n- Identify what work was completed during the conversation\n- Review git diff and git status to see actual changes made\n- Extract key details: what was changed, why, which files were affected\n- Determine the type of changes (feature, bugfix, refactor, etc.)\n- Check if there''s a related issue number mentioned in the conversation\n\nContext signals for PR type:\n- Feature signals: new functionality added, new files created, capabilities extended\n- Bugfix signals: fixed error, resolved issue, corrected behavior\n- Refactor signals: improved code structure, reorganized code, better patterns\n- Documentation signals: updated README, added comments, wrote guides\n- Test signals: added test coverage, modified test cases\n\n### 2. Git Changes Review\n\n**CRITICAL:** Before drafting the PR, the AI agent **MUST** review actual git changes:\n\n```bash\n# Check what files have changed\ngit status\n\n# Review the actual changes\ngit diff\n\n# Check commit history on current branch\ngit log origin/main..HEAD --oneline\n```\n\nThis ensures the PR description accurately reflects the actual code changes.\n\n### 3. Tag Selection Phase\n\n- Read `docs/git-msg-tags.md` to understand available tags\n- Analyze the changes and determine the primary purpose\n- Apply the tag logic described above\n- If multiple tags could apply, choose the most specific one\n- If the tag is ambiguous, ask the user to choose from 2-3 most relevant options\n\n### 4. Issue Number Extraction\n\n**CRITICAL:** The PR title **MUST** include an issue number in the format `[tag][#N]`.\n\n**How to find the issue number:**\n1. Search conversation history for explicit issue references:\n   - \"for issue #42\"\n   - \"closes #15\"\n   - \"related to #23\"\n   - GitHub issue URLs containing issue numbers\n\n2. If no issue number is found in conversation:\n   - Check if there are recent issues that match this work:\n     ```bash\n     gh issue list --limit 10\n     ```\n   - Ask the user: \"Which issue does this PR address? (Provide issue number)\"\n\n3. If user says there''s no related issue:\n   - **STOP** and inform the user:\n     ```\n     Cannot create PR without a related issue.\n     Please create an issue first using the open-issue skill, or provide an existing issue number.\n     ```\n\n**Never create a PR without an issue number.**\n\n### 5. PR Draft Construction\n\nBuild the PR following the format specification:\n\n**Title:**\n- Format: `[tag][#issue-number] Brief description`\n- The description should be in past tense (what was achieved)\n- Keep description concise (max 80 characters for the description portion)\n- Example: `[feat][#42] Add TypeScript SDK template support`\n- Example: `[bugfix][#15] Fix pre-commit hook test execution`\n\n**Summary section:**\n- Describe what has been achieved (past tense)\n- Focus on the value and purpose of the changes\n- Keep it concise but meaningful\n\n**Changes section:**\n- List specific files modified, added, or deleted\n- Include line ranges when relevant (e.g., `file.py:12-34`)\n- Describe what each change does\n- Order changes logically (not just alphabetically)\n- **DO NOT** include actual code snippets to save context length\n\n**Testing section:**\n- Describe what was tested\n- List new test files added with what they test\n- List modified test files with what new coverage was added\n- Include manual testing steps if applicable\n- Be specific about test scenarios and expected outcomes\n\n**Related Issue section:**\n- Use `Closes #N` if this PR fully resolves the issue\n- Use `Part of #N` if this PR partially addresses the issue\n- Use `Fixes #N` for bugfix PRs\n- GitHub will automatically link and close the issue when PR is merged\n\n### 6. User Confirmation Phase\n\n**CRITICAL:** The AI agent **MUST** display the complete PR draft to the user\nand wait for explicit confirmation before creating the PR.\n\nPresent the draft in a clear format:\n```\nI''ve prepared this pull request:\n\n---\n[Full PR content here]\n---\n\nShould I create this PR?\n```\n\n- Wait for explicit \"yes\", \"confirm\", \"create it\", or similar affirmative response\n- If the user requests modifications, update the draft and present again\n- If the user declines, abort PR creation gracefully\n\n### 6.5. Remote Branch Verification\n\n**CRITICAL:** Before creating the PR, verify the current branch exists on the remote repository.\n\nCheck if the current branch is tracking a remote branch:\n\n```bash\n# Check if current branch has an upstream branch\ngit rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n**If the command fails (no upstream branch):**\n1. Get the current branch name:\n   ```bash\n   git branch --show-current\n   ```\n2. Push the branch with tracking:\n   ```bash\n   git push -u origin <branch-name>\n   ```\n3. Confirm to user: \"Pushed branch to remote: origin/<branch-name>\"\n\n**If the command succeeds (upstream branch exists):**\n1. Check if local is ahead of remote:\n   ```bash\n   git status --porcelain --branch\n   ```\n2. If output contains `[ahead N]`, push changes:\n   ```bash\n   git push\n   ```\n3. If up-to-date, continue to PR creation\n\n**Error handling:**\n- If push fails due to authentication:\n  ```\n  Git push failed. Please check your Git credentials.\n  ```\n- If push fails due to conflicts:\n  ```\n  Cannot push: your branch has diverged from remote.\n  Please resolve conflicts manually with:\n    git pull --rebase origin <branch-name>\n  ```\n- For other push failures: Display the error and abort PR creation\n\n### 7. GitHub PR Creation\n\nOnce confirmed and the branch is on remote, create the PR using the GitHub CLI:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"TITLE_HERE\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nBODY_CONTENT_HERE\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n**Important:**\n- Use heredoc (`<<''EOF'' ... EOF`) to preserve markdown formatting\n- The body should include all sections from Summary onwards (not the title)\n- The PR will be created against the default branch (usually main/master)\n- After successful creation, display the PR URL to the user\n- Confirm: \"Pull request created successfully: [URL]\"\n\n**Optional flags:**\n- Add `--draft` if the user wants to create a draft PR\n- Add `--base BRANCH` if targeting a different base branch\n\n### 8. Error Handling\n\nHandle common error scenarios gracefully:\n\n**Missing git-msg-tags.md:**\n```\nCannot create PR: docs/git-msg-tags.md not found.\nPlease create this file with your project''s tag definitions.\n```\n\n**No issue number found:**\n```\nCannot create PR: No related issue number found.\n\nPlease either:\n1. Provide the issue number this PR addresses\n2. Create an issue first using the open-issue skill\n```\n\n**No git changes:**\n```\nCannot create PR: No changes detected in the working directory.\nPlease make and commit your changes first.\n```\n\n**GitHub CLI not authenticated:**\n```\nGitHub CLI is not authenticated. Please run:\n  gh auth login\n```\n\n**Not on a feature branch:**\n```\nWarning: You''re on the main/master branch.\nPRs should typically be created from feature branches.\n\nCreate a new branch with:\n  git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n\nOr confirm you want to create a PR from the current branch.\n```\n\n**No conversation context:**\n```\nI don''t have enough context to create a PR. Could you please provide:\n- What changes were made?\n- What issue does this PR address?\n- What was tested?\n```\n\n**PR creation failed:**\n```\nFailed to create pull request: [error message]\nPlease check your GitHub CLI configuration and try again.\n```\n\n## Ownership\n\nThe AI agent **SHALL NOT** claim authorship or co-authorship of the pull request.\nThe PR is created on behalf of the user, who is **FULLY** responsible for its content.\n\nDo not add any \"Created by AI\" or similar attributions to the PR body unless\nexplicitly requested by the user.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Note:** The following examples use tags like `[feat]`, `[bugfix]`, `[agent.skill]` etc.\nThese are illustrative only - actual tags must come from your project''s `docs/git-msg-tags.md`.\n\n### Example 1: Feature PR\n\n**Context:** User implemented TypeScript SDK template support to close issue #42.\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [feat][#42] Add TypeScript SDK template support\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded support for generating TypeScript SDK templates in the agentize project.\nDevelopers can now bootstrap TypeScript-based agent SDKs alongside existing\nPython templates.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Created `templates/typescript/` directory structure with standard layout\n- Added `templates/typescript/package.json` with default dependencies (typescript, @types/node)\n- Created `templates/typescript/tsconfig.json` with recommended compiler settings\n- Added `templates/typescript/src/index.ts` as the SDK entry point\n- Updated `claude/skills/sdk-init/SKILL.md` to include TypeScript as a language option\n- Modified `sdk-init` skill logic to handle TypeScript template generation\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `tests/test_typescript_template.py` to verify:\n  - Template directory creation\n  - All required files are generated correctly\n  - package.json has correct dependencies\n  - tsconfig.json has proper compiler options\n- Manually tested TypeScript template generation:\n  1. Ran sdk-init skill and selected TypeScript\n  2. Verified generated files compile without errors\n  3. Confirmed npm install works correctly\n  4. Built sample TypeScript SDK successfully\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #42\n```\n\n### Example 2: Bugfix PR\n\n**Context:** User fixed pre-commit hook not running tests (issue #15).\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [bugfix][#15] Fix pre-commit hook test execution\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the pre-commit hook to properly execute the test suite before allowing commits.\nThe hook was not running tests due to incorrect path resolution.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Modified `.git/hooks/pre-commit:8-12` to use absolute path for test script\n- Updated hook to check exit code and block commit on test failure\n- Added error message output when tests fail\n\n## Testing\n\n- Modified `tests/test_hooks.py:23-45` to verify pre-commit hook behavior\n- Manually tested the fix:\n  1. Made changes to a Python file in `claude/skills/`\n  2. Ran `git add .` and `git commit -m \"test\"`\n  3. Confirmed tests executed and commit was blocked when tests failed\n  4. Fixed the test failure\n  5. Confirmed commit succeeded after tests passed\n\n## Related Issue\n\nFixes #15\n```\n\n### Example 3: Agent Skill PR\n\n**Context:** User created the open-pr skill (issue #67).\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [agent.skill][#67] Add open-pr skill for creating pull requests\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the open-pr skill that guides AI agents through creating well-formatted\nGitHub pull requests with proper tag selection and mandatory issue references.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Created `claude/skills/open-pr/` directory\n- Added `claude/skills/open-pr/SKILL.md` with complete PR creation workflow\n- Skill enforces issue number requirement in PR titles\n- Includes comprehensive examples and error handling guidelines\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `tests/test_open_pr_skill.py` to verify:\n  - Skill file structure and format\n  - Tag selection logic correctness\n  - Issue number extraction from various formats\n- Manually tested skill workflow:\n  1. Invoked open-pr skill in conversation\n  2. Verified it correctly extracted issue number from context\n  3. Confirmed it generated proper PR format\n  4. Tested error handling for missing issue numbers\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #67\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T02:59:51.857Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for GitHub Integration Agents needing automated pull request creation with precise formatting and tagging","zh":"适用于需要自动创建拉取请求并具有精确格式化和标签的GitHub集成代理","ja":"GitHubの統合エージェントが自動的にプルリクエストを作成し、正確なフォーマットとタグ付けを行う必要がある場合に最適","ko":"정확한 형식 지정 및 태그 지정이 필요한 GitHub 통합 에이전트가 자동으로 풀 요청을 생성해야 하는 경우 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de integración de GitHub que necesitan la creación automática de solicitudes de extracción con formato preciso y etiquetado","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intégration GitHub nécessitant la création automatique de demandes de tirage avec un formatage précis et un étiquetage","de":"Ideal für GitHub-Integration-Agenten, die eine automatisierte Erstellung von Pull-Requests mit präzisem Formatierung und Tagging benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Integração do GitHub que necessitam de criação automática de solicitações de pull com formatação precisa e marcação","ru":"Идеально для агентов интеграции GitHub, которым требуется автоматизированное создание запросов на принятие изменений с точной форматировкой и тегированием","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المتكاملين مع GitHub الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء طلبات السحب التلقائي مع تنسيق دقيق وتسمية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate GitHub pull requests with meaningful titles, proper markdown formatting, and appropriate tag selection, leveraging conversation context for seamless issue tracking and project management through protocols like HTTP and Webhooks","zh":"赋予代理生成具有有意义的标题、适当的Markdown格式和适当的标签选择的GitHub拉取请求的能力，利用对话上下文实现无缝的问题跟踪和项目管理，通过HTTP和Webhooks等协议","ja":"エージェントが会話のコンテキストを利用して、意味のあるタイトル、適切なMarkdownフォーマット、適切なタグ選択を持つGitHubのプルリクエストを生成する能力を付与し、HTTPやWebhooksなどのプロトコルを介して問題の追跡やプロジェクト管理を円滑に行う","ko":"에이전트가 대화 맥락을 활용하여 의미 있는 제목, 적절한 Markdown 형식 및 적절한 태그 선택을 갖춘 GitHub 풀 요청을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 HTTP 및 Webhooks와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 문제 추적 및 프로젝트 관리를 원활하게 수행","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar solicitudes de extracción de GitHub con títulos significativos, formato de markdown adecuado y selección de etiquetas apropiada, aprovechando el contexto de la conversación para un seguimiento de problemas y gestión de proyectos sin problemas a través de protocolos como HTTP y Webhooks","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des demandes de tirage GitHub avec des titres significatifs, un formatage markdown approprié et une sélection de balises appropriée, en exploitant le contexte de la conversation pour un suivi des problèmes et une gestion de projet sans problème via des protocoles tels que HTTP et Webhooks","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, GitHub-Pull-Requests mit sinnvollen Titeln, ordnungsgemäßer Markdown-Formatierung und geeigneter Tag-Auswahl zu generieren, indem es den Konversationskontext für eine nahtlose Problemmeldung und Projektverwaltung über Protokolle wie HTTP und Webhooks nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar solicitações de pull do GitHub com títulos significativos, formatação de markdown apropriada e seleção de tags apropriada, utilizando o contexto da conversa para rastreamento de problemas e gerenciamento de projetos sem interrupções por meio de protocolos como HTTP e Webhooks","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать запросы на принятие изменений в GitHub с осмысленными названиями, правильной форматировкой markdown и подходящим выбором тегов, используя контекст разговора для бесперебойного отслеживания проблем и управления проектами через протоколы như HTTP и Webhooks","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء طلبات السحب من GitHub مع عناوين ذات معنى، تنسيق مناسب لتعليمات markdown، واختيار مناسب للعلامات، مستخدمين سياق المحادثة لتتبع المشكلات وإدارة المشاريع بسلاسة عبر بروتوكولات مثل HTTP و Webhooks"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pull request creation from conversation context","Formatting pull requests with markdown for better readability","Tagging and assigning issues for efficient project management"],"zh":["从对话上下文自动创建拉取请求","使用Markdown格式化拉取请求以提高可读性","标记和分配问题以实现高效的项目管理"],"ja":["会話のコンテキストから自動的にプルリクエストを作成する","Markdownでプルリクエストをフォーマットして可読性を高める","問題をタグ付けして割り当て、効率的なプロジェクト管理を行う"],"ko":["대화 맥락에서 자동으로 풀 요청을 생성","Markdown로 풀 요청을 형식화하여 가독성을 향상","이슈를 태그 지정하고 할당하여 효율적인 프로젝트 관리"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de solicitudes de extracción a partir del contexto de la conversación","Formato de solicitudes de extracción con markdown para una mejor legibilidad","Etiquetado y asignación de problemas para una gestión de proyectos eficiente"],"fr":["Automation de la création de demandes de tirage à pa