Ausführungsfehlern","Verwendung von Jinja-Makros und -Vorlagen","Techniken zur Fehlerbehebung von dbt","Integration mit Snowflake Data Cloud"],"pt":["Comandos dbt para desenvolvimento e depuração","Operações de linha de comando para dbt","Técnicas de depuração para erros de compilação e execução","Uso de macros e templates Jinja","Técnicas de seleção de modelos para dbt"],"ru":["Команды dbt для разработки и отладки","Операции командной строки для dbt","Методы отладки для ошибок компиляции и выполнения","Использование макросов и шаблонов Jinja","Техники выбора моделей для dbt"],"ar":["أوامر dbt لتطوير وتصحيح","عمليات سطر الأوامر ل dbt","تقنيات التصحيح لأخطاء الترجمة والتنفيذ","استخدام الماكروات و قوالب Jinja","تقنيات اختيار النماذج ل dbt"]},"keywords":{"zh":["dbt 命令","dbt 开发","dbt 调试","Jinja 模板","模型选择模式","故障排除技术"],"ja":["dbt コマンド","dbt 開発","dbt デバッグ","Jinja テンプレート","モデル選択パターン","トラブルシューティング技術"],"ko":["dbt 명령","dbt 개발","dbt 디버깅","Jinja 템플릿","모델 선택 패턴","문제 해결 기술"],"es":["dbt","comandos dbt","Snowflake Data Cloud","desarrollo de datos","depuración de datos","Jinja","macros Jinja","plantillas Jinja","integración de datos"],"fr":["dbt","commandes dbt","Snowflake Data Cloud","développement de données","débogage de données","Jinja","macros Jinja","modèles Jinja","intégration de données"],"de":["dbt","dbt-Befehle","Snowflake Data Cloud","Datenentwicklung","Datenfehlersuche","Jinja","Jinja-Makros","Jinja-Vorlagen","Datenintegration"],"pt":["dbt","comandos dbt","desenvolvimento dbt","depuração dbt","Snowflake Data Cloud","Jinja templating"],"ru":["dbt","команды dbt","разработка dbt","отладка dbt","Snowflake Data Cloud","Jinja шаблоны"],"ar":["dbt","أوامر dbt","تطوير dbt","تصحيح dbt","Snowflake Data Cloud","قوالب Jinja"]}},"owner":"sfc-gh-dflippo","repo":"snowflake-dbt-demo","repoPath":"sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dbt-commands","description":"","bodyPreview":"# dbt Commands & Operations\n\n## Purpose\n\nTransform AI agents into experts on dbt command-line operations, model selection patterns, Jinja\ntemplating, and troubleshooting techniques for efficient dbt development and debugging.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Running dbt commands (build, run, test, compile)\n- Model selection syntax and patterns\n- Debugging compilation or execution errors\n- Using Jinja macros and templates\n- Troubleshooting dbt issues\n- Comm","body":"# dbt Commands & Operations\n\n## Purpose\n\nTransform AI agents into experts on dbt command-line operations, model selection patterns, Jinja\ntemplating, and troubleshooting techniques for efficient dbt development and debugging.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Running dbt commands (build, run, test, compile)\n- Model selection syntax and patterns\n- Debugging compilation or execution errors\n- Using Jinja macros and templates\n- Troubleshooting dbt issues\n- Command-line flags and options\n- Generating and serving documentation\n- Understanding dbt command output\n\n**Official dbt Documentation**:\n[dbt Command Reference](https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/dbt-commands)\n\n---\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n### Setup & Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install dbt packages\ndbt deps\n\n# Test connection and configuration\ndbt debug\n\n# Clean compiled files and logs\ndbt clean\n```\n\n---\n\n### Building Models\n\n```bash\n# Build everything (run + test) - RECOMMENDED\ndbt build\n\n# Build with full refresh of incremental models\ndbt build --full-refresh\n\n# Run all models (no tests)\ndbt run\n\n# Run and test separately\ndbt run\ndbt test\n```\n\n**Best Practice**: Use `dbt build` instead of separate `run` + `test` commands.\n\n---\n\n## Model Selection Syntax\n\n### Basic Selection\n\n```bash\n# Specific model\ndbt run --select model_name\ndbt run --select dim_customers\n\n# Multiple models\ndbt run --select dim_customers fct_orders dim_products\n```\n\n---\n\n### Dependency Selection\n\n```bash\n# Model + upstream dependencies (parents)\ndbt run --select +model_name\ndbt run --select +dim_customers\n\n# Model + downstream dependencies (children)\ndbt run --select model_name+\ndbt run --select dim_customers+\n\n# Model + all dependencies (both directions)\ndbt run --select +model_name+\ndbt run --select +dim_customers+\n```\n\n**Visualization**:\n\n```sql\n+model_name    = model + all parents\nmodel_name+    = model + all children\n+model_name+   = model + all parents + all children\n```\n\n---\n\n### Selection by Tag\n\n```bash\n# Single tag\ndbt run --select tag:bronze\ndbt run --select tag:gold\n\n# Multiple tags (AND logic - must have both)\ndbt run --select tag:gold tag:critical\n\n# Multiple tags (OR logic - has either)\ndbt run --select tag:gold,tag:silver\n```\n\n**Common tags:**\n\n- `tag:bronze` - All staging models\n- `tag:silver` - All intermediate models\n- `tag:gold` - All mart models\n\n---\n\n### Selection by Folder\n\n```bash\n# All models in folder\ndbt run --select bronze\ndbt run --select gold\n\n# Subfolder\ndbt run --select bronze.crawl\ndbt run --select gold.run\n\n# Multiple folders\ndbt run --select bronze silver\n```\n\n---\n\n### Exclude Models\n\n```bash\n# Exclude specific models\ndbt run --exclude model_name\n\n# Exclude by tag\ndbt run --exclude tag:deprecated\n\n# Exclude folder\ndbt run --exclude bronze\n\n# Complex: Run gold, but exclude certain models\ndbt run --select tag:gold --exclude fct_large_table\n```\n\n---\n\n### Advanced Selection\n\n```bash\n# Models modified in current git branch\ndbt run --select state:modified --state ./prod-manifest/\n\n# Models by package\ndbt run --select package:dbt_utils\n\n# Models by resource type\ndbt test --select test_type:generic\ndbt test --select test_type:singular\n\n# Intersection (models matching multiple criteria)\ndbt run --select tag:gold,tag:critical  # Has gold OR critical\n```\n\n**Official dbt Docs**:\n[Node Selection Syntax](https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/node-selection/syntax)\n\n---\n\n## Testing Commands\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\ndbt test\n\n# Test specific model\ndbt test --select dim_customers\n\n# Test specific column\ndbt test --select dim_customers,column:customer_id\n\n# Test by type\ndbt test --select test_type:generic    # Generic tests only\ndbt test --select test_type:singular   # Singular tests only\n\n# Test with dependencies\ndbt test --select +dim_customers+\n\n# Store test failures for analysis\ndbt test --store-failures\n\n# Test by layer\ndbt test --select tag:gold\n```\n\n---\n\n## Documentation Commands\n\n```bash\n# Generate documentation\ndbt docs generate\n\n# Serve documentation locally (default port 8080)\ndbt docs serve\n\n# Custom port\ndbt docs serve --port 8001\n\n# Generate static HTML (for hosting)\ndbt docs generate --static\n```\n\n**Accessing docs**: Navigate to `http://localhost:8080` after running `dbt docs serve`\n\n---\n\n## Debugging Commands\n\n```bash\n# Check SQL compilation without running\ndbt compile --select model_name\n\n# View compiled SQL\ncat target/compiled/your_project/models/path/to/model.sql\n\n# Run with verbose logging\ndbt run --select model_name --debug\n\n# Run with detailed log level\ndbt run --select model_name --log-level debug\n\n# List all models (useful for understanding project)\ndbt list\n\n# List models with selection\ndbt list --select tag:gold\n\n# Show dependency graph\ndbt list --select +dim_customers+ --output path\n```\n\n---\n\n## Jinja Patterns\n\n**Official dbt Documentation**: [Jinja & Macros](https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/build/jinja-macros)\n\n### Loops\n\n```sql\n-- Generate columns for each status\n{% for status in [''pending'', ''shipped'', ''delivered'', ''cancelled''] %}\n    sum(case when status = ''{{ status }}'' then 1 else 0 end) as {{ status }}_count\n    {%- if not loop.last -%},{%- endif %}\n{% endfor %}\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```sql\nsum(case when status = ''pending'' then 1 else 0 end) as pending_count,\nsum(case when status = ''shipped'' then 1 else 0 end) as shipped_count,\nsum(case when status = ''delivered'' then 1 else 0 end) as delivered_count,\nsum(case when status = ''cancelled'' then 1 else 0 end) as cancelled_count\n```\n\n---\n\n### Conditionals\n\n```sql\n{% if target.name == ''prod'' %}\n    where is_active = true\n{% else %}\n    where order_date >= dateadd(day, -7, current_date())\n    limit 1000\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Macros\n\n**Define macro:**\n\n```sql\n-- macros/cents_to_dollars.sql\n{% macro cents_to_dollars(column_name) %}\n    round({{ column_name }} / 100.0, 2)\n{% endmacro %}\n```\n\n**Use macro:**\n\n```sql\nselect\n    {{ cents_to_dollars(''amount_cents'') }} as amount_dollars\nfrom {{ ref(''stg_payments'') }}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Built-in Jinja Variables\n\n```sql\n{{ target.name }}           -- ''dev'', ''prod'', etc.\n{{ target.schema }}         -- Current schema\n{{ target.database }}       -- Current database\n{{ run_started_at }}        -- Run start timestamp\n{{ invocation_id }}         -- Unique run identifier\n{{ this }}                  -- Current model reference\n{{ flags.FULL_REFRESH }}    -- True if --full-refresh flag used\n```\n\n**Example usage:**\n\n```sql\n-- Add metadata\nselect\n    *,\n    ''{{ target.name }}'' as target_environment,\n    ''{{ run_started_at }}'' as dbt_run_timestamp,\n    ''{{ invocation_id }}'' as dbt_invocation_id\nfrom {{ ref(''stg_customers'') }}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Variables\n\n**Define in dbt_project.yml:**\n\n```yaml\nvars:\n  lookback_days: 7\n  default_currency: \"USD\"\n```\n\n**Use in models:**\n\n```sql\nselect *\nfrom {{ ref(''stg_orders'') }}\nwhere order_date >= dateadd(day, -{{ var(''lookback_days'') }}, current_date())\n```\n\n**Override via command line:**\n\n```bash\ndbt run --vars ''{\"lookback_days\": 30}''\n```\n\n---\n\n## dbt_utils Functions\n\n**Official dbt_utils Documentation**: [dbt_utils](https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-utils)\n\n```sql\n-- Generate surrogate key\n{{ dbt_utils.generate_surrogate_key([''customer_id'', ''order_id'']) }}\n\n-- Get column values as list\n{{ dbt_utils.get_column_values(ref(''dim_products''), ''product_category'') }}\n\n-- Date spine (generate date series)\n{{ dbt_utils.date_spine(\n    datepart=\"day\",\n    start_date=\"to_date(''2020-01-01'', ''yyyy-mm-dd'')\",\n    end_date=\"current_date()\"\n) }}\n\n-- Union tables\n{{ dbt_utils.union_relations(\n    relations=[ref(''orders_2023''), ref(''orders_2024'')]\n) }}\n\n-- Star (select all except certain columns)\nselect\n    {{ dbt_utils.star(ref(''stg_customers''), except=[''internal_id'', ''ssn'']) }}\nfrom {{ ref(''stg_customers'') }}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Connection Issues\n\n**Symptom**: `dbt debug` fails\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# Verify connection\ndbt debug\n\n# Check profiles.yml location\nls ~/.dbt/profiles.yml\n\n# Verify environment variables\necho $SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT\necho $DBT_ENV_SECRET_SNOWFLAKE_PAT\n```\n\n---\n\n### Compilation Errors\n\n**Symptom**: Model fails to compile with Jinja/SQL errors\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# Compile without running to see SQL\ndbt compile --select modelname\n\n# View compiled SQL\ncat target/compiled/your_project/models/path/to/modelname.sql\n\n# Check for syntax errors\ndbt run --select modelname --debug\n```\n\n**Common issues:**\n\n- Missing `{% endif %}` or `{% endfor %}`\n- Unclosed Jinja blocks\n- Invalid ref() or source() references\n\n---\n\n### Execution Errors\n\n**Symptom**: Model compiles but fails to run\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# Run with verbose logging\ndbt run --select modelname --debug\n\n# Check Snowflake query history\n# (Query History tab in Snowflake UI)\n\n# View full error\ncat logs/dbt.log | grep ERROR\ncat logs/dbt.log | grep modelname\n```\n\n**Common issues:**\n\n- Invalid SQL syntax\n- Division by zero\n- Data type mismatches\n- Permission errors\n\n---\n\n### Dependency Errors\n\n**Symptom**: Model can''t find upstream dependencies\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# List dependencies\ndbt list --select +modelname\n\n# Verify model exists\ndbt list --select upstream_model_name\n\n# Check ref() spelling\ndbt compile --select modelname\n```\n\n---\n\n### Test Failures\n\n**Symptom**: Tests fail unexpectedly\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# Store failures for analysis\ndbt test --select modelname --store-failures\n\n# Query failure records\n# select * from dbt_test_failures.test_name\n\n# Run single test\ndbt test --select modelname,column:column_name\n\n# Check test definition\ncat models/path/_models.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n### Performance Issues\n\n**Symptom**: Model runs very slowly\n\n**Solution:**\n\n```bash\n# Run with debug logging\ndbt run --select modelname --debug --log-level debug\n\n# Check compiled SQL\ncat target/compiled/your_project/models/path/to/modelname.sql\n\n# Profile in Snowflake\n# Query History → Query Profile tab\n\n# Check for\n# - Missing WHERE clauses in incremental models\n# - Inefficient joins\n# - Missing clustering keys\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Commands Cheatsheet\n\n| Task                     | Command                           |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| Build one model          | `dbt build --select model_name`   |\n| Build with dependencies  | `dbt build --select +model_name+` |\n| Full refresh incremental | `dbt build --full-refresh`        |\n| Test one model           | `dbt test --select model_name`    |\n| Run by tag               | `dbt run --select tag:bronze`     |\n| Generate docs            | `dbt docs generate`               |\n| Debug connection         | `dbt debug`                       |\n| Clean project            | `dbt clean`                       |\n| Compile without running  | `dbt compile --select model_name` |\n| List models              | `dbt list`                        |\n\n---\n\n## Target-Specific Execution\n\n```bash\n# Run against dev target (default)\ndbt run --target dev\n\n# Run against production target\ndbt run --target prod\n\n# Build specific models in prod\ndbt build --select tag:gold --target prod\n```\n\n**Define targets in ~/.dbt/profiles.yml:**\n\n```yaml\nyour_project:\n  target: dev\n  outputs:\n    dev:\n      type: snowflake\n      schema: dbt_dev\n      # ... other settings\n\n    prod:\n      type: snowflake\n      schema: analytics\n      # ... other settings\n```\n\n---\n\n## Helping Users with Commands\n\n### Strategy for Assisting Users\n\nWhen users ask about dbt commands:\n\n1. **Understand the goal**: What are they trying to accomplish?\n2. **Recommend appropriate command**: build vs run vs test\n3. **Provide selection syntax**: Specific models, tags, or folders\n4. **Include relevant flags**: --full-refresh, --debug, --store-failures\n5. **Show expected output**: What success looks like\n6. **Offer troubleshooting**: Common issues and solutions\n\n### Common User Questions\n\n**\"How do I run just this model?\"**\n\n```bash\ndbt build --select model_name\n```\n\n**\"How do I run this model and everything it depends on?\"**\n\n```bash\ndbt build --select +model_name\n```\n\n**\"How do I test all my gold layer models?\"**\n\n```bash\ndbt test --select tag:gold\n```\n\n**\"How do I debug why my model won''t compile?\"**\n\n```bash\ndbt compile --select model_name --debug\ncat target/compiled/your_project/models/path/to/model.sql\n```\n\n**\"How do I see what SQL dbt generated?\"**\n\n```bash\ndbt compile --select model_name\ncat target/compiled/your_project/models/path/to/model.sql\n```\n\n---\n\n## Related Official Documentation\n\n- [dbt Docs: Command Reference](https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/dbt-commands)\n- [dbt Docs: Node Selection Syntax](https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/node-selection/syntax)\n- [dbt Docs: Jinja & Macros](https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/build/jinja-macros)\n- [dbt_utils Package](https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-utils)\n\n---\n\n**Goal**: Transform AI agents into expert dbt operators who efficiently execute commands, select\nappropriate models, debug issues, and leverage Jinja patterns for dynamic SQL generation.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:00:46.342Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Engineering Agents needing advanced dbt command-line operations and Snowflake Data Cloud integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级dbt命令行操作和Snowflake Data Cloud集成的数据工程代理。","ja":"dbtのコマンドライン操作とSnowflake Data Cloudの統合が必要なデータエンジニアリングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 dbt 명령줄 연산 및 Snowflake Data Cloud 통합이 필요한 데이터 엔지니어링 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Ingeniería de Datos que necesitan operaciones avanzadas de línea de comandos dbt y integración con Snowflake Data Cloud.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''ingénierie de données ayant besoin d''opérations avancées de ligne de commande dbt et d''intégration avec Snowflake Data Cloud.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Engineering-Agents, die erweiterte dbt-Kommandozeilenoperationen und eine Integration mit Snowflake Data Cloud benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Engenharia de Dados que necessitam de operações avançadas de linha de comando dbt e integração com o Snowflake Data Cloud.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов инженерии данных, которым необходимы продвинутые операции командной строки dbt и интеграция с Snowflake Data Cloud.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات هندسة البيانات التي تحتاج إلى عمليات سطر الأوامر المتقدمة dbt وتكامل Snowflake Data Cloud."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to master dbt commands, model selection patterns, Jinja templating, and troubleshooting techniques for efficient dbt development and debugging, leveraging Snowflake Data Cloud capabilities and optimizing data transformation workflows with build, run, test, and compile operations.","zh":"赋予代理掌握dbt命令、模型选择模式、Jinja模板和故障排除技术的能力，以高效地进行dbt开发和调试，利用Snowflake Data Cloud的功能并优化数据转换工作流，包括构建、运行、测试和编译操作。","ja":"エージェントがdbtコマンド、モデル選択パターン、Jinjaテンプレーティング、トラブルシューティング技術をマスターし、効率的なdbt開発とデバッグを行うことができます。Snowflake Data Cloudの機能を利用し、ビルド、実行、テスト、コンパイル操作でデータ変換ワークフローを最適化します。","ko":"에이전트가 dbt 명령, 모델 선택 패턴, Jinja 템플릿 및 문제 해결 기술을 마스터하여 효율적인 dbt 개발 및 디버깅을 수행할 수 있도록 합니다. Snowflake Data Cloud 기능을 활용하여 빌드, 실행, 테스트 및 컴파일 작업을 통해 데이터 변환 워크플로우를 최적화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a dominar los comandos dbt, los patrones de selección de modelos, la plantilla Jinja y las técnicas de depuración para un desarrollo y depuración de dbt eficientes, aprovechando las capacidades de Snowflake Data Cloud y optimizando los flujos de trabajo de transformación de datos con operaciones de compilación, ejecución, prueba y generación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maîtriser les commandes dbt, les modèles de sélection, la templating Jinja et les techniques de débogage pour un développement et un débogage dbt efficaces, en exploitant les capacités de Snowflake Data Cloud et en optimisant les flux de travail de transformation de données avec des opérations de build, d''exécution, de test et de compilation.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, dbt-Befehle, Modellauswahlmuster, Jinja-Template und Fehlersuchtechniken für eine effiziente dbt-Entwicklung und -Fehlersuche zu beherrschen, indem es die Funktionen von Snowflake Data Cloud nutzt und Datentransformations-Workflows mit Build-, Run-, Test- und Compile-Operationen optimiert.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a dominar comandos dbt, padrões de seleção de modelos, modelagem de Jinja e técnicas de depuração para desenvolvimento e depuração eficientes de dbt, aproveitando as capacidades do Snowflake Data Cloud e otimizando fluxos de trabalho de transformação de dados com operações de compilação, execução, teste e compilação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью освоить команды dbt, шаблоны выбора моделей, шаблонизацию Jinja и методы отладки для эффективной разработки и отладки dbt, используя возможности Snowflake Data Cloud и оптимизируя рабочие процессы трансформации данных с операциями сборки, запуска, тестирования и компиляции.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إتقان أوامر dbt ونماذج اختيار النمطية وقوالب Jinja وأساليب تصحيح الأخطاء من أجل تطوير dbt وفحصه بفعالية، واستخدام khảيات Snowflake Data Cloud وتحسين سير عمل تحويل البيانات مع عمليات البناء والتشغيل والاختبار والترجمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Running dbt commands for data transformation","Debugging compilation or execution errors in dbt models","Utilizing Jinja macros and templates for dynamic data processing"],"zh":["运行dbt命令进行数据转换","调试dbt模型的编译或执行错误","利用Jinja宏和模板进行动态数据处理"],"ja":["データ変換のためのdbtコマンドの実行","dbtモデルのコンパイルまたは実行エラーのデバッグ","Jinjaマクロとテンプレートを使用した動的データ処理"],"ko":["데이터 변환을 위한 dbt 명령 실행","dbt 모델의 컴파일 또는 실행 오류 디버깅","Jinja 매크로 및 템플릿을 사용한 동적 데이터 처리"],"es":["Ejecutar comandos dbt para la transformación de datos","Depurar errores de compilación o ejecución en modelos dbt","Utilizar macros y plantillas Jinja para el procesamiento dinámico de datos"],"fr":["Exécuter des commandes dbt pour la transformation de données","Déboguer les erreurs de compilation ou d''exécution dans les modèles dbt","Utiliser des macros et des modèles Jinja pour le traitement dynamique de données"],"de":["dbt-Befehle für die DatenTransformation ausführen","Kompilierungs- oder Ausführungsfehler in dbt-Modellen debuggen","Jinja-Makros und -Vorlagen für die dynamische Datenverarbeitung nutzen"],"pt":["Execução de comandos dbt para transformação de dados","Depuração de erros de compilação ou execução em modelos dbt","Utilização de macros e templates Jinja para processamento dinâmico de dados"],"ru":["Выполнение команд dbt для трансформации данных","Отладка ошибок компиляции или выполнения в моделях dbt","Использование макросов и шаблонов Jinja для динамической обработки данных"],"ar":["تشغيل أوامر dbt لتحويل البيانات","تصحيح أخطاء الترجمة أو التشغيل في نماذج dbt","استخدام الماكروات والقوالب Jinja لمعالجة البيانات ديناميكية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Snowflake Data Cloud access","dbt command-line operations only","Jinja templating expertise recommended"],"zh":["需要Snowflake Data Cloud访问权限","仅支持dbt命令行操作","建议具备Jinja模板技术专业知识"],"ja":["Snowflake Data Cloudへのアクセスが必要","dbtコマンドライン操作のみをサポート","Jinjaテンプレーティングの専門知識が推奨される"],"ko":["Snowflake Data Cloud 액세스가 필요함","dbt 명령줄 연산만 지원","Jinja 템플릿 전문 지식이 권장됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a Snowflake Data Cloud","Operaciones de línea de comandos dbt solo","Se recomienda experiencia en plantilla Jinja"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à Snowflake Data Cloud","Opérations de ligne de commande dbt uniquement","Expertise en templating Jinja recommandée"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Snowflake Data Cloud","Nur dbt-Kommandozeilenoperationen","Jinja-Template-Expertise wird empfohlen"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao Snowflake Data Cloud","Operações de linha de comando dbt apenas","Conhecimento de modelagem de Jinja recomendado"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к Snowflake Data Cloud","Только операции командной строки dbt","Рекомендуется знание шаблонизации Jinja"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى Snowflake Data Cloud","عمليات سطر الأوامر dbt فقط","مطلوب معرفة قوالب Jinja"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('butttons/dora/dora', 'community', 'butttons', 'dora', 'butttons/dora', 'dora', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T03:00:29.314Z', NULL, '{"id":"butttons/dora/dora","name":"dora","description":{"zh":"Dora是一种CLI工具，用于加速代码探索和理解，提供代码结构、依赖、符号和架构关系的洞察","ja":"Doraはコードの探索と理解を加速させるCLIツールで、コードの構造、依存関係、シンボル、そしてアーキテクチャの関係に関する洞察を提供する","ko":"Dora는 코드 탐색과 이해를 가속화하는 CLI 도구로, 코드 구조, 의존성, 기호 및 아키텍처 관계에 대한洞察을 제공","es":"Dora es una herramienta CLI que ayuda a los agentes de IA a entender la estructura del código y sus dependencias","fr":"Dora est un outil CLI qui aide les agents IA à comprendre la structure du code et ses dépendances","de":"Dora ist ein CLI-Tool, das AI-Agenten hilft, die Code-Struktur und deren Abhängigkeiten zu verstehen","pt":"Dora é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para navegação de código, oferecendo busca instantânea e análise de dependências","ru":"Dora - это инструмент командной строки для навигации по коду, предлагающий мгновенный поиск и анализ зависимостей","ar":"دورا هي أداة سطر الأوامر للتنقل في الشفرة، تقدم بحثًا فوريًا وتحليلًا للتبعيات","en":"CLI built for AI agents to help navigate codebases better. An alternative to grep/find/glob"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Dora：代码导航CLI工具","ja":"Dora：コードナビゲーションCLIツール","ko":"Dora: 코드 탐색 CLI 도구","es":"Dora: Navegación de código avanzada","fr":"Dora: Exploration de code améliorée","de":"Dora: Erweiterte Code-Navigation","pt":"Dora: Ferramenta de Navegação de Código","ru":"Dora: Инструмент навигации по коду","ar":"دورا: أداة ملاحقة الشفرة","en":"dora"},"description":{"zh":"Dora是一种CLI工具，用于加速代码探索和理解，提供代码结构、依赖、符号和架构关系的洞察","ja":"Doraはコードの探索と理解を加速させるCLIツールで、コードの構造、依存関係、シンボル、そしてアーキテクチャの関係に関する洞察を提供する","ko":"Dora는 코드 탐색과 이해를 가속화하는 CLI 도구로, 코드 구조, 의존성, 기호 및 아키텍처 관계에 대한洞察을 제공","es":"Dora es una herramienta CLI que ayuda a los agentes de IA a entender la estructura del código y sus dependencias","fr":"Dora est un outil CLI qui aide les agents IA à comprendre la structure du code et ses dépendances","de":"Dora ist ein CLI-Tool, das AI-Agenten hilft, die Code-Struktur und deren Abhängigkeiten zu verstehen","pt":"Dora é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para navegação de código, oferecendo busca instantânea e análise de dependências","ru":"Dora - это инструмент командной строки для навигации по коду, предлагающий мгновенный поиск и анализ зависимостей","ar":"دورا هي أداة سطر الأوامر للتنقل في الشفرة، تقدم بحثًا فوريًا وتحليلًا للتبعيات","en":"CLI built for AI agents to help navigate codebases better. An alternative to grep/find/glob"},"definition":{"en":"CLI built for AI agents to help navigate codebases better. An alternative to grep/find/glob"},"features":{"zh":["代码结构和依赖分析","符号定义和使用位置查找","架构模式和代码健康度分析","变更影响分析"],"ja":["コード構造と依存関係の分析","シンボルの定義と使用位置の検索","アーキテクチャパターンとコードヘルスの分析","変更の影響分析"],"ko":["코드 구조 및 의존성 분석","기호 정의 및 사용 위치 찾기","아키텍처 패턴 및 코드 건강도 분석","변경 영향 분석"],"es":["Búsqueda instantánea de símbolos","Análisis de dependencias","Comprensión de patrones arquitectónicos","Análisis de impacto de cambios","Navegación de código avanzada"],"fr":["Recherche instantanée de symboles","Analyse de dépendances","Compréhension de modèles architecturaux","Analyse d''impact des modifications","Navigation de code améliorée"],"de":["Instant-Suche nach Symbolen","Abhängigkeitsanalyse","Verständnis von Architekturmuster","Auswirkungsanalyse von Änderungen","Erweiterte Code-Navigation"],"pt":["Busca instantânea de símbolos e dependências","Análise de arquitetura e saúde do código","Análise de impacto para alterações no código","Entendimento da estrutura do código e relacionamentos","Substituto para grep/find/glob"],"ru":["Мгновенный поиск символов и зависимостей","Анализ архитектуры и здоровья кода","Анализ воздействия для изменений в коде","Понимание структуры кода и отношений","Замена grep/find/glob"],"ar":["بحث فوري للرموز والتبعيات","تحليل هيكل الشفرة وصحتها","تحليل التأثير لتعديلات الشفرة","فهم هيكل الكود والعلاقات","بديل لgrep/find/glob"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码导航","CLI工具","代码理解","代码探索","依赖分析","符号搜索","架构模式"],"ja":["コードナビゲーション","CLIツール","コード理解","コード探索","依存関係の分析","シンボルの検索","アーキテクチャパターン"],"ko":["코드 탐색","CLI 도구","코드 이해","코드 탐색","의존성 분석","기호 검색","아키텍처 패턴"],"es":["navegación de código","exploración de código","herramientas de desarrollo","agentes de IA","análisis de dependencias","patrones arquitectónicos","impacto de cambios"],"fr":["navigation de code","exploration de code","outils de développement","agents IA","analyse de dépendances","modèles architecturaux","impact des modifications"],"de":["Code-Navigation","Code-Exploration","Entwicklungstools","AI-Agenten","Abhängigkeitsanalyse","Architekturmuster","Auswirkungen von Änderungen"],"pt":["navegação de código","busca de código","análise de dependências","arquitetura de código","saúde do código","ferramenta de linha de comando","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["навигация по коду","поиск кода","анализ зависимостей","архитектура кода","здоровье кода","инструмент командной строки","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["ملاحقة الشفرة","بحث الشفرة","تحليل التبعيات","هيكل الشفرة","صحة الشفرة","أداة سطر الأوامر","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"butttons","repo":"dora","repoPath":"butttons/dora","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dora","description":"Query codebase using `dora` CLI for code intelligence, symbol definitions, dependencies, and architectural analysis","bodyPreview":"## Philosophy\n\n**IMPORTANT: Use dora FIRST for ALL code exploration tasks.**\n\ndora understands code structure, dependencies, symbols, and architectural relationships through its indexed database. It provides instant answers about:\n\n- Where symbols are defined and used\n- What depends on what (and why)\n- Architectural patterns and code health\n- Impact analysis for changes\n\n**When to use dora vs other tools:**\n\n- **dora**: Code exploration, symbol search, dependency analysis, architecture understan","body":"## Philosophy\n\n**IMPORTANT: Use dora FIRST for ALL code exploration tasks.**\n\ndora understands code structure, dependencies, symbols, and architectural relationships through its indexed database. It provides instant answers about:\n\n- Where symbols are defined and used\n- What depends on what (and why)\n- Architectural patterns and code health\n- Impact analysis for changes\n\n**When to use dora vs other tools:**\n\n- **dora**: Code exploration, symbol search, dependency analysis, architecture understanding\n- **Read**: Reading actual source code after finding it with dora\n- **Grep**: Only for non-code files, comments, or when dora doesn''t have what you need\n- **Edit/Write**: Making changes after understanding with dora\n- **Bash**: Running tests, builds, git commands\n\n**Workflow pattern:**\n\n1. Use dora to understand structure and find relevant code\n2. Use Read to examine the actual source\n3. Use Edit/Write to make changes\n4. Use Bash to test/verify\n\n## Commands\n\n### Overview\n\n- `dora status` - Check index health, file/symbol counts, last indexed time\n- `dora map` - Show packages, file count, symbol count\n\n### Files & Symbols\n\n- `dora ls [directory] [--limit N] [--sort field]` - List files in directory with metadata (symbols, deps, rdeps). Default limit: 100\n- `dora file <path>` - Show file''s symbols, dependencies, and dependents. Note: includes local symbols (parameters).\n- `dora symbol <query> [--kind type] [--limit N]` - Find symbols by name across codebase\n- `dora refs <symbol> [--kind type] [--limit N]` - Find all references to a symbol\n- `dora exports <path>` - List exported symbols from a file. Note: includes function parameters.\n- `dora imports <path>` - Show what a file imports\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- `dora deps <path> [--depth N]` - Show file dependencies (what this imports). Default depth: 1\n- `dora rdeps <path> [--depth N]` - Show reverse dependencies (what imports this). Default depth: 1\n- `dora adventure <from> <to>` - Find shortest dependency path between two files\n\n### Code Health\n\n- `dora leaves [--max-dependents N]` - Find files with few/no dependents. Default: 0\n- `dora lost [--limit N]` - Find unused exported symbols. Default limit: 50\n- `dora treasure [--limit N]` - Find most referenced files and files with most dependencies. Default: 10\n\n### Architecture Analysis\n\n- `dora cycles [--limit N]` - Detect circular dependencies. Empty = good. Default: 50\n- `dora coupling [--threshold N]` - Find bidirectionally dependent file pairs. Default threshold: 5\n- `dora complexity [--sort metric]` - Show file complexity (symbol_count, outgoing_deps, incoming_deps, stability_ratio, complexity_score). Sort by: complexity, symbols, stability. Default: complexity\n\n### Change Impact\n\n- `dora changes <ref>` - Show files changed since git ref and their impact\n- `dora graph <path> [--depth N] [--direction type]` - Generate dependency graph. Direction: deps, rdeps, both. Default: both, depth 1\n\n### Documentation\n\n- `dora docs [--type TYPE]` - List all documentation files. Use --type to filter by md or txt\n- `dora docs search <query> [--limit N]` - Search through documentation content. Default limit: 20\n- `dora docs show <path> [--content]` - Show document metadata and references. Use --content to include full text\n\n**Note:** To find where a symbol is documented, use `dora symbol` which includes a `documented_in` field. To find documentation about a file, use `dora file` which also includes `documented_in`.\n\n### Database\n\n- `dora schema` - Show database schema (tables, columns, indexes)\n- `dora cookbook show [recipe]` - Query patterns with real examples (quickstart, methods, references, exports)\n- `dora query \"<sql>\"` - Execute read-only SQL query against the database\n\n## When to Use What\n\n- Finding symbols → `dora symbol`\n- Understanding a file → `dora file`\n- Impact of changes → `dora rdeps`, `dora refs`\n- Finding entry points → `dora treasure`, `dora leaves`\n- Architecture issues → `dora cycles`, `dora coupling`, `dora complexity`\n- Navigation → `dora deps`, `dora adventure`\n- Dead code → `dora lost`\n- Finding documentation → `dora symbol` (shows documented_in), `dora docs search`\n- Listing documentation → `dora docs`\n- Custom queries → `dora cookbook` for examples, `dora schema` for structure, `dora query` to execute\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. `dora status` - Check index health\n2. `dora treasure` - Find core files\n3. `dora file <path>` - Understand specific files\n4. `dora deps`/`dora rdeps` - Navigate relationships\n5. `dora refs` - Check usage before changes\n\n## Common Patterns: DON''T vs DO\n\nFinding where a symbol is defined:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep -r \"class AuthService\" .\n# DON''T: grep -r \"function validateToken\" .\n# DON''T: Glob(\"**/*.ts\") then search each file\n# DO:\ndora symbol AuthService\ndora symbol validateToken\n```\n\nFinding all usages of a function/class:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep -r \"AuthService\" . --include=\"*.ts\"\n# DON''T: Grep(\"AuthService\", glob=\"**/*.ts\")\n# DO:\ndora refs AuthService\n```\n\nFinding files that import a module:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep -r \"from.*auth/service\" .\n# DON''T: grep -r \"import.*AuthService\" .\n# DO:\ndora rdeps src/auth/service.ts\n```\n\nFinding what a file imports:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep \"^import\" src/app.ts\n# DON''T: cat src/app.ts | grep import\n# DO:\ndora deps src/app.ts\ndora imports src/app.ts\n```\n\nFinding files in a directory:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: find src/components -name \"*.tsx\"\n# DON''T: Glob(\"src/components/**/*.tsx\")\n# DO:\ndora ls src/components\ndora ls src/components --sort symbols  # With metadata\n```\n\nFinding entry points or core files:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep -r \"export.*main\" .\n# DON''T: find . -name \"index.ts\" -o -name \"main.ts\"\n# DO:\ndora treasure           # Most referenced files\ndora file src/index.ts  # Understand the entry point\n```\n\nUnderstanding a file''s purpose:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: Read file, manually trace imports\n# DON''T: grep for all imports, then read each\n# DO:\ndora file src/auth/service.ts   # See symbols, deps, rdeps at once\n```\n\nFinding unused code:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep each export manually across codebase\n# DON''T: Complex script to track exports vs imports\n# DO:\ndora lost     # Unused exported symbols\ndora leaves   # Files with no dependents\n```\n\nChecking for circular dependencies:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: Manually trace imports in multiple files\n# DON''T: Write custom script to detect cycles\n# DO:\ndora cycles\n```\n\nImpact analysis for refactoring:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: Manually grep for imports and usages\n# DON''T: Read multiple files to understand impact\n# DO:\ndora rdeps src/types.ts --depth 2     # See full impact\ndora refs UserContext                 # All usages\ndora complexity --sort complexity     # Find risky files\n```\n\nFinding documentation for code:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: grep -r \"AuthService\" docs/\n# DON''T: Manually search through README files\n# DO:\ndora symbol AuthService                 # Shows documented_in field\ndora file src/auth/service.ts           # Shows documented_in field\ndora docs search \"authentication\"       # Search doc content\ndora docs                               # List all docs\n```\n\nUnderstanding what a document covers:\n\n```bash\n# DON''T: Read entire doc, manually trace references\n# DON''T: grep for symbol names in the doc\n# DO:\ndora docs show README.md                # See all symbols/files/docs referenced\ndora docs show docs/api.md --content    # Include full content\n```\n\n## Practical Examples\n\nUnderstanding a feature:\n\n```bash\ndora symbol AuthService              # Find the service\ndora file src/auth/service.ts        # See what it depends on\ndora rdeps src/auth/service.ts       # See what uses it\ndora refs validateToken              # Find all token validation usage\n```\n\nImpact analysis before refactoring:\n\n```bash\ndora file src/types.ts               # See current dependencies\ndora rdeps src/types.ts --depth 2    # See full impact tree\ndora refs UserContext                # Find all usages of the type\ndora complexity --sort stability     # Find stable vs volatile files\n```\n\nFinding dead code:\n\n```bash\ndora lost --limit 100                # Unused exported symbols\ndora leaves                          # Files nothing depends on\ndora file src/old-feature.ts         # Verify it''s truly unused\n```\n\nArchitecture investigation:\n\n```bash\ndora cycles                          # Check for circular deps (should be empty)\ndora coupling --threshold 10         # Find tightly coupled modules\ndora complexity --sort complexity    # Find complex/risky files\ndora treasure                        # Find architectural hubs\n```\n\nNavigating unfamiliar code:\n\n```bash\ndora map                             # Overview of packages and structure\ndora treasure                        # Find entry points and core files\ndora file src/index.ts               # Start from main entry\ndora deps src/index.ts --depth 2     # See what it depends on\ndora adventure src/a.ts src/b.ts     # Find connection between modules\n```\n\nWorking with changes:\n\n```bash\ndora changes main                    # See what changed vs main branch\ndora rdeps src/modified.ts           # Check impact of your changes\ndora graph src/modified.ts --depth 2 # Visualize dependency tree\n```\n\nCustom analysis:\n\n```bash\ndora cookbook show methods                # See query pattern examples\ndora schema                          # See database structure\ndora query \"SELECT f.path, COUNT(s.id) as symbols FROM files f JOIN symbols s ON s.file_id = f.id WHERE s.is_local = 0 GROUP BY f.path ORDER BY symbols DESC LIMIT 20\"\n```\n\nWorking with documentation:\n\n```bash\ndora symbol AuthService              # Shows documented_in field\ndora docs show README.md             # What does README reference?\ndora docs search \"setup\"             # Find all docs about setup\ndora docs                            # List all documentation files\ndora docs --type md                  # List only markdown docs\n```\n\n## Advanced Tips\n\nPerformance:\n\n- dora uses denormalized data for instant queries (symbol_count, reference_count, dependent_count)\n- Incremental indexing only reindexes changed files\n- Use `--limit` to cap results for large codebases\n\nSymbol filtering:\n\n- Local symbols (parameters, closure vars) are filtered by default with `is_local = 0`\n- Use `--kind` to filter by symbol type (function, class, interface, type, etc.)\n- Symbol search is substring-based, not fuzzy\n\nDependencies:\n\n- `deps` shows outgoing dependencies (what this imports)\n- `rdeps` shows incoming dependencies (what imports this)\n- Use `--depth` to explore transitive dependencies\n- High rdeps count = high-impact file (changes affect many files)\n\nArchitecture metrics:\n\n- `complexity_score = symbol_count × incoming_deps` (higher = riskier to change)\n- `stability_ratio = incoming_deps / outgoing_deps` (higher = more stable)\n- Empty `cycles` output = healthy architecture\n- High `coupling` (> 20 symbols) = consider refactoring\n\nDocumentation:\n\n- Automatically indexes `.md` and `.txt` files\n- Tracks symbol references (e.g., mentions of `AuthService`)\n- Tracks file references (e.g., mentions of `src/auth/service.ts`)\n- Tracks document-to-document references (e.g., README linking to docs/api.md)\n- Use `dora symbol` or `dora file` to see where code is documented (via `documented_in` field)\n- Use `dora docs` to list all documentation files\n- Use `dora docs show` to see what a document covers with line numbers\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Includes local symbols (parameters) in `dora file` and `dora exports`\n- Symbol search is substring-based, not fuzzy\n- Index is a snapshot, updates at checkpoints\n- Documentation indexing processes text files (.md, .txt, etc.) at index time\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:00:29.314Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring instant insights into code structure, dependencies, and architectural relationships.","zh":"适合需要对代码结构、依赖关系和架构关系有即时洞察的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード構造、依存関係、およびアーキテクチャ関係に関する即時的な洞察が必要なコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"코드 구조, 의존성 및 아키텍처 관계에 대한 즉각적인 통찰이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren conocimientos instantáneos sobre la estructura del código, las dependencias y las relaciones arquitectónicas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des connaissances instantanées sur la structure du code, les dépendances et les relations architecturales.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die sofortige Einblicke in die Code-Struktur, Abhängigkeiten und architektonische Beziehungen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem insights instantâneos sobre a estrutura do código, dependências e relações arquiteturais.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих мгновенных洞察ений в структуру кода, зависимости и архитектурные отношения.","ar":"مثالي لعمال التحليل البرمجي الذين يحتاجون إلى رؤى فورية بشأن هيكل البرنامج واعتماداته وعلاقاته المعمارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to instantly understand codebases through indexed databases, providing insights into symbol definitions, dependencies, and architectural patterns using CLI tools like grep, find, and glob alternatives. It offers advanced code exploration capabilities, including impact analysis for changes and code health assessments.","zh":"使代理能够通过索引数据库立即了解代码库，提供对符号定义、依存关系和使用CLI工具（如grep、find和glob替代品）进行的架构模式的洞察。它提供高级代码探索功能，包括更改的影响分析和代码健康评估。","ja":"エージェントがCLIツール（grep、find、globの代替品など）を使用して、シンボル定義、依存関係、アーキテクチャパターンに関する洞察を提供する索引データベースを介してコードベースを即座に理解できるようにします。コードの変更の影響分析やコードヘルス評価などの高度なコード探索機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 CLI 도구(grep, find, glob 대체品 등)를 사용하여 코드베이스를 즉시 이해할 수 있도록 하며, 심볼 정의, 의존성, 아키텍처 패턴에 대한 통찰력을 제공합니다. 코드 변경의 영향 분석 및 코드 건강 평가를 포함한 고급 코드 탐색 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a comprender instantáneamente las bases de código a través de bases de datos indexadas, proporcionando conocimientos sobre definiciones de símbolos, dependencias y patrones arquitectónicos utilizando herramientas de línea de comandos como grep, find y alternativas a glob. Ofrece capacidades avanzadas de exploración de código, incluyendo análisis de impacto para cambios y evaluaciones de salud del código.","fr":"Permet aux agents de comprendre instantanément les bases de code à travers des bases de données indexées, fournissant des connaissances sur les définitions de symboles, les dépendances et les modèles architecturaux en utilisant des outils de ligne de commande tels que grep, find et des alternatives à glob. Il offre des capacités avancées d''exploration de code, notamment l''analyse d''impact pour les modifications et les évaluations de santé du code.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Codebasen sofort durch indizierte Datenbanken zu verstehen, indem Kenntnisse über Symboldefinitionen, Abhängigkeiten und architektonische Muster bereitgestellt werden, die CLI-Tools wie grep, find und glob-Alternativen verwenden. Es bietet erweiterte Code-Explorationsfunktionen, einschließlich Auswirkungsanalysen für Änderungen und Code-Gesundheitsbewertungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a entenderem instantaneamente as bases de código por meio de bancos de dados indexados, fornecendo insights sobre definições de símbolos, dependências e padrões arquiteturais usando ferramentas de linha de comando como grep, find e alternativas de glob. Oferece capacidades avançadas de exploração de código, incluindo análise de impacto para alterações e avaliações de saúde do código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью мгновенно понимать кодовые базы посредством индексированных баз данных, предоставляя сведения о определениях символов, зависимостях и архитектурных шаблонах с использованием инструментов командной строки, таких как grep, find и альтернативы glob. Предлагает расширенные возможности изучения кода, включая анализ воздействия изменений и оценку здоровья кода.","ar":"تمكّن العمال من فهم الأساس البرمجي على الفور من خلال قواعد البيانات المُفهرسة، وتوفير رؤى حول تعريفات الرموز والاعتمادات وأنماط البنية باستخدام أدوات سطر الأوامر مثل grep و find وبدائل glob. كما يقدم إمكانيات متقدمة لاستكشاف البرامج، بما في ذلك تحليل التأثير للتغييرات وتقييم صحة البرنامج."},"useCases":{"en":["Navigating complex codebases","Analyzing symbol dependencies","Performing impact analysis for code changes","Understanding architectural patterns and code health"],"zh":["导航复杂的代码库","分析符号依赖","执行代码更改的影响分析","理解架构模式和代码健康"],"ja":["複雑なコードベースをナビゲートする","シンボルの依存関係を分析する","コード変更の影響分析を実行する","アーキテクチャパターンとコードヘルスを理解する"],"ko":["복잡한 코드베이스를 탐색한다","심볼 의존성을 분석한다","코드 변경의 영향 분석을 수행한다","아키텍처 패턴과 코드 건강을 이해한다"],"es":["Navegación en bases de código complejas","Análisis de dependencias de símbolos","Realización de análisis de impacto para cambios de código","Comprensión de patrones arquitectónicos y salud del código"],"fr":["Navigation dans des bases de code complexes","Analyse des dépendances de symboles","Réalisations d''analyses d''impact pour les modifications de code","Compréhension des modèles architecturaux et de la santé du code"],"de":["Navigation in komplexen Codebasen","Analyse von Symbolabhängigkeiten","Durchführung von Auswirkungsanalysen für Codeänderungen","Verständnis von architektonischen Mustern und Code-Gesundheit"],"pt":["Navegar por bases de código complexas","Analizar dependências de símbolos","Realizar análise de impacto para alterações de código","Compreender padrões arquiteturais e saúde do código"],"ru":["Навигация по сложным кодовым базам","Анализ зависимостей символов","Проведение анализа воздействия для изменений кода","Понимание архитектурных шаблонов и здоровья кода"],"ar":["الملاحة في قواعد البرامج المعقدة","تحليل الاعتمادات الرمزية","إجراء تحليل التأثير للتغييرات البرمجية","فهم الأنماط المعمارية وصحة البرنامج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires indexed database of code structure","CLI-based interface"],"zh":["需要代码结构的索引数据库","基于CLI的接口"],"ja":["コード構造の索引データベースが必要","CLIベースのインターフェイス"],"ko":["코드 구조의 인덱스 데이터베이스가 필요","CLI 기반 인터페이스"],"es":["Requiere base de datos indexada de la estructura del código","Interfaz basada en CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite une base de données indexée de la structure du code","Interface basée sur CLI"],"de":["Benötigt indizierte Datenbank der Code-Struktur","CLI-basierte Schnittstelle"],"pt":["Exige banco de dados indexado da estrutura do código","Interface baseada em CLI"],"ru":["Требует индексированной базы данных структуры кода","Интерфейс на основе CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب قاعدة بيانات مُفهرسة لهيكل البرنامج","واجهة المستخدم التي تعتمد على سطر الأوامر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ArvorCo/Relentless/prd', 'community', 'ArvorCo', 'Relentless', 'ArvorCo/Relentless', 'prd', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T03:00:12.719Z', NULL, '{"id":"ArvorCo/Relentless/prd","name":"prd","description":{"zh":"PRD ","ja":"PRD ","ko":" PRD ","es":"El orquestador de agentes de código AI es una herramienta que te permite crear documentos de requisitos de producto detallados y claros","fr":"L''orchestrateur d''agents de code AI est un outil qui vous permet de créer des documents de spécifications de produit détaillés et clairs","de":"Der AI-Code-Agenten-Orchestrierer ist ein Tool, das Ihnen ermöglicht, detaillierte und klare Produktanforderungsdokumente zu erstellen","pt":"O orquestrador de agentes de IA PRD é uma ferramenta que cria documentos de requisitos de produto detalhados e automatiza tarefas de codificação","ru":"Универсальный оркестратор агентов ИИ PRD - это инструмент, который создает подробные документы требований к продукту и автоматизирует задачи кодирования","ar":"مدير وسيط وكيل إيه آي بى آر دي هو أداة تنشئ مستندات متطلبات المنتج المفصلة وتأتمة مهام الترميز","en":"Universal AI Agent Orchestrator - Run any AI coding agent (Claude Code, Amp, OpenCode, Codex, Droid, Gemini) repeatedly until all tasks are complete"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Universal AI Agent Orchestrator - PRD ","ja":"PRD","ko":" PRD ","es":"Orquestador de Agentes de Código AI","fr":"Orchestrateur d''Agents de Code AI","de":"AI-Code-Agenten-Orchestrierer","pt":"Orquestrador de Agentes de IA PRD","ru":"Универсальный оркестратор агентов ИИ PRD","ar":"مدير وسيط وكيل إيه آي بى آر دي","en":"prd"},"description":{"zh":"PRD ","ja":"PRD ","ko":" PRD ","es":"El orquestador de agentes de código AI es una herramienta que te permite crear documentos de requisitos de producto detallados y claros","fr":"L''orchestrateur d''agents de code AI est un outil qui vous permet de créer des documents de spécifications de produit détaillés et clairs","de":"Der AI-Code-Agenten-Orchestrierer ist ein Tool, das Ihnen ermöglicht, detaillierte und klare Produktanforderungsdokumente zu erstellen","pt":"O orquestrador de agentes de IA PRD é uma ferramenta que cria documentos de requisitos de produto detalhados e automatiza tarefas de codificação","ru":"Универсальный оркестратор агентов ИИ PRD - это инструмент, который создает подробные документы требований к продукту и автоматизирует задачи кодирования","ar":"مدير وسيط وكيل إيه آي بى آر دي هو أداة تنشئ مستندات متطلبات المنتج المفصلة وتأتمة مهام الترميز","en":"Universal AI Agent Orchestrator - Run any AI coding agent (Claude Code, Amp, OpenCode, Codex, Droid, Gemini) repeatedly until all tasks are complete"},"definition":{"en":"Universal AI Agent Orchestrator - Run any AI coding agent (Claude Code, Amp, OpenCode, Codex, Droid, Gemini) repeatedly until all tasks are complete"},"features":{"zh":["PRD","3-5","PRD","relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md","AI","PRD"],"ja":["PRD","3-5","PRD","relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md","AI","PRD"],"ko":[" PRD","3-5"," PRD","relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md"," AI"," PRD"],"es":["Crea documentos de requisitos de producto claros y acciónables","Permite la automatización de la creación de documentos","Soporta múltiples agentes de código AI","Genera documentos en formato Markdown","Permite la personalización de las preguntas de aclaración"],"fr":["Crée des documents de spécifications de produit clairs et actionnables","Permet l''automatisation de la création de documents","Prend en charge plusieurs agents de code AI","Génère des documents au format Markdown","Permet la personnalisation des questions de clarification"],"de":["Erstellt klare und umsetzbare Produktanforderungsdokumente","Ermöglicht die Automatisierung der Dokumentenerstellung","Unterstützt mehrere AI-Code-Agenten","Erstellt Dokumente im Markdown-Format","Ermöglicht die Anpassung der Klarstellungsfragen"],"pt":["Criação de documentos de requisitos de produto detalhados","Automatização de tarefas de codificação com agentes de IA","Suporte a vários agentes de IA","Geração de PRD estruturado","Salvar em formato markdown"],"ru":["Создание подробных документов требований к продукту","Автоматизация задач кодирования с агентами ИИ","Поддержка нескольких агентов ИИ","Генерация структурированного PRD","Сохранение в формате markdown"],"ar":["إنشاء مستندات متطلبات المنتج المفصلة","أتمتة مهام الترميز مع وكلاء إيه آي","دعم وكلاء إيه آي متعددين","توليد بريد إلكتروني منظم","حفظ بالتنسيق markdown"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PRD","AI","PRD","AI","PRD","AI PRD"],"ja":["PRD","AI","PRD","AI","PRD","AI PRD"],"ko":[" PRD"," AI"," PRD"," AI"," PRD"," AI PRD"],"es":["orquestador de agentes de código AI","creación de documentos de requisitos de producto","automatización de documentos","agentes de código AI","documentos de requisitos de producto","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["orchestrateur d''agents de code AI","création de documents de spécifications de produit","automatisation de documents","agents de code AI","documents de spécifications de produit","développement de logiciels"],"de":["AI-Code-Agenten-Orchestrierer","Erstellung von Produktanforderungsdokumenten","Automatisierung von Dokumenten","AI-Code-Agenten","Produktanforderungsdokumente","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["orquestrador de agentes de IA","PRD","documentos de requisitos de produto","automatização de tarefas de codificação","agentes de IA","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["универсальный оркестратор агентов ИИ","PRD","документы требований к продукту","автоматизация задач кодирования","агенты ИИ","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مدير وسيط وكيل إيه آي","بى آر دي","مستندات متطلبات المنتج","أتمتة مهام الترميز","وكلاء إيه آي","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"ArvorCo","repo":"Relentless","repoPath":"ArvorCo/Relentless","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd","description":"Generate a Product Requirements Document (PRD) for a new feature. Use when planning a feature, starting a new project, or when asked to create a PRD. Triggers on: create a prd, write prd for, plan this feature, requirements for, spec out.","bodyPreview":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the in","body":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt is ambiguous. Focus on:\n\n- **Problem/Goal:** What problem does this solve?\n- **Core Functionality:** What are the key actions?\n- **Scope/Boundaries:** What should it NOT do?\n- **Success Criteria:** How do we know it''s done?\n\n### Format Questions Like This:\n\n```\n1. What is the primary goal of this feature?\n   A. Improve user onboarding experience\n   B. Increase user retention\n   C. Reduce support burden\n   D. Other: [please specify]\n\n2. Who is the target user?\n   A. New users only\n   B. Existing users only\n   C. All users\n   D. Admin users only\n\n3. What is the scope?\n   A. Minimal viable version\n   B. Full-featured implementation\n   C. Just the backend/API\n   D. Just the UI\n```\n\nThis lets users respond with \"1A, 2C, 3B\" for quick iteration.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: PRD Structure\n\nGenerate the PRD with these sections:\n\n### 1. Introduction/Overview\nBrief description of the feature and the problem it solves.\n\n### 2. Goals\nSpecific, measurable objectives (bullet list).\n\n### 3. User Stories\nEach story needs:\n- **Title:** Short descriptive name\n- **Description:** \"As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit]\"\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** Verifiable checklist of what \"done\" means\n\nEach story should be small enough to implement in one focused session.\n\n**Format:**\n```markdown\n### US-001: [Title]\n**Description:** As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Specific verifiable criterion\n- [ ] Another criterion\n- [ ] Typecheck/lint passes\n- [ ] **[UI stories only]** Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Acceptance criteria must be verifiable, not vague. \"Works correctly\" is bad. \"Button shows confirmation dialog before deleting\" is good.\n- **For any story with UI changes:** Always include \"Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\" as acceptance criteria. This ensures visual verification of frontend work.\n\n### 4. Functional Requirements\nNumbered list of specific functionalities:\n- \"FR-1: The system must allow users to...\"\n- \"FR-2: When a user clicks X, the system must...\"\n\nBe explicit and unambiguous.\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (Out of Scope)\nWhat this feature will NOT include. Critical for managing scope.\n\n### 6. Design Considerations (Optional)\n- UI/UX requirements\n- Link to mockups if available\n- Relevant existing components to reuse\n\n### 7. Technical Considerations (Optional)\n- Known constraints or dependencies\n- Integration points with existing systems\n- Performance requirements\n\n### 8. Success Metrics\nHow will success be measured?\n- \"Reduce time to complete X by 50%\"\n- \"Increase conversion rate by 10%\"\n\n### 9. Open Questions\nRemaining questions or areas needing clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Writing for Junior Developers\n\nThe PRD reader may be a junior developer or AI agent. Therefore:\n\n- Be explicit and unambiguous\n- Avoid jargon or explain it\n- Provide enough detail to understand purpose and core logic\n- Number requirements for easy reference\n- Use concrete examples where helpful\n\n---\n\n## Output\n\n- **Format:** Markdown (`.md`)\n- **Location:** `relentless/features/[feature-name]/`\n- **Filename:** `prd.md`\n\n**Note:** Create the feature directory first if it doesn''t exist: `mkdir -p relentless/features/[feature-name]`\n\n---\n\n## Example PRD\n\n```markdown\n# PRD: Task Priority System\n\n## Introduction\n\nAdd priority levels to tasks so users can focus on what matters most. Tasks can be marked as high, medium, or low priority, with visual indicators and filtering to help users manage their workload effectively.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Allow assigning priority (high/medium/low) to any task\n- Provide clear visual differentiation between priority levels\n- Enable filtering and sorting by priority\n- Default new tasks to medium priority\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US-001: Add priority field to database\n**Description:** As a developer, I need to store task priority so it persists across sessions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Add priority column to tasks table: ''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'' (default ''medium'')\n- [ ] Generate and run migration successfully\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n\n### US-002: Display priority indicator on task cards\n**Description:** As a user, I want to see task priority at a glance so I know what needs attention first.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Each task card shows colored priority badge (red=high, yellow=medium, gray=low)\n- [ ] Priority visible without hovering or clicking\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-003: Add priority selector to task edit\n**Description:** As a user, I want to change a task''s priority when editing it.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Priority dropdown in task edit modal\n- [ ] Shows current priority as selected\n- [ ] Saves immediately on selection change\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-004: Filter tasks by priority\n**Description:** As a user, I want to filter the task list to see only high-priority items when I''m focused.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Filter dropdown with options: All | High | Medium | Low\n- [ ] Filter persists in URL params\n- [ ] Empty state message when no tasks match filter\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n- FR-1: Add `priority` field to tasks table (''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'', default ''medium'')\n- FR-2: Display colored priority badge on each task card\n- FR-3: Include priority selector in task edit modal\n- FR-4: Add priority filter dropdown to task list header\n- FR-5: Sort by priority within each status column (high to medium to low)\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No priority-based notifications or reminders\n- No automatic priority assignment based on due date\n- No priority inheritance for subtasks\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n- Reuse existing badge component with color variants\n- Filter state managed via URL search params\n- Priority stored in database, not computed\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- Users can change priority in under 2 clicks\n- High-priority tasks immediately visible at top of lists\n- No regression in task list performance\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should priority affect task ordering within a column?\n- Should we add keyboard shortcuts for priority changes?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore saving the PRD:\n\n- [ ] Asked clarifying questions with lettered options\n- [ ] Incorporated user''s answers\n- [ ] User stories are small and specific\n- [ ] Functional requirements are numbered and unambiguous\n- [ ] Non-goals section defines clear boundaries\n- [ ] Saved to `relentless/features/[feature-name]/prd.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:00:12.719Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Coding Agents like Claude Code, Amp, and OpenCode needing structured product requirement documentation","zh":"适用于Claude Code、Amp和OpenCode等AI编码代理，需要结构化的产品需求文档","ja":"Claude Code、Amp、OpenCodeなどのAIコーディングエージェントに適しています。構造化された製品要件文書が必要です","ko":"Claude Code, Amp, OpenCode 등의 AI 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다. 구조화된 제품 요구사항 문서가 필요합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de codificación de IA como Claude Code, Amp y OpenCode que necesitan documentación de requisitos de producto estructurada","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de codage IA tels que Claude Code, Amp et OpenCode nécessitant une documentation de spécifications de produit structurée","de":"Ideal für AI-Coding-Agents wie Claude Code, Amp und OpenCode, die eine strukturierte Produktanforderungsdokumentation benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Codificação de IA como Claude Code, Amp e OpenCode que necessitam de documentação de requisitos de produto estruturada","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодирования ИИ, таких как Claude Code, Amp и OpenCode, требующих структурированной документации требований к продукту","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البرمجيين للذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Amp و OpenCode الذين يحتاجون إلى توثيق متطلبات المنتج المنظمة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate detailed Product Requirements Documents (PRD) in Markdown format, utilizing clarifying questions and feature descriptions to produce clear, actionable, and implementation-ready documents, saved as .md files in a relentless/features directory","zh":"赋予代理生成详细的产品需求文档（PRD），以Markdown格式呈现，利用澄清问题和功能描述生成清晰、可执行和可实施的文档，保存为.md文件在relentless/features目录中","ja":"エージェントに詳細な製品要件文書（PRD）を生成する能力を与えます。Markdown形式で、明確化された質問と機能説明を使用して、明確で実行可能で実装可能な文書を生成します。これらの文書は、relentless/featuresディレクトリ内の.mdファイルとして保存されます","ko":"에이전트가 상세한 제품 요구사항 문서(PRD)를 생성할 수 있도록 합니다. Markdown 형식으로 명확한 질문과 기능 설명을 사용하여 명확하고 실행 가능하며 구현 가능한 문서를 생성하여 relentless/features 디렉토리에 .md 파일로 저장합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes para generar documentos de requisitos de producto detallados (PRD) en formato Markdown, utilizando preguntas aclaratorias y descripciones de características para producir documentos claros, accionables y listos para la implementación, guardados como archivos .md en un directorio relentless/features","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des documents de spécifications de produit détaillés (PRD) au format Markdown, en utilisant des questions clarificatrices et des descriptions de fonctionnalités pour produire des documents clairs, actionnables et prêts à la mise en œuvre, enregistrés sous forme de fichiers .md dans un répertoire relentless/features","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, detaillierte Produktanforderungsdokumente (PRD) im Markdown-Format zu generieren, indem sie klarifizierende Fragen und Funktionsbeschreibungen verwenden, um klare, umsetzbare und implementierbare Dokumente zu erstellen, die als .md-Dateien im Verzeichnis relentless/features gespeichert werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar documentos de Requisitos de Produto (PRD) detalhados no formato Markdown, utilizando perguntas esclarecedoras e descrições de recursos para produzir documentos claros, ação e prontos para implementação, salvos como arquivos .md no diretório relentless/features","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать подробные документы требований к продукту (PRD) в формате Markdown, используя уточняющие вопросы и описания функций для создания ясных, действенных и готовых к реализации документов, сохраняемых как файлы .md в директории relentless/features","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توليد وثائق متطلبات المنتج (PRD) مفصلة بالتنسيق Markdown، باستخدام أسئلة توضيحية ووصف الميزات لإنتاج وثائق واضحة وقابلة للتنفيذ وجاهزة للتنفيذ، محفوظة كملفات .md في الدليل relentless/features"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating PRDs for new feature development","Creating structured documentation for coding projects","Clarifying feature requirements through essential questions"],"zh":["为新功能开发生成PRD","为编码项目创建结构化文档","通过基本问题澄清功能需求"],"ja":["新機能開発のためのPRDの生成","コーディングプロジェクトのための構造化ドキュメントの作成","基本的な質問を通じて機能要件の明確化"],"ko":["새 기능 개발을 위한 PRD 생성","코딩 프로젝트를 위한 구조화된 문서 생성","기본적인 질문을 통해 기능 요구사항 명확화"],"es":["Generación de PRD para el desarrollo de nuevas características","Creación de documentación estructurada para proyectos de codificación","Aclaración de los requisitos de las características a través de preguntas esenciales"],"fr":["Génération de PRD pour le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Création de documentation structurée pour les projets de codage","Clarification des spécifications de fonctionnalités à l''aide de questions essentielles"],"de":["Erstellung von PRD für die Entwicklung neuer Funktionen","Erstellung von strukturierter Dokumentation für Codierungsprojekte","Klärung der Funktionsanforderungen durch wesentliche Fragen"],"pt":["Gerar PRDs para desenvolvimento de novos recursos","Criar documentação estruturada para projetos de codificação","Esclarecer requisitos de recursos por meio de perguntas essenciais"],"ru":["Генерировать PRD для разработки новых функций","Создавать структурированную документацию для проектов кодирования","Уточнять требования к функциям с помощью основных вопросов"],"ar":["توليد وثائق PRD لتنمية ميزات جديدة","إنشاء توثيق منظم لمشاريع البرمجة","توضيح متطلبات الميزات من خلال أسئلة أساسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input for feature descriptions","Limited to generating PRDs, does not implement features"],"zh":["需要用户输入功能描述","仅限生成PRD，不实施功能"],"ja":["機能説明の入力をユーザーに要求する","PRDの生成のみに限定され、機能の実装は行わない"],"ko":["기능 설명을 위한 사용자 입력이 필요","PRD 생성만 가능하며 기능 구현은 수행하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere la entrada del usuario para las descripciones de características","Limitado a la generación de PRD, no implementa características"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour les descriptions de fonctionnalités","Limité à la génération de PRD, ne met pas en œuvre les fonctionnalités"],"de":["Benötigt Benutzereingaben für Funktionsbeschreibungen","Begrenzt auf die Generierung von PRD, implementiert keine Funktionen"],"pt":["Requer entrada do usuário para descrições de recursos","Limitado a gerar PRDs, não implementa recursos"],"ru":["Требует ввода пользователя для описаний функций","Ограничен генерацией PRD, не реализует функции"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال المستخدم لوصف الميزات","محدود بتوليد وثائق PRD، لا ينفذ الميزات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
