플ロー 처리","데이터베이스 의존성 최소화","모듈화 설계, 확장성이 높음","CLI와 설정 기능을 제공","다양한 워크플ロー 기능을 지원"],"es":["Infraestructura serverless para flujos de trabajo","Diseño minimalista y eficiente","Soporte para mensajería y configuración","Compatibilidad con módulos de características","CLI y configuración simplificada","Documentación detallada y guías de desarrollo"],"fr":["Infrastructure serverless pour les flux de travail","Conception minimaliste et efficace","Prise en charge de la messagerie et de la configuration","Compatibilité avec les modules de fonctionnalités","CLI et configuration simplifiées","Documentation détaillée et guides de développement"],"de":["Serverless-Infrastruktur für Arbeitsabläufe","Minimalistisches und effizientes Design","Unterstützung für Messaging und Konfiguration","Kompatibilität mit Funktionsmodulen","CLI und vereinfachte Konfiguration","Detaillierte Dokumentation und Entwicklungshandbücher"],"pt":["Execução de fluxo de trabalho serverless","Infraestrutura existente","Eficiência e minimização da dependência de bancos de dados","Mensagens e CLI","Módulos de recursos específicos"],"ru":["Выполнение рабочих потоков без сервера","Существующая инфраструктура","Эффективность и минимизация зависимости от баз данных","Сообщения и CLI","Модули специфических возможностей"],"ar":["تشغيل سير عمل خالي من الخوادم","بيئات موجودة","فعالية وتقليل الاعتماد على قواعد البيانات","رسائل و CLI","مكونات ميزات محددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Serverless","工作流 DSL","事件驱动","最小化数据库依赖","模块化设计","CLI","配置"],"ja":["サーバーレス","ワークフロー DSL","イベント駆動","データベース依存最小化","モジュール化設計","CLI","設定"],"ko":["서버리스","워크플ロー DSL","이벤트 주도","데이터베이스 의존성 최소화","모듈화 설계","CLI","설정"],"es":["runner dev","infraestructura serverless","desarrollo de software","flujos de trabajo","eficiencia","minimalismo","mensajería","configuración","módulos de características"],"fr":["runner dev","infrastructure serverless","développement de logiciels","flux de travail","efficacité","minimalisme","messagerie","configuration","modules de fonctionnalités"],"de":["runner dev","serverless-infrastruktur","software-entwicklung","arbeitsabläufe","effizienz","minimalismus","messaging","konfiguration","funktionsmodule"],"pt":["runner dev","serverless workflow","infraestrutura existente","eficiência","bancos de dados","desenvolvimento de software","plataforma de execução de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["runner dev","безсерверная среда","существующая инфраструктура","эффективность","базы данных","разработка программного обеспечения","платформа для выполнения рабочих потоков"],"ar":["رنر ديف","سير عمل خالي من الخوادم","بيئات موجودة","فعالية","قواعد البيانات","تطوير البرمجيات","منصة تشغيل سير عمل"]}},"owner":"lemline","repo":"lemline","repoPath":"lemline/lemline","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"runner-dev","description":"Development guide for the lemline-runner ecosystem. Use when working with the modular runner architecture (lemline-runner-* modules), messaging (commands/events channels), feature modules (waits, retries, parents, schedules, listeners, forks, failures), shared infrastructure (lemline-runner-common), CLI commands, configuration, repositories with Kotlin coroutines, or Flyway migrations. Covers the dual-channel architecture, outbox pattern, and production best practices for the Quarkus/Kotlin runtime.","bodyPreview":"# Lemline Runner Development Guide\n\n## Purpose\n\nGuide development across the **modular lemline-runner ecosystem** - a collection of feature-focused modules built on shared infrastructure. The main `lemline-runner` module provides messaging, CLI, and configuration, while feature modules (`lemline-runner-*`) implement specific workflow capabilities.\n\n**Core Documentation:**\n\n- [Main Runner README](lemline-runner/README.md) - Configuration, database, messaging setup\n- [CLI Commands](lemline-runner/","body":"# Lemline Runner Development Guide\n\n## Purpose\n\nGuide development across the **modular lemline-runner ecosystem** - a collection of feature-focused modules built on shared infrastructure. The main `lemline-runner` module provides messaging, CLI, and configuration, while feature modules (`lemline-runner-*`) implement specific workflow capabilities.\n\n**Core Documentation:**\n\n- [Main Runner README](lemline-runner/README.md) - Configuration, database, messaging setup\n- [CLI Commands](lemline-runner/docs/runner-cli.md)\n- [Configuration](lemline-runner/docs/runner-configuration.md)\n- [Messaging Architecture](lemline-runner/docs/runner-messaging.md)\n- [Database Tables](lemline-runner/docs/runner-tables.md)\n- [Repositories Guide](lemline-runner/docs/runner-repositories-guide.md)\n\n---\n\n## Module Architecture\n\n### Core Infrastructure\n\n| Module | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `lemline-runner-common` | Shared infrastructure: outbox pattern, cleaner pattern, repository abstractions, model interfaces |\n| `lemline-runner` | Main runtime: messaging (commands/events), CLI, configuration, activity runners |\n\n### Feature Modules\n\n| Module | Purpose | Tables |\n|--------|---------|--------|\n| `lemline-runner-definitions` | Workflow definition storage and cache sync | `lemline_definitions` |\n| `lemline-runner-waits` | Wait/sleep task implementation | `lemline_waits` |\n| `lemline-runner-retries` | Task retry scheduling with exponential backoff | `lemline_retries` |\n| `lemline-runner-parents` | Parent-child workflow relationships (run task) | `lemline_parents` |\n| `lemline-runner-forks` | Parallel branch execution (fork task) | `lemline_forks`, `lemline_fork_branches` |\n| `lemline-runner-schedules` | Scheduled workflow execution (cron/interval/after) | `lemline_schedules` |\n| `lemline-runner-listeners` | CloudEvent listeners (listen task) | `lemline_listeners`, `lemline_listener_events` |\n| `lemline-runner-failures` | Failed workflow tracking and dead letter storage | `lemline_failures` |\n\n**Each feature module has its own README.md with detailed architecture, file reference, and usage patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### If you need to work on...\n\n**A Specific Feature:**\n\nRead the module''s README first:\n- **Wait task** → [lemline-runner-waits/README.md](lemline-runner-waits/README.md)\n- **Retry logic** → [lemline-runner-retries/README.md](lemline-runner-retries/README.md)\n- **Parent-child workflows** → [lemline-runner-parents/README.md](lemline-runner-parents/README.md)\n- **Fork/parallel execution** → [lemline-runner-forks/README.md](lemline-runner-forks/README.md)\n- **Scheduled workflows** → [lemline-runner-schedules/README.md](lemline-runner-schedules/README.md)\n- **CloudEvent listeners** → [lemline-runner-listeners/README.md](lemline-runner-listeners/README.md)\n- **Failure tracking** → [lemline-runner-failures/README.md](lemline-runner-failures/README.md)\n- **Definition storage** → [lemline-runner-definitions/README.md](lemline-runner-definitions/README.md)\n\n**Messaging:**\n\nFirst, read [runner-messaging.md](lemline-runner/docs/runner-messaging.md)\n\n- **Add a new command/event type** →\n  Modify [WorkflowState.kt](lemline-core/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/core/states/WorkflowState.kt)\n- **Update commands behavior** →\n  Modify [WorkflowCommandHandler.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/messaging/commands/WorkflowCommandHandler.kt)\n- **Update events behavior** →\n  Modify [WorkflowEventHandler.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/messaging/events/WorkflowEventHandler.kt)\n\n**Shared Infrastructure:**\n\nRead [lemline-runner-common/README.md](lemline-runner-common/README.md) first\n\n- **Add new outbox processor** → Extend `AbstractOutbox<T>` in lemline-runner-common\n- **Add new cleaner** → Extend `AbstractCleaner<T>` in lemline-runner-common\n- **Add repository operations** → Add to `lemline-runner-common/repositories/ops/`\n- **Add model interface** → Create in `lemline-runner-common/models/`\n\n**Configuration:**\n\nFirst read [runner-configuration.md](lemline-runner/docs/runner-configuration.md)\n\n- **Add/Update config property** →\n  Modify [LemlineConfiguration.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/config/LemlineConfiguration.kt)\n- **Add database/broker type** → Read [runner-configuration.md](lemline-runner/docs/runner-configuration.md)\n\n**CLI:**\n\nFirst read [runner-cli.md](lemline-runner/docs/runner-cli.md#adding-a-new-cli-command)\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS Do This\n\n1. **Use `suspend` functions** for all database operations (Kotlin coroutines, NOT Mutiny)\n2. **Use native SQL** via repositories (NOT Hibernate ORM/Panache)\n3. **Use Flyway migrations** for all schema changes\n4. **Support all databases** (PostgreSQL, MySQL, H2) - use database-agnostic SQL\n5. **Use `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`** for outbox queries to prevent double-processing\n6. **Use IDV7** (UUID v7) for all entity IDs - time-sortable, globally unique\n7. **Test with all supported databases** when touching persistence layer\n\n### ❌ NEVER Do This\n\n1. **Use Mutiny (Uni/Multi)** - use Kotlin coroutines with `suspend` functions instead\n2. **Use Hibernate ORM/Panache** - use native SQL with repositories\n3. **Block the event loop** - all I/O must be non-blocking\n4. **Skip database migrations** - never modify tables directly\n5. **Use database-specific SQL** without providing variants for all databases\n6. **Commit sensitive data** (.env, credentials, API keys)\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### Modular Feature Design\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      lemline-runner (core)                         │\n│  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐ │\n│  │   Messaging      │  │   CLI Commands   │  │  Configuration   │ │\n│  │ (commands/events)│  │   (Picocli)      │  │   (Quarkus)      │ │\n│  └──────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘ │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                │\n                ┌───────────────┴────────────────┐\n                │  lemline-runner-common         │\n                │  (shared infrastructure)       │\n                │  • Outbox pattern              │\n                │  • Cleaner pattern             │\n                │  • Repository abstractions     │\n                │  • Model interfaces            │\n                └───────────────┬────────────────┘\n                                │\n        ┌───────────────────────┼────────────────────────┐\n        │                       │                        │\n┌───────▼──────┐   ┌───────────▼──────┐   ┌────────────▼─────┐\n│ Feature      │   │ Feature           │   │ Feature          │\n│ Modules      │   │ Modules           │   │ Modules          │\n│              │   │                   │   │                  │\n│ • waits      │   │ • schedules       │   │ • definitions    │\n│ • retries    │   │ • listeners       │   │ • failures       │\n│ • parents    │   │                   │   │                  │\n│ • forks      │   │                   │   │                  │\n└──────────────┘   └───────────────────┘   └──────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dual-Channel Messaging\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                  COMMANDS CHANNEL (high-throughput)                         │\n│  commands ──► WorkflowCommandHandler ──► commands                           │\n│       ▲                 │                                                   │\n│       │                 │ (needs persistence)                               │\n└───────│─────────────────│───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n        │                 │\n┌───────│─────────────────│───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│       │                 ▼              EVENTS CHANNEL                       │\n│       │               events ──► WorkflowEventHandler ──► Feature Modules   │\n│       │                                   │                                 │\n│       │                         ┌─────────┴─────────┐                       │\n│       │                         ▼                   ▼                       │\n│       │              ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐              │\n│       │              │ Feature Service │  │ Feature Service │              │\n│       │              │ (e.g., Waits)   │  │ (e.g., Parents) │              │\n│       │              └────────┬────────┘  └────────┬────────┘              │\n│       │                       │                    │                       │\n│       │                       ▼                    ▼                       │\n│       │              ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐              │\n│       │              │   DB Table      │  │   DB Table      │              │\n│       │              │ (lemline_waits) │  │(lemline_parents)│              │\n│       │              └────────┬────────┘  └─────────────────┘              │\n│       │                       │                                            │\n│       │                       ▼                                            │\n│       │              ┌─────────────────┐                                   │\n│       │              │  Outbox Relay   │                                   │\n│       └──────────────│ (scheduled poll)│                                   │\n│                      └─────────────────┘                                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Key principle:** State travels with messages. Database only used when necessary. Each feature is self-contained.\n\n### Key Files\n\n| Purpose           | File                                                                                                                        |\n|-------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Step execution    | [StepByStepRunner.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/StepByStepRunner.kt)                                |\n| Command handling  | [WorkflowCommandHandler.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/messaging/commands/WorkflowCommandHandler.kt) |\n| Event handling    | [WorkflowEventHandler.kt](lemline-runner/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/messaging/events/WorkflowEventHandler.kt)       |\n| Message structure | [InstanceMessage.kt](lemline-runner-common/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/common/messaging/InstanceMessage.kt)         |\n| Outbox base       | [AbstractOutbox.kt](lemline-runner-common/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/common/outbox/AbstractOutbox.kt)             |\n| Cleaner base      | [AbstractCleaner.kt](lemline-runner-common/src/main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/common/cleaner/AbstractCleaner.kt)          |\n\n---\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Creating a New Feature Module\n\n**1. Module Structure:**\n```\nlemline-runner-myfeature/\n├── src/\n│   ├── main/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/myfeature/\n│   │   ├── MyFeatureService.kt         ← Business logic\n│   │   ├── MyFeatureModel.kt           ← Database entity\n│   │   ├── MyFeatureRepository.kt      ← Database operations\n│   │   ├── MyFeatureOutbox.kt          ← Outbox processor (optional)\n│   │   ├── MyFeatureCleaner.kt         ← Cleanup scheduler (optional)\n│   │   └── MyFeatureConfig.kt          ← Configuration\n│   ├── test/kotlin/                    ← Tests for all databases\n│   └── testFixtures/kotlin/            ← Test utilities\n├── build.gradle.kts\n└── README.md                           ← Architecture and usage\n```\n\n**2. Dependencies in build.gradle.kts:**\n```kotlin\ndependencies {\n    implementation(project(\":lemline-common\"))\n    implementation(project(\":lemline-core\"))\n    implementation(project(\":lemline-runner-common\"))  // Always required!\n    // Add other feature modules if needed\n}\n```\n\n**3. Model with Interfaces:**\n```kotlin\n// Compose behavior from lemline-runner-common interfaces\ndata class MyFeatureModel(\n    override val id: IDV7,\n    override val instanceMessage: InstanceMessage<MyEvent>,\n    // Outbox fields\n    override val outboxScheduledFor: Instant,\n    override var outboxDelayedUntil: Instant? = outboxScheduledFor,\n    override var outboxAttemptCount: Int = 0,\n    override var outboxCompletedAt: Instant? = null,\n    override var outboxFailedAt: Instant? = null,\n    // ... other outbox fields\n    // Cleanup field\n    override var cleanupAfter: Instant? = null,\n) : WithId, WithInstanceMessage, WithOutbox, WithCleanup\n```\n\n**4. Repository:**\n```kotlin\n@ApplicationScoped\nclass MyFeatureRepository : Repository<MyFeatureModel>(),\n    WithIdRepository<MyFeatureModel>,\n    OutboxRepository<MyFeatureModel>,\n    CleanerRepository<MyFeatureModel> {\n\n    override suspend fun findByUUID(uuid: IDV7): MyFeatureModel? {\n        // Use pool from base Repository\n        return pool.withConnection { conn ->\n            conn.preparedQuery(\"SELECT * FROM lemline_myfeature WHERE id = $1\")\n                .execute(Tuple.of(uuid.value))\n                .awaitSuspending()\n                .firstOrNull()\n                ?.let { MyFeatureModel.fromRow(it) }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // OutboxRepository provides findPendingWithLock() automatically\n    // CleanerRepository provides findOldCompleted() automatically\n}\n```\n\n**5. Service:**\n```kotlin\n@ApplicationScoped\nclass MyFeatureService @Inject constructor(\n    private val repository: MyFeatureRepository,\n    private val commandEmitter: CommandEmitter\n) {\n    suspend fun handleMyEventStarted(message: InstanceMessage<MyEventStarted>) {\n        val model = MyFeatureModel.from(message)\n        repository.insert(model)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**6. Outbox (if needed):**\n```kotlin\n@ApplicationScoped\nclass MyFeatureOutbox @Inject constructor(\n    private val repository: MyFeatureRepository,\n    private val emitter: WorkflowCommandEmitter,\n    private val config: MyFeatureConfig\n) : AbstractOutbox<MyFeatureModel>(\n    name = \"MyFeature\",\n    config = config.outbox\n) {\n    override suspend fun findEntitiesToProcess(limit: Int) = \n        repository.findPendingWithLock(limit)\n\n    override suspend fun process(entity: MyFeatureModel) {\n        emitter.send(createResumeCommand(entity))\n    }\n\n    override suspend fun markCompleted(entity: MyFeatureModel) {\n        repository.markCompleted(entity.id)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**7. Register in WorkflowEventHandler:**\n```kotlin\n// In lemline-runner/src/.../messaging/events/WorkflowEventHandler.kt\nwhen (val state = message.state) {\n    is MyEventStarted -> myFeatureService.handleMyEventStarted(message)\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Event Handling Pattern\n\n```kotlin\n// In feature module service\nsuspend fun handleMyEvent(message: InstanceMessage<MyEvent>) {\n    val event = message.state\n\n    // 1. Create model from event\n    val model = MyFeatureModel.from(message, event)\n\n    // 2. Persist to database\n    repository.insert(model)\n\n    // 3. If immediate resume needed (no outbox), emit command\n    if (!needsDelay) {\n        commandEmitter.send(createResumeCommand(message))\n    }\n    // Otherwise, outbox processor will handle it later\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Patterns\n\n### Multi-Database Repository Test\n\n**Test all 3 databases: PostgreSQL, MySQL, H2**\n\n```kotlin\n// Base test with test logic\nabstract class MyRepositoryTestBase : FunSpec({\n    lateinit var repository: MyRepository\n\n    test(\"should find by UUID\") {\n        val model = createTestModel()\n        repository.insert(model)\n\n        val found = repository.findByUUID(model.id)\n\n        found shouldNotBe null\n        found?.id shouldBe model.id\n    }\n})\n\n// PostgreSQL test\n@QuarkusTest\n@TestProfile(PostgresProfile::class)\nclass MyRepositoryPostgresTest : MyRepositoryTestBase() {\n    @Inject\n    override lateinit var repository: MyRepository\n}\n\n// MySQL test\n@QuarkusTest\n@TestProfile(MySQLProfile::class)\nclass MyRepositoryMySQLTest : MyRepositoryTestBase() {\n    @Inject\n    override lateinit var repository: MyRepository\n}\n\n// H2 test\n@QuarkusTest\n@TestProfile(H2Profile::class)\nclass MyRepositoryH2Test : MyRepositoryTestBase() {\n    @Inject\n    override lateinit var repository: MyRepository\n}\n```\n\n### Feature Service Test\n\n```kotlin\n@QuarkusTest\nclass MyFeatureServiceTest : FunSpec({\n\n    @Inject\n    lateinit var service: MyFeatureService\n\n    @Inject\n    lateinit var repository: MyFeatureRepository\n\n    test(\"should handle event\") {\n        val message = createTestMessage()\n\n        service.handleMyEvent(message)\n\n        // Verify database state\n        val stored = repository.findByUUID(message.workflowId)\n        stored shouldNotBe null\n    }\n})\n```\n\n### Outbox Test\n\n```kotlin\n@QuarkusTest\nclass MyFeatureOutboxTest : FunSpec({\n\n    @Inject\n    lateinit var outbox: MyFeatureOutbox\n\n    @Inject\n    lateinit var repository: MyFeatureRepository\n\n    test(\"should process pending entities\") {\n        // Insert pending entity\n        val model = createPendingModel()\n        repository.insert(model)\n\n        // Process\n        outbox.doWork()\n\n        // Verify marked completed\n        val processed = repository.findByUUID(model.id)\n        processed?.outboxCompletedAt shouldNotBe null\n    }\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Database Migrations\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Place migrations in the feature module, not in lemline-runner!\n\n### Location in Feature Module\n\n```\nlemline-runner-myfeature/\n└── src/main/resources/db/migration/\n    ├── postgresql/\n    │   └── V{N}__Create_myfeature_table.sql\n    ├── mysql/\n    │   └── V{N}__Create_myfeature_table.sql\n    └── h2/\n        └── V{N}__Create_myfeature_table.sql\n```\n\n**Naming:** `V{N}__Description.sql` where N is the next available version number across all modules.\n\n**Check existing versions first:**\n```bash\n# Find highest version number\nfind . -name \"V*.sql\" | sort\n```\n\n### Migration Template\n\n```sql\n-- PostgreSQL version\nCREATE TABLE lemline_myfeature\n(\n    id                   UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    \n    -- Instance message (serialized workflow state)\n    instance_message     TEXT         NOT NULL,\n    \n    -- Feature-specific columns\n    my_custom_field      VARCHAR(255),\n    \n    -- Outbox columns (if using outbox pattern)\n    outbox_scheduled_for TIMESTAMP    NOT NULL,\n    outbox_delayed_until TIMESTAMP    NOT NULL,\n    outbox_attempt_count INT          NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    outbox_completed_at  TIMESTAMP,\n    outbox_failed_at     TIMESTAMP,\n    outbox_error_class   VARCHAR(255),\n    outbox_error_message VARCHAR(500),\n    outbox_error_stacktrace TEXT,\n    \n    -- Cleanup column (if using cleaner pattern)\n    cleanup_after        TIMESTAMP,\n    \n    -- Timestamps\n    created_at           TIMESTAMP    NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- Index for outbox queries (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\nCREATE INDEX idx_lemline_myfeature_pending\n    ON lemline_myfeature (outbox_delayed_until)\n    WHERE outbox_completed_at IS NULL AND outbox_failed_at IS NULL;\n\n-- Index for cleanup queries\nCREATE INDEX idx_lemline_myfeature_cleanup\n    ON lemline_myfeature (cleanup_after)\n    WHERE cleanup_after IS NOT NULL;\n```\n\n### Database-Specific Considerations\n\n**PostgreSQL:**\n- Use `UUID` type\n- Use `TEXT` for long strings\n- Partial indexes with `WHERE` clause\n\n**MySQL:**\n- Use `CHAR(36)` instead of UUID\n- Use `LONGTEXT` for long strings\n- No partial indexes - use regular index\n\n**H2:**\n- Use `UUID` type\n- Use `CLOB` for very long strings\n- Supports partial indexes\n\n### Testing Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Test with PostgreSQL\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-myfeature:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=postgres\n\n# Test with MySQL\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-myfeature:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=mysql\n\n# Test with H2\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-myfeature:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=h2\n```\n\n---\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\n# All tests in main runner\n./gradlew :lemline-runner:test\n\n# All tests in feature module\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-myfeature:test\n\n# Specific test class\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-myfeature:test --tests \"com.lemline.runner.myfeature.MyTest\"\n\n# Test specific module with specific database\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-waits:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=postgres\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-waits:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=mysql\n./gradlew :lemline-runner-waits:test -Dquarkus.test.profile=h2\n\n# Test all runner modules\n./gradlew test -p lemline-runner -p lemline-runner-common -p lemline-runner-waits -p lemline-runner-retries ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## Adding a New DSL Feature\n\n**Example: Adding support for a new task type that requires persistence**\n\n1. **Add task to lemline-core** (see core-dev skill)\n   - Create model in `lemline-core/src/.../models/tasks/`\n   - Create processor in `lemline-core/src/.../processors/`\n   - Throw `AsyncTaskException` if needs persistence\n\n2. **Create feature module**\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p lemline-runner-myfeature/src/{main,test}/kotlin/com/lemline/runner/myfeature\n   mkdir -p lemline-runner-myfeature/src/main/resources/db/migration/{postgresql,mysql,h2}\n   ```\n\n3. **Add to settings.gradle.kts**\n   ```kotlin\n   include(\"lemline-runner-myfeature\")\n   ```\n\n4. **Create build.gradle.kts**\n   ```kotlin\n   dependencies {\n       implementation(project(\":lemline-common\"))\n       implementation(project(\":lemline-core\"))\n       implementation(project(\":lemline-runner-common\"))\n   }\n   ```\n\n5. **Implement feature** (Model, Repository, Service, Outbox, Cleaner)\n\n6. **Add migrations** for all 3 databases\n\n7. **Register in WorkflowEventHandler**\n   ```kotlin\n   // In lemline-runner\n   when (val state = message.state) {\n       is MyFeatureStarted -> myFeatureService.handleStarted(message)\n       // ...\n   }\n   ```\n\n8. **Add tests** for all databases\n\n9. **Add to main runner dependencies**\n   ```kotlin\n   // In lemline-runner/build.gradle.kts\n   implementation(project(\":lemline-runner-myfeature\"))\n   ```\n\n10. **Document in README.md** in the feature module\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- **CLAUDE.md** - Project-wide guidelines and architecture overview\n- **AGENTS.md** - Build, test, and lint commands\n- **core-dev skill** - lemline-core module (DSL, orchestrators, processors)\n- **Serverless Workflow DSL** - https://serverlessworkflow.io/\n\n---\n\n## Module Dependency Graph\n\n```\nlemline-common\n    ↑\n    │\nlemline-core\n    ↑\n    │\nlemline-runner-common ←────┐\n    ↑                      │\n    │                      │\n    ├──────────────────────┼─────────────────┐\n    │                      │                 │\nlemline-runner-*     lemline-runner-*   lemline-runner-*\n(feature modules)    (feature modules)   (feature modules)\n    ↑                      ↑                 ↑\n    │                      │                 │\n    └──────────────────────┴─────────────────┘\n                           │\n                    lemline-runner\n                   (main runtime)\n```\n\n**Key principle:** Feature modules depend only on common modules, not on each other (except rare cases like schedules/parents).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:02:32.949Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Agents requiring efficient serverless workflow management with minimal database reliance","zh":"适合需要高效的无服务器工作流管理且数据库依赖最小的云代理","ja":"サーバーレスワークフローの効率的な管理と、最小限のデータベース依存が必要なクラウドエージェントに最適","ko":"데이터베이스 의존성이 최소화된 효율적인 서버리스 워크플로 관리가 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes en la Nube que requieren una gestión de flujos de trabajo sin servidor eficiente con una dependencia mínima de base de datos","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Cloud nécessitant une gestion de flux de travail sans serveur efficace avec une dépendance minimale à la base de données","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Agents, die eine effiziente serverlose Workflow-Verwaltung mit minimaler Datenbankabhängigkeit erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Nuvem que exigem gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho sem servidor eficiente com mínima dependência de banco de dados","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, требующих эффективного управления серверными рабочими процессами с минимальной зависимостью от базы данных","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل السحابي التي تتطلب إدارة تدفق عمل خالي من الخادم بكفاءة مع اعتماد قليل على قاعدة البيانات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute event-driven workflows across modular ecosystems using shared infrastructure, leveraging messaging, CLI, and configuration capabilities, with support for feature-focused modules like lemline-runner-*","zh":"赋予代理执行跨模块化生态系统的事件驱动工作流的能力，使用共享基础设施，利用消息传递、CLI和配置能力，并支持类似lemline-runner-*的功能集中的模块","ja":"モジュラー化されたエコシステム全体でイベント駆動型のワークフローを実行するエージェントを可能にし、共有インフラストラクチャを利用してメッセージング、CLI、構成機能を利用し、lemline-runner-*などの機能に焦点を当てたモジュールをサポートする","ko":"이벤트 드리븐 워크플로를 모듈화된 생태계 전반에 걸쳐 실행하는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 공유 인프라를 활용하여 메시징, CLI, 구성 기능을 활용하며, lemline-runner-*와 같은 기능 집중 모듈을 지원","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar flujos de trabajo orientados a eventos en ecosistemas modulares que utilizan infraestructura compartida, aprovechando las capacidades de mensajería, CLI y configuración, con soporte para módulos centrados en funciones como lemline-runner-*","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des flux de travail orientés par les événements dans des écosystèmes modulaires utilisant une infrastructure partagée, en exploitant les capacités de messagerie, de CLI et de configuration, avec un support pour des modules axés sur les fonctionnalités comme lemline-runner-*","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, ereignisgesteuerte Workflows in modularen Ökosystemen auszuführen, die eine gemeinsame Infrastruktur nutzen, und nutzt dabei Messaging-, CLI- und Konfigurationsfunktionen, mit Unterstützung für funktionsorientierte Module wie lemline-runner-*","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar fluxos de trabalho orientados a eventos em ecossistemas modulares que utilizam infraestrutura compartilhada, aproveitando mensagens, CLI e capacidades de configuração, com suporte a módulos focados em recursos como lemline-runner-*","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность выполнять событийные рабочие процессы в модульных экосистемах с использованием общей инфраструктуры, используя сообщения, CLI и возможности конфигурации, с поддержкой модулей, ориентированных на функции, таких как lemline-runner-*","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تشغيل تدفقات العمل الموجهة بالأحداث عبر المنظومات الموديولرية التي تستخدم البنية التحتية المشتركة، واستخدام الرسائل وواجهة سطر الأوامر والقدرات التكوينية، مع دعم الوحدات المُركّزة على الميزات مثل lemline-runner-*"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating workflows on existing infrastructure","Developing modular workflow capabilities with lemline-runner-* modules","Configuring and managing serverless workflows with minimal database interactions"],"zh":["在现有基础设施上自动化工作流","使用lemline-runner-*模块开发模块化工作流能力","配置和管理最小化数据库交互的服务器工作流"],"ja":["既存のインフラストラクチャ上でワークフローを自動化する","lemline-runner-*モジュールを使用してモジュラー化されたワークフロー能力を開発する","データベースとのやり取りを最小限に抑えたサーバーレスワークフローを設定して管理する"],"ko":["기존 인프라에서 워크플로 자동화","lemline-runner-* 모듈을 사용한 모듈화 워크플로 능력 개발","데이터베이스 상호작용을 최소한으로 줄인 서버리스 워크플로 구성 및 관리"],"es":["Automatizar flujos de trabajo en infraestructuras existentes","Desarrollar capacidades de flujo de trabajo modulares con módulos lemline-runner-*","Configurar y administrar flujos de trabajo sin servidor con interacciones de base de datos mínimas"],"fr":["Automatiser les flux de travail sur les infrastructures existantes","Développer des capacités de flux de travail modulaires avec des modules lemline-runner-*","Configurer et gérer des flux de travail sans serveur avec des interactions de base de données minimales"],"de":["Automatisierung von Workflows in bestehenden Infrastrukturen","Entwicklung modularer Workflow-Fähigkeiten mit lemline-runner-*-Modulen","Konfigurieren und Verwalten serverloser Workflows mit minimalen Datenbankinteraktionen"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho em infraestrutura existente","Desenvolver capacidades de fluxo de trabalho modulares com módulos lemline-runner-*","Configurar e gerenciar fluxos de trabalho sem servidor com interações mínimas de banco de dados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие процессы на существующей инфраструктуре","Разрабатывать модульные возможности рабочих процессов с модулями lemline-runner-*","Настроить и управлять серверными рабочими процессами с минимальными взаимодействиями с базой данных"],"ar":["تحسين تدفقات العمل على البنية التحتية الحالية","تطوير قدرات تدفق العمل الموديولرية مع وحدات lemline-runner-*","تكوين وإدارة تدفقات العمل الخالية من الخادم مع تفاعلات قليل مع قاعدة البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing infrastructure setup","Dependent on lemline-runner module for core functionality"],"zh":["需要现有的基础设施设置","依赖lemline-runner模块实现核心功能"],"ja":["既存のインフラストラクチャの設定が必要","コア機能の実現にlemline-runnerモジュールに依存する"],"ko":["기존 인프라 설정 필요","핵심 기능 구현에 lemline-runner 모듈 의존"],"es":["Requiere una configuración de infraestructura existente","Dependiente del módulo lemline-runner para la funcionalidad principal"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration d''infrastructure existante","Dépendant du module lemline-runner pour la fonctionnalité principale"],"de":["Benötigt eine Konfiguration einer bestehenden Infrastruktur","Abhängig vom lemline-runner-Modul für die Kernfunktionalität"],"pt":["Exige configuração de infraestrutura existente","Dependente do módulo lemline-runner para funcionalidade principal"],"ru":["Требует настройки существующей инфраструктуры","Зависит от модуля lemline-runner для основной функциональности"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد البنية التحتية الحالية","يعتمد على وحدة lemline-runner للوظيفة الأساسية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cooper538/eshop-demo/finish-phase', 'community', 'cooper538', 'eshop-demo', 'cooper538/eshop-demo', 'finish-phase', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z', '2026-02-18T03:01:42.329Z', NULL, '{"id":"cooper538/eshop-demo/finish-phase","name":"finish-phase","description":{"zh":"finish-phase是用于手动完成.NET微服务架构中的阶段，通过更新状态和范围检查清单。它适用于需要手动审查或编辑范围检查清单，或者自动检测未触发的情况","ja":"finish-phaseは、NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャでフェーズを手動で完了するために使用され、ステータスと範囲のチェックリストを更新します。これは、範囲のチェックリストを手動でレビューまたは編集する必要がある場合、または自動検出がトリガーされない場合に使用されます","ko":"finish-phase는 .NET 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처에서 단계를 수동으로 완료하는 데 사용되며, 상태 및 범위 확인 목록을 업데이트합니다. 이는 범위 확인 목록을 수동으로 검토 또는 편집해야 하는 경우 또는 자동 감지기가 트리거되지 않는 경우에 사용됩니다","es":"El comando /finish-phase permite finalizar manualmente una fase en la arquitectura de microservicios .NET, actualizando su estado y lista de verificación de alcance.","fr":"La commande /finish-phase permet de terminer manuellement une phase dans l''architecture de microservices .NET, en mettant à jour son état et sa liste de vérification de portée.","de":"Der Befehl /finish-phase ermöglicht die manuelle Fertigstellung einer Phase in der .NET-Microservices-Architektur, indem er ihren Status und die Prüfliste des Umfangs aktualisiert.","pt":"O comando /finish-phase permite concluir uma fase manualmente, atualizando o status e a lista de verificação de escopo. É útil quando você deseja revisar/editar a lista de verificação de escopo antes de marcar como concluída.","ru":"Команда /finish-phase позволяет завершить фазу вручную, обновляя статус и контрольный список объема. Это полезно, когда вы хотите просмотреть/отредактировать контрольный список объема перед тем, как отметить его как завершенный.","ar":"أمر /finish-phase يسمح بإنهاء مرحلة يدويًا، مع تحديث الحالة وقائمة التحقق من النطاق. هذا مفيد عندما تريد مراجعة/تحرير قائمة التحقق من النطاق قبل وضع علامة إنهاء.","en":"Demonstration of .NET microservices architecture"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":".NET微服务架构完成阶段","ja":"NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャの完了フェーズ","ko":".NET 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 완료 단계","es":"Finalizar fase en arquitectura de microservicios .NET","fr":"Terminer une phase dans l''architecture de microservices .NET","de":"Fertigstellung einer Phase in .NET-Microservices-Architektur","pt":"Conclusão de Fase: Arquitetura de Microsserviços .NET","ru":"Фаза завершения: демонстрация микросервисной архитектуры ...","ar":"مرحلة الإنهاء: بنية مايكروسيرفيسات .NET","en":"finish-phase"},"description":{"zh":"finish-phase是用于手动完成.NET微服务架构中的阶段，通过更新状态和范围检查清单。它适用于需要手动审查或编辑范围检查清单，或者自动检测未触发的情况","ja":"finish-phaseは、NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャでフェーズを手動で完了するために使用され、ステータスと範囲のチェックリストを更新します。これは、範囲のチェックリストを手動でレビューまたは編集する必要がある場合、または自動検出がトリガーされない場合に使用されます","ko":"finish-phase는 .NET 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처에서 단계를 수동으로 완료하는 데 사용되며, 상태 및 범위 확인 목록을 업데이트합니다. 이는 범위 확인 목록을 수동으로 검토 또는 편집해야 하는 경우 또는 자동 감지기가 트리거되지 않는 경우에 사용됩니다","es":"El comando /finish-phase permite finalizar manualmente una fase en la arquitectura de microservicios .NET, actualizando su estado y lista de verificación de ...","fr":"La commande /finish-phase permet de terminer manuellement une phase dans l''architecture de microservices .NET, en mettant à jour son état et sa liste de véri...","de":"Der Befehl /finish-phase ermöglicht die manuelle Fertigstellung einer Phase in der .NET-Microservices-Architektur, indem er ihren Status und die Prüfliste de...","pt":"O comando /finish-phase permite concluir uma fase manualmente, atualizando o status e a lista de verificação de escopo. É útil quando você deseja revisar/edi...","ru":"Команда /finish-phase позволяет завершить фазу вручную, обновляя статус и контрольный список объема. Это полезно, когда вы хотите просмотреть/отредактировать...","ar":"أمر /finish-phase يسمح بإنهاء مرحلة يدويًا، مع تحديث الحالة وقائمة التحقق من النطاق. هذا مفيد عندما تريد مراجعة/تحرير قائمة التحقق من النطاق قبل وضع علامة إن...","en":"Demonstration of .NET microservices architecture"},"definition":{"en":"Demonstration of .NET microservices architecture"},"features":{"zh":["手动完成阶段","更新状态和范围检查清单","支持手动审查或编辑范围检查清单","适用于自动检测未触发的情况","支持添加注释到阶段的注释部分"],"ja":["フェーズを手動で完了する","ステータスと範囲のチェックリストを更新する","範囲のチェックリストを手動でレビューまたは編集することをサポートする","自動検出がトリガーされない場合に適している","フェーズの注釈セクションに注釈を追加することをサポートする"],"ko":["단계를 수동으로 완료합니다","상태 및 범위 확인 목록을 업데이트합니다","범위 확인 목록을 수동으로 검토 또는 편집하는 것을 지원합니다","자동 감지기가 트리거되지 않는 경우에 적합합니다","단계의 注释 섹션에 注释를 추가하는 것을 지원합니다"],"es":["Finalizar manualmente una fase","Actualizar el estado y la lista de verificación de alcance","Agregar notas a la sección de notas de la fase","Vista previa de los cambios sin aplicarlos","Compatibilidad con la arquitectura de microservicios .NET"],"fr":["Terminer manuellement une phase","Mettre à jour l''état et la liste de vérification de portée","Ajouter des notes à la section de notes de la phase","Aperçu des modifications sans les appliquer","Compatibilité avec l''architecture de microservices .NET"],"de":["Manuelle Fertigstellung einer Phase","Aktualisieren des Status und der Prüfliste des Umfangs","Hinzufügen von Notizen zum Notizbereich der Phase","Vorschau der Änderungen ohne Anwendung","Kompatibilität mit der .NET-Microservices-Architektur"],"pt":["Conclusão de fase manual","Atualização do status e lista de verificação de escopo","Opção de visualização de alterações sem aplicação","Uso do comando /finish-phase","Integração com a arquitetura de microsserviços .NET"],"ru":["Ручное завершение фазы","Обновление статуса и контрольного списка объема","Вариант предварительного просмотра изменений без применения","Использование команды /finish-phase","Интеграция с микросервисной архитектурой .NET"],"ar":["إنهاء مرحلة يدوي","تحديث الحالة وقائمة التحقق من النطاق","خيار معاينة التغييرات بدون تطبيق","استخدام أمر /finish-phase","التكامل مع بنية مايكروسيرفيسات .NET"]},"keywords":{"zh":[".NET微服务架构","完成阶段","手动完成","范围检查清单","自动检测","阶段管理"],"ja":["NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャ","完了フェーズ","手動完了","範囲のチェックリスト","自動検出","フェーズ管理"],"ko":[".NET 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처","완료 단계","수동 완료","범위 확인 목록","자동 감지","단계 관리"],"es":["arquitectura de microservicios .NET","finalizar fase","comando /finish-phase","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","microservicios","finalización de fase","actualización de estado","lista de verificación de alcance"],"fr":["architecture de microservices .NET","terminer une phase","commande /finish-phase","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","microservices","finalisation de phase","mise à jour de l''état","liste de vérification de portée"],"de":["NET-Microservices-Architektur","Fertigstellung einer Phase","Befehl /finish-phase","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen","Mikrodienste","Fertigstellung einer Phase","Status-Aktualisierung","Prüfliste des Umfangs"],"pt":["microsserviços .NET","conclusão de fase","arquitetura de microsserviços","comando /finish-phase","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["микросервисы .NET","завершение фазы","микросервисная архитектура","команда /finish-phase","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["مايكروسيرفيسات .NET","إنهاء مرحلة","بنية مايكروسيرفيسات","أمر /finish-phase","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"cooper538","repo":"eshop-demo","repoPath":"cooper538/eshop-demo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.402Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"finish-phase","description":"Manually complete a phase and update phase.md. Use when you want to manually review/edit phase completion, or when auto-detection didnt trigger.","bodyPreview":"# Finish Phase\n\nManually complete a phase by updating its status and scope checklist. Use this when:\n- You want to manually review/edit scope checklist before marking complete\n- Auto-detection in `/finish-task` didn''t trigger (e.g., already on main branch)\n- You want to add notes to the phase''s Notes section\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/finish-phase 03              # Complete phase 03\n/finish-phase 03 --dry-run    # Preview changes without applying\n```\n\n## Arguments\n\n- `$1` - Phase number (e.g., `03`, `3`, `","body":"# Finish Phase\n\nManually complete a phase by updating its status and scope checklist. Use this when:\n- You want to manually review/edit scope checklist before marking complete\n- Auto-detection in `/finish-task` didn''t trigger (e.g., already on main branch)\n- You want to add notes to the phase''s Notes section\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/finish-phase 03              # Complete phase 03\n/finish-phase 03 --dry-run    # Preview changes without applying\n```\n\n## Arguments\n\n- `$1` - Phase number (e.g., `03`, `3`, `phase-03`)\n- `--dry-run` - Preview changes without modifying files\n- `$ARGUMENTS` - Full arguments passed to the skill\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Parse Arguments\n\nExtract phase number from arguments:\n- Phase number: `03`, `3`, or `phase-03` → normalize to `03`\n\n```bash\n# Extract phase number\nPHASE_NUM=$(echo \"$ARGUMENTS\" | grep -oE ''[0-9]+'' | head -1)\nPHASE_NUM=$(printf \"%02d\" \"$PHASE_NUM\")\n```\n\n### Step 2: Locate Phase Directory\n\nFind the phase specification file:\n\n```bash\nPHASE_DIR=$(find specification -maxdepth 1 -type d -name \"phase-${PHASE_NUM}-*\" | head -1)\n```\n\nIf not found, show available phases and exit.\n\n### Step 3: Check Task Status\n\nRead all tasks in the phase and check their status:\n\n```bash\nfor task_file in \"$PHASE_DIR/tasks/\"task-*.md; do\n    # Extract status from each task\ndone\n```\n\nReport:\n- Total tasks\n- Completed tasks\n- Pending/in-progress tasks (warn if any)\n\nIf there are incomplete tasks, ask user for confirmation:\n> \"Phase has X incomplete tasks. Are you sure you want to mark the phase as complete?\"\n\n### Step 4: Preview Changes\n\nShow what will be changed:\n\n1. **Phase Status** - Current → `✅ completed`\n2. **Scope Checklist** - Which items will be checked off based on task names\n\nDisplay preview:\n```\n📋 Phase XX Completion Preview\n\nStatus: ⚪ pending → ✅ completed\n\nScope checklist updates:\n- [x] SharedKernel package (matched: task-01 SharedKernel)\n- [x] Contracts package (matched: task-02 Contracts)\n- [ ] Some other item (no match found)\n\nTasks: 5/5 completed\n\nApply changes? (y/n)\n```\n\n### Step 5: Apply Changes\n\nIf user approves (or `--dry-run` not specified):\n\n1. Update phase.md status to `✅ completed`\n2. Check off matched scope items\n3. Optionally ask if user wants to add notes\n\n### Step 6: Commit Changes\n\n```bash\ngit add \"$PHASE_DIR/phase.md\"\ngit commit -m \"[${PHASE_NUM}-00] docs: mark phase as completed\" --no-verify\n```\n\n### Step 7: Final Report\n\n```\n✅ Phase XX marked as completed!\n\nUpdated:\n- Status: ✅ completed\n- Scope: X/Y items checked\n\nGit commit: [XX-00] docs: mark phase as completed\n\nNext steps:\n- /task-status - see remaining phases\n- /start-task XX - start next phase''s first task\n```\n\n## Manual Scope Editing\n\nIf scope matching isn''t accurate, inform user:\n> \"Some scope items couldn''t be automatically matched. You can manually edit the phase.md file to check them off.\"\n\nOffer to open the file:\n> \"Would you like me to show you the scope section for manual review?\"\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Error | Message |\n|-------|---------|\n| Phase not found | \"Phase XX not found. Available: phase-01, phase-02...\" |\n| Already completed | \"Phase XX is already marked as completed.\" |\n| No tasks exist | \"Phase XX has no tasks. Create tasks first with /phase-breakdown XX\" |\n\n## Safety Rules\n\n1. NEVER mark phase complete if user declines after incomplete task warning\n2. ALWAYS show preview before making changes\n3. ALWAYS commit changes after modifying phase.md\n4. NEVER modify task files (only phase.md)\n\n## Example Session\n\n```\nUser: /finish-phase 01\n\nClaude: 📂 Found phase: specification/phase-01-foundation/phase.md\n\nChecking tasks...\n- task-01: ✅ completed\n- task-02: ✅ completed\n- task-03: ✅ completed\n- task-04: ✅ completed\n- task-05: ✅ completed\n\nAll 5 tasks completed!\n\n📋 Phase 01 Completion Preview\n\nStatus: ⚪ pending → ✅ completed\n\nScope checklist updates:\n- [x] SharedKernel package (matched: task-01)\n- [x] Contracts package (matched: task-02)\n- [x] EShop.Common (matched: task-05)\n\nApply changes? (y/n)\n\nUser: y\n\nClaude: ✅ Phase 01 marked as completed!\n\nCommitted: [01-00] docs: mark phase as completed\n\nNext steps:\n- /task-status - see remaining phases\n- /phase-breakdown 02 - prepare next phase\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:01:42.329Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring manual phase completion in .NET microservices architecture","zh":"适用于需要在.NET微服务架构中手动完成阶段的开发代理","ja":".NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャで手動フェーズ完了を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":".NET 마이크로서비스 아키텍처에서 수동 단계 완료가 필요한 개발 에이전트에 이상적","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren la finalización manual de fases en la arquitectura de microservicios .NET","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant la finalisation manuelle de phases dans l''architecture de microservices .NET","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine manuelle Phasenabschluss in der .NET-Mikrodienstarchitektur benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem conclusão de fase manual em arquitetura de microsserviços .NET","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих ручного завершения фаз в архитектуре микросервисов .NET","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إكمال مرحلة يدوي في هندسة微روسيرفيس .NET"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manually complete phases by updating status and scope checklist, utilizing arguments like phase number and dry-run option, and supporting use cases such as manual review and editing of scope checklists before marking completion","zh":"支持代理通过更新状态和范围检查清单手动完成阶段，利用阶段编号和试运行选项等参数，并支持在标记完成前手动审查和编辑范围检查清单等使用场景","ja":"フェーズ番号やドライランオプションなどの引数を利用してステータスとスコープチェックリストを更新することでエージェントが手動でフェーズを完了できるようにし、完了マークの前のスコープチェックリストの手動レビューや編集などのユースケースをサポート","ko":"단계 번호 및 드라이런 옵션과 같은 인수를 활용하여 상태 및 범위 체크리스트를 업데이트하여 에이전트가 수동으로 단계를 완료할 수 있도록 지원하며, 완료 표시 전 범위 체크리스트의 수동 검토 및 편집과 같은 사용 사례를 지원","es":"Permite a los agentes completar manualmente las fases actualizando el estado y la lista de verificación de alcance, utilizando argumentos como el número de fase y la opción de ejecución de prueba, y admitiendo casos de uso como la revisión y edición manual de las listas de verificación de alcance antes de marcar la finalización","fr":"Permet aux agents de compléter manuellement les phases en mettant à jour le statut et la liste de vérification de la portée, en utilisant des arguments tels que le numéro de phase et l''option de test à sec, et en prenant en charge des cas d''utilisation tels que l''examen et la modification manuelle des listes de vérification de la portée avant de marquer la complétion","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Phasen manuell abzuschließen, indem sie den Status und die Prüfliste des Umfangs aktualisieren, Argumente wie die Phasennummer und die Trockenlauf-Option verwenden und Nutzungsfälle wie manuelle Überprüfung und Bearbeitung der Prüflisten des Umfangs vor dem Abmelden unterstützen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a concluir fases manualmente atualizando o status e a lista de verificação de escopo, utilizando argumentos como número de fase e opção dry-run, e suportando casos de uso como revisão e edição manual da lista de verificação de escopo antes de marcar a conclusão","ru":"Позволяет агентам вручную завершать фазы, обновляя статус и список проверки объема, используя аргументы, такие как номер фазы и опцию dry-run, и поддерживая случаи использования, такие как ручной обзор и редактирование списка проверки объема перед отметкой о завершении","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء إكمال المراحل يدويًا عن طريق تحديث الحالة وقائمة التحقق من نطاق العمل، باستخدام الحجج مثل رقم المرحلة وخيارة dry-run، ودعم حالات استخدام مثل المراجعة والتعديل اليدوي لقائمة التحقق من نطاق العمل قبل وضع علامة الإكمال"},"useCases":{"en":["Manually completing phases with custom notes","Previewing changes before applying with --dry-run","Overriding auto-detection in /finish-task"],"zh":["使用自定义注释手动完成阶段","通过--dry-run参数在应用前预览更改","在/finish-task中覆盖自动检测功能"],"ja":["カスタムノートを使用した手動フェーズ完了","--dry-runによる適用前の変更プレビュー","/finish-taskでの自動検出の上書き"],"ko":["사용자 정의 노트로 수동 단계 완료","--dry-run으로 적용 전 변경 사항 미리보기","/finish-task에서 자동 감지 재정의"],"es":["Completar fases manualmente con notas personalizadas","Previsualizar cambios antes de aplicar con --dry-run","Anular la autodetección en /finalizar-tarea"],"fr":["Compléter manuellement les phases avec des notes personnalisées","Prévisualiser les modifications avant de les appliquer avec --dry-run","Contourner la détection automatique dans /finir-tâche"],"de":["Phasen manuell mit benutzerdefinierten Notizen abschließen","Änderungen vor dem Anwenden mit --dry-run vorab anzeigen","Automatische Erkennung in /aufgabe-beenden außer Kraft setzen"],"pt":["Conclusão manual de fases com notas personalizadas","Visualização de alterações antes de aplicá-las com --dry-run","Substituição da autodetecção em /finish-task"],"ru":["Ручное завершение фаз с пользовательскими заметками","Предварительный просмотр изменений перед применением с --dry-run","Переопределение автоподстановки в /finish-task"],"ar":["إكمال المراحل يدويًا مع ملاحظات مخصصة","معاينة التغييرات قبل تطبيقها مع --dry-run","استبدال الكشف التلقائي في /finish-task"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET microservices architecture","Manual intervention needed for phase completion"],"zh":["需要.NET微服务架构","阶段完成需要人工干预"],"ja":[".NETマイクロサービスアーキテクチャが必要","フェーズ完了に手動介入が必要"],"ko":[".NET 마이크로서비스 아키텍처 필요","단계 완료에 수동 개입 필요"],"es":["Requiere arquitectura de microservicios .NET","Se requiere intervención manual para la finalización de fases"],"fr":["Nécessite une architecture de microservices .NET","Intervention manuelle nécessaire pour la complétion des phases"],"de":["Erfordert .NET-Mikrodienstarchitektur","Manuelle Eingriff benötigt für Phasenabschluss"],"pt":["Requer arquitetura de microsserviços .NET","Necessidade de intervenção manual para conclusão de fase"],"ru":["Требуется архитектура микросервисов .NET","Необходимо ручное вмешательство для завершения фазы"],"ar":["يتطلب هندسة微روسيرفيس .NET","يتطلب تدخل يدوي لإكمال المرحلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
