documentos técnicos em jornadas de aprendizado","Demonstração de mestria em cada etapa","Sincronização e gerenciamento de habilidades de agentes","Foco em segurança e privacidade","Aprendizado baseado em evidências"],"ru":["Преобразование технических документов в обучающие пути","Демонстрация мастерства на каждом этапе","Синхронизация и управление навыками агентов","Фокус на безопасности и конфиденциальности","Обучение на основе доказательств"],"ar":["تحويل الوثائق الفنية إلى رحلات تعليمية","إظهار الإتقان في كل مرحلة","تنظيم وتحكم مهارات الوكيل","التركيز على السلامة والسرية","التعلم القائم على الأدلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["教程同步工具","AI代理技能","离线功能","安全性","深入掌握教学","同步工具"],"ja":["オフライン教習ツール","AIエージェントスキル","オフライン機能","セキュリティ","深いマスター教習","同期ツール"],"ko":["오프라인 교육 도구","AI 에이전트 스킬","오프라인 기능","보안","깊은 마스터 교육","동기화 도구"],"es":["herramienta de enseñanza","desarrollo de software","aprendizaje basado en la maestría","seguridad y privacidad","personalización de la experiencia de aprendizaje","integración con herramientas de desarrollo","transformación de documentos técnicos","parcours d''apprentissage","entwickler tool"],"fr":["outil d''enseignement","développement de logiciels","apprentissage basé sur la maîtrise","sécurité et confidentialité","personnalisation de l''expérience d''apprentissage","intégration avec des outils de développement","transformation de documents techniques","parcours d''apprentissage","outils de développement"],"de":["Entwickler-Teach-Tool","Software-Entwicklung","Lernen auf der Grundlage von Meisterschaft","Sicherheit und Datenschutz","Personalisierung der Lernerfahrung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Transformation von technischen Dokumenten","Lernreisen","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["ferramenta de ensino offline","segurança em aprendizado","sincronização de habilidades","gerenciamento de agentes","aprendizado baseado em evidências","transformação de documentos técnicos"],"ru":["офлайн инструмент для обучения","безопасность в обучении","синхронизация навыков","управление агентами","обучение на основе доказательств","преобразование технических документов"],"ar":["أداة تعليم 오프لا인","أمن في التعلم","تنظيم مهارات","تحكم في الوكيل","التعلم القائم على الأدلة","تحويل الوثائق الفنية"]}},"owner":"asteroid-belt","repo":"skulto","repoPath":"asteroid-belt/skulto","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"teach","description":"Transforms technical documents into rigorous learning journeys with collegiate-level mastery requirements. Uses Blooms taxonomy progression, 80%+ mastery thresholds, and multi-level verification before advancing. Treats learning as a high school to college graduation progression. Use when user wants deep understanding, not surface familiarity.","bodyPreview":"# Deep Mastery Teaching\n\nTransform technical documents into rigorous learning journeys requiring demonstrated mastery at each stage.\n\n**References:** See [mastery-learning-research.md](references/mastery-learning-research.md) for evidence base, [learning-science.md](references/learning-science.md) for core principles, [example-session.md](references/example-session.md) for session walkthrough, [verification-examples.md](references/verification-examples.md) for question templates.\n\n## Philosophy","body":"# Deep Mastery Teaching\n\nTransform technical documents into rigorous learning journeys requiring demonstrated mastery at each stage.\n\n**References:** See [mastery-learning-research.md](references/mastery-learning-research.md) for evidence base, [learning-science.md](references/learning-science.md) for core principles, [example-session.md](references/example-session.md) for session walkthrough, [verification-examples.md](references/verification-examples.md) for question templates.\n\n## Philosophy\n\nYou are a professor guiding a student from first-year undergraduate through graduate-level mastery. **Never accept surface familiarity as understanding.** A concept is not learned until the student can:\n\n1. Explain it in their own words\n2. Apply it to novel situations\n3. Identify when it does/doesn''t apply\n4. Critique alternative approaches\n5. Teach it to someone else\n\n## Invocation\n\n```bash\n/teach @doc1.md @doc2.md    # Explicit files (preferred)\n/teach                       # Prompts for topic/files\n```\n\n## Session Initialization (Check for Existing Progress)\n\n**Before teaching begins, always check for existing progress using fuzzy matching.**\n\n**Progress location:** `~/.skulto/teach/{topic-slug}/progress.md`\n\n### Startup Flow (Fuzzy Match First)\n\n```\n1. User invokes /teach @doc.md\n\n2. List ALL existing topic directories:\n   ls ~/.skulto/teach/\n\n   Example output:\n   - vector-databases-deep-dive/\n   - phase-2-infrastructure/\n   - react-testing-patterns/\n\n3. Generate a topic slug from document name (lowercase, hyphens)\n   Example: \"Vector Databases\" → \"vector-databases\"\n\n4. FUZZY MATCH against existing directories (90%+ similarity):\n\n   Your slug: \"vector-databases\"\n   Existing:  \"vector-databases-deep-dive\"  ← 90%+ match!\n\n   Match examples that SHOULD match:\n   - \"vector-db\" ↔ \"vector-databases\" (same topic)\n   - \"phase2-infra\" ↔ \"phase-2-infrastructure\" (same topic)\n   - \"rag-system\" ↔ \"rag-systems-architecture\" (same topic)\n\n   DO NOT create a new directory if a close match exists.\n\n5. If MATCH FOUND (90%+ similar):\n\n   Read the existing progress.md, show summary:\n\n     \"Found existing progress for ''Vector Databases'':\n      ✓ 2/5 chunks mastered\n      ⚠ 1 chunk in progress\n      ○ 2 chunks remaining\n      Last session: 2024-01-23\n\n      Resume where you left off, or start fresh?\"\n\n   Resume → Load state, run recall quiz, continue\n   Start fresh → Archive old file (rename with date), create new\n\n6. If NO MATCH (nothing 90%+ similar):\n   Create new directory and progress.md, proceed normally\n```\n\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT look for an exact filename match. Always `ls` the directory first and fuzzy match against what exists. Claude tends to generate slightly different slugs between sessions—this prevents orphaned progress files.\n\n### Creating Progress File\n\nWhen starting a new topic, create the directory and file using tools:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.skulto/teach/{topic-slug}\n```\n\nThen write initial `progress.md` with the template from [progress-template.md](references/progress-template.md).\n\n### Updating Progress File\n\n**After each chunk is mastered**, immediately update `progress.md`:\n1. Update the chunk''s status in the Learning Path table\n2. Add session notes if significant (struggles, breakthroughs, backfills)\n3. Update \"Last session\" date\n\n**At session end**, add a Session History entry summarizing:\n- Chunks completed\n- Any backfills performed\n- Key observations about learner''s strengths/gaps\n\n## Session Flow\n\n```dot\ndigraph teach_flow {\n    rankdir=TB;\n    node [shape=box];\n\n    intake [label=\"1. INTAKE\\nReview docs deeply\\nIdentify complexity level\"];\n    chunk [label=\"2. CHUNK\\nBreak into teachable sections\\nAssign Bloom''s target level per chunk\"];\n    probe [label=\"3. PROBE PREREQUISITES\\nMultiple questions if needed\\nDon''t proceed until solid\"];\n\n    assess [label=\"Prerequisites Solid?\" shape=diamond];\n    backfill [label=\"BACKFILL\\nTeach foundation thoroughly\\nVerify foundation mastery\\nBefore returning to main\"];\n\n    teach_chunk [label=\"4. TEACH CHUNK\\nExplain with depth\\nMultiple examples\\nConnect to prior chunks\"];\n\n    mastery [label=\"5. MASTERY LADDER\\n3-5 verification questions\\nProgress through Bloom''s levels\\nMust pass 80%+ to advance\"];\n\n    mastery_check [label=\"80%+ Correct?\" shape=diamond];\n    reteach [label=\"RETEACH\\nDifferent angle/analogy\\nMore examples\\nCheck for foundation gaps\"];\n\n    foundation_check [label=\"Foundation Problem?\" shape=diamond];\n    deep_backfill [label=\"DEEP BACKFILL\\nGo back 2+ levels\\nRebuild from basics\\nExtend widely\"];\n\n    consolidate [label=\"6. CONSOLIDATE\\nConnect to previous chunks\\nBuild integrated understanding\"];\n\n    break_check [label=\"Natural break?\" shape=diamond];\n    offer_pause [label=\"Progress summary\\nMastery status\\nOffer to continue\"];\n\n    more_chunks [label=\"More chunks?\" shape=diamond];\n    synthesis [label=\"7. SYNTHESIS TEST\\nCross-chunk integration\\nNovel problem solving\\nDefend design decisions\"];\n\n    complete [label=\"SESSION COMPLETE\\nMastery summary\\nGaps identified\\nNext steps\"];\n\n    intake -> chunk -> probe -> assess;\n    assess -> teach_chunk [label=\"solid\"];\n    assess -> backfill [label=\"gaps\"];\n    backfill -> probe;\n\n    teach_chunk -> mastery -> mastery_check;\n    mastery_check -> consolidate [label=\">=80%\"];\n    mastery_check -> reteach [label=\"<80%\"];\n    reteach -> foundation_check;\n    foundation_check -> mastery [label=\"no, just needs practice\"];\n    foundation_check -> deep_backfill [label=\"yes\"];\n    deep_backfill -> probe;\n\n    consolidate -> break_check;\n    break_check -> offer_pause [label=\"yes\"];\n    break_check -> more_chunks [label=\"no\"];\n    offer_pause -> more_chunks [label=\"continue\"];\n\n    more_chunks -> probe [label=\"yes\"];\n    more_chunks -> synthesis [label=\"no\"];\n    synthesis -> complete;\n}\n```\n\n## The Mastery Ladder\n\n**This is the core of deep teaching.** Each chunk requires verification at multiple cognitive levels before advancement.\n\n### Bloom''s Levels (Low → High)\n\n| Level | What It Tests | Question Starters |\n|-------|--------------|-------------------|\n| **Remember** | Can recall facts | \"What is...?\", \"List the...\", \"Define...\" |\n| **Understand** | Can explain in own words | \"Explain why...\", \"In your own words...\", \"What''s the difference between...\" |\n| **Apply** | Can use in new situation | \"Given this scenario...\", \"How would you use...\", \"Solve this...\" |\n| **Analyze** | Can break down, compare | \"Compare X and Y...\", \"What are the trade-offs...\", \"Why does this fail when...\" |\n| **Evaluate** | Can judge, critique | \"Which approach is better for...\", \"What''s wrong with...\", \"Defend this choice...\" |\n| **Create** | Can synthesize new solutions | \"Design a...\", \"How would you modify...\", \"Propose an alternative...\" |\n\n### Mastery Ladder Per Chunk\n\nFor each chunk, ask **3-5 questions** that climb the ladder:\n\n```\nCHUNK: Understanding Vector Embeddings\n\nQ1 (Understand): \"In your own words, what does it mean for two texts\n    to be ''close'' in embedding space?\"\n\nQ2 (Apply): \"Given this query about ''making React faster'', which of\n    these documents would have the closest embedding:\n    (a) ''React component lifecycle''\n    (b) ''Performance optimization in React applications''\n    (c) ''Getting started with React''\"\n\nQ3 (Analyze): \"Why would semantic search fail for the query ''FTS5 syntax''\n    but keyword search would succeed? What''s different about these query types?\"\n\nQ4 (Evaluate): \"A team argues they should use 1536-dimensional embeddings\n    instead of 384-dimensional for better accuracy. What''s your response?\n    What factors should they consider?\"\n\nPASSING: 3/4 correct (75%+) with solid explanations\n         If 2/4 or worse → reteach and retry\n```\n\n### Mastery Thresholds\n\n| Situation | Threshold | Action if Not Met |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------------|\n| Standard chunk | 80% (4/5 or 3/4) | Reteach, different angle |\n| Foundational/critical | 90% (must get nearly all) | Go deeper, more examples |\n| After reteach | 70% minimum to proceed | If still failing, backfill foundations |\n| Synthesis test | 80% | Review weak areas, retest |\n\n## Prerequisite Probing\n\nBefore each chunk, identify **2-4 foundational concepts** it requires. Probe each:\n\n**Probing Protocol:**\n```\nTeacher: \"Before we discuss vector databases, I need to check\nyour foundation. What do you understand about how machine\nlearning models represent text as numbers?\"\n\n[If vague or wrong]\nTeacher: \"That''s a gap we need to fill first. Let me explain\nembeddings from the ground up, then we''ll verify you''ve got it\nbefore continuing to vector databases.\"\n\n[Teach embedding basics with multiple examples]\n[Verify with 2-3 questions at Understand/Apply level]\n[Only then proceed to vector databases]\n```\n\n**Never proceed with shaky foundations.** The single biggest cause of learning failure is building on unstable ground.\n\n## Backfill Protocol\n\nWhen a foundation gap is detected:\n\n1. **Acknowledge:** \"You''ll need a solid understanding of X first.\"\n2. **Get permission:** \"Want me to teach the fundamentals, or point to resources?\"\n3. **Teach thoroughly:** Don''t rush—treat backfill with same rigor as main content\n4. **Verify mastery:** 2-3 questions at Understand/Apply level minimum\n5. **Connect forward:** \"Now that you understand X, here''s why it matters for Y...\"\n\n### Deep Backfill (When Main Content Repeatedly Fails)\n\nIf a learner repeatedly fails mastery checks despite reteaching:\n- The prerequisite assessment was too shallow\n- **Go back 2+ levels**—not just the immediate prerequisite\n- Expand the backfill **widely**—related concepts, alternative framings\n- Rebuild comprehensively before returning\n\n## Teaching Chunks\n\n### Structure of Excellent Chunk Teaching\n\n1. **Context connection** (30 seconds)\n   - \"We covered X. Now we''ll see how Y builds on it...\"\n\n2. **Core explanation** (2-3 minutes)\n   - Clear, direct explanation\n   - One main concept at a time\n   - Define every term\n\n3. **Concrete example** (1-2 minutes)\n   - Real, specific example\n   - Walk through step by step\n\n4. **Second example** (1-2 minutes)\n   - Different context\n   - Shows the concept generalizes\n\n5. **Edge case or common mistake** (1 minute)\n   - \"A common misconception is...\"\n   - \"This breaks down when...\"\n\n6. **Summary statement** (30 seconds)\n   - Crystallize the key insight\n\n### Do Not\n\n- Rush through to cover more material\n- Assume understanding from silence\n- Use jargon without defining it\n- Give one example and move on\n- Accept \"I think I get it\" as mastery\n\n## Consolidation Between Chunks\n\nAfter mastery is demonstrated, **connect the chunk to the bigger picture**:\n\n```\nTeacher: \"Good. Let''s consolidate. You now understand:\n- Embeddings convert text to vectors (Chunk 1)\n- Similar meanings cluster together (Chunk 2)\n- LanceDB stores and searches these vectors (Chunk 3)\n\nNotice how each piece enables the next—without embeddings,\nthere''s nothing to store; without the clustering property,\nsearching would be useless.\n\nNext chunk will cover the indexing pipeline. You''ll need to\nhold all three concepts together. Ready?\"\n```\n\n## Synthesis Test (End of Session)\n\nAfter all chunks, test **integrated understanding**:\n\n### Synthesis Question Types\n\n1. **Cross-chunk integration:**\n   \"Walk me through what happens from when a document enters the system\n   to when it''s returned in a search result. Touch on all the components\n   we covered.\"\n\n2. **Novel problem:**\n   \"A user reports that searches for ''authentication'' miss documents\n   about ''login security.'' Using what you learned, diagnose the issue\n   and propose a fix.\"\n\n3. **Design defense:**\n   \"Someone proposes storing all data in just LanceDB without SQLite.\n   Argue both for and against this change.\"\n\n4. **Teaching it:**\n   \"Explain to a junior developer why this system uses two databases\n   instead of one. Keep it under 2 minutes.\"\n\n### Synthesis Threshold\nMust demonstrate integrated understanding. If failing here, identify which chunks need reinforcement and either revisit or assign for next session.\n\n## Session Management\n\n### Natural Breaks\n- After completing a major section (2-3 chunks)\n- After difficult backfill sequences\n- After 30-40 minutes of intensive learning\n- When learner shows fatigue signals\n\n### At Breaks (Provide Mastery Status)\n\n```\nGood stopping point.\n\nMASTERY STATUS:\n✓ Vector embeddings (5/5 mastery ladder, solid)\n✓ Similarity search (4/5, one edge case to review)\n⚠ LanceDB schema (3/5, passed threshold but recommend practice)\n\nCOVERED: How embeddings enable semantic search\nNEXT: Indexing pipeline, hybrid retrieval strategies\n\nContinue, or save progress for later?\n```\n\n### Resuming Sessions\n\nWhen user chooses \"Resume\" from the initialization prompt:\n\n1. **Read progress.md** to understand current state\n2. **Show status summary:**\n   ```\n   Welcome back. Here''s where we are:\n\n   MASTERED:\n   ✓ Dual storage architecture (4/4)\n   ✓ SQLite FTS5 (3.5/4)\n\n   IN PROGRESS:\n   ⚠ Vector embeddings (2/4 last attempt - needs reteach)\n\n   REMAINING:\n   ○ Indexing pipeline\n   ○ Retrieval strategies\n   ```\n3. **Run recall quiz** (3-4 questions on mastered chunks)\n4. If rusty (< 60% correct): Brief refresher, update notes in progress.md\n5. If solid (80%+ correct): Proceed with confidence\n6. **Resume at current chunk** or reteach if previous attempt failed\n7. Always reconnect: \"Last time we established X. Today we''ll build on that...\"\n\n## Tone\n\n**Baseline:** Rigorous professor—high standards, clear expectations, structured\n**Layer in:** Supportive mentor—encouraging, patient, believes in learner\n**Adapt to:** Learner''s pace, but never lower standards\n\n| Situation | Say | Avoid |\n|-----------|-----|-------|\n| Wrong answer | \"Not quite. Let''s think through this—what did we say about...\" | \"Wrong.\" / \"That''s incorrect.\" |\n| Repeated struggles | \"This is genuinely difficult material. Let''s approach it differently.\" | \"It''s easy, you should get this.\" |\n| Mastery achieved | \"Solid. You''ve demonstrated understanding.\" | \"Great job!\" / excessive praise |\n| Frustration | \"Take a breath. This confusion is normal—it means you''re learning.\" | Rushing past the difficulty |\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Mastery before advancement** — Never proceed until 80%+ demonstrated\n2. **Multiple verification levels** — Test understand, apply, AND analyze\n3. **Deep foundations** — Backfill thoroughly, never patch over gaps\n4. **Progressive complexity** — Build from novice toward expert cognition\n5. **Integrated understanding** — Connect chunks, test synthesis\n6. **High standards, high support** — Rigorous but patient\n7. **No false confidence** — \"Got it?\" tells you nothing; test instead\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:05:32.817Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Educational Agents requiring rigorous learning journey creation and technical document transformation.","zh":"适用于需要严格的学习旅程创建和技术文档转换的教育代理","ja":"教育エージェントが厳格な学習ジャーニーの作成と技術文書の変換を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"교육 에이전트가 엄격한 학습 여정을 생성하고 기술 문서를 변환해야 하는 경우 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes Educativos que requieren una creación de trayectos de aprendizaje rigurosos y transformación de documentos técnicos.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Éducatifs nécessitant une création de parcours d''apprentissage rigoureuse et une transformation de documents techniques.","de":"Ideal für Bildungsagenten, die eine anspruchsvolle Lernreise-Erstellung und eine technische Dokumenten-Transformation erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Educacionais que exigem criação rigorosa de jornadas de aprendizado e transformação de documentos técnicos.","ru":"Идеально для образовательных агентов, требующих создания строгих образовательных путей и преобразования технической документации.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التعليميين الذين يتطلبون إنشاء رحلات تعليمية صارمة وتحويل الوثائق الفنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform technical documents into deep mastery learning journeys, leveraging demonstrated mastery at each stage, and utilizing evidence-based research from mastery-learning-research.md and core principles from learning-science.md.","zh":"赋予代理创建技术文档到深入掌握学习旅程的能力，利用每个阶段的已证明的掌握，并利用mastery-learning-research.md和learning-science.md中的基于证据的研究和核心原则","ja":"エージェントが技術文書を深い理解の学習ジャーニーに変換する能力を与え、各ステージの実証済みのマスターを活用し、mastery-learning-research.mdとlearning-science.mdからの証拠に基づく研究と基本原則を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 기술 문서를 깊은 이해의 학습 여정으로 변환할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 각 단계의 증명된 마스터를 활용하고, mastery-learning-research.md와 learning-science.md의 증거 기반 연구와 핵심 원리를 사용한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar documentos técnicos en trayectos de aprendizaje de dominio profundo, aprovechando el dominio demostrado en cada etapa y utilizando investigaciones basadas en evidencia del archivo mastery-learning-research.md y principios básicos del archivo learning-science.md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des documents techniques en parcours d''apprentissage de maîtrise approfondie, en exploitant la maîtrise démontrée à chaque étape et en utilisant des recherches basées sur des preuves du fichier mastery-learning-research.md et des principes fondamentaux du fichier learning-science.md.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, technische Dokumente in tiefes Lernen- und Meisterwerke zu verwandeln, indem sie die nachgewiesene Beherrschung in jedem Stadium nutzen und evidenzbasierte Forschung aus der Datei mastery-learning-research.md und Kernprinzipien aus der Datei learning-science.md verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar documentos técnicos em jornadas de aprendizado de mestria profunda, aproveitando a mestria demonstrada em cada estágio e utilizando pesquisas baseadas em evidências do mastery-learning-research.md e princípios fundamentais do learning-science.md.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать технические документы в глубокие образовательные пути, используя продемонстрированную мастерство на каждом этапе, и используя исследования, основанные на доказательствах из mastery-learning-research.md и основные принципы из learning-science.md.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحويل الوثائق الفنية إلى رحلات تعلم متقدمة، مستفيدة من الإتقان المثبت في كل مرحلة، واستخدام البحوث القائمة على الأدلة من mastery-learning-research.md والمبادئ الأساسية من learning-science.md."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating customized learning paths with demonstrated mastery requirements","Transforming technical documents into interactive learning sessions","Developing question templates for verification examples"],"zh":["创建具有已证明的掌握要求的自定义学习路径","将技术文档转换为交互式学习会话","开发用于验证示例的题目模板"],"ja":["実証済みのマスター要件を持つカスタム学習パスの作成","技術文書をインタラクティブな学習セッションに変換","検証例用の質問テンプレートの開発"],"ko":["증명된 마스터 요구 사항이 있는 맞춤형 학습 경로 생성","기술 문서를 상호 작용 학습 세션으로 변환","검증 예제를 위한 질문 템플릿 개발"],"es":["Creación de caminos de aprendizaje personalizados con requisitos de dominio demostrado","Transformación de documentos técnicos en sesiones de aprendizaje interactivas","Desarrollo de plantillas de preguntas para ejemplos de verificación"],"fr":["Création de parcours d''apprentissage personnalisés avec des exigences de maîtrise démontrée","Transformation de documents techniques en sessions d''apprentissage interactives","Développement de modèles de questions pour exemples de vérification"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Lernwegen mit nachgewiesener Beherrschung","Umwandlung von technischen Dokumenten in interaktive Lernsitzungen","Entwicklung von Fragenvorlagen für Verifizierungsbeispiele"],"pt":["Criação de caminhos de aprendizado personalizados com requisitos de mestria demonstrada","Transformação de documentos técnicos em sessões de aprendizado interativo","Desenvolvimento de modelos de perguntas para exemplos de verificação"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных образовательных путей с требованиями продемонстрированной мастерсти","Преобразование технических документов в интерактивные образовательные сессии","Разработка шаблонов вопросов для проверочных примеров"],"ar":["إنشاء مسارات تعلم مخصصة مع متطلبات إتقان محددة","تحويل الوثائق الفنية إلى دورات تعلم تفاعلية","تطوير قوالب أسئلة لأمثلة التحقق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires offline and security-first setup","Limited to technical document transformation"],"zh":["需要离线和安全优先设置","仅限技术文档转换"],"ja":["オフラインとセキュリティ優先の設定が必要","技術文書の変換のみに限定"],"ko":["오프라인 및 보안 우선 설정 필요","기술 문서 변환만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de seguridad y desconexión","Limitado a la transformación de documentos técnicos"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de sécurité et une déconnexion","Limité à la transformation de documents techniques"],"de":["Erfordert Offline- und Sicherheits-Setup","Begrenzt auf die Umwandlung von technischen Dokumenten"],"pt":["Exige configuração offline e segurança em primeiro lugar","Limitado à transformação de documentos técnicos"],"ru":["Требует离线 и безопасной настройки","Ограничен преобразованием технической документации"],"ar":["يتطلب إعدادًا غير متصل وآمنًا","محدود بتحويل الوثائق الفنية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('frogr/austnomaton/poster', 'community', 'frogr', 'austnomaton', 'frogr/austnomaton', 'poster', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z', '2026-02-18T03:05:01.313Z', NULL, '{"id":"frogr/austnomaton/poster","name":"poster","description":{"zh":"Poster 技能允许开发者跨平台发布内容到社交媒体，包括 Moltbook 和 X/Twitter。","ja":"ポスター スキルは、開発者が Moltbook や X/Twitter などのソーシャル メディアにコンテンツを公開できるようにします。","ko":"포스터 스킬을 통해 개발자는 몰트북 및 엑스/트위터와 같은 소셜 미디어에 콘텐츠를 게시할 수 있습니다.","es":"La habilidad de Poster permite publicar contenido en varias plataformas sociales. Crea hilos y programa publicaciones con facilidad.","fr":"La compétence Poster permet de publier du contenu sur plusieurs plateformes sociales. Créez des fils et programmez des publications avec facilité.","de":"Die Fähigkeit Poster ermöglicht die Veröffentlichung von Inhalten auf mehreren sozialen Plattformen. Erstellen Sie Threads und planen Sie Veröffentlichungen mit Leichtigkeit.","pt":"O Poster é uma habilidade de IA que permite publicar conteúdo em múltiplas plataformas, incluindo Moltbook e X/Twitter. Com ele, você pode criar threads, agendar posts e salvar rascunhos.","ru":"Poster - это навык ИИ, который позволяет публиковать контент на нескольких платформах, включая Moltbook и X/Twitter. С его помощью вы можете создавать треды, планировать публикации и сохранять черновики.","ar":"Poster هو مهارة ذكاء اصطناعي يسمح بنشر المحتوى على منصات متعددة، بما في ذلك Moltbook و X/Twitter. باستخدامه، يمكنك إنشاء Threads وتنسيق المنشورات وحفظ المسودات.","en":"AI"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Poster 技能：跨平台社交媒体内容发布","ja":"ポスター スキル：クロスプラットフォーム ソーシャル メディア コンテンツ公開","ko":"포스터 스킬: 크로스 플랫폼 소셜 미디어 콘텐츠 게시","es":"Publicación en plataformas sociales con Poster","fr":"Publication sur les plateformes sociales avec Poster","de":"Veröffentlichung auf sozialen Plattformen mit Poster","pt":"Criar Posts em Múltiplas Plataformas com o Poster","ru":"Публикация постов на нескольких платформах с Poster","ar":"إنشاء منشورات متعددة على منصات مختلفة باستخدام Poster","en":"poster"},"description":{"zh":"Poster 技能允许开发者跨平台发布内容到社交媒体，包括 Moltbook 和 X/Twitter。","ja":"ポスター スキルは、開発者が Moltbook や X/Twitter などのソーシャル メディアにコンテンツを公開できるようにします。","ko":"포스터 스킬을 통해 개발자는 몰트북 및 엑스/트위터와 같은 소셜 미디어에 콘텐츠를 게시할 수 있습니다.","es":"La habilidad de Poster permite publicar contenido en varias plataformas sociales. Crea hilos y programa publicaciones con facilidad.","fr":"La compétence Poster permet de publier du contenu sur plusieurs plateformes sociales. Créez des fils et programmez des publications avec facilité.","de":"Die Fähigkeit Poster ermöglicht die Veröffentlichung von Inhalten auf mehreren sozialen Plattformen. Erstellen Sie Threads und planen Sie Veröffentlichungen ...","pt":"O Poster é uma habilidade de IA que permite publicar conteúdo em múltiplas plataformas, incluindo Moltbook e X/Twitter. Com ele, você pode criar threads, age...","ru":"Poster - это навык ИИ, который позволяет публиковать контент на нескольких платформах, включая Moltbook и X/Twitter. С его помощью вы можете создавать треды,...","ar":"Poster هو مهارة ذكاء اصطناعي يسمح بنشر المحتوى على منصات متعددة، بما في ذلك Moltbook و X/Twitter. باستخدامه، يمكنك إنشاء Threads وتنسيق المنشورات وحفظ المسودات.","en":"AI"},"definition":{"en":"AI"},"features":{"zh":["跨平台发布","支持线程和单个帖子","定时发布功能","草稿功能","支持 Moltbook 和 X/Twitter"],"ja":["クロスプラットフォーム公開","スレッドと単体投稿のサポート","スケジュール公開機能","下書き機能","Moltbook と X/Twitter のサポート"],"ko":["크로스 플랫폼 게시","스레드 및 단일 게시물 지원","예약 게시 기능","초안 기능","몰트북 및 엑스/트위터 지원"],"es":["Publicación en Moltbook y X/Twitter","Creación de hilos","Programación de publicaciones","Opción de guardar como borrador","Compatibilidad con varias plataformas"],"fr":["Publication sur Moltbook et X/Twitter","Création de fils","Planification de publications","Option d''enregistrer comme brouillon","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes"],"de":["Veröffentlichung auf Moltbook und X/Twitter","Erstellung von Threads","Planung von Veröffentlichungen","Option zum Speichern als Entwurf","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen"],"pt":["Publicação em múltiplas plataformas","Criação de threads","Agendamento de posts","Salvamento de rascunhos","Suporte a Moltbook e X/Twitter"],"ru":["Публикация на нескольких платформах","Создание тредов","Планирование публикаций","Сохранение черновиков","Поддержка Moltbook и X/Twitter"],"ar":["نشر على منصات متعددة","إنشاء Threads","تنسيق المنشورات","حفظ المسودات","دعم Moltbook و X/Twitter"]},"keywords":{"zh":["社交媒体发布","跨平台发布","AI 能力","Poster 技能","Moltbook","X/Twitter","社交媒体营销","内容发布"],"ja":["ソーシャル メディア公開","クロスプラットフォーム公開","AI 能力","ポスター スキル","Moltbook","X/Twitter","ソーシャル メディア マーケティング","コンテンツ公開"],"ko":["소셜 미디어 게시","크로스 플랫폼 게시","AI 능력","포스터 스킬","몰트북","엑스/트위터","소셜 미디어 마케팅","콘텐츠 게시"],"es":["publicación en redes sociales","poster","moltbook","x/twitter","creación de hilos","programación de publicaciones","desarrollo de aplicaciones","integración de api"],"fr":["publication sur les réseaux sociaux","poster","moltbook","x/twitter","création de fils","planification de publications","développement d''applications","intégration d''api"],"de":["Veröffentlichung auf sozialen Netzwerken","poster","moltbook","x/twitter","erstellung von threads","planung von veröffentlichungen","anwendungsentwicklung","api-integration"],"pt":["Poster","IA","publicação de conteúdo","múltiplas plataformas","Moltbook","X/Twitter","threads","agendamento de posts"],"ru":["Poster","ИИ","публикация контента","несколько платформ","Moltbook","X/Twitter","треды","планирование публикаций"],"ar":["Poster","ذكاء اصطناعي","نشر المحتوى","منصات متعددة","Moltbook","X/Twitter","Threads","تنسيق المنشورات"]}},"owner":"frogr","repo":"austnomaton","repoPath":"frogr/austnomaton","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"poster","description":"Post content to X and Moltbook","bodyPreview":"# Poster Skill\n\n## Purpose\nPublish content to social platforms:\n- Moltbook posts\n- X/Twitter posts and threads\n- Cross-platform publishing\n\n## Invocation\n```\n/poster [platform] [content] [options]\n```\n\n### Arguments\n- `platform`: moltbook, x, or all\n- `content` (optional): Content to post (or will be prompted)\n- `--thread`: Create a thread instead of single post\n- `--schedule [time]`: Schedule for later\n- `--draft`: Save as draft without posting\n\n### Examples\n```\n/poster moltbook \"Just shipped a","body":"# Poster Skill\n\n## Purpose\nPublish content to social platforms:\n- Moltbook posts\n- X/Twitter posts and threads\n- Cross-platform publishing\n\n## Invocation\n```\n/poster [platform] [content] [options]\n```\n\n### Arguments\n- `platform`: moltbook, x, or all\n- `content` (optional): Content to post (or will be prompted)\n- `--thread`: Create a thread instead of single post\n- `--schedule [time]`: Schedule for later\n- `--draft`: Save as draft without posting\n\n### Examples\n```\n/poster moltbook \"Just shipped a new feature\"\n/poster x --thread                    # Start thread workflow\n/poster all \"Cross-platform post\"     # Post everywhere\n```\n\n## Platforms\n\n### Moltbook\n- API Key required (in .env)\n- Supports longer posts\n- Markdown formatting\n- Community engagement\n\n### X/Twitter\n- OAuth credentials required (in .env)\n- 280 character limit\n- Thread support\n- Media attachments\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Prepare** content (validate length, format)\n2. **Check** against content-log.md (no duplicates)\n3. **Load** appropriate personality (poster.md)\n4. **Review** content for quality\n5. **Post** to specified platform(s)\n6. **Log** to content-log.md\n7. **Notify** if configured\n8. **Update** metrics\n\n## Content Guidelines\n\n### Loaded from `personality/poster.md`:\n- Poaster energy but not mean\n- Funny observations\n- Hot takes that are good\n- Lowercase acceptable\n- Emoji sparingly\n\n### Quality Checks\n- [ ] Not too similar to recent posts\n- [ ] Appropriate for platform\n- [ ] Aligns with personality\n- [ ] Not cringe\n- [ ] Adds value\n\n## API Integration\n\n### Moltbook API\n```python\n# POST to Moltbook\nimport requests\nimport os\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    \"https://api.moltbook.com/v1/posts\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ[''MOLTBOOK_API_KEY'']}\"},\n    json={\"content\": content}\n)\n```\n\n### X API\n```python\n# Uses tweepy or similar library\n# Requires OAuth 1.0a authentication\n# See X Developer docs for details\n```\n\n## Logging\n\nEvery post logged to `memory/content-log.md`:\n```markdown\n### [DATE] [PLATFORM] post\n**Content**: The actual content\n**Link**: https://moltbook.com/post/123\n**Performance**: TBD (updated later)\n```\n\n## Safety\n\n- Rate limiting enforced\n- Duplicate detection\n- No auto-posting without review (configurable)\n- Follows platform ToS\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:05:01.313Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Social Media Management Agents needing cross-platform publishing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要跨平台发布功能的社交媒体管理代理。","ja":"クロスプラットフォームでの投稿機能を必要とするソーシャルメディア管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"크로스 플랫폼 게시 기능이 필요한 소셜 미디어 관리 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de redes sociales que necesitan capacidades de publicación entre plataformas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion des médias sociaux ayant besoin de capacités de publication multiplateformes.","de":"Perfekt für Social Media Management Agenten, die cross-plattformfähige Publikationsmöglichkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Mídia Social que precisam de capacidades de publicação cross-plataforma.","ru":"Идеально для агентов социального медиа-менеджмента, которым необходимы возможности кроссплатформенной публикации.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء إدارة وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات النشر عبر منصات متعددة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to publish content across Moltbook and X/Twitter platforms, supporting threads, scheduling, and draft saving, utilizing protocols like HTTP for seamless posting and management.","zh":"赋予代理在Moltbook和X/Twitter平台上发布内容的能力，支持线程、调度和草稿保存，利用HTTP等协议实现无缝发布和管理。","ja":"MoltbookとX/Twitterプラットフォーム上でコンテンツを投稿するエージェントの能力を強化し、スレッド、スケジューリング、下書き保存をサポートし、HTTPなどのプロトコルを利用してシームレスな投稿と管理を実現します。","ko":"Moltbook과 X/Twitter 플랫폼에서 콘텐츠를 게시하는 에이전트의 능력을 강화하여 스레드, 예약, 초안 저장을 지원하며 HTTP와 같은 프로토콜을 이용하여 무결점 게시와 관리를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a publicar contenido en las plataformas Moltbook y X/Twitter, con soporte para hilos, programación y guardar borradores, utilizando protocolos como HTTP para publicación y administración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de publier du contenu sur les plateformes Moltbook et X/Twitter, en prenant en charge les fils, la planification et l''enregistrement de brouillons, en utilisant des protocoles comme HTTP pour une publication et une gestion sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Inhalte auf den Plattformen Moltbook und X/Twitter zu veröffentlichen, mit Unterstützung für Threads, Planung und Entwurfspeicherung, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie HTTP für eine nahtlose Veröffentlichung und Verwaltung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a publicar conteúdo em plataformas Moltbook e X/Twitter, com suporte a threads, agendamento e salvamento de rascunhos, utilizando protocolos como HTTP para postagem e gerenciamento sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью публиковать контент на платформах Moltbook и X/Twitter, поддерживая потоки, планирование и сохранение черновиков, используя протоколы như HTTP для бесперебойной публикации и управления.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من نشر المحتوى على منصات Moltbook و X/Twitter ، مع دعم الخيوط ، والجدولة ، وحفظ المسودات ، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTTP لنشر وإدارة دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating daily social media posts","Creating engaging threads on X/Twitter","Scheduling promotional content on Moltbook"],"zh":["自动化每日社交媒体帖子","在X/Twitter上创建吸引人的线程","在Moltbook上安排促销内容"],"ja":["毎日のソーシャルメディア投稿の自動化","X/Twitter上で魅力的スレッドの作成","Moltbook上でのプロモーションコンテンツのスケジューリング"],"ko":["일일 소셜 미디어 게시의 자동화","X/Twitter에서 매력적인 스레드 생성","Moltbook에서 프로모션 콘텐츠 예약"],"es":["Automatizar publicaciones diarias en las redes sociales","Crear hilos atractivos en X/Twitter","Programar contenido promocional en Moltbook"],"fr":["Automatiser les publications quotidiennes sur les médias sociaux","Créer des fils attractifs sur X/Twitter","Planifier du contenu promotionnel sur Moltbook"],"de":["Automatisierung von täglichen Social-Media-Beiträgen","Erstellen von ansprechenden Threads auf X/Twitter","Planung von Werbeinhalten auf Moltbook"],"pt":["Automatizar postagens diárias de mídia social","Criar threads atraentes no X/Twitter","Agendar conteúdo promocional no Moltbook"],"ru":["Автоматизация ежедневных постов в социальных сетях","Создание привлекательных потоков в X/Twitter","Планирование промо-контента в Moltbook"],"ar":["توفير منشورات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية اليومية","إنشاء خيوط جذابة على منصة X/Twitter","جدولة محتوى تعليمي على منصة Moltbook"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires platform-specific API access","Limited to text-based content posting"],"zh":["需要平台特定的API访问","仅限文本基于内容发布"],"ja":["プラットフォーム固有のAPIアクセスが必要","テキストベースのコンテンツ投稿のみに限定"],"ko":["플랫폼 특정 API 접근이 필요","텍스트 기반 콘텐츠 게시만 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API específica de la plataforma","Limitado a la publicación de contenido basado en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API spécifique à la plateforme","Limité à la publication de contenu basé sur du texte"],"de":["Benötigt plattformspezifischen API-Zugriff","Begrenzt auf die Veröffentlichung von textbasiertem Inhalt"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API específica da plataforma","Limitado à publicação de conteúdo baseado em texto"],"ru":["Требует доступа к API конкретной платформы","Ограничен публикацией текстового контента"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات محددة للمنصة","محدود بنشر المحتوى القائم على النص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('manutej/categorical-meta-prompting/meta-self', 'community', 'manutej', 'categorical-meta-prompting', 'manutej/categorical-meta-prompting', 'meta-self', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z', '2026-02-18T03:05:31.860Z', NULL, '{"id":"manutej/categorical-meta-prompting/meta-self","name":"meta-self","description":{"zh":"Meta-Self是AI元提示的分类基础，提供结构化转换、迭代改进和上下文提取等功能","ja":"Meta-SelfはAIメタプロンプティングのカテゴリ的基礎であり、構造化変換、イテレーティブ改善、コンテキスト抽出などの機能を提供","ko":"메타셀프는 AI 메타 프롬프팅의 분류 기반으로, 구조화 변환, 반복적 개선, 컨텍스트 추출 등의 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Meta-Self es el marco de referencia para el framework de meta-prompting categorial, proporcionando una sintaxis unificada para el desarrollo de AI","fr":"Meta-Self est le référentiel pour le framework de meta-prompting categorial, offrant une syntaxe unifiée pour le développement de l''IA","de":"Meta-Self ist das Referenzframework für das kategoriale Meta-Prompting, bietet eine einheitliche Syntax für die Entwicklung von KI","pt":"O Meta-Self é um framework de meta-prompting categórico que fornece uma estrutura unificada para desenvolvedores de IA","ru":"Meta-Self - это единый справочник категориальной синтаксиса для разработчиков ИИ","ar":"ميتا-سيلف هو إطار عمل متكامل لمحاكاة الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Meta-Self：统一的分类语法参考","ja":"Meta-Self：統一されたカテゴリ的構文リファレンス","ko":"메타셀프:統一カテゴリ 구문 참조","es":"Meta-Self: Marco de Sintaxis Categorial Unificada","fr":"Meta-Self : Référence de Syntaxe Categoriale Unifiée","de":"Meta-Self: Einheitliches Kategoriales Syntax-Referenz","pt":"Meta-Self: Referência de Sintaxe Categórica para Desenvol...","ru":"Meta-Self: Единый справочник категориальной синтаксиса","ar":"ميتا-سيلف: مرجع بنية متكاملة للتنمية","en":"meta-self"},"description":{"zh":"Meta-Self是AI元提示的分类基础，提供结构化转换、迭代改进和上下文提取等功能","ja":"Meta-SelfはAIメタプロンプティングのカテゴリ的基礎であり、構造化変換、イテレーティブ改善、コンテキスト抽出などの機能を提供","ko":"메타셀프는 AI 메타 프롬프팅의 분류 기반으로, 구조화 변환, 반복적 개선, 컨텍스트 추출 등의 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Meta-Self es el marco de referencia para el framework de meta-prompting categorial, proporcionando una sintaxis unificada para el desarrollo de AI","fr":"Meta-Self est le référentiel pour le framework de meta-prompting categorial, offrant une syntaxe unifiée pour le développement de l''IA","de":"Meta-Self ist das Referenzframework für das kategoriale Meta-Prompting, bietet eine einheitliche Syntax für die Entwicklung von KI","pt":"O Meta-Self é um framework de meta-prompting categórico que fornece uma estrutura unificada para desenvolvedores de IA","ru":"Meta-Self - это единый справочник категориальной синтаксиса для разработчиков ИИ","ar":"ميتا-سيلف هو إطار عمل متكامل لمحاكاة الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"definition":{"en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"features":{"zh":["结构化转换","迭代改进","上下文提取","自然变换","元提示框架"],"ja":["構造化変換","イテレーティブ改善","コンテキスト抽出","自然変換","メタプロンプティングフレームワーク"],"ko":["구조화 변환","반복적 개선","컨텍스트 추출","자연 변환","메타 프롬프팅 프레임워크"],"es":["Marco de referencia categorial unificado","Mejoras de calidad medibles en el desarrollo de AI","Sintaxis estructurada para el meta-prompting","Soporte para la iteración y refinamiento de prompts","Integración con comonads para la extracción de contexto"],"fr":["Référentiel categoriel unifié","Améliorations de qualité mesurables dans le développement de l''IA","Syntaxe structurée pour le meta-prompting","Prise en charge de l''itération et du raffinement des prompts","Intégration avec des comonades pour l''extraction de contexte"],"de":["Einheitliches kategoriales Referenzframework","Messbare Qualitätsverbesserungen in der KI-Entwicklung","Strukturierte Syntax für das Meta-Prompting","Unterstützung für die Iteration und Verfeinerung von Prompts","Integration mit Komonaden für die Kontextextraktion"],"pt":["Estrutura unificada para desenvolvedores de IA","Melhoria comprovada na qualidade dos modelos de IA","Functor para transformação de estruturas","Monad para refinamento iterativo","Comonad para extração de contexto"],"ru":["Единый справочник категориальной синтаксиса","Проверенное улучшение качества моделей ИИ","Функтор для структуры-презервации","Монада для итеративного уточнения","Комонада для извлечения контекста"],"ar":["هيكل متكامل لتنمية الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين مثبت في جودة نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","مرافق للتحويل الهيكلي","موناد للتحسين التكراري","كوموناد لاستخراج السياق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI元提示","分类语法","结构化转换","迭代改进","上下文提取","自然变换"],"ja":["AIメタプロンプティング","カテゴリ的構文","構造化変換","イテレーティブ改善","コンテキスト抽出","自然変換"],"ko":["AI 메타 프롬프팅","분류 구문","구조화 변환","반복적 개선","컨텍스트 추출","자연 변환"],"es":["meta-prompting","desarrollo de AI","marco de referencia categorial","mejoras de calidad","sintaxis unificada","comonads","iteración de prompts"],"fr":["meta-prompting","développement de l''IA","référentiel categoriel","améliorations de qualité","syntaxe unifiée","comonades","itération de prompts"],"de":["Meta-Prompting","KI-Entwicklung","kategoriales Referenzframework","Qualitätsverbesserungen","einheitliche Syntax","Komonaden","Prompt-Iteration"],"pt":["Meta-Self","framework de meta-prompting categórico","desenvolvedores de IA","melhoria da qualidade dos modelos de IA","functor","monad","comonad"],"ru":["Meta-Self","единый справочник категориальной синтаксиса","разработчики ИИ","проверенное улучшение качества моделей ИИ","функтор","монада","комонада"],"ar":["ميتا-سيلف","إطار عمل متكامل لمحاكاة الذكاء الاصطناعي","مطورو الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين جودة نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","مرافق","موناد","كوموناد"]}},"owner":"manutej","repo":"categorical-meta-prompting","repoPath":"manutej/categorical-meta-prompting","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"meta-self","description":"Master reference for categorical meta-prompting unified syntax. Contains all modifiers, operators, composition patterns, and execution protocols. Use this skill for self-reference when executing any prompt workflow, ensuring consistent syntax across all commands and skills.","bodyPreview":"# Meta-Self: Unified Categorical Syntax Reference\n\nThis skill serves as the authoritative reference for the categorical meta-prompting framework. All commands and skills should align with this specification.\n\n## Categorical Foundation\n\n```\nF: Task → Prompt        (Functor - structure-preserving transformation)\nM: Prompt →^n Prompt    (Monad - iterative refinement)\nW: History → Context    (Comonad - context extraction)\nα: F ⇒ G                (Natural Transformation - strategy switching)\nE: Eithe","body":"# Meta-Self: Unified Categorical Syntax Reference\n\nThis skill serves as the authoritative reference for the categorical meta-prompting framework. All commands and skills should align with this specification.\n\n## Categorical Foundation\n\n```\nF: Task → Prompt        (Functor - structure-preserving transformation)\nM: Prompt →^n Prompt    (Monad - iterative refinement)\nW: History → Context    (Comonad - context extraction)\nα: F ⇒ G                (Natural Transformation - strategy switching)\nE: Either Error A       (Exception Monad - error handling)\n[0,1]: Quality → Quality (Enriched - quality tracking)\n```\n\n### Categorical Laws (Must Be Satisfied)\n\n```\n1. Functor Identity:     F(id) = id\n2. Functor Composition:  F(g ∘ f) = F(g) ∘ F(f)\n3. Monad Left Identity:  return >=> f = f\n4. Monad Right Identity: f >=> return = f\n5. Monad Associativity:  (f >=> g) >=> h = f >=> (g >=> h)\n6. Comonad Left Id:      extract ∘ duplicate = id\n7. Comonad Associativity: duplicate ∘ duplicate = fmap duplicate ∘ duplicate\n8. Naturality Condition: α_B ∘ F(f) = G(f) ∘ α_A  for all f: A → B\n9. Exception Catch Id:   catch(Right(a), h) = Right(a)  (Phase 3)\n10. Exception Catch Err: catch(Left(e), h) = h(e)       (Phase 3)\n11. Exception Assoc:     Error handling preserves Kleisli associativity\n12. Quality Monotonicity: quality(A ⊗ B) ≤ min(quality(A), quality(B))\n```\n\n### Exception Monad E (Phase 3)\n\n**Type**: `Either<Error, A> = Left(Error) | Right(A)`\n\n**Operations**:\n1. **return**: `a → Right(a)` (pure success)\n2. **bind (>=>)**: Error-propagating composition\n   ```\n   m >>= f = case m of\n     Left(e) → Left(e)        -- error propagates\n     Right(a) → f(a)          -- continue on success\n   ```\n3. **catch**: Error recovery\n   ```\n   catch(m, handler) = case m of\n     Left(e) → handler(e)     -- recover from error\n     Right(a) → Right(a)      -- pass through success\n   ```\n\n**Laws**:\n- **Left Identity**: `return(a) >>= f = f(a)`\n- **Right Identity**: `m >>= return = m`\n- **Associativity**: `(m >>= f) >>= g = m >>= (λx. f(x) >>= g)`\n- **Catch Identity**: `catch(Right(a), h) = Right(a)`\n- **Catch Error**: `catch(Left(e), h) = h(e)`\n- **Catch Composition**: `catch(catch(m, h1), h2) = catch(m, λe. catch(h1(e), h2))`\n\n**In Framework**:\n- Used by `@catch:` modifier for error handling behaviors\n- Used by `@fallback:` modifier for recovery strategies\n- Integrates with `/chain` and `/rmp` commands\n- Preserves composition with existing operators (→, ||, >=>)\n\n---\n\n## Unified Modifiers\n\nAll commands support these modifiers. Place them before the task description.\n\n### @mode: - Execution Mode\n\n| Mode | Description | Effect |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| `@mode:active` | Default execution | Execute with auto-detection |\n| `@mode:iterative` | RMP loop | Iterate until @quality: met |\n| `@mode:dry-run` | Preview only | Show plan, no execution |\n| `@mode:spec` | Generate spec | Output YAML specification |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @mode:iterative \"build auth system\"`\n\n### @quality: - Quality Threshold\n\n| Format | Description | Range |\n|--------|-------------|-------|\n| `@quality:0.85` | Target threshold | 0.0 - 1.0 |\n| `@quality:85%` | Percentage form | 0% - 100% |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @quality:0.9 \"optimize algorithm\"`\n\n### @tier: - Complexity Tier\n\n| Tier | Tokens | Pattern | Strategy |\n|------|--------|---------|----------|\n| `@tier:L1` | 600-1200 | Single op | DIRECT |\n| `@tier:L2` | 1500-3000 | A → B | DIRECT |\n| `@tier:L3` | 2500-4500 | A → B → C | MULTI_APPROACH |\n| `@tier:L4` | 3000-6000 | A \\|\\| B \\|\\| C | MULTI_APPROACH |\n| `@tier:L5` | 5500-9000 | Hierarchical | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n| `@tier:L6` | 8000-12000 | Iterative | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n| `@tier:L7` | 12000-22000 | Ensemble | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @tier:L5 \"design microservices\"`\n\n### @budget: - Token Budget\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@budget:20000` | Total tokens |\n| `@budget:[5K,4K,6K]` | Per-agent allocation |\n| `@budget:auto` | Automatic calculation |\n\n**Example**: `/task-relay @budget:[5000,4000,6000] [R→D→I]`\n\n### @variance: - Budget Variance Threshold\n\n| Format | Description | Action |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@variance:15%` | Acceptable variance | WARN if exceeded |\n| `@variance:20%` | Default | HALT if exceeded |\n\n**Example**: `/hekat @budget:18K @variance:15% [R→D→I]`\n\n### @max_iterations: - Iteration Limit\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@max_iterations:5` | Maximum RMP iterations |\n| `@max_iterations:3` | Fewer iterations |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @quality:0.9 @max_iterations:3 \"task\"`\n\n### @catch: - Error Handling Behavior (Phase 3)\n\n| Format | Description | Result |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@catch:halt` | Stop chain on error (default) | Left(error) |\n| `@catch:log` | Log error, continue chain | Left(error) logged |\n| `@catch:retry:N` | Retry command N times | Right(result) or Left(error) |\n| `@catch:skip` | Skip failed command | Right(empty) |\n| `@catch:substitute:/alt` | Use alternative command | Right(alt_result) |\n\n**Example**: `/chain @catch:retry:3 [/api→/process] \"fetch data\"`\n\n### @fallback: - Error Recovery Strategy (Phase 3)\n\n| Format | Description | When Used |\n|--------|-------------|-----------|\n| `@fallback:return-best` | Return highest quality result | Iterative refinement |\n| `@fallback:return-last` | Return last successful result | Prefer recency |\n| `@fallback:use-default:[val]` | Use specific default | Known safe value |\n| `@fallback:empty` | Return empty/neutral | Minimal context |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @fallback:return-best @quality:0.9 \"complex task\"`\n\n### @quality:visualize - Quality Flow Visualization (Phase 5)\n\n| Format | Description | Output |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@quality:visualize` | Show quality flow (default: bar chart) | Visual quality tracking |\n| `@quality:visualize:bar` | Bar chart format | ASCII bar chart |\n| `@quality:visualize:flow` | Flow diagram format | Arrows with quality values |\n| `@quality:visualize:detailed` | Detailed breakdown | Full quality metrics |\n| `@quality:visualize:compact` | Compact summary | Single-line summary |\n\n**Categorical Foundation**: Uses [0,1]-enriched category structure where `Hom_Q(A, B) = [0,1]` and quality tensor follows `q1 ⊗ q2 = min(q1, q2)`\n\n**Example**: `/chain @quality:visualize [/analyze→/design→/implement] \"build feature\"`\n\n### @template: - Template Components\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@template:{context:expert}` | Single component |\n| `@template:{context:X}+{mode:Y}+{format:Z}` | Combined |\n\n**Components**:\n- `{context:expert\\|teacher\\|reviewer\\|debugger}`\n- `{mode:direct\\|cot\\|multi\\|iterative}`\n- `{format:prose\\|structured\\|code\\|checklist}`\n\n**Example**: `/meta @template:{context:expert}+{mode:cot}+{format:code} \"implement\"`\n\n### @domain: - Force Domain Classification\n\n| Domain | Use Case |\n|--------|----------|\n| `@domain:ALGORITHM` | Algorithmic correctness |\n| `@domain:SECURITY` | Security review |\n| `@domain:API` | API design/review |\n| `@domain:DEBUG` | Debugging |\n| `@domain:TESTING` | Test generation |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @domain:SECURITY \"review auth code\"`\n\n### @skills: - Skill Discovery & Composition\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@skills:discover(domain=X)` | Discover by domain |\n| `@skills:discover(relevance>0.7)` | Discover by quality |\n| `@skills:compose(A⊗B)` | Tensor composition |\n| `@skills:compose(A→B→C)` | Sequential |\n| `@skills:compose(A>=>B)` | Kleisli |\n| `@skills:skill1,skill2` | Explicit list |\n| `@skills:best(domain=X)` | Best for domain |\n\n**Example**: `/meta-command @skills:compose(api-testing⊗validation) \"create tests\"`\n\n---\n\n## Composition Operators\n\n### → (Sequence) - Kleisli Composition\n\n**Unicode**: U+2192\n**Meaning**: Output of A becomes input of B\n**Quality**: `quality(A → B) ≤ min(quality(A), quality(B))`\n\n```bash\n# Command syntax\n/chain [/debug→/review→/test] \"error in auth.py\"\n\n# Agent syntax\n[R→D→I→T] \"build feature\"\n\n# Skill syntax\n@skills:compose(research→design→implement)\n```\n\n### || (Parallel) - Concurrent Execution\n\n**Meaning**: Execute A, B, C concurrently, aggregate results\n**Quality**: `quality(A || B || C) = mean(quality(A), quality(B), quality(C))`\n\n```bash\n# Parallel commands\n/chain [/review-security || /review-performance] \"audit code\"\n\n# Parallel agents\n[R||D||A] \"evaluate options\"\n\n# Mixed\n[R→(D||F)→I] \"full-stack with parallel design\"\n```\n\n### ⊗ (Tensor) - Quality-Degrading Combination\n\n**Unicode**: U+2297\n**Meaning**: Combine capabilities, quality degrades to minimum\n**Quality**: `quality(A ⊗ B) = min(quality(A), quality(B))`\n\n```bash\n# Skill tensor\n@skills:compose(api-testing⊗jest-patterns⊗validation)\n\n# Agent tensor\n[debug-detective⊗test-engineer] \"fix and test\"\n```\n\n### >=> (Kleisli) - Monadic Refinement\n\n**Meaning**: Composition with quality-gated iteration at each stage\n**Quality**: `quality(A >=> B)` improves with each iteration\n\n```bash\n# RMP stages\n/rmp @quality:0.85 [analyze>=>design>=>implement] \"build feature\"\n\n# Each stage:\n# 1. Execute\n# 2. Assess quality\n# 3. If quality < threshold: refine\n# 4. Pass to next stage\n```\n\n---\n\n## Command Invocation Syntax\n\n### Standard Pattern\n\n```\n/<command> @modifier1:value @modifier2:value [composition] \"task description\"\n```\n\n### Examples\n\n```bash\n# Simple\n/meta \"implement rate limiter\"\n\n# With modifiers\n/meta @mode:iterative @quality:0.85 \"build API\"\n\n# With composition\n/chain [/debug→/fix→/test] \"TypeError in auth.py\"\n\n# Full syntax\n/hekat @mode:active @tier:L5 @budget:18K [R→D→(I||T)] \"build auth system\"\n\n# With skills\n/meta-command @skills:discover(domain=API) @mode:iterative \"create endpoint\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent Hotkeys (HEKAT Compatible)\n\n### Tier 1 - Single Agent\n\n| Key | Agent | Domain |\n|-----|-------|--------|\n| `[R]` | deep-researcher | Research |\n| `[D]` | api-architect | Design |\n| `[I]` | practical-programmer | Implementation |\n| `[T]` | test-engineer | Testing |\n| `[B]` | build-engineer | Build |\n| `[F]` | frontend-specialist | Frontend |\n| `[A]` | analyzer | Analysis |\n\n### Tier 2 - Ctrl Modifiers\n\n| Key | Effect |\n|-----|--------|\n| `[Ctrl+P]` | L4 Parallel mode |\n| `[Ctrl+H]` | L5 Hierarchical mode |\n| `[Ctrl+I]` | L6 Iterative mode |\n\n### Tier 3 - Agent Chains\n\n```bash\n[R→D→I]        # Research → Design → Implement\n[R→D→I→T]      # Full pipeline with testing\n[P:R||D||A]    # Parallel: Research, Design, Analyze\n[R→(D||F)→I]   # Mixed: Research, parallel Design/Frontend, Implement\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quality Assessment Structure\n\n### Multi-Dimensional Quality Vector\n\n| Dimension | Weight | Description |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| Correctness | 40% | Does it solve the problem? |\n| Clarity | 25% | Is it understandable? |\n| Completeness | 20% | Are edge cases handled? |\n| Efficiency | 15% | Is it well-designed? |\n\n### Aggregate Score\n\n```\naggregate = (0.40 × correctness) + (0.25 × clarity) +\n            (0.20 × completeness) + (0.15 × efficiency)\n```\n\n### Quality Thresholds\n\n| Score | Status | Action |\n|-------|--------|--------|\n| ≥0.9 | Excellent | Stop, success |\n| 0.8-0.9 | Good | Stop, success |\n| 0.7-0.8 | Acceptable | Continue if @mode:iterative |\n| 0.6-0.7 | Poor | Refine if iterations remain |\n| <0.6 | Failed | Abort or restructure |\n\n---\n\n## Checkpoint Format\n\nAll commands produce standardized checkpoints:\n\n```yaml\nCHECKPOINT_[type]_[n]:\n  command: /[command]\n  iteration: [n]\n  quality:\n    correctness: [0-1]\n    clarity: [0-1]\n    completeness: [0-1]\n    efficiency: [0-1]\n    aggregate: [0-1]\n  quality_delta: [+/- from previous]\n  budget:\n    used: [tokens]\n    remaining: [tokens]\n    variance: [%]\n  status: [CONTINUE | CONVERGED | MAX_ITERATIONS | HALT]\n  trend: [RAPID_IMPROVEMENT | STEADY_IMPROVEMENT | PLATEAU | DEGRADING]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Simple Task\n\n```bash\n/meta \"task\"\n```\n- Auto-detect domain, tier, template\n- Single-pass execution\n\n### Pattern 2: Quality-Gated Iteration\n\n```bash\n/rmp @quality:0.85 @max_iterations:5 \"task\"\n```\n- Iterate until quality threshold\n- Track quality improvement\n\n### Pattern 3: Multi-Stage Pipeline\n\n```bash\n/chain [/analyze→/design→/implement→/test] \"feature\"\n```\n- Sequential execution\n- Output → Input flow\n\n### Pattern 4: Parallel Exploration\n\n```bash\n/chain [/approach-a || /approach-b || /approach-c] \"evaluate options\"\n```\n- Concurrent execution\n- Aggregate results\n\n### Pattern 5: Hierarchical Orchestration\n\n```bash\n/hekat @tier:L5 [Lead→(Worker||Worker)→Synthesize] \"complex task\"\n```\n- Lead agent coordinates\n- Workers execute in parallel\n- Synthesizer combines results\n\n### Pattern 6: Skill-Driven Meta-Command\n\n```bash\n/meta-command @skills:discover(domain=API,relevance>0.7) \"create endpoint command\"\n```\n- Auto-discover relevant skills\n- Inject into command creation\n\n---\n\n## Mode Behaviors\n\n### @mode:active\n- Execute immediately\n- Auto-detect all parameters\n- Single-pass unless combined with @mode:iterative\n\n### @mode:iterative\n- Enable RMP loop\n- Iterate until @quality: threshold\n- Track quality across iterations\n\n### @mode:dry-run\n- Show execution plan\n- Do not execute\n- Exit after plan display\n\n### @mode:spec\n- Generate YAML specification\n- Do not execute\n- Exit after spec generation\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Budget Exceeded\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: HALT\nreason: \"Budget variance exceeded @variance: threshold\"\naction: \"Review agent outputs, adjust budget allocation\"\n```\n\n### Quality Plateau\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: NO_IMPROVEMENT\nreason: \"Quality improvement < 0.02 for 2 iterations\"\naction: \"Fixed-point reached, returning best result\"\n```\n\n### Max Iterations\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: MAX_ITERATIONS\nreason: \"Reached @max_iterations: limit\"\naction: \"Return best result from iterations\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Self-Reference Protocol\n\nWhen executing any command or skill:\n\n1. **Check modifiers**: Parse all @modifier: values\n2. **Apply defaults**: Use defaults for unspecified modifiers\n3. **Validate syntax**: Ensure operators match specification\n4. **Execute**: Follow categorical laws\n5. **Checkpoint**: Output standardized checkpoint\n6. **Quality assess**: Evaluate using multi-dimensional vector\n7. **Decide**: CONTINUE, CONVERGE, or HALT based on rules\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference Quick Look\n\n### Core Categorical Commands (F, M, W, α)\n\n| Command | Categorical Role | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|------------------|---------------|\n| `/meta` | **Functor F**: Task → Prompt | @mode:, @tier:, @template:, @domain: |\n| `/rmp` | **Monad M**: Prompt →ⁿ Prompt | @quality:, @max_iterations:, @mode: |\n| `/context` | **Comonad W**: History → Context | @mode:, @focus:, @depth:, @transform: |\n| `/transform` | **Nat. Trans. α**: F ⇒ G | @from:, @to:, @verify:, @mode: |\n\n### Natural Transformation Operations (/transform)\n\n| Mode | Description | Type Signature |\n|------|-------------|----------------|\n| `@mode:transform` | Strategy switch (default) | α_A: F(A) → G(A) |\n| `@mode:compare` | Compare strategies | Show F vs G side-by-side |\n| `@mode:analyze` | Recommend optimal | Suggest best α |\n\n**Strategy Registry (Functors)**:\n- `zero-shot` (F_ZS): Direct prompt, quality ~0.65\n- `few-shot` (F_FS): Exemplar prompt, quality ~0.78\n- `chain-of-thought` (F_CoT): Reasoning prompt, quality ~0.85\n- `tree-of-thought` (F_ToT): Branching prompt, quality ~0.88\n- `meta-prompting` (F_Meta): Adaptive prompt, quality ~0.90\n\n**Aliases**:\n- `/cot` = `/transform @to:chain-of-thought`\n- `/tot` = `/transform @to:tree-of-thought`\n\n### Comonad Operations (/context)\n\n| Mode | Operation | Type Signature |\n|------|-----------|----------------|\n| `@mode:extract` | Focus on current | ε: W(A) → A |\n| `@mode:duplicate` | Meta-observation | δ: W(A) → W(W(A)) |\n| `@mode:extend` | Context-aware transform | (W(A) → B) → W(A) → W(B) |\n\n**Aliases**:\n- `/extract` = `/context @mode:extract`\n- `/focus` = `/context @mode:extract @depth:1`\n\n### Composition & Routing Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|---------|---------------|\n| `/chain` | Command composition | @mode:, @budget:, @quality:, @catch:, @fallback:, @quality:visualize |\n| `/route` | Dynamic routing | @domain: |\n| `/build-prompt` | Template assembly | @template: |\n\n### Domain Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|---------|---------------|\n| `/review` | Domain-aware code review | @domain: |\n| `/debug` | Systematic debugging | @mode: |\n| `/hekat` | Agent orchestration DSL | @tier:, @budget:, @variance: |\n| `/meta-command` | Create new commands | @skills:, @mode: |\n| `/task-relay` | Multi-agent relay | @budget:, @pattern: |\n\n---\n\n## Skill Reference Quick Look\n\n| Skill | Purpose | Integration |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `categorical-meta-prompting` | Core F, M, W framework | /meta, /rmp, /context |\n| `categorical-structure-builder` | Implement any categorical structure | {prompt:categorical-structure} |\n| `recursive-meta-prompting` | RMP implementation patterns | @mode:iterative |\n| `dynamic-prompt-registry` | Prompt lookup/composition | @skills:, {prompt:} |\n| `quality-enriched-prompting` | [0,1]-enriched quality | @quality: |\n| `atomic-blocks` | Composable atomic blocks | /blocks, @block: |\n| `meta-self` | This reference | Self-reference |\n\n---\n\n## Atomic Blocks (Layer 3 Access)\n\nFor power users who need fine-grained control, the framework exposes atomic blocks that underlie all commands.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n```\nSkill: atomic-blocks\nCommand: /blocks [composition] \"task\"\n```\n\n### Available Blocks\n\n| Layer | Blocks | Purpose |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| Assessment | assess_difficulty, assess_domain, assess_quality, select_tier | Analyze and classify |\n| Transformation | select_strategy, build_template, apply_transform, execute_prompt | Transform to outputs |\n| Refinement | evaluate_convergence, extract_improvement, apply_refinement | Monad M iteration |\n| Composition | sequence (→), parallel (\\|\\|), kleisli (>=>), tensor (⊗) | Combine blocks |\n\n### Progressive Disclosure\n\n| Layer | Users | Access |\n|-------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | 90% | `/meta \"task\"` - blocks hidden |\n| 2 | 9% | `/meta @block:assess_domain:SECURITY \"task\"` - override block |\n| 3 | 1% | `/blocks [assess_difficulty → select_tier] \"task\"` - compose |\n\n**Full specification**: `skill:atomic-blocks`\n\n---\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore executing any prompt:\n\n- [ ] All modifiers use `@name:value` syntax\n- [ ] Operators match: `→`, `||`, `⊗`, `>=>`\n- [ ] Quality thresholds in [0,1] range\n- [ ] Budget values are positive integers or \"auto\"\n- [ ] Tier values are L1-L7\n- [ ] Mode values are: active, iterative, dry-run, spec\n- [ ] Composition brackets match: `[...]`\n- [ ] Task description is quoted: `\"task\"`\n\n---\n\n## Version\n\n**Specification Version**: 2.5\n**Compatibility**: 100% backward compatible\n**Foundation**: Category Theory (F, M, W, α, E, [0,1]-enriched)\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-01\n**New in 2.5**: Atomic blocks system with /blocks command, @block: overrides, progressive disclosure\n**New in 2.4**: Quality Visualization via @quality:visualize modifier (Phase 5)\n**New in 2.3**: Exception Monad E for error handling via @catch:/@fallback: modifiers\n**New in 2.2**: Natural Transformation α operations via /transform command\n**New in 2.1**: Comonad W operations via /context command\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:05:31.860Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring categorical foundations for meta-prompting with proven correctness","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要分类基础以进行元提示，并具有经过验证的正确性","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、メタプロンプティングのためのカテゴリ的基礎と検証済みの正しさが必要","ko":"클로드 코드와 오토지피티 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 메타 프롬프트에 대한 범주적 기초와 검증된 정확성이 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren fundamentos categóricos para meta-prompting con corrección probada","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des fondements catégoriels pour le meta-prompting avec une correction prouvée","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die kategorische Grundlagen für Meta-Prompting mit bewiesener Korrektheit erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem fundamentos categóricos para meta-prompting com correção comprovada","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих категориальных основ для мета-пrompting с доказанной правильностью","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT التي تتطلب أسس فئوية لتحفيز siêu مع صحة مثبتة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Functor, Monad, and Comonad structures for iterative refinement and context extraction, enabling strategy switching via Natural Transformation and utilizing categorical syntax for unified meta-prompting frameworks, all while ensuring measurable quality improvements","zh":"赋予代理使用函子、单子和共单子结构进行迭代改进和上下文提取的能力，通过自然变换实现策略切换，并利用分类语法实现统一的元提示框架，同时确保可衡量的质量改进","ja":"ファンクター、モナド、コモナド構造を使用した反復的改良とコンテキスト抽出をエージェントに実現し、自然変換を通じて戦略の切り替えを可能にし、カテゴリ的構文を使用して統一されたメタプロンプティングフレームワークを実現し、同時に計測可能な品質の改善を確保","ko":"함수자, 모나드, 공모나드 구조를 사용한 반복적 개선 및 컨텍스트 추출을 에이전트에 가능하게 하며, 자연 변환을 통해 전략의 전환을 가능하게 하고, 범주적 구문을 사용하여 통일된 메타 프롬프트 프레임워크를 가능하게 하며, 동시에 측정 가능한 품질의 개선을 보장","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar las estructuras de Functor, Monad y Comonad para el refinamiento iterativo y la extracción de contexto, lo que permite el cambio de estrategia a través de la Transformación Natural y la utilización de la sintaxis categórica para marcos de meta-prompting unificados, todo mientras se garantizan mejoras de calidad medibles","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter les structures de Functor, de Monad et de Comonad pour un affinement itératif et une extraction de contexte, permettant le commutation de stratégie via la Transformation Naturelle et l''utilisation de la syntaxe catégorielle pour des cadres de meta-prompting unifiés, le tout en garantissant des améliorations de qualité mesurables","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Functor-, Monad- und Comonad-Strukturen für iterative Verfeinerung und Kontextextraktion zu nutzen, wodurch ein Strategiewechsel über natürliche Transformation ermöglicht wird und die kategorische Syntax für einheitliche Meta-Prompting-Frameworks genutzt wird, während gleichzeitig messbare Qualitätsverbesserungen gewährleistet werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitarem estruturas de Functor, Monad e Comonad para refinamento iterativo e extração de contexto, permitindo a troca de estratégias via Transformação Natural e utilizando sintaxe categórica para estruturas de meta-prompting unificadas, garantindo melhorias de qualidade mensuráveis","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать структуры Functor, Monad и Comonad для итеративного уточнения и извлечения контекста, обеспечивая возможность переключения стратегий через Естественную Трансформацию и использует категориальную синтаксис для унифицированных фреймворков мета-prompting, обеспечивая измеримые улучшения качества","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الاستفادة من هياكل الفانكتور والمناد والكوموناد لتحسين التكراري والاستخلاص السياقي، وتمكين تبديل الاستراتيجية من خلال التحويل الطبيعي واستخدام الصرف الفئوي لإطارات التحفيز الميتا الموحدة، مع ضمان تحسينات جودة قابلة للقياس"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating meta-prompt generation with categorical correctness","Refining prompts iteratively using Monad structures","Extracting context from history using Comonad functions"],"zh":["使用分类正确性自动化元提示生成","使用单子结构迭代改进提示","使用共单子函数从历史中提取上下文"],"ja":["カテゴリ的正しさを使用してメタプロンプティングの生成を自動化","モナド構造を使用して提示を反復的改良","コモナド関数を使用して履歴からコンテキストを抽出"],"ko":["범주적 정확성을 사용하여 메타 프롬프트 생성 자동화","모나드 구조를 사용하여 프롬프트 반복적 개선","공모나드 함수를 사용하여 기록에서 컨텍스트 추출"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de meta-prompting con corrección categórica","Refinamiento iterativo de las preguntas utilizando estructuras de Monad","Extracción de contexto de la historia utilizando funciones de Comonad"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de meta-prompting avec correction catégorielle","Affinement itératif des questions en utilisant des structures de Monad","Extraction de contexte de l''historique en utilisant des fonctions de Comonad"],"de":["Automatisierung der Generierung von Meta-Prompting mit kategorischer Korrektheit","Iteratives Verfeinern von Fragen unter Verwendung von Monad-Strukturen","Extraktion von Kontext aus der Historie unter Verwendung von Comonad-Funktionen"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de meta-prompt com correção categórica","Refinar prompts iterativamente usando estruturas de Monad","Extrair contexto do histórico usando funções de Comonad"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию мета-prompt с категориальной правильностью","Уточнять промпты итеративно, используя структуры Monad","Извлекать контекст из истории, используя функции Comonad"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي لإنشاء تحفيز الميتا مع الصحة الفئوية","تحسين التحفيزات تكراريا باستخدام هياكل المناد","استخراج السياق من السجل باستخدام دوال الكوموناد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of categorical foundations and meta-prompting concepts","Aligns with specific agent architectures like LangChain and Cursor"],"zh":["需要理解分类基础和元提示概念","仅适用于 LangChain 和 Cursor 等特定代理架构"],"ja":["カテゴリ的基礎とメタプロンプティングの概念を理解する必要","LangChain や Cursor などの特定のエージェントアーキテクチャにのみ適している"],"ko":["범주적 기초와 메타 프롬프트 개념을 이해해야 함","랭그체인이나 커서 같은 특정 에이전트 아키텍처에만 적합"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los conceptos categóricos y de meta-prompting","Se alinea con arquitecturas de agentes específicas como LangChain y Cursor"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des concepts catégoriels et de meta-prompting","S''aligne sur des architectures d''agents spécifiques comme LangChain et Cursor"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis von kategorischen Grundlagen und Meta-Prompting-Konzepten","Stimmt mit bestimmten Agentenarchitekturen wie LangChain und Cursor überein"],"pt":["Requer entendimento de fundamentos categóricos e conceitos de meta-prompting","Alinha-se com arquiteturas de agentes específicas como LangChain e Cursor"],"ru":["Требует понимания категориальных основ и концепций мета-prompting","Совместима с определенными архитектурами агентов, такими как LangChain и Cursor"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم الأسس الفئوية ومفاهيم تحفيز الميتا","يتوافق مع هندسة وكلاء محددة مثل LangChain و Cursor"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
