ntação de cluster após alterações significativas","Requisitos de recursos mínimos e recomendados","Suporte a Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop e Podman","Testes de implantação limpa e E2E"],"ru":["Развертывание кластера Kagenti Kind","Переустановка кластера после значительных изменений","Минимальные и рекомендуемые требования к ресурсам","Поддержка Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop и Podman","Тесты чистой установки и E2E"],"ar":["تثبيت كلاستر Kagenti Kind","إعادة التثبيت بعد التغييرات الكبيرة","متطلبات الموارد الدنيا والموصى بها","دعم Docker Desktop و Rancher Desktop و Podman","اختبارات التثبيت النظيف و E2E"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kagenti","部署","集群","Python","安装程序","本地开发","测试","生产环境"],"ja":["Kagenti","デプロイ","クラスター","Python","インストーラー","ローカル開発","テスト","プロダクション環境"],"ko":["Kagenti","배포","클러스터","Python","설치 프로그램","로컬 개발","테스트","프로덕션 환경"],"es":["despliegue de clúster","Kagenti Kind","instalador de Python","desarrollo local","pruebas de extremo a extremo","Docker Desktop","Rancher Desktop","Podman"],"fr":["déploiement de cluster","Kagenti Kind","installateur Python","développement local","tests de bout en bout","Docker Desktop","Rancher Desktop","Podman"],"de":["Cluster-Bereitstellung","Kagenti Kind","Python-Installateur","lokale Entwicklung","End-to-End-Tests","Docker Desktop","Rancher Desktop","Podman"],"pt":["kagenti deploy","cluster kagenti","implantação de cluster","reimplantação de cluster","desenvolvimento de software","testes de implantação"],"ru":["kagenti deploy","кластер kagenti","развертывание кластера","переустановка кластера","разработка программного обеспечения","тесты установки"],"ar":["kagenti deploy","كلاستر kagenti","تثبيت كلاستر","إعادة التثبيت","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبارات التثبيت"]}},"owner":"kagenti","repo":"kagenti","repoPath":"kagenti/kagenti","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kagenti:deploy","description":"Deploy or redeploy the Kagenti Kind cluster using the Python installer - quick redeploy, manual steps, and troubleshooting","bodyPreview":"# Deploy Cluster Skill\n\nThis skill guides you through deploying or redeploying the Kagenti Kind cluster using the Python installer.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Setting up new local development cluster\n- Full cluster redeploy after major changes\n- Cluster is corrupted or unstable\n- Testing clean deployment\n- Running E2E tests locally\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n**Minimum** (from CLAUDE.md):\n- 12GB RAM\n- 4 CPU cores\n- Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop, or Podman\n\n**Recommended for development**:\n- 16GB RAM\n-","body":"# Deploy Cluster Skill\n\nThis skill guides you through deploying or redeploying the Kagenti Kind cluster using the Python installer.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Setting up new local development cluster\n- Full cluster redeploy after major changes\n- Cluster is corrupted or unstable\n- Testing clean deployment\n- Running E2E tests locally\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n**Minimum** (from CLAUDE.md):\n- 12GB RAM\n- 4 CPU cores\n- Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop, or Podman\n\n**Recommended for development**:\n- 16GB RAM\n- 6 CPU cores\n- 50GB free disk space\n\n## Multiple Clusters\n\nYou can run multiple Kind clusters:\n- **agent-platform** - Created by kagenti-installer (default)\n- **kagenti-demo** - Your existing cluster\n- Each cluster runs independently with its own name\n\nCheck existing clusters:\n```bash\nkind get clusters\n```\n\n## Quick Redeploy (Full Installation)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Setup environment (first time only)\ncp kagenti/installer/app/.env_template kagenti/installer/app/.env\n# Edit .env with:\n# - GITHUB_USER=<your-github-username>\n# - GITHUB_TOKEN=<ghcr.io-token>\n# - OPENAI_API_KEY=<openai-key>\n# - AGENT_NAMESPACES=team1,team2\n\n# 2. Full redeploy (creates new cluster + installs everything)\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer\n\n# What it does (15-25 minutes):\n# ✓ Creates Kind cluster \"agent-platform\"\n# ✓ Installs registry (optional)\n# ✓ Installs Tekton Pipelines\n# ✓ Installs Cert-Manager\n# ✓ Installs Platform Operator\n# ✓ Installs Istio Ambient\n# ✓ Installs Gateway API\n# ✓ Installs SPIRE\n# ✓ Installs MCP Gateway\n# ✓ Installs Keycloak + PostgreSQL\n# ✓ Installs Addons (Prometheus, Kiali, Phoenix)\n# ✓ Installs UI\n# ✓ Installs ToolHive\n# ✓ Creates agent namespaces (team1, team2)\n```\n\n## Use Existing Cluster\n\n```bash\n# Install on already running Kind cluster\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --use-existing-cluster\n```\n\n## Cleanup and Fresh Install\n\n```bash\n# 1. Delete existing cluster\nkind delete cluster --name agent-platform\n\n# 2. Clean Docker images (optional)\ndocker system prune -a\n\n# 3. Fresh install\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer\n```\n\n## Selective Component Installation\n\nSkip components you don''t need for faster deployment:\n\n```bash\n# Minimal install (no UI, no observability, no auth)\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer \\\n  --skip-install ui \\\n  --skip-install addons \\\n  --skip-install keycloak \\\n  --skip-install spire\n\n# Skip specific components\nuv run kagenti-installer \\\n  --skip-install tekton \\\n  --skip-install operator \\\n  --skip-install gateway \\\n  --skip-install mcp_gateway\n\n# Install only core platform (for testing)\nuv run kagenti-installer \\\n  --skip-install addons \\\n  --skip-install ui \\\n  --skip-install keycloak \\\n  --skip-install agents\n```\n\n**Available components to skip**:\n- `registry` - Internal container registry\n- `tekton` - Tekton Pipelines (build system)\n- `cert_manager` - Certificate management\n- `operator` - Platform Operator (deprecated, being replaced by kagenti-operator)\n- `istio` - Service mesh\n- `gateway` - Kubernetes Gateway API\n- `spire` - Workload identity\n- `mcp_gateway` - MCP Gateway\n- `addons` - Observability (Prometheus, Kiali, Phoenix)\n- `ui` - Kagenti UI\n- `keycloak` - Authentication\n- `agents` - Demo agents\n- `metrics_server` - Metrics server\n- `inspector` - MCP inspector\n- `toolhive` - ToolHive operator\n\n## Deploy Weather Agents (Demo)\n\n```bash\n# After platform is installed\nkubectl apply -f kagenti/examples/components/\n```\n\nThis creates:\n- **weather-tool** in team1 namespace\n- **weather-service** in team1 namespace\n\n## Check Deployment Health\n\n### Quick Health Check\n\n```bash\n# Run the health check script (from CI)\nchmod +x .github/scripts/verify_deployment.sh\n.github/scripts/verify_deployment.sh\n\n# What it checks:\n# ✓ Resource usage (RAM, disk, CPU, containers)\n# ✓ Deployment status (weather-tool, weather-service, keycloak, operator)\n# ✓ Pod health summary (total, running, pending, failed, crashloop)\n# ✓ Failed pod details (events, error logs)\n```\n\n### Manual Health Checks\n\n```bash\n# All pods\nkubectl get pods -A\n\n# Failed pods only\nkubectl get pods -A --field-selector=status.phase!=Running,status.phase!=Succeeded\n\n# Specific namespace\nkubectl get pods -n team1\nkubectl get pods -n keycloak\nkubectl get pods -n kagenti-system\n\n# Deployments\nkubectl get deployments -A\n\n# Services\nkubectl get svc -A\n```\n\n## Run E2E Tests Locally\n\nAfter platform is deployed:\n\n```bash\ncd kagenti\n\n# Install test dependencies\nuv pip install -r tests/requirements.txt\n\n# Run all deployment health tests\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v\n\n# Run only critical tests\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v --only-critical\n\n# Run specific test\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py::TestWeatherToolDeployment::test_weather_tool_deployment_ready -v\n\n# Exclude Keycloak tests\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v --exclude-app=keycloak\n\n# Increase timeout\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v --app-timeout=600\n```\n\n## Run Full CI Workflow Locally\n\nSimulate what runs in CI:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install platform\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --silent\n\n# 2. Deploy weather agents\ncd ../..\nkubectl apply -f kagenti/examples/components/\n\n# 3. Wait for deployments\nkubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=300s deployment/weather-tool -n team1\nkubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=300s deployment/weather-service -n team1\n\n# 4. Run health check\nchmod +x .github/scripts/verify_deployment.sh\n.github/scripts/verify_deployment.sh\n\n# 5. Run E2E tests\ncd kagenti\nuv pip install -r tests/requirements.txt\nuv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v \\\n  --timeout=300 \\\n  --tb=short\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting Deployment\n\n### Issue: Installer Timeout or Slow\n\n```bash\n# Check Docker resource allocation\ndocker info | grep -E \"CPUs|Total Memory\"\n\n# Increase timeout (images can be slow to pull)\n# The installer will retry - just re-run:\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --use-existing-cluster\n```\n\n### Issue: \"Error loading config file\" or kubectl errors\n\n```bash\n# Check kubeconfig\nkubectl config current-context\n\n# Should show: kind-agent-platform\n\n# If not, set context\nkubectl config use-context kind-agent-platform\n```\n\n### Issue: Pods stuck in ImagePullBackOff\n\n```bash\n# Check if images are available in Kind\ndocker exec agent-platform-control-plane crictl images\n\n# Reload images (for custom builds)\nkind load docker-image <image-name> --name agent-platform\n\n# Check pod description for error\nkubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n <namespace>\n```\n\n### Issue: Keycloak Connection Issues\n\n```bash\n# Restart Keycloak\nkubectl delete -n keycloak -f kagenti/installer/app/resources/keycloak.yaml\nkubectl apply -n keycloak -f kagenti/installer/app/resources/keycloak.yaml\n\n# Restart Istio ztunnel\nkubectl rollout restart daemonset -n istio-system ztunnel\n\n# Restart Gateway\nkubectl rollout restart -n kagenti-system deployment http-istio\n```\n\n### Issue: Need to Update Secrets\n\n```bash\n# Update GitHub token\nkubectl -n <namespace> delete secret github-token-secret\n\n# Re-run installer to recreate secrets\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --use-existing-cluster\n```\n\n### Issue: Blank UI on macOS\n\n```bash\n# Disable Screen Time Content & Privacy Restrictions\n# System Settings > Screen Time > Content & Privacy\n```\n\n### Issue: GitHub Token Errors\n\n```bash\n# Ensure token has correct scopes:\n# - repo:all\n# - write:packages\n# - read:packages\n\n# Clear cached credentials\ndocker logout ghcr.io\n```\n\n## Access Platform Services\n\nAfter deployment, access these services:\n\n```bash\n# Kagenti UI\nopen http://kagenti-ui.localtest.me:8080\n\n# Keycloak Admin Console\nopen http://keycloak.localtest.me:8080\n# Username: admin\n# Password: (from Keycloak secret)\nkubectl get secret -n keycloak keycloak-initial-admin -o jsonpath=''{.data.password}'' | base64 -d\n\n# Prometheus (if addons installed)\nkubectl port-forward -n observability svc/prometheus 9090:9090\nopen http://localhost:9090\n\n# Grafana (if addons installed)\nkubectl port-forward -n observability svc/grafana 3000:3000\nopen http://localhost:3000\n\n# Kiali (if addons installed)\nkubectl port-forward -n kiali svc/kiali 20001:20001\nopen http://localhost:20001\n```\n\n## Platform Configuration\n\n### Environment Variables (.env file)\n\nRequired in `kagenti/installer/app/.env`:\n\n```bash\n# GitHub access for ghcr.io\nGITHUB_USER=your-username\nGITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx  # Classic token with repo:all, write:packages, read:packages\n\n# OpenAI API (for agents)\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx\n\n# Agent namespaces\nAGENT_NAMESPACES=team1,team2\n\n# Optional: Slack (for Slack tool demo)\nSLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-xxx\n```\n\n### Cluster Configuration\n\nEdit `kagenti/installer/app/config.py`:\n\n```python\nCLUSTER_NAME = \"agent-platform\"  # Kind cluster name\nDOMAIN_NAME = \"localtest.me\"     # Domain for services\nCONTAINER_ENGINE = \"docker\"      # or \"podman\"\n```\n\n## Manual Step-by-Step Deployment (Advanced)\n\nFor debugging or understanding the installer:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create Kind cluster manually\ncat <<EOF | kind create cluster --name agent-platform --config=-\nkind: Cluster\napiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4\nnodes:\n- role: control-plane\n  extraPortMappings:\n  - containerPort: 30080\n    hostPort: 8080\n  - containerPort: 30443\n    hostPort: 9443\nEOF\n\n# 2. Set kubeconfig context\nkubectl config use-context kind-agent-platform\n\n# 3. Install components one by one\ncd kagenti/installer\n\n# Install Tekton\nkubectl apply -f https://storage.googleapis.com/tekton-releases/pipeline/previous/v0.66.0/release.yaml\n\n# Install Cert-Manager\nkubectl apply -f https://github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager/releases/download/v1.16.2/cert-manager.yaml\n\n# ... (see installer code for full sequence)\n```\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **k8s:health**: Check comprehensive platform health\n- **k8s:logs**: Query logs for debugging\n- **k8s:pods**: Debug pod issues\n\n## Pro Tips\n\n1. **Use --use-existing-cluster**: Faster reinstalls without recreating cluster\n2. **Skip components**: Use --skip-install for faster iteration\n3. **Multiple clusters**: Use different cluster names for parallel testing\n4. **Resource allocation**: Ensure Docker/Podman has enough RAM (16GB recommended)\n5. **Cache images**: Pulled images are cached - subsequent installs are faster\n6. **Silent mode**: Use --silent to skip interactive prompts\n7. **Check logs**: If installer fails, check pod logs in kagenti-system namespace\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Daily Development\n```bash\n# Use existing cluster, skip slow components\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --use-existing-cluster \\\n  --skip-install addons \\\n  --skip-install keycloak\n```\n\n### Full Test Before PR\n```bash\n# Fresh cluster, all components, run tests\nkind delete cluster --name agent-platform\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer --silent\nkubectl apply -f kagenti/examples/components/\n.github/scripts/verify_deployment.sh\ncd kagenti && uv run pytest tests/e2e/test_deployment_health.py -v\n```\n\n### Quick Agent Testing\n```bash\n# Minimal platform, just enough for agents\ncd kagenti/installer\nuv run kagenti-installer \\\n  --skip-install addons \\\n  --skip-install ui \\\n  --skip-install keycloak\nkubectl apply -f kagenti/examples/components/\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:07:58.820Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Agents needing automated Kagenti Kind cluster deployment and management using Python","zh":"非常适合需要使用Python自动化部署和管理Kagenti Kind集群的云代理","ja":"Pythonを使用してKagenti Kindクラスターを自動化してデプロイおよび管理する必要があるクラウドエージェントに最適","ko":"파이썬을 사용하여 Kagenti Kind 클러스터를 자동화하여 배포 및 관리해야 하는 클라우드 에이전트에게 최적","es":"Perfecto para agentes de nube que necesitan despliegue y administración automáticos del clúster Kagenti Kind mediante Python","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud nécessitant un déploiement et une gestion automatisés du cluster Kagenti Kind à l''aide de Python","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Agents, die ein automatisiertes Bereitstellen und Verwalten des Kagenti-Kind-Clusters mit Python benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Nuvem que precisam de implantação e gerenciamento automatizados do cluster Kagenti Kind usando Python","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, которым требуется автоматизированная развертка и управление кластером Kagenti Kind с использованием Python","ar":"مثالي للعميل السحابي الذي يحتاج إلى تثبيت وتشغيل تلقائي لclusetir Kagenti Kind باستخدام Python"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deploy or redeploy the Kagenti Kind cluster using Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop, or Podman, ensuring a stable and efficient development environment with minimum 12GB RAM and 4 CPU cores","zh":"赋予代理部署或重新部署Kagenti Kind集群的能力，使用Docker Desktop、Rancher Desktop或Podman，确保具有最低12GB RAM和4 CPU核心的稳定且高效的开发环境","ja":"Docker Desktop、Rancher Desktop、またはPodmanを使用して、Kagenti Kindクラスターをデプロイまたは再デプロイするエージェントの能力を提供し、最低12GB RAMと4 CPUコアのある安定した開発環境を提供する","ko":"Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop 또는 Podman을 사용하여 Kagenti Kind 클러스터를 배포하거나 재배포할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하여 최소 12GB RAM과 4 CPU 코어가 있는 안정적이고 효율적인 개발 환경을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desplegar o volver a desplegar el clúster Kagenti Kind mediante Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop o Podman, lo que garantiza un entorno de desarrollo estable y eficiente con un mínimo de 12 GB de RAM y 4 núcleos de CPU","fr":"Permet aux agents de déployer ou de rédéployer le cluster Kagenti Kind à l''aide de Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop ou Podman, garantissant ainsi un environnement de développement stable et efficace avec un minimum de 12 Go de RAM et 4 cœurs de processeur","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, den Kagenti-Kind-Cluster mithilfe von Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop oder Podman zu bereitstellen oder neu bereitzustellen, was einen stabilen und effizienten Entwicklungsumgebung mit mindestens 12 GB RAM und 4 CPU-Kernen gewährleistet","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implantarem ou reimplantarem o cluster Kagenti Kind usando Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop ou Podman, garantindo um ambiente de desenvolvimento estável e eficiente com no mínimo 12GB de RAM e 4 núcleos de CPU","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью развертки или повторной развертки кластера Kagenti Kind с использованием Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop или Podman, обеспечивая стабильную и эффективную среду разработки с минимальными 12ГБ ОЗУ и 4 ядрами CPU","ar":"يمكّن العميل من تثبيت إعادة تثبيت cluster Kagenti Kind باستخدام Docker Desktop أو Rancher Desktop أو Podman، وضمان بيئة تطوير مستقرة وفعالة مع الحد الأدنى 12 غيغابايت من ذاكرة الوصول العشوائي و 4 نوى معالج"},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying new local development clusters","Redeploying full clusters after major changes","Testing clean deployments","Running E2E tests locally"],"zh":["部署新的本地开发集群","在进行重大更改后重新部署完整集群","测试干净的部署","在本地运行端到端测试"],"ja":["新しいローカル開発クラスターをデプロイする","大きな変更を行った後にフルクラスターを再デプロイする","クリーンなデプロイをテストする","ローカルでエンドツーエンドテストを実行する"],"ko":["새로운 로컬 개발 클러스터 배포","주요 변경 후 전체 클러스터 재배포","깨끗한 배포 테스트","로컬에서 종단 간 테스트 실행"],"es":["Desplegar nuevos clústeres de desarrollo locales","Volver a desplegar clústeres completos después de cambios importantes","Probar despliegues limpios","Ejecutar pruebas E2E de forma local"],"fr":["Déployer de nouveaux clusters de développement locaux","Redéployer des clusters complets après des modifications majeures","Tester des déploiements propres","Exécuter des tests E2E en local"],"de":["Bereitstellen neuer lokaler Entwicklungskluster","Neu bereitstellen von vollständigen Klustern nach größeren Änderungen","Testen von sauberen Bereitstellungen","Ausführen von E2E-Tests lokal"],"pt":["Implantação de novos clusters de desenvolvimento local","Reimplantação de clusters completos após alterações significativas","Testes de implantação limpa","Execução de testes de ponta a ponta localmente"],"ru":["Развертка новых локальных кластеров разработки","Повторная развертка полных кластеров после значительных изменений","Тестирование чистой развертки","Запуск тестов от конца до конца локально"],"ar":["تثبيت مجاميع تطوير محلية جديدة","إعادة تثبيت المجاميع الكاملة بعد التغييرات الرئيسية","اختبارات التثبيت النظيف","تشغيل اختبارات النهاية إلى النهاية محليًا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires minimum 12GB RAM and 4 CPU cores","Needs Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop, or Podman installed"],"zh":["需要最低12GB RAM和4 CPU核心","需要安装Docker Desktop、Rancher Desktop或Podman"],"ja":["最低12GB RAMと4 CPUコアが必要","Docker Desktop、Rancher Desktop、またはPodmanをインストールする必要がある"],"ko":["최소 12GB RAM과 4 CPU 코어가 필요","Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop 또는 Podman을 설치해야 함"],"es":["Requiere un mínimo de 12 GB de RAM y 4 núcleos de CPU","Necesita tener instalado Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop o Podman"],"fr":["Nécessite un minimum de 12 Go de RAM et 4 cœurs de processeur","Nécessite d''avoir Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop ou Podman installé"],"de":["Benötigt mindestens 12 GB RAM und 4 CPU-Kerne","Benötigt die Installation von Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop oder Podman"],"pt":["Exige no mínimo 12GB de RAM e 4 núcleos de CPU","Necessita de Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop ou Podman instalado"],"ru":["Требует минимум 12ГБ ОЗУ и 4 ядра CPU","Требует установленного Docker Desktop, Rancher Desktop или Podman"],"ar":["يتطلب الحد الأدنى 12 غيغابايت من ذاكرة الوصول العشوائي و 4 نوى معالج","يتطلب تثبيت Docker Desktop أو Rancher Desktop أو Podman"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Screenly/Playground/create-an-edge-app', 'community', 'Screenly', 'Playground', 'Screenly/Playground', 'create-an-edge-app', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:03.185Z', NULL, '{"id":"Screenly/Playground/create-an-edge-app","name":"create-an-edge-app","description":{"zh":"创建边缘应用涉及设置新目录、遵循命名约定和设计指南。开发者可以使用 Screenly 和其 API 来构建强大的 Edge 应用","ja":"Edge アプリの作成には、新しいディレクトリの設定、命名規則の遵守、設計ガイドラインの使用が含まれます。開発者は、Screenly とその API を使用して強力な Edge アプリを構築できます","ko":"Edge 애플리케이션을 생성하는 것은 새로운 디렉토리를 설정하고命명 규칙 및 디자인 가이드를 따르는 것을 포함합니다. 개발자는 Screenly 및 API를 사용하여 강력한 Edge 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있습니다","es":"Screenly te permite crear aplicaciones de Edge personalizadas con su API. Sigue nuestros ejemplos y documentación para empezar.","fr":"Screenly vous permet de créer des applications Edge personnalisées avec son API. Suivez nos exemples et documentation pour commencer.","de":"Screenly ermöglicht es Ihnen, benutzerdefinierte Edge-Apps mit seiner API zu erstellen. Folgen Sie unseren Beispielen und Dokumentation, um loszulegen.","pt":"Criar um aplicativo de borda personalizado com Screenly e sua API. Acesse designs e especificações com o servidor Figma MCP.","ru":"Создание индивидуального приложения Edge с помощью Screenly и его API. Доступ к дизайнам и спецификациям с помощью сервера Figma MCP.","ar":"إنشاء تطبيق حافة مخصص مع Screenly وواجهة برمجة التطبيقات. الوصول إلى التصاميم والمواصفات مع خادم Figma MCP.","en":"Various examples of how developers can use Screenly and Screenly''s API"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"创建边缘应用：Screenly 和 API 示例","ja":"Edge アプリの作成：Screenly と API の例","ko":"Edge 애플리케이션 생성: Screenly 및 API 예시","es":"Crea una aplicación de Edge con Screenly","fr":"Créer une application Edge avec Screenly","de":"Erstellen Sie eine Edge-App mit Screenly","pt":"Crie um Aplicativo de Borda com Screenly","ru":"Создайте приложение Edge с Screenly","ar":"إنشاء تطبيق حافة مع Screenly","en":"create-an-edge-app"},"description":{"zh":"创建边缘应用涉及设置新目录、遵循命名约定和设计指南。开发者可以使用 Screenly 和其 API 来构建强大的 Edge 应用","ja":"Edge アプリの作成には、新しいディレクトリの設定、命名規則の遵守、設計ガイドラインの使用が含まれます。開発者は、Screenly とその API を使用して強力な Edge アプリを構築できます","ko":"Edge 애플리케이션을 생성하는 것은 새로운 디렉토리를 설정하고命명 규칙 및 디자인 가이드를 따르는 것을 포함합니다. 개발자는 Screenly 및 API를 사용하여 강력한 Edge 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있습니다","es":"Screenly te permite crear aplicaciones de Edge personalizadas con su API. Sigue nuestros ejemplos y documentación para empezar.","fr":"Screenly vous permet de créer des applications Edge personnalisées avec son API. Suivez nos exemples et documentation pour commencer.","de":"Screenly ermöglicht es Ihnen, benutzerdefinierte Edge-Apps mit seiner API zu erstellen. Folgen Sie unseren Beispielen und Dokumentation, um loszulegen.","pt":"Criar um aplicativo de borda personalizado com Screenly e sua API. Acesse designs e especificações com o servidor Figma MCP.","ru":"Создание индивидуального приложения Edge с помощью Screenly и его API. Доступ к дизайнам и спецификациям с помощью сервера Figma MCP.","ar":"إنشاء تطبيق حافة مخصص مع Screenly وواجهة برمجة التطبيقات. الوصول إلى التصاميم والمواصفات مع خادم Figma MCP.","en":"Various examples of how developers can use Screenly and Screenly''s API"},"definition":{"en":"Various examples of how developers can use Screenly and Screenly''s API"},"features":{"zh":["使用 Screenly 和其 API 创建边缘应用","遵循命名约定和设计指南","设置 Figma MCP 服务器以访问设计规范","提取设计令牌以实现一致的 UI","构建强大的 Edge 应用以满足特定需求"],"ja":["Screenly とその API を使用して Edge アプリを作成する","命名規則と設計ガイドラインの遵守","Figma MCP サーバーの設定による設計仕様へのアクセス","設計トークンの抽出による一貫した UI の実現","特定のニーズに応える強力な Edge アプリの構築"],"ko":["Screenly 및 API를 사용하여 Edge 애플리케이션을 생성","命명 규칙 및 디자인 가이드를 따름","Figma MCP 서버 설정을 통한 디자인 사양 액세스","디자인 토큰 추출을 통한 일관된 UI 구현","특정 요구 사항을 충족하는 강력한 Edge 애플리케이션 구축"],"es":["Crea aplicaciones de Edge personalizadas","Utiliza la API de Screenly para acceder a funciones avanzadas","Consulta diseños de Figma antes de empezar","Accede a tokens de diseño como colores y espaciado","Utiliza el servidor MCP de Figma para obtener especificaciones de diseño","Implementa aplicaciones de Edge con kebab-case naming convention"],"fr":["Créez des applications Edge personnalisées","Utilisez l''API Screenly pour accéder à des fonctions avancées","Consultez les conceptions Figma avant de commencer","Accédez à des jetons de conception tels que les couleurs et l''espacement","Utilisez le serveur MCP Figma pour obtenir des spécifications de conception","Mettez en œuvre des applications Edge avec la convention d''appellation kebab-case"],"de":["Erstellen Sie benutzerdefinierte Edge-Apps","Verwenden Sie die Screenly-API, um auf erweiterte Funktionen zuzugreifen","Überprüfen Sie Figma-Entwürfe, bevor Sie beginnen","Greifen Sie auf Design-Tokens wie Farben und Abstände zu","Verwenden Sie den Figma-MCP-Server, um Design-Spezifikationen zu erhalten","Implementieren Sie Edge-Apps mit kebab-case-Benennungskonvention"],"pt":["Crie aplicativos de borda personalizados com Screenly","Acesse designs e especificações com o servidor Figma MCP","Use a API de Screenly para desenvolver funcionalidades personalizadas","Implemente design tokens, como cores e espaçamento","Desenvolva aplicativos de borda escaláveis e seguros"],"ru":["Создайте индивидуальные приложения Edge с помощью Screenly","Получите доступ к дизайнам и спецификациям с помощью сервера Figma MCP","Используйте API Screenly для разработки индивидуальных функций","Реализуйте дизайн-токены, такие как цвета и интервалы","Разработайте масштабируемые и безопасные приложения Edge"],"ar":["إنشاء تطبيقات حافة مخصصة مع Screenly","الوصول إلى التصاميم والمواصفات مع خادم Figma MCP","استخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Screenly لتعزيز الوظائف المخصصة","تنفيذ رموز التصميم، مثل الألوان والفضاء","تطوير تطبيقات حافة قابلة للتحجيم وأمنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["边缘应用","Screenly","API","Edge 应用","设计指南","Figma MCP","设计令牌","UI 一致性","网络边缘"],"ja":["Edge アプリ","Screenly","API","エッジ アプリ","設計ガイドライン","Figma MCP","設計トークン","UI 一貫性","ネットワーク エッジ"],"ko":["Edge 애플리케이션","Screenly","API","에지 애플리케이션","디자인 가이드","피그마 MCP","디자인 토큰","UI 일관성","네트워크 에지"],"es":["aplicaciones de Edge","Screenly","API de Screenly","desarrollo de aplicaciones","Figma","diseño de aplicaciones","tokens de diseño","servidor MCP de Figma","kebab-case"],"fr":["applications Edge","Screenly","API Screenly","développement d''applications","Figma","conception d''applications","jetons de conception","serveur MCP Figma","kebab-case"],"de":["Edge-Apps","Screenly","Screenly-API","App-Entwicklung","Figma","App-Design","Design-Tokens","Figma-MCP-Server","kebab-case"],"pt":["aplicativo de borda","Screenly","API","desenvolvimento de software","design de interface","Figma MCP","design tokens","escalabilidade","segurança"],"ru":["приложение Edge","Screenly","API","разработка программного обеспечения","дизайн интерфейса","Figma MCP","дизайн-токены","масштабируемость","безопасность"],"ar":["تطبيق حافة","Screenly","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تطوير البرمجيات","تصميم الواجهة","Figma MCP","رموز التصميم","القدرة على التحجيم","الأمان"]}},"owner":"Screenly","repo":"Playground","repoPath":"Screenly/Playground","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-an-edge-app","description":"The recommended way to create an Edge App","bodyPreview":"# Creating an Edge App\n\n## When Creating an Edge App\n\n- Create a new directory for a new Edge App inside the `edge-apps/` directory.\n  - The directory name should follow the `kebab-case` naming convention.\n- **Consult Figma designs** before starting implementation.\n  - Ensure the [Figma MCP server](https://mcp.figma.com/mcp) is set up in Claude Code.\n  - Use the Figma MCP server to access design specifications, mockups, and UI requirements.\n  - Extract design tokens such as colors, spacing, typo","body":"# Creating an Edge App\n\n## When Creating an Edge App\n\n- Create a new directory for a new Edge App inside the `edge-apps/` directory.\n  - The directory name should follow the `kebab-case` naming convention.\n- **Consult Figma designs** before starting implementation.\n  - Ensure the [Figma MCP server](https://mcp.figma.com/mcp) is set up in Claude Code.\n  - Use the Figma MCP server to access design specifications, mockups, and UI requirements.\n  - Extract design tokens such as colors, spacing, typography, and component specifications from Figma.\n  - Ensure the implementation matches the approved designs in Figma before proceeding with development.\n\n## Directory Structure\n\nThe new Edge App directory structure should closely resemble that of the following Edge Apps:\n\n- QR Code (`edge-apps/qr-code/`)\n- Menu Board (`edge-apps/menu-board/`)\n- Grafana (`edge-apps/grafana/`)\n- CAP Alerting (`edge-apps/cap-alerting/`)\n\nThese Edge Apps heavily rely on the Edge Apps library, which lives inside the `edge-apps/edge-apps-library/` directory.\n\n- Most of the scripts inside the `package.json` of each of these apps execute the `edge-apps-scripts` command.\n- All of these apps depend on the `@screenly/edge-apps` library, which maps to `workspace:../edge-apps-library`.\n- `edge-apps/[new-edge-app]/src/main.ts` is a required file.\n  - Running `bun run build` inside `edge-apps/[new-edge-app]` will run `edge-apps-scripts build`, which is very opinionated.\n\nRefer to `edge-apps/qr-code/` as a complete working template to understand the full directory structure and configuration.\n\n- While it still uses the `@screenly/edge-apps` library, it features a simpler implementation with a lower code footprint compared to the other aforementioned Edge Apps, making it an excellent starting point for new projects.\n- The library abstracts much of the complexity, allowing developers to focus on core functionality with minimal boilerplate.\n\n### About the Manifest Files\n\nThe new app should have the following manifest files:\n\n- `screenly.yml`\n- `screenly_qc.yml`\n\nSee `edge-apps/qr-code/screenly.yml` for a working example. More information about the manifest files can be found in the [Edge Apps documentation in the `Screenly/cli` repository](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Screenly/cli/refs/heads/master/docs/EdgeApps.md).\n\nWhen creating the manifest files, ensure to:\n\n- Omit the `id` field, as it will be added later when the new app gets deployed.\n\n### About `index.html`\n\nThe `index.html` file should follow these best practices:\n- Organize HTML code into templates and Web Components as the app grows in complexity.\n- Use HTML content templates first for simpler structures.\n- Consider using Web Components for more complex UI components that require encapsulation and reusability.\n\n### About `README.md`\n\n- Include instructions on how to create, build, test, format, lint, and deploy the app.\n- Do not add details like the directory structure, as the code frequently changes."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:03.185Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing to integrate Screenly''s API for edge app development.","zh":"非常适合需要集成Screenly API进行边缘应用开发的全栈代理。","ja":"ScreenlyのAPIをエッジアプリ開発に統合する必要があるフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Screenly API를 에지 애플리케이션 개발에 통합해야 하는 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan integrar la API de Screenly para el desarrollo de aplicaciones de edge.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin d''intégrer l''API Screenly pour le développement d''applications de edge.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die die Screenly-API für die Entwicklung von Edge-Apps integrieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam integrar a API da Screenly para desenvolvimento de aplicativos de borda.","ru":"Идеально подходит для полнофункциональных агентов, которым необходимо интегрировать API Screenly для разработки приложений на уровне края.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الكاملون الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Screenly لتطوير تطبيقات الحافة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create customized edge apps using Screenly''s API, leveraging Figma designs and kebab-case naming conventions for seamless implementation, and extracting design tokens such as colors, spacing, and typography for consistent UI.","zh":"赋予代理创建使用Screenly API的自定义边缘应用的能力，利用Figma设计和短横线命名约定实现无缝集成，并提取设计令牌（如颜色、间距和排版）以实现一致的UI。","ja":"ScreenlyのAPIを使用してカスタムエッジアプリを作成するエージェントをEmpowerし、Figmaデザインとケバブケース命名規約を使用して無駄な実装を実現し、カラー、スペーシング、タイポグラフィーなどのデザイントークンを抽出してUIの一貫性を保ちます。","ko":"에이전트가 Screenly API를 사용하여 맞춤형 에지 애플리케이션을 만들 수 있도록 하며, Figma 디자인과 케밥 케이스命名 규칙을 사용하여 무шов한 구현을 가능하게 하고, 색상, 간격, 타이포그래피 등의 디자인 토큰을 추출하여 일관된 UI를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear aplicaciones de edge personalizadas utilizando la API de Screenly, aprovechando diseños de Figma y convenciones de nomenclatura en kebab-case para una implementación sin problemas, y extrayendo tokens de diseño como colores, espaciado y tipografía para una interfaz de usuario coherente.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications de edge personnalisées en utilisant l''API Screenly, en exploitant les conceptions Figma et les conventions de nommage en kebab-case pour une mise en œuvre sans problème, et en extrayant des jetons de conception tels que les couleurs, l''espacement et la typographie pour une interface utilisateur cohérente.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, benutzerdefinierte Edge-Apps mit der Screenly-API zu erstellen, indem sie Figma-Entwürfe und Kebab-Case-Benennungskonventionen für eine reibungslose Implementierung nutzen und Design-Tokens wie Farben, Abstände und Typografie für eine konsistente Benutzeroberfläche extrahieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar aplicativos de borda personalizados usando a API da Screenly, aproveitando projetos do Figma e convenções de nomenclatura em kebab-case para implementação sem problemas, e extrair tokens de design, como cores, espaçamento e tipografia, para consistência da IU.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать индивидуальные приложения на уровне края с использованием API Screenly, используя проекты Figma и соглашения об именах в стиле kebab-case для беспроблемной реализации, и извлекая токены дизайна, такие как цвета, интервалы и типографику, для согласованности пользовательского интерфейса.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء تطبيقات حافة مخصصة باستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Screenly، واستخدام تصاميم Figma وأساليب التسمية kebab-case للتطبيق السلس، واستخراج رموز التصميم مثل الألوان والتباعد والطباعة الحروفية لاتساق واجهة المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new edge apps with Screenly''s API","Consulting Figma designs for implementation guidance","Extracting design tokens for UI consistency"],"zh":["使用Screenly API创建新的边缘应用","咨询Figma设计以获取实现指导","提取设计令牌以实现UI一致性"],"ja":["ScreenlyのAPIを使用して新しいエッジアプリを作成する","Figmaデザインを参照して実装ガイダンスを取得する","デザイントークンを抽出してUIの一貫性を保つ"],"ko":["Screenly API를 사용하여 새로운 에지 애플리케이션을 생성하는こと","구현 가이드를 얻기 위해 Figma 디자인을 참조하는こと","UI 일관성을 유지하기 위해 디자인 토큰을 추출하는こと"],"es":["Crear nuevas aplicaciones de edge con la API de Screenly","Consultar diseños de Figma para orientación sobre la implementación","Extraer tokens de diseño para la coherencia de la interfaz de usuario"],"fr":["Créer de nouvelles applications de edge avec l''API Screenly","Consulter les conceptions Figma pour obtenir des conseils sur la mise en œuvre","Extraire des jetons de conception pour la cohérence de l''interface utilisateur"],"de":["Erstellen von neuen Edge-Apps mit der Screenly-API","Figma-Entwürfe zur Implementierungsanleitung konsultieren","Design-Tokens für die Konsistenz der Benutzeroberfläche extrahieren"],"pt":["Criar novos aplicativos de borda com a API da Screenly","Consultar projetos do Figma para orientação de implementação","Extrair tokens de design para consistência da IU"],"ru":["Создание новых приложений на уровне края с использованием API Screenly","Консультирование по проектам Figma для получения рекомендаций по реализации","Извлечение токенов дизайна для согласованности пользовательского интерфейса"],"ar":["إنشاء تطبيقات حافة جديدة باستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Screenly","استشارة تصاميم Figma لإرشادات التنفيذ","استخراج رموز التصميم لاتساق واجهة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Screenly API access","Figma MCP server setup necessary","Directory naming convention must follow kebab-case"],"zh":["需要Screenly API访问权限","Figma MCP服务器设置是必要的","目录命名约定必须遵循短横线命名规则"],"ja":["Screenly APIへのアクセス権が必要","Figma MCPサーバー設定が必要","ディレクトリ命名規約はケバブケース命名規則に従わなければならない"],"ko":["Screenly API 액세스 권한이 필요합니다.","Figma MCP 서버 설정이 필요합니다.","디렉토리命名 규칙은 케밥 케이스命名 규칙을 따라야 합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de Screenly","Configuración del servidor MCP de Figma necesaria","La convención de nomenclatura de directorios debe seguir kebab-case"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API Screenly","Configuration du serveur MCP Figma nécessaire","La convention de nommage de répertoire doit suivre kebab-case"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Screenly-API","Figma-MCP-Server-Einrichtung erforderlich","Die Namenskonvention für Verzeichnisse muss Kebab-Case folgen"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API da Screenly","Configuração do servidor Figma MCP necessária","Convenção de nomenclatura de diretório deve seguir kebab-case"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к API Screenly","Необходимо настроить сервер Figma MCP","Соглашение об именах каталогов должно следовать стилю kebab-case"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Screenly","يجب إعداد خادم Figma MCP","يجب اتباع اتفاقية تسمية الدليل بنمط kebab-case"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop/gates', 'community', 'alfredolopez80', 'multi-agent-ralph-loop', 'alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop', 'gates', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z', '2026-02-18T03:07:55.207Z', NULL, '{"id":"alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop/gates","name":"gates","description":{"zh":"Gates AI 代理技能提供了多语言质量验证和模型无关的 AI 编排，支持 9 种编程语言和 TLDR 辅助分析","ja":"Gates AI エージェントスキルは、マルチ言語の品質検証とモデル非依存の AI オーケストレーションを提供します。9 種類のプログラミング言語と TLDR アシスト分析をサポートしています","ko":"Gates AI 에이전트 스킬은 멀티 언어 품질 검증과 모델 비의존적인 AI 오케스트레이션을 제공합니다. 9종류의 프로그래밍 언어와 TLDR 보조 분석을 지원합니다","es":"Gates es una herramienta de validación de calidad que ofrece análisis asistido por TLDR y soporte para 9 lenguajes de programación, diseñada para desarrolladores","fr":"Gates est un outil de validation de la qualité qui propose une analyse assistée par TLDR et un support pour 9 langages de programmation, conçu pour les développeurs","de":"Gates ist ein Tool für die Qualitätssicherung, das eine TLDR-unterstützte Analyse und Unterstützung für 9 Programmiersprachen bietet, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"Gates é uma tecnologia de orquestração de IA multi-agente que fornece validação de qualidade em 9 linguagens de programação com análise assistida por TLDR","ru":"Gates — это технология многоагентной оркестрации ИИ, обеспечивающая проверку качества на 9 языках программирования с помощью анализа, поддерживаемого TLDR","ar":"بوابات هي تقنية تنسيق متعدد العوامل للذكاء الاصطناعي توفر التحقق من الجودة في 9 لغات برمجة مع التحليل بمساعدة TLDR","en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Gates AI 代理技能 - 多代理 AI 编排","ja":"Gates AI エージェントスキル - マルチエージェント AI オーケストレーション","ko":"Gates AI 에이전트 스킬 - 멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션","es":"Gates: Validación de Calidad para Desarrolladores","fr":"Gates: Validation de la Qualité pour les Développeurs","de":"Gates: Qualitätssicherung für Entwickler","pt":"Gates: Orquestração de IA Multi-Agente com Validação de Q...","ru":"Gates: Многоагентная Оркестрация ИИ с Проверкой Качества","ar":"بوابات: تنسيق متعدد العوامل للذكاء الاصطناعي مع التحقق من...","en":"gates"},"description":{"zh":"Gates AI 代理技能提供了多语言质量验证和模型无关的 AI 编排，支持 9 种编程语言和 TLDR 辅助分析","ja":"Gates AI エージェントスキルは、マルチ言語の品質検証とモデル非依存の AI オーケストレーションを提供します。9 種類のプログラミング言語と TLDR アシスト分析をサポートしています","ko":"Gates AI 에이전트 스킬은 멀티 언어 품질 검증과 모델 비의존적인 AI 오케스트레이션을 제공합니다. 9종류의 프로그래밍 언어와 TLDR 보조 분석을 지원합니다","es":"Gates es una herramienta de validación de calidad que ofrece análisis asistido por TLDR y soporte para 9 lenguajes de programación, diseñada para desarrollad...","fr":"Gates est un outil de validation de la qualité qui propose une analyse assistée par TLDR et un support pour 9 langages de programmation, conçu pour les dével...","de":"Gates ist ein Tool für die Qualitätssicherung, das eine TLDR-unterstützte Analyse und Unterstützung für 9 Programmiersprachen bietet, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"Gates é uma tecnologia de orquestração de IA multi-agente que fornece validação de qualidade em 9 linguagens de programação com análise assistida por TLDR","ru":"Gates — это технология многоагентной оркестрации ИИ, обеспечивающая проверку качества на 9 языках программирования с помощью анализа, поддерживаемого TLDR","ar":"بوابات هي تقنية تنسيق متعدد العوامل للذكاء الاصطناعي توفر التحقق من الجودة في 9 لغات برمجة مع التحليل بمساعدة TLDR","en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"definition":{"en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"features":{"zh":["多语言质量验证","模型无关的 AI 编排","支持 9 种编程语言","TLDR 辅助分析","模型配置通过环境变量","支持 GLM-5、Claude 等模型"],"ja":["マルチ言語の品質検証","モデル非依存の AI オーケストレーション","9 種類のプログラミング言語をサポート","TLDR アシスト分析","モデル設定を環境変数で行う","GLM-5、Claude などのモデルをサポート"],"ko":["멀티 언어 품질 검증","모델 비의존적인 AI 오케스트레이션","9종류의 프로그래밍 언어를 지원","TLDR 보조 분석","모델 설정을 환경 변수로进行","GLM-5, Claude 등의 모델을 지원"],"es":["Análisis asistido por TLDR","Compatibilidad con 9 lenguajes de programación","Modelo agnóstico","No requiere flags","Flexible y configurable","Soporte para GLM-5, Claude, Minimax y más"],"fr":["Analyse assistée par TLDR","Compatibilité avec 9 langages de programmation","Modèle agnostique","Pas de flags requis","Flexible et configurable","Support pour GLM-5, Claude, Minimax et plus"],"de":["TLDR-unterstützte Analyse","Kompatibilität mit 9 Programmiersprachen","Modell-agnostisch","Keine Flags erforderlich","Flexibel und konfigurierbar","Unterstützung für GLM-5, Claude, Minimax und mehr"],"pt":["Orquestração de IA multi-agente","Validação de qualidade em 9 linguagens de programação","Análise assistida por TLDR","Compatibilidade com GLM-5, Claude, Minimax e outros modelos","Configuração de modelo via variáveis de ambiente"],"ru":["Многоагентная оркестрация ИИ","Проверка качества на 9 языках программирования","Анализ, поддерживаемый TLDR","Совместимость с GLM-5, Claude, Minimax и другими моделями","Выбор модели через переменные окружения"],"ar":["تنسيق متعدد العوامل للذكاء الاصطناعي","التحقق من الجودة في 9 لغات برمجة","التحليل بمساعدة TLDR","التوافق مع GLM-5 و Claude و Minimax والطرازات الأخرى","اختيار الطراز عبر متغيرات البيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Gates AI 代理技能","多代理 AI 编排","质量验证","模型无关","GLM-5","Claude","AI 编程","TLDR 辅助分析"],"ja":["Gates AI エージェントスキル","マルチエージェント AI オーケストレーション","品質検証","モデル非依存","GLM-5","Claude","AI プログラミング","TLDR アシスト分析"],"ko":["Gates AI 에이전트 스킬","멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션","품질 검증","모델 비의존","GLM-5","Claude","AI 프로그래밍","TLDR 보조 분석"],"es":["validación de calidad","análisis asistido por TLDR","desarrollo de software","lenguajes de programación","modelo agnóstico","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["validation de la qualité","analyse assistée par TLDR","développement de logiciels","langages de programmation","modèle agnostique","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","outils de développement"],"de":["Qualitätssicherung","TLDR-unterstützte Analyse","Software-Entwicklung","Programmiersprachen","Modell-agnostisch","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["orquestração de IA","validação de qualidade","análise de código","desenvolvimento de software","linguagens de programação","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","TLDR"],"ru":["оркестрация ИИ","проверка качества","анализ кода","разработка программного обеспечения","языки программирования","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","TLDR"],"ar":["تنسيق الذكاء الاصطناعي","التحقق من الجودة","تحليل الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","لغات البرمجة","GLM-5","Claude","Minimax","TLDR"]}},"owner":"alfredolopez80","repo":"multi-agent-ralph-loop","repoPath":"alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"gates","description":"9-language quality gate validation: linting, formatting, type checking, and test execution. Validates code changes meet quality standards before completion. Use when: (1) after code implementation, (2) before PR creation, (3) as part of /orchestrator Step 6, (4) manual quality check. Triggers: /gates, quality gates, run validation, check quality, validate code.","bodyPreview":"# Gates - Quality Validation (v2.37)\n\nComprehensive quality validation across 9 programming languages with **TLDR-assisted analysis**.\n\n## v2.88 Key Changes (MODEL-AGNOSTIC)\n\n- **Model-agnostic**: Uses model configured in `~/.claude/settings.json` or CLI/env vars\n- **No flags required**: Works with the configured default model\n- **Flexible**: Works with GLM-5, Claude, Minimax, or any configured model\n- **Settings-driven**: Model selection via `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL` env vars\n\n## Quick Start","body":"# Gates - Quality Validation (v2.37)\n\nComprehensive quality validation across 9 programming languages with **TLDR-assisted analysis**.\n\n## v2.88 Key Changes (MODEL-AGNOSTIC)\n\n- **Model-agnostic**: Uses model configured in `~/.claude/settings.json` or CLI/env vars\n- **No flags required**: Works with the configured default model\n- **Flexible**: Works with GLM-5, Claude, Minimax, or any configured model\n- **Settings-driven**: Model selection via `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL` env vars\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n/gates              # Run all quality gates\nralph gates         # Via CLI\nralph gates src/    # Specific directory\n```\n\n## LSP Usage for Type Checking\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Use LSP for efficient type checking instead of reading entire files.\n\n### When to Use LSP\n- Type checking TypeScript/JavaScript files\n- Finding type errors without running `tsc --noEmit`\n- Getting hover information for symbols\n- Finding references across the codebase\n\n### LSP Commands\n```yaml\n# Type check a specific file (TypeScript)\nLSP:\n  server: typescript-language-server\n  action: diagnostics\n  file: src/auth/login.ts\n\n# Get hover information for a symbol\nLSP:\n  server: typescript-language-server\n  action: hover\n  file: src/auth/login.ts\n  line: 42\n  character: 10\n\n# Find all references\nLSP:\n  server: typescript-language-server\n  action: references\n  file: src/auth/login.ts\n  line: 42\n  character: 10\n\n# Python type checking with pyright\nLSP:\n  server: pyright\n  action: diagnostics\n  file: src/auth/login.py\n```\n\n### LSP vs Traditional Type Checking\n| Method | Tokens Used | Speed | Use Case |\n|--------|-------------|-------|----------|\n| `tsc --noEmit` | HIGH (reads all files) | Slow | Full project check |\n| `LSP diagnostics` | LOW (indexed access) | Fast | Single file check |\n| `LSP hover` | MINIMAL | Instant | Quick type lookup |\n\n## Pre-Gates: TLDR Language Detection (v2.37)\n\n**AUTOMATIC** - Detect project languages efficiently:\n\n```bash\n# Get codebase structure to detect languages (95% token savings)\ntldr structure . > /tmp/project-structure.md\n\n# From structure, identify:\n# - Primary language(s)\n# - Config files present\n# - Test frameworks used\n```\n\n## Supported Languages\n\n| Language | Linter | Formatter | Types |\n|----------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| TypeScript | ESLint | Prettier | tsc |\n| JavaScript | ESLint | Prettier | - |\n| Python | Ruff | Black | mypy |\n| Rust | Clippy | rustfmt | cargo check |\n| Go | golint | gofmt | go vet |\n| Java | Checkstyle | google-java-format | - |\n| Ruby | RuboCop | - | Sorbet |\n| PHP | PHP_CodeSniffer | php-cs-fixer | PHPStan |\n| Solidity | Solhint | prettier-solidity | - |\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Detect Languages\n```bash\n# Auto-detect based on file extensions and config files\n```\n\n### 2. Run Linters\n```bash\n# Per-language linting\nnpx eslint src/          # TypeScript/JavaScript\nruff check .             # Python\ncargo clippy             # Rust\ngolangci-lint run        # Go\n```\n\n### 3. Check Formatting\n```bash\nnpx prettier --check .   # JS/TS\nblack --check .          # Python\nrustfmt --check src/     # Rust\ngofmt -l .               # Go\n```\n\n### 4. Type Checking\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit         # TypeScript\nmypy .                   # Python\ncargo check              # Rust\ngo vet ./...             # Go\n```\n\n### 5. Run Tests\n```bash\nnpm test                 # Node projects\npytest                   # Python\ncargo test               # Rust\ngo test ./...            # Go\n```\n\n## Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | All gates passed |\n| 1 | Lint errors |\n| 2 | Format errors |\n| 3 | Type errors |\n| 4 | Test failures |\n\n## Gate Configuration\n\n### Minimal (fast)\n```bash\nralph gates --minimal    # Lint only\n```\n\n### Standard (default)\n```bash\nralph gates              # Lint + Format + Types\n```\n\n### Full (CI)\n```bash\nralph gates --full       # Lint + Format + Types + Tests\n```\n\n## Integration\n\n- Invoked by /orchestrator in Step 6\n- **Pre-step: tldr structure for language detection** (v2.37)\n- Must pass before VERIFIED_DONE\n- Hooks: `quality-gates.sh` (PostToolUse)\n\n## TLDR Integration (v2.37)\n\n| Phase | TLDR Command | Purpose |\n|-------|--------------|---------|\n| Language detection | `tldr structure .` | Identify languages |\n| Error context | `tldr context $FILE .` | Understand failing code |\n| Impact analysis | `tldr deps $FILE .` | Find related tests |\n\n## Agent Teams Integration (v2.88)\n\n**Optimal Scenario**: Integrated (Agent Teams + Custom Subagents)\n\nQuality gates use Agent Teams coordination with specialized ralph-tester agents for parallel quality validation.\n\n### Why Scenario C for Gates\n- Multiple quality checks require coordination (lint, format, type, test)\n- Quality gates are meta-validation (hooks validate the validators)\n- Language-specific specialization via ralph-tester\n- TeammateIdle/TaskCompleted hooks for quality enforcement\n\n### Subagent Roles\n\n| Subagent | Role in Gates |\n|----------|---------------|\n| `ralph-tester` | Execute test suites in parallel |\n| `ralph-reviewer` | Analyze code quality issues |\n| `ralph-coder` | Apply auto-fixes for linting/formatting |\n\n### Parallel Gates Execution\nWhen Agent Teams is active, gates run in parallel across subagents:\n1. **Team Lead** creates task list with gate phases\n2. **ralph-tester** runs tests concurrently\n3. **ralph-reviewer** reviews linter output\n4. **ralph-coder** applies fixes\n\n### Quality Gate Hooks\n- `TeammateIdle`: Triggers before agent goes idle\n- `TaskCompleted`: Validates gate completion\n\n## Action Reporting (v2.93.0)\n\n**Los resultados de `/gates` generan reportes automáticos completos**:\n\n### Reporte Automático\n\nCuando `/gates` completa, se genera automáticamente:\n\n1. **En la conversación de Claude**: Resultados visibles de todas las validaciones\n2. **En el repositorio**: `docs/actions/gates/{timestamp}.md`\n3. **Metadatos JSON**: `.claude/metadata/actions/gates/{timestamp}.json`\n\n### Contenido del Reporte\n\nCada reporte incluye:\n- ✅ **Summary**: Tipo de validación ejecutada\n- ✅ **Results**: Resultados de linters, formatters, type checkers, tests\n- ✅ **Errors**: Errores encontrados por categoría\n- ✅ **Recommendations**: Acciones correctivas sugeridas\n- ✅ **Next Steps**: Qué hacer según el resultado\n\n### Generación Manual (Opcional)\n\n```bash\n# Al inicio\nsource .claude/lib/action-report-lib.sh\nstart_action_report \"gates\" \"Running quality gates on src/\"\n\n# Ejecutar validaciones\nif ! npx tsc --noEmit; then\n    record_error \"TypeScript errors found\"\nfi\n\nif ! npx eslint .; then\n    record_error \"ESLint violations found\"\nfi\n\nif ! npm test; then\n    record_error \"Test failures found\"\nfi\n\n# Al completar\nif [[ ${#CURRENT_ACTION_ERRORS[@]} -eq 0 ]]; then\n    complete_action_report \\\n        \"success\" \\\n        \"All quality gates passed\" \\\n        \"Safe to commit: git commit -m ''chore: pass quality gates''\"\nelse\n    complete_action_report \\\n        \"failed\" \\\n        \"Quality gates failed\" \\\n        \"Fix errors and run /gates again\"\nfi\n```\n\n### Ver Reportes Anteriores\n\n```bash\n# Listar todos los reportes de gates\nls -lt docs/actions/gates/\n\n# Ver el reporte más reciente\ncat $(ls -t docs/actions/gates/*.md | head -1)\n\n# Buscar reportes fallidos\ngrep -l \"Status: FAILED\" docs/actions/gates/*.md\n\n# Ver tendencia de calidad\ngrep -c \"Status: COMPLETED\" docs/actions/gates/*.md\ngrep -c \"Status: FAILED\" docs/actions/gates/*.md\n```\n\n### Integración CI/CD\n\nLos metadatos JSON permiten integración con pipelines:\n\n```bash\n# En tu CI pipeline\nsource .claude/lib/action-report-generator.sh\n\n# Ejecutar gates\n/gates\n\n# Obtener resultado del último reporte\nlatest_report=$(find_latest_report \"gates\")\nstatus=$(grep \"Status:\" \"$latest_report\" | awk ''{print $2}'')\n\nif [[ \"$status\" != \"COMPLETED\" ]]; then\n    echo \"Quality gates failed - blocking commit\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n### Referencias del Sistema de Reportes\n\n- [Action Reports System](docs/actions/README.md) - Documentación completa\n- [action-report-lib.sh](.claude/lib/action-report-lib.sh) - Librería helper\n- [action-report-generator.sh](.claude/lib/action-report-generator.sh) - Generador\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- Never skip gates for \"quick fixes\"\n- Never ignore type errors\n- Never commit with lint warnings\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:07:55.207Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Multi-Agent AI Orchestration Agents needing advanced quality validation and model-agnostic analysis across various programming languages.","zh":"非常适合需要高级质量验证和跨多种编程语言的模型无关分析的多代理人AI编排代理。","ja":"マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーションエージェントが高度な品質検証と様々なプログラミング言語を横断するモデル非依存分析を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"다중 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션 에이전트가 고급 품질 검증과 다양한 프로그래밍 언어를横断하는 모델 비의존 분석을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Orquestación de Inteligencia Artificial Multi-Agente que necesitan una validación de calidad avanzada y un análisis agnóstico de modelos en varios lenguajes de programación.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Orchestration d''Intelligence Artificielle Multi-Agents nécessitant une validation de qualité avancée et une analyse agnostique de modèles dans divers langages de programmation.","de":"Perfekt für Multi-Agenten-KI-Orchestrierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Qualitätsvalidierung und eine modellagnostische Analyse in verschiedenen Programmiersprachen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Orquestração de IA Multi-Agente que precisam de validação de qualidade avançada e análise agnóstica de modelo em várias linguagens de programação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов оркестровки ИИ с несколькими агентами, которым требуется продвинутая проверка качества и модельно-независимый анализ в различных языках программирования.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة الوكلاء الذكية متعددة الوكلاء التي تحتاج إلى التحقق من الجودة المتقدم وتحليل نموذج مجاني عبر لغات برمجة متعددة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive quality validation using TLDR-assisted analysis, working seamlessly with models like GLM-4.7, Claude, and Codex, while leveraging a flexible settings-driven approach via ~/.claude/settings.json or CLI/env vars.","zh":"赋予代理人使用TLDR辅助分析执行全面质量验证的能力，与GLM-4.7、Claude和Codex等模型无缝合作，同时通过~/.claude/settings.json或CLI/env变量采用灵活的设置驱动方法。","ja":"TLDRアシスト分析を使用して包括的な品質検証を実行するエージェントの能力を付与し、GLM-4.7、Claude、Codexなどのモデルとシームレスに連携し、~/.claude/settings.jsonまたはCLI/env変数を介した柔軟な設定駆動アプローチを活用します。","ko":"TLDR 보조 분석을 사용하여 포괄적인 품질 검증을 수행할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, GLM-4.7, Claude 및 Codex와 같은 모델과無縫に 협력하고, ~/.claude/settings.json 또는 CLI/env 변수를 통해 유연한 설정 주도 접근 방식을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar una validación de calidad integral utilizando análisis asistido por TLDR, trabajando de forma fluida con modelos como GLM-4.7, Claude y Codex, mientras aprovecha un enfoque flexible basado en configuración a través de ~/.claude/settings.json o variables de entorno de CLI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser une validation de qualité complète en utilisant l''analyse assistée par TLDR, travaillant en toute transparence avec des modèles comme GLM-4.7, Claude et Codex, tout en exploitant une approche flexible basée sur les paramètres via ~/.claude/settings.json ou des variables d''environnement CLI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, eine umfassende Qualitätsvalidierung durchzuführen, indem sie eine TLDR-unterstützte Analyse verwenden, nahtlos mit Modellen wie GLM-4.7, Claude und Codex zusammenarbeitend, während sie einen flexiblen einstellungsgetriebenen Ansatz über ~/.claude/settings.json oder CLI-Umgebungsvariablen nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar uma validação de qualidade abrangente usando análise assistida por TLDR, trabalhando sem problemas com modelos como GLM-4.7, Claude e Codex, ao mesmo tempo em que aproveita uma abordagem flexível baseada em configurações via ~/.claude/settings.json ou variáveis de ambiente CLI.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять комплексную проверку качества с помощью анализа, поддерживаемого TLDR, работая без проблем с моделями типа GLM-4.7, Claude и Codex, а также использует гибридный подход, основанный на настройках, через ~/.claude/settings.json или переменные среды CLI.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من أداء التحقق من الجودة الشامل باستخدام التحليل المدعوم من TLDR، والعمل بسلاسة مع نماذج مثل GLM-4.7 و Claude و Codex، في الوقت نفسه استغلال نهج مرن قائم على الإعدادات عبر ~/.claude/settings.json أو متغيرات بيئة CLI."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating code quality across 9 programming languages","Performing model-agnostic analysis with configured default models","Integrating with memory systems and hooks for enhanced functionality"],"zh":["跨9种编程语言验证代码质量","使用配置的默认模型执行模型无关分析","与内存系统和钩子集成以增强功能"],"ja":["9種類のプログラミング言語を横断してコード品質を検証する","構成済みのデフォルトモデルを使用してモデル非依存分析を実行する","メモリシステムやフックと統合して機能を強化する"],"ko":["9개의 프로그래밍 언어를横断하여 코드 품질을 검증하는 것","구성된 기본 모델을 사용하여 모델 비의존 분석을 수행하는 것","메모리 시스템 및 후크와 통합하여 기능을 강화하는 것"],"es":["Validar la calidad del código en 9 lenguajes de programación","Realizar un análisis agnóstico de modelos con modelos predeterminados configurados","Integrarse con sistemas de memoria y ganchos para una funcionalidad mejorada"],"fr":["Valider la qualité du code dans 9 langages de programmation","Réalisé une analyse agnostique de modèles avec des modèles par défaut configurés","Intégrer avec des systèmes de mémoire et des crochets pour une fonctionnalité améliorée"],"de":["Überprüfen der Codequalität in 9 Programmiersprachen","Durchführen einer modellagnostischen Analyse mit konfigurierten Standardmodellen","Integrieren mit Speichersystemen und Haken für eine erweiterte Funktionalität"],"pt":["Validar a qualidade de código em 9 linguagens de programação","Realizar análise agnóstica de modelo com modelos padrão configurados","Integrar com sistemas de memória e ganchos para funcionalidade aprimorada"],"ru":["Проверять качество кода на 9 языках программирования","Выполнять модельно-независимый анализ с настроенными моделями по умолчанию","Интегрироваться с системами памяти и крючками для расширенной функциональности"],"ar":["التحقق من جودة الكود عبر 9 لغات برمجة","أداء تحليل نموذج مجاني مع نماذج افتراضية مضبوطة","التكامل مع أنظمة الذاكرة والسنادات من أجل وظيفة محسنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires configuration in ~/.claude/settings.json or CLI/env vars","Deprecates MiniMax, requiring migration to supported models"],"zh":["需要在~/.claude/settings.json或CLI/env变量中进行配置","废弃MiniMax，需要迁移到支持的模型"],"ja":["~/.claude/settings.jsonまたはCLI/env変数で構成する必要がある","MiniMaxは非推奨であり、サポート対象のモデルへの移行が必要"],"ko":["~/.claude/settings.json 또는 CLI/env 변수에서 구성해야 함","MiniMax는 더 이상 지원되지 않으며 지원되는 모델로 마이그레이션해야 함"],"es":["Requiere configuración en ~/.claude/settings.json o variables de entorno de CLI","Elimina MiniMax, lo que requiere una migración a modelos compatibles"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration dans ~/.claude/settings.json ou des variables d''environnement CLI","Déprécie MiniMax, ce qui nécessite une migration vers des modèles pris en charge"],"de":["Benötigt Konfiguration in ~/.claude/settings.json oder CLI-Umgebungsvariablen","Veraltet MiniMax, was eine Migration zu unterstützten Modellen erfordert"],"pt":["Exige configuração em ~/.claude/settings.json ou variáveis de ambiente CLI","Descontinua o MiniMax, exigindo migração para modelos compatíveis"],"ru":["Требует настройки в ~/.claude/settings.json или переменных среды CLI","Устаревает MiniMax, требуя миграции на поддерживаемые модели"],"ar":["يتطلب إعدادات في ~/.claude/settings.json أو متغيرات بيئة CLI","يحظر استخدام MiniMax، مما يتطلب هجرة إلى نماذج مدعومة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bountydotnew/bounty.new/Integrating Stripe Payments', 'community', 'bountydotnew', 'bounty.new', 'bountydotnew/bounty.new', 'Integrating Stripe Payments', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:31.800Z', NULL, '{"id":"bountydotnew/bounty.new/Integrating Stripe Payments","name":"Integrating Stripe Payments","description":{"zh":"Convex Next.js Stripe","ja":"Stripe Convex Next.js","ko":"Convex Next.js Stripe","es":"Integra pagos de Stripe en tu aplicación Convex y Next.js para aceptar pagos de forma segura.","fr":"Intégrez les paiements Stripe dans votre application Convex et Next.js pour accepter les paiements de manière sécurisée.","de":"Integrieren Sie Stripe-Zahlungen in Ihre Convex- und Next.js-Anwendung, um Zahlungen sicher zu akzeptieren.","pt":"Integre pagamentos Stripe em sua aplicação Convex + Next.js de forma eficaz. Nossa habilidade de pagamento oferece uma solução completa para sua necessidade de pagamento.","ru":"Интегрируйте платежи Stripe в ваше приложение Convex + Next.js эффективно. Наша платёжная навыка предлагает полное решение для ваших потребностей в оплате.","ar":"دمج مدفوعات سترايب في تطبيق Convex + Next.js بفعالية. مهارة الدفع الخاصة بنا توفر حلًا شاملاً لمتطلبات الدفع الخاصة بك.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Convex Next.js","ja":"Stripe","ko":"Convex Next.js","es":"Integrar Pagos de Stripe con Convex y Next.js","fr":"Intégrer les Paiements Stripe avec Convex et Next.js","de":"Stripe-Zahlungen mit Convex und Next.js integrieren","pt":"Integração de Pagamentos Stripe","ru":"Интеграция платежей Stripe","ar":"دمج مدفوعات سترايب","en":"Integrating Stripe Payments"},"description":{"zh":"Convex Next.js Stripe","ja":"Stripe Convex Next.js","ko":"Convex Next.js Stripe","es":"Integra pagos de Stripe en tu aplicación Convex y Next.js para aceptar pagos de forma segura.","fr":"Intégrez les paiements Stripe dans votre application Convex et Next.js pour accepter les paiements de manière sécurisée.","de":"Integrieren Sie Stripe-Zahlungen in Ihre Convex- und Next.js-Anwendung, um Zahlungen sicher zu akzeptieren.","pt":"Integre pagamentos Stripe em sua aplicação Convex + Next.js de forma eficaz. Nossa habilidade de pagamento oferece uma solução completa para sua necessidade ...","ru":"Интегрируйте платежи Stripe в ваше приложение Convex + Next.js эффективно. Наша платёжная навыка предлагает полное решение для ваших потребностей в оплате.","ar":"دمج مدفوعات سترايب في تطبيق Convex + Next.js بفعالية. مهارة الدفع الخاصة بنا توفر حلًا شاملاً لمتطلبات الدفع الخاصة بك.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Convex","Next.js","Stripe","API","Convex Next.js"],"ja":["Stripe","Convex","Next.js","API","Stripe"],"ko":["Convex Next.js","Stripe","API","Convex","Next.js"],"es":["Configuración de Checkout de Stripe","Soporte para pagos recurrentes y únicos","Integración con Convex y Next.js","Gestión de precios y productos","Seguridad de pagos con Stripe"],"fr":["Configuration de la passerelle de paiement Stripe","Prise en charge des paiements récurrents et uniques","Intégration avec Convex et Next.js","Gestion des prix et des produits","Sécurité des paiements avec Stripe"],"de":["Konfiguration des Stripe-Checkouts","Unterstützung für wiederkehrende und einmalige Zahlungen","Integration mit Convex und Next.js","Preis- und Produktverwaltung","Zahlungssicherheit mit Stripe"],"pt":["Integração com Convex e Next.js","Suporte a pagamentos recorrentes e únicos","Checkout personalizado com Stripe","Gerenciamento de preços e produtos","Confirmação de pagamento e notificação"],"ru":["Интеграция с Convex и Next.js","Поддержка регулярных и единовременных платежей","Персонализированный чеккаут с Stripe","Управление ценами и продуктами","Подтверждение платежа и уведомление"],"ar":["دمج مع Convex و Next.js","دعم المدفوعات المتكررة والفردية","شيك أوت مخصص مع سترايب","إدارة الأسعار والمنتجات","التأكيد على الدفع والإشعار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Convex Next.js","Stripe","API","Convex","Next.js","Stripe","Convex Next.js"],"ja":["Stripe","Convex","Next.js","API","Stripe","Convex Next.js"],"ko":["Convex Next.js","Stripe","API","Convex","Next.js","Stripe"],"es":["integrar pagos de Stripe","Convex y Next.js","pagos en línea","pasarela de pago","Stripe Checkout","pagos recurrentes","seguridad de pagos"],"fr":["intégrer les paiements Stripe","Convex et Next.js","paiements en ligne","passerelle de paiement","Stripe Checkout","paiements récurrents","sécurité des paiements"],"de":["Stripe-Zahlungen integrieren","Convex und Next.js","Online-Zahlungen","Zahlungs-Gateway","Stripe-Checkout","wiederkehrende Zahlungen","Zahlungssicherheit"],"pt":["integração de pagamentos stripe","convex e next.js","pagamentos recorrentes","checkout personalizado","gerenciamento de preços","desenvolvimento de aplicativos"],"ru":["интеграция платежей stripe","convex и next.js","регулярные платежи","персонализированный чеккаут","управление ценами","разработка приложений"],"ar":["دمج مدفوعات سترايب","convex و next.js","مدفوعات متكررة","شيك أوت مخصص","إدارة الأسعار","تطوير التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"bountydotnew","repo":"bounty.new","repoPath":"bountydotnew/bounty.new","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Integrating Stripe Payments","description":"Complete workflow for integrating Stripe payments (subscriptions or one-time) with Convex + Next.js. Includes hosted checkout, webhooks, UI components, and testing. Use when adding payment functionality to a Convex + Next.js app.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Integrating Stripe Payments\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nWhen user requests Stripe payment integration for Convex + Next.js:\n\n### 1. Requirements Gathering\nAsk these questions first:\n- **Payment type**: Subscription or one-time payment?\n- **Backend**: Confirm this is Convex (required for this skill)\n- **Checkout preference**: Hosted Stripe Checkout (recommended) or embedded?\n- **Pricing**: Amount, currency, billing interval for subscriptions?\n- **Product**: What does user get after payment?\n\n### 2. API","body":"# Integrating Stripe Payments\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nWhen user requests Stripe payment integration for Convex + Next.js:\n\n### 1. Requirements Gathering\nAsk these questions first:\n- **Payment type**: Subscription or one-time payment?\n- **Backend**: Confirm this is Convex (required for this skill)\n- **Checkout preference**: Hosted Stripe Checkout (recommended) or embedded?\n- **Pricing**: Amount, currency, billing interval for subscriptions?\n- **Product**: What does user get after payment?\n\n### 2. API Keys & Environment Setup\n**CRITICAL**: Gather these FIRST before proceeding - MCP tools require credentials.\n\n1. **Get Stripe API keys from user**:\n   - Ask for Stripe Secret Key (starts with `sk_test_` or `sk_live_`)\n   - Add to `.env.local`: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...`\n\n2. **Install dependencies**: `npm install stripe`\n\n3. **Set initial environment variables**:\n   - `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` (from step 1)\n   - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000` (default local development)\n\n4. **Use Stripe MCP tool** to create product/price and get price ID\n5. **Use Convex MCP tool** to set remaining environment variables\n6. **Manual fallback**: Follow `resources/environment-setup.md`\n\nComplete required env vars:\n- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` ✓ (set in step 1)\n- `STRIPE_PRICE_ID` (from Stripe MCP tool)\n- `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (set during webhook configuration)\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` ✓ (set in step 1)\n\n### 3. Database Schema\nUpdate `convex/schema.ts` with Stripe fields. See `resources/database-schema.ts` for complete schema.\n\n### 4. Backend Implementation\nCopy and customize these files:\n- `convex/stripe.ts` ← Use `resources/convex-stripe-actions.ts`\n- `convex/stripeDb.ts` ← Use `resources/convex-stripe-db.ts`\n- `convex/http.ts` ← Use `resources/convex-webhook-handler.ts`\n\n**Key customizations**:\n- Update membership tier names (`\"pro\"` vs `\"premium\"`)\n- Adjust auth field names (`clerkId` vs your auth system)\n- Set correct API version: `2025-08-27.basil`\n- Enable coupon codes by setting `allow_promotion_codes: true` in checkout session creation\n\n### 5. Frontend Components\nCreate UI components from `resources/ui-components.tsx`:\n- `UpgradeButton` - Shows different states based on membership\n- `ManageBillingButton` - Opens customer portal\n\n**UI Design Guidelines**:\n- Match existing app design system\n- Use gradients and proper state management\n- Show loading states and error handling\n- Keep prices in sync with Stripe Dashboard\n\n### 6. Webhook Configuration\n1. Get Convex deployment URL (use `.convex.site` domain)\n2. Create webhook in Stripe Dashboard: `https://your-deployment.convex.site/stripe/webhook`\n3. Select events: `checkout.session.completed`, `customer.subscription.*`, `invoice.*`\n4. Copy webhook secret to environment variables\n\n### 7. Testing\nFollow `resources/testing-checklist.md`:\n- Test successful payment flow\n- Test failed payments\n- Test customer portal\n- Verify webhook delivery\n- Use Stripe CLI for local testing\n\n### 8. Production Deployment\n- Switch to live Stripe keys\n- Create production webhook endpoint\n- Configure Customer Portal and Smart Retries\n- Test with real payment (then refund)\n\n## Best Practices\n\n**Always:**\n- Use hosted checkout for simplicity and security\n- Use `constructEventAsync` in webhooks (not `constructEvent`)\n- Include user metadata in checkout sessions\n- Handle missing `current_period_end` with fallbacks\n- Keep UI prices synchronized with Stripe prices\n- Use consistent Stripe API version across all files\n- Set `allow_promotion_codes: true` to enable coupon code input during checkout\n\n**Never:**\n- Use `.convex.cloud` for webhooks (use `.convex.site`)\n- Skip webhook idempotency in production\n- Forget to configure Customer Portal\n- Deploy without testing webhook delivery\n\n## Common Issues\n\n**Webhook not working**: Check domain (`.convex.site`) and webhook secret\n**Membership not updating**: Verify webhook events and metadata\n**API errors**: Ensure consistent API version usage\n\n## Documentation References\n\nUse **Stripe MCP tool** for latest documentation when:\n- Checking API changes or new features\n- Troubleshooting integration issues\n- Verifying best practices\n\nSee `resources/` folder for complete code examples and detailed setup instructions."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:31.800Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for E-commerce Agents requiring seamless Stripe payment integration with Convex and Next.js","zh":"适用于需要与 Convex 和 Next.js 无缝集成 Stripe 支付的电子商务代理","ja":"Convex と Next.js とのシームレスな Stripe 支付統合を必要とする電子商取引エージェントに最適","ko":"Convex와 Next.js와의 무결점 Stripe 결제 통합을 요구하는 전자상거래 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de comercio electrónico que requieren una integración de pago de Stripe sin problemas con Convex y Next.js","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de commerce électronique nécessitant une intégration de paiement Stripe fluide avec Convex et Next.js","de":"Ideal für E-Commerce-Agents, die eine nahtlose Stripe-Zahlungsintegration mit Convex und Next.js benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Comércio Eletrônico que exigem integração de pagamento seamless com Stripe, Convex e Next.js","ru":"Идеально для агентов электронной коммерции, требующих бесшовной интеграции оплаты Stripe с Convex и Next.js","ar":"مثالي لعميل تجارة إلكترونية يتطلب تكامل دفع متكامل مع Stripe و Convex و Next.js"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to process one-time and subscription-based payments using Stripe''s Hosted Checkout or embedded solutions, handling various pricing models and product offerings, all while leveraging Convex as the backend infrastructure and integrating with Next.js for a robust frontend experience","zh":"赋予代理商使用 Stripe 的托管结账或嵌入式解决方案处理一次性和基于订阅的支付，处理各种定价模型和产品提供，同时利用 Convex 作为后端基础设施，并与 Next.js 集成以提供强大的前端体验","ja":"エージェントが Stripe のホストされたチェックアウトまたはエンベデッド ソリューションを使用して、1 回限りの支払いとサブスクリプションベースの支払いを処理できるようにし、さまざまな価格モデルと製品オファリングを処理し、Convex をバックエンド インフラストラクチャとして活用し、Next.js と統合して堅牢なフロントエンド エクスペリエンスを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 스트라잎의 호스팅 체크아웃 또는 임베디드 솔루션을 사용하여 일회성 및 구독 기반 결제를 처리할 수 있도록 해주며, 다양한 가격 모델 및 제품 제공을 처리하며, Convex를 백엔드 인프라로 활용하며, Next.js와 통합하여 강력한 프론트엔드 경험을 제공한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a procesar pagos de una sola vez y basados en suscripción utilizando el Checkout hospedado de Stripe o soluciones integradas, manejo de varios modelos de precios y ofertas de productos, todo mientras aprovecha Convex como infraestructura de backend e integra con Next.js para una experiencia de frontend robusta","fr":"Permet aux agents de traiter des paiements à la fois ponctuels et basés sur abonnement en utilisant le Checkout hébergé de Stripe ou des solutions intégrées, gérant divers modèles de tarification et offres de produits, le tout en exploitant Convex comme infrastructure de backend et en intégrant avec Next.js pour une expérience de frontend robuste","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, einmalige und abonnementbasierte Zahlungen zu verarbeiten, indem sie den Hosted Checkout von Stripe oder eingebettete Lösungen verwenden, um verschiedene Preismodelle und Produktangebote zu handhaben, und zwar unter Nutzung von Convex als Backend-Infrastruktur und Integration mit Next.js für eine robuste Frontend-Erfahrung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a processar pagamentos de uma única vez e baseados em assinatura usando o Hosted Checkout da Stripe ou soluções incorporadas, lidando com vários modelos de preços e ofertas de produtos, tudo isso aproveitando Convex como infraestrutura de backend e integrando com Next.js para uma experiência de frontend robusta","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обрабатывать единовременные и подписные платежи с помощью Hosted Checkout от Stripe или встроенных решений, обрабатывая различные модели ценообразования и предложения продукции, все это при использовании Convex в качестве инфраструктуры бэкенда и интеграции с Next.js для прочного фронта","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على معالجة المدفوعات لمرة واحدة والمدفوعات القائمة على الاشتراك باستخدام Hosted Checkout من Stripe أو الحلول المدمجة ، ومعالجة أنواع مختلفة من نماذج التسعير وعروض المنتجات ، كل ذلك مع الاستفادة من Convex كبنية خلفية وتكامل مع Next.js من أجل تجربة واجهة أمامية قوية"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing subscription models with recurring billing intervals","Configuring one-time payments for digital products","Integrating Stripe Checkout for secure and streamlined payment processing"],"zh":["实施具有定期账单间隔的订阅模式","为数字产品配置一次性付款","集成 Stripe Checkout 以实现安全且流畅的付款处理"],"ja":["定期請求間隔を持つサブスクリプション モデルを実装する","デジタル製品のための1回限りの支払いを設定する","セキュアでストリームライン化された支払い処理を実現するための Stripe チェックアウトの統合"],"ko":["정기적 청구 간격을 갖는 구독 모델实施","디지털 제품을 위한 일회성 결제 설정","보안이 뛰어난 스트림 라인화된 결제 처리를 위한 스트라잎 체크아웃 통합"],"es":["Implementación de modelos de suscripción con intervalos de facturación recurrentes","Configuración de pagos de una sola vez para productos digitales","Integración de Stripe Checkout para un procesamiento de pagos seguro y fluido"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de modèles d''abonnement avec des intervalles de facturation récurrents","Configuration de paiements ponctuels pour des produits numériques","Intégration de Stripe Checkout pour un traitement de paiement sécurisé et fluide"],"de":["Implementierung von Abonnementmodellen mit wiederkehrenden Abrechnungsintervallen","Konfiguration von Einmalzahlungen für digitale Produkte","Integration von Stripe Checkout für ein sicheres und reibungsloses Zahlungsverarbeitung"],"pt":["Implementação de modelos de assinatura com intervalos de faturamento recorrentes","Configuração de pagamentos de uma única vez para produtos digitais","Integração do Stripe Checkout para processamento de pagamentos seguro e otimizado"],"ru":["Реализация моделей подписки с регулярными интервалами выставления счетов","Настройка единовременных платежей для цифровых продуктов","Интеграция Stripe Checkout для безопасной и оптимизированной обработки платежей"],"ar":["تنفيذ نماذج الاشتراك مع فترات فواتير متكررة","تكوين مدفوعات لمرة واحدة للمنتجات الرقمية","تكامل Stripe Checkout لمعالجة دفع آمنة ومُتطورة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Convex as the backend","Limited to Stripe payment gateway","Checkout preference restricted to Hosted Stripe Checkout or embedded solutions"],"zh":["需要 Convex 作为后端","仅限 Stripe 支付网关","结账首选项仅限托管 Stripe 结账或嵌入式解决方案"],"ja":["バックエンドとして Convex を必要とする","Stripe 支払いゲートウェイのみに限定される","チェックアウトの優先順位はホストされた Stripe チェックアウトまたはエンベデッド ソリューションに限定される"],"ko":["백엔드로서 Convex가 필요","스트라잎 결제 게이트웨이로 제한됨","체크아웃 우선순위는 호스팅된 스트라잎 체크아웃 또는 임베디드 솔루션으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere Convex como backend","Limitado a la pasarela de pago de Stripe","Preferencia de checkout restringida a Hosted Stripe Checkout o soluciones integradas"],"fr":["Nécessite Convex comme backend","Limité à la passerelle de paiement Stripe","Préférence de checkout restreinte au Checkout hébergé de Stripe ou aux solutions intégrées"],"de":["Benötigt Convex als Backend","Begrenzt auf die Stripe-Zahlungs-Gateway","Checkout-Präferenz beschränkt auf Hosted Stripe Checkout oder eingebettete Lösungen"],"pt":["Exige Convex como backend","Limitado ao gateway de pagamento Stripe","Preferência de checkout restrita ao Hosted Stripe Checkout ou soluções incorporadas"],"ru":["Требует Convex в качестве бэкенда","Ограничен только шлюзом оплаты Stripe","Предпочтение чекаута ограничено Hosted Stripe Checkout или встроенными решениями"],"ar":["يتطلب Convex كبنية خلفية","محدود بمحفظة دفع Stripe فقط","تقييد تفضيل Checkout بال Hosted Stripe Checkout أو الحلول المدمجة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
