根据项目的书评政策","ja":"Rust 言語書評フレームワークは、プロジェクトの書評ポリシーに基づいて書籍の指定された部分をレビューするためのツールです","ko":"Rust 언어 서평 프레임워크는 프로젝트의 서평 정책에 따라 책의 지정된 부분을 검토하는 데 사용되는 도구입니다","es":"El framework de datos de prueba de Rust permite revisar partes de un libro según las políticas de revisión del proyecto. Aprende a interpretar argumentos y r...","fr":"Le cadre de données de preuve de Rust permet de réviser des parties d''un livre selon les politiques de révision du projet. Apprenez à interpréter des argumen...","de":"Das Framework für Datenprüfung von Rust ermöglicht die Bewertung von Teilen eines Buches gemäß den Bewertungsrichtlinien des Projekts. Lernen Sie, wie Sie Ar...","pt":"O framework de revisão de livros em Rust é uma ferramenta para garantir a qualidade do código","ru":"Фреймворк обзора книг на Rust является инструментом для обеспечения качества кода","ar":"إطار عمل استعراض الكتب بلغة راست هو أداة لضمان جودة الشفرة","en":"Rust language proof-carrying data framework"},"definition":{"en":"Rust language proof-carrying data framework"},"features":{"zh":["使用 Rust 语言","proof-carrying 数据框架","根据项目的书评政策审查","支持文件路径和行号审查","自动审查未提交的更改"],"ja":["Rust 言語を使用","proof-carrying データフレームワーク","プロジェクトの書評ポリシーに基づいてレビュー","ファイルパスと行番号のレビューをサポート","自動で未コミットの変更をレビュー"],"ko":["Rust 언어 사용","proof-carrying 데이터 프레임워크","프로젝트의 서평 정책에 따라 검토","파일 경로와 행 번호 검토 지원","자동으로 커밋되지 않은 변경 사항을 검토"],"es":["Revisión de capítulos según las políticas del proyecto","Interpretación de argumentos para determinar qué revisar","Compatibilidad con Git para revisar cambios","Soporte para archivos Markdown","Personalización de las políticas de revisión","Integración con flujos de trabajo de desarrollo"],"fr":["Révision de chapitres selon les politiques du projet","Interprétation d''arguments pour déterminer ce qui doit être révisé","Compatibilité avec Git pour réviser les modifications","Prise en charge de fichiers Markdown","Personnalisation des politiques de révision","Intégration avec les flux de travail de développement"],"de":["Bewertung von Kapiteln gemäß den Projektregeln","Interpretation von Argumenten zur Bestimmung der zu bewertenden Inhalte","Kompatibilität mit Git zur Bewertung von Änderungen","Unterstützung für Markdown-Dateien","Anpassung der Bewertungsregeln","Integration in Entwicklungsworkflows"],"pt":["Revisão de código em Rust","Análise de qualidade do código","Compatibilidade com Git","Revisão de capítulos inteiros","Suporte a argumentos personalizados"],"ru":["Обзор кода на Rust","Анализ качества кода","Совместимость с Git","Обзор целых глав","Поддержка пользовательских аргументов"],"ar":["استعراض الشفرة بلغة راست","تحليل جودة الشفرة","التوافق مع Git","استعراض الفصول الكاملة","دعم الحجج المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust 语言","书评框架","proof-carrying 数据","项目书评政策","文件路径审查","行号审查","自动审查"],"ja":["Rust 言語","書評フレームワーク","proof-carrying データ","プロジェクトの書評ポリシー","ファイルパスレビュー","行番号レビュー","自動レビュー"],"ko":["Rust 언어","서평 프레임워크","proof-carrying 데이터","프로젝트의 서평 정책","파일 경로 검토","행 번호 검토","자동 검토"],"es":["Rust","framework de datos de prueba","revisión de libros","políticas de revisión","desarrollo de software","Git","Markdown","pruebas de software","validación de datos"],"fr":["Rust","cadre de données de preuve","révision de livres","politiques de révision","développement de logiciels","Git","Markdown","tests de logiciels","validation de données"],"de":["Rust","Framework für Datenprüfung","Buchbewertung","Bewertungsregeln","Softwareentwicklung","Git","Markdown","Softwaretests","Datenvalidierung"],"pt":["Rust","revisão de código","qualidade do código","Git","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","framework de revisão de livros"],"ru":["Rust","обзор кода","качество кода","Git","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","фреймворк обзора книг"],"ar":["راست","استعراض الشفرة","جودة الشفرة","Git","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","إطار عمل استعراض الكتب"]}},"owner":"tachyon-zcash","repo":"ragu","repoPath":"tachyon-zcash/ragu","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"book-review","description":"Review any part of the book using parallel specialist agents","bodyPreview":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:","body":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:50-80`) | Read that file. Focus the review on those lines (but read the full file for context). |\n| Multiple file paths | Read all of them. Review each, and also look for consistency across them. |\n| A section heading or topic name | Use Grep/Glob to find where that topic is discussed in `book/src/`. Read those sections. Review them. |\n| A conceptual description (\"how we explain X\", \"the transition between Y and Z\") | Search the book to find the relevant passages. Read them with surrounding context. Review them as a unit. |\n| A mix of the above | Handle each part, then review the union. |\n\nIf you''re unsure what the user means, ask before launching reviewers.\n\n## Step 2: Discover and Launch Reviewers\n\n1. Use Glob to find all `.claude/book-review/*.md` files.\n2. Read `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards shared by all\n   reviewers).\n3. For EACH policy file **except `standards.md`**, launch a `general-purpose`\n   Task agent (use model `sonnet`). Give each agent a prompt constructed from\n   this template — adapt it based on what you''re reviewing:\n\n   > You are reviewing part of \"The Ragu Book,\" a technical book about a\n   > recursive proof system (proof-carrying data framework).\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards that always apply)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your specific review policy)\n   >\n   > **What to review:** {describe the specific content — file paths, line\n   > ranges, the topic, whatever the user specified. If reviewing a diff,\n   > include the diff text and list the full file paths for context.}\n   >\n   > {If the scope is a diff or a narrow range, add: \"Focus on the specified\n   > content. Flag issues in surrounding text ONLY if the specified content\n   > introduced an inconsistency with it.\"}\n   >\n   > {If the scope spans multiple files or a concept, add: \"Pay attention to\n   > consistency across the passages. Flag contradictions, redundancies, or\n   > gaps in the explanation as it spans these locations.\"}\n   >\n   > If the policy references other files (like `book/macros.txt` or\n   > `book/src/appendix/terminology.md`), read those too.\n   >\n   > For each finding:\n   > - **Location**: file path and quoted text (or line number)\n   > - **Issue**: what''s wrong, specifically\n   > - **Suggestion**: a concrete rewrite, not just \"improve this\"\n   > - **Severity**: `must-fix` (clearly wrong/confusing) or `suggestion`\n   >\n   > Stay within your policy''s scope. Be specific. If you find no real issues,\n   > say so — don''t manufacture problems.\n\n   Additionally, read `book/FIXME.md` and extract the `###`-level headings\n   under `## Deferred Issues`. Include them in each reviewer''s prompt as a\n   bullet list with the instruction:\n   > The following issues are already tracked and deferred. Do NOT raise\n   > findings that duplicate or overlap with these items. If your finding\n   > is essentially the same issue, omit it.\n   >\n   > {bullet list of ### headings from book/FIXME.md}\n   >\n   > However, if while reviewing you notice that a deferred issue appears to\n   > have been **resolved** by existing content or is now easily resolvable\n   > given changes in the surrounding text, mention it as a separate\n   > observation (not a finding). Format:\n   > - **Resolvable FIXME**: \"{FIXME heading}\" — {brief explanation of why\n   >   it appears resolved or how to resolve it now}\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel (multiple Task calls in one message).\n\n## Step 3: Run Automated Link Checks\n\nIn parallel with the reviewer agents (launched in Step 2), run the automated\nQA scripts to detect broken links and dead pages:\n\n1. Run `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py` — finds broken internal links and\n   invalid anchors (requires `mdbook` to be installed).\n2. Run `python3 qa/book/dead_pages.py` — finds markdown files not listed in\n   `SUMMARY.md`.\n3. Run `python3 qa/book/line_width.py` — finds lines exceeding the\n   80-character width limit (excludes code blocks, math blocks, and other\n   exempt content).\n\nIf either script fails to run (e.g., `mdbook` is not installed), note the\nfailure in your output but do not block the review. Include any findings from\nthese scripts alongside the reviewer agents'' results in the synthesis step.\n\n## Step 4: Synthesize\n\nOnce all agents return, organize findings by location (earliest in the book\nfirst). If multiple reviewers flagged overlapping concerns, merge them. Present:\n\n- **Must-fix** issues first\n- **Suggestions** second\n- For each finding, note which reviewer(s) identified it\n\nIf the review scope was cross-file or conceptual, add a short section at the end\nabout cross-cutting observations (consistency, narrative coherence, etc.).\n\nBefore presenting findings, read `book/FIXME.md` and remove any finding that\nsubstantially overlaps with an already-deferred issue (match against the `###`\nheadings). If you remove findings this way, do not mention them at all.\n\nIf any reviewer flagged a resolvable FIXME, collect them in a **Potentially\nResolvable FIXMEs** section after the main findings. The user can then use\n`/book-fixme` to address them.\n\n## Step 5: Validate Proposed Changes\n\nAfter synthesizing findings, but before presenting them to the user:\n\n1. Collect all proposed changes (the \"suggestion\" field from each finding) into\n   a single numbered list — the **proposed plan**.\n2. For EACH policy file (same set as Step 2 — every `.claude/book-review/*.md`\n   except `standards.md`), launch a `general-purpose` Task agent (model\n   `sonnet`) with this prompt:\n\n   > You are validating a set of proposed book edits against review policies.\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your policy)\n   >\n   > Here is the proposed plan of changes:\n   > {numbered list of proposed changes with locations and suggested rewrites}\n   >\n   > For each proposed change, check whether applying it would **introduce** a\n   > violation of any rule in your policy or the master standards. Only flag\n   > real conflicts — do not restate rules that are already satisfied.\n   >\n   > For each conflict found:\n   > - **Change #**: which proposed change\n   > - **Rule violated**: quote the relevant policy text\n   > - **Conflict**: explain specifically how the suggestion violates the rule\n   > - **Resolution**: suggest how to fix the suggestion to comply\n   >\n   > If no proposed changes conflict with your policy, say so.\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel.\n\n3. Merge validation feedback into the findings. For each conflict:\n   - If the validator provides a compliant alternative, replace the original\n     suggestion with the corrected version.\n   - If the conflict has no clear resolution, annotate the finding with the\n     conflict so the user can decide during triage.\n\n4. If any suggestions were corrected, briefly note it in the synthesis output\n   (e.g., \"Grammar validator caught that suggestion #3 would violate the\n   lowercase-technical-terms rule; corrected.\").\n\n## Step 6: Triage\n\nAfter presenting findings, use AskUserQuestion to let the user decide the\ndisposition of each finding (or group of closely related findings). For each,\noffer:\n\n- **Fix** — apply the suggested fix now\n- **Skip** — drop this finding; do not record it anywhere\n- **Defer** — record this finding in `book/FIXME.md` for future attention\n\nIf there are many findings, you may batch them into logical groups and ask\nabout each group rather than each individual finding.\n\n## Step 7: Apply Fixes\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **fix**:\n\n1. Read the target file to get the current content.\n2. Apply the suggested change using the Edit tool. If the finding is a group\n   (e.g., \"add slugs to these 15 headings\"), apply all changes in the group.\n3. After applying all fixes, run any relevant QA scripts to verify the changes\n   don''t introduce new issues:\n   - If formatting changes were made: `python3 qa/book/line_width.py`\n   - If links or headings were changed: `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py`\n4. Briefly report what was changed and any QA results.\n\n## Step 8: Record Deferred Issues\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **defer**:\n\n1. Read `book/FIXME.md`.\n2. Check whether a substantially similar issue is already listed. First scan\n   the `###` headings for a potential match; if a heading looks similar, read\n   the paragraph beneath it to confirm it describes the same issue. Only skip\n   if both the heading and description match — do not treat a heading match\n   alone as a duplicate.\n3. If the issue is new, append it as a new `###`-level subsection under\n   `## Deferred Issues`, following the existing format: a short descriptive\n   heading, then a concise paragraph explaining the issue and its location.\n4. Write the updated file.\n\nAfter recording, confirm what was deferred and remind the user they can use\n`/book-refine` to turn feedback into policy improvements.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:29.368Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced book review capabilities with Rust language proof-carrying data framework","zh":"适合需要高级书籍审查功能的代码审查代理，特别是使用Rust语言的证明携带数据框架","ja":"Rust言語の証明を携帯したデータフレームワークを使用するコードレビュー代理に適しています","ko":"Rust 언어의 증명 携帶 데이터 프레임워크를 사용하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades de revisión de libros avanzadas con el marco de datos de prueba de lenguaje Rust","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant des capacités de révision de livres avancées avec le cadre de données de preuve de langage Rust","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die erweiterte Buch-Review-Funktionen mit dem Rust-Sprach-Nachweissystem für Daten benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam de capacidades avançadas de revisão de livros com framework de dados de prova de linguagem Rust","ru":"Идеально для агентов код-ревью, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности проверки книг с фреймворком данных языка Rust","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة الكودية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات مراجعة كتاب متقدمة مع إطار بيانات لغة روست"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to review book chapters using Git diff and project policies, leveraging file paths and line numbers to provide detailed feedback, and utilizing Rust for robust data validation and security","zh":"赋予代理审查书籍章节的能力，使用Git diff和项目策略，利用文件路径和行号提供详细的反馈，并利用Rust进行强大的数据验证和安全","ja":"エージェントがGit diffとプロジェクトポリシーを使用して書籍の章をレビューし、ファイルパスと行番号を使用して詳細なフィードバックを提供し、またRustを使用してデータの検証とセキュリティを強化する","ko":"에이전트가 Git diff와 프로젝트 정책을 사용하여 책의 장을 리뷰하고 파일 경로와 줄 번호를 사용하여 상세한 피드백을 제공하며, 또한 Rust를 사용하여 데이터 검증과 보안을 강화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a revisar capítulos de libros utilizando Git diff y políticas de proyecto, aprovechando rutas de archivos y números de línea para proporcionar comentarios detallados, y utilizando Rust para una validación de datos robusta y seguridad","fr":"Permet aux agents de réviser des chapitres de livres en utilisant Git diff et les politiques de projet, en exploitant les chemins de fichiers et les numéros de ligne pour fournir des commentaires détaillés, et en utilisant Rust pour une validation de données robuste et une sécurité","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Buchkapitel mit Git diff und Projekt-Richtlinien zu überprüfen, indem Dateipfade und Zeilennummern genutzt werden, um detaillierte Feedback zu liefern, und Rust für eine robuste Datenvalidierung und Sicherheit zu verwenden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a revisar capítulos de livros usando Git diff e políticas de projeto, aproveitando caminhos de arquivos e números de linhas para fornecer feedback detalhado e utilizando Rust para validação de dados robusta e segurança","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять главы книг с помощью Git diff и политики проекта, используя пути файлов и номера строк для предоставления подробной обратной связи и используя Rust для надежной проверки данных и безопасности","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على مراجعة فصول الكتب باستخدام Git diff وسياسات المشروع، واستخدام مسارات الملفات وأرقام السطور لتوفير ملاحظات مفصلة، واستخدام لغة روست لتأكيد البيانات والأمان"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing uncommitted book chapter changes","Analyzing specific file paths and line numbers for errors","Generating book review reports based on project policies"],"zh":["审查未提交的书籍章节更改","分析特定文件路径和行号以查找错误","根据项目策略生成书籍审查报告"],"ja":["コミットしていない書籍の章の変更をレビューする","特定のファイルパスと行番号を分析してエラーを探す","プロジェクトポリシーに基づいて書籍レビューレポートを生成する"],"ko":["커밋하지 않은 책의 장 변경을 리뷰","특정 파일 경로와 줄 번호를 분석하여 오류를 찾기","프로젝트 정책을 기반으로 책 리뷰 보고서를 생성"],"es":["Revisar cambios de capítulos de libros no comprometidos","Analizar rutas de archivos y números de línea específicos para errores","Generar informes de revisión de libros basados en políticas de proyecto"],"fr":["Réviser les modifications de chapitres de livres non validés","Analyser des chemins de fichiers et des numéros de ligne spécifiques pour les erreurs","Générer des rapports de révision de livres basés sur les politiques de projet"],"de":["Überprüfung nicht committeter Buchkapitel-Änderungen","Analyse spezifischer Dateipfade und Zeilennummern auf Fehler","Erstellung von Buch-Review-Berichten basierend auf Projekt-Richtlinien"],"pt":["Revisar alterações de capítulos de livros não comprometidas","Analisar caminhos de arquivos e números de linhas específicos para erros","Gerar relatórios de revisão de livros com base em políticas de projeto"],"ru":["Проверять не зафиксированные изменения глав книг","Анализировать конкретные пути файлов и номера строк для ошибок","Генерировать отчеты о проверке книг на основе политики проекта"],"ar":["مراجعة تغييرات فصول الكتب غير الملتزمة","تحليل مسارات الملفات وأرقام السطور المحددة لأخطاء","توليد تقارير مراجعة الكتب استنادا إلى سياسات المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to reviewing book chapters in Markdown format","Dependent on project''s book review policies being well-defined"],"zh":["需要Git的安装和配置","仅限于审查Markdown格式的书籍章节","依赖于项目的书籍审查策略被明确定义"],"ja":["Gitのインストールと設定が必要","Markdown形式の書籍の章のみをレビューする","プロジェクトの書籍レビューポリシーが明確に定義されていることを前提とする"],"ko":["Git의 설치와 구성이 필요","마크다운 형식의 책의 장만을 리뷰","프로젝트의 책 리뷰 정책이 명확하게 정의되어 있는 것을 전제"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado a la revisión de capítulos de libros en formato Markdown","Dependiente de que las políticas de revisión de libros del proyecto estén bien definidas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité à la révision de chapitres de livres au format Markdown","Dépendant de ce que les politiques de révision de livres du projet soient bien définies"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Überprüfung von Buchkapiteln im Markdown-Format","Abhängig davon, dass die Buch-Review-Richtlinien des Projekts gut definiert sind"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado à revisão de capítulos de livros no formato Markdown","Dependente das políticas de revisão de livros do projeto estarem bem definidas"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки Git","Ограничен проверкой глав книг в формате Markdown","Зависит от того, что политики проверки книг проекта хорошо определены"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين Git","محدود بمراجعة فصول الكتب بتنسيق Markdown","يعتمد على أن تكون سياسات مراجعة الكتب للمشروع محددة جيدا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":25}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('VilnaCRM-Org/user-service/quality-standards', 'community', 'VilnaCRM-Org', 'user-service', 'VilnaCRM-Org/user-service', 'quality-standards', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:42.453Z', NULL, '{"id":"VilnaCRM-Org/user-service/quality-standards","name":"quality-standards","description":{"zh":"代码质量标准技能旨在帮助开发者理解质量指标，并将问题路由到合适的专门技能","ja":"コード品質標準スキルは、開発者が品質メトリックを理解し、問題を適切な専門スキルにルーティングするのに役立ちます","ko":"코드 품질 표준 스킬은 개발자가 품질 측정 항목을 이해하고, 문제를 적절한 전문 스킬로 라우팅 하는데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Los estándares de calidad son fundamentales para el desarrollo de software. Aprende a entender y aplicar estas normas en tus proyectos","fr":"Les normes de qualité sont essentielles pour le développement de logiciels. Découvrez comment comprendre et appliquer ces normes dans vos projets","de":"Qualitätsstandards sind für die Softwareentwicklung von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Normen in Ihren Projekten anwenden können","pt":"Entenda como aplicar padrões de qualidade em seu código e garantir a entrega de software de alta qualidade","ru":"Узнайте, как применять стандарты качества в вашем коде и обеспечить поставку программного обеспечения высокого качества","ar":"تعرف على كيفية تطبيق معايير الجودة في كودك وضمان تسليم برامجيات ذات جودة عالية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码质量标准技能","ja":"コード品質標準スキル","ko":"코드 품질 표준 스킬","es":"Estándares de Calidad para Desarrolladores","fr":"Normes de Qualité pour les Développeurs","de":"Qualitätsstandards für Entwickler","pt":"Padrões de Qualidade: Entendendo Métricas e Ferramentas","ru":"Стандарты качества: понимание метрик и инструментов","ar":"معايير الجودة: فهم المقاييس والأدوات","en":"quality-standards"},"description":{"zh":"代码质量标准技能旨在帮助开发者理解质量指标，并将问题路由到合适的专门技能","ja":"コード品質標準スキルは、開発者が品質メトリックを理解し、問題を適切な専門スキルにルーティングするのに役立ちます","ko":"코드 품질 표준 스킬은 개발자가 품질 측정 항목을 이해하고, 문제를 적절한 전문 스킬로 라우팅 하는데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Los estándares de calidad son fundamentales para el desarrollo de software. Aprende a entender y aplicar estas normas en tus proyectos","fr":"Les normes de qualité sont essentielles pour le développement de logiciels. Découvrez comment comprendre et appliquer ces normes dans vos projets","de":"Qualitätsstandards sind für die Softwareentwicklung von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Normen in Ihren Projekten anwenden können","pt":"Entenda como aplicar padrões de qualidade em seu código e garantir a entrega de software de alta qualidade","ru":"Узнайте, как применять стандарты качества в вашем коде и обеспечить поставку программного обеспечения высокого качества","ar":"تعرف على كيفية تطبيق معايير الجودة في كودك وضمان تسليم برامجيات ذات جودة عالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["理解质量指标","运行全面质量检查","确定合适的专门技能","快速参考质量工具命令","保护质量阈值"],"ja":["品質メトリックの理解","全面的品質チェックの実行","適切な専門スキルの決定","品質ツールコマンドのクイックリファレンス","品質閾値の保護"],"ko":["품질 측정 항목 이해","포괄적인 품질 검사 실행","적절한 전문 스킬 결정","품질 도구 명령快速 참조","품질 임계값 보호"],"es":["Comprende los umbrales de calidad protegidos","Ejecuta comprobaciones de calidad exhaustivas antes de comprometer","Determina qué habilidad especializada utilizar para problemas específicos","Referencia rápida para comandos de herramientas de calidad"],"fr":["Comprendre les seuils de qualité protégés","Exécuter des vérifications de qualité exhaustives avant de valider","Déterminez quelle compétence spécialisée utiliser pour des problèmes spécifiques","Référence rapide pour les commandes d''outils de qualité"],"de":["Verstehe geschützte Qualitäts-Schwellenwerte","Führe umfassende Qualitätsprüfungen vor dem Commit aus","Bestimme, welche spezialisierte Fähigkeit für bestimmte Probleme verwendet werden soll","Schnellreferenz für Qualitäts-Tool-Befehle"],"pt":["Entendendo métricas de qualidade","Aplicação de padrões de qualidade em código","Uso de ferramentas de qualidade","Determinação de habilidades especializadas para problemas de qualidade","Referência rápida para comandos de ferramentas de qualidade"],"ru":["Понимание метрик качества","Применение стандартов качества в коде","Использование инструментов качества","Определение специализированных навыков для проблем качества","Быстрая справка по командам инструментов качества"],"ar":["فهم مقاييس الجودة","تطبيق معايير الجودة في الكود","استخدام أدوات الجودة","تحديد المهارات المتخصصة لمشاكل الجودة","مرجع سريع لأوامر أدوات الجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码质量标准","质量指标","质量检查","专门技能","质量工具","代码质量"],"ja":["コード品質標準","品質メトリック","品質チェック","専門スキル","品質ツール","コード品質"],"ko":["코드 품질 표준","품질 측정 항목","품질 검사","전문 스킬","품질 도구","코드 품질"],"es":["estándares de calidad","desarrollo de software","calidad del código","pruebas de calidad","herramientas de calidad","mejora de la calidad"],"fr":["normes de qualité","développement de logiciels","qualité du code","tests de qualité","outils de qualité","amélioration de la qualité"],"de":["Qualitätsstandards","Softwareentwicklung","Code-Qualität","Qualitätsprüfungen","Qualitäts-Tools","Qualitätsverbesserung"],"pt":["padrões de qualidade","métricas de qualidade","ferramentas de qualidade","desenvolvimento de software","entrega de software","alta qualidade"],"ru":["стандарты качества","метрики качества","инструменты качества","разработка программного обеспечения","поставка программного обеспечения","высокое качество"],"ar":["معايير الجودة","مقاييس الجودة","أدوات الجودة","تطوير البرمجيات","تسليم البرمجيات","جودة عالية"]}},"owner":"VilnaCRM-Org","repo":"user-service","repoPath":"VilnaCRM-Org/user-service","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"quality-standards","description":"Overview of protected quality thresholds and quick reference for all quality tools. Use when you need to understand quality metrics, run comprehensive quality checks, or learn which specialized skill to use. For specific issues, use dedicated skills (deptrac-fixer for Deptrac, complexity-management for PHPInsights, testing-workflow for coverage).","bodyPreview":"# Quality Standards Skill\n\n## Context (Input)\n\n- Need to understand protected quality thresholds\n- Running comprehensive quality checks before commit\n- Determining which specialized skill to use for specific issues\n- Quick reference for quality tool commands\n\n## Task (Function)\n\nUnderstand quality metrics and route to appropriate specialized skill for fixes.\n\n**Success Criteria**: Know which skill to use for your specific quality issue.\n\n## Protected Quality Thresholds\n\n**CRITICAL**: These thres","body":"# Quality Standards Skill\n\n## Context (Input)\n\n- Need to understand protected quality thresholds\n- Running comprehensive quality checks before commit\n- Determining which specialized skill to use for specific issues\n- Quick reference for quality tool commands\n\n## Task (Function)\n\nUnderstand quality metrics and route to appropriate specialized skill for fixes.\n\n**Success Criteria**: Know which skill to use for your specific quality issue.\n\n## Protected Quality Thresholds\n\n**CRITICAL**: These thresholds are protected and must NEVER be lowered.\n\n### PHPInsights (Source Code)\n\n| Metric       | Required | Fix With                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Quality      | 100%     | [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md) |\n| Complexity   | 94%      | [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md) |\n| Architecture | 100%     | [deptrac-fixer](../deptrac-fixer/SKILL.md)                 |\n| Style        | 100%     | Run `make phpcsfixer`                                      |\n\n### PHPInsights (Tests)\n\n| Metric       | Required | Fix With                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Quality      | 95%      | [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md) |\n| Complexity   | 95%      | [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md) |\n| Architecture | 90%      | [deptrac-fixer](../deptrac-fixer/SKILL.md)                 |\n| Style        | 95%      | Run `make phpcsfixer`                                      |\n\n### Other Tools\n\n| Tool      | Metric          | Required | Fix With                                         |\n| --------- | --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Deptrac   | Violations      | 0        | [deptrac-fixer](../deptrac-fixer/SKILL.md)       |\n| Psalm     | Errors          | 0        | Fix reported issues                              |\n| Psalm     | Security Issues | 0        | Fix tainted flows                                |\n| Infection | MSI             | 100%     | [testing-workflow](../testing-workflow/SKILL.md) |\n| PHPUnit   | Coverage        | 100%     | [testing-workflow](../testing-workflow/SKILL.md) |\n\n## Quick Reference Commands\n\n### Comprehensive Checks\n\n```bash\n# Run all CI checks (recommended before commit)\nmake ci\n```\n\n**Success**: Must output \"✅ CI checks successfully passed!\"\n\n### Individual Quality Checks\n\n| Check               | Command                  | Purpose                      |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| Code quality        | `make phpinsights`       | All PHPInsights metrics      |\n| Complexity analysis | `make phpmd`             | Find high-complexity methods |\n| Static analysis     | `make psalm`             | Type checking and errors     |\n| Security taint      | `make psalm-security`    | Security vulnerability scan  |\n| Architecture        | `make deptrac`           | Layer boundary validation    |\n| Code style          | `make phpcsfixer`        | Auto-fix PSR-12 style        |\n| Composer validation | `make composer-validate` | Validate composer.json       |\n\n### Testing Commands\n\n| Check             | Command                    | Purpose                     |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Unit tests        | `make unit-tests`          | Domain/Application logic    |\n| Integration tests | `make integration-tests`   | Component interactions      |\n| E2E tests         | `make behat`               | Full user scenarios (Behat) |\n| All tests         | `make all-tests`           | Unit + Integration + E2E    |\n| Test coverage     | `make tests-with-coverage` | Generate coverage report    |\n| Mutation tests    | `make infection`           | Test quality validation     |\n\n## Routing to Specialized Skills\n\nWhen quality checks fail, use the appropriate specialized skill:\n\n### Architecture Issues\n\n- **Deptrac violations** → [deptrac-fixer](../deptrac-fixer/SKILL.md)\n\n  - Domain depends on Infrastructure\n  - Layer boundary violations\n  - \"must not depend on\" errors\n\n- **DDD architecture patterns** → [implementing-ddd-architecture](../implementing-ddd-architecture/SKILL.md)\n  - Creating new entities/value objects\n  - Implementing CQRS patterns\n  - Understanding layer responsibilities\n\n### Code Quality Issues\n\n- **High cyclomatic complexity** → [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md)\n\n  - PHPInsights complexity < 94%\n  - PHPMD reports high CCN\n  - Methods too complex\n\n- **Code style issues** → Run `make phpcsfixer`\n  - PSR-12 violations\n  - Line length > 100 chars\n  - Formatting issues\n\n### Testing Issues\n\n- **Test failures** → [testing-workflow](../testing-workflow/SKILL.md)\n  - Unit/Integration/E2E failures\n  - Mutation testing (Infection)\n  - Test coverage < 100%\n\n### Workflow Integration\n\n- **Before committing** → [ci-workflow](../ci-workflow/SKILL.md)\n\n  - Run all checks systematically\n  - Fix failures in priority order\n  - Ensure all checks pass\n\n- **PR review feedback** → [code-review](../code-review/SKILL.md)\n  - Fetch and address PR comments\n  - Systematic comment resolution\n\n## Quality Improvement Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Run Comprehensive Checks\n\n```bash\nmake ci\n```\n\n### Step 2: Identify Failing Check\n\nCheck output for specific failure:\n\n```\n❌ CI checks failed:\n  - phpinsights: Complexity score too low (93.5% < 94%)\n```\n\n### Step 3: Use Specialized Skill\n\nBased on failure type, use appropriate skill:\n\n| Failure Pattern            | Skill to Use             |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| \"Complexity score too low\" | complexity-management    |\n| \"Deptrac violations\"       | deptrac-fixer            |\n| \"must not depend on\"       | deptrac-fixer            |\n| \"tests failed\"             | testing-workflow         |\n| \"Psalm found errors\"       | Fix type errors directly |\n| \"escaped mutants\"          | testing-workflow         |\n\n### Step 4: Re-run CI\n\n```bash\nmake ci\n```\n\nRepeat until: \"✅ CI checks successfully passed!\"\n\n## Constraints (Parameters)\n\n### NEVER\n\n- Lower quality thresholds in config files (`phpinsights.php`, `infection.json5`, etc.)\n- Skip failing checks to \"save time\"\n- Commit code without all CI checks passing\n- Modify `deptrac.yaml` to allow violations (fix code, not config)\n- Disable security checks\n\n### ALWAYS\n\n- Fix code to meet standards (not config to meet code)\n- Run `make ci` before creating commits\n- Use specialized skills for specific quality issues\n- Maintain 100% test coverage\n- Keep cyclomatic complexity low (target: < 5 per method)\n- Respect hexagonal architecture boundaries\n\n## Format (Output)\n\n### Expected CI Output\n\n```\n✅ CI checks successfully passed!\n```\n\n### Expected PHPInsights Output\n\n```\n[CODE] 100.0 pts       ✅ Target: 100%\n[COMPLEXITY] 94.0 pts  ✅ Target: 94%\n[ARCHITECTURE] 100 pts ✅ Target: 100%\n[STYLE] 100.0 pts      ✅ Target: 100%\n```\n\n### Expected Deptrac Output\n\n```\n✅ No violations found\n```\n\n### Expected Infection Output\n\n```\nMutation Score Indicator (MSI): 100%\n```\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nAfter using this skill:\n\n- [ ] Identified which quality check is failing\n- [ ] Selected appropriate specialized skill for the issue\n- [ ] Ready to execute specialized skill workflow\n- [ ] Understand which threshold applies to the failure\n- [ ] Know the command to re-run the check after fixes\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- [ci-workflow](../ci-workflow/SKILL.md) - Run comprehensive CI validation\n- [complexity-management](../complexity-management/SKILL.md) - Reduce complexity, improve quality\n- [deptrac-fixer](../deptrac-fixer/SKILL.md) - Fix architectural violations\n- [implementing-ddd-architecture](../implementing-ddd-architecture/SKILL.md) - Understand DDD patterns\n- [testing-workflow](../testing-workflow/SKILL.md) - Fix test failures, improve coverage\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\nFor detailed examples and patterns, see:\n\n- **Refactoring patterns** → complexity-management skill\n- **Architecture rules** → implementing-ddd-architecture skill\n- **Layer boundaries** → deptrac-fixer skill\n- **Testing strategies** → testing-workflow skill\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:42.453Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents needing advanced quality metrics analysis and threshold management.","zh":"适用于需要高级质量指标分析和阈值管理的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが高度な品質メトリクス分析としきい値管理を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 품질 지표 분석 및 임계값 관리가 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan un análisis de métricas de calidad avanzado y gestión de umbrales.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une analyse de métriques de qualité avancée et une gestion de seuils.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die eine erweiterte Analyse von Qualitätsmetriken und eine Schwellenwertverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise de métricas de qualidade avançadas e gerenciamento de limiares.","ru":"Идеально для агентов проверки кода, требующих расширенного анализа метрик качества и управления порогами.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل متقدم لقياس جودة وادارة العتبات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to understand protected quality thresholds, run comprehensive quality checks, and determine the best specialized skill for specific issues, leveraging quality tool commands and metrics for informed decision-making.","zh":"赋予代理理解受保护的质量阈值、运行全面质量检查和确定特定问题的最佳专用技能的能力，利用质量工具命令和指标进行明智的决策。","ja":"保護された品質しきい値を理解し、包括的な品質チェックを実行し、特定の問題に最適な専門スキルを決定するエージェントを可能にし、品質ツールコマンドとメトリクスを使用して情報に基づいた意思決定を行います。","ko":"보호된 품질 임계값을 이해하고 포괄적인 품질 확인을 실행하며 특정 문제에 가장 적합한 전문 기술을 결정할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 품질 도구 명령과 지표를 사용하여 정보에 기반한 의사 결정을 지원합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes comprender los umbrales de calidad protegidos, ejecutar controles de calidad exhaustivos y determinar la habilidad especializada más adecuada para problemas específicos, utilizando comandos y métricas de herramientas de calidad para la toma de decisiones informadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de comprendre les seuils de qualité protégés, d''exécuter des contrôles de qualité exhaustifs et de déterminer la compétence spécialisée la plus adaptée à des problèmes spécifiques, en utilisant des commandes et des métriques d''outils de qualité pour une prise de décision éclairée.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die geschützten Qualitäts-Schwellenwerte zu verstehen, umfassende Qualitätskontrollen durchzuführen und die am besten geeignete spezialisierte Fähigkeit für bestimmte Probleme zu bestimmen, indem Qualitätstool-Befehle und -Metriken für eine fundierte Entscheidungsfindung genutzt werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes entendam limiares de qualidade protegidos, executem verificações de qualidade abrangentes e determinem a melhor habilidade especializada para questões específicas, utilizando comandos de ferramentas de qualidade e métricas para tomada de decisões informadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью понимать защищенные пороги качества, выполнять комплексные проверки качества и определять лучшую специализированную навык для конкретных проблем, используя команды инструментов качества и метрики для принятия обоснованных решений.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء فهم العتبات المحمية لجودة، وتنفيذ فحص جودة شاملة وتحديد أفضل مهارة متخصصة لمشاكل محددة، باستخدام أوامر أدوات جودة وقياسات لأخذ قرارات مستنيرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating quality checks before code commit","Determining specialized skills for issue resolution","Routing to appropriate fixes based on quality metrics"],"zh":["提交代码前自动执行质量检查","确定问题解决的专用技能","根据质量指标路由到适当的修复"],"ja":["コードコミット前の自動品質チェック","問題解決のための専門スキルの決定","品質メトリクスに基づいた適切な修正へのルーティング"],"ko":["코드 커밋 전 자동 품질 확인","문제 해결을 위한 전문 기술 결정","품질 지표에 따른 적절한 수정으로의 라우팅"],"es":["Automatización de controles de calidad antes del compromiso de código","Determinación de habilidades especializadas para la resolución de problemas","Enrutamiento a soluciones adecuadas en función de las métricas de calidad"],"fr":["Automatisation des contrôles de qualité avant l''engagement du code","Détermination des compétences spécialisées pour la résolution de problèmes","Acheminement vers des correctifs appropriés en fonction des métriques de qualité"],"de":["Automatisierung von Qualitätskontrollen vor dem Code-Commit","Bestimmung von spezialisierten Fähigkeiten für die Problemlösung","Weiterleitung an geeignete Korrekturen basierend auf Qualitätsmetriken"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações de qualidade antes do compromisso de código","Determinar habilidades especializadas para resolução de questões","Encaminhar para correções apropriadas com base em métricas de qualidade"],"ru":["Автоматизация проверок качества перед фиксацией кода","Определение специализированных навыков для решения проблем","Направление к соответствующим исправлениям на основе метрик качества"],"ar":["أتمتة فحص الجودة قبل الالتزام بالشفرة","تحديد المهارات المتخصصة لحل المشاكل","توجيه إلى إصلاحات مناسبة بناءً على مقاييس الجودة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to quality metrics and thresholds","Dependent on specialized skills for issue resolution"],"zh":["需要访问质量指标和阈值","依赖于问题解决的专用技能"],"ja":["品質メトリクスとしきい値へのアクセスが必要","問題解決のための専門スキルに依存"],"ko":["품질 지표 및 임계값에 대한 액세스가 필요","문제 해결을 위한 전문 기술에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a métricas y umbrales de calidad","Depende de habilidades especializadas para la resolución de problemas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux métriques et aux seuils de qualité","Dépend de compétences spécialisées pour la résolution de problèmes"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Qualitätsmetriken und -Schwellenwerte","Hängt von spezialisierten Fähigkeiten für die Problemlösung ab"],"pt":["Requer acesso a métricas e limiares de qualidade","Dependente de habilidades especializadas para resolução de questões"],"ru":["Требует доступа к метрикам и порогам качества","Зависит от специализированных навыков для решения проблем"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مقاييس وعتبات الجودة","يعتمد على مهارات متخصصة لحل المشاكل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('aircrushin/promptMinder/agent-sdk', 'community', 'aircrushin', 'promptMinder', 'aircrushin/promptMinder', 'agent-sdk', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:11.230Z', NULL, '{"id":"aircrushin/promptMinder/agent-sdk","name":"agent-sdk","description":{"zh":"agent-sdk 是一个开源的提示词管理平台，提供了丰富的功能和配置选项，帮助开发者提高提示词管理能力","ja":"agent-sdk はオープンソースのプロンプト管理プラットフォームであり、豊富な機能と設定オプションを提供して、開発者のプロンプト管理能力を向上させます","ko":"agent-sdk는 오픈소스의 프롬프트 관리 플랫폼으로, 풍부한 기능과 설정 옵션을 제공하여 개발자의 프롬프트 관리 능력을 향상시킵니다","es":"El SDK de Agente es una plataforma de código abierto para la gestión de prompts. Ofrece funciones como query, tool y createSdkMcpServer.","fr":"Le SDK d''Agent est une plate-forme open source pour la gestion de prompts. Il propose des fonctions telles que query, tool et createSdkMcpServer.","de":"Das Agent-SDK ist eine Open-Source-Plattform für Prompt-Management. Es bietet Funktionen wie query, tool und createSdkMcpServer.","pt":"O SDK de Agente é uma plataforma de código aberto para gerenciamento de prompts, oferecendo funcionalidades avançadas para desenvolvedores.","ru":"Agent SDK — это открытая платформа для управления подсказками, предлагающая расширенные функции для разработчиков.","ar":"SDK للوكيل هي منصة مفتوحة المصدر لإدارة النصائح، توفر ميزات متقدمة للمطورين.","en":"一个开源的，专注于提示词管理的平台 / An open-source platform focused on prompt management"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"agent-sdk 开源平台：提示词管理专家","ja":"agent-sdk オープンソースプラットフォーム：プロンプト管理の専門家","ko":"agent-sdk 오픈소스 플랫폼: 프롬프트 관리 전문가","es":"SDK de Agente: Gestión de Prompts de Código Abierto","fr":"SDK d''Agent: Plate-forme de Gestion de Prompts Open Source","de":"Agent-SDK: Open-Source-Plattform für Prompt-Management","pt":"SDK de Agente: Plataforma de Gerenciamento de Prompt","ru":"Agent SDK: Платформа управления подсказками","ar":"SDK للوكيل: منصة إدارة النصائح","en":"agent-sdk"},"description":{"zh":"agent-sdk 是一个开源的提示词管理平台，提供了丰富的功能和配置选项，帮助开发者提高提示词管理能力","ja":"agent-sdk はオープンソースのプロンプト管理プラットフォームであり、豊富な機能と設定オプションを提供して、開発者のプロンプト管理能力を向上させます","ko":"agent-sdk는 오픈소스의 프롬프트 관리 플랫폼으로, 풍부한 기능과 설정 옵션을 제공하여 개발자의 프롬프트 관리 능력을 향상시킵니다","es":"El SDK de Agente es una plataforma de código abierto para la gestión de prompts. Ofrece funciones como query, tool y createSdkMcpServer.","fr":"Le SDK d''Agent est une plate-forme open source pour la gestion de prompts. Il propose des fonctions telles que query, tool et createSdkMcpServer.","de":"Das Agent-SDK ist eine Open-Source-Plattform für Prompt-Management. Es bietet Funktionen wie query, tool und createSdkMcpServer.","pt":"O SDK de Agente é uma plataforma de código aberto para gerenciamento de prompts, oferecendo funcionalidades avançadas para desenvolvedores.","ru":"Agent SDK — это открытая платформа для управления подсказками, предлагающая расширенные функции для разработчиков.","ar":"SDK للوكيل هي منصة مفتوحة المصدر لإدارة النصائح، توفر ميزات متقدمة للمطورين.","en":"一个开源的，专注于提示词管理的平台 / An open-source platform focused on prompt management"},"definition":{"en":"一个开源的，专注于提示词管理的平台 / An open-source platform focused on prompt management"},"features":{"zh":["核心 SDK 函数：query()、tool()、createSdkMcpServer()","配置选项和用例","代理定义和子代理模式","工具输入/输出类型","MCP 服务器配置"],"ja":["コア SDK 関数：query()、tool()、createSdkMcpServer()","設定オプションと用例","エージェント定義とサブエージェントパターン","ツール入力/出力タイプ","MCP サーバー設定"],"ko":["코어 SDK 함수：query()、tool()、createSdkMcpServer()","설정 옵션과 사용 사례","에이전트 정의와 서브 에이전트 패턴","도구 입력/출력 유형","MCP 서버 설정"],"es":["Funciones de consulta y herramientas","Configuraciones de servidor MCP","Definiciones de agentes y patrones de subagentes","Tipos de entrada y salida de herramientas","Compatibilidad con TypeScript"],"fr":["Fonctions de requête et d''outils","Configurations de serveur MCP","Définitions d''agents et modèles de sous-agents","Types d''entrée et de sortie d''outils","Compatibilité avec TypeScript"],"de":["Abfrage- und Werkzeugfunktionen","MCP-Server-Konfigurationen","Agenten-Definitionen und Subagenten-Muster","Eingabe- und Ausgabetypen für Werkzeuge","Kompatibilität mit TypeScript"],"pt":["Funções principais do SDK: query(), tool(), createSdkMcpServer()","Opções de configuração e casos de uso","Definições de agentes e padrões de subagentes","Tipos de entrada/saída de ferramentas para todas as ferramentas integradas","Configurações do servidor MCP: stdio, SSE, HTTP, SDK"],"ru":["Основные функции SDK: query(), tool(), createSdkMcpServer()","Варианты конфигурации и их применения","Определения агентов и шаблоны субагентов","Типы входных/выходных данных инструментов для всех встроенных инструментов","Конфигурации сервера MCP: stdio, SSE, HTTP, SDK"],"ar":["الوظائف الأساسية للSDK: query(), tool(), createSdkMcpServer()","خيارات التكوين وحالات الاستخدام","تعريفات الوكيل وأنماط الفرع","أنواع الإدخال/الإخراج للأدوات لجميع الأدوات المدمجة","تكوينات خادم MCP: stdio, SSE, HTTP, SDK"]},"keywords":{"zh":["agent-sdk","提示词管理","TypeScript SDK API","最佳实践","开源平台","核心 SDK 函数","配置选项","代理定义","MCP 服务器配置"],"ja":["agent-sdk","プロンプト管理","TypeScript SDK API","ベストプラクティス","オープンソースプラットフォーム","コア SDK 関数","設定オプション","エージェント定義","MCP サーバー設定"],"ko":["agent-sdk","프롬프트 관리","TypeScript SDK API","최적의 관행","오픈소스 플랫폼","코어 SDK 함수","설정 옵션","에이전트 정의","MCP 서버 설정"],"es":["SDK de Agente","Gestión de prompts","Desarrollo de aplicaciones","TypeScript","MCP","Agentes","Subagentes","Herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["SDK d''Agent","Gestion de prompts","Développement d''applications","TypeScript","MCP","Agents","Sous-agents","Outils de développement"],"de":["Agent-SDK","Prompt-Management","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","TypeScript","MCP","Agenten","Subagenten","Entwicklertools"],"pt":["SDK de Agente","gerenciamento de prompts","desenvolvimento de software","plataforma de código aberto","Agent SDK","TypeScript SDK API"],"ru":["Agent SDK","управление подсказками","разработка программного обеспечения","открытая платформа","SDK для агентов","TypeScript SDK API"],"ar":["SDK للوكيل","إدارة النصائح","تطوير البرمجيات","منصة مفتوحة المصدر","SDK للوكيل","TypeScript SDK API"]}},"owner":"aircrushin","repo":"promptMinder","repoPath":"aircrushin/promptMinder","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-sdk","description":"Expert in Claude Agent SDK development. Use when users ask about SDK API, agent configuration, MCP servers, hooks, permissions, file checkpointing, or when they mention @AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md. Provides accurate API reference, code examples with TypeScript types, and best practices.","bodyPreview":"You are a Claude Agent SDK expert with deep knowledge of the TypeScript SDK API, architecture, and best practices.\n\n## Your Expertise\n\n- Core SDK functions: `query()`, `tool()`, `createSdkMcpServer()`\n- Configuration options and their use cases (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:90-133)\n- Agent definitions and subagent patterns (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:166-185)\n- Tool input/output types for all built-in tools (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:819-1816)\n- MCP server configurations: stdio, SSE, HTTP, SDK (see AGENT_SDK_DO","body":"You are a Claude Agent SDK expert with deep knowledge of the TypeScript SDK API, architecture, and best practices.\n\n## Your Expertise\n\n- Core SDK functions: `query()`, `tool()`, `createSdkMcpServer()`\n- Configuration options and their use cases (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:90-133)\n- Agent definitions and subagent patterns (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:166-185)\n- Tool input/output types for all built-in tools (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:819-1816)\n- MCP server configurations: stdio, SSE, HTTP, SDK (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:323-374)\n- Hook events and callback patterns (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:571-817)\n- Permission modes and custom authorization (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:280-322)\n- File checkpointing and rewind functionality (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:134-165)\n- Session management and resumption (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:104-127)\n- Structured outputs with JSON schemas (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:120)\n- Sandbox configuration and security (see AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:2025-2167)\n\n## When Answering Questions\n\n1. **Be Accurate**: Base all answers on AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md. Reference specific sections with file paths and line numbers (e.g., \"See AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:90-133\")\n\n2. **Include Code Examples**: Always provide TypeScript examples with proper types:\n   ```typescript\n   import { query } from \"@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk\";\n\n   const result = await query({\n     prompt: \"Analyze this code\",\n     options: {\n       model: \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n       permissionMode: \"bypassPermissions\"\n     }\n   });\n   ```\n\n3. **Explain Trade-offs**: When multiple approaches exist, explain the pros and cons of each:\n   - \"Using `settingSources: [''project'']` loads only team settings, while `[''user'', ''project'', ''local'']` loads all settings with precedence rules\"\n   - \"Stream mode with AsyncIterable<SDKUserMessage> enables interactive features but requires managing the async generator\"\n\n4. **Suggest Best Practices**:\n   - Use `settingSources: [''project'']` in CI/CD for consistency\n   - Enable `enableFileCheckpointing: true` when you might need to undo changes\n   - Define agents programmatically for SDK-only applications\n   - Use hooks for cross-cutting concerns like logging, telemetry, or custom permissions\n\n5. **Warn About Security**:\n   - `permissionMode: ''bypassPermissions''` requires `allowDangerfullySkipPermissions: true`\n   - Sandbox exclusions (`excludedCommands`) bypass all restrictions automatically\n   - `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` requires careful `canUseTool` validation\n   - Never commit secrets or credentials\n\n6. **Keep It Concise but Thorough**: Provide complete information but avoid verbosity. Focus on what the user needs to know.\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Basic Query\n```typescript\nimport { query } from \"@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk\";\n\nfor await (const message of query({ prompt: \"Hello!\" })) {\n  console.log(message);\n}\n```\n\n### With Streaming Input\n```typescript\nimport { query } from \"@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk\";\n\nasync function* userInput() {\n  yield { type: ''user'', content: ''Step 1'' };\n  // ... some logic ...\n  yield { type: ''user'', content: ''Step 2'' };\n}\n\nconst q = query({\n  prompt: userInput(),\n  options: { includePartialMessages: true }\n});\n\nfor await (const msg of q) {\n  console.log(msg);\n}\n```\n\n### Custom MCP Tool\n```typescript\nimport { tool, createSdkMcpServer } from \"@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst myTool = tool(\n  \"my-tool\",\n  \"Does something useful\",\n  {\n    param1: z.string(),\n    param2: z.number().optional()\n  },\n  async (args, extra) => {\n    return {\n      content: [{ type: \"text\", text: `Result: ${args.param1}` }]\n    };\n  }\n);\n\nconst server = createSdkMcpServer({\n  name: \"my-server\",\n  tools: [myTool]\n});\n```\n\n### Permission Hook\n```typescript\nconst result = query({\n  prompt: \"Make changes\",\n  options: {\n    hooks: {\n      PreToolUse: [{\n        hooks: [async (input) => {\n          if (input.tool_name === \"Write\" && input.tool_input.file_path.endsWith(\".env\")) {\n            return { decision: ''block'', reason: \"Cannot write to .env files\" };\n          }\n          return { decision: ''approve'' };\n        }]\n      }]\n    }\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Key Documentation Sections\n\n| Topic | Location |\n|-------|----------|\n| Installation | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:13-17 |\n| query() Function | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:21-45 |\n| Options Reference | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:90-133 |\n| Agent Definition | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:166-185 |\n| Setting Sources | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:186-279 |\n| Permission Modes | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:280-288 |\n| MCP Server Configs | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:323-374 |\n| Hook Events | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:575-593 |\n| Tool Input Types | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:819-1278 |\n| Tool Output Types | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:1279-1816 |\n| Sandbox Settings | AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:2025-2167 |\n\n## When Uncertain\n\nIf you''re not 100% sure about an answer:\n1. Say \"Let me check the documentation\"\n2. Read AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md using the Read tool\n3. Provide the specific reference (e.g., \"According to AGENT_SDK_DOCS.md:90-133...\")\n4. Never make up API details or assume behavior\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:11.230Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced prompt management and customization, such as Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain.","zh":"适用于需要高级提示管理和自定义的AI代理，例如Claude、AutoGPT和LangChain。","ja":"Claude、AutoGPT、LangChainなどの高度なプロンプト管理とカスタマイズを必要とするAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"Claude, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 고급 프롬프트 관리 및 사용자 정의가 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que requieren una gestión de solicitudes avanzada y personalización, como Claude, AutoGPT y LangChain.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant une gestion de requêtes avancée et une personnalisation, tels que Claude, AutoGPT et LangChain.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die eine erweiterte Promptverwaltung und Anpassung benötigen, wie Claude, AutoGPT und LangChain.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que requerem gerenciamento de prompts avançado e personalização, como Claude, AutoGPT e LangChain.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, требующих продвинутого управления промптами и настройки, таких как Claude, AutoGPT и LangChain.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يتطلبون إدارة مسبقة متقدمة وتخصيص، مثل Claude و AutoGPT و LangChain."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage the TypeScript SDK API for fine-tuned control over prompt management, utilizing core functions like `query()`, `tool()`, and `createSdkMcpServer()` to optimize agent performance and efficiency through standardized MCP server configurations and tool input/output types.","zh":"赋予代理使用TypeScript SDK API实现对提示管理的细粒度控制，利用诸如`query()`、`tool()`和`createSdkMcpServer()`等核心函数，通过标准化的MCP服务器配置和工具输入/输出类型优化代理性能和效率。","ja":"エージェントがTypeScript SDK APIを使用してプロンプト管理を微調整することを可能にし、`query()`、`tool()`、`createSdkMcpServer()`などのコア関数を使用して、標準化されたMCPサーバー構成とツールの入出力タイプを通じてエージェントのパフォーマンスと効率を最適化します。","ko":"에이전트가 TypeScript SDK API를 사용하여 프롬프트 관리를 세부적으로 제어할 수 있도록 하여 `query()`、`tool()` 및 `createSdkMcpServer()`와 같은 핵심 함수를 사용하여 표준화된 MCP 서버 구성 및 도구 입력/출력 유형을 통해 에이전트 성능 및 효율성을 최적화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar el API de SDK de TypeScript para un control afinado sobre la gestión de solicitudes, utilizando funciones principales como `query()`, `tool()` y `createSdkMcpServer()` para optimizar el rendimiento y la eficiencia del agente a través de configuraciones de servidor MCP estandarizadas y tipos de entrada/salida de herramientas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter l''API SDK TypeScript pour un contrôle affiné de la gestion des requêtes, en utilisant des fonctions principales comme `query()`, `tool()` et `createSdkMcpServer()` pour optimiser les performances et l''efficacité de l''agent via des configurations de serveur MCP standardisées et des types d''entrée/sortie d''outils.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die TypeScript-SDK-API für eine fein abgestimmte Steuerung der Promptverwaltung zu nutzen, indem sie Kernfunktionen wie `query()`, `tool()` und `createSdkMcpServer()` verwenden, um die Leistung und Effizienz des Agents durch standardisierte MCP-Serverkonfigurationen und Tool-Eingabe/Ausgabetypen zu optimieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a utilizarem a API do SDK do TypeScript para controle refinado sobre o gerenciamento de prompts, utilizando funções principais como `query()`, `tool()` e `createSdkMcpServer()` para otimizar o desempenho e a eficiência do agente por meio de configurações de servidor MCP padrão e tipos de entrada/saída de ferramentas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать API SDK TypeScript для тонкого управления управлением промптами, используя основные функции như `query()`, `tool()` и `createSdkMcpServer()`, чтобы оптимизировать производительность и эффективность агента за счет стандартизированных конфигураций сервера MCP и типов ввода/вывода инструментов.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من استخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات SDK TypeScript للسيطرة الدقيقة على إدارة المسبقة، باستخدام الوظائف الأساسية مثل `query()` و `tool()` و `createSdkMcpServer()` لتحسين أداء وكيل الفعالية من خلال تكوينات خادم MCP معيارية وأنواع إخراج أداة الإدخال."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring agent definitions and subagent patterns for complex tasks","Managing tool input/output types for seamless integration with built-in tools","Optimizing MCP server configurations for enhanced performance and scalability"],"zh":["为复杂任务配置代理定义和子代理模式","管理工具输入/输出类型以实现与内置工具的无缝集成","优化MCP服务器配置以提高性能和可扩展性"],"ja":["複雑なタスクのエージェント定義とサブエージェントパターンの構成","ツール入出力タイプの管理によるビルトインツールとのシームレスな統合","パフォーマンスとスケーラビリティの向上のためのMCPサーバー構成の最適化"],"ko":["복잡한 작업을 위한 에이전트 정의 및 하위 에이전트 패턴 구성","내장 도구와의无缝 통합을 위한 도구 입력/출력 유형 관리","성능 및 확장성 향상을 위한 MCP 서버 구성 최적화"],"es":["Configuración de definiciones de agentes y patrones de subagentes para tareas complejas","Gestión de tipos de entrada/salida de herramientas para una integración sin problemas con herramientas integradas","Optimización de configuraciones de servidor MCP para un mejor rendimiento y escalabilidad"],"fr":["Configuration des définitions d''agents et des modèles de sous-agents pour des tâches complexes","Gestion des types d''entrée/sortie d''outils pour une intégration sans problème avec les outils intégrés","Optimisation des configurations de serveur MCP pour de meilleures performances et une meilleure évolutivité"],"de":["Konfiguration von Agentendefinitionen und Subagentenmustern für komplexe Aufgaben","Verwaltung von Tool-Eingabe/Ausgabetypen für eine nahtlose Integration mit integrierten Tools","Optimierung von MCP-Serverkonfigurationen für eine verbesserte Leistung und Skalierbarkeit"],"pt":["Configurando definições de agente e padrões de subagente para tarefas complexas","Gerenciando tipos de entrada/saída de ferramentas para integração sem problemas com ferramentas incorporadas","Otimizando configurações de servidor MCP para desempenho e escalabilidade aprimorados"],"ru":["Настройка определений агентов и шаблонов субагентов для сложных задач","Управление типами ввода/вывода инструментов для бесперебойной интеграции с встроенными инструментами","Оптимизация конфигураций сервера MCP для повышения производительности и масштабируемости"],"ar":["تكوين تعريفات الوكيل وأنماط الفرع لعمليات معقدة","إدارة أنواع الإدخال والإخراج للأدوات لتكامل بدون مشاكل مع الأدوات المدمجة","تحسين تكوينات خادم MCP لأداء وتمكين متقدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of TypeScript SDK API and architecture","Limited to agents compatible with the agent-sdk platform"],"zh":["需要TypeScript SDK API和体系结构的知识","仅限与agent-sdk平台兼容的代理"],"ja":["TypeScript SDK APIとアーキテクチャの知識が必要","agent-sdkプラットフォームと互換性のあるエージェントのみ"],"ko":["TypeScript SDK API 및 아키텍처에 대한 지식이 필요","에이전트-SDK 플랫폼과 호환되는 에이전트만 해당"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del API de SDK de TypeScript y arquitectura","Limitado a agentes compatibles con la plataforma agent-sdk"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance de l''API SDK TypeScript et de l''architecture","Limité aux agents compatibles avec la plateforme agent-sdk"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der TypeScript-SDK-API und Architektur","Begrenzt auf Agents, die mit der agent-sdk-Plattform kompatibel sind"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento da API do SDK do TypeScript e arquitetura","Limitado a agentes compatíveis com a plataforma agent-sdk"],"ru":["Требует знания API SDK TypeScript и архитектуры","Ограничен агентами, совместимыми с платформой agent-sdk"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة واجهة برمجة تطبيقات SDK TypeScript والهيكل","محدود بالوكلاء المتوافقة مع منصة الوكيل-SDK"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
