ilidades de Comunicação em Tempo Real","ru":"Создание навыков для коммуникации в реальном времени","ar":"إنشاء مهارات التواصل في الوقت الفعلي","en":"creating-skills"},"description":{"zh":"创建技能是为了实现实时智能代理间高效通信，提供快速可行的解决方案","ja":"スキルの作成は、リアルタイムエージェント間の効率的なコミュニケーションを実現するための方法","ko":"스킬 생성은 실시간 에이전트 간의 효율적인 통신을 구현하기 위한 방법","es":"Las habilidades son guías de referencia para técnicas, patrones o herramientas probadas. Ayudan a futuras instancias de Claude a encontrar y aplicar enfoques...","fr":"Les compétences sont des guides de référence pour des techniques, des modèles ou des outils éprouvés. Ils aident les futures instances de Claude à trouver et...","de":"Fähigkeiten sind Referenzleitfäden für bewährte Techniken, Muster oder Tools. Sie helfen zukünftigen Claude-Instanzen, effektive Ansätze zu finden und anzuwe...","pt":"As habilidades são guias de referência para técnicas, padrões ou ferramentas comprovadas, projetadas para ajudar futuras instâncias do Claude a encontrar e a...","ru":"Навыки являются справочными руководствами для проверенных техник, шаблонов или инструментов, предназначенных для помощи будущим экземплярам Claude в поиске и...","ar":"المهارات هي أدلة مرجعية لتقنيات ونمطيات وأدوات موثوقة، مصممة لمساعدة مثيلات كلود المستقبلية على العثور على نهج فعال وتطبيقه","en":"Real-time agent to agent communication"},"definition":{"en":"Real-time agent to agent communication"},"features":{"zh":["实时通信","智能代理","快速发现","可行解决方案","高效通信"],"ja":["リアルタイム通信","スマートエージェント","迅速な発見","実行可能なソリューション","効率的なコミュニケーション"],"ko":["실시간 통신","스마트 에이전트","빠른 발견","실행 가능한 솔루션","효율적인 통신"],"es":["Comunicación en tiempo real","Guías de referencia para técnicas probadas","Descubrimiento y evaluación rápidos","Ejemplos claros y acciónables","Principio de asunción de inteligencia preexistente"],"fr":["Communication en temps réel","Guides de référence pour des techniques éprouvées","Découverte et évaluation rapides","Exemples clairs et actionables","Principe d''hypothèse d''intelligence préexistante"],"de":["Echtzeitkommunikation","Referenzleitfäden für bewährte Techniken","Schnelles Entdecken und Bewerten","Klare und handhabbare Beispiele","Prinzip der Annahme von vorheriger Intelligenz"],"pt":["Comunicação em tempo real entre agentes","Técnicas comprovadas para melhorar a eficiência","Guias de referência para futuras instâncias do Claude","Abordagens eficazes para tomada de decisões","Descoberta e aplicação rápida de soluções","Flexibilidade e escalabilidade para diferentes cenários"],"ru":["Коммуникация в реальном времени между агентами","Проверенные техники для повышения эффективности","Справочники для будущих экземпляров Claude","Эффективные подходы для принятия решений","Быстрое обнаружение и применение решений","Гибкость и масштабируемость для различных сценариев"],"ar":["التواصل في الوقت الفعلي بين الوكلاء","تقنيات موثوقة لتحسين الكفاءة","أدلة مرجعية لمثيلات كلود المستقبلية","نهج فعالة لصنع القرار","اكتشاف وتطبيق سريع للحلول","المرونة والتوسعة لسيناريوهات مختلفة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["智能代理","实时通信","创建技能","高效通信","快速发现","可行解决方案","实时智能代理间通信"],"ja":["スマートエージェント","リアルタイム通信","スキルの作成","効率的なコミュニケーション","迅速な発見","実行可能なソリューション","リアルタイムエージェント間のコミュニケーション"],"ko":["스마트 에이전트","실시간 통신","스킬 생성","효율적인 통신","빠른 발견","실행 가능한 솔루션","실시간 에이전트 간의 통신"],"es":["creación de habilidades","comunicación en tiempo real","guías de referencia","técnicas probadas","desarrollo de agentes","inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["création de compétences","communication en temps réel","guides de référence","techniques éprouvées","développement d''agents","intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","Echtzeitkommunikation","Referenzleitfäden","bewährte Techniken","Entwicklung von Agenten","künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["comunicação em tempo real","habilidades de agente","técnicas comprovadas","eficiência","tomada de decisões","desenvolvimento de habilidades","guias de referência","comunicação entre agentes"],"ru":["коммуникация в реальном времени","навыки агента","проверенные техники","эффективность","принятие решений","разработка навыков","справочники","коммуникация между агентами"],"ar":["التواصل في الوقت الفعلي","مهارات الوكيل","تقنيات موثوقة","الكفاءة","صنع القرار","تطوير المهارات","أدلة مرجعية","التواصل بين الوكلاء"]}},"owner":"AgentWorkforce","repo":"relay","repoPath":"AgentWorkforce/relay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.403Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"creating-skills","description":"Use when creating new Claude Code skills or improving existing ones - ensures skills are discoverable, scannable, and effective through proper structure, CSO optimization, and real examples","bodyPreview":"# Creating Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Skills are reference guides for proven techniques, patterns, or tools.** Write them to help future Claude instances quickly find and apply effective approaches.\n\nSkills must be **discoverable** (Claude can find them), **scannable** (quick to evaluate), and **actionable** (clear examples).\n\n**Core principle**: Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Create a skill when:**\n- Technique was","body":"# Creating Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Skills are reference guides for proven techniques, patterns, or tools.** Write them to help future Claude instances quickly find and apply effective approaches.\n\nSkills must be **discoverable** (Claude can find them), **scannable** (quick to evaluate), and **actionable** (clear examples).\n\n**Core principle**: Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Create a skill when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious\n- Pattern applies broadly across projects\n- You''d reference this again\n- Others would benefit\n\n**Don''t create for:**\n- One-off solutions specific to single project\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project conventions (put those in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`)\n\n## Required Structure\n\n### Frontmatter (YAML)\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: skill-name-with-hyphens\ndescription: Use when [triggers/symptoms] - [what it does and how it helps]\ntags: relevant-tags\n---\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n- Only `name` and `description` fields supported (max 1024 chars total)\n- Name: letters, numbers, hyphens only (max 64 chars). Use gerund form (verb + -ing)\n- Avoid reserved words: \"anthropic\", \"claude\" in names\n- Description: Third person, starts with \"Use when...\" (max 1024 chars)\n- Include BOTH triggering conditions AND what skill does\n- Match specificity to task complexity (degrees of freedom)\n\n### Document Structure\n\n```markdown\n# Skill Name\n\n## Overview\nCore principle in 1-2 sentences. What is this?\n\n## When to Use\n- Bullet list with symptoms and use cases\n- When NOT to use\n\n## Quick Reference\nTable or bullets for common operations\n\n## Implementation\nInline code for simple patterns\nLink to separate file for heavy reference (100+ lines)\n\n## Common Mistakes\nWhat goes wrong + how to fix\n\n## Real-World Impact (optional)\nConcrete results from using this technique\n```\n\n## Degrees of Freedom\n\n**Match specificity to task complexity:**\n\n- **High freedom**: Flexible tasks requiring judgment\n  - Use broad guidance, principles, examples\n  - Let Claude adapt approach to context\n  - Example: \"Use when designing APIs - provides REST principles and patterns\"\n\n- **Low freedom**: Fragile or critical operations\n  - Be explicit about exact steps\n  - Include validation checks\n  - Example: \"Use when deploying to production - follow exact deployment checklist with rollback procedures\"\n\n**Red flag**: If skill tries to constrain Claude too much on creative tasks, reduce specificity. If skill is too vague on critical operations, add explicit steps.\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n**Critical:** Future Claude reads the description to decide if skill is relevant. Optimize for discovery.\n\n### Description Best Practices\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD - Too vague, doesn''t mention when to use\ndescription: For async testing\n\n# ❌ BAD - First person (injected into system prompt)\ndescription: I help you with flaky tests\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Triggers + what it does\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions or pass/fail inconsistently - replaces arbitrary timeouts with condition polling for reliable async tests\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Technology-specific with explicit trigger\ndescription: Use when using React Router and handling auth redirects - provides patterns for protected routes and auth state management\n```\n\n### Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- **Error messages**: \"ENOENT\", \"Cannot read property\", \"Timeout\"\n- **Symptoms**: \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"race condition\", \"memory leak\"\n- **Synonyms**: \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\", \"timeout/hang/freeze\"\n- **Tools**: Actual command names, library names, file types\n\n### Naming Conventions\n\n**Use gerund form (verb + -ing):**\n- ✅ `creating-skills` not `skill-creation`\n- ✅ `testing-with-subagents` not `subagent-testing`\n- ✅ `debugging-memory-leaks` not `memory-leak-debugging`\n- ✅ `processing-pdfs` not `pdf-processor`\n- ✅ `analyzing-spreadsheets` not `spreadsheet-analysis`\n\n**Why gerunds work:**\n- Describes the action you''re taking\n- Active and clear\n- Consistent with Anthropic conventions\n\n**Avoid:**\n- ❌ Vague names like \"Helper\" or \"Utils\"\n- ❌ Passive voice constructions\n\n## Code Examples\n\n**One excellent example beats many mediocre ones.**\n\n### Choose Language by Use Case\n\n- Testing techniques → TypeScript/JavaScript\n- System debugging → Shell/Python\n- Data processing → Python\n- API calls → TypeScript/JavaScript\n\n### Good Example Checklist\n\n- [ ] Complete and runnable\n- [ ] Well-commented explaining **WHY** not just what\n- [ ] From real scenario (not contrived)\n- [ ] Shows pattern clearly\n- [ ] Ready to adapt (not generic template)\n- [ ] Shows both BAD (❌) and GOOD (✅) approaches\n- [ ] Includes realistic context/setup code\n\n### Example Template\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ GOOD - Clear, complete, ready to adapt\ninterface RetryOptions {\n  maxAttempts: number;\n  delayMs: number;\n  backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n}\n\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: RetryOptions\n): Promise<T> {\n  const { maxAttempts, delayMs, backoff = ''linear'' } = options;\n\n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (attempt === maxAttempts) throw error;\n\n      const delay = backoff === ''exponential''\n        ? delayMs * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1)\n        : delayMs * attempt;\n\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(''Unreachable'');\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst data = await retryOperation(\n  () => fetchUserData(userId),\n  { maxAttempts: 3, delayMs: 1000, backoff: ''exponential'' }\n);\n```\n\n### Don''t\n\n- ❌ Implement in 5+ languages (you''re good at porting)\n- ❌ Create fill-in-the-blank templates\n- ❌ Write contrived examples\n- ❌ Show only code without comments\n\n## File Organization\n\n### Self-Contained (Preferred)\n\n```\ntypescript-type-safety/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\n\n**When:** All content fits in ~500 words, no heavy reference needed\n\n### With Supporting Files\n\n```\napi-integration/\n  SKILL.md           # Overview + patterns\n  retry-helpers.ts   # Reusable code\n  examples/\n    auth-example.ts\n    pagination-example.ts\n```\n\n**When:** Reusable tools or multiple complete examples needed\n\n### With Heavy Reference\n\n```\naws-sdk/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  s3-api.md      # 600 lines API reference\n  lambda-api.md  # 500 lines API reference\n```\n\n**When:** Reference material > 100 lines\n\n## Token Efficiency\n\nSkills load into every conversation. Keep them concise.\n\n### Target Limits\n\n- **SKILL.md**: Keep under 500 lines\n- Getting-started workflows: <150 words\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words total\n- Other skills: <500 words\n- Files > 100 lines: Include table of contents\n\n**Challenge each piece of information**: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\"\n\n### Compression Techniques\n\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD - Verbose (42 words)\nYour human partner asks: \"How did we handle authentication errors in React Router before?\"\nYou should respond: \"I''ll search past conversations for React Router authentication patterns.\"\nThen dispatch a subagent with the search query: \"React Router authentication error handling 401\"\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Concise (20 words)\nPartner: \"How did we handle auth errors in React Router?\"\nYou: Searching...\n[Dispatch subagent → synthesis]\n```\n\n**Techniques:**\n- Reference tool `--help` instead of documenting all flags\n- Cross-reference other skills instead of repeating content\n- Show minimal example of pattern\n- Eliminate redundancy\n- Use progressive disclosure (reference additional files as needed)\n- Organize content by domain for focused context\n\n## Workflow Recommendations\n\nFor multi-step processes, include:\n\n1. **Clear sequential steps**: Break complex tasks into numbered operations\n2. **Feedback loops**: Build in verification/validation steps\n3. **Error handling**: What to check when things go wrong\n4. **Checklists**: For processes with many steps or easy-to-miss details\n\n**Example structure:**\n```markdown\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Preparation**\n   - Check prerequisites\n   - Validate environment\n\n2. **Execution**\n   - Step 1: [action + expected result]\n   - Step 2: [action + expected result]\n\n3. **Verification**\n   - [ ] Check 1 passes\n   - [ ] Check 2 passes\n\n4. **Rollback** (if needed)\n   - Steps to undo changes\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Why It Fails | Fix |\n|---------|--------------|-----|\n| Narrative example | \"In session 2025-10-03...\" | Focus on reusable pattern |\n| Multi-language dilution | Same example in 5 languages | One excellent example |\n| Code in flowcharts | `step1 [label=\"import fs\"]` | Use markdown code blocks |\n| Generic labels | helper1, helper2, step3 | Use semantic names |\n| Missing description triggers | \"For testing\" | \"Use when tests are flaky...\" |\n| First-person description | \"I help you...\" | \"Use when... - provides...\" |\n| Deeply nested file references | Multiple @ symbols, complex paths | Keep references simple and direct |\n| Windows-style file paths | `C:\\path\\to\\file` | Use forward slashes |\n| Offering too many options | 10 different approaches | Focus on one proven approach |\n| Punting error handling | \"Claude figures it out\" | Include explicit error handling in scripts |\n| Time-sensitive information | \"As of 2025...\" | Keep content evergreen |\n| Inconsistent terminology | Mixing synonyms randomly | Use consistent terms throughout |\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\n**Only use flowcharts for:**\n- Non-obvious decision points\n- Process loops where you might stop too early\n- \"When to use A vs B\" decisions\n\n**Never use for:**\n- Reference material → Use tables/lists\n- Code examples → Use markdown blocks\n- Linear instructions → Use numbered lists\n\n## Cross-Referencing Skills\n\n```markdown\n# ✅ GOOD - Name only with clear requirement\n**REQUIRED:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development before proceeding\n\n**RECOMMENDED:** See typescript-type-safety for proper type guards\n\n# ❌ BAD - Unclear if required\nSee skills/testing/test-driven-development\n\n# ❌ BAD - Force-loads file, wastes context\n@skills/testing/test-driven-development/SKILL.md\n```\n\n## Advanced Practices\n\n### Iterative Development\n\n**Best approach**: Develop skills iteratively with Claude\n1. Start with minimal viable skill\n2. Test with real use cases\n3. Refine based on what works\n4. Remove what doesn''t add value\n\n### Build Evaluations First\n\nBefore extensive documentation:\n1. Create test scenarios\n2. Identify what good looks like\n3. Document proven patterns\n4. Skip theoretical improvements\n\n### Utility Scripts\n\nFor reliability, provide:\n- Scripts with explicit error handling (don''t defer errors to Claude)\n- Exit codes for success/failure\n- Clear error messages\n- Examples of usage\n- List required dependencies explicitly\n\n**Example:**\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -e  # Exit on error\n\nif [ ! -f \"config.json\" ]; then\n  echo \"Error: config.json not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Script logic here\necho \"Success\"\nexit 0\n```\n\n### Verifiable Intermediate Outputs\n\nFor complex operations, create validation checkpoints:\n1. Have Claude produce a structured plan file\n2. Validate the plan with a script\n3. Execute only after validation passes\n\nThis catches errors before they compound.\n\n### Templates for Structured Output\n\nWhen skills produce consistent formats:\n```markdown\n## Output Template\n\n\\`\\`\\`typescript\ninterface ExpectedOutput {\n  status: ''success'' | ''error'';\n  data: YourDataType;\n  errors?: string[];\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Usage**: Copy and adapt for your context\n```\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist\n\n**Before writing:**\n- [ ] Technique isn''t obvious or well-documented elsewhere\n- [ ] Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- [ ] I would reference this across multiple projects\n\n**Frontmatter:**\n- [ ] Name uses only letters, numbers, hyphens\n- [ ] Description starts with \"Use when...\"\n- [ ] Description includes triggers AND what skill does\n- [ ] Description is third person\n- [ ] Total frontmatter < 1024 characters\n\n**Content:**\n- [ ] Overview states core principle (1-2 sentences)\n- [ ] \"When to Use\" section with symptoms\n- [ ] Quick reference table for common operations\n- [ ] One excellent code example (if technique skill)\n- [ ] Common mistakes section\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for searchability\n\n**Quality:**\n- [ ] Word count appropriate for frequency (see targets above)\n- [ ] SKILL.md under 500 lines\n- [ ] No narrative storytelling\n- [ ] Flowcharts only for non-obvious decisions\n- [ ] Supporting files only if needed (100+ lines reference)\n- [ ] Cross-references use skill name, not file paths\n- [ ] No time-sensitive information\n- [ ] Consistent terminology throughout\n- [ ] Concrete examples (not templates)\n- [ ] Degrees of freedom match task complexity\n\n**Testing:**\n- [ ] Tested with Claude Haiku, Sonnet, and Opus (instructions effective for Opus may need more detail for Haiku)\n- [ ] Tested with subagent scenarios (if discipline-enforcing skill)\n- [ ] Addresses common rationalizations\n- [ ] Includes red flags list\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Required\n    supporting-file.*     # Optional\n    examples/             # Optional\n      example1.ts\n    scripts/              # Optional\n      helper.py\n```\n\n**Flat namespace** - all skills in one searchable directory\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\n**Good skills:**\n- Future Claude finds them quickly (CSO optimization)\n- Can be scanned in seconds (quick reference)\n- Provide clear actionable examples\n- Prevent repeating same research\n- Stay under 500 lines (token efficient)\n- Match specificity to task needs (right degrees of freedom)\n\n**Bad skills:**\n- Get ignored (vague description)\n- Take too long to evaluate (no quick reference)\n- Leave gaps in understanding (no examples)\n- Waste token budget (verbose explanations of obvious things)\n- Over-constrain creative tasks or under-specify critical operations\n- Include time-sensitive or obsolete information\n\n---\n\n**Remember:** Skills are for future Claude, not current you. Optimize for discovery, scanning, and action.\n\n**Golden rule:** Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:07:50.869Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, requiring efficient real-time agent-to-agent communication and skill discovery","zh":"适用于像 Claude 这样的高级 AI 智能体，需要高效的实时智能体间通信和技能发现","ja":"Claude のような高度な AI エージェントに適しており、エージェント間の効率的なリアルタイム通信とスキル発見が必要","ko":"Claude 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 효율적인 실시간 에이전트 간 통신과 스킬 발견이 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude, que requieren una comunicación eficiente en tiempo real entre agentes y descubrimiento de habilidades","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude, nécessitant une communication efficace en temps réel entre agents et découverte de compétences","de":"Ideal für erweiterte KI-Agents wie Claude, die eine effiziente Echtzeit-Kommunikation zwischen Agents und Fähigkeitsentdeckung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude, que exigem comunicação em tempo real eficiente entre agentes e descoberta de habilidades","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, требующих эффективного обмена информацией в режиме реального времени между агентами и обнаружения навыков","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم مثل Claude ، الذي يتطلب اتصالًا فعّالًا في الوقت الفعلي بين العميل واكتشاف المهارات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create discoverable, scannable, and actionable skills using reference guides for proven techniques, patterns, or tools, leveraging core principles that assume the agent''s existing intelligence and only add necessary context","zh":"使得智能体能够使用已证明的技术、模式或工具的参考指南创建可发现、可扫描和可执行的技能，利用核心原则假设智能体的现有智能并仅添加必要的上下文","ja":"エージェントが既存のテクニック、パターン、またはツールの参考ガイドを使用して、発見可能、スキャナブル、実行可能なスキルを作成できるようにし、エージェントの既存の知能を仮定するコアプリンシプルを活用し、必要なコンテキストのみを追加","ko":"에이전트가 증명된 기술, 패턴 또는 도구의 참조 가이드를 사용하여 발견 가능, 스캔 가능 및 실행 가능한 스킬을 만들 수 있도록 하며 에이전트의 기존 지능을 가정하는 핵심 원칙을 활용하여 필요한 컨텍스트만 추가","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear habilidades descubribles, escaneables y accionables utilizando guías de referencia para técnicas, patrones o herramientas comprobadas, aprovechando principios básicos que asumen la inteligencia existente del agente y solo agregan el contexto necesario","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des compétences découvrables, scannables et actionnables en utilisant des guides de référence pour des techniques, des modèles ou des outils éprouvés, en exploitant les principes de base qui supposent l''intelligence existante de l''agent et n''ajoutent que le contexte nécessaire","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, handhabbare, scannbare und ausführbare Fähigkeiten zu erstellen, indem sie Referenzhandbücher für bewährte Techniken, Muster oder Werkzeuge verwenden, die Kernprinzipien nutzend, die die bereits bestehende Intelligenz des Agents voraussetzen und nur den notwendigen Kontext hinzufügen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar habilidades descobríveis, scaneáveis e ações usando guias de referência para técnicas, padrões ou ferramentas comprovadas, aproveitando princípios básicos que presumem a inteligência existente do agente e apenas adicionam contexto necessário","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать обнаруживаемые, сканируемые и действенные навыки, используя справочные пособия для проверенных техник, шаблонов или инструментов, используя основные принципы, которые предполагают существующий интеллект агента и добавляют только необходимый контекст","ar":"تمكن العملاء من إنشاء مهارات قابلة للكشف والفحص والتشغيل باستخدام دلائل مرجعيةสำหรเทคนيكات ونماذج وأدوات مجربة، مستفيدة من المبادئ الأساسية التي تفترض ذكاء العميل الحالي وإضافة السياق الضروري فقط"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating skill discovery for future instances","Generating reference guides for effective approaches","Enhancing agent collaboration through real-time communication"],"zh":["自动为将来的实例发现技能","为有效的方法生成参考指南","通过实时通信增强智能体协作"],"ja":["将来のインスタンスのスキルを自動で発見する","効果的なアプローチの参考ガイドを生成する","リアルタイムコミュニケーションを通じてエージェントのコラボレーションを強化する"],"ko":["미래의 인스턴스에 대한 스킬 자동 발견","효과적인 접근 방식에 대한 참조 가이드 생성","실시간 통신을 통해 에이전트 협업 강화"],"es":["Automatizar el descubrimiento de habilidades para futuras instancias","Generar guías de referencia para enfoques efectivos","Mejorar la colaboración de los agentes a través de la comunicación en tiempo real"],"fr":["Automatiser la découverte de compétences pour les instances futures","Générer des guides de référence pour des approches efficaces","Améliorer la collaboration des agents via la communication en temps réel"],"de":["Automatisieren des Fähigkeitsentdeckungsprozesses für zukünftige Instanzen","Erstellen von Referenzhandbüchern für effektive Ansätze","Verbessern der Agenten-Kollaboration durch Echtzeit-Kommunikation"],"pt":["Automatizar a descoberta de habilidades para instâncias futuras","Gerar guias de referência para abordagens eficazes","Melhorar a colaboração entre agentes por meio da comunicação em tempo real"],"ru":["Автоматизация обнаружения навыков для будущих экземпляров","Генерация справочных пособий для эффективных подходов","Усиление сотрудничества между агентами за счет обмена информацией в режиме реального времени"],"ar":["تutomatizar اكتشاف المهارات لمثيلات المستقبلية","إيجاد دلائل مرجعية للنّحو الفعّال","تعزيز تعاون العملاء من خلال الاتصال الفعّال في الوقت الفعلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to core principle of assuming agent intelligence","Skills must be discoverable, scannable, and actionable"],"zh":["需要遵守假设智能体智能的核心原则","技能必须是可发现、可扫描和可执行"],"ja":["エージェントの知能を仮定するコアプリンシプルに従う必要","スキルは発見可能、スキャナブル、実行可能でなければならない"],"ko":["에이전트 지능을 가정하는 핵심 원칙을 따라야","스킬은 발견 가능, 스캔 가능 및 실행 가능해야"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión al principio básico de asumir la inteligencia del agente","Las habilidades deben ser descubribles, escaneables y accionables"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au principe de base qui suppose l''intelligence de l''agent","Les compétences doivent être découvrables, scannables et actionnables"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Grundprinzips, das die Intelligenz des Agents voraussetzt","Die Fähigkeiten müssen handhabbar, scannbar und ausführbar sein"],"pt":["Exige aderência ao princípio básico de presumir a inteligência do agente","As habilidades devem ser descobríveis, scaneáveis e ações"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения основного принципа, предполагающего интеллект агента","Навыки должны быть обнаруживаемыми, сканируемыми и действенными"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمبدأ أساسي يفترض ذكاء العميل","يجب أن تكون المهارات قابلة للكشف والفحص والتشغيل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('proffesor-for-testing/sentinel-api-testing/quality-metrics', 'community', 'proffesor-for-testing', 'sentinel-api-testing', 'proffesor-for-testing/sentinel-api-testing', 'quality-metrics', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:42.547Z', NULL, '{"id":"proffesor-for-testing/sentinel-api-testing/quality-metrics","name":"quality-metrics","description":{"zh":"质量指标是衡量软件质量的关键指标，包括测量结果、DORA 指标和避免虚荣指标","ja":"品質メトリクスは、結果の測定、DORA メトリクス、虚栄指標の回避を含むソフトウェア品質を測定するための重要な指標です","ko":"품질 메트릭스는 결과 측정, DORA 메트릭스 및 허위 지표를 피하는 것을 포함하여 소프트웨어 품질을 측정하는 데 중요한 지표입니다","es":"Métricas de calidad para desarrolladores: medir resultados, enfocarse en métricas DORA y evitar métricas vanidad","fr":"Métriques de qualité pour les développeurs : mesurer les résultats, se concentrer sur les métriques DORA et éviter les métriques vanité","de":"Qualitätsmetriken für Entwickler: Ergebnisse messen, sich auf DORA-Metriken konzentrieren und Vanity-Metriken vermeiden","pt":"Métricas de qualidade para desenvolvedores, focando em resultados e evitando métricas de vaidade","ru":"Метрики качества для разработчиков, фокусирующиеся на результатах и избегающие метрик тщеславия","ar":"مetrics جودة للمانحين، تركز على النتائج وتتجنب معايير الانانية","en":"AI Agentic API Testing Platform - Automated testing with specialized ephemeral agents"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"质量指标：AI Agent 测试平台","ja":"品質メトリクス：AI エージェント テスト プラットフォーム","ko":"품질 메트릭스: AI 에이전트 테스트 플랫폼","es":"Métricas de Calidad para Desarrolladores","fr":"Métriques de Qualité pour les Développeurs","de":"Qualitätsmetriken für Entwickler","pt":"Métricas de Qualidade para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Метрики качества для разработчиков","ar":"مetrics جودة للمانحين","en":"quality-metrics"},"description":{"zh":"质量指标是衡量软件质量的关键指标，包括测量结果、DORA 指标和避免虚荣指标","ja":"品質メトリクスは、結果の測定、DORA メトリクス、虚栄指標の回避を含むソフトウェア品質を測定するための重要な指標です","ko":"품질 메트릭스는 결과 측정, DORA 메트릭스 및 허위 지표를 피하는 것을 포함하여 소프트웨어 품질을 측정하는 데 중요한 지표입니다","es":"Métricas de calidad para desarrolladores: medir resultados, enfocarse en métricas DORA y evitar métricas vanidad","fr":"Métriques de qualité pour les développeurs : mesurer les résultats, se concentrer sur les métriques DORA et éviter les métriques vanité","de":"Qualitätsmetriken für Entwickler: Ergebnisse messen, sich auf DORA-Metriken konzentrieren und Vanity-Metriken vermeiden","pt":"Métricas de qualidade para desenvolvedores, focando em resultados e evitando métricas de vaidade","ru":"Метрики качества для разработчиков, фокусирующиеся на результатах и избегающие метрик тщеславия","ar":"مetrics جودة للمانحين، تركز على النتائج وتتجنب معايير الانانية","en":"AI Agentic API Testing Platform - Automated testing with specialized ephemeral agents"},"definition":{"en":"AI Agentic API Testing Platform - Automated testing with specialized ephemeral agents"},"features":{"zh":["自动化测试","DORA 指标支持","虚荣指标回避","结果测量","门槛设置"],"ja":["自動テスト","DORA メトリクス サポート","虚栄指標回避","結果の測定","しきい値設定"],"ko":["자동 테스트","DORA 메트릭스 지원","허위 지표 피하기","결과 측정","임계값 설정"],"es":["Medición de resultados","Enfoque en métricas DORA","Evitación de métricas vanidad","Establecimiento de umbrales de calidad","Análisis de tendencias en el tiempo"],"fr":["Mesure des résultats","Concentration sur les métriques DORA","Évitement des métriques vanité","Définition de seuils de qualité","Analyse des tendances dans le temps"],"de":["Ergebnismessung","Fokus auf DORA-Metriken","Vermeidung von Vanity-Metriken","Festlegung von Qualitäts-Schwellenwerten","Trendanalyse im Zeitverlauf"],"pt":["Medição de resultados em vez de atividades","Foco em métricas DORA","Evitar métricas de vaidade","Definição de limites para comportamento","Análise de tendências ao longo do tempo"],"ru":["Измерение результатов вместо действий","Фокус на метриках DORA","Избежание метрик тщеславия","Определение порогов для поведения","Анализ тенденций во времени"],"ar":["قياس النتائج بدلاً من الأنشطة","التركيز على معايير DORA","تجنب معايير الانانية","تحديد حدود للسلوك","تحليل الاتجاهات بمرور الوقت"]},"keywords":{"zh":["质量指标","AI Agent","自动化测试","DORA 指标","虚荣指标","软件质量","测试平台","结果测量"],"ja":["品質メトリクス","AI エージェント","自動テスト","DORA メトリクス","虚栄指標","ソフトウェア品質","テスト プラットフォーム","結果の測定"],"ko":["품질 메트릭스","AI 에이전트","자동 테스트","DORA 메트릭스","허위 지표","소프트웨어 품질","테스트 플랫폼","결과 측정"],"es":["métricas de calidad","pruebas automatizadas","desarrollo de software","métricas DORA","vanity metrics","umbrales de calidad"],"fr":["métriques de qualité","tests automatisés","développement de logiciel","métriques DORA","métriques vanité","seuils de qualité"],"de":["Qualitätsmetriken","automatisierte Tests","Software-Entwicklung","DORA-Metriken","Vanity-Metriken","Qualitäts-Schwellenwerte"],"pt":["métricas de qualidade","desenvolvimento de software","teste de código","métricas DORA","qualidade de código","desenvolvedores"],"ru":["метрики качества","разработка программного обеспечения","тестирование кода","метрики DORA","качество кода","разработчики"],"ar":["مetrics جودة","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبار الكود","معايير DORA","جودة الكود","المانحين"]}},"owner":"proffesor-for-testing","repo":"sentinel-api-testing","repoPath":"proffesor-for-testing/sentinel-api-testing","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"quality-metrics","description":"Measure quality effectively with actionable metrics. Use when establishing quality dashboards, defining KPIs, or evaluating test effectiveness.","tags":["metrics","dora","quality-gates","dashboards","kpis","measurement"],"bodyPreview":"# Quality Metrics\n\n<default_to_action>\nWhen measuring quality or building dashboards:\n1. MEASURE outcomes (bug escape rate, MTTD) not activities (test count)\n2. FOCUS on DORA metrics: Deployment frequency, Lead time, MTTD, MTTR, Change failure rate\n3. AVOID vanity metrics: 100% coverage means nothing if tests don''t catch bugs\n4. SET thresholds that drive behavior (quality gates block bad code)\n5. TREND over time: Direction matters more than absolute numbers\n\n**Quick Metric Selection:**\n- Speed:","body":"# Quality Metrics\n\n<default_to_action>\nWhen measuring quality or building dashboards:\n1. MEASURE outcomes (bug escape rate, MTTD) not activities (test count)\n2. FOCUS on DORA metrics: Deployment frequency, Lead time, MTTD, MTTR, Change failure rate\n3. AVOID vanity metrics: 100% coverage means nothing if tests don''t catch bugs\n4. SET thresholds that drive behavior (quality gates block bad code)\n5. TREND over time: Direction matters more than absolute numbers\n\n**Quick Metric Selection:**\n- Speed: Deployment frequency, lead time for changes\n- Stability: Change failure rate, MTTR\n- Quality: Bug escape rate, defect density, test effectiveness\n- Process: Code review time, flaky test rate\n\n**Critical Success Factors:**\n- Metrics without action are theater\n- What you measure is what you optimize\n- Trends matter more than snapshots\n</default_to_action>\n\n## Quick Reference Card\n\n### When to Use\n- Building quality dashboards\n- Defining quality gates\n- Evaluating testing effectiveness\n- Justifying quality investments\n\n### Meaningful vs Vanity Metrics\n| ✅ Meaningful | ❌ Vanity |\n|--------------|-----------|\n| Bug escape rate | Test case count |\n| MTTD (detection) | Lines of test code |\n| MTTR (recovery) | Test executions |\n| Change failure rate | Coverage % (alone) |\n| Lead time for changes | Requirements traced |\n\n### DORA Metrics\n| Metric | Elite | High | Medium | Low |\n|--------|-------|------|--------|-----|\n| Deploy Frequency | On-demand | Weekly | Monthly | Yearly |\n| Lead Time | < 1 hour | < 1 week | < 1 month | > 6 months |\n| Change Failure Rate | < 5% | < 15% | < 30% | > 45% |\n| MTTR | < 1 hour | < 1 day | < 1 week | > 1 month |\n\n### Quality Gate Thresholds\n| Metric | Blocking Threshold | Warning |\n|--------|-------------------|---------|\n| Test pass rate | 100% | - |\n| Critical coverage | > 80% | > 70% |\n| Security critical | 0 | - |\n| Performance p95 | < 200ms | < 500ms |\n| Flaky tests | < 2% | < 5% |\n\n---\n\n## Core Metrics\n\n### Bug Escape Rate\n```\nBug Escape Rate = (Production Bugs / Total Bugs Found) × 100\n\nTarget: < 10% (90% caught before production)\n```\n\n### Test Effectiveness\n```\nTest Effectiveness = (Bugs Found by Tests / Total Bugs) × 100\n\nTarget: > 70%\n```\n\n### Defect Density\n```\nDefect Density = Defects / KLOC\n\nGood: < 1 defect per KLOC\n```\n\n### Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)\n```\nMTTD = Time(Bug Reported) - Time(Bug Introduced)\n\nTarget: < 1 day for critical, < 1 week for others\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dashboard Design\n\n```typescript\n// Agent generates quality dashboard\nawait Task(\"Generate Dashboard\", {\n  metrics: {\n    delivery: [''deployment-frequency'', ''lead-time'', ''change-failure-rate''],\n    quality: [''bug-escape-rate'', ''test-effectiveness'', ''defect-density''],\n    stability: [''mttd'', ''mttr'', ''availability''],\n    process: [''code-review-time'', ''flaky-test-rate'', ''coverage-trend'']\n  },\n  visualization: ''grafana'',\n  alerts: {\n    critical: { bug_escape_rate: ''>20%'', mttr: ''>24h'' },\n    warning: { coverage: ''<70%'', flaky_rate: ''>5%'' }\n  }\n}, \"qe-quality-analyzer\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quality Gate Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"qualityGates\": {\n    \"commit\": {\n      \"coverage\": { \"min\": 80, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"lint\": { \"errors\": 0, \"blocking\": true }\n    },\n    \"pr\": {\n      \"tests\": { \"pass\": \"100%\", \"blocking\": true },\n      \"security\": { \"critical\": 0, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"coverage_delta\": { \"min\": 0, \"blocking\": false }\n    },\n    \"release\": {\n      \"e2e\": { \"pass\": \"100%\", \"blocking\": true },\n      \"performance_p95\": { \"max_ms\": 200, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"bug_escape_rate\": { \"max\": \"10%\", \"blocking\": false }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent-Assisted Metrics\n\n```typescript\n// Calculate quality trends\nawait Task(\"Quality Trend Analysis\", {\n  timeframe: ''90d'',\n  metrics: [''bug-escape-rate'', ''mttd'', ''test-effectiveness''],\n  compare: ''previous-90d'',\n  predictNext: ''30d''\n}, \"qe-quality-analyzer\");\n\n// Evaluate quality gate\nawait Task(\"Quality Gate Evaluation\", {\n  buildId: ''build-123'',\n  environment: ''staging'',\n  metrics: currentMetrics,\n  policy: qualityPolicy\n}, \"qe-quality-gate\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent Coordination Hints\n\n### Memory Namespace\n```\naqe/quality-metrics/\n├── dashboards/*         - Dashboard configurations\n├── trends/*             - Historical metric data\n├── gates/*              - Gate evaluation results\n└── alerts/*             - Triggered alerts\n```\n\n### Fleet Coordination\n```typescript\nconst metricsFleet = await FleetManager.coordinate({\n  strategy: ''quality-metrics'',\n  agents: [\n    ''qe-quality-analyzer'',         // Trend analysis\n    ''qe-test-executor'',            // Test metrics\n    ''qe-coverage-analyzer'',        // Coverage data\n    ''qe-production-intelligence'',  // Production metrics\n    ''qe-quality-gate''              // Gate decisions\n  ],\n  topology: ''mesh''\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Traps\n\n| Trap | Problem | Solution |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| Coverage worship | 100% coverage, bugs still escape | Measure bug escape rate instead |\n| Test count focus | Many tests, slow feedback | Measure execution time |\n| Activity metrics | Busy work, no outcomes | Measure outcomes (MTTD, MTTR) |\n| Point-in-time | Snapshot without context | Track trends over time |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n- [agentic-quality-engineering](../agentic-quality-engineering/) - Agent coordination\n- [cicd-pipeline-qe-orchestrator](../cicd-pipeline-qe-orchestrator/) - Quality gates\n- [risk-based-testing](../risk-based-testing/) - Risk-informed metrics\n- [shift-right-testing](../shift-right-testing/) - Production metrics\n\n---\n\n## Remember\n\n**Measure outcomes, not activities.** Bug escape rate > test count. MTTD/MTTR > coverage %. Trends > snapshots. Set gates that block bad code. What you measure is what you optimize.\n\n**With Agents:** Agents track metrics automatically, analyze trends, trigger alerts, and make gate decisions. Use agents to maintain continuous quality visibility.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:42.547Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Testing Agents needing advanced quality metrics analysis and DORA metrics implementation.","zh":"适合需要高级质量指标分析和DORA指标实施的AI测试代理。","ja":"高度な品質指標分析とDORA指標の実装が必要なAIテストエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 품질 지표 분석 및 DORA 지표 구현이 필요한 AI 테스트 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de prueba de IA que necesitan un análisis avanzado de métricas de calidad y una implementación de métricas DORA.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de test d''IA ayant besoin d''une analyse avancée des métriques de qualité et d''une mise en œuvre des métriques DORA.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Testagenten, die eine fortschrittliche Analyse von Qualitätsmetriken und eine Implementierung von DORA-Metriken benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Teste de IA que necessitam de análise de métricas de qualidade avançadas e implementação de métricas DORA.","ru":"Идеально для агентов тестирования ИИ, требующих расширенного анализа метрик качества и реализации метрик DORA.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات اختبار الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تحتاج إلى تحليل متقدم لقياس جودة العمل وتنفيذ مقاييس DORA."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to measure outcomes like bug escape rate and MTTD, focus on key metrics such as Deployment frequency and Lead time, and set quality gates to drive behavior, all while avoiding vanity metrics and trending quality over time using metrics like Change failure rate and MTTR.","zh":"赋予代理测量结果，如bug逃逸率和MTTD，关注关键指标，如部署频率和引领时间，并设置质量门限来驱动行为，同时避免虚荣指标，并使用指标如变化故障率和MTTR随时间推移趋势质量。","ja":"エージェントにバグエスケープ率やMTTDなどの結果を測定し、デプロイ頻度やリードタイムなどの重要な指標に焦点を当て、品質ゲートを設定して行動を推進し、虚栄指標を避け、変更故障率やMTTRなどの指標を使用して品質の傾向を時系列で追跡することができます。","ko":"에이전트가 버그 탈출률 및 MTTD와 같은 결과를 측정하고 배포 빈도 및 리드 타임 등의 주요 지표에 집중하고 품질 게이트를 설정하여 행동을 구동하고 허위 지표를 피하고 변경 실패률 및 MTTR와 같은 지표를 사용하여 품질을 시간에 따라 추세하는 데 사용됩니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a medir resultados como la tasa de escape de errores y MTTD, centrarse en métricas clave como la frecuencia de implementación y el tiempo de espera, y establecer puertas de calidad para impulsar el comportamiento, todo mientras evita métricas vanas y sigue las tendencias de calidad con el tiempo utilizando métricas como la tasa de fallo de cambios y MTTR.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mesurer les résultats tels que le taux d''échappement de bogues et MTTD, de se concentrer sur des métriques clés telles que la fréquence de déploiement et le temps de latence, et de définir des portes de qualité pour stimuler le comportement, le tout en évitant les métriques vanité et en suivant les tendances de qualité dans le temps en utilisant des métriques telles que le taux d''échec de modification et MTTR.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Ergebnisse wie die Fehlerentweichungsrate und MTTD zu messen, sich auf Schlüsselmetriken wie die Bereitstellungs Häufigkeit und die Vorlaufzeit zu konzentrieren und Qualitätsziele zu setzen, um das Verhalten zu beeinflussen, und vermeidet gleichzeitig sinnlose Metriken und verfolgt die Qualitätsentwicklung im Laufe der Zeit mithilfe von Metriken wie der Änderungsfehlerquote und MTTR.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a medir resultados como taxa de escape de bugs e MTTD, focar em métricas-chave como frequência de implantação e tempo de lead, e definir portas de qualidade para impulsionar o comportamento, tudo isso enquanto evita métricas de vaidade e tendências de qualidade ao longo do tempo usando métricas como taxa de falha de alteração e MTTR.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью измерять результаты, такие как уровень побега ошибок и MTTD, фокусироваться на ключевых метриках, таких как частота развертывания и время ожидания, и устанавливать ворота качества для стимулирования поведения, все это при избегании метрик тщеславия и отслеживании тенденций качества во времени с использованием метрик, таких как уровень неудачи изменений и MTTR.","ar":"يمكن للعميل قياس النتائج مثل معدل هروب العيوب و MTTR، والتركيز على المقاييس الرئيسية مثل تكرار التثبيت ووقت الإحضار، ووضع بوابات الجودة لدفع السلوك، مع تجنب مقاييس التكلف ومراقبة اتجاهات الجودة بمرور الوقت باستخدام مقاييس مثل معدل فشل التغيير و MTTR."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating testing with ephemeral agents to measure quality metrics","Generating dashboards to track DORA metrics and quality gates","Debugging low-quality code by analyzing trends in MTTD and MTTR"],"zh":["使用暂时代理自动化测试以测量质量指标","生成仪表盘以跟踪DORA指标和质量门限","通过分析MTTD和MTTR的趋势调试低质量代码"],"ja":["一時的なエージェントを使用して自動テストを行い品質指標を測定する","DORA指標と品質ゲートを追跡するためのダッシュボードを生成する","MTTDとMTTRの傾向を分析して品質の低いコードをデバッグする"],"ko":["임시 에이전트를 사용하여 자동 테스트를 수행하고 품질 지표를 측정하는 것","DORA 지표 및 품질 게이트를 추적하기 위한 대시보드를 생성하는 것","MTTD 및 MTTR의 추세를 분석하여 품질이 낮은 코드를 디버깅하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar pruebas con agentes efímeros para medir métricas de calidad","Generar paneles de control para realizar un seguimiento de las métricas DORA y las puertas de calidad","Depurar código de baja calidad analizando tendencias en MTTD y MTTR"],"fr":["Automatiser les tests avec des agents éphémères pour mesurer les métriques de qualité","Générer des tableaux de bord pour suivre les métriques DORA et les portes de qualité","Déboguer le code de mauvaise qualité en analysant les tendances dans MTTD et MTTR"],"de":["Automatisieren von Tests mit ephemeren Agenten, um Qualitätsmetriken zu messen","Erstellen von Dashboards, um DORA-Metriken und Qualitätsziele zu verfolgen","Fehlerhafte Code-Debugging durch Trendanalyse in MTTD und MTTR"],"pt":["Automatizar testes com agentes efêmeros para medir métricas de qualidade","Gerar painéis para acompanhar métricas DORA e portas de qualidade","Depurar código de baixa qualidade analisando tendências em MTTD e MTTR"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тестирование с помощью эфемерных агентов для измерения метрик качества","Генерировать панели для отслеживания метрик DORA и ворот качества","Отлаживать код низкого качества, анализируя тенденции в MTTD и MTTR"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في الاختبارات باستخدام وكلاء مؤقتين لقياس مقاييس الجودة","توليد لوحات تحكم لتتبع مقاييس DORA وبوابات الجودة","تصحيح الأخطاء في أكواد الجودة المنخفضة من خلال تحليل الاتجاهات في MTTD و MTTR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of DORA metrics and quality gates","Limited to measuring outcomes and trends, not activities or test counts"],"zh":["需要了解DORA指标和质量门限","仅限于测量结果和趋势，不包括活动或测试次数"],"ja":["DORA指標と品質ゲートを理解する必要がある","結果と傾向のみを測定し、活動やテスト回数は含まない"],"ko":["DORA 지표 및 품질 게이트에 대한 이해가 필요","결과 및 추세만 측정하고 활동 또는 테스트 횟수는 포함하지 않는다"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las métricas DORA y las puertas de calidad","Limitado a la medición de resultados y tendencias, no actividades o recuentos de pruebas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des métriques DORA et des portes de qualité","Limité à la mesure des résultats et des tendances, et non des activités ou des décomptes de tests"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis von DORA-Metriken und Qualitätszielen","Begrenzt auf die Messung von Ergebnissen und Trends, nicht auf Aktivitäten oder Testzählungen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das métricas DORA e portas de qualidade","Limitado à medição de resultados e tendências, não atividades ou contagens de testes"],"ru":["Требует понимания метрик DORA и ворот качества","Ограничен измерением результатов и тенденций, а не деятельности или подсчета тестов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لمقاييس DORA وبوابات الجودة","محدود بقياس النتائج والاتجاهات، وليس الأنشطة أو عدد الاختبارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('johnlindquist/script-kit-next/script-kit-logging', 'community', 'johnlindquist', 'script-kit-next', 'johnlindquist/script-kit-next', 'script-kit-logging', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:08:54.580Z', NULL, '{"id":"johnlindquist/script-kit-next/script-kit-logging","name":"script-kit-logging","description":{"zh":"Script Kit 日志记录提供结构化的日志模式，用于调试和可观察性。它使用 Rust 和 GPUI（Zed 的 UI 框架）实现","ja":"Script Kit ロギングは、デバッグと可観測性のための構造化ログパターンを提供します。Rust と GPUI（Zed の UI フレームワーク）を使用して実装されています","ko":"Script Kit 로깅은 디버깅과 관찰 가능성을 위한 구조화된 로그 패턴을 제공합니다. Rust와 GPUI(Zed의 UI 프레임워크)를 사용하여 구현되어 있습니다","es":"Script Kit Logging proporciona patrones de registro estructurado para depuración y observabilidad. Se basa en Rust y utiliza GPUI, el marco de UI de Zed.","fr":"Script Kit Logging fournit des modèles de journalisation structurée pour le débogage et l''observabilité. Il est basé sur Rust et utilise GPUI, le cadre d''UI de Zed.","de":"Script Kit Logging bietet strukturierte Protokollmuster für Fehlersuche und Überwachung. Es basiert auf Rust und verwendet GPUI, den UI-Rahmen von Zed.","pt":"O Script Kit Logging é uma ferramenta de logging em Rust para debugging e observabilidade, com padrões de logging estruturados","ru":"Скрипт Кит Логгинг - это инструмент логирования в Rust для отладки и наблюдаемости, с структурированными шаблонами логирования","ar":"Script Kit تسجيل هو أداة تسجيل في Rust للتصحيح ومراقبة الأداء، مع أنماط تسجيل متسلسلة","en":"Script Kit rewritten in Rust using GPUI (Zed''s UI framework)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Script Kit 日志记录 - Rust 实现的结构化日志","ja":"Script Kit ロギング - Rust で実装された構造化ログ","ko":"Script Kit 로깅 - Rust로 구현된 구조화 로그","es":"Script Kit Logging: Patrones de registro estructurado","fr":"Script Kit Logging: Modèles de journalisation structurée","de":"Script Kit Logging: Strukturierte Protokollmuster","pt":"Kit de Script de Logging em Rust","ru":"Скрипт Кит Логгинг на Rust","ar":"ascript Kit تسجيل في Rust","en":"script-kit-logging"},"description":{"zh":"Script Kit 日志记录提供结构化的日志模式，用于调试和可观察性。它使用 Rust 和 GPUI（Zed 的 UI 框架）实现","ja":"Script Kit ロギングは、デバッグと可観測性のための構造化ログパターンを提供します。Rust と GPUI（Zed の UI フレームワーク）を使用して実装されています","ko":"Script Kit 로깅은 디버깅과 관찰 가능성을 위한 구조화된 로그 패턴을 제공합니다. Rust와 GPUI(Zed의 UI 프레임워크)를 사용하여 구현되어 있습니다","es":"Script Kit Logging proporciona patrones de registro estructurado para depuración y observabilidad. Se basa en Rust y utiliza GPUI, el marco de UI de Zed.","fr":"Script Kit Logging fournit des modèles de journalisation structurée pour le débogage et l''observabilité. Il est basé sur Rust et utilise GPUI, le cadre d''UI ...","de":"Script Kit Logging bietet strukturierte Protokollmuster für Fehlersuche und Überwachung. Es basiert auf Rust und verwendet GPUI, den UI-Rahmen von Zed.","pt":"O Script Kit Logging é uma ferramenta de logging em Rust para debugging e observabilidade, com padrões de logging estruturados","ru":"Скрипт Кит Логгинг - это инструмент логирования в Rust для отладки и наблюдаемости, с структурированными шаблонами логирования","ar":"Script Kit تسجيل هو أداة تسجيل في Rust للتصحيح ومراقبة الأداء، مع أنماط تسجيل متسلسلة","en":"Script Kit rewritten in Rust using GPUI (Zed''s UI framework)"},"definition":{"en":"Script Kit rewritten in Rust using GPUI (Zed''s UI framework)"},"features":{"zh":["结构化日志记录","Rust 实现","GPUI 集成","调试和可观察性","紧凑的 stderr 格式"],"ja":["構造化ログ記録","Rust 実装","GPUI 統合","デバッグと可観測性","コンパクトな stderr フォーマット"],"ko":["구조화된 로그 기록","Rust 구현","GPUI 통합","디버깅과 관찰 가능성","紧凑한 stderr 형식"],"es":["Registro estructurado para depuración y observabilidad","Compatibilidad con Rust y GPUI","Formato de registro compacto para stderr","Categorías personalizables para registro","Niveles de registro ajustables"],"fr":["Journalisation structurée pour le débogage et l''observabilité","Compatibilité avec Rust et GPUI","Format de journal compact pour stderr","Catégories personnalisables pour la journalisation","Niveaux de journalisation ajustables"],"de":["Strukturierte Protokollierung für Fehlersuche und Überwachung","Kompatibilität mit Rust und GPUI","Kompaktes Protokollformat für stderr","Anpassbare Kategorien für Protokollierung","Einstellbare Protokollniveaus"],"pt":["Padrões de logging estruturados","Modo de log compacto","Categorias de logging personalizáveis","Suporte a stderr","Implementado em Rust"],"ru":["Структурированные шаблоны логирования","Компактный режим логирования","Настраиваемые категории логирования","Поддержка stderr","Реализовано на Rust"],"ar":["أنماط تسجيل متسلسلة","وضع تسجيل مدمج","فئات تسجيل قابلة للتخصيص","دعم stderr","م実装 بلغة Rust"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Script Kit","日志记录","Rust","GPUI","结构化日志","调试","可观察性","紧凑的 stderr 格式"],"ja":["Script Kit","ロギング","Rust","GPUI","構造化ログ","デバッグ","可観測性","コンパクトな stderr フォーマット"],"ko":["Script Kit","로깅","Rust","GPUI","구조화된 로그","디버깅","관찰 가능성","紧凑한 stderr 형식"],"es":["Script Kit Logging","registro estructurado","depuración","observabilidad","Rust","GPUI","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Script Kit Logging","journalisation structurée","débogage","observabilité","Rust","GPUI","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Script Kit Logging","strukturierte Protokollierung","Fehlersuche","Überwachung","Rust","GPUI","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["logging em rust","debugging em rust","observabilidade em rust","script kit logging","rust logging","ferramentas de logging"],"ru":["логирование в rust","отладка в rust","наблюдаемость в rust","скрипт кит логгинг","rust логгинг","инструменты логирования"],"ar":["تسجيل في Rust","تصحيح في Rust","مراقبة الأداء في Rust","Script Kit تسجيل","Rust تسجيل","أدوات تسجيل"]}},"owner":"johnlindquist","repo":"script-kit-next","repoPath":"johnlindquist/script-kit-next","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"script-kit-logging","description":"Logging and observability patterns for Script Kit GPUI. Use when adding logs, debugging, or understanding the logging system. Covers JSONL format, compact AI log mode, correlation IDs, and error handling.","bodyPreview":"# Script Kit Logging\n\nStructured logging patterns for debugging and observability.\n\n## AI Compact Log Mode (SCRIPT_KIT_AI_LOG=1)\n\nCompact stderr format: `SS.mmm|L|C|message`\n\n- `L`: `i` INFO, `w` WARN, `e` ERROR, `d` DEBUG, `t` TRACE\n- `C` categories:\n  - `P` position, `A` app, `U` UI, `S` stdin, `H` hotkey\n  - `V` visibility, `E` exec, `K` key, `F` focus, `T` theme\n  - `C` cache, `R` perf, `W` window_mgr, `X` error\n  - `M` mouse_hover, `L` scroll_state, `Q` scroll_perf\n  - `D` design, `B` scrip","body":"# Script Kit Logging\n\nStructured logging patterns for debugging and observability.\n\n## AI Compact Log Mode (SCRIPT_KIT_AI_LOG=1)\n\nCompact stderr format: `SS.mmm|L|C|message`\n\n- `L`: `i` INFO, `w` WARN, `e` ERROR, `d` DEBUG, `t` TRACE\n- `C` categories:\n  - `P` position, `A` app, `U` UI, `S` stdin, `H` hotkey\n  - `V` visibility, `E` exec, `K` key, `F` focus, `T` theme\n  - `C` cache, `R` perf, `W` window_mgr, `X` error\n  - `M` mouse_hover, `L` scroll_state, `Q` scroll_perf\n  - `D` design, `B` script, `N` config, `Z` resize\n\nExample:\n- Standard: `... INFO ... Selected display origin=(0,0)`\n- Compact: `13.150|i|P|Selected display origin=(0,0)`\n\nEnable:\n```bash\nSCRIPT_KIT_AI_LOG=1 ./target/debug/script-kit-gpui 2>&1\n```\n\n## Log Modes\n\n| Mode | Command | Use Case |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| Compact AI logs | `SCRIPT_KIT_AI_LOG=1` | Default for AI agents (saves ~70% tokens) |\n| Full debug logs | `RUST_LOG=debug` | Deep debugging |\n| Specific module | `RUST_LOG=script_kit::theme=debug` | Target one module |\n\n## JSONL Logging\n\nLogs to: `~/.scriptkit/logs/script-kit-gpui.jsonl`\n\nLine example:\n```json\n{\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"level\":\"INFO\",\"target\":\"script_kit::executor\",\"message\":\"Script executed\",\"fields\":{\"script_name\":\"hello.ts\",\"duration_ms\":142,\"exit_code\":0}}\n```\n\n## Tracing Patterns\n\nUse `tracing` + `tracing-subscriber`:\n- `#[instrument]` for spans\n- Record `duration_ms`; warn if slow (e.g. >100ms)\n\nCorrelation IDs:\n- Generate UUID per user action/run\n- Attach to spans so nested logs inherit it\n\nRequired fields when relevant: `correlation_id`, `duration_ms`, `bead_id`, `agent_name`, `files_touched`\n\n## Log Level Guide\n\n- `error`: failure\n- `warn`: unexpected but handled\n- `info`: key events\n- `debug`: development\n- `trace`: very verbose\n\nFilter by targets (module paths): `script_kit::ui`, `script_kit::executor`, `script_kit::theme`\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Application errors: `anyhow::Result`; add `.context()` at boundaries\n- Domain/library errors: `thiserror` when callers match variants\n- User-facing errors: `NotifyResultExt` → log first (`tracing::error!`) then toast\n\nBest practices:\n- Don''t `unwrap()`/`expect()`\n- Add context at each level (\"which file?\", \"what operation?\")\n- Use typed fields in logs (avoid interpolated strings)\n\n## Log Queries\n\n```bash\ngrep ''\"correlation_id\":\"abc-123\"'' ~/.scriptkit/logs/script-kit-gpui.jsonl\ngrep ''\"duration_ms\":'' ~/.scriptkit/logs/script-kit-gpui.jsonl | jq ''select(.fields.duration_ms > 100)''\ngrep ''\"level\":\"ERROR\"'' ~/.scriptkit/logs/script-kit-gpui.jsonl | tail -50\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:08:54.580Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Debugging Agents requiring structured logging patterns for enhanced observability and error tracking.","zh":"适用于需要结构化日志模式以提高可观察性和错误跟踪的调试代理。","ja":"構造化されたログパターンを使用した観察可能性とエラートラッキングの強化が必要なデバッグエージェントに適しています。","ko":"구조화된 로깅 패턴을 사용하여 관찰 가능성과 오류 추적을 강화해야 하는 디버깅 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de depuración que requieren patrones de registro estructurados para una mejor observabilidad y seguimiento de errores.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de débogage nécessitant des modèles de journalisation structurés pour une meilleure observabilité et un suivi des erreurs.","de":"Ideal für Debugging-Agents, die strukturierte Protokollmuster für eine verbesserte Beobachtbarkeit und Fehlernachverfolgung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de depuração que requerem padrões de registro estruturados para observabilidade e rastreamento de erros aprimorados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов отладки, требующих структурированных шаблонов ведения журнала для улучшенной наблюдаемости и отслеживания ошибок.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء لتصحيح الأخطاء الذين يتطلبون أنماط تسجيل منظمة لتعزيز الرصد وتعقب الأخطاء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage compact stderr formats, such as `SS.mmm|L|C|message`, incorporating log levels like `i` INFO, `w` WARN, and categories including `P` position and `A` app, to streamline debugging processes using GPUI and Zed''s UI framework.","zh":"使代理能够利用紧凑的stderr格式，例如`SS.mmm|L|C|message`，其中包括日志级别，如`i` INFO，`w` WARN，以及类别，包括`P` 位置和`A` 应用程序，以使用GPUI和Zed的UI框架简化调试过程。","ja":"エージェントがコンパクトなstderr形式（例： `SS.mmm|L|C|message`）を利用できるようにし、ログレベル（`i` INFO、`w` WARNなど）やカテゴリ（`P` 位置、`A` アプリケーションなど）を組み込んで、GPUIとZedのUIフレームワークを使用したデバッグプロセスを簡素化します。","ko":"에이전트가紧凑한 stderr 형식(예: `SS.mmm|L|C|message`)을 사용할 수 있도록 하여 로그 수준(`i` INFO, `w` WARN 등) 및 카테고리(`P` 위치, `A` 애플리케이션 등)를 포함하여 GPUI 및 Zed의 UI 프레임워크를 사용한 디버깅 프로세스를 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar formatos compactos de stderr, como `SS.mmm|L|C|mensaje`, que incorporan niveles de registro como `i` INFO, `w` WARN, y categorías que incluyen `P` posición y `A` aplicación, para agilizar los procesos de depuración utilizando GPUI y el marco de UI de Zed.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser des formats de stderr compacts, tels que `SS.mmm|L|C|message`, incorporant des niveaux de journalisation tels que `i` INFO, `w` WARN, et des catégories comprenant `P` position et `A` application, pour rationaliser les processus de débogage à l''aide de GPUI et du framework d''interface utilisateur de Zed.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, kompakten stderr-Formate wie `SS.mmm|L|C|Nachricht` zu nutzen, die Protokollstufen wie `i` INFO, `w` WARN und Kategorien wie `P` Position und `A` App enthalten, um die Debugging-Prozesse mit GPUI und Zeds UI-Framework zu rationalisieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar formatos compactos de stderr, como `SS.mmm|L|C|mensagem`, incorporando níveis de log como `i` INFO, `w` WARN e categorias que incluem `P` posição e `A` aplicativo, para simplificar os processos de depuração usando GPUI e a estrutura de UI do Zed.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать компактные форматы stderr, такие как `SS.mmm|L|C|сообщение`, включающие уровни журнала, такие как `i` INFO, `w` WARN и категории, включая `P` позицию и `A` приложение, для оптимизации процессов отладки с использованием GPUI и фреймворка UI Zed.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من تنسيقات stderr المضغوطة مثل `SS.mmm|L|C|رسالة` ، ودمج مستويات السجل مثل `i` INFO و `w` WARN والفئات التي تشمل `P` الموضع و `A` التطبيق ، لتبسيط عمليات تصحيح الأخطاء باستخدام GPUI وإطار UI ل Zed."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing AI Compact Log Mode for efficient error tracking","Debugging UI issues with categories like `U` UI and `H` hotkey","Enhancing observability with structured logging patterns for `stdin` and `stdout`"],"zh":["实现AI紧凑日志模式以高效跟踪错误","使用类别如`U` UI和`H`热键调试UI问题","使用结构化日志模式增强`stdin`和`stdout`的可观察性"],"ja":["エラートラッキングの効率化のためにAIコンパクトログモードを実装する","カテゴリ`U` UIや`H`ホットキーを使用してUIの問題をデバッグする","構造化ログパターンを使用して`stdin`と`stdout`の観察可能性を高める"],"ko":["효율적인 오류 추적을 위해 AI 컴팩트 로그 모드를 구현합니다","카테고리 `U` UI 및 `H` 핫키를 사용하여 UI 문제를 디버깅합니다","구조화된 로깅 패턴을 사용하여 `stdin` 및 `stdout`의 관찰 가능성을 향상합니다"],"es":["Implementar el modo de registro compacto de IA para un seguimiento de errores eficiente","Depurar problemas de la interfaz de usuario con categorías como `U` interfaz de usuario y `H` tecla de acceso directo","Mejorar la observabilidad con patrones de registro estructurados para `stdin` y `stdout`"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre le mode de journalisation compact de l''IA pour un suivi d''erreurs efficace","Déboguer les problèmes d''interface utilisateur avec des catégories telles que `U` interface utilisateur et `H` raccourci clavier","Améliorer l''observabilité avec des modèles de journalisation structurés pour `stdin` et `stdout`"],"de":["Implementierung des kompakten Protokollmodus von KI für eine effiziente Fehlernachverfolgung","Debuggen von Benutzeroberflächenproblemen mit Kategorien wie `U` Benutzeroberfläche und `H` Hotkey","Verbesserung der Beobachtbarkeit mit strukturierten Protokollmustern für `stdin` und `stdout`"],"pt":["Implementar o modo de log compacto da IA para rastreamento de erros eficiente","Depurar problemas de UI com categorias como `U` UI e `H` hotkey","Aprimorar a observabilidade com padrões de registro estruturados para `stdin` e `stdout`"],"ru":["Реализовать компактный режим ведения журнала ИИ для эффективного отслеживания ошибок","Отладка проблем UI с категориями, такими как `U` UI и `H` хоткей","Улучшить наблюдаемость с помощью структурированных шаблонов ведения журнала для `stdin` и `stdout`"],"ar":["تنفيذ وضع سجل مضغوط للذكاء الاصطناعي لتتبع الأخطاء بكفاءة","تصحيح أخطاء واجهة المستخدم مع فئات مثل `U` واجهة المستخدم و `H` مفتاح سريع","تعزيز الرصد باستخدام أنماط سجل منظمة لـ `stdin` و `stdout`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GPUI and Zed''s UI framework compatibility","Specific to Rust programming language","Limited to compact stderr format"],"zh":["需要GPUI和Zed的UI框架兼容性","特定于Rust编程语言","仅限紧凑的stderr格式"],"ja":["GPUIとZedのUIフレームワークの互換性が必要","Rustプログラミング言語に特有","コンパクトなstderr形式に限定"],"ko":["GPUI 및 Zed의 UI 프레임워크와의 호환성이 필요합니다","Rust 프로그래밍 언어에 특정합니다","컴팩트한 stderr 형식으로 제한됩니다"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con GPUI y el marco de UI de Zed","Específico del lenguaje de programación Rust","Limitado al formato de stderr compacto"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec GPUI et le framework d''interface utilisateur de Zed","Spécifique au langage de programmation Rust","Limité au format de stderr compact"],"de":["Erfordert Kompatibilität mit GPUI und Zeds UI-Framework","Spezifisch für die Programmiersprache Rust","Begrenzt auf das kompakten stderr-Format"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade com GPUI e a estrutura de UI do Zed","Específico para a linguagem de programação Rust","Limitado ao formato de stderr compacto"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с GPUI и фреймворком UI Zed","Специфичен для языка программирования Rust","Ограничен компактным форматом stderr"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع GPUI وإطار UI ل Zed","محدد للغة البرمجة الرست","محدود بنسيق stderr المضغوط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
