,"ru":"CUDA Руководство: Разработка Высокопроизводительных Прило...","ar":"دليل CUDA: تطوير تطبيقات عالية الأداء","en":"cuda-guide"},"description":{"zh":"CUDA 指南是一种极简却强大的 AI 辅助开发框架，提供生产就绪的 CLAUDE.md 和 AGENTS.md 系统","ja":"CUDA ガイドは、最小限の設計ながら強力な AI アシスト開発フレームワークです","ko":"CUDA 가이드는 최소한의 설계ながら 강력한 AI 지원 개발 프레임워크입니다","es":"La guía de CUDA es un marco de desarrollo minimalista pero poderoso para aplicaciones de GPU, que incluye principios de parallelismo y acceso a memoria","fr":"La guide CUDA est un cadre de développement minimaliste mais puissant pour les applications GPU, qui inclut des principes de parallelisme et d''accès à la mém...","de":"Die CUDA-Anleitung ist ein minimalistisches, aber leistungsfähiges Entwicklungsfamework für GPU-Anwendungen, das Parallelismus- und Speicherzugriffsprinzipie...","pt":"A guia CUDA é um framework de desenvolvimento minimalista, mas poderoso, que ajuda a criar aplicações de alto desempenho para GPU","ru":"CUDA-руководство - это минималистичный, но мощный фреймворк для разработки высокопроизводительных приложений для GPU","ar":"دليل CUDA هو إطار開発 بسيط ولكن قوي يساعد على إنشاء تطبيقات عالية الأداء للوحدات الحوسبية الرسومية","en":"Minimalist yet powerful AI-assisted development framework. Production-ready CLAUDE.md & AGENTS.md system with 35+ guardrails, 4D methodology, and auto-loadin..."},"definition":{"en":"Minimalist yet powerful AI-assisted development framework. Production-ready CLAUDE.md & AGENTS.md system with 35+ guardrails, 4D methodology, and auto-loading language guides for TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust."},"features":{"zh":["生产就绪的 CLAUDE.md 和 AGENTS.md 系统","35+ 守护线","4D 方法论","自动加载语言指南","支持 TypeScript、Python、Go 和 Rust"],"ja":["CLAUDE.md と AGENTS.md システム","35 個以上のガードレール","4D 方法論","自動ローディング言語ガイド","TypeScript、Python、Go、Rust をサポート"],"ko":["프로덕션 레디의 CLAUDE.md와 AGENTS.md 시스템","35개 이상의 가드레일","4D 방법론","자동 로딩 언어 가이드","TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust 지원"],"es":["Diseño de algoritmos para miles de hilos concurrentes","Conciencia de la jerarquía de memoria","Acceso coalescido a la memoria","Compatibilidad con CUDA 11+","Soporte para TypeScript, Python, Go y Rust"],"fr":["Conception d''algorithmes pour des milliers de threads concurrents","Conscience de la hiérarchie de la mémoire","Accès coalescé à la mémoire","Compatibilité avec CUDA 11+","Prise en charge de TypeScript, Python, Go et Rust"],"de":["Entwurf von Algorithmen für Tausende von konkurrierenden Threads","Bewusstsein für die Speicherhierarchie","Koaleszierter Zugriff auf den Speicher","Kompatibilität mit CUDA 11+","Unterstützung für TypeScript, Python, Go und Rust"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de aplicações de alto desempenho para GPU","Princípios de paralelismo e hierarquia de memória","Suporte a linguagens de programação como TypeScript, Python, Go e Rust","Sistema de guardrails para garantir a estabilidade e o desempenho","Métodologia 4D para desenvolvimento de aplicações de alto desempenho"],"ru":["Разработка высокопроизводительных приложений для GPU","Принципы параллелизма и иерархии памяти","Поддержка языков программирования seperti TypeScript, Python, Go и Rust","Система guardrails для обеспечения стабильности и производительности","Методология 4D для разработки высокопроизводительных приложений"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات عالية الأداء للوحدات الحوسبية الرسومية","مبادئ التALLELISM وهرمية الذاكرة","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل TypeScript و Python و Go و Rust","نظام الحماية لضمان الاستقرار والأداء","منهجية 4D لتطوير تطبيقات عالية الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CUDA","GPU 计算","深度学习","AI 辅助开发","CLAUDE.md","AGENTS.md","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"],"ja":["CUDA","GPU コンピューティング","ディープラーニング","AI アシスト開発","CLAUDE.md","AGENTS.md","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"],"ko":["CUDA","GPU 컴퓨팅","딥러닝","AI 지원 개발","CLAUDE.md","AGENTS.md","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"],"es":["desarrollo de GPU","CUDA","parallelismo","acceso a memoria","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust","GPU computing","deep learning"],"fr":["développement GPU","CUDA","parallelisme","accès à la mémoire","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust","calcul GPU","apprentissage profond"],"de":["GPU-Entwicklung","CUDA","Parallelismus","Speicherzugriff","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust","GPU-Rechnen","tiefes Lernen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de alto desempenho","GPU","CUDA","paralelismo","hierarquia de memória","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"],"ru":["высокопроизводительное программирование","GPU","CUDA","параллелизм","иерархия памяти","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات عالية الأداء","الوحدات الحوسبية الرسومية","CUDA","التALLELISM","هرمية الذاكرة","TypeScript","Python","Go","Rust"]}},"owner":"ar4mirez","repo":"samuel","repoPath":"ar4mirez/samuel","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cuda-guide","description":"|","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# CUDA Guide\n\n> Applies to: CUDA 11+, GPU Computing, Deep Learning, Scientific Computing, HPC\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Parallelism First**: Design algorithms for thousands of concurrent threads; serial thinking is the primary enemy of GPU performance\n2. **Memory Hierarchy Awareness**: Global memory is 100x slower than shared memory and 1000x slower than registers; every kernel design starts with memory access planning\n3. **Coalesced Access**: Adjacent threads must access adjacent memory address","body":"# CUDA Guide\n\n> Applies to: CUDA 11+, GPU Computing, Deep Learning, Scientific Computing, HPC\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Parallelism First**: Design algorithms for thousands of concurrent threads; serial thinking is the primary enemy of GPU performance\n2. **Memory Hierarchy Awareness**: Global memory is 100x slower than shared memory and 1000x slower than registers; every kernel design starts with memory access planning\n3. **Coalesced Access**: Adjacent threads must access adjacent memory addresses; a single misaligned access pattern can reduce bandwidth by 32x\n4. **Occupancy Over Cleverness**: Maximize active warps per SM by managing register count, shared memory usage, and block dimensions together\n5. **Minimize Host-Device Transfers**: PCIe bandwidth is the bottleneck; overlap transfers with computation using streams and pinned memory\n\n## Guardrails\n\n### Error Checking\n\n- ALWAYS check CUDA API return values with a macro wrapper\n- ALWAYS call `cudaGetLastError()` after every kernel launch\n- ALWAYS call `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` before reading kernel results on the host\n- Use `compute-sanitizer` (successor to `cuda-memcheck`) in development builds\n- Handle `cudaErrorMemoryAllocation` gracefully; never assume GPU memory is infinite\n\n```cuda\n#define CUDA_CHECK(call)                                                    \\\n    do {                                                                    \\\n        cudaError_t err = call;                                            \\\n        if (err != cudaSuccess) {                                          \\\n            fprintf(stderr, \"CUDA error at %s:%d: %s\\n\",                   \\\n                    __FILE__, __LINE__, cudaGetErrorString(err));           \\\n            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);                                            \\\n        }                                                                   \\\n    } while (0)\n\n#define CUDA_CHECK_KERNEL()                                                 \\\n    do {                                                                    \\\n        cudaError_t err = cudaGetLastError();                              \\\n        if (err != cudaSuccess) {                                          \\\n            fprintf(stderr, \"Kernel launch error at %s:%d: %s\\n\",          \\\n                    __FILE__, __LINE__, cudaGetErrorString(err));           \\\n            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);                                            \\\n        }                                                                   \\\n    } while (0)\n```\n\n### Memory Management\n\n- Pair every `cudaMalloc` with a `cudaFree`; prefer RAII wrappers in C++ host code\n- Use `cudaMallocManaged` (Unified Memory) for prototyping; switch to explicit transfers for production\n- Use `cudaMallocHost` (pinned memory) when streaming data to the GPU; pageable memory cannot overlap with compute\n- Prefer `cudaMemcpyAsync` with streams over synchronous `cudaMemcpy`\n- Never access device pointers from host code or host pointers from device code (except Unified Memory)\n- Call `cudaMemset` or `cudaMemsetAsync` to zero-initialize device buffers\n\n### Kernel Design\n\n- Block size must be a multiple of warp size (32); prefer 128, 256, or 512\n- Calculate grid size as `(n + block_size - 1) / block_size`\n- Always include bounds checking: `if (idx < n)` at the top of every kernel\n- Use grid-stride loops for kernels that must handle arbitrary data sizes\n- Document thread mapping: which dimension maps to which data axis\n- Mark device-only helpers as `__device__`, host+device as `__host__ __device__`\n\n```cuda\n// Grid-stride loop: works with any grid size, any data size\n__global__ void saxpy(float a, const float* x, float* y, int n) {\n    for (int i = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n         i < n;\n         i += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        y[i] = a * x[i] + y[i];\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Synchronization\n\n- Use `__syncthreads()` after every shared memory write before any thread reads another thread''s value\n- Never place `__syncthreads()` inside a conditional branch that not all threads in a block will reach (deadlock)\n- Use `__syncwarp()` (CUDA 9+) for warp-level synchronization instead of relying on implicit warp-synchronous execution\n- Use `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` sparingly in production; prefer stream synchronization with `cudaStreamSynchronize()`\n- Use CUDA events (`cudaEventRecord` / `cudaEventSynchronize`) for fine-grained inter-stream ordering\n\n### Performance\n\n- Profile before optimizing: use Nsight Compute for kernel analysis, Nsight Systems for system-level view\n- Target >50% theoretical occupancy; use the CUDA Occupancy Calculator to tune block dimensions\n- Aim for >60% of peak memory bandwidth in memory-bound kernels\n- Avoid warp divergence: ensure threads within a warp take the same branch when possible\n- Prefer `float` over `double` on consumer GPUs (2x throughput difference)\n- Minimize atomic operations on global memory; use shared memory atomics with a final reduction\n\n## Memory Hierarchy\n\nUnderstanding the memory hierarchy is the single most important factor in CUDA performance.\n\n| Memory Type | Scope | Latency (cycles) | Size | Cached | Read/Write |\n|-------------|-------|-------------------|------|--------|------------|\n| Registers | Thread | 1 | ~255 per thread | N/A | R/W |\n| Shared | Block | ~5 | 48-164 KB per SM | N/A | R/W |\n| L1 Cache | SM | ~28 | 48-192 KB per SM | Auto | R |\n| L2 Cache | Device | ~200 | 4-40 MB | Auto | R/W |\n| Global | Device | ~400-600 | 4-80 GB (HBM/GDDR) | Yes | R/W |\n| Constant | Device | ~5 (cached) | 64 KB | Yes (broadcast) | R |\n| Texture | Device | ~400 (cached) | Global pool | Yes (spatial) | R |\n\n**Decision guide:**\n- Data reused within a thread -> registers (automatic via local variables)\n- Data shared across threads in a block -> `__shared__` memory\n- Read-only data broadcast to all threads -> `__constant__` memory\n- Large read-only data with spatial locality -> texture memory\n- Everything else -> global memory with coalesced access patterns\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Kernel Launch Configuration\n\n```cuda\n// Query device for optimal configuration\nvoid launch_optimized(const float* input, float* output, int n) {\n    int block_size;\n    int min_grid_size;\n\n    // Let the runtime suggest optimal block size for maximum occupancy\n    cudaOccupancyMaxPotentialBlockSize(\n        &min_grid_size, &block_size, my_kernel, 0, n);\n\n    int grid_size = (n + block_size - 1) / block_size;\n    my_kernel<<<grid_size, block_size>>>(input, output, n);\n    CUDA_CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### Coalesced Memory Access\n\n```cuda\n// BAD: Strided access -- adjacent threads access non-adjacent memory\n// Each warp issues 32 separate memory transactions\n__global__ void transpose_naive(const float* in, float* out, int W, int H) {\n    int x = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n    int y = blockIdx.y * blockDim.y + threadIdx.y;\n    if (x < W && y < H) {\n        out[x * H + y] = in[y * W + x];  // Write is strided\n    }\n}\n\n// GOOD: Use shared memory to coalesce both reads and writes\n__global__ void transpose_coalesced(\n    const float* in, float* out, int W, int H\n) {\n    __shared__ float tile[32][33]; // +1 padding avoids bank conflicts\n\n    int x = blockIdx.x * 32 + threadIdx.x;\n    int y = blockIdx.y * 32 + threadIdx.y;\n\n    if (x < W && y < H) {\n        tile[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = in[y * W + x]; // Coalesced read\n    }\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    x = blockIdx.y * 32 + threadIdx.x;\n    y = blockIdx.x * 32 + threadIdx.y;\n\n    if (x < H && y < W) {\n        out[y * H + x] = tile[threadIdx.x][threadIdx.y]; // Coalesced write\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Shared Memory Tiling\n\n```cuda\n// Dot product of two vectors using shared memory reduction\n__global__ void dot_product(\n    const float* a, const float* b, float* result, int n\n) {\n    __shared__ float cache[256];\n\n    int tid = threadIdx.x;\n    int idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n\n    // Each thread computes its partial sum via grid-stride\n    float partial = 0.0f;\n    for (int i = idx; i < n; i += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        partial += a[i] * b[i];\n    }\n    cache[tid] = partial;\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    // Tree reduction in shared memory\n    for (int s = blockDim.x / 2; s > 0; s >>= 1) {\n        if (tid < s) {\n            cache[tid] += cache[tid + s];\n        }\n        __syncthreads();\n    }\n\n    if (tid == 0) {\n        atomicAdd(result, cache[0]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Warp-Level Primitives (CUDA 9+)\n\n```cuda\n// Warp-level reduction using shuffle instructions -- no shared memory needed\n__device__ float warp_reduce_sum(float val) {\n    for (int offset = warpSize / 2; offset > 0; offset /= 2) {\n        val += __shfl_down_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, val, offset);\n    }\n    return val;\n}\n\n// Block-level reduction combining warp shuffles and shared memory\n__device__ float block_reduce_sum(float val) {\n    __shared__ float warp_sums[32]; // One slot per warp (max 32 warps/block)\n\n    int lane = threadIdx.x % warpSize;\n    int warp_id = threadIdx.x / warpSize;\n\n    val = warp_reduce_sum(val);\n\n    if (lane == 0) {\n        warp_sums[warp_id] = val;\n    }\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    // First warp reduces the warp sums\n    int num_warps = (blockDim.x + warpSize - 1) / warpSize;\n    val = (threadIdx.x < num_warps) ? warp_sums[threadIdx.x] : 0.0f;\n    if (warp_id == 0) {\n        val = warp_reduce_sum(val);\n    }\n\n    return val;\n}\n```\n\n## Performance\n\n### Occupancy Calculator\n\n```cuda\n// Query occupancy at compile time for tuning\nvoid report_occupancy() {\n    int block_size = 256;\n    int num_blocks;\n\n    cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMultiprocessor(\n        &num_blocks, my_kernel, block_size, 0);\n\n    cudaDeviceProp prop;\n    cudaGetDeviceProperties(&prop, 0);\n\n    int active_warps = num_blocks * (block_size / prop.warpSize);\n    int max_warps = prop.maxThreadsPerMultiProcessor / prop.warpSize;\n    float occupancy = (float)active_warps / max_warps;\n\n    printf(\"Occupancy: %.1f%% (%d/%d warps)\\n\",\n           occupancy * 100, active_warps, max_warps);\n}\n```\n\n### Nsight Profiling Workflow\n\n```bash\n# System-level trace: find CPU/GPU idle gaps, stream concurrency\nnsys profile -o trace ./program\nnsys stats trace.nsys-rep\n\n# Kernel-level analysis: roofline, memory throughput, occupancy\nncu --set full -o kernel_report ./program\nncu -i kernel_report.ncu-rep    # Open in Nsight Compute GUI\n\n# Quick single-metric check\nncu --metrics sm__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsed ./program\n```\n\n### Memory Bandwidth Measurement\n\n```cuda\n// Measure effective bandwidth of a kernel\nvoid measure_bandwidth(int n) {\n    size_t bytes = 2 * n * sizeof(float); // Read A + Write B\n\n    cudaEvent_t start, stop;\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventCreate(&start));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventCreate(&stop));\n\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventRecord(start));\n    copy_kernel<<<grid, block>>>(d_in, d_out, n);\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventRecord(stop));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventSynchronize(stop));\n\n    float ms = 0;\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventElapsedTime(&ms, start, stop));\n\n    float gb_per_sec = bytes / (ms * 1e6);\n    printf(\"Effective bandwidth: %.2f GB/s\\n\", gb_per_sec);\n\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(start));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(stop));\n}\n```\n\n## Tooling\n\n### Essential Commands\n\n```bash\n# Compile CUDA code\nnvcc -arch=sm_80 -O3 -o program main.cu         # Single file\nnvcc -arch=native -lineinfo -o program main.cu   # With debug line info\n\n# CMake build\ncmake -B build -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=\"70;80;86\"\ncmake --build build -j$(nproc)\n\n# Runtime debugging\ncompute-sanitizer ./program                      # Memory errors (replaces cuda-memcheck)\ncompute-sanitizer --tool racecheck ./program     # Shared memory race conditions\ncompute-sanitizer --tool initcheck ./program     # Uninitialized device memory reads\ncompute-sanitizer --tool synccheck ./program     # Synchronization errors\n\n# Profiling\nnsys profile ./program                           # System-level timeline\nncu ./program                                    # Kernel-level metrics\nncu --kernel-name my_kernel --launch-skip 2 --launch-count 1 ./program\n\n# Device info\nnvidia-smi                                       # GPU status and memory usage\nnvcc --version                                   # CUDA compiler version\n```\n\n### CMakeLists.txt Template\n\n```cmake\ncmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)\nproject(myproject LANGUAGES CXX CUDA)\n\nset(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_STANDARD 17)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES 70 80 86)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_SEPARABLE_COMPILATION ON)\n\nfind_package(CUDAToolkit REQUIRED)\n\nadd_library(kernels src/kernels.cu)\ntarget_include_directories(kernels PUBLIC include)\n\nadd_executable(main src/main.cpp)\ntarget_link_libraries(main kernels CUDA::cudart)\n\nenable_testing()\nadd_executable(tests tests/test_kernels.cu)\ntarget_link_libraries(tests kernels CUDA::cudart)\nadd_test(NAME gpu_tests COMMAND tests)\n```\n\n## References\n\nFor detailed patterns and examples, see:\n\n- [references/patterns.md](references/patterns.md) -- Tiled matrix multiply, parallel reduction tree, stream overlap pipeline\n\n## External References\n\n- [CUDA C++ Programming Guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/)\n- [CUDA C++ Best Practices Guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-best-practices-guide/)\n- [Nsight Compute Documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-compute/)\n- [Nsight Systems Documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-systems/)\n- [Thrust Documentation](https://nvidia.github.io/cccl/thrust/)\n- [CUDA Samples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples)\n- [NVIDIA Occupancy Calculator](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-occupancy-calculator/)\n- [GPU Memory Hierarchy (GTC talk)](https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tag/cuda/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:11:12.298Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for GPU Computing Agents requiring optimized CUDA development with parallelism and memory hierarchy awareness","zh":"适用于需要优化CUDA开发的GPU计算代理，具有并行性和内存层次感知","ja":"GPUコンピューティングエージェントが最適化されたCUDA開発と並列性、およびメモリ階層の認識を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"GPU 컴퓨팅 에이전트가 최적화된 CUDA 개발 및 병렬성과 메모리 계층 구조 인식이 필요한 경우에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de computación de GPU que requieren un desarrollo de CUDA optimizado con conciencia de paralelismo y jerarquía de memoria","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de calcul GPU nécessitant un développement CUDA optimisé avec une prise en compte du parallélisme et de la hiérarchie de mémoire","de":"Ideal für GPU-Computing-Agents, die ein optimiertes CUDA-Entwicklung mit Parallelismus und Speicherhierarchie-Bewusstsein erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes de computação GPU que requerem desenvolvimento de CUDA otimizado com paralelismo e conscientização da hierarquia de memória","ru":"Идеально для агентов GPU-вычислений, требующих оптимизированного развития CUDA с параллелизмом и осведомленностью о иерархии памяти","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الحوسبة GPU التي تتطلب تنمية CUDA محسنة مع متوازيّة ووعي هرمية الذاكرة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design high-performance algorithms with thousands of concurrent threads, leveraging core principles like Parallelism First, Memory Hierarchy Awareness, and Coalesced Access, while utilizing languages like TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust","zh":"赋予代理设计高性能算法的能力，具有数千个并发线程，利用并行性优先、内存层次感知和合并访问等核心原则，同时使用TypeScript、Python、Go和Rust等语言","ja":"エージェントが高性能アルゴリズムを設計する能力を付与します。数千の同時スレッドを利用し、並列性优先、メモリ階層の認識、まとめられたアクセスなどの基本原則を利用し、TypeScript、Python、Go、Rustなどの言語を使用する","ko":"에이전트가 높은 성능의 알고리즘을 설계할 수 있는 능력을 제공합니다. 수천 개의 동시 스레드를 활용하여 병렬성 우선, 메모리 계층 구조 인식 및 집합된 액세스와 같은 핵심 원칙을 활용하며 TypeScript, Python, Go 및 Rust와 같은 언어를 사용","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar algoritmos de alto rendimiento con miles de threads concurrentes, aprovechando principios básicos como Primero el paralelismo, conciencia de la jerarquía de memoria y acceso coalescido, mientras utiliza lenguajes como TypeScript, Python, Go y Rust","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des algorithmes haute performance avec des milliers de threads concurrents, en exploitant les principes fondamentaux tels que Parallélisme d''abord, Conscience de la hiérarchie de mémoire et Accès coalescé, tout en utilisant des langages tels que TypeScript, Python, Go et Rust","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Algorithmen mit hoher Leistung zu entwerfen, mit Tausenden von gleichzeitigen Threads, unter Ausnutzung von Kernprinzipien wie Parallelismus zuerst, Speicherhierarchie-Bewusstsein und koalesziertem Zugriff, während die Verwendung von Sprachen wie TypeScript, Python, Go und Rust","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar algoritmos de alto desempenho com milhares de threads concorrentes, aproveitando princípios básicos como Paralelismo Primeiro, Conscientização da Hierarquia de Memória e Acesso Coalescido, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza linguagens como TypeScript, Python, Go e Rust","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать высокопроизводительные алгоритмы с тысячами конкурирующих потоков, используя основные принципы, такие как Параллелизм Первый, Осведомленность о иерархии памяти и Слияние доступа, одновременно используя языки, такие как TypeScript, Python, Go и Rust","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصميم خوارزميات أداء عالية مع آلاف الخيوط المتزامنة، مستفيداً من مبادئ أساسية مثل المتوازيّة أولاً ووعي هرمية الذاكرة والوصول المتحد، في الوقت نفسه استخدام لغات مثل TypeScript و Python و Go و Rust"},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing deep learning models for GPU acceleration","Developing high-performance scientific computing applications with CUDA 11+","Implementing 4D methodology for efficient GPU resource utilization"],"zh":["为GPU加速优化深度学习模型","使用CUDA 11+开发高性能科学计算应用","实施4D方法以实现GPU资源的高效利用"],"ja":["GPUアクセラレーションのための深層学習モデルを最適化する","CUDA 11+を使用して高性能科学計算アプリケーションを開発する","GPUリソースの効率的な使用のための4D方法を実装する"],"ko":["GPU 가속을 위한 깊은 학습 모델 최적화","CUDA 11+를 사용하여 고성능 과학 계산 응용 프로그램 개발","GPU 리소스 효율적인 활용을 위한 4D 방법론 구현"],"es":["Optimizar modelos de aprendizaje profundo para la aceleración de GPU","Desarrollar aplicaciones de computación científica de alto rendimiento con CUDA 11+","Implementar la metodología 4D para una utilización eficiente de los recursos de GPU"],"fr":["Optimiser les modèles d''apprentissage profond pour l''accélération GPU","Développer des applications de calcul scientifique haute performance avec CUDA 11+","Mettre en œuvre la méthodologie 4D pour une utilisation efficace des ressources GPU"],"de":["Optimieren Sie tiefe Lernmodelle für die GPU-Beschleunigung","Entwickeln Sie Hochleistungs-Anwendungen für wissenschaftliches Rechnen mit CUDA 11+","Implementieren Sie die 4D-Methodik für eine effiziente Ausnutzung der GPU-Ressourcen"],"pt":["Otimizando modelos de aprendizado profundo para aceleração GPU","Desenvolvendo aplicações científicas de computação de alto desempenho com CUDA 11+","Implementando metodologia 4D para utilização eficiente de recursos GPU"],"ru":["Оптимизация моделей глубокого обучения для ускорения GPU","Разработка высокопроизводительных научных вычислительных приложений с CUDA 11+","Реализация методологии 4D для эффективного использования ресурсов GPU"],"ar":["تحسين نماذج التعلم العميق لتسريع GPU","تطوير تطبيقات الحوسبة العلمية عالية الأداء مع CUDA 11+","تنفيذ منهجية 4D لاستخدام موارد GPU بكفاءة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CUDA 11+ compatibility","GPU Computing environment necessary","Limited to languages supported by auto-loading language guides (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"zh":["需要CUDA 11+兼容性","需要GPU计算环境","仅限于自动加载语言指南支持的语言（TypeScript、Python、Go、Rust）"],"ja":["CUDA 11+の互換性が必要","GPUコンピューティング環境が必要","自動ロード言語ガイドでサポートされている言語（TypeScript、Python、Go、Rust）のみ"],"ko":["CUDA 11+ 호환성이 필요","GPU 컴퓨팅 환경이 필요","자동 로드 언어 가이드에서 지원하는 언어만 해당 (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con CUDA 11+","Entorno de computación de GPU necesario","Limitado a los lenguajes compatibles con las guías de idioma de auto-carga (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité CUDA 11+","Environnement de calcul GPU nécessaire","Limité aux langages pris en charge par les guides de langage de chargement automatique (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"de":["Erfordert CUDA 11+-Kompatibilität","GPU-Computing-Umgebung erforderlich","Begrenzt auf Sprachen, die von den Auto-Loading-Sprachführern unterstützt werden (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade com CUDA 11+","Ambiente de computação GPU necessário","Limitado a linguagens suportadas por guias de linguagem de carregamento automático (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с CUDA 11+","Необходимо окружение GPU-вычислений","Ограничен языками, поддерживаемыми автозагрузкой языковых справочников (TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust)"],"ar":["يتطلب التوافق مع CUDA 11+","بيئة حوسبة GPU ضرورية","محدود بلغات المدعومة من قبل أدلة لغة التحميل التلقائي (TypeScript و Python و Go و Rust)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('sanand0/scientific-research/matchms', 'community', 'sanand0', 'scientific-research', 'sanand0/scientific-research', 'matchms', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z', '2026-02-18T03:11:12.603Z', NULL, '{"id":"sanand0/scientific-research/matchms","name":"matchms","description":{"zh":"MatchmsPython","ja":"Matchms","ko":"Matchms","es":"Matchms es una biblioteca Python de código abierto para procesar y analizar datos de espectrometría de masas. Permite importar espectros desde varios formatos y construir flujos de trabajo analíticos","fr":"Matchms est une bibliothèque Python open-source pour traiter et analyser les données de spectrométrie de masse. Elle permet d''importer des spectres depuis plusieurs formats et de construire des flux de travail analytiques","de":"Matchms ist eine Open-Source-Python-Bibliothek zur Verarbeitung und Analyse von Massenspektrometrie-Daten. Sie ermöglicht das Importieren von Spektren aus verschiedenen Formaten und den Aufbau von analytischen Workflows","pt":"Matchms é uma biblioteca Python de código aberto para processamento e análise de dados de espectrometria de massa. Oferece funcionalidades para importar espectros, filtrar picos e calcular similaridades espectrais.","ru":"Matchms - это открытая библиотека Python для обработки и анализа данных масс-спектрометрии. Предоставляет функции для импорта спектров, фильтрации пиков и расчета спектральных сходств.","ar":"ماتش إم إس هي مكتبة بايثون مفتوحة المصدر لتحليل بيانات مطياف الكتلة. توفر وظائف لاستيراد المطياف، وفلاتر الذروات و حساب التشابه الطيفي.","en":"Scientific Research"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Matchms_python_","ja":"Matchms","ko":"Matchms","es":"Matchms: Biblioteca Python para Análisis de Espectrometrí...","fr":"Matchms: Bibliothèque Python pour l''Analyse de Spectromét...","de":"Matchms: Python-Bibliothek für Massenspektrometrie-Datena...","pt":"Matchms: Biblioteca Python para Análise de Espectrometria...","ru":"Matchms: Открытая библиотека Python для обработки данных ...","ar":"ماتش إم إس: مكتبة بايثون مفتوحة المصدر لتحليل مطياف الكتلة","en":"matchms"},"description":{"zh":"MatchmsPython","ja":"Matchms","ko":"Matchms","es":"Matchms es una biblioteca Python de código abierto para procesar y analizar datos de espectrometría de masas. Permite importar espectros desde varios formato...","fr":"Matchms est une bibliothèque Python open-source pour traiter et analyser les données de spectrométrie de masse. Elle permet d''importer des spectres depuis pl...","de":"Matchms ist eine Open-Source-Python-Bibliothek zur Verarbeitung und Analyse von Massenspektrometrie-Daten. Sie ermöglicht das Importieren von Spektren aus ve...","pt":"Matchms é uma biblioteca Python de código aberto para processamento e análise de dados de espectrometria de massa. Oferece funcionalidades para importar espe...","ru":"Matchms - это открытая библиотека Python для обработки и анализа данных масс-спектрометрии. Предоставляет функции для импорта спектров, фильтрации пиков и ра...","ar":"ماتش إم إس هي مكتبة بايثون مفتوحة المصدر لتحليل بيانات مطياف الكتلة. توفر وظائف لاستيراد المطياف، وفلاتر الذروات و حساب التشابه الطيفي.","en":"Scientific Research"},"definition":{"en":"Scientific Research"},"features":{"zh":["Matchms","API","Python","Matchms","Matchms","Matchms"],"ja":["Matchms","MatchmsAPI","Python","Matchms","Matchms","Matchms"],"ko":["Matchms","MatchmsAPI","Python","Matchms","Matchms","Matchms"],"es":["Importación de espectros desde varios formatos","Estándarización de metadatos","Filtrado de picos","Cálculo de similitudes espectrales","Construcción de flujos de trabajo analíticos"],"fr":["Importation de spectres depuis plusieurs formats","Standardisation des métadonnées","Filtrage des pics","Calcul de similitudes spectrales","Construction de flux de travail analytiques"],"de":["Importieren von Spektren aus verschiedenen Formaten","Standardisierung von Metadaten","Filtrieren von Peaks","Berechnung von spektralen Ähnlichkeiten","Aufbau von analytischen Workflows"],"pt":["Importação de espectros de vários formatos","Filtragem de picos","Cálculo de similaridades espectrais","Construção de fluxos de trabalho analíticos reprodutíveis","Exportação de dados processados"],"ru":["Импорт спектров из различных форматов","Фильтрация пиков","Расчет спектральных сходств","Создание воспроизводимых аналитических рабочих процессов","Экспорт обработанных данных"],"ar":["استيراد المطياف من صيغ مختلفة","فلاتر الذروات","حساب التشابه الطيفي","بناء سلاسل عمل تحليلية قابلة للتكرار","استخراج البيانات المعالجة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Matchms","Python","Matchms","MatchmsAPI","Matchms","Matchms"],"ja":["Matchms","MatchmsAPI","Python","Matchms","Matchms","Matchms"],"ko":["Matchms","MatchmsAPI","Python","Matchms","Matchms","Matchms"],"es":["espectrometría de masas","análisis de datos","biblioteca Python","procesamiento de datos","flujos de trabajo analíticos","similitudes espectrales"],"fr":["spectrométrie de masse","analyse de données","bibliothèque Python","traitement de données","flux de travail analytiques","similitudes spectrales"],"de":["Massenspektrometrie","Datenanalyse","Python-Bibliothek","Datenverarbeitung","analytische Workflows","spektrale Ähnlichkeiten"],"pt":["espectrometria de massa","análise de dados","biblioteca python","processamento de dados","mass spectrometry","data analysis"],"ru":["масс-спектрометрия","обработка данных","библиотека python","анализ данных","mass spectrometry","data processing"],"ar":["مطياف الكتلة","تحليل البيانات","مكتبة بايثون","معالجة البيانات","mass spectrometry","تحليل البيانات"]}},"owner":"sanand0","repo":"scientific-research","repoPath":"sanand0/scientific-research","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.404Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"matchms","description":"Mass spectrometry analysis. Process mzML/MGF/MSP, spectral similarity (cosine, modified cosine), metadata harmonization, compound ID, for metabolomics and MS data processing.","bodyPreview":"# Matchms\n\n## Overview\n\nMatchms is an open-source Python library for mass spectrometry data processing and analysis. Import spectra from various formats, standardize metadata, filter peaks, calculate spectral similarities, and build reproducible analytical workflows.\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Importing and Exporting Mass Spectrometry Data\n\nLoad spectra from multiple file formats and export processed data:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms.importing import load_from_mgf, load_from_mzml, load_from_msp,","body":"# Matchms\n\n## Overview\n\nMatchms is an open-source Python library for mass spectrometry data processing and analysis. Import spectra from various formats, standardize metadata, filter peaks, calculate spectral similarities, and build reproducible analytical workflows.\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Importing and Exporting Mass Spectrometry Data\n\nLoad spectra from multiple file formats and export processed data:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms.importing import load_from_mgf, load_from_mzml, load_from_msp, load_from_json\nfrom matchms.exporting import save_as_mgf, save_as_msp, save_as_json\n\n# Import spectra\nspectra = list(load_from_mgf(\"spectra.mgf\"))\nspectra = list(load_from_mzml(\"data.mzML\"))\nspectra = list(load_from_msp(\"library.msp\"))\n\n# Export processed spectra\nsave_as_mgf(spectra, \"output.mgf\")\nsave_as_json(spectra, \"output.json\")\n```\n\n**Supported formats:**\n- mzML and mzXML (raw mass spectrometry formats)\n- MGF (Mascot Generic Format)\n- MSP (spectral library format)\n- JSON (GNPS-compatible)\n- metabolomics-USI references\n- Pickle (Python serialization)\n\nFor detailed importing/exporting documentation, consult `references/importing_exporting.md`.\n\n### 2. Spectrum Filtering and Processing\n\nApply comprehensive filters to standardize metadata and refine peak data:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms.filtering import default_filters, normalize_intensities\nfrom matchms.filtering import select_by_relative_intensity, require_minimum_number_of_peaks\n\n# Apply default metadata harmonization filters\nspectrum = default_filters(spectrum)\n\n# Normalize peak intensities\nspectrum = normalize_intensities(spectrum)\n\n# Filter peaks by relative intensity\nspectrum = select_by_relative_intensity(spectrum, intensity_from=0.01, intensity_to=1.0)\n\n# Require minimum peaks\nspectrum = require_minimum_number_of_peaks(spectrum, n_required=5)\n```\n\n**Filter categories:**\n- **Metadata processing**: Harmonize compound names, derive chemical structures, standardize adducts, correct charges\n- **Peak filtering**: Normalize intensities, select by m/z or intensity, remove precursor peaks\n- **Quality control**: Require minimum peaks, validate precursor m/z, ensure metadata completeness\n- **Chemical annotation**: Add fingerprints, derive InChI/SMILES, repair structural mismatches\n\nMatchms provides 40+ filters. For the complete filter reference, consult `references/filtering.md`.\n\n### 3. Calculating Spectral Similarities\n\nCompare spectra using various similarity metrics:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms import calculate_scores\nfrom matchms.similarity import CosineGreedy, ModifiedCosine, CosineHungarian\n\n# Calculate cosine similarity (fast, greedy algorithm)\nscores = calculate_scores(references=library_spectra,\n                         queries=query_spectra,\n                         similarity_function=CosineGreedy())\n\n# Calculate modified cosine (accounts for precursor m/z differences)\nscores = calculate_scores(references=library_spectra,\n                         queries=query_spectra,\n                         similarity_function=ModifiedCosine(tolerance=0.1))\n\n# Get best matches\nbest_matches = scores.scores_by_query(query_spectra[0], sort=True)[:10]\n```\n\n**Available similarity functions:**\n- **CosineGreedy/CosineHungarian**: Peak-based cosine similarity with different matching algorithms\n- **ModifiedCosine**: Cosine similarity accounting for precursor mass differences\n- **NeutralLossesCosine**: Similarity based on neutral loss patterns\n- **FingerprintSimilarity**: Molecular structure similarity using fingerprints\n- **MetadataMatch**: Compare user-defined metadata fields\n- **PrecursorMzMatch/ParentMassMatch**: Simple mass-based filtering\n\nFor detailed similarity function documentation, consult `references/similarity.md`.\n\n### 4. Building Processing Pipelines\n\nCreate reproducible, multi-step analysis workflows:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms import SpectrumProcessor\nfrom matchms.filtering import default_filters, normalize_intensities\nfrom matchms.filtering import select_by_relative_intensity, remove_peaks_around_precursor_mz\n\n# Define a processing pipeline\nprocessor = SpectrumProcessor([\n    default_filters,\n    normalize_intensities,\n    lambda s: select_by_relative_intensity(s, intensity_from=0.01),\n    lambda s: remove_peaks_around_precursor_mz(s, mz_tolerance=17)\n])\n\n# Apply to all spectra\nprocessed_spectra = [processor(s) for s in spectra]\n```\n\n### 5. Working with Spectrum Objects\n\nThe core `Spectrum` class contains mass spectral data:\n\n```python\nfrom matchms import Spectrum\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Create a spectrum\nmz = np.array([100.0, 150.0, 200.0, 250.0])\nintensities = np.array([0.1, 0.5, 0.9, 0.3])\nmetadata = {\"precursor_mz\": 250.5, \"ionmode\": \"positive\"}\n\nspectrum = Spectrum(mz=mz, intensities=intensities, metadata=metadata)\n\n# Access spectrum properties\nprint(spectrum.peaks.mz)           # m/z values\nprint(spectrum.peaks.intensities)  # Intensity values\nprint(spectrum.get(\"precursor_mz\")) # Metadata field\n\n# Visualize spectra\nspectrum.plot()\nspectrum.plot_against(reference_spectrum)\n```\n\n### 6. Metadata Management\n\nStandardize and harmonize spectrum metadata:\n\n```python\n# Metadata is automatically harmonized\nspectrum.set(\"Precursor_mz\", 250.5)  # Gets harmonized to lowercase key\nprint(spectrum.get(\"precursor_mz\"))   # Returns 250.5\n\n# Derive chemical information\nfrom matchms.filtering import derive_inchi_from_smiles, derive_inchikey_from_inchi\nfrom matchms.filtering import add_fingerprint\n\nspectrum = derive_inchi_from_smiles(spectrum)\nspectrum = derive_inchikey_from_inchi(spectrum)\nspectrum = add_fingerprint(spectrum, fingerprint_type=\"morgan\", nbits=2048)\n```\n\n## Common Workflows\n\nFor typical mass spectrometry analysis workflows, including:\n- Loading and preprocessing spectral libraries\n- Matching unknown spectra against reference libraries\n- Quality filtering and data cleaning\n- Large-scale similarity comparisons\n- Network-based spectral clustering\n\nConsult `references/workflows.md` for detailed examples.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nuv pip install matchms\n```\n\nFor molecular structure processing (SMILES, InChI):\n```bash\nuv pip install matchms[chemistry]\n```\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\nDetailed reference documentation is available in the `references/` directory:\n- `filtering.md` - Complete filter function reference with descriptions\n- `similarity.md` - All similarity metrics and when to use them\n- `importing_exporting.md` - File format details and I/O operations\n- `workflows.md` - Common analysis patterns and examples\n\nLoad these references as needed for detailed information about specific matchms capabilities.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:11:12.603Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Scientific Research Agents needing advanced mass spectrometry data processing and analysis capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级质谱数据处理和分析能力的科学研究代理。","ja":"高度な質量分析データ処理および分析機能を必要とする科学研究エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급質量分析 데이터 처리 및 분석 기능을 필요로 하는 과학 연구 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Investigación Científica que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de procesamiento y análisis de datos de espectrometría de masas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de recherche scientifique ayant besoin de capacités avancées de traitement et d''analyse de données de spectrométrie de masse.","de":"Perfekt für wissenschaftliche Forschungsagenten, die erweiterte Fähigkeiten zur Datenverarbeitung und -analyse von Massenspektrometrie benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Pesquisa Científica que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de processamento e análise de dados de espectrometria de massa.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов научных исследований, которым необходимы передовые возможности обработки и анализа данных масс-спектрометрии.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البحث العلمي الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لمعالجة وتحليل بيانات مطياف الكتلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to import and export mass spectrometry data from various formats like MGF, MZML, and MSP, standardize metadata, filter peaks, and calculate spectral similarities using the matchms Python library.","zh":"使代理能够从各种格式（如MGF、MZML和MSP）导入和导出质谱数据，标准化元数据，过滤峰值，并使用matchms Python库计算光谱相似性。","ja":"エージェントがさまざまなフォーマット（MGF、MZML、MSPなど）から質量分析データをインポートおよびエクスポートし、メタデータを標準化し、ピークをフィルタし、matchms Pythonライブラリを使用してスペクトル類似性を計算できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 다양한 형식(MGF, MZML, MSP 등)에서 질량 분석 데이터를 가져오고 내보내고, 메타데이터를 표준화하고, 피크를 필터링하고, matchms Python 라이브러리를 사용하여 스펙트럼 유사성을 계산할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a importar y exportar datos de espectrometría de masas desde varios formatos como MGF, MZML y MSP, estandarizar metadatos, filtrar picos y calcular similitudes espectrales utilizando la biblioteca Python matchms.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''importer et d''exporter des données de spectrométrie de masse à partir de différents formats tels que MGF, MZML et MSP, de normaliser les métadonnées, de filtrer les pics et de calculer des similarités spectrales à l''aide de la bibliothèque Python matchms.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Massenspektrometriedaten aus verschiedenen Formaten wie MGF, MZML und MSP zu importieren und zu exportieren, Metadaten zu standardisieren, Peaks zu filtern und spektrale Ähnlichkeiten mit der Python-Bibliothek matchms zu berechnen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a importar e exportar dados de espectrometria de massa de vários formatos como MGF, MZML e MSP, padronizar metadados, filtrar picos e calcular semelhanças espectrais usando a biblioteca Python matchms.","ru":"Позволяет агентам импортировать и экспортировать данные масс-спектрометрии из различных форматов, таких как MGF, MZML и MSP, стандартизировать метаданные, фильтровать пики и рассчитывать спектральные сходства с помощью библиотеки Python matchms.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء باستيراد وتصدير بيانات مطياف الكتلة من صيغ متعددة مثل MGF و MZML و MSP، وتمكينهم من توحيد البيانات الوصفية وتصفية القمم وحساب الشبه بين الأطياف باستخدام مكتبة بايثون matchms."},"useCases":{"en":["Importing and exporting mass spectrometry data from multiple file formats","Standardizing metadata for reproducible analytical workflows","Calculating spectral similarities for advanced data analysis"],"zh":["从多个文件格式导入和导出质谱数据","标准化元数据以实现可复现的分析工作流","计算光谱相似性以进行高级数据分析"],"ja":["複数のファイル形式からの質量分析データのインポートおよびエクスポート","再現可能な分析ワークフローを実現するためのメタデータの標準化","高度なデータ分析のためのスペクトル類似性の計算"],"ko":["여러 파일 형식에서 질량 분석 데이터를 가져오고 내보내는 것","재현 가능한 분석 워크플로를 위한 메타데이터 표준화","고급 데이터 분석을 위한 스펙트럼 유사성 계산"],"es":["Importación y exportación de datos de espectrometría de masas desde múltiples formatos de archivo","Estandarización de metadatos para flujos de trabajo analíticos reproducibles","Cálculo de similitudes espectrales para un análisis de datos avanzado"],"fr":["Importation et exportation de données de spectrométrie de masse à partir de plusieurs formats de fichiers","Normalisation des métadonnées pour des flux de travail analytiques reproductibles","Calcul de similarités spectrales pour une analyse de données avancée"],"de":["Importieren und Exportieren von Massenspektrometriedaten aus mehreren Dateiformaten","Standardisierung von Metadaten für reproduzierbare analytische Workflows","Berechnung von spektralen Ähnlichkeiten für eine erweiterte Datenanalyse"],"pt":["Importação e exportação de dados de espectrometria de massa de vários formatos de arquivo","Padronização de metadados para fluxos de trabalho analíticos reprodutíveis","Cálculo de semelhanças espectrais para análise de dados avançada"],"ru":["Импорт и экспорт данных масс-спектрометрии из нескольких форматов файлов","Стандартизация метаданных для воспроизводимых аналитических рабочих процессов","Расчет спектральных сходств для расширенного анализа данных"],"ar":["استيراد وتصدير بيانات مطياف الكتلة من صيغ ملفات متعددة","توحيد البيانات الوصفية لتدفقات العمل التحليلية القابلة للتكرار","حساب الشبه بين الأطياف لتحليل البيانات المتقدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","Limited to mass spectrometry data processing and analysis"],"zh":["需要Python环境","仅限于质谱数据处理和分析"],"ja":["Python環境が必要","質量分析データ処理および分析に限定される"],"ko":["Python 환경이 필요","질량 분석 데이터 처리 및 분석에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python","Limitado al procesamiento y análisis de datos de espectrometría de masas"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","Limité au traitement et à l''analyse de données de spectrométrie de masse"],"de":["Benötigt eine Python-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf die Verarbeitung und Analyse von Massenspektrometriedaten"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Limitado ao processamento e análise de dados de espectrometria de massa"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Ограничен обработкой и анализом данных масс-спектрометрии"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون","محدود بمعالجة وتحليل بيانات مطياف الكتلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
